treet-level fight of neighborhood canvassing and phone banks conducted largely out of sight and distinct from the ad wars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/us/politics/door-knocking-army-tries-to-tip-virginia-senate-race.html', 'snippet': 'The election has become a street-level fight of neighborhood canvassing and phone banks conducted largely out of sight and distinct from the ad wars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STERLING, Va. — Faiza Abdulle hopscotched through the tidy middle-class streets of exurban Washington one evening last month, carrying an iPod Touch that directed her surgically to the houses of a very certain type of voter.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/us/01dominion4/01dominion4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/us/01dominion4/01dominion4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trying to Tip Virginia Senate Race With Pinpoint Door-Knocking', 'kicker': 'New Dominion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Pinpoint Door-Knocking, Trying to Tip Virginia Senate Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaine, Timothy M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLEN, GEORGE F', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T01:22:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f81da366-e799-55bf-8e0c-413479edc818', 'word_count': 1289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f81da366-e799-55bf-8e0c-413479edc818'}, {'abstract': 'In announcing the closing, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg cited damage to school buildings as the reason, but said he expected almost all schools to reopen Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/nyregion/new-york-city-schools-shut-for-the-week.html', 'snippet': 'In announcing the closing, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg cited damage to school buildings as the reason, but said he expected almost all schools to reopen Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City public schools will remain closed through the rest of the week, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg said Wednesday, creating an enormous scheduling headache for harried parents.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/nyregion/SCHOOLS/SCHOOLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/01/nyregion/SCHOOLS/SCHOOLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/nyregion/SCHOOLS/SCHOOLS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/nyregion/SCHOOLS/SCHOOLS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Storm Closes City Schools for a Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Storm Closes City Schools for a Week, the System’s Longest Suspension in Decades', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T01:27:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenny Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f612c4a-55c9-51e7-a47b-db7b8ea34678', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f612c4a-55c9-51e7-a47b-db7b8ea34678'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Fitch was a superstar speedster whose greatest achievement, the Fitch Inertial Barrier, can be found on public highways.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/sports/autoracing/john-cooper-fitch-glamorous-racer-with-a-flair-for-danger-dies-at-95.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Fitch was a superstar speedster whose greatest achievement, the Fitch Inertial Barrier, can be found on public highways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He seemed bathed in golden sunlight, this John Cooper Fitch, who put on goggles and a polo helmet and drove racing cars as fast as anybody in the world, including his sometime partner, Stirling Moss. He shot a newly introduced German jet from the sky in World War II, raced yachts, built his own sports cars.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/u