 'word_count': 1432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66395156-8f2f-5445-8514-8870ce9db788'}, {'abstract': 'An administrator described third-world conditions, with no hot water, no lab or radiology services and pails of water hauled up the stairs to use for flushing toilets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/nyregion/bellevue-hospital-evacuates-patients-after-backup-power-fails.html', 'snippet': 'An administrator described third-world conditions, with no hot water, no lab or radiology services and pails of water hauled up the stairs to use for flushing toilets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bellevue Hospital Center, New York City’s flagship public hospital and the premier trauma center in Manhattan, shut down Wednesday after fuel pumps for its backup power generators failed, and it worked into the night to evacuate the 300 patients left in its darkened building. There were 725 patients there when Hurricane Sandy hit. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/nyregion/HOSPITAL/HOSPITAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/nyregion/HOSPITAL/HOSPITAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bellevue Hospital Evacuates Patients After Backup Power Fails', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bellevue Hospital Evacuated After Backup Power Fails', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bellevue Hospital Center', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 3, 'maj