seeking $469.9 million in penalties from the bank, and $18 million from four former traders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Latest Headache at Barclays', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T12:41:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e888f08c-4dfb-5c29-b414-962721ae5004', 'word_count': 1539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e888f08c-4dfb-5c29-b414-962721ae5004'}, {'abstract': 'Steven P. Jobs pushed Apple’s software designers to use virtual doodads that mimic the appearance and behavior of real-world things, like wooden shelves for organizing newspapers. But the company’s management shake-up is likely to mean that Apple will shift away from such tricks, Nick Wingfield and Nick Bilton report in Thursday’s New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/daily-report-apple-shake-up-may-lead-to-design-shift/', 'snippet': 'Steven P. Jobs pushed Apple’s software designers to use virtual doodads that mimic the appearance and behavior of real-world things, like wooden shelves for organizing newspapers. But the company’s management shake-up is likely to mean that Apple ...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Steven P. Jobs, the Apple chief executive who died a year ago, pushed the company’s software designers to use virtual doodads that mimic the appearance and behavior of real-world things, like wooden shelves for organizing newspapers and the page-flipping motion of a book. But the management shake-up that Apple announced on Monday is likely to mean that Apple will shift away from such visual tricks, which many people within the company look down upon, Nick Wingfield and Nick Bilton report in Thursday’s New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: Apple Shake-Up May Lead to Design Shift', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T12:41:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/112f533f-0ae7-564d-bbc3-854feb55f776', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/112f533f-0ae7-564d-bbc3-854feb55f776'}, {'abstract': 'RedPrairie agreed on Thursday to buy JDA Software for $1.9 billion in cash, combining two firms that make software that helps companies manage their supply chains.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/redprairie-to-buy-jda-software-for-1-9-billion/', 'snippet': 'RedPrairie agreed on Thursday to buy JDA Software for $1.9 billion in cash, combining two firms that make software that helps companies manage their supply chains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RedPrairie agreed on Thursday to acquire the JDA Software Group for $1.9 billion in cash, combining two firms that make software that helps companies manage their supply chains.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'RedPrairie to Buy JDA Software for $1.9 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JDA Software Group Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T13:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f7abdc5-80ea-596d-9916-7c91c2e9c93d', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f7abdc5-80ea-596d-9916-7c91c2e9c93d'}, {'abstract': 'C. Wonder’s fun and festive Mad for Plaid gazelle slippers are perfect for the holiday season.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/the-get-c-wonder-slippers/', 'snippet': 'C. Wonder’s fun and festive Mad for Plaid gazelle slippers are perfect for the holiday season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not yet Thanksgiving, but the holidays are fast approaching, along with party planning — and party dressing. Enter C. Wonder‘s fun and festive Mad for Plaid gazelle slippers. Lightweight and whimsical, they’ll give a silk faille A-line party dress understated elegance and ease, but look just at home with a pair of jeans and a cozy knit. “I always wear Shipton & Heneage velvet slippers with words embroidered on them, and they make people smile,” says Chris Burch, the brand’s founder. “The design team took inspiration from my slippers and created these in time for the holidays.” With a red embroidered stag on the vamp, let Rudolph be your guide this season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | C. Wonder Slippers', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'C Wonder', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T13:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/610fce44-61c5-5d8f-a70a-fe31344fb016', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/610fce44-61c5-5d8f-a70a-fe31344fb016'}, {'abstract': 'Mumbai’s antiquated drainage and lack of planning and building standards mean the city would be devastated by a big storm.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/what-if-mumbai-gets-hit-by-a-storm-like-sandy/', 'snippet': 'Mumbai’s antiquated drainage and lack of planning and building standards mean the city would be devastated by a big storm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the New York metropolitan region reels in the aftermath of Hurricane Sandy, those outside the area may wonder how their own cities would fare in such a disaster.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What If…Mumbai Gets Hit by a Storm Like Sandy?', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T13:13:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0df62693-4e84-5c4e-affe-a764d012d162', 'word_count': 973, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0df62693-4e84-5c4e-affe-a764d012d162'}, {'abstract': 'The campaigns roared back to life with urgent closing arguments and a flurry of cross-country rallies as Mitt Romney raced to overtake President Obama in the election’s final 100 hours.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/us/politics/after-storm-hiatus-presidential-race-is-back-in-full-swing.html', 'snippet': 'The campaigns roared back to life with urgent closing arguments and a flurry of cross-country rallies as Mitt Romney raced to overtake President Obama in the election’s final 100 hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The two presidential campaigns roared back to life on Thursday, ending a storm-imposed