/JP-YOUTH-1-LN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poetry Pairing | ‘Though Some Saith That Youth Ruleth Me’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T14:25:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0094ca65-cc64-5e00-93fb-47e57571b915', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0094ca65-cc64-5e00-93fb-47e57571b915'}, {'abstract': 'Retailers enjoyed an average 2.7 percent increase in same-store sales, but analysts were looking ahead to November’s results to assess Hurricane Sandy’s impact.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/business/economy/retailers-report-an-upbeat-october.html', 'snippet': 'Retailers enjoyed an average 2.7 percent increase in same-store sales, but analysts were looking ahead to November’s results to assess Hurricane Sandy’s impact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shoppers continued to spend steadily at retailers in October, from discounters all the way to the high end, suggesting consumer confidence heading into the holiday season.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/business/SHOP/SHOP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/business/SHOP/SHOP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/business/SHOP/SHOP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/02/business/SHOP/SHOP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/business/SHOP/SHOP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Month of Gains for Stores, Before a Storm’s Toll', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Month of Gains for Stores, Before a Storm’s Toll', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T14:29:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99abc123-6da9-508d-9249-73fbe87f2e4f', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99abc123-6da9-508d-9249-73fbe87f2e4f'}, {'abstract': 'Asian-Americans are tangled up in race-conscious admissions in complicated ways. Some see themselves as victims of affirmative action. Others as benefiting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/education/edlife/affirmative-action-a-complicated-issue-for-asian-americans.html', 'snippet': 'Asian-Americans are tangled up in race-conscious admissions in complicated ways. Some see themselves as victims of affirmative action. Others as benefiting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A COLLEGE education aims to guide students through unfamiliar territory — Arabic, Dante, organic chemistry — so what was once alien comes to feel a lot less so. But sometimes an issue starts so close to home that the educational goal is the inverse: to take what students think of as familiar and place it in a new and surprising light.', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/education/04AFFIRM_SPAN/04AFFIRM_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/04/education/04AFFIRM_SPAN/04AFFIRM_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/education/04AFFIRM_SPAN/04AFFIRM_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/education/04AFFIRM_SPAN/04AFFIRM_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/education/04AFFIRM_SPAN/04AFFIRM_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/04/education/04AFFIRM_SPAN/04AFFIRM_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/education/04AFFIRM_SPAN/04AFFIRM_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Asian-Americans in the Argument', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Asian-American Affirmation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asian-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Texas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AFFIRMATIVE ACTION', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Abigail Noel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T14:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'EdLife', 'section_name': 'Education', 'subsection_name': 'Education Life', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccc6c78c-8fc1-55e5-b6fd-f565ce1dad5d', 'word_count': 2377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccc6c78c-8fc1-55e5-b6fd-f565ce1dad5d'}, {'abstract': 'Policy makers are being urged to address long-term unemployment before those looking for work decide to give up trying for good.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/business/economy/lingering-unemployment-poses-long-term-risk.html', 'snippet': 'Policy makers are being urged to address long-term unemployment before those looking for work decide to give up trying for good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In the economy-focused presidential campaign, the two candidates and their teams have scarcely mentioned what economists desc