 could hinge on how he negotiates with Senate Democrats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For those of us with a Twitter-enabled polling addiction and a bad crosstab habit, it’s almost become possible to lose sight of the fact that there’s more at stake in this election than whether state pollsters are more reliable than national ones, or whether Gallup’s likely-voter screen is an outlier or spot-on, or which party’s demographic projections makes more sense. Maybe that explains why this Politico story on the Romney transition effort seemed to come and go last week with hardly any comment. Obviously the various on-background quotes need to be taken with a grain of salt (not least because the most important players in Romney’s inner circle are still absorbed with the campaign), but this seemed like a striking passage:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'If Romney Wins', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T15:03:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fb6a3fe-c18b-5d9b-a4d1-845023e9dacf', 'word_count': 1549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fb6a3fe-c18b-5d9b-a4d1-845023e9dacf'}, {'abstract': 'For cancer patients like me, and for others who suffer from chronic or life-threatening illnesses, natural disasters don’t put health on the back burner. In fact, disasters like this one only add another layer of concern.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/life-interrupted-hurricanes-and-cancer/', 'snippet': 'For cancer patients like me, and for others who suffer from chronic or life-threatening illnesses, natural disasters don’t put health on the back burner. In fact, disasters like this one only add another layer of concern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Hurricane Sandy prepared to make landfall on Monday, my boyfriend, Seamus, was making a checklist: Do we have candles, flashlights? Could a tree fall through our window? Have we stocked up on enough water and food? Are our loved ones safe? ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/health/20121101_suleika/20121101_suleika-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/health/20121101_suleika/20121101_suleika-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1638, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/health/20121101_suleika/20121101_suleika-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/01/health/20121101_suleika/20121101_suleika-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/health/20121101_suleika/20121101_suleika-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Life, Interrupted: Hurricanes and Cancer', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One More Source of Stress For Those in Medical Crisis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chemother