ick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/602a77b2-478b-5a8c-80fa-fea067399188', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/602a77b2-478b-5a8c-80fa-fea067399188'}, {'abstract': 'A new study by a graduate student in computer science and law at Stanford University, reports that both the Romney and Obama campaign Web sites are leaking information about site visitors to a number of third-party trackers operating on their pages.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/romney-and-obama-campaigns-leaking-web-site-visitor-data/', 'snippet': 'A new study by a graduate student in computer science and law at Stanford University, reports that both the Romney and Obama campaign Web sites are leaking information about site visitors to a number of third-party trackers operating on their page...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The presidential campaign sites BarackObama.com and MittRomney.com have recently ratcheted up their use of third-party Web trackers. These are companies, like ad networks and data brokers working on behalf of the campaigns, that collect information about users’ online activities to show political ads to people tailored to their own interests and beliefs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01bits-obama/01bits-obama-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 255, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01bits-obama/01bits-obama-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 255, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01bits-obama/01bits-obama-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01bits-obama/01bits-obama-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01bits-obama/01bits-obama-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 89, 'width': 89, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney and Obama Campaigns Leaking Web Site Visitor Data', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T16:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natasha Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natasha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/893c0030-64f4-5d8c-8b3c-7dd5b9d90302', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/893c0030-64f4-5d8c-8b3c-7dd5b9d90302'}, {'abstract': 'During the primaries Mr. Romney said the states should handle disaster relief. Post Sandy, he’s not so down on the federal government.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/romney-on-fema-then-and-now/', 'snippet': 'During the primaries Mr. Romney said the states should handle disaster relief. Post Sandy, he’s not so down on the federal government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a Republican primary debate in June of 2011, CNN’s John King asked Mitt Romney for his views on disaster relief. “FEMA is about to run out of money, and there are some people who say, ‘Do it on a case-by-case basis.’ And there are some people who say, ‘You know what, maybe we’re learning a lesson here that the states should take on more of this role.’ How do you deal with something like that?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney on FEMA, Then and Now', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Emergency Management Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T16:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c66c83c-c51a-5e06-bc1a-e1e347179a0c', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c66c83c-c51a-5e06-bc1a-e1e347179a0c'}, {'abstract': 'Justin Patterson and Anna Burke are perfecting the art of hosting foolproof vegan/carnivore dinner parties.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/balancing-act/', 'snippet': 'Justin Patterson and Anna Burke are perfecting the art of hosting foolproof vegan/carnivore dinner parties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lately it seems that everybody is either a gluten-free vegan or a fanatical connoisseur of meat. What’s a host to do? For a start, take a lesson from Justin Patterson and Anna Burke. By day Burke is a designer at Kemble Interiors and Patterson runs an investment partnership. By night they are perfecting the art of hosting the foolproof vegan/carnivore dinner party for their picky-eater friends and family at their house on the Hudson River in Palisades, N.Y. Patterson is intimately acquainted with both herbivorous eating and excellent meat: he grew up in Virginia in a family of vegetarians — who happen to run a heritage grass-fed-cattle farm. These days, Patterson, who started eating meat at the age of 21, enjoys the yield of the family business (though he avoids gluten). He and Burke, who eats everything and loves to cook, are avid entertainers. They’re passionate about high-quality ingredients (just listen to them wax rhapsodic about Le Saunier de Camargue Fleur de Sel or the merits of cooking with high-smoke-point fats, like ghee or macadamia nut oil) and meticulous about style and presentation. And rather than balk at preparing a menu that has to do double duty, they’ve figured out the formula for making it a breeze. See the interactive slide show >>', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '54', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Balancing Act', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Balancing Act', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T16:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Felsenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Felsenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa099a32-be77-52c2-93fb-94ad6e71d2dc', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa099a32-be77-52c2-93fb-94ad6e71d2dc'}, {'abstract': 'A Pakistani terrorist organization offers relief aid to the U.S. government after Hurricane Sandy — its latest attempt to improve its image through public service.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/the-charitable-face-of-pakistani-militants/', 'snippet': 'A Pakistani terrorist organization offers relief aid to the U.S. government after Hurricane Sandy — its latest attempt to improve its image through public service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — New York officials received an offer from an unlikely source to help deal with the damage caused by Hurricane Sandy: Hafiz Saeed, the founder of an outlawed Pakistan-based militant group with a $10 million bounty on his head. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Charitable Face of Pakistani Militants', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saeed, Hafiz Muhammad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jamaat-ud-Dawa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T16:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Huma Yusuf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Huma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yusuf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9759b5f-52b0-522e-9a42-910c4355266e', 'word_count': 689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9759b5f-52b0-522e-9a42-910c4355266e'}, {'abstract': 'Paula Wagner, who went from actress to agent to Hollywood studio chief, has come to Broadway as a producer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/theater/paula-wagner-turns-to-producing-on-broadway.html', 'snippet': 'Paula Wagner, who went from actress to agent to Hollywood studio chief, has come to Broadway as a producer.', 'lead_paragraph': '“PAUL!” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04WAGNER1_SPAN/04JPWAGNER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04WAGNER1_SPAN/04JPWAGNER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04WAGNER1_SPAN/04JPWAGNER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04WAGNER1_SPAN/04JPWAGNER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1463, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04WAGNER1_SPAN/04JPWAGNER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04WAGNER1_SPAN/04JPWAGNER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04WAGNER1_SPAN/04JPWAGNER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width'