ding to an announcement made today by Antoni Cimolino, the festival’s new artistic director. Mr. Cimolino, who has been the general director of what is now called the Stratford Festival since 2006, officially took the reins today from Des McAnuff, who recently completed his final season as artistic director.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/arts/01artsbeat-cimolino/01artsbeat-cimolino-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/arts/01artsbeat-cimolino/01artsbeat-cimolino-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/arts/01artsbeat-cimolino/01artsbeat-cimolino-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/01/arts/01artsbeat-cimolino/01artsbeat-cimolino-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/arts/01artsbeat-cimolino/01artsbeat-cimolino-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stratford Festival Drops ‘Shakespeare’ From Name', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stratford Festival Drops ‘Shakespeare’ From Name', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stratford Shakespeare Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cimolino, Antoni', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T17:25:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b194795-5415-546e-b3d4-172ccc2f1289', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b194795-5415-546e-b3d4-172ccc2f1289'}, {'abstract': 'Microsoft’s focus on forming patterns and predictions with computers could make machine learning a core part of all its businesses. The grand plan involves not just selling software, but data, algorithms, even answers to questions.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/microsofts-plan-to-sell-answers/', 'snippet': 'Microsoft’s focus on forming patterns and predictions with computers could make machine learning a core part of all its businesses. The grand plan involves not just selling software, but data, algorithms, even answers to questions.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Microsoft may be looking at its ventures into machine learning as providing more than just better features for products. They may be a way to transform itself, and many other companies too.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01bits-mundie/01bits-mundie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01bits-mundie/01bits-mundie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01bits-mundie/01bits-mundie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01bits-mundie/01bits-mundie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01bits-mundie/01bits-mundie-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Microsoft’s Plan to Sell Answers', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T17:31:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/534ee847-88e1-5da8-9230-e160d0150141', 'word_count': 688, 'uri': 'nyt://article/534ee847-88e1-5da8-9230-e160d0150141'}, {'abstract': 'Home to dozens of casinos, Macau can overwhelm the senses. But the former Portuguese colony also has a quieter side that’s defined by lush landscapes, art galleries and design shops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/travel/36-hours-in-macau.html', 'snippet': 'Home to dozens of casinos, Macau can overwhelm the senses. But the former Portuguese colony also has a quieter side that’s defined by lush landscapes, art galleries and design shops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LIKE an unabashed exhibitionist, Macau can’t help itself. This former Portuguese colony perpetually flaunts its frenetic side. Bungee jumpers diving from the 61st floor of a gleaming tower. Surfers hanging 10 in a rooftop wave pool. Dragons materializing in surreal fog during dazzling multimedia shows. And let’s not forget the gambling and gaming that saturates Macau’s 35 casinos, including the Sands Cotai Central, a resort complex that opened earlier this year. But don’t let the sensory overload eclipse a more serene, sophisticated side that’s defined by lush landscapes, art galleries, avant-garde design shops and low-key bars.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04HOURS3/04HOURS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04HOURS3/04HOURS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04HOURS3/04HOURS3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 816, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04HOURS3/04HOURS3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1632, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04HOURS3/04HOURS3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04HOURS3/04HOURS3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04HOURS3/04HOURS3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}],