s some American collectors wary of the political future decide to sell, fearing that capital gains taxes could rise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TWENTY-FIVE years ago, just three weeks after Black Monday — the worst one-day plunge in stock market history — Sotheby’s sale of Impressionist and modern art topped $100 million for the first time, a 45 percent increase from six months before. During times of financial uncertainty collectors with cash have parted with untold millions of dollars, putting their liquid assets into Picassos and Giacomettis, Rothkos and Warhols.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/design/20121104-AUCTIONS-slide-4L83/20121104-AUCTIONS-slide-4L83-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 596, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/design/20121104-AUCTIONS-slide-4L83/20121104-AUCTIONS-slide-4L83-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1191, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/design/20121104-AUCTIONS-slide-4L83/20121104-AUCTIONS-slide-4L83-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/design/20121104-AUCTIONS-slide-4L83/20121104-AUCTIONS-slide-4L83-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/design/20121104-AUCTIONS-slide-4L83/20121104-AUCTIONS-slide-4L83-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headl