n says in an e-mail.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/netflix-says-it-is-open-to-icahns-perspective/', 'snippet': '“We have many shareholders, now including Mr. Icahn, and we’re always open to their perspective on how to build on our success,” a Netflix spokesman says in an e-mail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Netflix isn’t giving Carl C. Icahn the cold shoulder — at least not yet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Netflix Says It Is Open to Icahn’s ‘Perspective’', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T17:59:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2adae3b5-6287-5a87-a757-e987f9a95d9e', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2adae3b5-6287-5a87-a757-e987f9a95d9e'}, {'abstract': 'Five women from the North American Quilling Guild reimagined our “T” as a magical field bursting with sunflowers and dandelions.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/second-nature/', 'snippet': 'Five women from the North American Quilling Guild reimagined our “T” as a magical field bursting with sunflowers and dandelions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Quilling is the art of rolling and pinching thin strips of paper into multidimensional designs. It’s something Sherry Rodehaver has been doing since 1971, and for “Second Nature,” she, along with four women from the North American Quilling Guild, reimagined our “T” as a magical field bursting with sunflowers and dandelions. “I never want anybody to walk away from my work without having that wow factor,” said Rodehaver, who recently presented her quilled animals at the Yankee Peddler Festival in Ohio. Hardly a paper pet was left unsold. ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '65', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Second Nature', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'T', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T18:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b164633-d4f7-57a0-965b-79fd4367cbe0', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b164633-d4f7-57a0-965b-79fd4367cbe0'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to a recent review of Kurt Eichenwald’s “500 Days: Secrets and Lies in the Terror Wars.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/books/review/500-days.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to a recent review of Kurt Eichenwald’s “500 Days: Secrets and Lies in the Terror Wars.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘500 Days’', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘500 Days’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T18:01:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/2adc800b-6d66-5317-a4e4-3ad