ue': 'Kimmel, Jimmy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Letterman, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T18:15:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3d55139-19ab-5a72-b5a5-65946787a0b6', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3d55139-19ab-5a72-b5a5-65946787a0b6'}, {'abstract': 'The play, which was scheduled to open Thursday night, will be performed as a reading by flashlight as a pay-what-you-can benefit.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/living-theaters-homesick-to-open-with-storm-benefit/', 'snippet': 'The play, which was scheduled to open Thursday night, will be performed as a reading by flashlight as a pay-what-you-can benefit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Theaters across the city are rolling up their sleeves to deal with the wake of Hurricane Sandy. At the Living Theater at 21 Clinton Street, the return engagement of the production of “Home/sick” will be performed as a reading by flashlight on Thursday night at 8 p.m. The show’s $18 tickets are pay-what-you-can, with proceeds to benefit hurricane relief.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Living Theater’s ‘Home/sick’ to Open With Storm Benefit', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Outages and Blackouts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Living Theater', 'rank':