 '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ffd66ac-c2b2-5bed-adf3-2282b3f378a7', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ffd66ac-c2b2-5bed-adf3-2282b3f378a7'}, {'abstract': 'A proposal to protect a vital ocean ecosystem in the Ross Sea and East Antarctic fails to win adoption.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/group-adjourns-without-acting-on-antarctic-reserve/', 'snippet': 'A proposal to protect a vital ocean ecosystem in the Ross Sea and East Antarctic fails to win adoption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Frustrating advocates, an international commission charged with overseeing the Southern Ocean took no action Thursday on a proposal championed by the United States and New Zealand to create the world’s largest marine reserve in the seas around Antarctica.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Group Adjourns Without Acting on Antarctic Reserve', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commission for the Conservation of Antarctic Marine Living Resources', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T18:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a387b64-d55d-5d1a-bd16-190c8ef51427', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a387b64-d55d-5d1a-bd16-190c8ef51427'}, {'abstract': 'Muddling through a 10-day stretch without electricity and Internet (not to mention heat or hot water). Sometimes, the technologies that a tech columnist and his family crave most are 100 years old.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/how-to-keep-electronics-going-with-no-power/', 'snippet': 'Muddling through a 10-day stretch without electricity and Internet (not to mention heat or hot water). Sometimes, the technologies that a tech columnist and his family crave most are 100 years old.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Hurricane Sandy storm damage here in my Connecticut town was fairly extensive — beautiful old trees are down everywhere, 85 percent of our homes are without power, and officials are saying it will take at least 10 days to restore electricity — but at least our homes are standing. I’ve seen the photos of New York and New Jersey; in our way, we were lucky.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01pogue-npowerpeg/01pogue-npowerpeg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 291, 'width': 411, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01pogue-npowerpeg/01pogue-npowerpeg-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 291, 'width': 411, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01pogue-npowerpeg/01pogue-npowerpeg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01pogue-npowerpeg/01pogue-npowerpeg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01pogue-npowerpeg/01pogue-npowerpeg-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Keep Electronics Going With No Power', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Outages and Blackouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T18:42:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6f3b701-c58a-583d-85a6-e2b32074e53a', 'word_count': 1010, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6f3b701-c58a-583d-85a6-e2b32074e53a'}, {'abstract': 'At a concert in Hartford attended by the United States attorney for Manhattan last week, Bruce Springsteen shouted, “This is for Preet Bharara!” before ripping into “Death to My Hometown,” a rollicking Celtic-inspired anthem.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/the-bruce-bharara-bromance/', 'snippet': 'At a concert in Hartford attended by the United States attorney for Manhattan last week, Bruce Springsteen shouted, “This is for Preet Bharara!” before ripping into “Death to My Hometown,” a rollicking Celtic-inspired anthem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Preet Bharara, the United States attorney in Manhattan, had already had a pretty good week as he and his family traveled to Hartford last Thursday for a Bruce Springsteen show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bruce-Bharara Bromance', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bharara, Preet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Springsteen, Bruce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T18:44:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/307dabf5-82f8-5f00-9d22-29a24c46340d', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/307dabf5-82f8-5f00-9d22-29a24c46340d'}, {'abstract': 'The New York City Marathon doesn’t offer any one challenge that matches Boston’s Heartbreak Hill, but that doesn’t mean that aren’t inclines to conquer.', 'web_url': 'https://marathon.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/quirks-of-the-race-where-the-going-gets-toughest/', 'snippet': 'The New York City Marathon doesn’t offer any one challenge that matches Boston’s Heartbreak Hill, but that doesn’t mean that aren’t inclines to conquer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No one ever said running a marathon is easy. That’s kind of the whole point. But not all marathons are created equal either. Chicago’s is famously flat all the way through. Boston’s is largely downhill (tough on the quads) except for one spurt that features the notorious Heartbreak Hill around the 20-mile mark. San Francisco’s starts and ends easy but most of the race is as hilly as, well, as the streets of San Francisco. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quirks of the Race: Where the Going Gets Toughest', 'kicker': 'On the Run', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York City Marathon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T18:46:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10d43bd5-b494-5df5-93fc-6614ecdc9e30', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10d43bd5-b494-5df5-93fc-6614ecdc9e30'}, {'abstract': 'Daniel Delaney is poised to open BrisketTown, a restaurant for Texas beef barbecue in Williamsburg, Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/nyregion/daniel-delaney-to-bring-texas-barbecue-to-williamsburg.html', 'snippet': 'Daniel Delaney is poised to open BrisketTown, a restaurant for Texas beef barbecue in Williamsburg, Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': '“BARBECUE,” Daniel Delaney said, opening a smoker filled with briskets, some wrapped in shiny brown paper, others sporting thick black crusts, “is about mastering the art of being reactive.” He targeted the slab closest to him, working two fingers inside the wrapping and holding them there, as if taking a pulse. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02STAGE/02STAGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02STAGE/02STAGE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1360, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy':