endlessly nuanced painted surfaces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Koichi Yanagi Oriental Fine Arts', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shiro Tsujimura', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shiro Tsujimura', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T21:08:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5c3ad3d-61e8-50b3-983e-3da3b1f6a1b2', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5c3ad3d-61e8-50b3-983e-3da3b1f6a1b2'}, {'abstract': 'The concerts will take place on Saturday at 8 p.m. at the State Theater in New Brunswick and on Sunday at 3 p.m. at the New Jersey Performing Arts Center in Newark.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/new-jersey-symphony-orchestra-to-provide-free-tickets/', 'snippet': 'The concerts will take place on Saturday at 8 p.m. at the State Theater in New Brunswick and on Sunday at 3 p.m. at the New Jersey Performing Arts Center in Newark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New Jersey Symphony Orchestra, based in one of the states most devastated by Hurricane Sandy, said it would provide free tickets to performances of an all-Mozart program this weekend. The concerts will take place on Saturday at 8 p.m. at the State Theater in New Brunswick and on Sunday at 3 p.m. at the New Jersey Performing Arts Center in Newark. Tickets will be available on a first-come, first-serve basis two hours before the performances. The orchestra said it wanted to help those “who need to escape from life’s current challenges.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Jersey Symphony Orchestra to Provide Free Tickets', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Jersey Orchestra To Provide Free Tickets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T21:08:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4fc906f-3a8c-5f7b-a002-8c6862a5cb7a', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4fc906f-3a8c-5f7b-a002-8c6862a5cb7a'}, {'abstract': 'Anything Richard Prince or John Baldessari or Ed Ruscha can do, Eric Doeringer can do too, as he demonstrates in a show at Mulherin & Pollard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/arts/design/eric-doeringer-the-rematerialization-of-the-art-object.html', 'snippet': 'Anything Richard Prince or John Baldessari or Ed Ruscha can do, Eric Doeringer can do too, as he demonstrates in a show at Mulherin & Pollard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mulherin & Pollard', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eric Doeringer: ‘The Rematerialization of the Art Object’', 'kicker': 'Art In Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eric Doeringer: ‘The Rematerialization of the Art Object’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doeringer, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T21:09:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_des