umbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02RDP_VAMPS_SPAN/02RDP_VAMPS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02RDP_VAMPS_SPAN/02RDP_VAMPS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02RDP_VAMPS_SPAN/02RDP_VAMPS_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vampire Girls Just Want to Have Dates', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vamps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vampires', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heckerling, Amy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silverstone, Alicia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ritter, Krysten', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Vamps (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T21:21:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/beddbcd0-9977-54b4-b23f-f550de0e7535', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/beddbcd0-9977-54b4-b23f-f550de0e7535'}, {'abstract': '“The Twelve,” the second installment in Justin Cronin’s vampire trilogy, moves from the wreckage left by the first book, “The Passage,” to a battle cry for the third installment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/books/the-twelve-by-justin-cronin.html', 'snippet': '“The Twelve,” the second installment in Justin Cronin’s vampire trilogy, moves from the wreckage left by the first book, “The Passage,” to a battle cry for the third installment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a best-selling book that spanned a thousand years, demolished human civilization, unleashed marauding, virus-infected vampires on much of America and turned a sweet little girl named Amy into an unlikely superhero, Justin Cronin’s “Passage” made a remarkably weak impression. It had insufferable pretensions. It was both overwritten and overrated. It sprawled all over the post-apocalyptic map as a horror story, western, father-daughter tear-jerker and paramilitary action-adventure. And its timing was terrible. When “The Passage” arrived in 2010, the market for splashy vampire tales was already drenched in blood. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BOOK/BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BOOK/BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1800, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BOOK/02BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BOOK/02BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BOOK/02BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 149, 'width'