 have been making progress. Here’s what they have to report.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/carriers-hurricane-sandy/', 'snippet': 'Three days into the aftermath of Sandy, wireless service is still lacking in parts of New York City and other hard-hit zones. The carriers have been struggling to keep their services running, mostly because of the loss of power. But they say they ...', 'lead_paragraph': '6:12 p.m. | Updated  Adding the latest statement from Sprint. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01bits-sandyphone/01bits-sandyphone-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01bits-sandyphone/01bits-sandyphone-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1428, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01bits-sandyphone/01bits-sandyphone-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01bits-sandyphone/01bits-sandyphone-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/technology/01bits-sandyphone/01bits-sandyphone-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Cellphone Carriers Say About Hurricane Recovery', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sprint Nextel Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T-Mobile', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T22:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5941242e-b577-5745-a426-015ca6724b1d', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5941242e-b577-5745-a426-015ca6724b1d'}, {'abstract': 'Judith Berkson uses her classical and Jewish musical heritage to inform “The Vienna Rite,” which focuses on Salomon Sulzer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/arts/music/judith-berksons-new-opera-the-vienna-rite.html', 'snippet': 'Judith Berkson uses her classical and Jewish musical heritage to inform “The Vienna Rite,” which focuses on Salomon Sulzer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More by accident than by design, Judith Berkson has followed a circuitous and genre-hopping musical path. Her introduction to the art form was through her father, a cantor in a conservative synagogue in Chicago who taught her Jewish sacred music. As a high school student, she got interested in opera and art song, and she earned a degree in voice from the New England Conservatory, in Boston, where she also studied composition and piano.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BERKSON_SPAN/02BERKSON_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BERKSON_SPAN/02BERKSON_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BERKSON_SPAN/BERKSON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BERKSON_SPAN/BERKSON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1601, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BERKSON_SPAN/02BERKSON_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BERKSON_SPAN/02BERKSON_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BERKSON_SPAN/02BERKSON_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mash-Up of Schubert and Synagogue Tradition', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mash-Up of Schubert and Synagogue Tradition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T22:01:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d7d9d2f-2a29-5aaa-93a8-5bed608ff2fd', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d7d9d2f-2a29-5aaa-93a8-5bed608ff2fd'}, {'abstract': 'How can we better protect New York City from flooding?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/roomfordebate/2012/11/01/should-new-york-build-sea-gates/', 'snippet': 'How can we better protect New York City from flooding?', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should New York Build Sea Gates?', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T22:03:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b26392e-859f-58e6-a157-48297edf06fc', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b26392e-859f-58e6-a157-48297edf06fc'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Man With the Iron Fists,” the hip-hop artist RZA of the Wu-Tang Clan has assembled a homage to the martial arts genre known as wuxia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/movies/the-man-with-the-iron-fists-directed-by-and-starring-rza.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Man With the Iron Fists,” the hip-hop artist RZA of the Wu-Tang Clan has assembled a homage to the martial arts genre known as wuxia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As erratically enjoyable as it is consistently ridiculous, the martial arts pastiche “The Man With the Iron Fists” is the latest evidence that the vogue for neo-exploitation cinema shows no sign of flagging. Directed by the hip-hop impresario turned would-be auteur RZA (a k a Robert Diggs), of the group Wu-Tang Clan, “Iron Fists” is a sweetly sincere, lightly cheeky gloss on the film genre wuxia (“martial chivalry”) and those entertainments known for their flying swordsmen (and women), crouching tigers, hidden dragons and often fabulous hair, gowns and wirework. This is a movie as drenched in genre love as it is in the arterial spray from its hordes of sliced and diced characters.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02MANFISTS2_SPAN/02MANFISTS2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02MANFISTS2_SPAN/02MANFISTS2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02MANFISTS2_SPAN/MANFISTS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02MANFISTS2_SPAN/MANFISTS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02MANFISTS2_SPAN/02MANFISTS2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02MANFISTS2_SPAN/02MANFISTS2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02MANFISTS2_SPAN/02MANFISTS2_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Swordsman’s Arms Dealer of Choice (Wires Not Included)', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Swordsman’s Arms Dealer of Choice (Wires Not Included)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'RZA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Man with the Iron Fists (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crowe, Russell', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu, Lucy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T22:06:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1626748-108a-536a-8171-8128f68588bd', 'word_count': 658, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1626748-108a-536a-8171-8128f68588bd'}, {'abstract': 'In each of the last three school years, the number of education jobs in state and local government has declined. The October employment report out Friday will show whether that trend has finally ended.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/01/are-there-finally-more-teachers/', 'snippet': 'In each of the last three school years, the number of education jobs in state and local government has declined. The October employment report out Friday will show whether that trend has finally ended.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The October job numbers out Friday will show whether the erosion of teaching jobs in public schools has ended. It will reflect the month when all teachers who are going to work in the fall semester have jobs, and allow comparisons of the non-seasonally adjusted figures for state and local government education jobs from one October to the next, showing what school districts did around the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are There (Finally) More Teachers?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T22:09:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44bbddca-b28e-5c1e-80f2-21235a579afb', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44bbddca-b28e-5c1e-80f2-21235a579afb'}, {'abstract': 'The editor fueled a scandal when he charged that Greece was governed by a small group of business elites who were above paying taxes while the rest of the population suffered deep cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/world/europe/greek-editor-not-guilty-in-publishing-names-with-swiss-accounts.html', 'snippet': 'The editor fueled a scandal when he charged that Greece was governed by a small group of business elites who were above paying taxes while the rest of the population suffered deep cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — The owner and editor of a respected investigative magazine was acquitted Thursday on charges of breaching privacy laws in publishing the names of more than 2,000 Greeks believed to be holding accounts at a bank in Switzerland. The case tested news media freedom in Greece and fueled a scandal over whether officials here failed to aggressively pursue people suspected of evading taxes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/world/greece/greece-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/02/world/greece/greece-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/world/greece/greece-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/world/greece/greece-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1639, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/world/greece/greece-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/02/world/greece/greece-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/world/greece/greece-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Greek Editor Not Guilty in Publishing Names With Swiss Accounts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greek Editor Acquitted In Listing Swiss Accounts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Athens (Greece)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject',