 handwriting not all that different from the one she used in 1893, when she wrote a letter to a 5-year-old acquaintance about four little rabbits named Flopsy, Mopsy, Cottontail and Peter. But in this 1940 document about the origins of Peter Rabbit — shown in a suggestive, engrossing new exhibition at the Morgan Library & Museum, “Beatrix Potter: The Picture Letters”  — she admits to being puzzled: “I never quite understood the secret of Peter’s perennial charm.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BEATRIX_SPAN/02BEATRIX_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BEATRIX_SPAN/02BEATRIX_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BEATRIX_SPAN/02BEATRIX1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 560, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BEATRIX_SPAN/02BEATRIX1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1120, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BEATRIX_SPAN/02BEATRIX_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BEATRIX_SPAN/02BEATRIX_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BEATRIX_SPAN/02BEATRIX_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'heigh