pet': '“The Bay” is a collage of escalating grossness, as innocent, water-based fun turns into a grisly epidemic fueled by ecological malfeasance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A case can be made that the craze for found-footage horror movies — see “Paranormal Activity,” Volumes 1-4 — began in Maryland. The real town of Burkittsville, in the western part of the state, was the setting of “The Blair Witch Project” back in 1999. “The Bay,” which takes place in a fictional Chesapeake Bay hamlet called Claridge, is something of a homecoming. It also represents an earnest if not entirely persuasive attempt to tease out some of the latent allegorical meanings of the genre, and to use fright to raise questions about the state of the environment.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BAY_SPAN/02BAY_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BAY_SPAN/02BAY_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BAY_SPAN/02BAY_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BAY_SPAN/02BAY_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BAY_SPAN/02BAY_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BAY_SPAN/02BAY_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/02BAY_SPAN/02BAY_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'There’s Something Bubbling Off the Shore of a Chesapeake Hamlet', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'There’s Something Bubbling Off the Shore of a Chesapeake Hamlet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levinson, Barry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Bay (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-01T22:24:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e600a9b7-a0f1-57ac-aa85-fe2b12ef566c', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e600a9b7-a0f1-57ac-aa85-fe2b12ef566c'}, {'abstract': 'A Winslow Homer exhibition and studio prove that Prouts Neck, Me., had more dimensions than those depicted in his paintings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/arts/design/winslow-homers-comfortably-rugged-maine.html', 'snippet': 'A Winslow Homer exhibition and studio prove that Prouts Neck, Me., had more dimensions than those depicted in his paintings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PROUTS NECK, Me. — There he is, the old man and the sea, out on his lonesome, storm-battered spit of land, paintbrush in hand, canvas rattling on its easel, and looking out to the vastness of the Atlantic Ocean, which crashes and explodes onto nearby craggy rocks. This was the Winslow Homer (1836-1910) of my imagination, where he lived like a hermit, braved the elements and made the best paintings of his career, those luxuriantly sensuous, unpeopled pictures of rocks, waves, ocean and sky.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/design/02MAINE_SPAN/02MAINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/design/02MAINE_SPAN/02MAINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/design/02MAINE_SPAN/02MAINE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/design/02MAINE_SPAN/02MAINE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1298, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/design/02MAINE_SPAN/02MAINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/design/02MAINE_SPAN/02MAINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/design/02MAINE_SPAN/02MAINE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Comfortable Maine, Ruggedly Depicted', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_he