ke Woodson spent a significant portion of practice impersonating LeBron James, who will lead the Heat into Madison Square Garden for the Knicks’ season opener Friday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The person with the basketball for a significant part of the Knicks’ practice Thursday was not a player. Instead, it was Coach Mike Woodson, who was dribbling, pointing and explaining to his team what the best player in the N.B.A. could, and most likely would, do against them with the ball in his hands Friday night.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woodson Keeps Focus on Defending James', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Woodson Keeps Focus On Defending James', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodson, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T00:19:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82dc4246-8e5f-5ee5-9910-6fffdb47d8f6', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82dc4246-8e5f-5ee5-9910-6fffdb47d8f6'}, {'abstract': 'Sony, Sharp and Panasonic have all reported significant losses, their boom years ended by global crisis and their own poor decisions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/business/global/sony-sharp-and-panasonic-report-significant-l