tml', 'snippet': 'The aftermath of Hurricane Sandy and the New York City Marathon were brought together under the Javits Convention Center’s roof, as the event’s exposition opened.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Upstairs at the Jacob K. Javits Convention Center on Thursday, exhibitors commanded rows of booths showcasing things like brightly colored compression socks, dry-fit shirts, green cups of Gatorade samples and nutrition bars made with chia seeds — items that apparently appeal to people who are three days away from running a marathon.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/sports/RUNNERS1/RUNNERS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/sports/RUNNERS1/RUNNERS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Storm Recovery, Marathon Expo Opens Doors to Runners', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid Storm Recovery, Marathon Expo Opens Doors to Runners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York City Marathon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marathon Running', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Road Runners Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conventions, Fairs and Trade Shows', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T01:37:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Pilon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pilon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cd2ae1d-a50e-52f3-b2f5-7c59e792abd4', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cd2ae1d-a50e-52f3-b2f5-7c59e792abd4'}, {'abstract': 'Elzbieta Plackowska is charged with the murders of Olivia Dworakowski, a 5-year-old girl she was baby-sitting, and her own son, Justin Plackowska, 7.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/us/nanny-in-illinois-held-in-2-killings.html', 'snippet': 'Elzbieta Plackowska is charged with the murders of Olivia Dworakowski, a 5-year-old girl she was baby-sitting, and her own son, Justin Plackowska, 7.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the killings proved anything, it was that a parent’s worst nightmare — the slaying of small children by a person entrusted with their care — could play out anywhere, in uptown Manhattan or the streets of an affluent Chicago suburb.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/us/STABBING/STABBING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 441, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/us/STABBING/STABBING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 441, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nanny in Illinois Held in 2 Killings', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nanny in Illinois Held in Killing Of Her Son and a Young Charge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T01:45:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Goode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91c855b9-f80f-5b17-82b7-fb340b674ef0', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91c855b9-f80f-5b17-82b7-fb340b674ef0'}, {'abstract': 'Matt Romney, one of Mitt Romney’s sons, went to Moscow seeking investors for his real estate firm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/us/politics/matt-romney-goes-to-russia-for-business.html', 'snippet': 'Matt Romney, one of Mitt Romney’s sons, went to Moscow seeking investors for his real estate firm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Matt Romney, a son of the Republican presidential nominee, traveled to Moscow this week seeking Russian investors for his California-based real estate firm just days before his father is to wrap up a campaign in which he has vowed to take a tougher stance with the Kremlin.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Romney Travels to Russia, but on Strictly Friendly Terms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Romney Travels to Russia, but on Strictly Friendly Terms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Matt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T01:47:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'sectio