etts, said he would introduce a bill on Friday requiring that compounding pharmacies that produce on a large scale be regulated by the Food and Drug Administration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/us/bill-would-target-compounding-pharmacies.html', 'snippet': 'Representative Edward J. Markey, Democrat of Massachusetts, said he would introduce a bill on Friday requiring that compounding pharmacies that produce on a large scale be regulated by the Food and Drug Administration.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Representative Edward J. Markey, Democrat of Massachusetts, said he would introduce a bill on Friday requiring that compounding pharmacies that produce on a large scale be regulated by the Food and Drug Administration as drug manufacturers and that compounded drugs be labeled as such. The move comes after a deadly meningitis outbreak was traced to a contaminated injectable steroid made by the New England Compounding Center in Framingham, Mass. The F.D.A. said Thursday that it had identified several types of fungus that were contained in two other drug products made by the company. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Would Target Compounding Pharmacies', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bill Would Target Compounding Pharmacies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Compounding Center', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meningitis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steroids', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Markey, Edward J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T02:38:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8bc87fd-999a-58f5-89b4-887720906df7', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8bc87fd-999a-58f5-89b4-887720906df7'}, {'abstract': 'Judy L. Bonner became the first woman president of the University of Alabama on Thursday, a day after the previous president stepped down after less than two months on the job.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/education/alabama-university-gets-second-leader-in-2-months.html', 'snippet': 'Judy L. Bonner became the first woman president of the University of Alabama on Thursday, a day after the previous president stepped down after less than two months on the job.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Judy L. Bonner became the first woman president of the University of Alabama on Thursday, a day after the previous president stepped down after less than two months on the job. Trustees named Dr. Bonner, a longtime professor and administrator at the university, effective immediately. The university had named Guy H. Bailey as president in July, and he took office in early September, but he resigned Wednesday, citing his wife’s illness. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alabama: University Gets Second Leader in 2 Months', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alabama: University Gets Second Leader In 2 Months', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bonner, Judy L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3,