s 17 Years in Terrorist Plot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferdaus, Rezwan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T04:56:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a0ffd81-c126-54b1-bbce-0c1227f8b92f', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a0ffd81-c126-54b1-bbce-0c1227f8b92f'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:20 P.M. (Cinemax) THIS MEANS WAR (2012) Two C.I.A. officers, Tuck (Tom Hardy) and F D R (Chris Pine), find their friendship — and their mission to prevent an international criminal (Til Schweiger) from obtaining a weapon of mass destruction — disrupted by Lauren (Reese Witherspoon, above, with Mr. Pine, left, and Mr. Hardy), a product-testing executive they’re both dating. This romantic comedy was directed by McG from a script by Timothy Dowling and Simon Kinberg. “The clever hook in ‘Mr. and Mrs. Smith,’ which Mr. Kinberg also wrote, is that its mister and missus are covert assassins (neither knows what the other does), whose marriage blahs vanish once they turn their gun sights on each other,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. And while the filmmakers try a variation on that theme here, Lauren is a “weak sister” to Angelina Jolie’s Mrs. Smith. “It doesn’t help that the men’s rivalry soon escalates into spy versus spy shenanigans,” Ms. Dargis added. “And while it’s initially amusing to see them snoop on Lauren, by the time each has planted surveillance bugs in her house, you’re watching a cuddly stalker flick.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T05:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/69353e98-d735-51e1-b0bf-ac6cc7623a8c', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69353e98-d735-51e1-b0bf-ac6cc7623a8c'}, {'abstract': 'Waterfront property values in the New York area are unlikely to suffer in the long term, but new regulations — and buyers’ expectations — could affect how it is built and sold.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/realestate/after-hurricane-sandy-would-you-buy-on-the-waterfront.html', 'snippet': 'Waterfront property values in the New York area are unlikely to suffer in the long term, but new regulations — and buyers’ expectations — could affect how it is built and sold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF tropical storm Irene last year was an eye-opener, Hurricane Sandy was a reality check.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image