N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T11:49:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron and Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b82b75f-73ce-5efe-bc07-b85897b09274', 'word_count': 1136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b82b75f-73ce-5efe-bc07-b85897b09274'}, {'abstract': 'The storm cancels SAT tests in several states, Westin hotels lend gear so travelers can exercise, how to keep electronics going with no power and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/friday-reading-no-sat-in-several-states-due-to-storm/', 'snippet': 'The storm cancels SAT tests in several states, Westin hotels lend gear so travelers can exercise, how to keep electronics going with no power and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Reading: No SAT Test in Several States Because of Storm', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T11:58:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8459a067-4661-59b1-802e-f58faf9d6e7b', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8459a067-4661-59b1-802e-f58faf9d6e7b'}, {'abstract': 'Jon Meacham’s biography of Thomas Jefferson looks at how the founding father balanced his ideals with pragmatism while also bending others to his will.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/books/review/thomas-jefferson-the-art-of-power-by-jon-meacham.html', 'snippet': 'Jon Meacham’s biography of Thomas Jefferson looks at how the founding father balanced his ideals with pragmatism while also bending others to his will.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The political biographies most popular in the modern era often tell us less about their subjects than about the moment in which the books themselves are published. John F. Kennedy’s “Profiles in Courage” won the Pulitzer Prize in 1957. But few remember its portraits of Senate lions like Thomas Hart Benton and George Norris. What lingers is its status as a kind of campaign document that set the table for Kennedy’s own rise from the Senate to the presidency. Similarly, “The Age of Jackson,” Arthur M. Schlesinger Jr.’s vivid book, published in 1945, the year Franklin D. Roose\xadvelt died, recast the populist Andrew Jackson as the bold progenitor of the New Deal — and also won a Pulitzer. Schlesinger’s multivolume history of the New Deal was called “The Age of Roose\xadvelt” — tightening the link between the two projects and the two presidents.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/books/review/1111-Abramson/1111-Abramson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 508, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/books/review/1111-Abramson/1111-Abramson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1016, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/books/review/1111-Abramson/1111-Abramson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/11/books/review/1111-Abramson/1111-Abramson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/books/review/1111-Abramson/1111-Abramson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Grand Bargainer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grand Bargainer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meacham, Jon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jefferson, Thomas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T12:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jill Abramson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abramson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9634fdb-a1fb-581e-89b2-56e65b29008a', 'word_count': 2786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9634fdb-a1fb-581e-89b2-56e65b29008a'}, {'abstract': 'On the constant threat from Pakistan, and why the Armed Forces Special Powers Act should not be repealed.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/a-conversation-with-lt-gen-baljit-singh-jaswal-former-commander-of-kashmir/', 'snippet': 'On the constant threat from Pakistan, and why the Armed Forces Special Powers Act should not be repealed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After two decades of militancy, the Kashmir Valley has been relatively calm during the past two years. Tourists from India and around the world flooded into the scenic valley last summer, and the chief minister of Jammu and Kashmir, Omar Abdullah, has called for troop reductions and a repeal of the Armed Forces Special Powers Act.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With: Lt. Gen. Baljit Singh Jaswal, Former Commander of Kashmir', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T12:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Betwa Sharma', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Betwa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sharma', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/763cf969-4157-5b89-aaed-1708429b22e1', 'word_count': 1804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/763cf969-4157-5b89-aaed-1708429b22e1'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: A night bike ride in post-Hurricane Sandy New York was a surreal experience.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/the-spookiest-halloween/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A night bike r