'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0708ee85-ef64-51a5-a454-d03b7aa0824d', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0708ee85-ef64-51a5-a454-d03b7aa0824d'}, {'abstract': 'To suggest, as Mitt Romney does, that Spain’s current woes are due to government profligacy is to take the wrong lesson from its experience and risk making its problems worse.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/spain-an-unlikely-talking-point-in-the-u-s-presidential-campaign/', 'snippet': 'To suggest, as Mitt Romney does, that Spain’s current woes are due to government profligacy is to take the wrong lesson from its experience and risk making its problems worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — Never before has Spain been so central to an American presidential election, Spanish newspapers have been marveling. The country’s prominence in the U.S. campaign, the result of its protracted recession and soaring unemployment, is painfully unprecedented: Mitt Romney first mentioned Spain in the opening presidential debate, then last week it was President Barack Obama. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Misunderestimating Spain', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T12:08:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Blitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3047abe-f54b-5f8c-a04a-15aa3909aba2', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3047abe-f54b-5f8c-a04a-15aa3909aba2'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Todd Akin, abandoned by the Republican establishment after his controversial comments on rape months ago, is seeing an influx of more than $2 million in the final days of his campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/akin-finds-funding-in-final-days-of-senate-race/', 'snippet': 'Representative Todd Akin, abandoned by the Republican establishment after his controversial comments on rape months ago, is seeing an influx of more than $2 million in the final days of his campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANSAS CITY, Mo. – Representative Todd Akin, abandoned by the Republican establishment after his contentious comments on rape months ago, is receiving an influx of more than $2 million in the final days of his campaign against incumbent Senator Claire McCaskill of Missouri.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Akin Finds Funding in Final Days of Senate Race', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T12:22:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f993aed4-de50-5714-a69f-9acfab37e25b', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f993aed4-de50-5714-a69f-9acfab37e25b'}, {'abstract': 'With the holidays approaching, Warren E. Buffett has found a way to stock up on all the elf hats and reindeer paper plates anyone could ever need: by buying an 80-year-old retailer overflowing with them.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/berkshire-to-buy-oriental-trading-company/', 'snippet': 'With the holidays approaching, Warren E. Buffett has found a way to stock up on all the elf hats and reindeer paper plates anyone could ever need: by buying an 80-year-old retailer overflowing with them.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:10 p.m. | Updated ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Berkshire to Buy Oriental Trading Company', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Berkshire to Buy Retailer Of Arts and Crafts Wares', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buffett, Warren E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berkshire Hathaway Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oriental Trading Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T12:22:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbb7a31b-ab6f-5ece-990d-143d52c32a41', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbb7a31b-ab6f-5ece-990d-143d52c32a41'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Energy Regulatory Commission is becoming a thorn in the side of big banks, The Royal Bank of Scotland said it expected to face penalties related to the Libor investigation, and JPMorgan Chase and Citigroup are in the top “bucket” of institutions that are considered “systemically important.”', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/wall-streets-new-foe/', 'snippet': 'The Federal Energy Regulatory Commission is becoming a thorn in the side of big banks, The Royal Bank of Scotland said it expected to face penalties related to the Libor investigation, and JPMorgan Chase and Citigroup are in the top “bucket” of in...', 'lead_paragraph': ' WALL STREET’S NEW FOE \xa0|\xa0 A little-known agency, the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission, is becoming a thorn in the side of big banks. This week, the agency threatened to impose its largest-ever fine against Barclays, after previously turning up the heat on JPMorgan Chase and Deutsche Bank. “It’s the most powerful agency that no one knows about,” said Tyson Slocum, the director of the energy program for the nonprofit advocacy group Public Citizen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wall Street’s New Foe', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T12:26:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2888025-dd99-5d3f-959d-f5952eb609c6', 'word_count': 1622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2888025-dd99-5d3f-959d-f5952eb609c6'}, {'abstract': 'The Labor Department’s last pre-election figures showed 171,000 jobs added in October. Unemployment edged up to 7.9 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/business/economy/us-added-171000-jobs-in-october.html', 'snippet': 'The Labor Department’s last pre-election figures showed 171,000 jobs added in October. Unemployment edged up to 7.9 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American job market is looking a little stronger than had been feared just a few months ago, according to the government’s final labor snapshot before the presidential election. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/business/economy/03jobs/03jobs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/business/economy/03jobs/03jobs-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1421, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/business/economy/03jobs/03jobs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/03/business/economy/03jobs/03jobs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/business/economy/03jobs/03jobs-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Latest Jobs Report Shows Persistent Economic Growth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Adds 171,000 Jobs, More Than Estimated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Labor Statistics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T12:41:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/446cb2f9-c183-5c27-ab2e-83f0eb96d0d0', 'word_count': 1156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/446cb2f9-c183-5c27-ab2e-83f0eb96d0d0'}, {'abstract': 'Do dogs need designer digs? A new collection begs the question.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/my-barkitect/', 'snippet': 'Do dogs need designer digs? A new collection begs the question.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '75', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Barkitect', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Barkitect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban, Shigeru', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grcic, Konstantin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sejima, Kazuyo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T13:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andreas Kokkino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andreas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kokkino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aafc128e-696e-5b16-b83d-3a0a55488ebc', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aafc128e-696e-5b16-b83d-3a0a55488ebc'}, {'abstract': 'HBO has ordered eight episodes of “Hello Ladies,” a new series that will star Stephen Merchant as “a gawky Englishman searching for the woman of his dreams in Los Angeles.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/hbo-adds-comedy-from-office-co-creator-stephen-merchant/', 'snippet': 'HBO has ordered eight episodes of “Hello Ladies,” a new series that will star Stephen Merchant as “a gawky Englishman searching for the woman of his dreams in Los Angeles.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes even the members of accomplished comedy teams need to get up and stretch their legs a bit, and in the case of Stephen Merchant, those are some very long legs to stretch. Mr. Merchant, the 6-foot-7 comedian who with Ricky Gervais created the original British incarnation of “The Office,” and with him created and starred in HBO’s “Extras,” “Life’s Too Short” and “The Ricky Gervais Show,” will be stepping out in his own HBO series, that cable network said. The new series, called “Hello Ladies,” will star Mr. Merchant as a character named Stephen, described by HBO in an e-mail as “a gawky Englishman searching for the woman of his dreams in Los Angeles.” The network said it has ordered eight episodes of the series, for which Mr. Merchant directed the pilot, and which he wrote with Lee Eisenberg and Gene Stupnitsky (whose credits include NBC’s American version of “The Office” and films like “Bad Teacher”). The unlucky love life of Mr. Merchant, who has also been featured in comedy films like “Hall Pass,” tends to be a recurring theme of his humor; as he recently wrote on his Twitter account: “Attitude from Siri when I cancelled writing a text. She said ‘Ok, forget it then!’ Now failing to charm virtual women as well as real ones.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/merchant/merchant-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/merchant/merchant-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/merchant/merchant-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/merchant/merchant-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/arts/merchant/merchant-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'HBO Adds Comedy From a Creator of ‘The Office’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'HBO Adds a Comedy From an ‘Office’ Creator', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eisenberg, Lee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gervais, Ricky', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merchant, Stephen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T13:09:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bdf4930-c691-5713-932d-9002db740f85', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bdf4930-c691-5713-932d-9002db740f85'}, {'abstract': 'Observers from the Organization for Security and Cooperation in Europe have been monitoring U.S. elections for a decade. This year, however, conservatives have expressed concern about the presence of watchdogs from the old Continent.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/republican-angst-over-european-election-monitors/', 'snippet': 'Observers from the Organization for Security and Cooperation in Europe have been monitoring U.S. elections for a decade. This year, however, conservatives have expressed concern about the presence of watchdogs from the old Continent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — American voters have been alerted to be on the lookout for sinister strangers lurking near polling places next Tuesday. They may be part of a crack team sent from Europe to snoop on the election.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/blogs/02rdv-election/02rdv-election-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 766, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/blogs/02rdv-election/02rdv-election-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1532, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Angst Over European Election Monitors', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization for Security and Cooperation in Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T13:10:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b01320c-311e-5601-9e41-5043ecc39aea', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b01320c-311e-5601-9e41-5043ecc39aea'}, {'abstract': 'Angry Iranians commemorated the taking of the American Embassy in Tehran in 1979, and a senior security official warned against any compromise with the “great Satan.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/world/middleeast/iranian-hard-liners-reject-any-talks-with-us.html', 'snippet': 'Angry Iranians commemorated the taking of the American Embassy in Tehran in 1979, and a senior security official warned against any compromise with the “great Satan.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Angry Iranians gathered in front of the former American Embassy here in Tehran on Friday to celebrate the annual “Day of Fighting the Global Arrogance,” and a senior security official warned against any compromise with the “great Satan.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/global-home/3iran-image/3iran-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name