er for human rights, said China’s suppression of the rights of Tibetans had driven them to “desperate forms of protest” like self-immolation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/world/asia/un-rights-official-faults-china-on-tibetan-suppression.html', 'snippet': 'Navi Pillay, the United Nations’ high commissioner for human rights, said China’s suppression of the rights of Tibetans had driven them to “desperate forms of protest” like self-immolation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — The top human rights official of the United Nations took China to task on Friday over the suppression of Tibetans’ rights that she said had driven them to “desperate forms of protest,” referring to about 60 self-immolations by Tibetans protesting Chinese rule that have been reported since March 2011, including seven since mid-October. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/global-home/3tibet-image/3tibet-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/global-home/3tibet-image/3tibet-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1387, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Rights Official Faults China on Tibetan Suppression', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Rights Official Criticizes China’s Limits on Tibetans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pillay, Navi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immolation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T13:20:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf5bc1b7-2571-5fdd-871b-e8c05bd7461f', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf5bc1b7-2571-5fdd-871b-e8c05bd7461f'}, {'abstract': 'On Friday, the Japanese bank said it was likely involved in a new insider trading case, months after the firm’s chief executive, Kenichi Watanabe, resigned following similar allegations.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/nomura-faces-another-insider-trading-case/', 'snippet': 'On Friday, the Japanese bank said it was likely involved in a new insider trading case, months after the firm’s chief executive, Kenichi Watanabe, resigned following similar allegations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Japanese bank Nomura faces more legal problems.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nomura Faces Another Insider Trading Case', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Legal Problem For Nomura', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watanabe, Kenichi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T13:21:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6cd31f8-1f21-5e44-9d69-689ddd9098f7', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6cd31f8-1f21-5e44-9d69-689ddd9098f7'}, {'abstract': 'Gains reflected in October make this the first year in the last four to show an increase.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/answer-yes-teachers-are-being-hired/', 'snippet': 'Gains reflected in October make this the first year in the last four to show an increase.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a post on Thursday, I asked whether the erosion of teaching jobs in public schools was coming to an end. The October jobs report, just out, has an answer: teachers are finally being hired.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Answer: Yes, Teachers Are Being Hired', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T13:22:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/038e5242-4501-5d97-85ae-92ba95e8efbb', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/038e5242-4501-5d97-85ae-92ba95e8efbb'}, {'abstract': 'Paralyzed because of a building crane across the street left dangling by the storm, the hall rescheduled some concerts and moved others to new locations.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/carnegie-hall-scrambles-to-reschedule-cancelled-concerts/', 'snippet': 'Paralyzed because of a building crane across the street left dangling by the storm, the hall rescheduled some concerts and moved others to new locations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carnegie Hall, plunged into suspended animation because of the threat posed by the building crane across the street left dangling by Hurricane Sandy, is struggling to accommodate singers, pianists and string players whose dates have been canceled this weekend. Among changes it announced late on Thursday: the King’s Singers concert scheduled for Friday was moved to Feb. 18; Murray Perahia’s piano recital was moved from Friday to Sunday at Avery Fisher Hall; the Belcea Quartet performance on Saturday moves to Tuesday, but only if authorities reopen 57th Street, which was closed because of the crane; a performance by Opera Lafayette of “L’Invitation au Voyage” on Friday in Weill Recital Hall will take place at the Colony Club; Monday’s Oratorio Society of New York performance will take place some time in early 2013. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carnegie Hall Scrambles to Reschedule Canceled Concerts', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Carnegie Hall Scrambles To Reschedule Concerts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "king's singers", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oratorio Society of New York', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T13:26:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5acc7a57-65db-59b8-bb03-79db892adbf1', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5acc7a57-65db-59b8-bb03-79db892adbf1'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/what-were-reading-558/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Food and Wine: For those post-Sandy occupants of the East Coast who are trying to figure out what to do with what’s left in their pantries and refrigerators, here are some helpful dishes that involve throwing a bunch of stuff in a Dutch oven. …', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T13:31:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c195a17-4396-5ac6-9c7c-8fc20fdd3580', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c195a17-4396-5ac6-9c7c-8fc20fdd3580'}, {'abstract': 'Also, government officials turned to social networking to get the word out about Hurricane Sandy.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/the-breakfast-meeting-martha-stewart-retrenches-and-romney-stagecraft/', 'snippet': 'Also, government officials turned to social networking to get the word out about Hurricane Sandy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martha Stewart Living Omnimedia on Thursday announced cuts to its business, Christine Haughney reported, laying off 70 people (12 percent of its staff) and scaling back two of its four magazines. The company’s three divisions — publishing, merchandising and broadcasting — have all experienced declining income in recent years, but the latest cuts go to the heart of the company, its publishing division, which still provides 64 percent of total revenue, according to the latest public filings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Martha Stewart Retrenches, and Romney Stagecraft', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T13:45:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72fd41c3-0f05-5fa2-bd66-815f6192394d', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72fd41c3-0f05-5fa2-bd66-815f6192394d'}, {'abstract': 'Scott M. Stringer, the Manhattan borough president, said the race should be postponed “in order to focus all of the city’s resources on the crucial task of helping our neighbors recover from this disaster.”', 'web_url': 'https://marathon.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/manhattan-borough-president-adds-voice-to-those-opposing-marathon/', 'snippet': 'Scott M. Stringer, the Manhattan borough president, said the race should be postponed “in order to focus all of the city’s resources on the crucial task of helping our neighbors recover from this disaster.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scott M. Stringer, the Manhattan borough president, became the latest in an increasingly long line of public officials to call for Sunday’s New York City Marathon to be postponed or canceled.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Manhattan Borough President Adds Voice to Those Opposing Marathon', 'kicker': 'On the Run', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York City Marathon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stringer, Scott M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T13:53:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61ffcda9-2c29-5995-b02b-8314d2df4d20', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61ffcda9-2c29-5995-b02b-8314d2df4d20'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney called the numbers “a sad reminder that the economy is at a virtual standstill,” but the White House cited the report as further evidence that the nation’s economy is recovering.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/us/politics/jobs-report-offers-little-change-in-dynamic-between-obama-and-romney.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney called the numbers “a sad reminder that the economy is at a virtual standstill,” but the White House cited the report as further evidence that the nation’s economy is recovering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The jobs report on Friday had held the potential to inject an unpredictable, last-minute jolt into the race for the White House.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economic Data Offers Little Change in Dynamic Between Obama and Romney', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jobs Report Offers Little Change in Dynamic Between Obama and Romney', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'ma