re people live to be very old, wasn’t always held in high esteem. “The Iliad,” for one, suggests Ikaria is a wind-wracked place surrounded by messy seas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joseph Georgirenes isn’t the only man of letters to devote a few of them to the Greek island of Ikaria. As Dan Buettner noted in the magazine last weekend, Georgirenes found the air and water there “most commendable,” and a major reason for the residents’ long lives. But then he would, I suppose — he was the bishop of Ikaria back in the 17th century.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/magazine/01-ikaria/01-ikaria-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/magazine/01-ikaria/01-ikaria-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/magazine/01-ikaria/01-ikaria-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/01/magazine/01-ikaria/01-ikaria-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/magazine/01-ikaria/01-ikaria-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 151, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Unkempt’ Ikaria', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T15:11:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dean Robinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/079c7b44-947c-54d1-8919-0944fb3b6ae2', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/079c7b44-947c-54d1-8919-0944fb3b6ae2'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, Nov. 2', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-friday-nov-2.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, Nov. 2', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been pumping gas for 36 hours; I pumped 1,500 gallons. My nose, my mouth is bleeding from the fumes. The fighting just makes it worse.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, Nov. 2', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T15:12:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/b59158e4-bf7b-54ca-9308-ceb03531b191', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b59158e4-bf7b-54ca-9308-ceb03531b191'}, {'abstract': 'Plans to revive papers started by Jawaharlal Nehru in 1938 are targeted by a sharp critic of the Gandhi family.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/at-the-heart-of-a-political-brawl-in-india-two-historic-newspapers/', 'snippet': 'Plans to revive papers started by Jawaharlal Nehru in 1938 are targeted by a sharp critic of the Gandhi family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Subramanian Swamy, chief of the Janata Party, on Thursday accused Sonia Gandhi, the Congress Party presiden