5}}], 'headline': {'main': "'Somm'", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T15:47:54+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'Forgotten Man Films', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Forgotten', 'middlename': 'Man', 'lastname': 'Films', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/cf4cf5e9-0a38-563f-b2fb-1aa340b25a9e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/cf4cf5e9-0a38-563f-b2fb-1aa340b25a9e'}, {'abstract': 'The Manhattan borough president added his name to those opposed to running the marathon on Sunday, as did Bill de Blasio, the public advocate, who had supported the race earlier this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/sports/backlash-builds-as-new-york-city-marathon-divides-city.html', 'snippet': 'The Manhattan borough president added his name to those opposed to running the marathon on Sunday, as did Bill de Blasio, the public advocate, who had supported the race earlier this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two days before nearly 50,000 runners are scheduled to gather in Staten Island for the start of the New York City Marathon, opposition to the race continued to swell Friday and the Police Department, stretched thin from handling relief efforts, has called for department retirees to help with storm work and the marathon on Sunday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/03marathon1/03marathon1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/03marathon1/03marathon1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1390, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/03marathon1/03marathon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/03marathon1/03marathon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/03marathon1/03marathon1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Growing Outcry Over Proceeding With Marathon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marathon Presses On Amid Backlash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York City Marathon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Road Runners Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wittenberg, Mary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T15:48:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b0b34ca-6471-50ff-b8c7-38cb3e49e2de', 'word_count': 1526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b0b34ca-6471-50ff-b8c7-38cb3e49e2de'}, {'abstract': 'The FiveThirtyEight model represents a complicated analysis of the polls, but simplicity is on its side in finding that President Obama is the Electoral College favorite.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/nov-1-the-simple-case-for-saying-obama-is-the-favorite/', 'snippet': 'The FiveThirtyEight model represents a complicated analysis of the polls, but simplicity is on its side in finding that President Obama is the Electoral College favorite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are following some of the same people that I do on Twitter, you may have noticed some pushback about our contention that Barack Obama is a favorite (and certainly not a lock) to be re-elected. I haven’t come across too many analyses suggesting that Mitt Romney is the favorite. (There are exceptions.) But there are plenty of people who say that the race is a “tossup.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nov. 1: The Simple Case for Saying Obama Is the Favorite', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Simple Case For Saying That Obama Is Favored', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T15:50:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40c60515-6707-5a07-b5e1-1ddfbeb39ad6', 'word_count': 1340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40c60515-6707-5a07-b5e1-1ddfbeb39ad6'}, {'abstract': 'States will almost certainly request billions in federal aid, which could stir concerns about fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/us/politics/first-federal-dollars-allotted-in-hurricane-sandys-aftermath.html', 'snippet': 'States will almost certainly request billions in federal aid, which could stir concerns about fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The first trickle of federal funds has started to go out after Hurricane Sandy — $29 million to rebuild highways, $30 million to hire temporary workers to help with the cleanup. But lawmakers are just beginning to tally what is certain to be a multibillion-dollar bill for the federal government at a time of fiscal restraint.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federal Relief Costs Likely to Be Big, and Contested', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First Federal Money Is Dealt Out to States In Hurricane Aftermath', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northeastern States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York Metropolitan Area', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Emergency Management Agency', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T15:54:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Lipton and Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4ca63e7-b3b0-5aa6-b204-b5d3ce86ce60', 'word_count': 1056, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4ca63e7-b3b0-5aa6-b204-b5d3ce86ce60'}, {'abstract': 'A million dollars-worth of plug-in hybrid vehicles, including 16 Fisker Karma luxury sedans, caught fire at Port Newark during Hurricane Sandy.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/mystery-at-port-newark-why-did-17-plug-in-cars-burn/', 'snippet': 'A million dollars-worth of plug-in hybrid vehicles, including 16 Fisker Karma luxury sedans, caught fire at Port Newark during Hurricane Sandy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid all the damage left in Hurricane Sandy’s wake is an automotive whodunit, or rather, what-dunit? What caused more than a million dollars-worth of plug-in hybrid vehicles, including 16 Fisker Karma luxury sedans, to catch fire Monday night at Port Newark?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mystery at Port Newark: Why Did 17 Plug-In Cars Burn?', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Batteries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fisker Automotive', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T15:57:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josie Garthwaite', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garthwaite', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/989d09a5-af0a-5c56-bd5f-51a5441ef8bd', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/989d09a5-af0a-5c56-bd5f-51a5441ef8bd'}, {'abstract': 'Six Knicks are rehabbing from injuries, but point guards Raymond Felton, Jason Kidd and Pablo Prigioni are not among them.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/knicks-enter-season-healthy-at-point-guard/', 'snippet': 'Six Knicks are rehabbing from injuries, but point guards Raymond Felton, Jason Kidd and Pablo Prigioni are not among them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Knicks have growing concerns regarding their health as the oldest team in the N.B.A. this season. That will be one of the story lines when the Knicks play the defending N.B.A. champion Miami Heat in their season opener Friday night at Madison Square Garden.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knicks Enter Season Healthy at Point Guard', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Felton, Raymond', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kidd, Jason', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prigioni, Pablo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T15:58:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0