r East. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04CHE2_SPAN/04CHE2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04CHE2_SPAN/04CHE2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04CHE2_SPAN/04CHE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04CHE2_SPAN/04CHE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04CHE2_SPAN/04CHE2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04CHE2_SPAN/04CHE2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'City-Bred Comic Has His Heart in the Club', 'kicker': 'Comedy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City-Bred Comic Has His Heart In the Club', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Che, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T16:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Megan Angelo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Megan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Angelo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc62b403-304c-59b6-a3dc-1117ede29cc1', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc62b403-304c-59b6-a3dc-1117ede29cc1'}, {'abstract': 'Lourdes Lopez, a founder of Morphoses with Christopher Wheeldon, talks about continuing that company after his departure, even as she takes on new duties as artistic director of Miami City Ballet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/arts/dance/lourdes-lopez-on-new-role-with-miami-city-ballet.html', 'snippet': 'Lourdes Lopez, a founder of Morphoses with Christopher Wheeldon, talks about continuing that company after his departure, even as she takes on new duties as artistic director of Miami City Ballet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON the Thursday before Labor Day weekend Lourdes Lopez received a call from Miami City Ballet. In the spring she had been named to succeed the outgoing artistic director Edward Villella. His departure was controversial — an unhappy board, heartbroken dancers, financial problems. Instead of following through on plans to leave in April, Mr. Villella abruptly ended his tenure that weekend; by the time the dancers returned on Tuesday, he was gone. For Ms. Lopez, who like Mr. Villella is a former New York City Ballet principal under George Balanchine, it’s been a whirlwind. She arrived in Miami, with one big suitcase, at 1 a.m. that Tuesday. Eight hours later she was in charge of both the company and its school.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04LOURDES1_SPAN/04LOURDES2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04LOURDES1_SPAN/04LOURDES2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04LOURDES1_SPAN/04LOURDES2_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04LOURDES1_SPAN/04LOURDES2_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1385, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04LOURDES1_SPAN/04LOURDES2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04LOURDES1_SPAN/04LOURDES2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04LOURDES1_SPAN/04LOURDES2_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'First Position, and Others, in Miami', 'kicker': 'Dance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First Position, And Others, In Miami', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami City Ballet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Lourdes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T16:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/a02c4bb6-d960-54ab-affd-244c3212bfb6', 'word_count': 1229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a02c4bb6-d960-54ab-affd-244c3212bfb6'}, {'abstract': 'Carnegie Hall looks abroad for its latest big festival, bringing talent like Gilberto Gil and Gustavo Dudamel for its Voices of Latin America event.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/arts/music/voices-of-latin-america-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Carnegie Hall looks abroad for its latest big festival, bringing talent like Gilberto Gil and Gustavo Dudamel for its Voices of Latin America event.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN Carnegie Hall kicked off what has become an annual series of big festivals based on big personalities and big cultures, it planted a flag first in familiar soil. Berlin in Lights, which ran for 17 days in November 2007, contextualized a Berlin Philharmonic residency with a healthy sampling of other musical styles associated with the city, as well as a clutch of related visual-arts and literary presentations. Bernstein: The Best of All Possible Worlds, in the fall of 2008, paid comparable tribute to an artist indelibly linked with New York’s musical identity.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04LATINVOICES2_SPAN/04LATINVOICES2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04LATINVOICES2_SPAN/04LATINVOICES2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04LATINVOICES2_SPAN/04LATINVOICES2_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image