 Crisis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T16:27:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc2233c0-0b65-5ee0-8b6d-d2ec07cbef70', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc2233c0-0b65-5ee0-8b6d-d2ec07cbef70'}, {'abstract': 'As the Civil War raged in the East, settler-Indian violence tore apart northern California.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/bad-blood-in-the-bald-hills/', 'snippet': 'As the Civil War raged in the East, settler-Indian violence tore apart northern California.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though his memoirs make no mention of the event, Col. Francis J. Lippitt may very well have let out a sigh of relief on the September day in 1862 when the steamer Panama finally docked at Bucksport, Calif. It was not the vessel itself he would have been keen to receive, but rather the cargo it was picking up: 800 surrendered American Indians, ready to ship north to Smith’s River Reservation near the Oregon border. Perhaps now the guerrilla war that had stalked the counties of remote Northern California for the previous months would finally abate. Perhaps now Colonel Lippitt could finally partake in the titanic struggle to save the Union being waged far to the east.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bad Blood in the Bald Hills', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'conten