', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/education/edl-04mooc-t_CA3/edl-04mooc-t_CA3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1101, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Big Three, at a Glance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Big Three', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EdX', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Udacity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T17:37:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'EdLife', 'section_name': 'Education', 'subsection_name': 'Education Life', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/072de94d-10e2-59d2-bbe5-0a1867e27cb0', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/072de94d-10e2-59d2-bbe5-0a1867e27cb0'}, {'abstract': 'In what his aides called Mitt Romney’s closing argument to electorate after 18 months of bruising politics, he asked that Americans “look to the record, the accomplishments and failures, and the judgment.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/romneys-closing-argument-i-promise-change-and-i-have-a-record-of-achieving-it/', 'snippet': 'In what his aides called Mitt Romney’s closing argument to electorate after 18 months of bruising politics, he asked that Americans “look to the record, the accomplishments and failures, and the judgment.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEST ALLIS, Wis.—At the start of a frenetic final weekend of campaigning, Mitt Romney put on a suit and tie, flipped on a teleprompter and did something on Friday that he had avoided for much of the past two years: he made an explicit case for his own lengthy résumé.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Closing Argument: ‘Look to the Record’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romney Changes Tack, Emphasizing Readiness and Giving Specifics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T17:37:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro and Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/712f5d17-ce31-573b-bfa3-f5b08de72396', 'word_count': 858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/712f5d17-ce31-573b-bfa3-f5b08de72396'}, {'abstract': 'Universities with the highest and lowest student-loan default rates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/education/edlife/where-theyre-defaulting.html', 'snippet': 'Universities with the highest and lowest student-loan default rates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The default rate is perhaps the best snapshot of how graduates are struggling with student debt. (Default is the worst-case scenario, when no payment is received on a loan for 270 days.) The Department of Education has typically tracked borrowers who default on federal loans within two years of entering their repayment period. The window has just been extended to three years, with the hope of getting a better picture of how many are in distress. An average 13.4 percent of borrowers who entered repayment in fiscal year 2009 defaulted within three years; 47 percent of them attended for-profit colleges and universities. The accompanying charts show the colleges and universities with highest and lowest three-year default rates (only institutions offering graduate degrees and with at least 500 borrowers entering repayment were considered).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where They’re Defaulting', 'kicker': 'Data | Cost of College', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T17:43:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'EdLife', 'section_name': 'Education', 'subsection_name': 'Education Life', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d58678a4-2796-5d05-8071-054344ea3b6a', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d58678a4-2796-5d05-8071-054344ea3b6a'}, {'abstract': 'Survivors of disasters like Hurricane Sandy frequently suffer post-traumatic stress symptoms like recurrent nightmares, flashbacks and a hair-trigger temper, but research has also revealed that we can mitigate the psychological fallout.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/the-trauma-after-the-storm/', 'snippet': 'Survivors of disasters like Hurricane Sandy frequently suffer post-traumatic stress symptoms like recurrent nightmares, flashbacks and a hair-trigger temper, but research has also revealed that we can mitigate the psychological fallout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the small Connecticut town where I grew up, the tornado of 1979 remains the storm, a freak tornado packing 86-mile-per-hour winds that churned through the streets, killing three people, injuring hundreds and destroying several hundred homes and businesses, including many in my neighborhood. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/health/01well_chen/01well_chen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/health/01well_chen/01well_chen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1439, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/health/01well_chen/01well_chen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/01/health/01well_chen/01well_chen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/health/01well_chen/01well_chen-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Easing the Trauma After the Storm', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After the Tempest Passes, Easing the Trauma It Left', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fear (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Katrina (2005)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tornadoes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T17:43:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byl