'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T17:45:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9e36291-d147-59a1-999b-dc6830cea04b', 'word_count': 39, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9e36291-d147-59a1-999b-dc6830cea04b'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of cultural events this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/arts/nov-4-10.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of cultural events this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ELECTION Day is upon us. But for those wishing to distract themselves from the blizzard of exit polls, talking heads and dazzling digital graphics the networks and cable news stations will be inundating us with, the Public Theater offers a respite of sorts: Tuesday brings the opening night of “SORRY,” a new play written and directed by Richard Nelson, the latest in his series about the Apple family in Rhinebeck, N.Y.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04GUIDE1_SPAN/04GUIDE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04GUIDE1_SPAN/04GUIDE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04GUIDE1_SPAN/04GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/arts/04GUIDE1_SPAN/04GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1402, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 't