 time of year to be with the one you love the most: yourself.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04SINGLE/04SINGLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 554, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04SINGLE/04SINGLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 554}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04SINGLE/04SINGLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 948, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04SINGLE/04SINGLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 948, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04SINGLE/04SINGLE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04SINGLE/04SINGLE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04SINGLE/04SINGLE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Single for the Holidays', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Single for The Holidays', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Single Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T17:54:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Rosenbloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenbloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f693cd61-1fc3-5e40-9a36-c1d23551b5d0', 'word_count': 3746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f693cd61-1fc3-5e40-9a36-c1d23551b5d0'}, {'abstract': 'It’s taken time, but gritty North Amsterdam has evolved into a creative hub, charged by “a lot of raw energy.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/travel/from-blue-collar-to-red-hot-in-amsterdam.html', 'snippet': 'It’s taken time, but gritty North Amsterdam has evolved into a creative hub, charged by “a lot of raw energy.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE free commuter ferries leaving Central Station in Amsterdam and heading north across the IJ (pronounced Eye) harbor are invariably packed with local designers, food lovers and film buffs. They brace themselves against the cold wind, steady their bikes, and look expectantly toward a structure that resembles a shiny white spaceship. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04HEADSUP_SPAN/04HEADSUP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04HEADSUP_SPAN/04HEADSUP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/travel/04HEADSUP_SPAN/04HEADSUP_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i