nt_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Martha Graham Sets and Costumes Damaged by Hurricane Sandy', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flooding Damages Sets And Costumes for Graham', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Noguchi, Isamu', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Graham, Martha, Center for Contemporary Dance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Graham, Martha, Dance Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T19:57:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70c3fc99-bfc3-5d3e-be75-b3f830585948', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70c3fc99-bfc3-5d3e-be75-b3f830585948'}, {'abstract': 'Nine months ago, FiveThirtyEight made mention of a 150,000-jobs-per-month figure in the jobs report as a possible over-under benchmark number. What this may all mean, now that we’re merely days before the election.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/revisiting-our-february-jobs-prediction/', 'snippet': 'Nine months ago, FiveThirtyEight made mention of a 150,000-jobs-per-month figure in the jobs report as a possible over-under benchmark number. What this may all mean, now that we’re merely days before the election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Friday’s jobs report was a reasonably strong one, economically speaking. The economy added 171,000 jobs in October, according to the government’s survey of business establishments. In addition, estimates of jobs growth were revised upward for August and September. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Revisiting Our February Jobs Prediction', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T19:59:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/941f3954-ae7d-5d1f-ae70-04ae9d90dbd1', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/941f3954-ae7d-5d1f-ae70-04ae9d90dbd1'}, {'abstract': 'A new residence hall, La Casa, offers commuter students from Chicago’s South Side a safe, quiet place to eat, sleep and study.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/education/edlife/dorm-offers-safe-haven-for-commuter-students-from-chicagos-south-side.html', 'snippet': 'A new residence hall, La Casa, offers commuter students from Chicago’s South Side a safe, quiet place to eat, sleep and study.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON that August morning, when the new college dormitory was scheduled to open here in the Pilsen section of Chicago, Martha Elena Nieto and her son, Teohua Villalobos, were first to arrive. It was 7 a.m. Move-in time wasn’t for several hours — the dorm director wasn’t even there yet — but Ms. Nieto was anxious to get on with it. She and Teohua hadn’t slept the night before, they were so excited. That this dormitory even existed felt like a small miracle, almost as if someone had built it specifically with Teohua and his mother in mind.', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/education/edl-04dorm-t_CA1/edl-04dorm-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 