stract': 'Awarding achievements with information-age credentials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/education/edlife/how-to-earn-your-cyber-stripes.html', 'snippet': 'Awarding achievements with information-age credentials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A number of institutions are developing badge systems to recognize specific skills.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/education/edlife/04badges1/04badges1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 533, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/education/edlife/04badges1/04badges1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 533, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Earn Your Cyber Stripes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Badges', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T20:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'EdLife', 'section_name': 'Education', 'subsection_name': 'Education Life', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/30f9ad70-3500-5312-a51a-d5003a31cafc', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30f9ad70-3500-5312-a51a-d5003a31cafc'}, {'abstract': 'James R. Flynn has spent more than 25 years trying to explain why each generation has significantly higher I.Q. scores than the previous one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/education/edlife/james-r-flynn-on-rising-iqs.html', 'snippet': 'James R. Flynn has spent more than 25 years trying to explain why each generation has significantly higher I.Q. scores than the previous one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN the social scientist James R. Flynn started analyzing more than 50 years’ worth of I.Q. scores, he noticed something peculiar. On tests that assessed vocabulary used in everyday life, adults showed enormous gains — nearly 18 points. That made sense. Many more people attend college and work in professions now than in 1950. But when he examined children’s scores, he was surprised by how far behind they lagged. Usually facility with words trickles down; children hear and absorb parents’ expanded vocabulary and discussions. But that hadn’t happened. Children’s I.Q. showed only a 4.4 percent gain.', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I.Q. Rising', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I.Q. Rising', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flynn, James R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intelligence and Intelligence Tests (IQ)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T20:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'EdLife', 'section_name': 'Education', 'subsection_name': 'Education Life', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1268fb2-e345-53ff-8672-b41874e992f8', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1268fb2-e345-53ff-8672-b41874e992f8'}, {'abstract': 'Information-age credentials may be the first serious competitor to traditional degrees since college-going became the norm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/education/edlife/show-me-your-badge.html', 'snippet': 'Information-age credentials may be the first serious competitor to traditional degrees since college-going became the norm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT the end of “Fundamentals of Atomic Force Microscopy,” a short online course offered by Purdue University, students who score at least 60 percent on the final exam will receive an e-mail with a file attached. It will contain a picture of a blue-and-white circle, roughly one inch in diameter, embossed with the stylized image of an atomic force microscope bouncing a laser beam off a cantilever into a photodiode, which is how scientists take photographs and measure the size of very small (nanoscale) things.', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/education/edlife/04badges4/04badges4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/education/edlife/04badges4/04badges4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/education/edlife/04badges4/04badges4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/04/education/edlife/04badges4/04badges4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/education/edlife/04badges4/04badges4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Show Me Your Badge', 'kicker': No