humbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/01/health/recipehealth_squash/recipehealth_squash-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/01/health/recipehealth_squash/recipehealth_squash-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Many Colors of Squash', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Squash (Vegetable)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T20:13:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbd3c0c0-50df-5d0e-b154-d8e562af3ba9', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbd3c0c0-50df-5d0e-b154-d8e562af3ba9'}, {'abstract': 'Just like his apartment in Cologne, Germany, Mike Meiré’s world is constantly expanding.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/having-it-all/', 'snippet': 'Just like his apartment in Cologne, Germany, Mike Meiré’s world is constantly expanding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sixteen years ago, Mike Meiré was a poster boy for minimalism. “I only listened to techno and wore Yohji Yamamoto and Comme des Garçons,” says the German artist and art director, whose clients include companies like Dornbracht, Mini and Artek as well as high-profile independent magazines like 032c, Garage and Kid’s Wear. His apartment, on the fourth floor of a turn-of-the-century building in Cologne’s Belgian Quarter, had white lacquered floors, painted brown walls, silver curtains and sharp-edged walnut sofas with suede cushions. If there was a kitchen, he never used it. “It was very much like a hotel,” he says. And that was exactly how he wanted it.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '69', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Having It All', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Having It All', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T20:15:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marco Velardi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marco', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Velardi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/719b2041-321d-507b-a70f-1ef623faa695', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/719b2041-321d-507b-a70f-1ef623faa695'}, {'abstract': 'Ordinary voters aren’t the only ones to confront foreclosures, tax woes and child-support payment problems. Consider the situation of Representative Joe Walsh, Republican of Illinois.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/your-money/even-capitol-hill-gets-the-financial-blues.html', 'snippet': 'Ordinary voters aren’t the only ones to confront foreclosures, tax woes and child-support payment problems. Consider the situation of Representative Joe Walsh, Republican of Illinois.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Right or wrong, many voters think their elected representatives are above it all financially. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/your-money/03money/03money-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 919, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/your-money/03money/03money-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1838, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Being Elected Is No Shield Against Money Woes', 'kicker': 'Your Money', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Being Elected Is No Shield Against Money Woes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Michael S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duckworth, L Tammy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walsh, William Joseph', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T20:17:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/001fbed2-c708-5ec0-9716-bd048bab5225', 'word_count': 1247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/001fbed2-c708-5ec0-9716-bd048bab5225'}, {'abstract': 'Readers weigh in on what, if any, personal financial failings should be disqualifying for politicians who ask for our vote.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/politicians-and-their-personal-finances/', 'snippet': 'Readers weigh in on what, if any, personal financial failings should be disqualifying for politicians who ask for our vote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For this weekend’s Your Money column, I tried to profile the poorest members of Congress in all the land. Given the limited financial disclosures that our elected representatives must make, which the Center for Responsive Politics does a nice job of collecting in one place, it’s hard to say for sure who has the lowest net worth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Politicians and Their Personal Finances', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Custody and Support', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T20:19:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65f83ea6-2589-5152-b742-554c8bbe92c5', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65f83ea6-2589-5152-b742-554c8bbe92c5'}, {'abstract': 'With Chelsea galleries and many New York artists struggling with the devastation of Hurricane Sandy, the Museum of Modern Art, together with conservators from the American Institute for Conservation Collections Emergency Response Team, are offering a presentation on saving flood-damaged artworks.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/museum-of-modern-art-to-offer-presentation-on-conserving-flood-damaged-artworks/', 'snippet': 'With Chelsea galleries and many New York artists struggling with the devastation of Hurricane Sandy, the Museum of Modern Art, together with conservators from the American Institute for Conservation Collections Emergency Response Team, are offerin...', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Chelsea galleries and many New York artists struggling with the devastation of Hurricane Sandy, the Museum of Modern Art, together with conservators from the American Institute for Conservation Collections Emergency Response Team, are offering a presentation on saving flood-damaged artworks. The session is to be held at the museum on Sunday from noon until 2:00 p.m. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum of Modern Art to Offer Presentation on Conserving Flood-Damaged Artworks', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'MoMA Gives Advice On Damaged Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T20:22:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c997ffb-e4d0-5928-96e7-0b44ced73b1e', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c997ffb-e4d0-5928-96e7-0b44ced73b1e'}, {'abstract': 'In the 62 years of the Formula One championship, 32 drivers from 14 nations have won the title, but only two have been Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/automobiles/of-champions-few-americans.html', 'snippet': 'In the 62 years of the Formula One championship, 32 drivers from 14 nations have won the title, but only two have been Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF you are looking for a reason Formula One racing is not as popular as it might be in the United States, consider this: in the 62 years of the championship, 32 drivers from 14 nations have won the championship title. Only two, Phil Hill in 1961 and Mario Andretti in 1978, have been Americans. ', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/automobiles/04DRIVER1/04DRIVER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/automobiles/04DRIVER1/04DRIVER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 1999, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/automobiles/04DRIVER1/04DRIVER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/04/automobiles/04DRIVER1/04DRIVER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/automobiles/04DRIVER1/04DRIVER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Of Champions, Few Americans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Of Champions, Few Americans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Phil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N