rated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHERE college is concerned, nothing can’t be ranked. To crown this year’s “most beautiful campus,” Newsweek and The Daily Beast considered College Prowler’s hot guys and girls polls; its campus architecture and aesthetics ratings; and because weather should never be underestimated in the college search, the number of sunny days and the average comfort index (based on temperature and humidity) as supplied by Sperling’s Best Places.', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eye of the Beholder', 'kicker': 'Blackboard | Rankings News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eye of the Beholder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T22:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'EdLife', 'section_name': 'Education', 'subsection_name': 'Education Life', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19f3727c-657a-5cf3-8017-b7e8ed5554f9', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19f3727c-657a-5cf3-8017-b7e8ed5554f9'}, {'abstract': 'With the new Learning Annex, just call it in (or e-mail or Skype).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/education/edlife/instant-advice-at-the-learning-annex.html', 'snippet': 'With the new Learning Annex, just call it in (or e-mail or Skype).', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Learning Annex, provider of “edutainment” classics like “How to Flirt,” has reinvented itself with an online marketplace for the social media age.', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Learning by Phone', 'kicker': 'Blackboard | Adult Ed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Learning (Annex) by the Meter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULT EDUCATION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Learning Annex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T22:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'EdLife', 'section_name': 'Education', 'subsection_name': 'Education Life', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Saavedra Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saavedra', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52216f30-4af3-56ff-8fa4-2b89b185b609', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52216f30-4af3-56ff-8fa4-2b89b185b609'}, {'abstract': 'I was the bare-minimum student, checking off “to do” boxes, and the plan worked. I didn’t learn much of anything.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/education/edlife/brown-alumna-recalls-what-she-failed-to-learn.html', 'snippet': 'I was the bare-minimum student, checking off “to do” boxes, and the plan worked. I didn’t learn much of anything.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN my high school, as in most schools of upper-middle-class overachievers across the country, there were the students who strived and stressed out, the students who knew just what it took to get the job done and then that one kid who unnervingly surpassed us all even though he showed up in class stoned every day.', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/education/edl-04notebook-t_CA0/edl-04notebook-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 512, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/education/edl-04notebook-t_CA0/edl-04notebook-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg