18 Months,” Calvin Harris is after bona fide pop stardom in the United States, but giving up some of the usual influence of a producer in dance music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who’s in charge: the person out in front or the person behind the boards? This is an eternal pop music question with no firm answer. Rock and country largely don’t pretend that producers could be on equal footing with their stars, while hip-hop is more balanced, with producers having become a new class of celebrity.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/arts/03HARRIS/03HARRIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/03/arts/03HARRIS/03HARRIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/arts/03HARRIS/03HARRIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/arts/03HARRIS/03HARRIS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1322, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/arts/03HARRIS/03HARRIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/03/arts/03HARRIS/03HARRIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/arts/03HARRIS/03HARRIS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A D.J. Seeks a New Spotlight in Pop', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A D.J. Seeks a New Spotlight in Pop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Calvin (1984- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T22:06:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0ab1ac9-6622-53e3-aad0-d3f4baa930d1', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0ab1ac9-6622-53e3-aad0-d3f4baa930d1'}, {'abstract': 'SAP paid $4.3 billion for Ariba, a cloud-based marketplace for business supplies, in the hope that even corporate commerce is social.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/saps-marketplace-dream/', 'snippet': 'SAP paid $4.3 billion for Ariba, a cloud-based marketplace for business supplies, in the hope that even corporate commerce is social.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Last spring SAP, the big German business software company, agreed to pay $4.3 billion for a company called Ariba, which runs an online marketplace for businesses selling to other businesses. The deal was for a 20 percent premium to Ariba’s stock price, and more than six times the usual multiple of earnings for an enterprise software acquisition. For a deal like that to make sense, SAP must have been thinking about ways Ariba could create new strategic businesses for the company. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/technology/02bits-sap/02bits-sap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 510, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/technology/02bits-sap/02bits-sap-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 510, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/technology/02bits-sap/02bits-sap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/02/technology/02bits-sap/02bits-sap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/technology/02bits-sap/02bits-sap-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 0, 'width': 0, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'SAP’s Marketplace Dream', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARIBA INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SAP AG', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T22:10:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90c92d2d-a29a-5c0c-8829-75b099afaa38', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90c92d2d-a29a-5c0c-8829-75b099afaa38'}, {'abstract': 'John Pizzarelli and Jessica Molaskey’s new show, “This Must Be the Place?,” explores the concept of home with an awareness that its solidity is illusory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/arts/music/john-pizzarelli-and-jessica-molaskey-at-cafe-carlyle.html', 'snippet': 'John Pizzarelli and Jessica Molaskey’s new show, “This Must Be the Place?,” explores the concept of home with an awareness that its solidity is illusory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Why does the title of John Pizzarelli and Jessica Molaskey’s brilliant new show, “This Must Be the Place?” (that’s the Talking Heads song with new punctuation), end with a question mark? That song, ingeniously wound around the Beatles’ “Two of Us,” led off this married couple’s opening-night program at the Café Carlyle on Wednesday evening. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/arts/03PIZZARELLI/03PIZZARELLI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 881, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/arts/03PIZZARELLI/03PIZZARELLI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1761, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/arts/03PIZZARELLI/03PIZZARELLI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/03/arts/03PIZZARELLI/03PIZZARELLI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/arts/03PIZZARELLI/03PIZZARELLI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Many Notions of Home, Redefined and Questioned in an Evening of Songs', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Many Notions of Home, Redefined and Questioned in an Evening of Songs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Molaskey, Jessica', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pizzarelli, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cafe Carlyle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-02T22:12:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b718773-8aa3-561f-b1bf-92ed518f72a0', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b718773-8aa3-561f-b1bf-92ed518f72a0'}, {'abstract': 'Richie Hawtin, a leading proponent of spooky-sounding techno, talks about the motivation for his unusual tour.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/taking-electronic-dance-music-to-both-college-campuses-and-clubs/', 'snippet': 'Richie Hawtin, a leading proponent of spooky-sounding techno, talks about the motivation for his unusual tour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the last week, the D.J. and producer Richie Hawtin has been traveling with an unusual tour: “CNTRL: Beyond E.D.M.,” which during the day visits college campuses for discussions about the past and present of electronic dance music (E.D.M.) and at night goes to clubs to show the music in action.', 'source':