: '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47c14b9c-7c63-5e52-8c54-258c8451ce59', 'word_count': 1139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47c14b9c-7c63-5e52-8c54-258c8451ce59'}, {'abstract': 'Four days after Hurricane Sandy, the major carriers — AT&T, Verizon Wireless, T-Mobile USA and Sprint — were still rebuilding their networks in the hardest-hit areas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/technology/cellphone-users-steaming-at-hit-or-miss-service.html', 'snippet': 'Four days after Hurricane Sandy, the major carriers — AT&T, Verizon Wireless, T-Mobile USA and Sprint — were still rebuilding their networks in the hardest-hit areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To wireless customers, cellphone networks might seem to be made out of thin air. But they are plenty vulnerable to catastrophic storms — and bringing service back can take an excruciatingly long time.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/business/CELL-1/CELL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/03/business/CELL-1/CELL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/business/CELL-1/CELL-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/business/CELL-1/CELL-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cellphone Users Steaming at Hit-or-Miss Service', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cellphone Users Steaming at Hit-or-Miss Service', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northeastern States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T00:39:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d842fb57-9896-5bcd-897e-423bb486f98a', 'word_count': 964, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d842fb57-9896-5bcd-897e-423bb486f98a'}, {'abstract': 'The main floor of the National September 11 Memorial Museum, still under construction nearly 70 feet below the memorial plaza at the World Trade Center, filled with at least seven feet of water.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/nyregion/floodwater-pours-into-9-11-museum-hampering-further-work-on-the-site.html', 'snippet': 'The main floor of the National September 11 Memorial Museum, still under construction nearly 70 feet below the memorial plaza at the World Trade Center, filled with at least seven feet of water.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The main floor of the National September 11 Memorial Museum, still under construction nearly 70 feet below the memorial plaza at the World Trade Center, filled with at least seven feet of water during the storm, its president said Friday. The flooding nearly immersed two fire trucks that have already been placed in the museum and it surrounded the symbolic last column taken from the twin towers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/nyregion/MEMORIAL/MEMORIAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/nyregion/MEMORIAL/MEMORIAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 842, 'width': 1263, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/nyregion/MEMORIAL/MEMORIAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/03/nyregion/MEMORIAL/MEMORIAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/nyregion/MEMORIAL/MEMORIAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Floodwater Pours Into 9/11 Museum, Hampering Further Work on the Site', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Floodwater Pours Into 9/11 Museum, Hampering Further Work on the Site', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National September 11 Memorial and Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T00:42:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/705eb470-a2a5-5b13-8756-396fd5d652c3', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/705eb470-a2a5-5b13-8756-396fd5d652c3'}, {'abstract': 'A running store closes — and with it, an era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/opinion/running-on-empty-an-american-sports-tradition-fades.html', 'snippet': 'A running store closes — and with it, an era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE announcement this week that Bill Rodgers would shutter his last running store, in Boston’s Faneuil Hall, was a sad farewell to a bygone era of great American runners. Rodgers was the four-time Boston Marathon and New York City Marathon winner and, along with Frank Shorter and Alberto Salazar, ruled the roads in the 1970s and early ’80s. (In large part because of their achievements, it is estimated that the New York City Marathon brings $340 million to the city, making its cancellation an economic — as well as an athletic — bust.)\xa0 Yet the men, like the store, are creaky with age, and no fountain of youth renews them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/opinion/1103oped-stracher-art/1103oped-stracher-art-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/opinion/1103oped-stracher-art/1103oped-stracher-art-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/02/opinion/1103oped-stracher-art/1103oped-stracher-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'wid