ar that offer is not on the table.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 2008 campaign offered voters a once-in-a-lifetime chance to make history. This year that offer is not on the table.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Face More Careworn, a Crowd Less Joyful', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T00:51:18+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/248bfa7d-c844-54df-a45f-4f362a5abb6e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/248bfa7d-c844-54df-a45f-4f362a5abb6e'}, {'abstract': 'Animal Kingdom, a Kentucky Derby winner who has been twice injured, will make his second start in 16 months in the Breeders’ Cup Mile.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/sports/animal-kingdom-to-end-long-time-off-in-breeders-cup-mile.html', 'snippet': 'Animal Kingdom, a Kentucky Derby winner who has been twice injured, will make his second start in 16 months in the Breeders’ Cup Mile.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARCADIA, Calif. — Animal Kingdom is a Kentucky Derby winner, a horse who has shown talent by winning races on dirt, turf and synthetic surfaces. He is tough, too. He fractured a hind leg in the 2011 Belmont Stakes and came back seven months later to win in Florida. In March, when he fractured his pelvis, most owners and trainers would have retired him.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'm