s or FEMA.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adam Goodman spent Friday afternoon threading his way up darkened staircases to reach older people stranded by power failures in the high-rises of Midtown East. Maribeth Dono baked banana bread and cupcakes for a Girl Scouts bake sale to benefit a shelter in Park Slope, Brooklyn. Tammy Shapiro helped manage a swirl of volunteers arriving at a relief distribution center in Sunset Park, Brooklyn, sending them out to battered neighborhoods.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/nyregion/HELP1-sub/HELP1-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/03/nyregion/HELP1-sub/HELP1-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/nyregion/HELP1-sub/HELP1-sub-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/nyregion/HELP1-sub/HELP1-sub-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/nyregion/HELP1-sub/HELP1-sub-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/03/nyregion/HELP1-sub/HELP1-sub-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/nyregion/HELP1-sub/HELP1-sub-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Relief Efforts of All Sizes and Forms Spring Up Across New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Relief Efforts of All Sizes and Forms Spring Up Across New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN RED CROSS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volunteers and Community Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Emergency Management Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T01:08:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon Otterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69144dc9-e577-5e02-abf4-46f104a64655', 'word_count': 893, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69144dc9-e577-5e02-abf4-46f104a64655'}, {'abstract': 'The trend in unemployment is promising, but the politics of job creation remain clouded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/opinion/jobs-are-growing-not-stagnating.html', 'snippet': 'The trend in unemployment is promising, but the politics of job creation remain clouded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, when the unemployment rate dropped by three-tenths of a percentage point to dip below 8 percent for the first time in 43 months, Mitt Romney dismissed the drop as meaningless. Some Republicans said federal officials manipulated the numbers to help President Obama win re-election. This month, when the jobless rate went up by a smaller amount, Mr. Romney took it as gospel, proof that Mr. Obama’s policies are a failure. Last month, Mr. Romney focused on a reduction in the work force. This month, he would not admit that the work force had expanded.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jobs Are Growing, Not Stagnating', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jobs Are Growing, Not Stagnating', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T01:10:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e44a1d5-5b5d-515d-b60c-f8ac7c5a4adf', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e44a1d5-5b5d-515d-b60c-f8ac7c5a4adf'}, {'abstract': 'New York has nothing to prove, and officials made the right decision to cancel the marathon after Hurricane Sandy, although it was 72 hours too late.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/sports/george-vecsey-canceling-the-marathon-was-the-right-thing-to-do.html', 'snippet': 'New York has nothing to prove, and officials made the right decision to cancel the marathon after Hurricane Sandy, although it was 72 hours too late.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The right decision, to call off the New York City Marathon, was only 72 hours late. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Tim