n newspaper, his Taurus PT145 pistol ready for action against any sudden attack by the eggs and burgers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oklahomans Packing Heat', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oklahomans Packing Heat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T01:22:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9aed5272-c228-520f-a000-47d92ebdc14e', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9aed5272-c228-520f-a000-47d92ebdc14e'}, {'abstract': 'A state scientist says that a department involved in a lawsuit over the effects of fracking on drinking water did not request full test results.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/us/pennsylvania-omitted-poison-data-in-water-report.html', 'snippet': 'A state scientist says that a department involved in a lawsuit over the effects of fracking on drinking water did not request full test results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — Pennsylvania officials reported incomplete test results that omitted data on some toxic metals that were found in drinking water taken from a private well near a natural gas drilling site, according to legal documents released this week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/us/PENNSYLVANIA/PENNSYLVANIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 648, 'width': 1024, '