 Thursday, compared with the same period last year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/nyregion/a-rise-in-burglary-reports-follows-storm.html', 'snippet': 'Many are arrested in the looting of stores since Hurricane Sandy hit, a 7 percent rise in burglary complaints from Monday through Thursday, compared with the same period last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the night that Hurricane Sandy hit New York, burglars broke into Kixclusive, a shoe store on the Lower East Side where rare pairs of basketball shoes are priced as high as $1,400. The proprietor told the police that 30 pairs of sneakers were stolen, saying the shoes were worth $30,000 in all, according to the police.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Burglaries Are Up After Storm, City Police Say, While Other Crimes Have Dropped', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Burglaries Are Up After Storm, City Police Say, While Other Crimes Have Dropped', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Looting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T01:41:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d8e4c97-317d-5382-a332-8785852f6e36', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d8e4c97-317d-5382-a332-8785852f6e36'}, {'abstract': 'While other college assistant coaches tend to move around to new jobs, Gary Campbell has stayed at Oregon for three decades, in part because of his son.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/sports/ncaafootball/gary-campbell-keeps-coaching-oregons-running-backs.html', 'snippet': 'While other college assistant coaches tend to move around to new jobs, Gary Campbell has stayed at Oregon for three decades, in part because of his son.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EUGENE, Ore. — Gary Campbell is the longest-tenured assistant coach at one university in major college football, at least as far as Oregon can tell. He arrived here in 1983 with an itinerant reputation, yet he has stayed, not for one, not for two, not for 10 seasons, but for 30 — three decades spent in the same place.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/DUCKS/DUCKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/DUCKS/DUCKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/DUCKS/DUCKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/DUCKS/DUCKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Staying at Oregon, and Happy About It', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Staying Put, And Happy About It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Oregon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'nam