a glided to victory at Santa Anita Park, Hall of Famer Mike Smith became the winningest jockey in the history of the Breeders’ Cup event.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARCADIA, Calif. — She made it look easy. Again. Royal Delta hit the stretch, and there wasn’t a soul in the grandstands of Santa Anita Park who doubted that she was on her way to a second consecutive victory in the Breeders’ Cup Ladies’ Classic.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Smith Guides Royal Delta to Ladies’ Classic Win', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smith Guides Royal Delta to Ladies’ Classic Win', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jockeys, Drivers and Trainers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Breeders' Cup (Horse Races)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Records and Achievements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T02:06:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b69b71c-6067-5369-ac5f-7d83ac15b1f1', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b69b71c-6067-5369-ac5f-7d83ac15b1f1'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks have one of the oldest lineups ever assembled in the N.B.A., while last season’s bright young star, Jeremy Lin, is playing elsewhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/sports/basketball/knicks-begin-season-devoid-of-jeremy-lin-and-youth.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks have one of the oldest lineups ever assembled in the N.B.A., while last season’s bright young star, Jeremy Lin, is playing elsewhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In early May at Madison Square Garden, just six months ago, it is not true that one-half of all the Knicks fans attending the first-round playoff games wore Jeremy Lin jerseys. It only seemed that way.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/PENNINGTON-1351902425502/PENNINGTON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/PENNINGTON-1351902425502/PENNINGTON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Knicks Begin Season Scrubbed of Lin and Youth', 'kicker': 'On Pro Basketball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knicks Begin Season\r\nScrubbed of Lin\r\nAnd Youth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': "Stoudemire, Amar'e", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lin, Jeremy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T02:06:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/613f7465-7135-5ae4-b6a6-3fe50b179c4b', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/613f7465-7135-5ae4-b6a6-3fe50b179c4b'}, {'abstract': 'There was destruction all along the New Jersey coastline, longtime restaurants and beach clubs face long and costly repairs, but the residents have an overwhelming belief that the area will come back stronger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/nyregion/at-the-jersey-shore-a-shared-determination-to-rebuild-and-restore.html', 'snippet': 'There was destruction all along the New Jersey coastline, longtime restaurants and beach clubs face long and costly repairs, but the residents have an overwhelming belief that the area will come back stronger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'POINT PLEASANT BEACH, N.J. — John Schaad, 53 a longtime Jersey Shore resident, was staring out to the sea and looking shellshocked on the Boardwalk just across from what is known as the Sinatra House, where the sounds of big-band music waft into the air all summer long as an endless parade of people sashay by.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Shared Determination to Rebuild and Restore the Jersey Shore', 'kicker': 'Point Pleasant Beach Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Shared Determination to Rebuild and Restore the Jersey Shore', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seaside Heights (NJ)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaches', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlantic City (NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sea Bright (NJ)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cape May (NJ)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T02:10:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Applebome', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Applebome', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/baef3e20-9c26-5edb-afe6-34806b0caf2b', 'word_count': 1080, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baef3e20-9c26-5edb-afe6-34806b0caf2b'}, {'abstract': 'Here are some ideas for New York to think about after Hurricane Sandy, especially if the city wants to better protect itself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/opinion/nocera-mayor-bloombergs-barrier.html', 'snippet': 'Here are some ideas for New York to think about after Hurricane Sandy, especially if the city wants to better protect itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of my enduring childhood memories is going with my mother to the lobby of The Providence Journal, where she had once worked, to see the high water mark of the fearsome 1938 hurricane. It was the worst storm that had ever been recorded in New England, with winds of 115 miles per hour and a storm surge 16 feet high. Parts of Providence were 8 feet under water. Nearly 400 Rhode Islanders died.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty