otice. Don’t get me wrong — some of my best friends are fans of detective fiction in all its forms. But I’ve always found it silly: A character I don’t know or care about dies at the start, a series of shifty but ultimately innocent suspects leads me astray in the middle, and a ridiculously far-fetched solution leaves me feeling like I’ve been had at the end.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/nyregion/04ARTSCT2/04ARTSCT2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/nyregion/04ARTSCT2/04ARTSCT2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/nyregion/04ARTSCT2/04ARTSCT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/04/nyregion/04ARTSCT2/04ARTSCT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/nyregion/04ARTSCT2/04ARTSCT2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking for Clues, and Laughs', 'kicker': 'Arts | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking for Clues, And Laughs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goodspeed Opera House', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Haddam (Conn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T02:25:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylviane Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylviane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b11782b-0d7a-53b6-8bd8-f04f77187930', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b11782b-0d7a-53b6-8bd8-f04f77187930'}, {'abstract': 'Among those killed on Monday was Ricardo Tochimani, but his name appears on no list of storm casualties. It stands alone, a homicide, and the identity of his killers remains a mystery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/nyregion/one-death-hurricane-sandy-didnt-cause.html', 'snippet': 'Among those killed on Monday was Ricardo Tochimani, but his name appears on no list of storm casualties. It stands alone, a homicide, and the identity of his killers remains a mystery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was in the wee hours on Monday, and the whole city seemed to be looking east, toward the incoming Hurricane Sandy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/07/18/multimedia/author-michael-wilson/author-michael-wilson-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/07/18/multimedia/author-michael-wilson/author-michael-wilson-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/07/18/multimedia/author-michael-wilson/author-michael-wilson-jumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', '