41e36e0429', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31f07ca6-c069-589a-832b-2741e36e0429'}, {'abstract': 'Pascual Perez, who was killed this week in the Dominican Republic, could pitch brilliantly when he wasn’t incarcerated or hampered by bad spirits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/sports/baseball/pitcher-pascual-perez-was-known-for-his-quirks.html', 'snippet': 'Pascual Perez, who was killed this week in the Dominican Republic, could pitch brilliantly when he wasn’t incarcerated or hampered by bad spirits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Baseball history is full of eccentrics. Jimmy Piersall once ran the bases backward to celebrate a home run. Mark Fidrych chatted with the ball as if he expected a conversation to break out. Dock Ellis pitched under the influence of LSD. Bill Lee’s nickname, the Spaceman, suggested his out-thereness. And Yogi Berra became a quotable guru without even trying.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/subYPEREZ/subYPEREZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 558, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/subYPEREZ/subYPEREZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1116, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/subYPEREZ/subYPEREZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/subYPEREZ/subYPEREZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/subYPEREZ/