document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Applebome', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Applebome', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a22a323-abbb-56dc-9039-c03b62e256a4', 'word_count': 1405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a22a323-abbb-56dc-9039-c03b62e256a4'}, {'abstract': 'New “super PACs” have sprung up in the last days of the race, buying up advertising and exploiting a loophole that keeps their donors anonymous until long after votes are counted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/us/politics/new-super-pacs-add-to-last-minute-rush-of-spending.html', 'snippet': 'New “super PACs” have sprung up in the last days of the race, buying up advertising and exploiting a loophole that keeps their donors anonymous until long after votes are counted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In mid-October, a Republican lawyer in Washington sent paperwork overnight to the Federal Election Commission forming a new “super PAC” called Freedom Fund North America. The group did nothing for more than a week, until the last deadline passed for publicly disclosing donors before Election Day. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Super PACs Provide Last-Minute Rush of Campaign Spending', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Last-Minute Rush of Campaign Spending With Murky Origins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T02:58:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore and Derek Willis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Willis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f7142e0-861d-5bbe-a4d1-6e5b2f6e46fd', 'word_count': 999, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f7142e0-861d-5bbe-a4d1-6e5b2f6e46fd'}, {'abstract': 'A ban on financial transactions with Iran has inadvertently affected critical supplies that are exempted from Western sanctions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/world/middleeast/iran-sanctions-take-toll-on-medical-imports.html', 'snippet': 'A ban on financial transactions with Iran has inadvertently affected critical supplies that are exempted from Western sanctions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Sitting on one of the many crowded benches in the waiting room of the International Red Crescent’s pharmacy in central Tehran, Ali, 26, was working his phone. After nearly six weeks of chasing down batches of Herceptin, an American-made cancer medicine, Ali, an engineer, was wearing out his welcome with friends and relatives in other Iranian cities, who had done all they could to rustle up the increasingly elusive drug.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/world/sanctions/sanctions-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/world/sanctions/sanctions-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Sanctions Take Unexpected Toll on Medical Imports', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran Sanctions Take Unexpected Toll on Medical Imports', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Herceptin (Drug)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shortages', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T03:06:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/450b737d-2094-50f9-a603-726a1c6aceaa', 'word_count': 1251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/450b737d-2094-50f9-a603-726a1c6aceaa'}, {'abstract': 'NASA’s rover Curiosity has come up empty in its search for the gas methane on the red planet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/science/space/hopes-for-methane-on-mars-deflated.html', 'snippet': 'NASA’s rover Curiosity has come up empty in its search for the gas methane on the red planet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deflating, at least for now, hopes of microbial life forms inhabiting the soils of Mars, NASA’s rover Curiosity has so far come up empty in its search for the gas methane. At a NASA news conference on Friday, scientists reported that the Mars rover’s instruments had seen no signs of methane, which, had it been there, would have signaled that there might currently be methane-exhaling microorganisms on Mars that are similar to those found on Earth. In Martian air, methane molecules are broken down by sunlight and chemical reactions within a few hundred years. Thus, when three teams of scientists reported in 2004 that they had detected methane there, it raised the possibility that something on present-day Mars was creating methane, and the most exciting possibility was tiny life forms.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hope of Methane on Mars Fades', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Science', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hope Of Methane On Mars Fades', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mars (Planet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Curiosity (Mars Rover)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Methane', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T03:06:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/71d8cc89-0daa-5498-9d14-b3e0254319ef', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71d8cc89-0daa-5498-9d14-b3e0254319ef'}, {'abstract': 'Robin Van Persie has continued his impressive goalscoring form since moving to Manchester United, but has United become as reliant on him as Arsenal was often perceived to be?', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/02/van-persie-is-the-same-but-which-team-is-better/', 'snippet': 'Robin Van Persie has continued his impressive goalscoring form since moving to Manchester United, but has United become as reliant on him as Arsenal was often perceived to be?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Robin Van Persie, Old Trafford was once an unforgiving place. As an Arsenal player the Dutchman never sampled victory at Manchester United’s Theatre of Dreams. United’s unbeaten home run against Arsene Wenger’s side dates to 2006; in fact, the Gunners sustained their biggest Premier League defeat the last time they visited.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Van Persie Is the Same, but Which Team Is Better?', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T03:09:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By GRAHAM RUTHVEN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'RUTHVEN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72bcc21c-c84f-554c-893c-440c887269be', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72bcc21c-c84f-554c-893c-440c887269be'}, {'abstract': 'After their season opener had been delayed by Hurricane Sandy, Carmelo Anthony and the Knicks were fueled by the home crowd as they took an early lead against the Heat and never looked back.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/sports/basketball/knicks-beat-heat-to-provide-new-york-a-reason-to-cheer.html', 'snippet': 'After their season opener had been delayed by Hurricane Sandy, Carmelo Anthony and the Knicks were fueled by the home crowd as they took an early lead against the Heat and never looked back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Returning to Madison Square Garden was supposed to be a marquee event for the Knicks. The N.B.A. scheduled it that way, with LeBron James and his Miami Heat, the defending champions, in New York on the first Friday night of November.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/JPKNICKS/JPKNICKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 673, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/JPKNICKS/JPKNICKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1346, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/JPKNICKS/JPKNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/JPKNICKS/JPKNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/sports/JPKNICKS/JPKNICKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Anthony Sets Tone as Knicks Provide a Reason to Cheer', 'kicker': 'Knicks 104, Heat 84', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Anthony Sets Tone as Knicks Provide a Reason to Cheer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'ra