 Harrison Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Harrison', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aad34541-fc12-5453-bf6f-497ea5523638', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aad34541-fc12-5453-bf6f-497ea5523638'}, {'abstract': 'More betting on tennis matches is leading to increased vitriol in social media.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/online-abuse-and-betting-go-hand-in-hand/', 'snippet': 'More betting on tennis matches is leading to increased vitriol in social media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just six points from defeat against the qualifier Jerzy Janowicz in the quarterfinals of the Paris Masters on Friday, ninth-ranked Janko Tipsarevic retired due to what was later cited as “sudden fatigue,” pulling the ripcord and giving Janowicz an anticlimactic 3-6, 6-1, 4-1 win. Tipsarevic had been visited by a doctor on the previous changeover, and was booed by the French crowd both as he walked to the net and off the court.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Online Abuse and Betting Go Hand in Hand', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T04:02:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By BEN ROTHENBERG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ROTHENBERG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a5dcfd3-a707-5e69-a34a-2fbd4f4732a0', 'word_count': 683, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a5dcfd3-a707-5e69-a34a-2fbd4f4732a0'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate’s future is being decided largely beyond the focus of the presidential contest, in states like North Dakota and Indiana where neither presidential candidate has campaigned.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/us/politics/senate-races-get-little-lift-from-obama-and-romney.html', 'snippet': 'The Senate’s future is being decided largely beyond the focus of the presidential contest, in states like North Dakota and Indiana where neither presidential candidate has campaigned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As Mitt Romney and President Obama close out their campaigns, the elections for control of the Senate are taking place across a different set of states, with neither presidential candidate providing coattails to ensure that his agenda will have strong support in Congress’s upper chamber.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/us/COATTAILS-3/COATTAILS-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/us/COATTAILS-3/COATTAILS-3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Candidates See Little Coattail Effect', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senate Candidates Find Coattails in Presidential Race Don’t Extend Very Far', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berg, Richard Alan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donnelly, Joseph Simon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mourdock, Richard E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Dakota', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montana', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heitkamp, Heidi', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T04:02:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37e45c11-902d-52a2-84cb-d134083e4f75', 'word_count': 972, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37e45c11-902d-52a2-84cb-d134083e4f75'}, {'abstract': 'A member of the band Pussy Riot said Friday that the band’s name should not be used for commercial gain after it was revealed that the wife of the band’s lawyer had applied for a patent to register the name as a trademark.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/world/europe/russian-band-in-trademark-dispute.html', 'snippet': 'A member of the band Pussy Riot said Friday that the band’s name should not be used for commercial gain after it was revealed that the wife of the band’s lawyer had applied for a patent to register the name as a trademark.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A member of the band Pussy Riot said Friday that the band’s name should not be used for commercial gain after it was revealed that the wife of the band’s lawyer had applied for a patent to register the name as a trademark. “This simply shocks me; I am completely surprised,” the band member, Yekaterina Samutsevich, who was released from prison last month on bail, told the radio station Kommersant FM. She said she and her two band mates, who remain in prison, had agreed that they should protect their intellectual property rights, but opposed commercial use of their name. The lawyer, Mark Feygin, denied that he or his wife, who owns a film production company, were trying to profit from the band, and he said they filed the application in April at the request of the three band members “to prevent someone from producing condoms and pornography films” featuring the band’s name. But Russia’s patent office rejected the trademark application. Also on Friday, Prime Minister Dmitri A. Medvedev said again that he thought the jailed band members should be released, The Associated Press reported. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russian Band in Trademark Dispute', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Band in Trademark Dispute', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samutsevich, Yekaterina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pussy Riot', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trademarks and Trade Names', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T04:04:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Kordunsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kordunsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3a308d3-4c69-5306-9835-cd1b69bb1887', 'word_count': 185, 