'value': 'Connecticut Light and Power', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T13:44:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9588e86-2494-580e-8945-90b58c5769fe', 'word_count': 1263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9588e86-2494-580e-8945-90b58c5769fe'}, {'abstract': 'And other supply-side myths.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/soup-kitchens-caused-the-great-depression/', 'snippet': 'And other supply-side myths.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some readers have been asking me to reply to Casey Mulligan’s latest attack on my recent book. Um, no. Life is short, and if I spent my time responding to every attack on yours truly — or indeed, every thing Mulligan himself writes that I consider foolish — I would have no time to do anything else. So let me just outsource this to John Quiggin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Soup Kitchens Caused the Great Depression', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T13:44:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/297c03d0-2c39-5e56-8b40-809e3f16aca8', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/297c03d0-2c39-5e56-8b40-809e3f16aca8'}, {'abstract': 'Games like L.S.U. versus Alabama create a quandary for scouts: how much weight should be put on one game compared with a player’s body of work?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/sports/ncaafootball/alabama-vs-lsu-is-where-pro-prospects-meet.html', 'snippet': 'Games like L.S.U. versus Alabama create a quandary for scouts: how much weight should be put on one game compared with a player’s body of work?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the N.F.L. scout’s cosmos, there cannot be a more perfect game than Saturday night’s matchup of Alabama versus Louisiana State. The two programs have produced 11 first-round picks in the last two N.F.L. drafts — eight by Alabama — and there will be at least 56 players in the game who could wear N.F.L. jerseys before their football careers are over, according to scouts and staff who are familiar with the two-deep depth charts for both programs. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/sports/YPROSPECTS2/YPROSPECTS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/sports/YPROSPECTS2/YPROSPECTS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/sports/YPROSPECTS2/YPROSPECTS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/04/sports/YPROSPECTS2/YPROSPECTS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/sports/YPROSPECTS2/YPROSPECTS2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Big Game Doesn’t Mean the Only Game', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Big Game Doesn&#8217;t Mean The Only Game', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louisiana State University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T13:54:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ray Glier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78176942-187f-5f95-b0e2-c3f041447791', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78176942-187f-5f95-b0e2-c3f041447791'}, {'abstract': 'For the nine men in Marie-Agnès Gillot’s new “Sous Apparence,” learning the dance has been a crash course in the daily life of their female colleagues: blisters, pain and point-shoe-taming.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/men-in-point-shoes/', 'snippet': 'For the nine men in Marie-Agnès Gillot’s new “Sous Apparence,” learning the dance has been a crash course in the daily life of their female colleagues: blisters, pain and point-shoe-taming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS—Marie-Agnès Gillot’s new “Sous Apparence,” which opened at the Palais Garnier on Wednesday night, has no shortage of strange features—dancing trees, indefinable bubble-shaped creatures and mysterious sculptural objects. But one particularity takes a while to sink in: The men, as well as the women, are on point for the entire piece.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/arts/03rdv-point/03rdv-point-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/arts/03rdv-point/03rdv-point-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Men in Point Shoes', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T14:31:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd9a7dca-7a37-5e02-9dbf-16177e20f3ee', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd9a7dca-7a37-5e02-9dbf-16177e20f3ee'}, {'abstract': 'In the Soviet era, the health of Kremlin leaders was regarded as a state secret. Now, under the presidency of Vladimir V. Putin, an official has criticized the press for asking too many questions about the Russian leader’s sore back.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/health-concerns-for-russias-alpha-dog/', 'snippet': 'In the Soviet era, the health of Kremlin leaders was regarded as a state secret. Now, under the presidency of Vladimir V. Putin, an official has criticized the press for asking too many questions about the Russian leader’s sore back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The news from Russia this week has been mostly about President Vladimir V. Putin’s sore back.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/blogs/03rdv-putin/03rdv-putin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/blogs/03rdv-putin/03rdv-putin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1285, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Concerns for Russia’s Alpha Dog', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T14:46:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80a6b19f-e77e-56e5-8400-853be5058389', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80a6b19f-e77e-56e5-8400-853be5058389'}, {'abstract': 'Contrary to perception, operation of game clocks at N.F.L. stadiums is handled by employees of the league, not hometown timekeepers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/sports/football/in-the-nfls-game-of-beat-the-clock-time-is-on-no-ones-side.html', 'snippet': 'Cont