:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Huguenin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huguenin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67cad148-a096-5169-a513-7f991470a416', 'word_count': 4355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67cad148-a096-5169-a513-7f991470a416'}, {'abstract': 'The responses from the runners have ranged from anger to disappointment to understanding to relief to disbelief.', 'web_url': 'https://marathon.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/runners-react-to-canceled-marathon/', 'snippet': 'The responses from the runners have ranged from anger to disappointment to understanding to relief to disbelief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After days of intensifying pressure from runners, politicians and the general public to call off the New York City Marathon in the wake of Hurricane Sandy, city officials and the event’s organizers decided Friday afternoon to cancel the race. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Runners React to Canceled Marathon', 'kicker': 'On the Run', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York City Marathon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T15:47:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0167736-dee0-58a6-8492-d0a40796425f', 'word_count': 66, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0167736-dee0-58a6-8492-d0a40796425f'}, {'abstract': 'Of the runners slated to compete in the New York City Marathon, the contenders — and those hoping to join them — felt the biggest financial loss.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/sports/no-nyc-marathon-means-no-prize-money.html', 'snippet': 'Of the runners slated to compete in the New York City Marathon, the contenders — and those hoping to join them — felt the biggest financial loss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tens of thousands of weekend warriors will return to their day jobs, having lost only travel costs and entry fees with the cancellation of the New York City Marathon. But contenders missed a chance to earn what amounted to half a year’s salary.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Contenders Miss Out on Chance for Big Payday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Contenders Miss Out on Chance for Big Payday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York City Marathon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wittenberg, Mary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marathon Running', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kiplagat, Edna', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keflezighi, Mebrahtom', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Road Runners Club', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T15:58:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87312d2d-31bf-5db7-a244-53240065