ht': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/04/sunday-review/04MEXICO/04MEXICO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/sunday-review/04MEXICO/04MEXICO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Mexico, a Deadly Warning', 'kicker': 'Exposures', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Mexico, A Deadly Warning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T18:30:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Víctor Hugo Ornelas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Víctor', 'middlename': 'Hugo', 'lastname': 'Ornelas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/15595afa-5cf8-58c3-bda3-729b4463304f', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15595afa-5cf8-58c3-bda3-729b4463304f'}, {'abstract': 'The program to enlist immigrants with special abilities in languages and medicine in exchange for citizenship should be expanded beyond the Army.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/opinion/sunday/the-militarys-swift-path-to-citizenship.html', 'snippet': 'The program to enlist immigrants with special abilities in languages and medicine in exchange for citizenship should be expanded beyond the Army.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pentagon has just restarted a program to enlist skilled immigrants into the Army, giving recruits a swift path to citizenship in return for their special abilities in languages and medicine. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Military’s Swift Path to Citizenship', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Military’s Swift Path to Citizenship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Military)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T18:35:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c46ecceb-35e8-5c54-92ed-d15a34e65752', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c46ecceb-35e8-5c54-92ed-d15a34e65752'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans have tried hard to disqualify millions of voters. A heavy turnout at the polls would send a strong message.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/opinion/sunday/voting-rights-upholding-democracy.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans have tried hard to disqualify millions of voters. A heavy turnout at the polls would send a strong message.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year, voting is more than just the core responsibility of citizenship; it is an act of defiance against malicious political forces determined to reduce access to democracy. Millions of ballots on Tuesday — along with those already turned in — will be cast despite the best efforts of Republican officials around the country to prevent them from playing a role in the 2012 election.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Upholding Democracy, Ballot by Ballot', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The Struggle to Cast a Vote', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Upholding Democracy, Ballot By Ballot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T18:36:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fd5bff1-ea28-5b7b-b8df-464b3c2039d3', 'word_count': 688, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fd5bff1-ea28-5b7b-b8df-464b3c2039d3'}, {'abstract': 'Denying the vote to people who have committed felonies but have completed their sentences offends fundamental tenets of democracy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/opinion/sunday/voting-rights-former-felons.html', 'snippet': 'Denying the vote to people who have committed felonies but have completed their sentences offends fundamental tenets of democracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States maintains a shortsighted and punitive set of laws, some of them dating back to Reconstruction, denying the vote to people who have committed felonies. They will bar about 5.85 million people from voting in this year’s election. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wrongly Turning Away Ex-Offenders', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The Struggle to Cast a Vote', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wrongly turning away ex-offenders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ex-Convicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sentencing Project', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T18:40:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/21e7ed47-1875-52d8-8699-1d751099baa6', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21e7ed47-1875-52d8-8699-1d751099baa6'}, {'abstract': 'If barriers are built to save Lower Manhattan, the water won’t just disappear. It will flood other neighborhoods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/opinion/sunday/deciding-where-future-disasters-will-strike.html', 'snippet': 'If barriers are built to save Lower Manhattan, the water won’t just disappear. It will flood other neighborhoods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WE all have an intuitive sense of how water works: block it, and it flows elsewhere. When a storm surge hits a flood barrier, for instance, the water does not simply dissipate. It does the hydrological equivalent of a bounce, and it lands somewhere else. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/sunday-review/04BRIDGE/04BRIDGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/04/sunday-review/04BRIDGE/04BRIDGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/sunday-review/04BRIDGE/04BRIDGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/sunday-review/04BRIDGE/04BRIDGE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/sunday-review/04BRIDGE/04BRIDGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/04/sunday-review/04BRIDGE/04BRIDGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/sunday-review/04BRIDGE/04BRIDGE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Deciding Where Future Disasters Will Strike', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deciding Where Future Disasters Will Strike', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Levees and Dams', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rotterdam (Netherlands)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T18:51:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By McKenzie Funk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mckenzie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Funk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b8d6a30-526b-5a42-aedd-7a5845d73e38', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b8d6a30-526b-5a42-aedd-7a5845d73e38'}, {'abstract': 'He was in jail, the hurricane was coming and he needed $500 for bail.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/what-do-i-owe-my-neighbor/', 'snippet': 'He was in jail, the hurricane was coming and he needed $500 for bail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sure, I had moved to Bedford-Stuyvesant, Brooklyn, as a white, middle-class woman from the Midwestern suburbs, and sure, I knew I was naïve, but I did not confront the reality of my own neighborhood, or myself, until I was asked, a week ago, to post bail for my neighbor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Do I Owe My Neighbor?', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rikers Island Prison Complex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T19:23:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hanna Pylvainen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pylvainen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e19f5c42-5342-53c3-8b56-916308e83565', 'word_count': 1534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e19f5c42-5342-53c3-8b56-916308e83565'}, {'abstract': 'We don’t get to use our names, but we do get to fight for our beliefs.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/the-political-speechwriters-life/', 'snippet': 'We don’t get to use our names, but we do get to fight for our beliefs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kurt Vonnegut once wrote that “only nut cases want to be president.” But he helped me become a White House speechwriter. In 1965, Vonnegut was my adviser at the University of Iowa Writers’ Workshop, where I was studying fiction. One day, he said he could get me an assistantship, but I’d have to teach speech.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Political Speechwriter’s Life', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reading and Writing Skills', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T19:24:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Lehrman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lehrman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cb9c82b-ae2e-5615-9219-56b55a82956f', 'word_count': 1188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cb9c82b-ae2e-5615-9219-56b55a82956f'}, {'abstract': 'The influential conservative pundit Glenn Beck has emerged as an unlikely theological bridge between the first Mormon presidential nominee and a critical electorate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/us/politics/beck-acts-as-a-bridge-between-romney-and-evangelical-christians.html', 'snippet': 'The influential conservative pundit Glenn Beck has emerged as an unlikely theological bridge between the first Mormon presidential nominee and a critical electorate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On radio and on his Internet network, the influential conservative pundit Glenn Beck frequently invokes God, religious freedom and the founding fathers, but he does not regularly discuss his own Mormon faith.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beck Acts as a Bridge Between Romney and Evangelical Christians', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beck Acts as a Bridge Between Romney and Evangelical Christians', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Glenn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mormons (Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evangelical Movement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T19:33:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4ec10fe-2d2f-5a38-8785-164399673888', 'word_count': 1376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4ec10fe-2d2f-5a38-8785-164399673888'}, {'abstract': 'The difficulty of finding gasoline persisted 