id Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. “He wants to turn that clock back so desperately. This time he can really do it tonight.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARVADA, Colo. – Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. took a few last swings at Mitt Romney in Colorado during two stops on Saturday before heading to a final stretch of campaigning in a pair of other crucial swing states, Virginia and Ohio, telling a crowd of 900 at a suburban Denver high school that while the Republican presidential nominee is a “decent” man, he is also “absolutely shameless” and has shown he lacks the character required of a president by preying upon the fears of desperate and worried Americans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden Takes a Daylight Saving Time-Themed Swipe at Romney', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T23:28:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf4e3b75-fb51-5467-9a93-c09085656b56', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf4e3b75-fb51-5467-9a93-c09085656b56'}, {'abstract': 'Many of the supplies for the marathon, such as blankets and water, are being donated to storm victims.', 'web_url': 'https://marathon.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/bloomberg-doesnt-apologize-doesnt-explain/', 'snippet': 'Many of the supplies for the marathon, such as blankets and water, are being donated to storm victims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A day after he yielded to mounting pressure to cancel the New York City Marathon, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg declined to say why he had waited until less than 48 hours before the race to call it off.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg Doesn’t Apologize, Doesn’t Explain', 'kicker': 'On the Run', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York City Marathon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Road Runners Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T23:28:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson and Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82288062-0ca0-5ee5-b2b0-6a832589c892', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82288062-0ca0-5ee5-b2b0-6a832589c892'}, {'abstract': 'Some business owners managed to open their doors even without electricity as residents pummeled by Hurricane Sandy sought out gasoline, food and other after-storm necessities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/11/03/business/BACKDROP.html', 'snippet': 'Some business owners managed to open their doors even without electricity as residents pummeled by Hurricane Sandy sought out gasoline, food and other after-storm necessities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some business owners managed to open their doors even without electricity as residents pummeled by Hurricane Sandy sought out gasoline, food and other after-storm necessities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/business/BACKDROP-slide-0PRX/BACKDROP-slide-0PRX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/business/BACKDROP-slide-0PRX/BACKDROP-slide-0PRX-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1197, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/business/BACKDROP-slide-0PRX/BACKDROP-slide-0PRX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/03/business/BACKDROP-slide-0PRX/BACKDROP-slide-0PRX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/business/BACKDROP-slide-0PRX/BACKDROP-slide-0PRX-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Power or Without, Commerce Must Go On', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T23:39:10+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ba0563ff-0cef-59f2-9fdd-425b659a8992', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ba0563ff-0cef-59f2-9fdd-425b659a8992'}, {'abstract': 'In the aftermath of Hurricane Sandy, James L. Dolan, the normally silent Knicks’ owner, opened up to members of the news media for about a minute.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/dolan-speaks/', 'snippet': 'In the aftermath of Hurricane Sandy, James L. Dolan, the normally silent Knicks’ owner, opened up to members of the news media for about a minute.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James L. Dolan, the owner of the Knicks, wanted to speak to the members of the news media who cover the team. He hadn’t done so in more than five years, yet he felt this was the right time — a decision that was spontaneous and surprised the group of reporters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knicks’ Dolan Speaks', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dolan, James L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-03T23:46:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3877a329-8b96-5e2a-9839-bc651e64eaff', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3877a329-8b96-5e2a-9839-bc651e64eaff'}, {'abstract': 'There had been minor doubts about Mariano Rivera’s return to the Yankees, but on Friday the pitcher informed General Manager Brian Cashman that he would indeed return.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/sports/baseball/yankees-and-rivera-working-toward-deal.html', 'snippet': 'There had been minor doubts about Mariano Rivera’s return to the Yankees, but on Friday the pitcher informed General Manager Brian Cashman that he would indeed return.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The day after Mariano Rivera sustained a season-ending knee injury on May 3, he vowed he would pitch again in 2013 at age 43. He also said he would continue to shag fly balls in batting practice, which was how he injured the knee.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Doubts for Rivera and Yankees', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Doubts For Rivera And Yankees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Mariano', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cashman, Brian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T00:18:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dccc23e9-3fd8-55c8-8217-6b6cb6099e16', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dccc23e9-3fd8-55c8-8217-6b6cb6099e16'}, {'abstract': 'It might be hard for the Knicks to sustain the type of effective ball movement they displayed on Friday against the Heat, but it could benefit the team on both sides of the court this season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/sports/basketball/sharp-passing-in-opener-against-heat-may-bode-well-for-knicks.html', 'snippet': 'It might be hard for the Knicks to sustain the type of effective ball movement they displayed on Friday against the Heat, but it could benefit the team on both sides of the court this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREENBURGH, N.Y. — Steve Novak rotated around the 3-point arc. A machine under one of the baskets at the Knicks’ practice center fed him pass after pass, and Novak fired open 3-pointer after open 3-pointer. He made more than he missed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/sports/YKNICKS/YKNICKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 934, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/sports/YKNICKS/YKNICKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1656, 'width': 1510, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/sports/YKNICKS/YKNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/04/sports/YKNICKS/YKNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/sports/YKNICKS/YKNICKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'mai