080-b1ba-510b-a3af-9853e696883d', 'word_count': 1303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6aae7080-b1ba-510b-a3af-9853e696883d'}, {'abstract': 'A Des Moines Register poll released Saturday evening found President Obama with a lead over Mitt Romney, 47 percent to 42 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/obama-up-by-5-points-in-iowa-des-moines-register-poll-finds/', 'snippet': 'A Des Moines Register poll released Saturday evening found President Obama with a lead over Mitt Romney, 47 percent to 42 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Iowa is at the center of President Obama’s and Mitt Romney’s dueling strategies for victory, and the president holds a narrow edge over Mr. Romney there, according to a Des Moines Register poll released Saturday evening, which found Mr. Obama with 47 percent, to 42 percent for Mr. Romney.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Up by 5 Points in Iowa, Des Moines Register Poll Finds', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Des Moines Register', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T01:17:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50bd85e9-9568-57aa-9cab-4a9d75dfacb4', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50bd85e9-9568-57aa-9cab-4a9d75dfacb4'}, {'abstract': 'Among the day’s best in college football, the senior receiver Cobi Hamilton set Arkansas’s single-season receptions record.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/college-football-around-the-country-7/', 'snippet': 'Among the day’s best in college football, the senior receiver Cobi Hamilton set Arkansas’s single-season receptions record.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COBI HAMILTON The senior\xa0 set Arkansas’s single-season receptions record as the Razorbacks rallied for a 19-15 win over Tulsa. Hamilton finished with 11 catches for 177 yards and now has 69 receptions for 1,077 yards this season. He is just 40 yards behind the team’s single-season yards record.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'College Football Around the Country', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Around The Country: The Day’s Best', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T01:23:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0af84d1-8a41-5804-82ad-912abc6eac70', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0af84d1-8a41-5804-82ad-912abc6eac70'}, {'abstract': 'Shanghai Bobby, undefeated in five starts, held off He’s Had Enough to win the Juvenile and allow Rosie Napravnik to join Julie Krone as the only female jockeys to win Breeders’ Cup races.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/sports/shanghai-bobby-and-jockey-rosie-napravnik-win-at-breeders-cup.html', 'snippet': 'Shanghai Bobby, undefeated in five starts, held off He’s Had Enough to win the Juvenile and allow Rosie Napravnik to join Julie Krone as the only female jockeys to win Breeders’ Cup races.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARCADIA, Calif. — Rosie Napravnik was warming up Shanghai Bobby before his career debut April 19 at Aqueduct Racetrack when she sensed that something about him was different from other horses she had ridden since she became a jockey in 2005. She remembered that it was more a powerful feeling than anything she could pinpoint.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unbeaten Shanghai Bobby Adds Breeders’ Cup Win', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unbeaten Shanghai Bobby Adds Breeders’ Cup Win', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Breeders' Cup (Horse Races)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Napravnik, Rosie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jockeys, Drivers and Trainers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T01:28:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Pedulla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pedulla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/110a5034-e982-5dcd-9e95-b7221295061a', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/110a5034-e982-5dcd-9e95-b7221295061a'}, {'abstract': 'Yoselyn Ortega, 50, who was accused of stabbing two children under her care in their apartment, was interviewed by the police at her bedside in the hospital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/nyregion/upper-west-side-nanny-is-charged-with-murder.html', 'snippet': 'Yoselyn Ortega, 50, who was accused of stabbing two children under her care in their apartment, was interviewed by the police at her bedside in the hospital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A nanny accused of killing the two young children she was caring for on Oct. 25 in their Upper West Side apartment was charged on Saturday night with first-degree murder, the police said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Upper West Side Nanny Is Charged With Murder in 2 Children’s Deaths', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Upper West Side Nanny Is Charged With Murder in 2 Children’s Deaths', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krim, Lucia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ortega, Yoselyn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krim, Leo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T01:31:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c11bf2fa-8901-5160-b4bc-76552c5f5319', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c11bf2fa-8901-5160-b4bc-76552c5f5319'}, {'abstract': 'With only sporadic access to text messaging and the Web, many in Hurricane Sandy’s no-power zone quickly cobbled together systems for passing along information and arranging when and where to meet.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/03/how-new-yorkers-adjusted-to-sudden-smartphone-withdrawal/', 'snippet': 'With only sporadic access to text messaging and the Web, many in Hurricane Sandy’s no-power zone quickly cobbled together systems for passing along information and arranging when and where to meet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While Hurricane Sandy left hundreds of thousands of New Yorkers without electricity or heat, the loss of one utility left some especially bewildered: cellphone service.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/technology/05social-pic/05social-pic-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 565, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/technology/05social-pic/05social-pic-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1130, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/technology/05social-pic/05social-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/05/technology/05social-pic/05social-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/technology/05social-pic/05social-pic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How New Yorkers Adjusted to Sudden Smartphone Withdrawal', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Life Goes On Without Cellphones in the No-Power Zone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T01:33:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3b165ec-13ce-590d-8824-2d3f70d75936', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3b165ec-13ce-590d-8824-2d3f70d75936'}, {'abstract': 'A vessel of timber and lore was hammered by the hurricane, and the captain has not been found.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/us/evoking-18th-century-drama-bounty-finds-storm-tragedy.html', 'snippet': 'A vessel of timber and lore was hammered by the hurricane, and the captain has not been found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A fateful meeting of the maritime past and present began amid the Monday morning dread of Hurricane Sandy, when distressing word came from the murk of the roiling Atlantic: the captain and crew of the H.M.S. Bounty, a vessel of timber rigged to evoke 18th-century adventure, were abandoning ship. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/us/BULLDOG-BOUNTY-1/BULLDOG-BOUNTY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 276, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/03/us/BULLDOG-BOUNTY-1/BULLDOG-BOUNTY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 276}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/03/us/BULLDOG-BOUNTY-1/BULLDOG-BOUNTY-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', '