', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5adf06c-46a2-54be-a360-21c81bdecd5b', 'word_count': 941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5adf06c-46a2-54be-a360-21c81bdecd5b'}, {'abstract': 'Best of long-form journalism this week.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/newswallah-long-reads-edition-48/', 'snippet': 'Best of long-form journalism this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an article in Open magazine, \xa0“The Riot and the Rot,” Dhirendra K. Jha examines the communal violence that broke out on Oct. 24 in Faizabad, Uttar Pradesh, while a Hindu procession was carrying idols of the Goddess Durga for immersion in the Saryu River. The violence, Mr. Jha writes, was not spur-of-the-moment but carefully orchestrated by Hindu rioters against minority Muslims.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Long Reads Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Open (Magazine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tehelka', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uttar Pradesh State (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T06:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4b7533f-4e7c-5bd3-9fa8-ac0644dccdc0', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4b7533f-4e7c-5bd3-9fa8-ac0644dccdc0'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/arts/television/whats-on-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '7 P.M. (BET) BLACK GIRLS ROCK! 2012 Black Girls Rock!, a nonprofit organization dedicated to the healthy emotional development of young black women, joins forces with BET to pay tribute to role models who have contributed through their careers and public service. Tracee Ellis Ross and Regina King host this special, taped at the Paradise Theater in the Bronx, which honors women in business, politics, entertainment, sports and community service, including Kerry Washington, Dionne Warwick, Alicia Keys, Janelle Monáe, Susan L. Taylor and Dr. Hawa Abdi. India.Arie, above, performs, along with Ms. Keys, Brandy, Keyshia Cole, Ciara, SWV, Missy Elliott, Anthony Hamilton, Eric Benét and Luke James. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s on Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T06:07:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/526db741-6322-54b2-85ec-a343470fd732', 'word_count': 703, 'uri': 'nyt://article/526db741-6322-54b2-85ec-a343470fd732'}, {'abstract': 'Circuit of the Americas, the new Formula One track outside Austin, is getting ready for its first race