ist-party-expels-bo-xilai.html', 'snippet': 'The party’s Central Committee endorsed the expulsion of Bo Xilai, who had been a contender for one of the party’s highest positions until his spectacular fall this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Several hundred of the Chinese Communist Party’s top leaders decided Sunday on a raft of measures that pave the way for a once-in-a-decade leadership transition scheduled to start this week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Party Endorses Expulsion in Scandal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Party Endorses Expulsion In Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fan Changlong', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xu Qiliang', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bo Xilai', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T17:56:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a4ac907-bf33-5195-b832-9c720974b68e', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a4ac907-bf33-5195-b832-9c720974b68e'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Clinton’s career has had more highs and lows than a Hollywood marriage. Whoever wins on Tuesday, he will play a big role over the next four years.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/bill-clinton-the-indispensable-politician/', 'snippet': 'Bill Clinton’s career has had more highs and lows than a Hollywood marriage. Whoever wins on Tuesday, he will play a big role over the next four years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I write in my latest column: “Whoever captures the White House on Nov. 6, the election season produced one clear winner: William Jefferson Clinton.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/blogs/clinton-obama-04rdv/clinton-obama-04rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/blogs/clinton-obama-04rdv/clinton-obama-04rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1439, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Clinton: The Indispensable Politician', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T17:59:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Albert R. Hunt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Albert', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Hunt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e148704d-bfcc-594e-bd54-56d407da9c1d', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e148704d-bfcc-594e-bd54-56d407da9c1d'}, {'abstract': 'Joseph R. Biden Jr. highlighted the auto bailout in a last-ditch plea for the votes of Ohio residents.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/biden-tells-crowd-we-need-ohio-to-win/', 'snippet': 'Joseph R. Biden Jr. highlighted the auto bailout in a last-ditch plea for the votes of Ohio residents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAKEWOOD, Ohio – On the last day he was to campaign in the state that might decide the election, Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. called for a return to an earlier bipartisan era – but warned that Mitt Romney was not the man to get there – and exhorted more than a thousand supporters at a high school gymnasium near Cleveland to turn out to vote on Tuesday because “we need Ohio, we need you. We win Ohio, we win this election.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden Tells Crowd, ‘We Need Ohio’ to Win', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagel, Chuck', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powell, Colin L', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowe, Olympia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T19:24:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/388081ec-8a65-5af1-96a3-221c9981533d', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/388081ec-8a65-5af1-96a3-221c9981533d'}, {'abstract': 'Kimi Raikkonen has truly returned after two years away from Formula One, winning the Abu Dhabi Grand Prix. The big story on Sunday was the reduction of the championship contenders to just two, but Raikkonen’s sharp tongue provided the most entertaining story.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/raikkonen-a-real-human-among-the-f1-automatons/', 'snippet': 'Kimi Raikkonen has truly returned after two years away from Formula One, winning the Abu Dhabi Grand Prix. The big story on Sunday was the reduction of the championship contenders to just two, but Raikkonen’s sharp tongue provided the most enterta...', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABU DHABI — There were several stories all tied together at the Abu Dhabi Grand Prix on Sunday. The biggest, in sporting terms, was the narrowing of the battle for the 2012 drivers’ title to just two: Sebastian Vettel of Red Bull, who finished the race in third and leads the series, and Fernando Alonso of Ferrari, who finished the race in second and trails Vettel by 10 points in the series.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/blogs/04rdv-iceman-solo-f1/04rdv-iceman-solo-f1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/04/blogs/04rdv-iceman-solo-f1/04rdv-iceman-solo-f1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1290, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Raikkonen, A Real Human Among the F1 Automatons', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raikkonen, Kimi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T19:25:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f942fdae-5cad-5b65-8ab9-324470148deb', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f942fdae-5cad-5b65-8ab9-324470148deb'}, {'abstract': 'A variety of factors have led Wisconsin to be considered a tossup at the vote nears.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/the-ryan-effect-proves-limited-in-wisconsin/', 'snippet': 'A variety of factors have led Wisconsin to be considered a tossup at the vote nears.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREEN BAY, Wis. — How many points does Representative Paul D. Ryan put up on the Republican scoreboard in his native Wisconsin? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The ‘Ryan Effect’ Proves Limited in Wisconsin', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 