 lines and other problems at the polls have hampered early voting.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:40 p.m. | Updated MIAMI – In a state where legal action often goes hand in hand with presidential elections, the Florida Democratic Party filed a federal lawsuit early Sunday to force the state government to extend early voting hours in South Florida.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Sue to Extend Florida’s Early Voting', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Richard L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Rod', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami (Fla)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami-Dade County (Fla)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Palm Beach (Fla)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T19:42:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3527d3fc-9608-5f87-9992-7e6bdc69adec', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3527d3fc-9608-5f87-9992-7e6bdc69adec'}, {'abstract': 'Runners showed up in Central Park early Sunday to race in an underground marathon, complete with spectators holding signs, competition bibs and a finish line.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/sports/marathoners-hold-race-of-their-own-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Runners showed up in Central Park early Sunday to race in an underground marathon, complete with spectators holding signs, competition bibs and a finish line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some called it the shadow race. Others the underground marathon. Plenty of people did not know what to call it at all.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/05runners_image3/05runners_image3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/05runners_image3/05runners_image3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/05runners_image3/05runners_image3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/05runners_image3/05runners_image3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/05runners_image3/05runners_image3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/05runners_image3/05runners_image3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/05runners_image3/05runners_image3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shadow Marathon Quenches a Desire to Run', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quenching the Desire to Run', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York City Marathon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CENTRAL PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T19:53:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Pilon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pilon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3ec5022-4712-5b4c-bf35-1852f1341ada', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3ec5022-4712-5b4c-bf35-1852f1341ada'}, {'abstract': 'It’s the polls, not the analysts, driving the nerd story.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/math-is-hard/', 'snippet': 'It’s the polls, not the analysts, driving the nerd story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, this might be my last post until tomorrow night — life will intrude. And it’s more about polling; sorry, even I am finding it hard to focus on macroeconomics until this thing is over.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Math Is Hard', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T20:08:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc5c51f8-e5cc-5122-8180-9d333a6c5f31', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc5c51f8-e5cc-5122-8180-9d333a6c5f31'}, {'abstract': 'With power returning to much of Lower Manhattan, some Off Broadway theaters and playhouses in the area are offering discounted tickets to entice audiences to return as well.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/off-broadway-offers-post-storm-discounts/', 'snippet': 'With power returning to much of Lower Manhattan, some Off Broadway theaters and playhouses in the area are offering discounted tickets to entice audiences to return as well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With power returning to much of Lower Manhattan, some Off Broadway theaters and playhouses in the area are offering discounted tickets to entice audiences to return as well. Through next Sunday, potential theatergoers can use the discount code “SANDY” for $20 tickets to the following shows: “Checkers” at the Vineyard Theater, “Don’t Go Gentle” at the Lucille Lortel Theater, “Falling” at the Minetta Lane Theater, “Fuerza Bruta” at the Daryl Roth Theater, “The Golden Land” at the Baruch Performing Arts Center, “The Other Josh Cohen” at the Soho Playhouse, “Stomp” at the Orpheum Theater and “A Summer Day” at the Cherry Lane Theater. In addition, “Giant,” “The Twenty-Seventh Man,” “Wild With Happy” and “Sorry” will all be discounted at The Public Theater. Tickets for “Through the Yellow Hour” at the Rattlestick Playwrights Theater will be $15. Tickets buyers should check with participating theaters for schedules and availability.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Off Broadway Offers Post-Storm Discounts', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Off Broadway Offers Post-Storm Discounts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T20:08:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ba40948-a63b-5159-937e-ef996e8586dc', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ba40948-a63b-5159-937e-ef996e8586dc'}, {'abstract': 'With a sports arena opening at the corner of Flatbush and Atlantic Avenues in Brooklyn, it was easy to wonder what might have been had a plan to build a stadium for the Dodgers across the street from where Barclays Center now stands not been scuttled 55 years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/nets-opener-in-brooklyn-has-shades-of-old-and-new/', 'snippet': 'With a sports arena opening at the corner of Flatbush and Atlantic Avenues in Brooklyn, it was easy to wonder what might have been had a plan to build a stadium for the Dodgers across the street from where Barclays Center now stands not been scutt...', 'lead_paragraph': '12:45 p.m. | Updated With a sports arena opening at the corner of Flatbush and Atlantic Avenues in Brooklyn, it was easy to wonder what might have been had a plan to build a stadium for the Dodgers across the street from where Barclays Center now stands not been scuttled 55 years ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nets’ Opener in Brooklyn Has Shades of Old and New', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Branca, Ralph', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hodges, Gil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pignatano, Joe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Dodgers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T20:17:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4075022e-5484-5903-8adf-b80e5ee3ff36', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4075022e-5484-5903-8adf-b80e5ee3ff36'}, {'abstract': 'For what they’re worth.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/betting-markets/', 'snippet': 'For what they’re worth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, one last entry. I see some commenters referring to results from betting markets — and some of them reading the numbers upside down. I’m personally not a big fan of the “wisdom of crowds” thing in this case: people laying bets are working from the same information the rest of us have, and in some cases (Intrade) recent movements have suggested that some players are, at the very least, putting their money on the candidate they want to win rather than the candidate they think will win.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Betting Markets', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name