'Des Moines (IA)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T20:49:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/407a2633-cab8-5322-8afc-f3b91d420ce5', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/407a2633-cab8-5322-8afc-f3b91d420ce5'}, {'abstract': 'Getting the government out of the marriage business sounds like a good idea, until we consider the dangers to women and girls.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/the-end-of-marriage/', 'snippet': 'Getting the government out of the marriage business sounds like a good idea, until we consider the dangers to women and girls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The institution of marriage has become the focus of public debate and reform, not just in the state-by-state political battles familiar to us in the United States, but across the world. Some of the longstanding practices currently being scrutinized both here and in other countries include parental approval in the choice of a spouse, permission for a husband to take more than one wife (polygyny), temporary marriage, close relative (incestuous) marriage, strict or permissive divorce terms, mandatory bride virginity, child marriage or betrothal and gender-structured marriage in which wives and husbands have different duties and privileges and therefore must be gender “opposites.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The End of ‘Marriage’', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T21:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie Shrage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shrage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9736cd8-2071-5637-9740-436ebe9f52ed', 'word_count': 2021, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9736cd8-2071-5637-9740-436ebe9f52ed'}, {'abstract': 'Grupo Corpo, the Brazilian dance troupe, performed two pieces Friday: one to a jazzy score by the Brazilian band + 2, the other based on a Portuguese song cycle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/arts/dance/grupo-corpo-brazilian-dance-company-at-bam.html', 'snippet': 'Grupo Corpo, the Brazilian dance troupe, performed two pieces Friday: one to a jazzy score by the Brazilian band + 2, the other based on a Portuguese song cycle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The popular Brazilian dance company Grupo Corpo, which was formed in 1975, is a family affair. Paulo Pederneiras, the artistic director, designs the lighting and sets; Rodrigo Pederneiras, his brother, is in charge of the choreography. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/jpcorpo/jpcorpo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/jpcorpo/jpcorpo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/jpcorpo/jpcorpo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 619, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/jpcorpo/jpcorpo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1238, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/jpcorpo/jpcorpo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/jpcorpo/jpcorpo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/jpcorpo/jpcorpo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Whiplash Jumps and Spins, and Oceanic Laments for Lovers Lost', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Whiplash Jumps and Spins, and Oceanic Laments for Lovers Lost', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grupo Corpo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T21:10:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a647332-6708-51e7-95cc-942a0dfa0e1b', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a647332-6708-51e7-95cc-942a0dfa0e1b'}, {'abstract': 'Works by Sarah Michelson and Deborah Hay finished the “Some sweet day” dance series in an atrium at the Museum of Modern Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/arts/dance/sarah-michelson-and-deborah-hay-in-moma-series.html', 'snippet': 'Works by Sarah Michelson and Deborah Hay finished the “Some sweet day” dance series in an atrium at the Museum of Modern Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The final installment of the Museum of Modern Art’s dance series “Some sweet day” came as New York artists were only beginning to grapple with larger cultural ramifications of Hurricane Sandy. Conversations in the museum’s atrium on Saturday afternoon were of losses beyond canceled premieres and temporary power failures: important interdisciplinary hubs like the Kitchen in Chelsea, which was shuttered while its staff tried to recover from flooding that had wreaked havoc on its building and equipment; individual artists whose studios had also been swamped, destroying decades of work. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/HAY/HAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/HAY/HAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/HAY/HAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/HAY/HAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thu