'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/business/05Pandora/05Pandora-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/business/05Pandora/05Pandora-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1401, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fight Builds Over Online Royalties', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fight Builds Over Online Royalties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royalties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pandora Media Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T23:23:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a1a1041-c4c8-58fa-b315-35c947fa0682', 'word_count': 1089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a1a1041-c4c8-58fa-b315-35c947fa0682'}, {'abstract': 'Mosireen, a media collective in downtown Cairo that has become a vital source of video reports about life in post-revolutionary Egypt, is engaged in an online crowdfunding campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/crowdfunding-citizen-journalism-in-cairo/', 'snippet': 'Mosireen, a media collective in downtown Cairo that has become a vital source of video reports about life in post-revolutionary Egypt, is engaged in an online crowdfunding campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mosireen, a media collective in downtown Cairo that offers equipment and training to citizen journalists, was born out of the effort by activists to document the Egyptian revolution online. As the group’s mission statement says, that was vital during the street protests that drove Hosni Mubarak from the presidential palace 21 months ago, when “armed with mobile phones and cameras, thousands upon thousands of citizens kept the balance of truth in their country by recording events as they happened in front of them, wrong-footing censorship and empowering the voice of a street-level perspective.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crowdfunding Citizen Journalism in Cairo', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T23:24:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7ab03e9-d13a-5245-a3e0-d3b2aa66f84a', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7ab03e9-d13a-5245-a3e0-d3b2aa66f84a'}, {'abstract': 'Martin Fleisher of New York City; Michael Kamil of Holmdel, N.J.; Jay Borker of Greenwich, Conn.; and Doug Doub of West Hartford, Conn., won the Sunday Swiss Teams at the District 3 Autumn Leaf Regional in Danbury, Conn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/crosswords/bridge/bridge-district-3-autumn-leaf-regional-in-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Martin Fleisher of New York City; Michael Kamil of Holmdel, N.J.; Jay Borker of Greenwich, Conn.; and Doug Doub of West Hartford, Conn., won the Sunday Swiss Teams at the District 3 Autumn Leaf Regional in Danbury, Conn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martin Fleisher of New York City; Michael Kamil of Holmdel, N.J.; Jay Borker of Greenwich, Conn.; and Doug Doub of West Hartford, Conn., won the Sunday Swiss Teams at the District 3 Autumn Leaf Regional in Danbury, Conn., played from Oct. 22 to 28.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'District 3 Autumn Leaf Regional in Connecticut', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bridge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T23:25:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d31062e-71af-53cb-8697-125047721650', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d31062e-71af-53cb-8697-125047721650'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton said last week that the Syrian National Council had outlived its usefulness and should be replaced by a larger umbrella organization.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/world/middleeast/syrias-rebels-discuss-united-political-front.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton said last week that the Syrian National Council had outlived its usefulness and should be replaced by a larger umbrella organization.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Syria’s fractious opposition groups began negotiations in Doha, Qatar, on Sunday to forge a more unified front to reshape the political landscape in a bloody conflict that claims more than 100 lives virtually every day.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria’s Disparate Opposition Groups Open Talks on Forging United Political Front', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria’s Disparate Opposition Groups Open Talks on Forging United Political Front', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syrian National Council', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Doha (Qatar)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War and Revolution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T23:47:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c00d6d42-9f48-555e-8bc0-022155d21e37', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c00d6d42-9f48-555e-8bc0-022155d21e37'}, {'abstract': 'The mammoth retailer finds that its efforts to upend the traditional publishing model have unintended consequences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/technology/shunning-amazon-booksellers-resist-a-transformation.html', 'snippet': 'The mammoth retailer finds that its efforts to upend the traditional publishing model have unintended consequences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Amazon prides itself on unraveling the established order. This fall, signs of Amazon-inspired disruption are everywhere.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/technology/05amazon-sf/05amazon-sf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/technology/05amazon-sf/05amazon-sf-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1317, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Booksellers Resisting Amazon’s Disruption', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Booksellers Resisting Amazon’s Disruption', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferriss, Timothy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The 4-Hour Chef (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amazon Kindle', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The 4-Hour Workweek (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-04T23:48:33+00