 'byline': {'original': 'Bennett Singer, David Deschamps and Leslie D. Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bennett', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Deschamps', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/6ba74bf6-fed3-505b-93d9-cf4d1c630b91', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/6ba74bf6-fed3-505b-93d9-cf4d1c630b91'}, {'abstract': 'Data to be released will include I.S.M. service for October, consumer credit for September, weekly jobless claims and the trade deficit for September.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/business/economy/economic-reports-for-the-week-of-nov-5.html', 'snippet': 'Data to be released will include I.S.M. service for October, consumer credit for September, weekly jobless claims and the trade deficit for September.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ECONOMIC REPORTS Data to be released will include I.S.M. service for October (Monday); consumer credit for September (Wednesday); weekly jobless claims and the trade deficit for September (Thursday); and import prices for October, wholesale trade for September and Thomson Reuters/University of Michigan consumer sentiment index (Friday).', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economic Reports for the Week Ahead', 'kicker': 'Looking Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Economic Reports for the Week Ahead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T01:29:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb802c4f-33f2-5865-9205-9389afd0f52c', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb802c4f-33f2-5865-9205-9389afd0f52c'}, {'abstract': 'The bride and groom must agree to let all of the decisions about their special day be voted on and curated by followers on social media like Facebook and Twitter.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/a-wedding-with-followers/', 'snippet': 'The bride and groom must agree to let all of the decisions about their special day be voted on and curated by followers on social media like Facebook and Twitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For couples planning a wedding, the process usually includes facing a jury of mothers, aunts and future sisters-in-law — all offering a verdict on gowns, hairstyles and an array of other details.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wedding, With Followers', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Wedding, With Followers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brides (Magazine)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conde Nast Publications Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T01:33:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ec6fcad-c940-52c4-ac92-037e3c11e585', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ec6fcad-c940-52c4-ac92-037e3c11e585'}, {'abstract': 'The shortage of fuel was on the minds of thousands of fans at MetLife Stadium on Sunday. Fans described the Giants game as a diversion from the devastation in New Jersey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/sports/football/celebrating-an-nfl-sunday-after-hurricane-sandy.html', 'snippet': 'The shortage of fuel was on the minds of thousands of fans at MetLife Stadium on Sunday. Fans described the Giants game as a diversion from the devastation in New Jersey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Tunes from Bon Jovi wafted over the rooftops of thousands of vehicles in the sun-washed parking lots outside MetLife Stadium early Sunday afternoon, accompanying the hiss from smoking grills and the hum from tiny generators and the din from a thousand conversations seemingly centering on two topics: gasoline and football.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/YBLUE/YBLUE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/YBLUE/YBLUE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/YBLUE/YBLUE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 587, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/YBLUE/YBLUE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1174, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/YBLUE/YBLUE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/YBLUE/YBLUE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/YBLUE/YBLUE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrating an N.F.L. Sunday, No Matter What It Took', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Celebrating an N.F.L. Sunday, No Matter What It Took', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T01:34:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03afaaf4-b9b1-5817-bc36-b1de7f93be98', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03afaaf4-b9b1-5817-bc36-b1de7f93be98'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney seemed determined to play down any hint of tension between his campaign and Mr. Christie, the New Jersey governor, whose kind words have given the president an unexpected bipartisan credential.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/romney-thanks-christie-while-ignoring-his-praise-for-obama/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney seemed determined to play down any hint of tension between his campaign and Mr. Christie, the New Jersey governor, whose kind words have given the president an unexpected bipartisan credential.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MORRISVILLE, Pa. — Gov. Chris Christie’s lavish praise for President Obama in the days since Hurricane Sandy has raised eyebrows across the Republican establishment. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Overlooks Christie’s Praise for Obama', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T01:35:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/617b33df-6765-5aab-8953-f939fac9c866', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/617b33df-6765-5aab-8953-f939fac9c866'}, {'abstract': 'Dodge teamed with The Onion to devise a fictitious network lineup presentation to reach young consumers.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/tvs-upfront-ad-sales-get-the-onion-treatment/', 'snippet': 'Dodge teamed with The Onion to devise a fictitious network lineup presentation to reach young consumers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few people outside of the media industry know about the upfront presentations, the annual early selling of television and, increasingly, digital media shows to advertisers. But the event’s obscurity is not stopping Dodge and the marketing team at The Onion, the satirical news Web site, from using it as the backdrop to the first branded entertainment collaboration between the two companies.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TV’s Upfront Ad Sales Get the Onion Treatment', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'TV’s Upfront Ad Sales Get the Onion Treatment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dodge Division of Chrysler Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Onion, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T01:38:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/decbab50-6482-5377-b514-0846a1203417', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/decbab50-6482-5377-b514-0846a1203417'}, {'abstract': 'On NBC’s Facebook page, the naming of Erica Hill to Jenna Wolfe’s co-host spot on “Weekend Today” raised hackles reminiscent of the anger over Ann Curry’s departure from the “Today” show.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/04/nbc-peppered-by-online-critics-in-shuffle-of-hosts/', 'snippet': 'On NBC’s Facebook page, the naming of Erica Hill to Jenna Wolfe’s co-host spot on “Weekend Today” raised hackles reminiscent of the anger over Ann Curry’s departure from the “Today” show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Same outrage, same channel, different co-host.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NBC Peppered by Online Critics in Shuffle of Hosts', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'NBC Peppered by Critics In Shuffle of Weekend Hosts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T01:41:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0132c11b-2996-59f4-aa76-bfb416761321', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0132c11b-2996-59f4-aa76-bfb416761321'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands of volunteers and runners dedicated their Sunday to helping families whose houses were damaged or destroyed by Hurricane Sandy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/sports/marathon-runners-embrace-chance-to-help-storm-stricken-new-yorkers.html', 'snippet': 'Thousands of volunteers and runners dedicated their Sunday to helping families whose houses were damaged or destroyed by Hurricane Sandy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the New York City Marathon had not been canceled because of Hurricane Sandy last week, Michelle Leichtling would not have found herself in a grief-stricken neighborhood on Sta