ger, Ben', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T02:33:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd97da4b-852e-5281-a498-4dfe7a2b41a3', 'word_count': 1055, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd97da4b-852e-5281-a498-4dfe7a2b41a3'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court is considering whether the law protects copyright holders who want to sell their works for reduced prices abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/opinion/copyright-on-imported-works.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court is considering whether the law protects copyright holders who want to sell their works for reduced prices abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Supap Kirtsaeng bought textbooks published overseas by John Wiley & Sons and resold them on eBay and other Web sites for a profit in the United States. The publisher sued Mr. Kirtsaeng for violating its copyright, and the case went before the Supreme Court last week. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Copyright on Imported Works', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Copyright on Imported Works', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'John Wiley & Sons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirtsaeng, Supap', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suit