tthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Purdy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b457873-0a4a-59d7-abaa-82fc7339ff55', 'word_count': 2769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b457873-0a4a-59d7-abaa-82fc7339ff55'}, {'abstract': 'If the Palestinians are admitted as a “nonmember” observer state in the U.N. General Assembly, they will win a short-term victory with serious long term risks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/opinion/palestinians-at-the-united-nations-again.html', 'snippet': 'If the Palestinians are admitted as a “nonmember” observer state in the U.N. General Assembly, they will win a short-term victory with serious long term risks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With peace negotiations at an impasse since 2008 and unlikely to resume any time soon, the Palestinians have only one diplomatic card left — their status at the United Nations — and once again they are trying to play it. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palestinians at the U.N., Again', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Palestinians at the U.N., Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T02:36:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dbd272d-36d1-5099-bfd6-dabca7f0a80d', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dbd272d-36d1-5099-bfd6-dabca7f0a80d'}, {'abstract': 'Missteps and mistakes — by offense and officials, even by coaches — could not undo the best effort the Steelers’ defense has had this season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/sports/football/defense-lifts-steelers-in-road-win-against-giants.html', 'snippet': 'Missteps and mistakes — by offense and officials, even by coaches — could not undo the best effort the Steelers’ defense has had this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. —\xa0 The Pittsburgh Steelers’ long Sunday began with an early-morning trip to the airport and then a late-night flight home. It was the middle of the day, bogged by questionable officiating and a sometimes stagnant offense, that must have seemed interminable until the Steelers uncovered an identity that made even a laborious travel itinerary worthwhile.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/YJPGIANTS/YJPGIANTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/YJPGIANTS/YJPGIANTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/YJPGIANTS/YJPGIANTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/YJPGIANTS/YJPGIANTS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1546, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Steelers’ Defense Keeps Anything From Spoiling Time on Road', 'kicker': 'On Pro Football', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Steelers’ Defense Keeps Anything From Spoiling Time on Road', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T02:36:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/baad261f-ed8e-5bfd-a327-691587781da7', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baad261f-ed8e-5bfd-a327-691587781da7'}, {'abstract': 'With bipartisanship nowhere in sight, the public can only hope that something civil and creative follows the election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/opinion/desperate-for-civility-on-capitol-hill.html', 'snippet': 'With bipartisanship nowhere in sight, the public can only hope that something civil and creative follows the election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What sounds like a tall order for Capitol Hill — civility — is being increasingly invoked now that actual bipartisanship seems as distant as Pluto. Senator Olympia Snowe, for one, is ending her 34 years on Capitol Hill by becoming a board member of the National Institute for Civil Discourse, a nonpartisan advocacy group founded after the Arizona shooting last year that killed six people and gravely wounded Representative Gabrielle Giffords.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Desperate for Civility', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Desperate for Civility', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowe, Olympia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T02:37:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f1be626-3ec5-550a-8565-e58c9bfce8d1', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f1be626-3ec5-550a-8565-e58c9bfce8d1'}, {'abstract': 'Both campaigns altered course this week to react to the devastation of Hurricane Sandy before jumping back into the fray for a final dash to election day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/11/03/us/politics/1103wip.html', 'snippet': 'Both campaigns altered course this week to react to the devastation of Hurricane Sandy before jumping back into the fray for a final dash to election day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Both campaigns altered course this week to react to the devastation of Hurricane Sandy before jumping back into the fray for a final dash