l', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DC United', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Red Bulls (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T03:03:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe86d138-c41a-5023-bb75-437dd16e7e23', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe86d138-c41a-5023-bb75-437dd16e7e23'}, {'abstract': 'As Alabama and Oregon seem destined to play for a national championship, Crimson Tide Coach Nick Saban has questioned whether the Ducks’ no-huddle offense is a risk to player safety.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/sports/ncaafootball/alabama-coach-nick-saban-questions-oregons-offense.html', 'snippet': 'As Alabama and Oregon seem destined to play for a national championship, Crimson Tide Coach Nick Saban has questioned whether the Ducks’ no-huddle offense is a risk to player safety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To some, it is art. Marcus Mariota, Oregon’s quarterback, directs an offense that promises the spectacular. Anywhere, anytime, it can score. Don’t blink — Kenjon Barner is gone again, racing down the sideline. At their best, the Ducks move beautifully, Coach Chip Kelly’s masterpiece. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/sports/YCOLLEGES1/YCOLLEGES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name':