 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/us/politics/ohio-canvassers-pitch-the-opposition-in-calls.html', 'snippet': 'Just outside Cincinnati, Greg Davis was dialing numbers from a list of ostensibly pro-Republican households when, unexpectedly, he found an Obama supporter at the other end of the line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the campaign entering its final hours, Mitt Romney’s Ohio satellite offices can take on an echo-chamber air, with pumped-up staff members taking jabs at President Obama’s missteps, his perceived policy failures and just about anything else negative about him that comes to mind. It keeps the adrenaline flowing, and doubtless eases the drudgery of hours of get-out-the-vote phone calls.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ohio Canvassers Pitch the Opposition in Calls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Other End Of the Line', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cincinnati (Ohio)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Greg', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T03:34:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f179dda-b008-561b-b9df-0002728afc1c', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f179dda-b008-561b-b9df-0002728afc1c'}, {'abstract': 'In New York’s “outer boroughs,” accusations of neglect seemed colored by a growing belief that the recovery from Hurricane Sandy has split along predictable class lines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/nyregion/in-sight-of-manhattan-skyline-a-population-lives-forlorn-and-in-the-dark.html', 'snippet': 'In New York’s “outer boroughs,” accusations of neglect seemed colored by a growing belief that the recovery from Hurricane Sandy has split along predictable class lines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Watching the Manhattan skyline shimmer over Jamaica Bay had always been one of the charms of life in the Rockaways. But now, when the Empire State Building winks on each night, those lights feel almost like a punch in the gut.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Sight of Manhattan Skyline, Living Forlorn and in the Dark', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Sight of Manhattan Skyline, Living Forlorn and in the Dark', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Red Hook (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockaway Beach (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Outages and Blackouts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Dorp (NYC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'GERRITSEN BEACH (NYC)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T03:34:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddc9be73-4a88-5584-ba18-8936510fbdea', 'word_count': 1238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddc9be73-4a88-5584-ba18-8936510fbdea'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Dupin was the author of a biography and monographs on Miró and for a long time one of the directors of the renowned Galerie Maeght in Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/arts/jacques-dupin-french-art-critic-and-poet-dies-at-85.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Dupin was the author of a biography and monographs on Miró and for a long time one of the directors of the renowned Galerie Maeght in Paris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jacques Dupin, a poet, art critic and cultural eminence in France whose influence straddled the avant-garde literary world and the commercial market in paintings and sculptures by major 20th-century artists, died on Oct. 27 at his home in Paris. He was 85. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/obit-DUPIN/obit-DUPIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/obit-DUPIN/obit-DUPIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/obit-DUPIN/obit-DUPIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/obit-DUPIN/obit-DUPIN-superJumbo.jpg', '