n': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53a0b9c9-a272-5bc2-9b68-459abe6147f0', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53a0b9c9-a272-5bc2-9b68-459abe6147f0'}, {'abstract': 'Larger buildings at N.Y.U. did not lose electricity or heat because of the university’s decision to make its own.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/how-n-y-u-stayed-partly-warm-and-lighted/', 'snippet': 'Larger buildings at N.Y.U. did not lose electricity or heat because of the university’s decision to make its own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When much of Manhattan south of Midtown was blacked out, the lights were on at most of New York University, as was the heat and hot water. As I wrote in January 2011, N.Y.U.  installed a small network of its own, burning natural gas in a unit that not only made electricity but also delivered the heat that would otherwise go to waste for use in heating and cooling. That process is known as cogeneration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How N.Y.U. Stayed (Partly) Warm and Lighted', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T12:45:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ca98a7f-06ad-53a9-af0b-c6f08511d207', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ca98a7f-06ad-53a9-af0b-c6f08511d207'}, {'abstract': 'The latest indignities befalling the disgraced British television host Jimmy Savile reflect a broad popular revulsion at the widening accusations that he molested children.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/a-disgusted-britain-tries-to-delete-memories-of-savile/', 'snippet': 'The latest indignities befalling the disgraced British television host Jimmy Savile reflect a broad popular revulsion at the widening accusations that he molested children.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:25 p.m. | Updated LONDON — The headstone of his grave has been removed, destroyed and buried at the request of his family. The Roman Catholic Church is considering whether to strip away his papal knighthood. And, on Monday, city councilors in the northern British seaside resort of Scarborough voted to delete his name, at least temporarily, from the roll-call of freemen of their city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/blogs/05rdv-cowell-savile/05rdv-cowell-savile-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/blogs/05rdv-cowell-savile/05rdv-cowell-savile-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Disgusted Britain Tries to Delete Memories of Savile', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savile, Jimmy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T12:49:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname'