N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T13:50:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/229c6aa7-ef4a-5114-84d1-436f0c0a4638', 'word_count': 1108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/229c6aa7-ef4a-5114-84d1-436f0c0a4638'}, {'abstract': 'South Sudan, which gained independence from Sudan last year, objected to a United Nations report raising allegations of atrocities by South Sudan’s army.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/world/africa/south-sudan-expels-un-rights-officer.html', 'snippet': 'South Sudan, which gained independence from Sudan last year, objected to a United Nations report raising allegations of atrocities by South Sudan’s army.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KAMPALA, Uganda — South Sudan, which gained independence from Sudan last year after decades of civil war, has expelled a United Nations human rights officer after the government objected to a report raising allegations of atrocities by South Sudan’s army. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Sudan Expels a U.N. Rights Officer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Sudan Expels a U.N. Rights Officer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T13:59:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Kron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12ab118c-a952-5da7-8256-91f102e2055c', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12ab118c-a952-5da7-8256-91f102e2055c'}, {'abstract': 'Renaissance-era cabinets of curiosities are the inspiration behind a new temporary gallery-cum-shop in Berlin.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/salon-des-invites/', 'snippet': 'Renaissance-era cabinets of curiosities are the inspiration behind a new temporary gallery-cum-shop in Berlin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Renaissance-era cabinets of curiosities — those rooms filled with exotic geological samples, horns and feathers purportedly from fabled animals, and other arcane bric-a-brac — were the precursors to the modern museum. Now they are the inspiration behind Le Cabinet de Curiosités de Thomas Erber, a temporary gallery-cum-shop at Berlin’s Andreas Murkudis boutique (Potsdamer Strasse 81E), assembled by the creative consultant Thomas Erber. From Nov. 22 through Jan. 19, the store will highlight unique pieces, all for sale, by 50 designers, artists and fashion brands.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Salon des Invites', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Salon des Invites', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T14:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy MacDonell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dc92f4e-2ab0-5fde-876a-c9981b9b9a53', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dc92f4e-2ab0-5fde-876a-c9981b9b9a53'}, {'abstract': 'One of the consequences of the shale gas boom in the United States has been an increase in the amount of coal, the most CO2-polluting fossil fuel, coming to Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/environmentally-correct-europe-turns-to-coal/', 'snippet': 'One of the consequences of the shale gas boom in the United States has been an increase in the amount of coal, the most CO2-polluting fossil fuel, coming to Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — You may think that coal is fading away as a fuel, but it isn’t. It’s booming. As I write in my latest Green Column, last year coal as a proportion of world energy was at its highest since the 1960s. A lot of the growth in coal use is happening in Asia, particularly China. But coal — the largest CO2 emitter among fossil fuels — is also in demand in Europe, including in ultra-green Germany.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/blogs/05rdv-green-germany-coal/05rdv-green-germany-coal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/blogs/05rdv-green-germany-coal/05rdv-green-germany-coal-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1232, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Environmentally Correct Europe Turns to Coal', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T14:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Reed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38f8b0c4-d01b-5d20-91a4-0695af240873', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38f8b0c4-d01b-5d20-91a4-0695af240873'}, {'abstract': 'Amazon.com inspires anxiety just about everywhere, but its publishing arm is getting pushback from all sorts of booksellers, David Streitfeld reports in Monday’s New York Times. They are scorning the imprint’s most prominent title, Timothy Ferriss’s “The 4-Hour Chef.” That book is coming out just before Thanksgiving into a fragmented book-selling landscape.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/daily-report-a-cold-shoulder-for-amazon-as-publisher/', 'snippet': 'Amazon.com inspires anxiety just about everywhere, but its publishing arm is getting pushback from all sorts of booksellers, David Streitfeld reports in Monday’s New York Times. They are scorning the imprint’s most prominent title, Timothy Ferriss...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Amazon.com inspires anxiety just about everywhere, but its publishing arm is getting pushback from all sorts of booksellers, David Streitfeld reports in Monday’s New York Times. They are scorning the imprint’s most prominent title, Timothy Ferriss’s “The 4-Hour Chef.” That book is coming out just before Thanksgiving into a fragmented book-selling landscape that Amazon has done much to create but that eludes its control.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: A Cold Shoulder for Amazon as Publisher', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T14:08:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e931d0fa-4c07-5c2e-9411-8834f8792105', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e931d0fa-4c07-5c2e-9411-8834f8792105'}, {'abstract': 'Changes are a-coming to the Puzzles & Games page.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/an-exciting-new-look/', 'snippet': 'Changes are a-coming to the Puzzles & Games page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SPECIAL POST — Don’t panic. This will be a good thing, believe me. A new Web page, complete with smooth, improved game play, is exactly what this place needed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Exciting New Look', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T14:25:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ec4de70-8686-5dc8-a9de-60fe988abe78', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ec4de70-8686-5dc8-a9de-60fe988abe78'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/what-were-reading-560/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Telegraph: Pippa Middleton responds to the scathing reviews of her new cookbook, including one that called it a “cultural tea bag for the American market.” — Julia Moskin', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T14:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/162d1312-3d6e-539c-a8af-9d93d1d9d91b', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/162d1312-3d6e-539c-a8af-9d93d1d9d91b'}, {'abstract': 'The cast members of “Jersey Shore” will be among those featured in a Nov. 15 fundraising special on MTV that will benefit reconstruction efforts in Seaside Heights, N.J., where that reality series is filmed.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/mtv-sets-restore-the-shore-fundraiser/', 'snippet': 'The cast members of “Jersey Shore” will be among those featured in a Nov. 15 fundraising special on MTV that will benefit reconstruction efforts in Seaside Heights, N.J., where that reality series is filmed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MTV, which helped shine a spotlight on Seaside Heights, N.J., and its surroundings with the success of its reality series “Jersey Shore,” said on Monday that it would broadcast a one-hour fund-raising special next week to benefit rebuilding efforts in that area, which was one of many coastal regions hit hard by Hurricane Sandy. The special, called “Restore the Shore,” will be shown at 11 p.m., Eastern time, on Nov. 15 and broadcast from the Times Square studios of MTV. The cable network said it was working with Architecture for Humanity, a nonprofit organization that provides design and construction services, and will establish a fund for rebuilding the boardwalk in Seaside Heights and assisting individuals and businesses affected by the storm. MTV said the cast members of “Jersey Shore,” which is currently in its final season, will be featured in the “Restore the Shore” special, with additional guest appearances to be announced later. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/snooki/snooki-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 746, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/snooki/snooki-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1093, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/snooki/snooki-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/snooki/snooki-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/snooki/snooki-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'MTV Schedules ‘Restore the Shore’ Fund-Raiser', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'MTV Schedules a Fund-Raiser, ‘Restore the Shore,’ for Next Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seaside Heights (NJ)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T14:32:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b48aa1f-3c8a-5cbb-ba79-29f6283ec79f', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b48aa1f-3c8a-5cbb-ba79-29f6283ec79f'}, {'abstract': 'Netflix announced that its board had adopted a shareholder rights plan, or poison pill, just days after the activist investor Carl C. Icahn disclosed he had acquired a 9.98 percent stake.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/netflix-adopts-poison-pill/', 'snippet': 'Netflix announced that its board had adopted a shareholder rights plan, or poison pill, just days after the activist investor Carl C. Icahn disclosed he had acquired a 9.98 percent stake.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:28 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Netflix Adopts Poison Pill', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T14:35:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff5e4e1d-4fba-557f-998a-f2f8d9b3bf95', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff5e4e1d-4fba-557f-998a-f2f8d9b3bf95'}, {'abstract': 'A flawed candidate, but a far better one than many people (myself included) often thought.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/let-us-now-praise-mitt-romney/', 'snippet': 'A flawed candidate, but a far better one than many people (myself included) often thought.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Later today, I will publish my prediction for tomorrow’s outcome\xa0— electoral, popular, the whole shebang — and unless something dramatic changes in the next few hours I’ll be prophesying an excruciatingly narrow Obama win. But before I explain why I think he’s going to just barely lose this election, let me say a few words in praise of Willard Mitt Romney, candidate for president of the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Let Us Now Praise Mitt Romney', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T14:42:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5eb4db5a-3a37-5efe-a0df-be28e129e1dd', 'word_count': 1325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5eb4db5a-3a37-5efe-a0df-be28e129e1dd'}, {'abstract': 'In a surprise move, Nicolas Ghesquière is parting ways with Balenciaga, the Paris house he transformed into a modern luxury brand with a following for its clothing and accessories.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/nicolas-ghesquiere-to-leave-balenciaga/', 'snippet': 'In a surprise move, Nicolas Ghesquière is parting ways with Balenciaga, the Paris house he transformed into a modern luxury brand with a following for its clothing and accessories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a surprise move, Nicolas Ghesquière is parting ways with Balenciaga, the Paris house he transformed into a modern luxury brand with a following for its clothing and accessories. A company announcement Monday morning said the decision for him to leave Balenciaga after 15 years as creative director was made jointly by Mr. Ghesquière and PPR, which owns the label. A spokesman for Balenciaga, Lionel Vermeil, had no additional information.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nicolas Ghesquière to Leave Balenciaga', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luxury Goods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghesquiere, Nicolas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BALENCIAGA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T14:53:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8eb6cedb-b1d7-5dad-9ed8-63881a4503ab', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8eb6cedb-b1d7-5dad-9ed8-63881a4503ab'}, {'abstract': 'Naturally, when selling, we spend most, if not all, of our time highlighting the positive attributes of our product or service. But there are exceptions.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/on-volunteering-negative-information-when-selling/', 'snippet': 'Naturally, when selling, we spend most, if not all, of our time highlighting the positive attributes of our product or service. But there are exceptions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that TerraCycle is almost a decade old and operating in 22 countries, I have realized how much sales styles differ throughout the world, especially in Europe. While the American style of sales is typically gung ho – energetic and positive — the European style is quite different, much more conservative.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Volunteering Negative Information When Selling', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TerraCycle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T15:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Szaky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szaky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/649b5965-2533-5a27-ac47-765719446f42', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/649b5965-2533-5a27-ac47-765719446f42'}, {'abstract': 'After months of planning, six days of trekking and days of reconnaissance work, scientists begin collecting important information that will help identify links among glaciers, climate and water resources in Bhutan.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/laying-down-stakes-to-measure-glacier-melt/', 'snippet': 'After months of planning, six days of trekking and days of reconnaissance work, scientists begin collecting important information that will help identify links among glaciers, climate and water resources in Bhutan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aaron Putnam, a postdoctoral research scientist at the Lamont-Doherty Earth Observatory of Columbia University, is a leader of an expedition to Bhutan to examine links among climate, glaciers and water resources in the Himalaya.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Laying Down Stakes to Measure Glacier Melt', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glaciers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {