By Julie Turkewitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turkewitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/832a6fb9-952e-561a-870b-47c420d2b542', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/832a6fb9-952e-561a-870b-47c420d2b542'}, {'abstract': 'Replacing the customary noodles or potatoes with grains gives these delicious and comforting dishes a nutritional boost. Today: a quinoa and carrot kugel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/health/quinoa-and-carrot-kugel-sweet-and-savory-kugels.html', 'snippet': 'Replacing the customary noodles or potatoes with grains gives these delicious and comforting dishes a nutritional boost. Today: a quinoa and carrot kugel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recently I received an e-mail from a reader describing a kugel made with carrots and quinoa that she’d tasted at a buffet dinner. “It was delicious served at room temperature, cut into cubes, which were firm in texture, sweet but not overly, and\xa0 prepared with quinoa,” she wrote. “I am wondering if you might be willing and able to conjure up the ingredients to make this particular kugel incorporating quinoa.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/06/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': 