n’s 25- to 29-year-olds have earned at least a bachelor’s degree, according to an analysis of newly available census data.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although the United States no longer leads the world in educational attainment, record numbers of young Americans are completing high school, going to college and finishing college, according to a Pew Research Center analysis of newly available census data. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/us/DEGREES/DEGREES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/us/DEGREES/DEGREES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Record Number Complete High School and College', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Record Number Complete High School and College', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduation Rates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T17:01:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d13e66d-17e6-5ac4-834d-889f3372ecd8', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d13e66d-17e6-5ac4-834d-889f3372ecd8'}, {'abstract': 'Audra McDonald, Kelli O’Hara, Josh Groban and Michael Feinstein are among the performers who will participate in the Philharmonic’s New Year’s Eve concert, which was originally scheduled to be conducted by Marvin Hamlisch.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/new-york-philharmonic-to-celebrate-hamlisch/', 'snippet': 'Audra McDonald, Kelli O’Hara, Josh Groban and Michael Feinstein are among the performers who will participate in the Philharmonic’s New Year’s Eve concert, which was originally scheduled to be conducted by Marvin Hamlisch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before the ball drops and the Champagne corks are popped, the New York Philharmonic will spend its New Year’s Eve celebrating the music of Marvin Hamlisch with an all-star lineup of talent. The Philharmonic said on Monday that its New Year’s Eve concert, held annually at Lincoln Center, was scheduled this year to be hosted and conducted by Hamlisch, the composer of “A Chorus Line” and pop hits like “The Way We Were.” Following Hamlisch’s death on Aug. 6, this concert will now be a salute to his work as performed by artists he knew and worked with closely, including Audra McDonald, Kelli O’Hara, Josh Groban, Michael Feinstein, Raúl Esparza, Megan Hilty, Joshua Bell, Maria Friedman and Frederica von Stade. The concert, which will emphasize Hamlisch’s film and stage work like “A Chorus Line” and “Sweet Smell of Success,” will be conducted by Paul Gemignani and directed by Lonny Price. It will be hosted by Ms. McDonald and broadcast on “Live From Lincoln Center” on PBS. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/hamlisch/hamlisch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 279, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/hamlisch/hamlisch-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 279, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/hamlisch/hamlisch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/hamlisch/hamlisch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/arts/hamlisch/hamlisch-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Philharmonic to Celebrate Hamlisch', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York Philharmonic To Celebrate Hamlisch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamlisch, Marvin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T17:06:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7de6e88-8a0d-59bb-8310-c5b9b6aa2844', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7de6e88-8a0d-59bb-8310-c5b9b6aa2844'}, {'abstract': 'Seersucker in Brooklyn will host “Eat Pork, Help New York” tonight, with four sliders for $10, to benefit the Red Hook Initiative.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/pork-sliders-for-sandy-relief-and-other-fundraising-events/', 'snippet': 'Seersucker in Brooklyn will host “Eat Pork, Help New York” tonight, with four sliders for $10, to benefit the Red Hook Initiative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What to do with a 175-pound heritage Berkshire pig that was delivered from an upstate farm, intended for a fund-raiser that was canceled by the hurricane? Why, make 1,000 roast pork sliders with green tomato barbecue sauce on mini Martin’s potato rolls. Then sell four of them for $10, and give all the money to a more urgent cause: the relief effort in Sandy-ravaged Red Hook. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pork Sliders for Sandy Relief, and Other Fundraising Events', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T17:08:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ddcff83-365c-5f8c-a0aa-34bfe8677ea8', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ddcff83-365c-5f8c-a0aa-34bfe8677ea8'}, {'abstract': 'Sunday seemed like the wrong time for New York quarterback Eli Manning to sink deeper into a slump.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/sports/for-the-giants-the-wrong-kind-of-spotlight.html', 'snippet': 'Sunday seemed like the wrong time for New York quarterback Eli Manning to sink deeper into a slump.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a Sunday at least, the N.F.L. served its purest purpose as entertainment vehicle, serving as a gripping distraction for anyone with a taste for football and a need to escape from storm-related calamity, election fatigue or the overwhelming desire to throw eggs at a mayor. The Giants really wanted to be the kings of that distraction. If they were going to play in East Rutherford, N.J., amid the aftermath of Hurricane Sandy’s wallop — and it wasn’t a given to everyone that they should have — they wanted to do it right, beat the Steelers, give the blue jersey set a reason to forget everything and cheer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/sports/football/06leadingpic/06leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 872, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/sports/football/06leadingpic/06leadingpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1744, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/sports/football/06leadingpic/06leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/06/sports/football/06leadingpic/06leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/sports/football/06leadingpic/06leadingpic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For the Giants, the Wrong Kind of Spotlight', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Gia