: 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/05/health/05well_running/05well_running-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/health/05well_running/05well_running-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lessons From a Marathon Not Run', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T22:10:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Lyons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83aaf967-38b0-580d-9f1d-4b826cff201a', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83aaf967-38b0-580d-9f1d-4b826cff201a'}, {'abstract': 'A northeaster knocked out power to homes in New York and New Jersey and interrupted train service, setting back recovery after Hurricane Sandy, but several utilities said they had already brought back most of their customers.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/storm-aftermath-live-updates-5/', 'snippet': 'A northeaster knocked out power to homes in New York and New Jersey and interrupted train service, setting back recovery after Hurricane Sandy, but several utilities said they had already brought back most of their customers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Odd-even gas rationing went into effect Friday in New York City and Long Island as officials moved to shorten the hours-long lines that have become an exasperating feature of daily life for drivers since last week’s storm. Lines seemed to be a bit shorter, and though some people with even-numbered plates flouted the law with apparent impunity, there was little reported chaos.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Storm Aftermath: Continuing Coverage', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Zero May Be a Strange Number, but It’s Not Odd', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T22:17:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d6e0ec4-1d80-598a-9780-2c69152210ae', 'word_count': 18121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d6e0ec4-1d80-598a-9780-2c69152210ae'}, {'abstract': 'The young pianist Jenny Q Chai took an eclectic approach to her concert at Le Poisson Rouge in both repertory and artistry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/arts/music/jenny-q-chai-at-le-poisson-rouge.html', 'snippet': 'The young pianist Jenny Q Chai took an eclectic approach to her concert at Le Poisson Rouge in both repertory and artistry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent years the piano recital format has become more flexible. While many performers stick to the standard recipe of large-scale sonatas, multimovement pieces and oft-heard shorter works, others, like the pianists Pierre-Laurent Aimard and David Greilsammer, might juxtapose a dozen smaller pieces by composers as varied as Cage and Chopin, Scarlatti and Stockhausen. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/arts/JENNY/JENNY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/arts/JENNY/JENNY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/arts/JENNY/JENNY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/06/arts/JENNY/JENNY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/arts/JENNY/JENNY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Piano, an iPad, a Mirror: Tools for a Modern Recital', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Piano, an iPad, a Mirror: Tools for a Modern Recital', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Poisson Rouge', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chai, Jenny Q', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T22:22:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/52496a80-ae57-5b38-bdee-9518dfc01586', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52496a80-ae57-5b38-bdee-9518dfc01586'}, {'abstract': 'A crash course in Ohio, the ultimate swing state: geography, history, law and even religion (the Amish vote).', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/app-snapshot-ohio-ground-zero/', 'snippet': 'A crash course in Ohio, the ultimate swing state: geography, history, law and even religion (the Amish vote).', 'lead_paragraph': 'The  Election 2012 app has a crash course in Ohio: geography, history, law and even religion (the Amish vote). Throughout the campaign, we’ve been gathering essential politics news from The Times and around the Web, and tomorrow evening, the app will be unlocked as we roll out live election results, video and other coverage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'App Snapshot: Ohio Ground Zero', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T22:24:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/156be8df-e5c0-59bc-8d6c-1c704b10bbdd', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/156be8df-e5c0-59bc-8d6c-1c704b10bbdd'}, {'abstract': 'Bryan Norcross’s criticism of the National Hurricane Center and of New York City’s mayor for briefly playing down Hurricane Sandy’s severity raised some debate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/science/bryan-norcross-speaking-beyond-whats-forecast.html', 'snippet': 'Bryan Norcross’s criticism of the National Hurricane Center and of New York City’s mayor for briefly playing down Hurricane Sandy’s severity raised some debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Hurricane Sandy made its way up the coast, Bryan Norcross sat at his desk in the Weather Channel’s headquarters in Atlanta, waiting for the National Hurricane Center to issue a warning for the Northeast. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/science/06PROF_SPAN/06PROF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/06/science/06PROF_SPAN/06PROF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/science/06PROF_SPAN/06PROF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/science/06PROF_SPAN/06PROF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/science/06PROF_SPAN/06PROF_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/06/science/06PROF_SPAN/06PROF_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/science/06PROF_SPAN/06PROF_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Speaking His Mind, Beyond the Forecast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Speaking His Mind, Beyond the Forecas