s struck me as necessary but not sufficient. Community matters, and if what your neighbor needs is a grocery run, some hot soup or a reminder to keep drinking water during a heat wave, you can make an important difference.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Old, Frail and in Harm’s Way', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Elderly, Often Less Mobile, Are More Vulnerable in Disasters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrios-Paoli, Lilliam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Lisa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aging, Department for the (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gerontological Society of America', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T22:42:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24d2749a-3402-5f04-8fb6-7ee6667084d3', 'word_count': 936, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24d2749a-3402-5f04-8fb6-7ee6667084d3'}, {'abstract': 'With the hotel industry recovering, operators are breathing a sigh of relief. But business travelers used to low rates, last-minute availability and perks like free Wi-Fi are less enthusiastic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/business/travel-managers-brace-for-an-upturn-in-lodging-rates.html', 'snippet': 'With the hotel industry recovering, operators are breathing a sigh of relief. But business travelers used to low rates, last-minute availability and perks like free Wi-Fi are less enthusiastic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the domestic hotel industry on the cusp of a widespread recovery, operators are breathing a sigh of relief. But business travelers who have gotten used to low rates, the ability to book at the last minute and perks like free Wi-Fi and parking are less enthusiastic. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/business/Hotels/Hotels-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/business/Hotels/Hotels-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1435, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/business/Hotels/Hotels-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/06/business/Hotels/Hotels-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/business/Hotels/Hotels-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Travel Managers Brace for an Upturn in Lodging Rates', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lean Days for Hotel Deals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T22:44:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha C. White', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'White', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbd6da0a-7dc9-52b3-90a3-4360cacb03d6', 'word_count': 936, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbd6da0a-7dc9-52b3-90a3-4360cacb03d6'}, {'abstract': 'Carnegie Hall, which has canceled all events since Oct. 28 because of a dangling crane boom across West 57th Street, will remain closed for at least another day.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/carnegie-hall-to-remain-closed-on-tuesday/', 'snippet': 'Carnegie Hall, which has canceled all events since Oct. 28 because of a dangling crane boom across West 57th Street, will remain closed for at least another day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite the reopening of West 57th Street on Sunday, Carnegie Hall was forced to cancel concerts on Tuesday because utilities had not been restored to the building. Carnegie said the Emerson String Quartet concert in the Stern Auditorium would take place on Jan. 7, and a performance by the Belcea Quartet in Zankel Hall, part of the Carnegie complex, was canceled. Carnegie has canceled or postponed 24 events since Oct. 28, after high winds from Hurricane Sandy left a crane boom dangling at an apartment tower being built across the street. The boom was secured over the weekend, allowing the area to reopen to traffic. Carnegie said it hoped to know on Tuesday when utilities would be restored.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carnegie Hall to Remain Closed on Tuesday', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Belcea Quartet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emerson String Quartet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T22:47:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3acef931-53a5-5cf7-985c-a3863fb09c15', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3acef931-53a5-5cf7-985c-a3863fb09c15'}, {'abstract': 'A professional golfer has flown more than 15 million miles, and once scared a woman who thought he had died in the aisle of a plane.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/business/a-golf-pro-learns-to-be-comfortable-in-the-air.html', 'snippet': 'A professional golfer has flown more than 15 million miles, and once scared a woman who thought he had died in the aisle of a plane.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALL I can say is, I would like to meet the person who has flown more than me. I have been traveling for about 60 years, 90 percent of which has been on commercial airlines. I’ve logged more than 15 million miles. \xa0', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/business/Flier/Flier-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/business/Flier/Flier-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1329, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 