 search queries about the presidential candidates and a look at corporation getting hacked and how much they tell anyone.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/todays-scuttlebot-coca-cola-hacking-and-class-photos/', 'snippet': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Monday’s selection includes questions about why students take phone photos in class, common search queries about the presidential candidates...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently.\xa0See more here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Coca-Cola Hacking, and Class Photos', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T23:14:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c911700-8e57-594e-bb4c-43ae13d08d50', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c911700-8e57-594e-bb4c-43ae13d08d50'}, {'abstract': 'Hurricane Sandy was logged as Category 1 — the weakest — but that did not take account of the low pressure that increased the size of its storm surge and widened its impact.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/science/a-call-to-rethink-storm-classification.html', 'snippet': 'Hurricane Sandy was logged as Category 1 — the weakest — but that did not take account of the low pressure that increased the size of its storm surge and widened its impact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some researchers say Hurricane Sandy should prompt scientists to devise new methods to categorize coastal storms. S. Jeffress Williams, a coastal scientist with the United States Geological Survey and the University of Hawaii, noted that Sandy was barely a Category 1 hurricane — the weakest — on the widely used Saffir-Simpson scale, which measures hurricane intensity largely according to wind speeds. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Call to Rethink Storm Classification', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Call to Rethink Storm Classification', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Geological Survey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-05T23:26:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cornelia Dean', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cornelia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dean', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}