election on Tuesday, the historical memory of the race might turn on the role played by Hurricane Sandy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Factoring Hurricane Sandy Into the Election Equation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Factoring Hurricane Sandy Into the Election Equation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T00:47:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78acb488-8d22-52e0-b33e-e3a0613fbb8c', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78acb488-8d22-52e0-b33e-e3a0613fbb8c'}, {'abstract': 'Twenty-five fans, most of them high school students from Long Island who were grounded by Hurricane Sandy, were initially told they would not be able to exchange their tickets if they missed Monday night’s Nets game.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/hoping-to-save-a-lost-field-trip/', 'snippet': 'Twenty-five fans, most of them high school students from Long Island who were grounded by Hurricane Sandy, were initially told they would not be able to exchange their tickets if they missed Monday night’s Nets game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty-five seats in Section 214 were empty when the Nets took the court Monday night at Barclays Center. Twenty-five fans, most of them high school students from Long Island, had been grounded by Hurricane Sandy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hoping to Save a Lost Field Trip', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T00:49:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81e4d35d-4366-5e69-aa21-dd1260c85081', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81e4d35d-4366-5e69-aa21-dd1260c85081'}, {'abstract': 'The Vatican computer expert accused of aiding and abetting the theft of the pope’s confidential papers began his trial on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/world/europe/the-vatican-leaks-trial-part-ii.html', 'snippet': 'The Vatican computer expert accused of aiding and abetting the theft of the pope’s confidential papers began his trial on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Vatican computer expert accused of helping Pope Benedict XVI’s former butler of stealing the pope’s confidential papers had no reason to risk his career to help the butler because he did not know him well, his lawyer argued on Monday in the opening hearing of the second trial related to a security breach at the Vatican. The pope’s former butler, Paolo Gabriele, was convicted of leaking the stolen documents to the news media. The computer expert, Claudio Sciarpelletti, 48, is charged with helping Mr. Gabriele by giving “wavering and contradictory” answers to the authorities about a closed envelope addressed personally to Mr. Gabriele and containing material that was found in his desk, the indictment read. Mr. Sciarpelletti’s lawyer explained his client’s contradictory statements as a reflection of his confused “emotional state.” The trial was adjourned until Saturday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Vatican: Leaks Trial, Part II', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Vatican: Leaks Trial, Part II', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sciarpelletti, Claudio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gabriele, Paolo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vatican City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T00:50:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gaia Pianigiani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gaia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec58eaba-25d2-5cbc-8f63-667c131a80b9', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec58eaba-25d2-5cbc-8f63-667c131a80b9'}, {'abstract': 'Eric Ritter of Queens broke the Class C speed record by running 338 miles an hour at the Bonneville Salt Flats.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/speed-king-of-queens-breaks-a-record/', 'snippet': 'Eric Ritter of Queens broke the Class C speed record by running 338 miles an hour at the Bonneville Salt Flats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Queens native Eric Ritter tripped the timing lights last month at the Southern California Timing Association‘s World Finals at Utah’s Bonneville Salt Flats, setting a record for its engine class at 339 miles an hour, he also earned a lifetime membership in the exclusive 300 m.p.h. chapter of Bonneville’s prestigious “200 MPH Club.” In the process he became the first New Yorker to earn that distinction, according to S.C.T.A. records. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Speed King of Queens Breaks a Record', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Records and Achievements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ritter, Eric', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bonneville Salt Flats (Utah)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T00:53:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Louise Ann Noeth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Louise', 'middlename': 'Ann', 'lastname': 'Noeth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1415db0-8b65-5c68-8e39-63bf12c784e3', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1415db0-8b65-5c68-8e39-63bf12c784e3'}, {'abstract': 'Hong Kong’s standing as a key Asian location for foreign firms is under threat, analysts say, due to skyrocketing rents and a shortage of commercial and residential space.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.ny