'pub_date': '2012-11-06T01:56:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winnie Hu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e28637dd-0b66-542d-a131-04da28188472', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e28637dd-0b66-542d-a131-04da28188472'}, {'abstract': 'The killings of two Guatemalans by a state sharpshooter raises many questions about policies on shooting at vehicles and the handling of human- and drug-trafficking cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/opinion/a-texas-injustice-at-the-border.html', 'snippet': 'The killings of two Guatemalans by a state sharpshooter raises many questions about policies on shooting at vehicles and the handling of human- and drug-trafficking cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Which is more unbelievable: that a state trooper in Texas decided to stop a fleeing pickup by shooting at it from a helicopter, even though the truck was crammed with people, or that nothing in the official policies of the trooper’s employer, the Texas Department of Public Safety, forbids such lethal recklessness?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Texas Injustice', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Texas Injustice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T01:59:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/750b661a-66f3-56a0-818c-9fd671e3833c', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/750b661a-66f3-56a0-818c-9fd671e3833c'}, {'abstract': '“Uncertainty” has become the watchword over the last several years as an explanation — or perhaps an excuse — for the economy’s slow growth, for the lack of hiring by business and for the volatility in the stock market.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/05/the-election-wont-solve-all-puzzles/', 'snippet': '“Uncertainty” has become the watchword over the last several years as an explanation — or perhaps an excuse — for the economy’s slow growth, for the lack of hiring by business and for the volatility in the stock market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here comes more uncertainty.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Election Won’t Solve All Puzzles', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Election Won’t Solve All Puzzles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T02:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ross Sorkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea9bea28-695c-5886-9aed-d878cf2d1623', 'word_count': 958, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea9bea28-695c-5886-9aed-d878cf2d1623'}, {'abstract': 'Republican hopes for control of the United States Senate have been curtailed by rigid or unappealing candidates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/opinion/the-battle-for-the-senate.html', 'snippet': 'Republican hopes for control of the United States Senate have been curtailed by rigid or unappealing candidates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Republicans intent on unraveling President Obama’s accomplishments, electing Mitt Romney has been only one part of the equation. Almost as important was installing a Republican majority in the United States Senate, where 50 votes (plus the vice president) would be necessary to repeal much of health care reform, roll back tax increases on the rich and gut social welfare programs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Battle for the Senate', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Battle for the Senate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T02:03:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec649ce8-f18b-5657-bf99-5ffa1922cc25', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec649ce8-f18b-5657-bf99-5ffa1922cc25'}, {'abstract': 'Coach Tom Coughlin does not want to say his team is in a slump, but quarterback Eli Manning’s performance has been mediocre in the last two games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/sports/football/eli-mannings-poor-play-lately-is-a-key-to-giants-problems.html', 'snippet': 'Coach Tom Coughlin does not want to say his team is in a slump, but quarterback Eli Manning’s performance has been mediocre in the last two games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Neither Tom Coughlin nor Eli Manning was particularly quick to embrace the term that many observers, and even one or two players in their quieter moments, have used to describe the Giants’ offense over the past few weeks.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/06/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 603, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1206, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/06/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 