'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T02:41:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53f37b5d-1e94-56b5-a30a-1749bab5e188', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53f37b5d-1e94-56b5-a30a-1749bab5e188'}, {'abstract': 'In Barbados, Andrew Branch, who has quadriplegic cerebral palsy, went to the museum and the zoo; in Brooklyn, he is more or less trapped in his apartment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/nyregion/stuck-on-2nd-floor-daydreaming-of-going-outside.html', 'snippet': 'In Barbados, Andrew Branch, who has quadriplegic cerebral palsy, went to the museum and the zoo; in Brooklyn, he is more or less trapped in his apartment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wearing a baggy gray sweatshirt, looking like a small, shy Buddha, Andrew Branch sat on the clean hardwood floor. His legs, which he cannot fully extend, were curled under him. His wheelchair offers neither maneuverability nor comfort, so he spends a lot of time on all fours in a cluttered, one-bedroom apartment in Crown Heights, Brooklyn, parts of which are covered in protective plastic. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/nyregion/06NEEDIEST/06NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/nyregion/06NEEDIEST/06NEEDIEST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/nyregion/06NEEDIEST/06NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/06/nyregion/06NEEDIEST/06NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/nyregion/06NEEDIEST/06NEEDIEST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stuck on the 2nd Floor, Daydreaming of Going Outside', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stuck on the 2nd Floor, Daydreaming of Going Outside', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office for People With Developmental Disabilities (NYS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cerebral Palsy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Cerebral Palsy Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Community Services', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T02:41:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Higgins DeSmet', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': 'Higgins', 'lastname': 'DeSmet', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fecc6697-e362-51c1-adca-097435df3855', 'word_count': 850, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fecc6697-e362-51c1-adca-097435df3855'}, {'abstract': 'More and more groups are emerging to make protecting women — and shaming the do-nothing police — a cause, combating a longstanding problem in Egypt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/world/middleeast/egyptian-vigilantes-crack-down-on-abuse-of-women.html', 'snippet': 'More and more groups are emerging to make protecting women — and shaming the do-nothing police — a cause, combating a longstanding problem in Egypt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — The young activists lingered on the streets around Tahrir Square, scrutinizing the crowds of holiday revelers. Suddenly, they charged, pushing people aside and chasing down a young man. As the captive thrashed to get away, the activists pounded his shoulders, flipped him around and spray-painted a message on his back: “I’m a harasser.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/world/JP-EGYPT/JP-EGYPT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/06/world/JP-EGYPT/JP-EGYPT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/world/JP-EGYPT/JP-EGYPT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/world/JP-EGYPT/JP-EGYPT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'super