: 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd42a833-be61-5851-914f-e798be7431b4'}, {'abstract': 'The father of Brendan Marrocco, who lost his limbs in Iraq, said his family was “a lot better off than other people” after his son’s custom-built home in Staten Island flooded during Hurricane Sandy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/nyregion/after-home-is-damaged-quadruple-amputee-shows-concern-for-others.html', 'snippet': 'The father of Brendan Marrocco, who lost his limbs in Iraq, said his family was “a lot better off than other people” after his son’s custom-built home in Staten Island flooded during Hurricane Sandy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The custom-built house had every imaginable bell and whistle aimed at giving a young Staten Island native who had lost his limbs in the Iraq war a measure of independence — wheelchair ramps and an elevator to the second story, plus electronic controls to adjust cabinets and work faucets at the touch of an iPad.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/nyregion/06staten2/06brendan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/nyregion/06staten2/06brendan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1360, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/nyregion/06staten2/06staten2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/06/nyregion/06staten2/06staten2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/nyregion/06staten2/06staten2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Home Is Damaged, Quadruple Amputee and Relatives Show Concern for Others', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marrocco, Brendan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T05:04:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Leigh Cowan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'Leigh', 'lastname': 'Cowan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0765995a-e46b-56c9-83b7-e9f34f7d6508', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0765995a-e46b-56c9-83b7-e9f34f7d6508'}, {'abstract': 'Mikhail D. Prokhorov, the Nets owner spoke with Herb Turetzky, the Nets scorekeeper and perhaps the man who best understands the franchise’s past.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/in-brooklyn-an-eye-on-the-past-and-excitement-for-the-future/', 'snippet': 'Mikhail D. Prokhorov, the Nets owner spoke with Herb Turetzky, the Nets scorekeeper and perhaps the man who best understands the franchise’s past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Oct. 23, 1967, Herb Turetzky went to see the New Jersey Americans play the Pittsburgh Pipers in their first game in the American Basketball Association. Turetzky ventured to the Teaneck Armory to watch good friend Tony Jackson, the all-American from St. John’s, play. By the end of the night, Turetzky was the Americans’ official scorekeeper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Brooklyn, an Eye on the Past and Excitement for the Future', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prokhorov, Mikhail D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T05:29:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Appleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f4e11cc-6e94-5152-8106-1f40b7ff068d', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f4e11cc-6e94-5152-8106-1f40b7ff068d'}, {'abstract': 'John McEnroe just wanted to win and give New York City, his hometown, a good show, but Pat Rafter stood in his way at the PowerShares Series champions tour event.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/mcenroe-returns-to-madison-square-garden-to-face-younger-foes/', 'snippet': 'John McEnroe just wanted to win and give New York City, his hometown, a good show, but Pat Rafter stood in his way at the PowerShares Series champions tour event.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Talking to the news media hours before his PowerShares Series match at Madison Square Garden on Monday, John McEnroe kept looking over his shoulder, eyeing his younger competitors —Andre Agassi, Pete Sampras and Pat Rafter — as they took deafening thwacks at the ball.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McEnroe Returns to Madison Square Garden to Face Younger Foes', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T05:43:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By NICHOLAS MCCARVEL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MCCARVEL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/feef29b3-4c4e-5f04-a64e-987147e81b1e', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/feef29b3-4c4e-5f04-a64e-987147e81b1e'}, {'abstract': 'Although most New York public schools reopened on Monday, some were still closed, and their pupils had to move elsewhere temporarily.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/nyregion/100000001887223/back-to-school-for-some.html', 'snippet': 'Although most New York public schools reopened on Monday, some were still closed, and their pupils had to move elsewhere temporarily.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although most New York public schools reopened on Monday, some were still closed, and their pupils had to move elsewhere temporarily.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/nyregion/video-schoolsback/video-schoolsback-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/05/nyregion/video-schoolsback/video-schoolsback-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/nyregion/video-schoolsback/video-schoolsback-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/05/nyre