', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/53259d84-d2cd-54a4-8e43-5d645a1e044b', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53259d84-d2cd-54a4-8e43-5d645a1e044b'}, {'abstract': 'It’s Election Day in America and you know what that means. Yes, lawyers fanning out to polling stations from sea to shining sea.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/the-u-s-election-campaign-that-was-and-what-to-watch-tonight/', 'snippet': 'It’s Election Day in America and you know what that means. Yes, lawyers fanning out to polling stations from sea to shining sea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — The debate about the place and the role of the United States in a rapidly changing world grows ever louder and, sometimes it seems, more urgent: China is ascendant while the liberal free-market West is beset by a crisis of confidence, cleavages between politicians and their constituents and ideological civil wars; the United States is a debtor nation, indebted to China, the second largest economy in the world after the United States and closing fast; America, supposedly the mightiest military in the world, has recently fought two wars in the Middle East and won neither. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/blogs/06rdv-voting-us/06rdv-voting-us-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/blogs/06rdv-voting-us/06rdv-voting-us-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1443, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The U.S. Election Campaign That Was and What to Watch Tonight', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T06:17:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marcus Mabry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marcus', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mabry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dcc33f2-6fcf-5787-a0aa-d62fcea07086', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dcc33f2-6fcf-5787-a0aa-d62fcea07086'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/news-quiz-november-6-2012-2/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | November 6, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T06:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Taylor Adams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Taylor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Adams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c31bb76d-b547-5e7f-9b25-a21441877815', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c31bb76d-b547-5e7f-9b25-a21441877815'}, {'abstract': 'The Playboy Club’s opening here prompts a redesign of the cleavage-baring bunny costume.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/from-india-a-more-modest-playboy-bunny/', 'snippet': 'The Playboy Club’s opening here prompts a redesign of the cleavage-baring bunny costume.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the Playboy Club gets set to open in Goa this winter, its first venture in India, one pressing question keeps cropping up: What, exactly, will the bunnies wear? ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From India, a More Modest Playboy Bunny', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bunny Makeover For a New Locale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Playboy Magazine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Goa (India)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T06:42:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c182640a-557f-5387-8612-a1bb440af357', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c182640a-557f-5387-8612-a1bb440af357'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama appears to have gained ground in the closing days of the race: among 12 national polls published on Monday, he led Mitt Romney by an average of 1.6 percentage points.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/nov-5-late-poll-gains-for-obama-leave-romney-with-longer-odds/', 'snippet': 'President Obama appears to have gained ground in the closing days of the race: among 12 national polls published on Monday, he led Mitt Romney by an average of 1.6 percentage points.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney has always had difficulty drawing a winning Electoral College hand. Even during his best period of polling, in the week or two after the first presidential debate in Denver, he never quite pulled ahead in the polling averages in Ohio and other states that would allow him to secure 270 electoral votes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nov. 5: Late Poll Gains for Obama Leave Romney With Longer Odds', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T06:43:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e183f90-d195-5304-a51f-d6cfda8cb20a', 'word_count': 1247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e183f90-d195-5304-a51f-d6cfda8cb20a'}, {'abstract': 'At his final rally before Election Day, Mitt Romney took the stage after 11 p.m. after a brief performance by Kid Rock. The crowd shouted “U-S-A” and waved “Romney-Ryan” and “Women for Mitt” signs. The Republican candidate took it all in.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/in-new-hampshire-romneys-last-pre-election-rally/', 'snippet': 'At his final rally before Election Day, Mitt Romney took the stage after 11 p.m. after a brief performance by Kid Rock. The crowd shouted “U-S-A” and waved “Romney-Ryan” and “Women for Mitt” signs. The Republican candidate took it all in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — Even Mitt Romney looked a little surprised to see a crowd of 13,000 and several thousand more waiting in the below-freezing temperatures to get into the Verizon Wireless Arena here Monday night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In New Hampshire, Romney’s Last Pre-Election Rally', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Ann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T07:40:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a6b66f4-dd09-55d4-bce5-a3760d10c8d7', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a6b66f4-dd09-55d4-bce5-a3760d10c8d7'}, {'abstract': 'News, arts, fashion and sports in today’s International Herald Tribune.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/iht-quick-read-nov-6/', 'snippet': 'News, arts, fashion and sports in today’s International Herald Tribune.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWS Amid corruption scandals and the appearance of excessive lobbying, the European Parliament has become a symbol of how institutions designed to build a united Europe have faltered. James Kanter reports from Brussels.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/201