s put ideology ahead of economic reality, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/republicans-censor-what-they-cant-refute/', 'snippet': 'By forcing the Congressional Research Service to withdraw a report that found no link between tax cuts on the wealthy and economic growth, Republicans put ideology ahead of economic reality, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul. He is the author of “The Benefit and the Burden: Tax Reform – Why We Need It and What It Will Take.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Censor What They Can’t Refute', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Research Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T11:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9ee457f-c81a-5d39-a614-605e47851a73', 'word_count': 1079, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9ee457f-c81a-5d39-a614-605e47851a73'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com