81', 'word_count': 1204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c18f5b67-cb10-58fd-b990-9620b6da7781'}, {'abstract': 'After a devastating storm, the question is front and center: Should New York City armor itself with steel and concrete at a cost of billions of dollars?', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/the-big-barrier-question/', 'snippet': 'After a devastating storm, the question is front and center: Should New York City armor itself with steel and concrete at a cost of billions of dollars?', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the storm chugged toward the Eastern Seaboard at 3 p.m. on Oct. 27, \xa0an engineering crew in Stamford, Conn., was at the ready. It was time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Big Barrier Question', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Levees and Dams', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARMY CORPS OF ENGINEERS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Stamford (Conn)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T13:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/776e7ed4-17ee-55cd-9215-674c8e7c481a', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/776e7ed4-17ee-55cd-9215-674c8e7c481a'}, {'abstract': 'At Free Republic, an online forum for passionate right-wing discussion, the commentariat’s divided over how best to respond to a fatal border shooting in La Joya.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/a-shooting-in-broad-daylight-rationalized/', 'snippet': 'At Free Republic, an online forum for passionate right-wing discussion, the commentariat’s divided over how best to respond to a fatal border shooting in La Joya.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is widespread concern, disgust and outrage in Texas over a fatal border shooting last month in La Joya, a few miles from the Rio Grande. A state trooper\xa0 shot at a fleeing truck packed not with drugs – as he apparently believed – but with Guatemalan immigrants, two of whom were killed. That the trooper was in a helicopter, in broad daylight, and should have seen that the truck’s apparent contraband was human, not chemical, have intensified the calls for investigations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Shooting in Broad Daylight, Rationalized', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T13:01:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78497b19-062e-50d0-9aff-9ae1a81daf38', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78497b19-062e-50d0-9aff-9ae1a81daf38'}, {'abstract': 'The government of Laos said on Tuesday that it would build a huge hydroelectric dam on the Mekong River despite concerns that it could do irreparable damage to the environment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/world/asia/laos-presses-ahead-with-mekong-dam-project.html', 'snippet': 'The government of Laos said on Tuesday that it would build a huge hydroelectric dam on the Mekong River despite concerns that it could do irreparable damage to the environment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — Ignoring criticism that a huge hydroelectric dam could irreparably damage the ecology of the Mekong River, the government of Laos said on Tuesday that it was pushing ahead with the multibillion-dollar project, the first dam to be built on the lower portion of the iconic river.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Laos Presses Ahead With Mekong Dam Project', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Laos to Proceed With Dam Project on Mekong River', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydroelectric Power', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mekong River', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Laos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Levees and Dams', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T13:07:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Fuller and Poypiti Amatatham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Poypiti', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amatatham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6df004e-7bce-5494-9182-79d79b83dc69', 'word_count': 690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6df004e-7bce-5494-9182-79d79b83dc69'}, {'abstract': 'Myanmar’s recent political liberalization has attracted feminists and advocates of women’s rights as well as businesses.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/a-fresh-start-for-women-in-myanmar/', 'snippet': 'Myanmar’s recent political liberalization has attracted feminists and advocates of women’s rights as well as businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — Feminists, like business people, are sensing opportunity amid the recent political liberalization in Myanmar.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/blogs/06rdv-myanmar-femalefactor/06rdv-myanmar-femalefactor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/blogs/06rdv-myanmar-femalefactor/06rdv-myanmar-femalefactor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1378, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/blogs/06rdv-myanmar-femalefactor/06rdv-myanmar-femalefactor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/06/blogs/06rdv-myanmar-femalefactor/06rdv-myanmar-femalefactor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/blogs/06rdv-myanmar-femalefactor/06rdv-myanmar-femalefactor-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fresh Start for Women in Myanmar?', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Millennium Development Goals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Asean', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Laos', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vientiane (Laos)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T13:15:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25f2330d-6b34-59f3-99f8-252fe7789776', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25f2330d-6b34-59f3-99f8-252fe7789776'}, {'abstract': 'Reassessing flu shots, states accommodate voters displaced by Hurricane Sandy, hacking of tax records puts states on guard and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/tuesday-reading-reassessing-flu-shots/', 'snippet': 'Reassessing flu shots, states accommodate voters displaced by Hurricane Sandy, hacking of tax records puts states on guard and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Reassessing Flu Shots', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T13:17:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78407876-c11c-56d7-a36a-7a3b8fe05cb5', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78407876-c11c-56d7-a36a-7a3b8fe05cb5'}, {'abstract': 'It may be Election Day, but the outcome won’t end uncertainty for Wall Street. | Morgan Stanley is betting that Colm Kelleher has what it takes to revive its securities unit. | Mark E. Tucker, chief executive and president of the AIA Group, is joining Goldman Sachs’s board.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/the-big-day-but-more-uncertainty-to-come/', 'snippet': 'It may be Election Day, but the outcome won’t end uncertainty for Wall Street. | Morgan Stanley is betting that Colm Kelleher has what it takes to revive its securities unit. | Mark E. Tucker, chief executive and president of the AIA Group, is joi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE BIG DAY, BUT MORE UNCERTAINTY TO COME \xa0|\xa0 It may be Election Day, but the outcome won’t end uncertainty for Wall Street,  Andrew Ross Sorkin writes in the DealBook column. Regardless of whether President Obama or Mitt Romney wins, the business world will face a series of political unknowns that could last through much of next year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Big Day, but More Uncertainty to Come', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T13:17:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e98f8de-0774-5d32-9313-e363f587abb8', 'word_count': 1545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e98f8de-0774-5d32-9313-e363f587abb8'}, {'abstract': 'Voters returned President Obama to the White House, but he will face a Congress with the same divisions that marked his first term.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/us/politics/obama-romney-presidential-election-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Voters returned President Obama to the White House, but he will face a Congress with the same divisions that marked his first term.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barack Hussein Obama was re-elected president of the United States on Tuesday, overcoming powerful economic headwinds, a lock-step resistance to his agenda by Republicans in Congress and an unprecedented torrent of advertising as a divided nation voted to give him more time.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Divided U.S. Gives Obama More Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Obama's Night: Tops Romney For 2nd Term In Bruising Run; Democrats Turn Back G.O.P Bid For Senate", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T13:24:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny and Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/973387f3-d940-5702-8ad6-d86e70b5d210', 'word_count': 2026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/973387f3-d940-5702-8ad6-d86e70b5d210'}, {'abstract': 'Approval from the new head of the Coptic Church could be the best boost to Mohamed Morsi’s democratic credentials.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/could-the-new-coptic-pope-be-the-egyptian-presidents-best-ally/', 'snippet': 'Approval from the new head of the Coptic Church could be the best boost to Mohamed Morsi’s democratic credentials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — The weight of the moment showed on the child’s face, his bowl cut framing a tense expression. His serious brown eyes stared fixedly as prayers were recited. Then he was blindfolded, and it was all over in an instant. The long-bearded bishop grabbed his hand, shoved it into a glass bowl that contained papers with the names of the three contenders, and the boy pulled one out. The bishop slowly unfurled the piece of paper, revealing the name of Bishop Tawadros.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pope and the President', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T13:26:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By ISSANDR EL AMRANI', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Issandr', 'middlename': 'El', 'lastname': 'AMRANI', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f200048-8b2e-5dbe-8083-68eab3566e14', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f200048-8b2e-5dbe-8083-68eab3566e14'}, {'abstract': 'You can make your own animated GIF files on your computer, the Web or even your smartphone.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/qa-animating-your-own-gif/', 'snippet': 'You can make your own animated GIF files on your computer, the Web or even your smartphone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Animating Your Own GIF', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Converting Photos\r\nTo Animated GIFs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T13:30:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.D. BIERSDORFER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01189759-526d-56c5-a8e1-7d2718b4df8d', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01189759-526d-56c5-a8e1-7d2718b4df8d'}, {'abstract': 'The centuries-old Muslim tomb has stopped allowing women to enter the area where a saint is buried, activist says.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/mumbais-historic-haji-ali-bans-women-from-most-sacred-area/', 'snippet': 'The centuries-old Muslim tomb has stopped allowing women to enter the area where a saint is buried, activist says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An iconic image of Mumbai – the Haji Ali mausoleum, 500 yards off the shoreline in the glittering Arabian sea – attracted controversy Tuesday after a Muslim women’s group said women have been banned from entering the inner tomb. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mumbai’s Historic Haji Ali Bans Women From Most Sacred Area', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mosques', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shariah (Islamic Law)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T13:32:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sruthi Gottipati', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sruthi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gottipati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6eff43b-e023-5078-8eb5-78924530cc11', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6eff43b-e023-5078-8eb5-78924530cc11'}, {'abstract': 'Europe only earned a rare mention during the course of the U.S. election campaign. But the economic fate of the Continent is likely to loom large in the calculations of whoever occupies the White House for the next four years.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/europes-problems-likely-to-loom-post-election/', 'snippet': 'Europe only earned a rare mention during the course of the U.S. election campaign. But the economic fate of the Continent is likely to loom large in the calculations of whoever occupies the White House for the next four years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — As Americans headed out on Tuesday to choose their next president, there was no disguising the fact that Europe was feeling singularly left out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe’s Problems Likely to Loom Post-Election', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T13:36:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d77452f-ae8b-59c5-974c-182c564bc877', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d77452f-ae8b-59c5-974c-182c564bc877'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: In the 2012 election, it feels as if New York has been neglected more than necessary. But the city wasn’t totally abandoned by White House aspirants. We had our moments.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/a-campaign-season-of-neglect-with-some-notable-exceptions/', 'snippet': 'The Day: In the 2012 election, it feels as if New York has been neglected more than necessary. But the city wasn’t totally abandoned by White House aspirants. We had our moments.', 'lead_paragraph': ' With Election Day upon us, New Yorkers can finally exhale. The long season of our being ignored by the presidential campaigns is finally over. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Campaign Season of Neglect, With Some Notable Exceptions', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T13:43:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce4ea7ef-3ef8-54f8-b822-2f3951d800b0', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce4ea7ef-3ef8-54f8-b822-2f3951d800b0'}, {'abstract': 'Honolulu’s Chinatown, a creative hub of the city, is now evolving into an eating and shopping destination.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/hawaiian-punch/', 'snippet': 'Honolulu’s Chinatown, a creative hub of the city, is now evolving into an eating and shopping destination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the early 2000s, Honolulu’s Chinatown — a cluster of downtown streets lined with attractive turn-of-the-20th-century buildings — began its transformation from a seedy red-light district into the city’s creative hub. Galleries and bars popped up in the once-empty storefronts, and the First Friday art party, when artists open their studios, bands play in the streets, and everything stays open late, became one of the hottest events in town. In the past year, Chinatown’s evolution has taken a new turn, as a number of restaurants and boutiques have set up shop in the neighborhood. They’re bringing a welcome dose of urbanity to the party — and with a distinctly Hawaiian feel.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hawaiian Punch', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hawaiian Punch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Honolulu (Hawaii)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T14:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathan Lump', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lump', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2effed2e-57fd-57de-983c-279c0775c762', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2effed2e-57fd-57de-983c-279c0775c762'}, {'abstract': 'The versatility of the American flag as seen at campaign events.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/the-caucus-click-stars-and-stripes-from-the-campaign-trail/', 'snippet': 'The versatility of the American flag as seen at campaign events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The versatility of the American flag as seen at campaign events. Go to Slide Show »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Caucus Click: Stars and Stripes From the Campaign Trail', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T14:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66d0a2a0-e1fb-57f3-b3d7-f3db06638c14', 'word_count': 16, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66d0a2a0-e1fb-57f3-b3d7-f3db06638c14'}, {'abstract': 'Cecilia Chang, a former dean of St. John’s University, was found dead; her death is being investigated as a suicide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/nyregion/cecilia-chang-ex-dean-of-st-johns-found-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Cecilia Chang, a former dean of St. John’s University, was found dead; her death is being investigated as a suicide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hers was the kind of rise through the academic ranks that could have epitomized the American dream, if not for the way she crashed. Fresh from Taiwan in 1975, she enrolled at St. John’s University as a student in Asian studies, becoming a dean in just five years and, soon after, winning the ear of the university’s top echelon as she raised more than $20 million for the school. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/07dean-web/07dean-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 942, 'width': 667, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/07dean-web/07dean-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 942, 'width': 667, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/07dean-web/07dean-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/07dean-web/07dean-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/07dean-web/07dean-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Dean of St. John’s, on Trial for Stealing Over $1 Million, Is Found Dead at Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Dean of St. John’s, on Trial for Stealing Over $1 Million, Is Found Dead at Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chang, Cecilia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "St John's University", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T14:01:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mosi Secret and William K. Rashbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mosi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Secret', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3da4e431-5410-5d98-bea5-4d50cb8ceded', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3da4e431-5410-5d98-bea5-4d50cb8ceded'}, {'abstract': 'John Malkovich, who played the Vicomte de Valmont in Stephen Frears’s 1988 film version of “Dangerous Liaisons,” will direct a French-language production of the play – which adds some modern-day twists – presented by Shakespeare Theater Company.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/malkovich-bringing-a-modernized-dangerous-liaisons-to-washington/', 'snippet': 'John Malkovich, who played the Vicomte de Valmont in Stephen Frears’s 1988 film version of “Dangerous Liaisons,” will direct a French-language production of the play – which adds some modern-day twists – presented by Shakespeare Theater Company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Evidently it wasn’t enough for John Malkovich to manipulate the lives of the Marquise de Merteuil, Cécile de Volanges and Madame de Tourvel for his own amusement in “Dangerous Liaisons” — now he has to direct the action of everyone in that story. And the Shakespeare Theater Company is giving him the opportunity: The Washington-based theater company said it would present a new stage production of “Les Liaisons Dangereuses,” the Christopher Hampton play adapted from the Choderlos de Laclos novel, directed by Mr. Malkovich, who played the Vicomte de Valmont in Stephen Frears‘s 1988 film version of “Dangerous Liaisons.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/arts/malkovich/malkovich-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 581, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/arts/malkovich/malkovich-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 581, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/arts/malkovich/malkovich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/06/arts/malkovich/malkovich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/arts/malkovich/malkovich-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 126, 'width': 126, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Malkovich to Direct a Modernized ‘Dangerous Liaisons’ in Washington', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hampton, Christopher', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malkovich, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shakespeare Theater Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T14:13:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11206765-9566-59ac-817c-20599b23fca2', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11206765-9566-59ac-817c-20599b23fca2'}, {'abstract': 'The pianist Andras Schiff postponed a performance in Maryland after the piano he uses had already made the trip. As a result, the instrument, which would otherwise have been trapped in Steinway Hall in an area closed by Hurricane Sandy, was available for a second New York recital.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/piano-travels-without-pianist/', 'snippet': 'The pianist Andras Schiff postponed a performance in Maryland after the piano he uses had already made the trip. As a result, the instrument, which would otherwise have been trapped in Steinway Hall in an area closed by Hurricane Sandy, was availa...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many pianists form a close bond with a particular instrument, and the more prominent performers have the luxury of touring with their favorites. So it is for Andras Schiff, who performed Book 1 of Bach’s “Well-Tempered Clavier” on Oct. 27 at the 92nd Street Y on his preferred Steinway. With the onslaught of Hurricane Sandy two days later, a fluke allowed Mr. Schiff to use the same instrument last Thursday in a performance of Book 2.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Piano Travels Without Pianist', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Well-Traveled Clavier', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiff, Andras', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ninety-Second Street Y', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T14:45:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4689e9e-f195-5955-9d24-c6eade3d2feb', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4689e9e-f195-5955-9d24-c6eade3d2feb'}, {'abstract': 'Also, an array of big-name performers campaigned with President Obama in the final days of the race, and AOL reported higher-than-expected revenue for the third quarter.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/the-breakfast-meeting-the-fox-news-msnbc-campaign-and-adult-films-anti-h-i-v-strategy/', 'snippet': 'Also, an array of big-name performers campaigned with President Obama in the final days of the race, and AOL reported higher-than-expected revenue for the third quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This presidential election, Fox News and MSNBC have become the poles that mainstream, two-party politics in the United States revolve around, Jeremy W. Peters reports, as they have pushed their stridency to new levels. Not only does that mean that the candidate for the other side receives barely any positive coverage, according to research, but the negative coverage can turn disturbingly personal. Both Fox News and MSNBC have idly speculated on the mental health of candidates on the presidential tickets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: The Fox News-MSNBC Campaign, and Sex Films’ Anti-H.I.V. Strategy', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condoms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Springsteen, Bruce', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AOL', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MSNBC', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T14:46:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f001889b-46b4-553c-8b59-712b3f2be6b3', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f001889b-46b4-553c-8b59-712b3f2be6b3'}, {'abstract': 'An explosion on Tuesday killed dozens of people, but there were conflicting accounts of what caused the blast, and some reports put the death toll higher.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/world/middleeast/blast-rocks-iraq-military-base-killing-26.html', 'snippet': 'An explosion on Tuesday killed dozens of people, but there were conflicting accounts of what caused the blast, and some reports put the death toll higher.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — A blast at a military base north of Baghdad killed more than two dozen people on Tuesday, but there were conflicting accounts of what caused the explosion.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bombing at Iraqi Base Kills Dozens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bombing At Iraqi Base Kills Dozens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Bases and Installations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T14:58:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Yasir Ghazi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Yasir', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ghazi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29c95a23-6b1f-55f6-b7c9-e24e8acc64b4', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29c95a23-6b1f-55f6-b7c9-e24e8acc64b4'}, {'abstract': 'The Arts Dealers Association of America announced on Tuesday that it will provide grants and loans to galleries that have been unable to conduct business since the hurricane.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/an-aid-program-for-hard-hit-new-york-galleries/', 'snippet': 'The Arts Dealers Association of America announced on Tuesday that it will provide grants and loans to galleries that have been unable to conduct business since the hurricane.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As art galleries and museums on the East Coast come to terms with loss and damage to their collections by Hurricane Sandy, a trade group, the Art Dealers Association of America, has assembled an aid program that will help New York City galleries that have been hardest hit by the flooding. The group, which was founded in 1962 and has 175 members in 25 cities, announced on Tuesday that it would provide grants and loans to galleries in Zone A – including those that are not members of the organization – that have been unable to conduct business since the hurricane.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Aid Program for Hard-Hit New York Galleries', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aid Program Begun For Hard-Hit Galleries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ART DEALERS ASSN OF AMERICA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T15:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb982b33-7141-5bea-92bf-a5a32c795c39', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb982b33-7141-5bea-92bf-a5a32c795c39'}, {'abstract': 'The murder of the British businessman, Neil Heywood, is still seen as stemming from a financial dispute, but the intelligence links add an enticing subplot to his death.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/world/asia/chinas-security-ministry-suspected-neil-heywood-british-businessman-was-a-spy.html', 'snippet': 'The murder of the British businessman, Neil Heywood, is still seen as stemming from a financial dispute, but the intelligence links add an enticing subplot to his death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — China’s external intelligence agency, the Ministry of State Security, suspected a British businessman of being a spy before his murder last year at the hands of a senior politician’s wife, ac