pub_date': '2012-11-06T16:29:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig and Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c33446a3-da0b-5781-aa77-4de2e5993462', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c33446a3-da0b-5781-aa77-4de2e5993462'}, {'abstract': 'The presence of cellphones has become ubiquitous during the campaign, whether for taking photographs or shoring up support.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/the-caucus-click-cellphone-nation/', 'snippet': 'The presence of cellphones has become ubiquitous during the campaign, whether for taking photographs or shoring up support.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The presence of cellphones has become ubiquitous during the campaign, whether for taking photographs or shoring up support. Go to Slide Show »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Caucus Click: Cellphone Nation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T16:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08ac88a3-0094-5f24-9cb1-d6cb44e43a0d', 'word_count': 23, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08ac88a3-0094-5f24-9cb1-d6cb44e43a0d'}, {'abstract': 'The president, whoever he is, will frequently disregard party principles. That’s a good thing.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/the-man-or-the-platform/', 'snippet': 'The president, whoever he is, will frequently disregard party principles. That’s a good thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney and Barack Obama appear to agree about at least one thing on this tense Election Day: They are standing on\xa0mutually exclusive party platforms, offering Americans what Obama called “the clearest choice of any time in a generation.” The candidates – and their partisans – insist voters are deciding today between a country that will be prospering or bankrupt, with a foreign policy that is firm or flaccid, and with abortion either remaining legal or abruptly outlawed. Nevertheless, after Inauguration Day, the challenges of governance, unexpected events, and the strong, confining American center will probably blur these differences.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Man or the Platform?', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T16:34:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gil Troy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Troy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66983018-2743-59de-a679-ea549149c32f', 'word_count': 1923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66983018-2743-59de-a679-ea549149c32f'}, {'abstract': 'There are excellent reasons for using the correct anatomical terms for our reproductive systems with our children, but for many, there remains a linguistic taboo.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/the-vagina-and-penis-dialogues/', 'snippet': 'There are excellent reasons for using the correct anatomical terms for our reproductive systems with our children, but for many, there remains a linguistic taboo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a perfect afternoon for a bike ride, breezy and springtime bright. My husband, Bill, and I unloaded our bikes and passed them to our children, who stood waiting by our side.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Vagina (and Penis) Dialogues', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Penis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vagina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T16:39:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Buni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_mate