e': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c305ec5-56db-59b2-a225-1fad23eb3c8d', 'word_count': 1154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c305ec5-56db-59b2-a225-1fad23eb3c8d'}, {'abstract': 'Like Ms. Raitt, the Tedeschi Trucks Band has a comforting sound that blends blues and rock with down-home jamming.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/booming/if-you-like-bonnie-raitt.html', 'snippet': 'Like Ms. Raitt, the Tedeschi Trucks Band has a comforting sound that blends blues and rock with down-home jamming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each week, Val Haller, the founder of the music Web site Valslist.com, matches music from her baby boom generation to music of her 20-something sons’ generation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/booming/06match-booming-bonnie-raitt/06match-booming-bonnie-raitt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/06/booming/06match-booming-bonnie-raitt/06match-booming-bonnie-raitt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/booming/06match-booming-bonnie-raitt/06match-booming-bonnie-raitt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/booming/06match-booming-bonnie-raitt/06match-booming-bonnie-raitt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/booming/06match-booming-bonnie-raitt/06match-booming-bonnie-raitt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/06/booming/06match-booming-bonnie-raitt/06match-booming-bonnie-raitt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/booming/06match-booming-bonnie-raitt/06match-booming-bonnie-raitt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If You Like Bonnie Raitt. . .', 'kicker': 'Music Match', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raitt, Bonnie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALLMAN BROTHERS BAND', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T19:11:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Val Haller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Val', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e27e33b-483d-598b-8b9e-16369f573f59', 'word_count': 962, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e27e33b-483d-598b-8b9e-16369f573f59'}, {'abstract': 'In seeking to prevent a sale of the company on the cheap, Netflix tries to be noncontroversial. But its battle with the activist investor Carl Icahn is far from over.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/netflixs-poison-pill-has-a-shareholder-friendly-flavor/', 'snippet': 'In seeking to prevent a sale of the company on the cheap, Netflix tries to be noncontroversial. But its battle with the activist investor Carl Icahn is far from over.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Netflix’s adoption of a shareholder rights plan, commonly known as a poison pill, to fend off the activist investor Carl C. Icahn is no surprise. Still, Netflix, the video-streaming and DVD rental company, couldn’t resist putting some unusual terms into the pill just to keep things exciting and place a shareholder-friendly spin on the event. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Netflix’s Poison Pill Has a Shareholder-Friendly Flavor', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burkle, Ronald W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T19:14:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11436900-8243-5f1c-b950-a726d5e84195', 'word_count': 1106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11436900-8243-5f1c-b950-a726d5e84195'}, {'abstract': 'As they stand in hourlong lines to cast a ballot, voters might ask themselves, why isn’t the government making it easier for me to vote, rather than forcing me through an endurance contest?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/problems-at-the-polls/', 'snippet': 'As they stand in hourlong lines to cast a ballot, voters might ask themselves, why isn’t the government making it easier for me to vote, rather than forcing me through an endurance contest?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is the day when voters raised on a reverence for democracy realize the utter disregard their leaders hold for that concept. The moment state and local officials around the country get elected, they stop caring about making it easy for their constituents to vote. Some do so deliberately, for partisan reasons, while others just don’t pay attention or decide they have bigger priorities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Problems at the Polls', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Board of Elections (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T19:17:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f599bfe7-89ee-5b6a-937f-cf7d0ecba101', 'word_count': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f599bfe7-89ee-5b6a-937f-cf7d0ecba101'}, {'abstract': 'Microsoft has posted a “Get to Know Windows 8″ guide for those curious or nervous about its new operating system.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/tip-of-the-week-an-introduction-to-windows-8/', 'snippet': 'Microsoft has posted a “Get to Know Windows 8″ guide for those curious or nervous about its new operating system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Microsoft’s just-released Windows 8 operating system has a much different user interface than previous versions of Windows, which may have some people nervous about the learning curve. To help new computer owners see the Windows 8 system in action or give shoppers some idea of what to expect whenever they do upgrade, Microsoft has posted several introductory guides on its site. These guides explain what has changed in Windows 8 and how to do basic tasks on the new system; they can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: An Introduction to Windows 8', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Windows (Operating System)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T19:22:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81c850ab-0b1f-5804-ac33-bf99fdd4274b', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81c850ab-0b1f-5804-ac33-bf99fdd4274b'}, {'abstract': 'Restaurants in the blackout zone in southern Manhattan lost their perishables and the better part of a week’s revenues, a big hit for businesses that get by on small margins, and for their workers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/dining/reviews/restaurant-review-after-hurricane-sandy-downtown-restaurants-need-patr