 tied to Election Day.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/hotels-and-zipcar-are-offering-election-day-deals/', 'snippet': 'Hotels and other companies across the country are offering deals tied to Election Day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For months, hotels across the country have been capitalizing on the presidential campaign by offering election-themed promotions to entice travelers of all political stripes. Like the candidates themselves, hotels and other companies are down to the last minute to vie for your business, with these Election Day deals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hotels — and Zipcar — Are Offering Election Day Deals', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T19:56:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Brennan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brennan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6039c6c-261f-5143-bb67-10522e316b51', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6039c6c-261f-5143-bb67-10522e316b51'}, {'abstract': 'Test your presidential I.Q. with our quiz on the various health issues of presidents and presidential candidates.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/the-presidential-health-quiz/', 'snippet': 'Test your presidential I.Q. with our quiz on the various health issues of presidents and presidential candidates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether it’s George Washington’s teeth or Bill Clinton’s former hamburger habit, Americans have always been fascinated by the health of the president and presidential candidates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/health/06wellquiz_lead/06wellquiz_lead-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/health/06wellquiz_lead/06wellquiz_lead-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/health/06wellquiz_lead/06wellquiz_lead-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/06/health/06wellquiz_lead/06wellquiz_lead-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/health/06wellquiz_lead/06wellquiz_lead-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Presidential Health Quiz', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T19:57:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/719bac18-b7b9-5f32-82c6-18c076369abf', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/719bac18-b7b9-5f32-82c6-18c076369abf'}, {'abstract': 'Anne Menke juxtaposes hyper-stylized fashion imagery with documentary-style photographs of remote locations in her new book.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/off-the-beaten-path/', 'snippet': 'Anne Menke juxtaposes hyper-stylized fashion imagery with documentary-style photographs of remote locations in her new book.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Beaten Path', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T20:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azadeh Ensha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azadeh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ensha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8997ec6a-01fa-5351-b1cc-5c7cdaa658ba', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8997ec6a-01fa-5351-b1cc-5c7cdaa658ba'}, {'abstract': 'The Good & Evil bar, made from dark Peruvian Pure Nacional chocolate that grows wild, is likely to put the artisanal company Éclat in the limelight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/dining/eclat-chocolate-bar-from-peru-via-pennsylvania.html', 'snippet': 'The Good & Evil bar, made from dark Peruvian Pure Nacional chocolate that grows wild, is likely to put the artisanal company Éclat in the limelight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are plenty of better-known chocolates than Éclat, because Christopher Curtin, 47, a master chocolatier who owns the artisanal company in West Chester, Pa., has not sought publicity or a wide distribution network for his finely made truffles, caramels, mendiants and bars. But a sleek new bar called Good & Evil, made from dark Peruvian Pure Nacional chocolate that grows wild, is likely to put Éclat in the limelight. The bar, embedded with crushed nibs, is a collaboration with the chefs Eric Ripert and Anthony Bourdain. In all his chocolates, Mr. Curtin starts with single-origin beans or a chocolate base, mostly around 70 percent dark, and adds flavorings and fillings like Aleppo pepper, shiraz wine, coffee and toasted corn. He just introduced bonbons filled with pumpkin and with gingerbread. You need a bib for his silky caramels. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/dining/07STUFF1/07STUFF1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 911, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/dining/07STUFF1/07STUFF1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1822, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/dining/07STUFF1/07STUFF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/07/dining/07STUFF1/07STUFF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/dining/07STUFF1/07STUFF1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrity Chocolate', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Celebrity Chocolate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eclat Chocolate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'