.com/2012/11/07/sports/hockey/nhl-and-players-union-resuming-negotiations.html', 'snippet': 'The N.H.L. and players’ association were back at the bargaining table Tuesday, a constructive turn in the seven-week lockout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bargaining resumed Tuesday afternoon between the N.H.L. and its players union, a constructive turn in the seven-week lockout. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'League and Players Union Resume Bargaining, but Progress Isn’t Guaranteed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'League and Players Union Resume Bargaining, but Progress Isn’t Guaranteed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T20:17:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5fe7640-9dfc-5f27-ae37-b0c038069c81', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5fe7640-9dfc-5f27-ae37-b0c038069c81'}, {'abstract': 'In time for the holidays, a hybrid walnut that shows off a bit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/dining/sanguinetti-red-walnuts-now-sold-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'In time for the holidays, a hybrid walnut that shows off a bit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A walnut of a different color has arrived in New York. Its shell looks normal, but the skin that covers the nutmeat inside is burgundy red. Grown in California, like most walnuts sold in the United States, this one is a hybrid of a red-skinned Persian variety and the common, or English, walnut. The flavor is deeply nutty, with a touch of characteristic bitterness, a worthy adornment for a salad, a cheese tray or the snowy icing on a holiday cake.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/dining/07STUFF4/07STUFF4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/dining/07STUFF4/07STUFF4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/dining/07STUFF4/07STUFF4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/07/dining/07STUFF4/07STUFF4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/dining/07STUFF4/07STUFF4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeing Red Inside the Shell', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeing Red Inside the Shell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T20:17:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5af473e1-6898-569f-a158-ccfdcc480d11', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5af473e1-6898-569f-a158-ccfdcc480d11'}, {'abstract': 'The Frugal Traveler set out to take the cheapest all-inclusive Caribbean vacation he could find. Here’s where he went, what it cost and what he thought of the trip.', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/one-low-low-price-for-sun-and-sand/', 'snippet': 'The Frugal Traveler set out to take the cheapest all-inclusive Caribbean vacation he could find. Here’s where he went, what it cost and what he thought of the trip.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometime this winter, many of you might wonder: What’s the least it would cost to skip town and head to a Caribbean resort, leaving behind scarves, snowbanks and sniffling co-workers?', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/travel/06-frugal-beach/06-frugal-beach-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/travel/06-frugal-beach/06-frugal-beach-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/travel/06-frugal-beach/06-frugal-beach-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/06/travel/06-frugal-beach/06-frugal-beach-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/travel/06-frugal-beach/06-frugal-beach-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Low, Low Price for Sun and Sand', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Low Can You Go for Some Sun and Sand?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T20:22:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By SETH KUGEL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KUGEL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2d4950d-14bb-5649-a313-ad70a1cf7534', 'word_count': 1603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2d4950d-14bb-5649-a313-ad70a1cf7534'}, {'abstract': 'Dickson’s Farmstand Meats is selling smoked turkeys.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/dining/amish-turkeys-brined-and-smoked.html', 'snippet': 'Dickson’s Farmstand Meats is selling smoked turkeys.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Jake Dickson, David Schuttenberg and Robbie Richter on the case, a smoked turkey becomes worthy of the Thanksgiving feast. Mr. Schuttenberg, the executive chef of Dickson’s Farmstand Meats in the Chelsea Market, rubs Amish country turkeys (raised without hormones or antibiotics) with herbs and soy sauce, brines them and sends them to Connecticut, where Mr. Richter, who was the pitmaster at Fatty ’Cue, hot-smokes them for three and a half hours. The white and dark meat emerge delicately smoky, moist and succulent after reheating (about an hour at 250 degrees). The birds, 12 to 14 pounds, come wrapped with netting; remove it before reheating.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '