f Figaro” taps 21st-century parallels to Beaumarchais’s original skewering of the rich and powerful.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/theater/reviews/sean-mcnall-in-charles-moreys-figaro-at-pearl-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Charles Morey’s spry adaptation of “The Marriage of Figaro” taps 21st-century parallels to Beaumarchais’s original skewering of the rich and powerful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s entirely in keeping with the infectious metatheatrical spirit of the Pearl Theater Company’s staging of “Figaro” that the actor Sean McNall blurs the line between the title character and this 18th-century comedy’s author, Pierre-Augustin Caron de Beaumarchais, while blithely straddling the gulf separating pre-Revolution France from the present-day America.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/FIGARO/FIGARO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/FIGARO/FIGARO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/FIGARO/FIGARO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/FIGARO/FIGARO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1082, 'width': 1504, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/FIGARO/FIGARO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/FIGARO/FIGARO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/FIGARO/FIGARO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tracing the 99% Fight to the 18th Century', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tracing the 99% Fight To the 18th Century', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pearl Theater Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Hal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNall, Sean', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T20:35:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Rooney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rooney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/22d17442-1f77-58c2-b6af-560cb72ecb49', 'word_count': 536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22d17442-1f77-58c2-b6af-560cb72ecb49'}, {'abstract': 'The show’s producer says the unusual delay is a matter of logistics, not an effort to sell more tickets before critics weigh in.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/glengarry-glen-ross-pushes-back-opening-by-a-month/', 'snippet': 'The show’s producer says the unusual delay is a matter of logistics, not an effort to sell more tickets before critics weigh in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Opening nights are serious business on Broadway, and not just because of the parties: Critics’ reviews usually come out the next day, and ticket sales often fluctuate depending on the strength (or sourness) of those notices. Producers usually schedule their opening nights months in advance, and rarely change the dates – which is why it was unusual when the producers of Broadway’s “Glengarry Glen Ross” announced on Monday that they were delaying the opening by nearly four weeks, from this Sunday to Saturday, Dec. 8.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/arts/06artsbeat-glengarry/06artsbeat-glengarry-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 793, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/arts/06artsbeat-glengarry/06artsbeat-glengarry-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1586, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/arts/06artsbeat-glengarry/06artsbeat-glengarry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/06/arts/06artsbeat-glengarry/06artsbeat-glengarry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/arts/06artsbeat-glengarry/06artsbeat-glengarry-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Glengarry Glen Ross’ Pushes Back Opening by a Month', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Glengarry Glen Ross’ Delays Opening', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mamet, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pacino, Al', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Jeffrey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Daniel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T20:36:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff43788b-5bed-5277-a200-170626f8c03e', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff43788b-5bed-5277-a200-170626f8c03e'}, {'abstract': 'Two home renovators visit fellow bloggers and lend a hand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/garden/talking-with-meryl-phillips-and-chris-miller.html', 'snippet': 'Two home renovators visit fellow bloggers and lend a hand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like many do-it-yourself home renovators, Meryl Phillips and Chris Miller like to blog about their adventures. For three years, readers have logged on to PicardyProject.com to follow the couple’s efforts to fix up their 90-year-old stucco “storybook”-style home in Oakland, Calif. Meanwhile, as they gutted bathrooms, laid brick flooring in their entry and removed paint with a power washer, Ms. Phillips, 27, and Mr. Miller, 33, turned to other renovation bloggers for advice and support. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/garden/07webonlyqa/07webonlyqa-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/garden/07webonlyqa/07webonlyqa