FA Champions League, Matchday 4(A)', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/champions-league-matchday-4a/', 'snippet': 'A video recap of the day’s action in the UEFA Champions League, Matchday 4(A)', 'lead_paragraph': 'With games on Matchday 4(A) of the group stage of the UEFA Champions League on Tuesday, we continue a featurette in which we hope to bring Goal readers video of the best (and most important) goals of the day, courtesy of Fox Soccer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Champions League: Matchday 4(A)', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T23:09:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf2a0a06-f394-561c-a6d5-9b344d53e8c4', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf2a0a06-f394-561c-a6d5-9b344d53e8c4'}, {'abstract': 'You can transfer photos directly from a camera to an iPad, as long as you have the right adapter.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/qa-photos-from-camera-to-ipad/', 'snippet': 'You can transfer photos directly from a camera to an iPad, as long as you have the right adapter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Photos from Camera to iPad', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Loading Photos\r\nFrom Camera to iPad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cameras', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-06T23:10:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00492c18-06cd-5640-8ed4-1058c725d01b', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00492c18-06cd-5640-8ed4-1058c725d01b'}, {'abstract': 'After a panel called for a “competitiveness shock,” the government said it would cut payroll taxes for businesses by $25.6 billion to help reduce labor costs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/business/global/france-announces-cut-in-payroll-taxes-for-businesses.html', 'snippet': 'After a panel called for a “competitiveness shock,” the government said it would cut payroll taxes for businesses by $25.6 billion to help reduce labor costs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Responding to calls to make French industry more competitive by reducing labor costs, the Socialist government of President François Hollande said Tuesday that it would cut payroll taxes for businesses. But the government stopped short of adopting the broader changes that an expert panel led by a prominent business executive, Louis Gallois, recommended a day earlier in a report that called for a “competitiveness shock” to the French economy.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/business/GALLOIS/GALLOIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/07/business/GALLOIS/GALLOIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption'