blic hospital, and nearby NYU Langone Medical Center, a leading private institution, had become flooded and lost their primary power when the storm hit on Monday night. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hospital Evacuations for Future Storms', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hospital Evacuations for Future Storms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York University Langone Medical Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bellevue Hospital Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coney Island Hospital', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T01:27:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a143ad5c-1d5b-597d-91d0-2752d6c64129', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a143ad5c-1d5b-597d-91d0-2752d6c64129'}, {'abstract': 'Afghanistan’s leader, once again, is conjuring up scapegoats and false alarms to divert attention from the challenges facing his country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/opinion/president-hamid-karzais-misplaced-priorities.html', 'snippet': 'Afghanistan’s leader, once again, is conjuring up scapegoats and false alarms to divert attention from the challenges facing his country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It would be impossible to overstate the challenges facing Afghanistan and the urgency of addressing them while American troops are still in the 