ights to prevail.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bad Medicine for Women', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bad Medicine for Women', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brewer, Jan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teilborg, James A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T02:03:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/94d7c8ee-d74a-5151-960b-95c0a527a147', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94d7c8ee-d74a-5151-960b-95c0a527a147'}, {'abstract': 'The activist investor Nelson Peltz plans to begin a campaign against the French food maker Danone, having acquired a 1 percent stake in the company, according to a person briefed on the matter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/peltz-said-to-take-stake-in-danone/', 'snippet': 'The activist investor Nelson Peltz plans to begin a campaign against the French food maker Danone, having acquired a 1 percent stake in the company, according to a person briefed on the matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nelson Peltz is learning how to say “shareholder activism” in French. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peltz Said to Take Stake in Danone', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peltz, Nelson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Danone SA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T02:03:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4913c6b3-ee07-59c4-93a8-f1c4954effd8', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4913c6b3-ee07-59c4-93a8-f1c4954effd8'}, {'abstract': 'The arrests came a day after a deadly bombing in Bahrain’s capital, a sharp intensification of the violence that has simmered in the island nation since the beginning of a pro-democracy uprising 21 months ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/world/middleeast/bahrain-four-arrested-in-bombings-officials-hint-at-hezbollah-role.html', 'snippet': 'The arrests came a day after a deadly bombing in Bahrain’s capital, a sharp intensification of the violence that has simmered in the island nation since the beginning of a pro-democracy uprising 21 months ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The authorities said Tuesday that four suspects had been arrested in connection with deadly bombings the day before, and that the Shiite militant group Hezbollah may have played a role. The blasts were a major escalation of the violence that has roiled Bahrain, a tiny Persian Gulf state ruled by a Sunni monarchy, because of a 21-month-old uprising by the Shiite majority. Hundreds of antigovernment demonstrators clashed with the police on Tuesday in the village of Sanabis, west of Manama, the capital. Bahrain’s chief of public security, Maj. Gen. Tariq al-Hassan, said that the bombing suspects, who were not identified, had been taken into custody and that further arrests were possible.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/world/BAHRAIN-FLOATER/BAHRAIN-FLOATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/07/world/BAHRAIN-FLOATER/BAHRAIN-FLOATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/world/BAHRAIN-FLOATER/BAHRAIN-FLOATER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/world/BAHRAIN-FLOATER/BAHRAIN-FLOATER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/world/BAHRAIN-FLOATER/BAHRAIN-FLOATER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/07/world/BAHRAIN-FLOATER/BAHRAIN-FLOATER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/world/BAHRAIN-FLOATER/BAHRAIN-FLOATER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bahrain: Four Arrested in Bombings; Officials Hint at Hezbollah Role', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bahrain: Four Arrested in Bombings; Officials Hint at Hezbollah Role', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords