f the Republican presidential nominee had political objectives and was not solely for business. The prosecutor’s office made no comment on the request. Mikhail I. Serdyuk, a deputy in the State Duma, asked the prosecutor general to “recommend that Mitt Romney use official channels of communication in the future.” He said the fact that the visit included a conversation with “a Russian known to be able to deliver messages to Mr. Putin,” as The New York Times reported last week, was a sign that the Republican nominee sought to improve his image after having described Russia as America’s top “geopolitical foe.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Lawmaker Asks for Inquiry on Romney Son’s Visit', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Lawmaker Asks for Inquiry on Romney Son’s Visit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Matt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T02:25:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Kordunsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kordunsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f23a7b5-3b25-50b8-8c1a-b37211538a96', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f23a7b5-3b25-50b8-8c1a-b37211538a96'}, {'abstract': 'A diagram showing the steps required to get the crane at 157 West 57th Street operational again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/11/07/nyregion/a-rescue-for-the-crippled-crane