one, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Ann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T02:44:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker and Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be90fcd9-40ca-51ab-a2d1-316809b966ee', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be90fcd9-40ca-51ab-a2d1-316809b966ee'}, {'abstract': 'Election Day had its share of flaws and partisan disputes, but it was unclear whether any would cause a major shift in the result or set the stage for a big lawsuit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/us/politics/long-lines-id-demands-and-provisional-ballots-mar-voting.html', 'snippet': 'Election Day had its share of flaws and partisan disputes, but it was unclear whether any would cause a major shift in the result or set the stage for a big lawsuit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Virginia and Texas some voters waited in line for four hours. In Pennsylvania, there were inappropriate demands for official photo IDs. Recorded calls went out to residents of Florida saying misleadingly that they had until 7 p.m. “tomorrow” to vote. And in Ohio, there seemed to be an unusually high number of provisional ballots, causing concern that they might not all get counted. ', 'print_section': 'P', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/07turnout/07turnout-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/07turnout/07turnout-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/07turnout/07turnout-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/07/us/07turnout/07turnout-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/07turnout/07turnout-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Long Lines, Demands for ID and Provisional Ballots Mar Voting for Some', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Long Lines, Demands for ID and Provisional Ballots Mar Voting for Some', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T02:49:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb85132e-fe27-5b67-8191-38f279a5e44b', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb85132e-fe27-5b67-8191-38f279a5e44b'}, {'abstract': 'As Fox News’s own polling showed an advantage for Mr. Obama late in the campaign, commentators on the network questioned whether the news organization had its numbers right.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/us/politics/web-sites-and-networks-focus-on-claims-of-fraud-and-intimidation.html', 'snippet': 'As Fox News’s own polling showed an advantage for Mr. Obama late in the campaign, commentators on the network questioned whether the news organization had its numbers right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Karl Rove was incredulous. His colleagues at the Fox News decision desk had called Ohio for President Obama, a move he insisted just a few minutes earlier would be premature.', 'print_section': 'P', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/sub-07media/sub-07media-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/sub-07media/sub-07media-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1440, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Fox News, a Mistrust of Pro-Obama Numbers Lasts Late Into the Night', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Fox News, a Mistrust Of Pro-Obama Numbers Lasts Late Into the Night', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rove, Karl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T02:52:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters and Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf26b95c-e8aa-5628-a4b6-c45f0a3066e2', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf26b95c-e8aa-5628-a4b6-c45f0a3066e2'}, {'abstract': 'In Georgia, where nearly half of the nation’s peanuts are grown, the annual fall harvest has yielded a record crop that farmers say tastes better than average.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/us/in-the-south-a-good-year-for-farmers-of-peanuts.html', 'snippet': 'In Georgia, where nearly half of the nation’s peanuts are grown, the annual fall harvest has yielded a record crop that farmers say tastes better than average.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — Amid worries over climate change, farm bill politics and a recent peanut butter recall comes some good news from the peanut fields of the South: the crop is great this year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/PEANUTS-2/PEANUTS-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/07/us/PEANUTS-2/PEANUTS-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/PEANUTS-2/PEANUTS-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/PEANUTS-2/PEANUTS-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1414, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/PEANUTS-2/PEANUTS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/07/us/PEANUTS-2/PEANUTS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/PEANUTS-2/PEANUTS-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the South, a Good Year for Farmers of Peanuts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the South, A Good Year For Farmers Of Peanuts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Peanuts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Peanut Butter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farm Bill (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T02:55:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Severson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c47b5ab-5d97-5e9c-bc15-479e1b237456', 'word_count': 740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c47b5ab-5d97-5e9c-bc15-479e1b237456'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama is known to play a game of basketball for luck on days he faces an electoral contest. Tuesday was no different.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/us/politics/obama-headquarters.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama is known to play a game of basketball for luck on days he faces an electoral contest. Tuesday was no different.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — He woke up in his old bed, here in sweet home Chicago. He played a superstitious game of basketball with old pals and aides from the 2008 glory days, as he did on many primary poll days back then. He did a few final interviews. And at the end of the long election night, after he was re-elected president, he congratulated his rival, Mitt Romney, saying, “We may have battled fiercely, but it’s only because we love this country deeply.”', 'print_section': 'P', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/07obama/07obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/07/us/07obama/07obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/07obama/07obama-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/07obama/07obama-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1305, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/07obama/07obama-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/07/us/07obama/07obama-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/07obama/07obama-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bit of Quiet Optimism, and Some Superstition, Before a Tight Victory', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bit of Quiet Optimism, And Some Superstition, Before Victory at the Polls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T02:57:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e2af88b-4214-5472-b22d-b4da51317296', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e2af88b-4214-5472-b22d-b4da51317296'}, {'abstract': 'Singing a certain kind of song, with George Fitzgerald and Nancy Salomon.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/06/far-from-klutzy/', 'snippet': 'Singing a certain kind of song, with George Fitzgerald and Nancy Salomon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEDNESDAY’S PUZZLE — Even if you’ve got THE BLUES, this one should make you smile. It certainly made me smile, and I had a tough day yesterday. So thank you for that, George Fitzgerald and Nancy Salomon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Far From Klutzy', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T03:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e005ac2d-c593-5289-aa79-5bd82564ce18', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e005ac2d-c593-5289-aa79-5bd82564ce18'}, {'abstract': 'The anticipated closeness of the presidential race did not deter Republican and Democratic political die-hards from heading into ballrooms and bars around the state to watch election returns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/us/politics/florida-parties-presidential-election.html', 'snippet': 'The anticipated closeness of the presidential race did not deter Republican and Democratic political die-hards from heading into ballrooms and bars around the state to watch election returns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — The two major parties did not agree on much\xa0 in Florida this year — not the state of the economy, the panacea for a broken health care system or the overall role of government. But they did agree on this: The race for president was bitter, it was hard-fought and, all too often, it was too personal.', 'print_section': 'P', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/PARTIES/PARTIES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/07/us/PARTIES/PARTIES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xla