ion_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b90a3a6-c79a-5752-9738-7482c26337a2', 'word_count': 1364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b90a3a6-c79a-5752-9738-7482c26337a2'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s victory gives him a second chance to deliver the renewal he still promises, but without a clear mandate, a healthy economy or willing Republican partners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/us/politics/now-a-chance-to-catch-up-to-his-epochal-vision.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s victory gives him a second chance to deliver the renewal he still promises, but without a clear mandate, a healthy economy or willing Republican partners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the first time Barack Obama summoned the country’s leading presidential historians to dinner, they saw that the type of discussion he wanted would be different from their talks with previous Oval Office occupants.', 'print_section': 'P', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/HISTORY/HISTORY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/HISTORY/HISTORY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1256, 'width': 1885, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/HISTORY/HISTORY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/07/us/HISTORY/HISTORY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/HISTORY/HISTORY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Now, a Chance to Catch Up to His Epochal Vision', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Now, a Chance to Catch Up to His Epochal Vision', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T05:32:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Kantor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kantor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21cf5768-adda-5e65-bee4-f6f2faf120a5', 'word_count': 1430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21cf5768-adda-5e65-bee4-f6f2faf120a5'}, {'abstract': 'The generational shift President Obama embodied is under way, but it will not change Washington as quickly as voters once hoped.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/us/politics/in-president-obamas-second-term-familiar-challenges.html', 'snippet': 'The generational shift President Obama embodied is under way, but it will not change Washington as quickly as voters once hoped.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As President Obama turns his attention once again to filling out a cabinet and writing an Inaugural Address, this much is clear: he should not expect to bask in a surge of national unity, or to witness a crowd of millions overrun the Mall just to say they were there.', 'print_section': 'P', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/us/08mood/08mood-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/08/us/08mood/08mood-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/us/08mood/08mood-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/us/08mood/08mood-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Winning a Second Term, Obama Will Confront Familiar Headwinds', 'kicker': 'Political Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winning a Second Term, Obama Will Confront Familiar Headwinds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T05:32:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Bai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9c6aa18-43c5-5743-a7f6-1f696f964a45', 'word_count': 1168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9c6aa18-43c5-5743-a7f6-1f696f964a45'}, {'abstract': 'Albany-watchers said it could be days before one party will be able to claim control of the Senate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/nyregion/new-york-state-senate-races.html', 'snippet': 'Albany-watchers said it could be days before one party will be able to claim control of the Senate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York Democrats said early Wednesday that they believed they would take control of the State Senate — currently the last significant power base of Republicans in Albany — after Democrats won several critical legislative races on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'P', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/ALBANY-01/ALBANY-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/ALBANY-01/ALBANY-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. in Surprise Fight to Hold New York Senate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.O.P. in Surprise Fight To Hold New York Senate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, State Legislature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T05:38:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0249447e-b36f-58b4-9bd9-ab7e0519a3de', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0249447e-b36f-58b4-9bd9-ab7e0519a3de'}, {'abstract': 'Emmanuel Morantus worked three jobs to support his family as an immigrant nearly 30 years ago, but now his failing health keeps him tied to an oxygen tank and to electricity bills he cannot afford.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/nyregion/a-retiree-on-oxygen-trying-to-pay-his-power-bills.html', 'snippet': 'Emmanuel Morantus worked three jobs to support his family as an immigrant nearly 30 years ago, but now his failing health keeps him tied to an oxygen tank and to electricity bills he cannot afford.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wherever Emmanuel Morantus goes, a long length of plastic tubing trails behind him. Whether he is padding into his tiny bathroom or stepping outside to retrieve his mail or resting on his living room hospital bed, he always makes sure the line does not get tangled.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/07NEEDIEST/07NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/07NEEDIEST/07NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/07NEEDIEST/07NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/07NEEDIEST/07NEEDIEST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1259, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's