dia', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T08:01:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons, Vivekananda Nemana and Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Vivekananda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nemana', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e953565-e620-5441-9da0-d14fb97105d9', 'word_count': 1035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e953565-e620-5441-9da0-d14fb97105d9'}, {'abstract': 'World leaders are vying for favor as President Obama embarks on a second term with many major issues unresolved from the first.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/world/obama-victory-brings-a-welcome-for-the-familiar-abroad.html', 'snippet': 'World leaders are vying for favor as President Obama embarks on a second term with many major issues unresolved from the first.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — World leaders sought comfort from the familiar on Wednesday after President Obama’s re-election but, with the global political landscape substantially unchanged and crises on hold while the vote unfolded, many vied with new vigor for his attention and favor as he embarks on a second term.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/us/politics/20121107_HP_OBAMA-slide-Z8RG/20121107_HP_OBAMA-slide-Z8RG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height':