ported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c865656-b00a-594b-971c-a7591f90eebc', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c865656-b00a-594b-971c-a7591f90eebc'}, {'abstract': 'For his next feat, “Kung Fu,” the playwright David Henry Hwang reimagines an icon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/magazine/david-henry-hwang-the-man-who-can-make-bruce-lee-talk.html', 'snippet': 'For his next feat, “Kung Fu,” the playwright David Henry Hwang reimagines an icon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a late summer morning, in a room far west on 42nd Street, Bruce Lee, who has yet to become the greatest martial artist of all time, is putting the moves on a young Japanese-American dancer.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/magazine/11hwang/11hwang-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 527, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/11/magazine/11hwang/11hwang-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 527}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/magazine/11hwang/mag-11hwang-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/magazine/11hwang/mag-11hwang-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/magazine/11hwang/11hwang-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/11/magazine/11hwang/11hwang-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/magazine/11hwang/11hwang-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Man Who Can Make Bruce Lee Talk', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Man Who Can Make Bruce Lee Talk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Bruce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hwang, David Henry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T12:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Witchel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witchel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8a7e904-4fd0-514b-b377-466c06388f14', 'word_count': 2774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8a7e904-4fd0-514b-b377-466c06388f14'}, {'abstract': 'The sense of urgency about dealing with global warming depends on where natural disasters like Hurricane Sandy strike. We should make the most of it this time.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/a-change-in-the-weather-on-wall-street/', 'snippet': 'The sense of urgency about dealing with global warming depends on where natural disasters like Hurricane Sandy strike. We should make the most of it this time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few weeks ago I was talking to a friend who works at an environmental organization. We were discussing the absence of any talk about climate change in the presidential campaign, and joked that the United States would decide to get serious only when Wall Street found itself under water.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Change in the Weather on Wall Street', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T12:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20569e10-fcf0-5d85-8fb5-3b2cb2e98044', 'word_count': 1593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20569e10-fcf0-5d85-8fb5-3b2cb2e98044'}, {'abstract': 'When you own a microbusiness, burning time is just like burning money.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/the-joys-and-dangers-of-owning-a-microbusiness/', 'snippet': 'When you own a microbusiness, burning time is just like burning money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today, there are about 27 million businesses in the United States. Of these, the vast majority are what we call microbusinesses, those that typically have fewer than five employees and less than $1 million in sales. This was where I started my business career and, after having gone through all three stages of business growth, I’m happy to be back there again today with my wealth management and consulting business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Joys (and Dangers) of Owning a Microbusiness', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T12:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Patrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patrick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1c5a5e6-b5bd-5116-937d-e3d390bb525e', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1c5a5e6-b5bd-5116-937d-e3d390bb525e'}, {'abstract': 'Unemployment will remain at “very high” levels, according to a gloomy set of forecasts issued by the European Commission.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/business/global/europe-foresees-weak-recovery-next-year.html', 'snippet': 'Unemployment will remain at “very high” levels, according to a gloomy set of forecasts issued by the European Commission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — The European Union will experience only a very weak economic recovery next year and unemployment will remain at “very high” levels, according to a gloomy set of forecasts issued Wednesday by the European Commission. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Foresees Weak Recovery Next Year', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe Foresees Weak Recovery Next Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organization