12-11-07T14:14:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ac07991-2d7d-5ac0-b37e-7aa4ab9d1c79', 'word_count': 13, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ac07991-2d7d-5ac0-b37e-7aa4ab9d1c79'}, {'abstract': 'Whining because Obama didn’t seem to like you enough was not a smart move.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/wall-streets-bad-investment-decision/', 'snippet': 'Whining because Obama didn’t seem to like you enough was not a smart move.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are many lists now circulating of the biggest winners and losers from the election; oddly, however, none of the lists I’ve seen mentions just how bad this result is for Wall Street’s Masters of the Universe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wall Street’s Bad Investment Decision', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T14:20:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49b19b18-e065-5571-8850-8ab16a68708e', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49b19b18-e065-5571-8850-8ab16a68708e'}, {'abstract': 'A California initiative aimed at labeling some genetically engineered foods is defeated, but a discussion of transparency is begun.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/california-votes-no-on-37-flawed-proposition-on-food-labeling/', 'snippet': 'A California initiative aimed at labeling some genetically engineered foods is defeated, but a discussion of transparency is begun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'California’s\xa0Proposition 37, or #Prop37 as it was known on Twitter, failed last night by a substantial margin — 53 percent to 47 percent. The ballot initiative would have required labeling for some genetically engineered foods. (Click here for an illuminating interactive county-by-county map of the vote. Upscale urban and coastal regions wanted it; inland areas mostly rejected it.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California Votes No on 37: Flawed Proposition on Food Labeling', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T14:21:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37567607-4ee2-54fd-ab42-add97a292650', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37567607-4ee2-54fd-ab42-add97a292650'}, {'abstract': 'Matt Ryan, Eli Manning and Aaron Rodgers are among the suggested selections halfway through the N.F.L. season.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/midseason-report-n-f-c-pro-bowl-picks/', 'snippet': 'Matt Ryan, Eli Manning and Aaron Rodgers are among the suggested selections halfway through the N.F.L. season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the elections over, football fans can shift their voting focus back to the N.F.L. Pro Bowl ballots opened a few weeks ago. With most of the teams having played exactly half their schedule, it’s time for a look at midseason honors. This \xa0N.F.C. Pro Bowl roster represents one man’s opinion, based on what the film has shown this season. (Players are listed in order of merit.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Midseason Report: N.F.C. Pro Bowl Picks', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pro Bowl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T14:30:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58a0e44d-490e-576f-839e-ac6cc1824d19', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58a0e44d-490e-576f-839e-ac6cc1824d19'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/what-were-reading-562/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Associated Press: California voters rejected a ballot proposition to make their state the first in the nation to require labeling of genetically modified foods. — Patrick Farrell', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T14:41:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f24b56fd-2dfb-51ba-8245-d23c53c35746', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f24b56fd-2dfb-51ba-8245-d23c53c35746'}, {'abstract': 'The Grammy-winning folk-rock duo said it could not continue touring “due to internal discord and irreconcilable differences of ambition.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/citing-irreconcilable-differences-the-civil-wars-cancels-tour-dates/', 'snippet': 'The Grammy-winning folk-rock duo said it could not continue touring “due to internal discord and irreconcilable differences of ambition.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'These are the moments when you perhaps regret naming your band after an epochal internecine struggle: the Civil Wars, the Grammy Award-winning folk-rock duo, abruptly announced in the midst of a European tour that it was canceling its upcoming concert dates, in language that suggested the house has become divided against itself. The band mates Joy Williams and John Paul White said in a statement on the group’s Facebook page on Monday: “We sincerely apologize for the canceling of all of our tour dates. It is something we deeply regret. However, due to internal discord and irreconcilable differences of ambition we are unable to continue as a touring entity at this time. We thank each and every one of you for your amazing love & support. Our sincere hope is to have new music for you in 2013.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/civilwars/civilwars-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,