.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even though President Barack Obama railed against outsourcing in his campaign, information technology titans and trade groups in India warmly welcomed his re-election, as they were optimistic that he would cement bilateral ties and improve the United States economy in his second term, which in turn would improve their business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India’s Outsourcing Industry Welcomes Obama Win', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Outsourcing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bain Capital', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Software and Services Companies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tata Consultancy Services', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T15:01:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sruthi Gottipati', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sruthi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gottipati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfc32ce5-919d-5760-be43-b53e7a52e21f', 'word_count': 562, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfc32ce5-919d-5760-be43-b53e7a52e21f'}, {'abstract': 'The meetings signal further progress