-networks-help-time-warners-quarterly-profit/', 'snippet': 'Time Warner’s suite of cable networks, including TBS and HBO, contributed to the company’s 1.9 percent increase in third-quarter net profit, but revenue was offset by continued weakness at its magazine and movie divisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A strong quarter at Time Warner’s suite of cable channels contributed to a 1.9 percent increase in net profit for the third quarter, but revenue was offset by continued weakness at its magazine and movie divisions.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cable Networks Help Time Warner’s Quarterly Profit', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cable Channels Help Push Time Warner’s Profit Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bewkes, Jeffrey L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T15:33:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5df70517-55f0-59c6-a979-fdb32c0a2007', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5df70517-55f0-59c6-a979-fdb32c0a2007'}, {'abstract': 'Advocates of the labeling of genetically modified food vowed to carry their fight to other states and to the federal government after suffering a defeat in California.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/business/california-bid-to-label-genetically-modified-crops.html', 'snippet': 'Advocates of the labeling of genetically modified food vowed to carry their fight to other states and to the federal government after suffering a defeat in California.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Advocates for the labeling of genetically modified food vowed to carry their fight to other states and to the federal government after suffering a defeat in California on Tuesday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Loss, the Fight to Label Modified Food Continues', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Loss, the Fight to Label Modified Food Continues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biotechnology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T15:48:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d72f9141-5f51-5e05-9d2b-81abaf573a0b', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d72f9141-5f51-5e05-9d2b-81abaf573a0b'}, {'abstract': 'Some owners of Hyundai Motor Group cars were not surprised when the company admitted it had overstated the fuel economy of 900,000 vehicles sold in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/hyundais-fuel-economy-admission-leaves-some-car-owners-cold/', 'snippet': 'Some owners of Hyundai Motor Group cars were not surprised when the company admitted it had overstated the fuel economy of 900,000 vehicles sold in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Friday, following an investigation by the Environmental Protection Agency, Hyundai Motor Group admitted it had overstated the fuel economy of 900,000 vehicles sold in the United States over the last two years. But for many Hyundai and Kia owners, the company was merely stating the obvious.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hyundai’s Fuel Economy Admission Leaves Some Car Owners Cold', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Buyers Fume at Hyundai’s M.P.G. Admission', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fuel Efficiency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Edmunds.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hyundai Motor Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kia Motors Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T15:56:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cheryl Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cheryl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1880679-a805-5ef1-87c7-6b7b19521179', 'word_count': 1141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1880679-a805-5ef1-87c7-6b7b19521179'}, {'abstract': 'Colombia’s city, home to the poshest residences, is now also known for its hip eateries.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/a-bite-of-bogot/', 'snippet': 'Colombia’s city, home to the poshest residences, is now also known for its hip eateries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The northern section of Bogotá, Colombia, is already home to many of the city’s poshest residences. Now, hip (chévere in the local lingo) eateries are popping up practically on top of one another. Just this year, the restaurateurs Maurizio Mancini and Gerónimo Basile of the Chinese cantina Kong opened up two more spots: Magnolio (Calle 69A No. 5-19; 011-57-1 -211-0627; entrees $17 to $27), a 1950s-themed restaurant in a three-floor house (with a V.I.P. room done up as a library) that serves comfort food with French and Spanish influences; and N. N. (Calle 71 No. 5-65; entrees $16 to $33), a two-month-old speakeasy with knockout small plates — try the banana croquettes stuffed with rabbit.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bite of Bogotá', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bite of Bogota', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T16:01:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b77edd7f-8210-5d7c-9a74-ac667ad331f0', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b77edd7f-8210-5d7c-9a74-ac667ad331f0'}, {'abstract': 'TimesCast Politics: The election results and what they mean for governin