gs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/trading-recyclables-for-rosemary/', 'snippet': 'Part bottle depot, part farmers’ market, a program in Mexico City promotes recycling in a region with serious waste management and littering issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday morning, Francisco Reyes brought three boxes of empty beer bottles to a market in Mexico City’s Chapultepec Park, a local landmark that can be considered the lungs of this high-altitude expanse of 21 million people.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trading Recyclables for Rosemary', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T17:08:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Agren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Agren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/147e81be-2cd4-580c-9c23-db35cba8f9e1', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/147e81be-2cd4-580c-9c23-db35cba8f9e1'}, {'abstract': 'With President Obama having won a second term, lobbyists are readying a varied agenda to influence the makeup of crucial Congressional committees and regulatory agencies while working to avert the so-called fiscal cliff and temper the Dodd-Frank regulatory overhaul.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/with-an-obama-victory-wall-street-pivots-to-plan-b/', 'snippet': 'With President Obama having won a second term, lobbyists are readying a varied agenda to influence the makeup of crucial Congressional committees and regulatory agencies while working to avert the so-called fiscal cliff and temper the Dodd-Frank r...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wall Street is moving to Plan B.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With an Obama Victory, Wall Street Pivots to Plan B', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities Industry and Financial Markets Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T17:14:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess and Jessica Silver-Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c30421e9-26dd-51ca-a38d-f543c10c404d', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c30421e9-26dd-51ca-a38d-f543c10c404d'}, {'abstract': 'With same-sex marriage endorsed in several states, and the election of the nation’s first openly lesbian senator, advocates celebrated victories “across the board and across the country.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/us/same-sex-marriage-gains-cheer-gay-rights-advocates.html', 'snippet': 'With same-sex marriage endorsed in several states, and the election of the nation’s first openly lesbian senator, advocates celebrated victories “across the board and across the country.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gay rights advocates savored multiple victories on Wednesday, with the first election victories for same-sex marriage in Maine, Maryland and Minnesota, the election in Wisconsin of the nation’s first openly gay senator and the re-election of President Obama, who had taken a risk by endorsing same-sex marriage. ', 'print_section': 'P', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Victories Pile Up, Gay Rights Advocates Cheer ‘Milestone Year’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Victories Pile Up, Gay Rights Advocates Cheer ‘Milestone Year’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baldwin, Tammy Suzanne Green', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T17:20:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/466689ac-f567-5a10-a792-36d07cd63e75', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/466689ac-f567-5a10-a792-36d07cd63e75'}, {'abstract': 'One of the best-known American designers of the postwar era gets his first comprehensive retrospective.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/see-it-now-george-nelson-at-yale/', 'snippet': 'One of the best-known American designers of the postwar era gets his first comprehensive retrospective.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The exhibition “George Nelson: Architect, Writer, Designer, Teacher” opens on Thursday at the Yale School of Architecture Gallery, its final stop on a four-year international tour, where it will be on view until Jan. 26, 2013. The exhibition, which was organized by the Vitra Design Museum in Weil am Rhein, Germany, includes more than 120 examples of furniture designs for home and office as well as over 50 drawings, models, photographs, films and other materials, and is the first comprehensive retrospective devoted to Nelson (1908-1986), one of the best-known American designers of the postwar era. Although he’s most famous for eye-catching designs like the Marshmallow Sofa, the Coconut Chair and the Ball Clock, Nelson — who was trained as an architect at Yale and was an influential editor at Architectural Forum magazine in the 1930s and ’40s — was most passionate about design’s role in the way people lived and worked. His 1945 book, “Tomorrow’s Houses” (with Henry Wright), espoused the family room and the storage wall; the latter, which was produced by Herman Miller, where Nelson was the director of design from 1945 to 1972, was one of his lasting contributions to the field. (He designed an L-shaped desk for Herman Miller that was a forerunner of the office workstation.) Among many other projects in his productive career, Nelson also did corporate image design for clients like General Electric and I.B.M.; he was the head designer for the American National Exhibition in Moscow in 1959; and he came up with a 64-foot-long car and a walk-in engine for Chrysler’s pavilion at the 1964 New York World’s Fair.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'See It Now | George Nelson at Yale', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker