ail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/08/business/Small-Business-slide-21SJ/Small-Business-slide-21SJ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/business/Small-Business-slide-21SJ/Small-Business-slide-21SJ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Aftermath of Sandy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T17:39:56+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ae211e83-a6a5-54e9-8128-9db24ca2005f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ae211e83-a6a5-54e9-8128-9db24ca2005f'}, {'abstract': 'The tiny Corn Islands lack designer boutiques, sprawling resorts and, sometimes, even a name for a town. But that may be precisely the reason to visit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/travel/off-nicaragua-a-quieter-caribbean.html', 'snippet': 'The tiny Corn Islands lack designer boutiques, sprawling resorts and, sometimes, even a name for a town. But that may be precisely the reason to visit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE darkness was as deep and pure as squid ink. I swiped my foot across the ground, feeling for rocks, roots and voids. Around me there was rustling, scurrying and crashing — the sounds of creatures meeting branches and leaves. Startled by some unseen threat, I stopped abruptly, colliding with my travel companion, Ashley, who followed close behind. Each time we slammed into each other, hapless as slapstick Stooges, we were reduced to fits of hysterical laughter — laughter masking fear and frustration.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/travel/11NEXT5_SPAN/11NEXT5_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/11/travel/11NEXT5_SPAN/11NEXT5_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/travel/11NEXT5_SPAN/11NEXT5_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/travel/11NEXT5_SPAN/11NEXT5_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1533, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/travel/11NEXT5_SPAN/11NEXT5_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/11/travel/11NEXT5_SPAN/11NEXT5_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/travel/11NEXT5_SPAN/11NEXT5_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Off Nicaragua, a Quieter Caribbean', 'kicker': 'Next Stop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Off the Nicaragua Coast, a Rustic Idyll', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Islands', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nicaragua', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Caribbean Area', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T17:46:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Freda Moon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Freda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/451fbfcf-ffd5-588c-b5ba-572a5cb201b3', 'word_count': 1696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/451fbfcf-ffd5-588c-b5ba-572a5cb201b3'}, {'abstract': 'Ari Brand, who has a starring role in the Off Broadway adaptation of Chaim Potok’s “My Name Is Asher Lev,” talks about the play and his “Broadway Bound” disappointment three years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/theater/ari-brand-on-my-name-is-asher-lev.html', 'snippet': 'Ari Brand, who has a starring role in the Off Broadway adaptation of Chaim Potok’s “My Name Is Asher Lev,” talks about the play and his “Broadway Bound” disappointment three years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARI BRAND, 28, suffered the professional heartbreak of seeing his Broadway debut go up in smoke three years ago. He was cast to understudy the role of Eugene in “Broadway Bound,” half of “The Neil Simon Plays,” but the other half closed early, and his production never happened. Last year he rebounded with a well-received performance Off Broadway as the bridegroom in A. R. Gurney’s “Black Tie.” And now he has the starring role in another Off Broadway production: the stage adaptation of Chaim Potok’s “My Name Is Asher Lev,” the story of an artist clashing with his Hasidic parents, which began performances at the Westside Theater on Thursday. He played the role this year to wildly admiring reviews at the Long Wharf Theater in New Haven.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/arts/11SNAPSHOT/11SILOSNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 497, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/arts/11SNAPSHOT/11SILOSNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 993, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/arts/11SNAPSHOT/11SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/11/arts/11SNAPSHOT/11SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/arts/11SNAPSHOT/11SNAPSHOT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rebounding Off Broadway, After a Detour', 'kicker': 'Snapshot | Ari Brand', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rebounding Off Broadway, After a Detour', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brand, Ari', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T17:46:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank':