e the machinery.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/nyregion/video-crane/video-crane-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/06/nyregion/video-crane/video-crane-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/nyregion/video-crane/video-crane-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/06/nyregion/video-crane/video-crane-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rescuing the Crippled Crane', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Derricks and Cranes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T19:23:13+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'Shayla Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shayla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/f56f5382-1e93-5d4d-858c-4b451f54f0a2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/f56f5382-1e93-5d4d-858c-4b451f54f0a2'}, {'abstract': 'Jason Bay, who was signed through the end of the 2013 season and had a $3 million buyout clause for 2014, had three hugely disappointing years with the Mets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/sports/baseball/mets-and-jason-bay-agree-to-part-ways.html', 'snippet': 'Jason Bay, who was signed through the end of the 2013 season and had a $3 million buyout clause for 2014, had three hugely disappointing years with the Mets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIAN WELLS, Calif. — Over three ignominious seasons, Jason Bay evolved into the most visible symbol of the Mets’ recent frustrations and the chief target of their fans’ scorn. That all came to an abrupt end on Wednesday, as the team and the outfielder reached an agreement for the early expiration of his contract, granting him unrestricted free agency.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/sports/baseball/08mets-pic/08mets-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/08/sports/baseball/08mets-pic/08mets-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/sports/baseball/08mets-pic/08mets-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/sports/baseball/08mets-pic/08mets-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/sports/baseball/08mets-pic/08mets-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/08/sports/baseball/08mets-pic/08mets-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/sports/baseball/08mets-pic/08mets-pic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Three Seasons of Failure, Bay and the Mets Go Their Separate Ways', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Three Seasons of Failure, Bay and the Mets Go Their Separate Ways', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bay, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T19:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb4a1ff0-706b-53d6-8c74-9f4c5a3d9b8d', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb4a1ff0-706b-53d6-8c74-9f4c5a3d9b8d'}, {'abstract': 'After a severe storm hits, New York City’s wild animals seem to bounce right back, and some even benefit from the damage.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/where-do-the-wild-ones-go/', 'snippet': 'After a severe storm hits, New York City’s wild animals seem to bounce right back, and some even benefit from the damage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a damaging storm, an outpouring of support often flows to the people affected and even their pets. But the day after last week’s superstorm hit New York City, I noticed sparrows pecking away as usual at the freshly turned earth. My thoughts turned to how the city’s wildlife fared — the birds, raccoons, red foxes, mice and so on. Are they as resilient as they seem?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Do the Wild Ones Go?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T19:33:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma Bryce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bryce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b1a71f1-9686-543b-ac09-81bb580d77f1', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b1a71f1-9686-543b-ac09-81bb580d77f1'}, {'abstract': 'Although voters complained of long lines, the turnout in New York City seems to be lower than it was four years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/voter-turnout-was-lower-than-in-2008-according-to-early-count/', 'snippet': 'Although voters complained of long lines, the turnout in New York City seems to be lower than it was four years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite complaints from voters about long lines, fewer people cast ballots on Tuesday than in the 2008 presidential election, according to unofficial results from the city’s Board of Elections.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/07polling/07polling-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/07polling/07polling-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/07polling/07polling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/07polling/07polling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/nyregion/07polling/07polling-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Voter Turnout Was Lower Than in 2008, According to Early Count', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Board of Elections (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T19:34:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a57a0b10-caab-50c2-bac7-9ac4d0c8e7f9', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a57a0b10-caab-50c2-bac7-9ac4d0c8e7f9'}, {'abstract': 'In “Louis Armstrong: Jazz Ambassador,” by Myla Churchill, Armstrong defends his life at the gates of heaven.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/theater/reviews/louis-armstrong-from-making-books-sing.html', 'snippet': 'In “Louis Armstrong: Jazz Ambassador,” by Myla Churchill, Armstrong defends his life at the gates of heaven.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of Louis Armstrong’s best-known hits is “What a Wonderful World.” In “Louis Armstrong: Jazz Ambassador,” now playing at Theater 3, Jeremy Giraud Abram, in the title role, sings it, while behind him a montage of projected images shows the Jim Crow South: whites-only facilities, a boy in a Ku Klux Klan costume and a sign that reads, “Southern Whites Are the Negroes’ Best Friends, but No Integration.” The world Armstrong lived in was often far from wonderful.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/louis/louis-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/louis/louis-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/louis/louis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/louis/louis-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1151, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/louis/louis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/louis/louis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/louis/louis-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Trumpeter’s Voice, Onstage and Beyond', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Trumpeter’s Voice, Onstage and Beyond', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'su