 the hubbub of Election Day and when the results came in at night, along with storm coverage.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/times-was-slower-but-sure-in-calling-the-presidential-election/', 'snippet': 'The public editor takes a critical look at the hubbub of Election Day and when the results came in at night, along with storm coverage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few observations on Tuesday night’s online coverage and Wednesday’s print edition:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Times Was Slower, but Sure, in Calling the Presidential Election', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T20:32:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fdfb0a0-595a-5c23-b5a2-e8a4cba91ba4', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fdfb0a0-595a-5c23-b5a2-e8a4cba91ba4'}, {'abstract': 'In this lesson, students research different ideas to protect New York City from future hurricane damage and determine which they believe is the best option. Then, students research local hazards, and develop plans for mitigating impacts to housing, transportation, utilities and more.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/manage-the-damage-preparing-for-natural-disasters/', 'snippet': 'In this lesson, students research different ideas to protect New York City from future hurricane damage and determine which they believe is the best option. Then, students research local hazards, and develop plans for mitigating impacts to housing...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Overview | Is i