y': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/08/fashion/08ELECTION1_SPAN/08ELECTION1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/fashion/08ELECTION1_SPAN/08ELECTION1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Politics as Usual on Party Circuit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Politics as Usual on Party Circuit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T20:47:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bee-Shyuan Chang and Jacob Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bee-shyuan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a208ef6c-cb31-597b-a4ca-3947e12219f5', 'word_count': 1527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a208ef6c-cb31-597b-a4ca-3947e12219f5'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Seinfeld will perform an additional show on Dec. 19 at the NYCB Theater in Westbury, N.Y., and donate his income from that event (as well as previously scheduled shows in Brooklyn and Staten Island) to relief organizations.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/seinfeld-adds-show-to-benefit-hurricane-sandy-relief/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Seinfeld will perform an additional show on Dec. 19 at the NYCB Theater in Westbury, N.Y., and donate his income from that event (as well as previously scheduled shows in Brooklyn and Staten Island) to relief organizations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jerry Seinfeld may joke that his comedy is about nothing, but he’s found something to which he will be dedicating his upcoming standup shows. Mr. Seinfeld said on Wednesday that he\xa0 would\xa0 perform an additional show on Long Island, as part of his current comedy tour of New York, and that he would\xa0 donate his income from that show to local organizations providing relief for people affected by Hurricane Sandy. This new show will take place on Dec. 19 at the NYCB Theater in Westbury, N.Y., and tickets will go on sale Nov. 30. Mr. Seinfeld, who grew up on Long Island, said that he and fellow comedian Colin Quinn would also donate their profits from sold-out shows at the Walt Whitman Theater in Brooklyn (on Thursday) and the St. George Theater in Staten Island (on Dec. 6) to local relief organizations.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/seinfeld/seinfeld-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 493, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/seinfeld/seinfeld-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 493, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/seinfeld/seinfeld-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/seinfeld/seinfeld-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/seinfeld/seinfeld-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seinfeld Adds Show to Benefit Hurricane  Relief', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seinfeld Adds Show For Storm Relief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Colin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seinfeld, Jerry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T20:52:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e87a69eb-6090-50a0-8c52-38ecd9c8c541', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e87a69eb-6090-50a0-8c52-38ecd9c8c541'}, {'abstract': '“Mr. Penumbra’s 24-Hour Bookstore” is an easygoing novel imbued with a romantic appreciation of the tech-free life, and centered around a culture clash between old and new.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/books/mr-penumbras-24-hour-bookstore-by-robin-sloan.html', 'snippet': '“Mr. Penumbra’s 24-Hour Bookstore” is an easygoing novel imbued with a romantic appreciation of the tech-free life, and centered around a culture clash between old and new.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man walks into a bookstore. He is young, smart, and charmingly hapless, lost in the West Coast techie culture in which rock climbing is the exercise of choice, typographical fonts are conversation pieces, and Google whiz kids represent the highest form of human perfection. According to “Mr. Penumbra’s 24-Hour Bookstore,” Robin Sloan’s slyly arch novel about technology and its discontents, one of the many projects under way at Google’s Mountain View, Calif., campus is “developing a form of renewable energy that runs on hubris.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 783, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/book/book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1567, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Aces Can’t Defeat Bibliophiles', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Google Aces Can’t Defeat Bibliophiles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sloan, Robin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T20:55:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0eea6a8-7674-5870-8b92-d9cf30e21570', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0eea6a8-7674-5870-8b92-d9cf30e21570'}, {'abstract': 'While Lower Manhattan was widely affected by the storm, a handful of stores were seriously damaged by flooding.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/fashion/some-stores-in-chelsea-struggle-to-reopen-after-storm.html', 'snippet': 'While Lower Manhattan was widely affected by the storm, a handful of stores were seriously damaged by flooding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY afternoon in the street-level headquarters of Showroom Seven, in the Terminal Warehouse building in the heart of flood-damaged West Chelsea, three dozen employees and volunteers huddled over card tables, sitting in the dark, sorting, cleaning, washing and drying countless piles of crystal beads — each tiny, shiny one by hand. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/fashion/08ROW_SPAN/08zROW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/08/fashion/08ROW_SPAN/08zROW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/fashion/08ROW_SPAN/08zROW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/fashion/08ROW_SPAN/08zROW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/fashion/08ROW_SPAN/08zROW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/08/fashion/08ROW_SPAN/08zROW-thumbStandard.jpg', 