: 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd7aa245-d0aa-5375-98f7-88c764ed07c0', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd7aa245-d0aa-5375-98f7-88c764ed07c0'}, {'abstract': 'Photos from Ghana, Greece, Iraq and Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/pictures-of-the-day-ghana-and-elsewhere/', 'snippet': 'Photos from Ghana, Greece, Iraq and Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos from Ghana, Greece, Iraq and Syria.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Ghana and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T21:34:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11f69cac-705d-5bb5-bfc7-6f86c67aacec', 'word_count': 12, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11f69cac-705d-5bb5-bfc7-6f86c67aacec'}, {'abstract': 'Stylish plus-size women, hungry for fashion but ignored by designers, are finding their own community on the Internet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/fashion/plus-size-fashion-bloggers-are-role-models.html', 'snippet': 'Stylish plus-size women, hungry for fashion but ignored by designers, are finding their own community on the Internet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EARLIER this year, Gabi Gregg, a Chicago fashion blogger who wears a size 18, posted a photo of herself wearing a bikini. It caused such a ruckus that Ms. Gregg, 26, was invited on the “Today” show.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/fashion/08PLUS1_SPAN/08zPLUS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/08/fashion/08PLUS1_SPAN/08zPLUS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/fashion/08PLUS1_SPAN/08zPLUS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 752, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/fashion/08PLUS1_SPAN/08zPLUS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1505, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/fashion/08PLUS1_SPAN/08PLUS1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/08/fashion/08PLUS1_SPAN/08PLUS1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/fashion/08PLUS1_SPAN/08PLUS1_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Plus-Size and Blazing a New Path', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plus-Size And Blazing A New Path', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T21:38:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marisa Meltzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meltzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50dc0de5-e241-5fe0-abfe-d596ce0dde43', 'word_count': 1266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50dc0de5-e241-5fe0-abfe-d596ce0dde43'}, {'abstract': 'Behind the “breast is best” push has always been an uncomfortable truth: that breastfeeding is more supported by lip service, promotion and hospital nudges than by giving women the time and opportunity to do it.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/bottle-or-breast-shouldnt-define-whats-best/', 'snippet': 'Behind the “breast is best” push has always been an uncomfortable truth: that breastfeeding is more supported by lip service, promotion and hospital nudges than by giving women the time and opportunity to do it.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Breast is best” is a slogan so universal that it’s even touted by companies advertising the competing product. Suzanne Barston, author of “Bottled Up: How the Way We Feed Babies Has Come to Define Motherhood, and Why It Shouldn’t,” argues that the “breast is best” forces have inadvertently sent a more comprehensive message: breastfeeding mothers are best, and bottle-feeding mothers just can’t compete. It’s a distracting message — because there’s still a conversation to be had surrounding the choices women make in feeding their infants, and who wins the “best feeder” award isn’t it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bottle or Breast Shouldn’t Define What’s Best', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breastfeeding', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T21:54:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ffdbaba-ce17-5ca0-8ef9-536c90cb38e9', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ffdbaba-ce17-5ca0-8ef9-536c90cb38e9'}, {'abstract': 'Booby-trapped ammunition has a extensive history, but the practice is controversial, its legality is questionable and governments have rarely disclosed information about programs intended to pass lethal products into others’ hands.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/dirty-tricks-of-government-forces-where-deception-and-deadliness-meet-inside-a-gun/', 'snippet': 'Booby-trapped ammunition has a extensive history, but the practice is controversial, its legality is questionable and governments have rarely disclosed information about programs intended to pass lethal products into others’ hands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When out on patrols in Afghanistan, Western soldiers often uncover ammunition caches used by the region’s many fighting groups. And when on the archipelago of outposts from which they work, these same soldiers routinely have access to weapons carried by the Taliban, including Kalashnikov assault rifles, PK machine guns, rocket-propelled-grenade launchers and 82-millimeter mortars. But soldiers and Marines have been told for years not to combine these two naturally paired items — captured ammunition with captured arms — for training or other uses, even though practice with the most common weapons in Afghanistan could reasonably be seen as a valuable part of preparing for the war’s daily work. Western forces are also discouraged from collecting ammunition in the field and passing it on to the Afghan Army and police forces, who often carry weapons that could use it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/world/07atwar-chivers-spike-2/07atwar-chivers-spike-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 724, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/world/07atwar-chivers-spike-2/07atwar-chivers-spike-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1449, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/world/07atwar-chivers-spike-2/07atwar-chivers-spike-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/07/world/07atwar-chivers-spike-2/07atwar-chivers-spike-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/world/07atwar-chivers-spike-2/07atwar-chivers-spike-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dirty Tricks of Government Forces: Where Deception and Deadliness Meet Inside a Gun', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T21:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebe4558f-8415-565b-827b-c9097e99490a', 'word_count': 2690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebe4558f-8415-565b-827b-c9097e99490a'}, {'abstract': 'House Speaker John A. Boehner of Ohio said he is ready to accept a budget deal that raises federal revenues as long as it is linked to an overhaul of entitlements and a reform of the tax code that closes loopholes, curtails or eliminates deductions and lowers income tax rates.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/boehner-strikes-conciliatory-tone-on-fiscal-cliff/', 'snippet': 'House Speaker John A. Boehner of Ohio said he is ready to accept a budget deal that raises federal revenues as long as it is linked to an overhaul of entitlements and a reform of the tax code that closes loopholes, curtails or eliminates deduction...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The House speaker, John A. Boehner of Ohio, striking a conciliatory tone a day after the Republican Party’s electoral drubbing, said on Wednesday that he was ready to accept a budget deal that raises federal revenue as long as it is linked to an overhaul of entitlements and a reform of the tax code that closes loopholes, curtails or eliminates deductions and lowers income tax rates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boehner Strikes Conciliatory Tone on ‘Fiscal Cliff’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords':