esday to sell “Draped Seated Woman,” the 1957 bronze that Henry Moore sold to the ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Against the very vocal opposition of important figures in the British art world the council of the Borough of Tower Hamlets in the East End of London decided on Wednesday to sell “Draped Seated Woman,” the 1957 bronze that Henry Moore sold to the London County Council at a steep discount in 1960. And the reason given for the decision by Lutfur Rahman, the mayor of Tower Hamlets, is basically: the Government is forcing his hand. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Controversial Sale of Henry Moore Sculpture to Go Forward', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adjaye, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boyle, Danny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deller, Jeremy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Henry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tate Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yorkshire (England)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T22:14:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4ec300e-4b0e-5c00-8fbf-85109adf209d', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4ec300e-4b0e-5c00-8fbf-85109adf209d'}, {'abstract': 'Sam Mendes, the director of “Skyfall,” discusses making the latest film in the James Bond franchi