ge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Obama’s Data Crunchers, Movie Computers and the Perils of E-Voting', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T22:37:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebf34a08-075f-5fa0-a191-24808eb402a7', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebf34a08-075f-5fa0-a191-24808eb402a7'}, {'abstract': '“Before Hoboken had power, we had Danny,” says a customer of Danny Vignola, who was back in his delivery truck on Friday, a few days after Hurricane Sandy left the waterfront city flooded and dark.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/a-sense-of-comfort-in-hoboken-as-the-u-p-s-man-makes-his-rounds/', 'snippet': '“Before Hoboken had power, we had Danny,” says a customer of Danny Vignola, who was back in his delivery truck on Friday, a few days after Hurricane Sandy left the waterfront city flooded and dark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Their New Jersey city had been steamrollered by Hurricane Sandy, forcing a major evacuation from waterlogged homes. They went days without power and heat and basic necessities like food and water. So as the people of Hoboken struggle to recover, some beleaguered residents have taken solace at the sight of a man in a brown suit carrying boxes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/nyregion/07cityroom-ups/07cityroom-ups-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/nyregion/07cityroom-ups/07cityroom-ups-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/nyregion/07cityroom-ups/07cityroom-ups-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/08/nyregion/07cityroom-ups/07cityroom-ups-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/nyregion/07cityroom-ups/07cityroom-ups-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sense of Comfort in Hoboken as the U.P.S. Man Makes His Rounds', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Comfort in Weary Hoboken Comes in a U.P.S. Uniform', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hoboken (NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T22:47:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Schweber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd4cfbdc-6953-5f5b-90af-9af7edf7a7cc', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd4cfbdc-6953-5f5b-90af-9af7edf7a7cc'}, {'abstract': 'A lawsuit against the gallery owner Larry Gagosian is pulling back the curtain slightly on the way high-end deals are made in the contemporary art world.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/gagosian-suit-offers-rare-look-at-art-dealing/', 'snippet': 'A lawsuit against the gallery owner Larry Gagosian is pulling back the curtain slightly on the way high-end deals are made in the contemporary art world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lawsuit claiming that the gallery owner Larry Gagosian defrauded a prominent collector is pulling back the curtain, if ever so slightly, on the way high-end deals are sometimes made in the contemporary art world. The collector, Jan Cowles, 93, sued in January, accusing Mr. Gagosian of selling a 1964 Roy Lichtenstein painting, “Girl in Mirror,” from her collection without her consent. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/07artsbeat-gagosian/07artsbeat-gagosian-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/07artsbeat-gagosian/07artsbeat-gagosian-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1367, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/07artsbeat-gagosian/07artsbeat-gagosian-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/07artsbeat-gagosian/07artsbeat-gagosian-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/arts/07artsbeat-gagosian/07artsbeat-gagosian-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gagosian Suit Offers Rare Look at Art Dealing', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gagosian Suit Offers Rare Look at Dealing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gagosian, Larry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lichtenstein, Roy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gagosian Gallery', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T22:50:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91e48d48-eaea-556e-bdb1-dcc58909bb89', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91e48d48-eaea-556e-bdb1-dcc58909bb89'}, {'abstract': 'Jurors were “entitled to conclude” that a city councilwoman changed her mind about supporting a development project in order to benefit an operative who had showered her with gifts, a judge ruled.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/judge-upholds-convictions-in-yonkers-corruption-case/', 'snippet': 'Jurors were “entitled to conclude” that a city councilwoman changed her mind about supporting a development project in order to benefit an operative who had showered her with gifts, a judge ruled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge in Manhattan on Wednesday upheld the convictions of a former Yonkers councilwoman, Sandy Annabi, and a political operative who had testified that he had given her gifts out of love and not for corrupt reasons, as the government had charged.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Upholds Convictions in Yonkers Corruption Case', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Annabi, Sandy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jereis, Zehy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMahon, Colleen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Forest City Ratner Companies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yonkers (NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T22:52:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a95ac260-c86c-5cf9-a979-c85f4fabf2a7', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a95ac260-c86c-5cf9-a979-c85f4fabf2a7'}, {'abstract': 'Pregame at Red Bull Arena in the snow before Game 2 of the Eastern Conference playoffs in M.L.S.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/red-bull-arena-in-the-snow/', 'snippet': 'Pregame at Red Bull Arena in the snow before Game 2 of the Eastern Conference playoffs in M.L.S.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:38 p.m. |Update', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Red Bull Arena in the Snow', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Red Bulls (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T23:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98302b7d-7a4f-5bec-81d6-1a1c58c66928', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98302b7d-7a4f-5bec-81d6-1a1c58c66928'}, {'abstract': 'China is set to implement a new organ-donation system that officials say will ease the country’s dependence on organs taken from executed prisoners. But few Chinese are willing to pledge to donate their organs.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/organ-donation-struggles-to-take-hold-in-china/', 'snippet': 'China is set to implement a new organ-donation system that officials say will ease the country’s dependence on organs taken from executed prisoners. But few Chinese are willing to pledge to donate their organs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — A senior official with the Chinese Ministry of Health says the country must end its dependence on organs taken from executed prisoners even as it struggles to establish “an ethical and sustainable organ donation system.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/blogs/organs-rdv/organs-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 755, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/blogs/organs-rdv/organs-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1510, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/blogs/organs-rdv/organs-rdv-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/05/blogs/organs-rdv/organs-rdv-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/05/blogs/organs-rdv/organs-rdv-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China Fights to Go Beyond Organs Harvested From Executed Prisoners', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organ Donation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transplants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T23:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e7a93d3-08a9-5012-ad2a-67fd8974d207', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e7a93d3-08a9-5012-ad2a-67fd8974d207'}, {'abstract': 'Here is the difference between 4G and 4G LTE.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/what-is-a-4g-network/', 'snippet': 'Here is the difference between 4G and 4G LTE.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From today’s mailbag:Dear Mr. Pogue,What is the difference between 4G and 4G LTE?And my reply:Well, 4G is supposed to mean 4G LTE.But AT&T has come up with a network type that’s halfway in between 3G and LTE — something it calls 4G. It’s faster than 3G, but nowhere near as good as LTE. So all the other companies, like Verizon, use the term “4G LTE” to emphasize that they have real 4G — the super fast type. This explains why AT&T can advertise “the biggest 4G network” — because none of its competitors even count 4G area! For them, and for you, LTE is the really desirable network type.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Is a 4G Network?', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T23:01:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ce6a735-d8ab-53db-8755-b0b6b211ad44', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ce6a735-d8ab-53db-8755-b0b6b211ad44'}, {'abstract': 'The Rolling Stones perform “The Last Time” in Peter Whitehead’s documentary of a chaotic 1965 tour, which was just been released on DVD.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/arts/100000001891615/excerpt-charlie-is-my-darling.html', 'snippet': 'The Rolling Stones perform “The Last Time” in Peter Whitehead’s documentary of a chaotic 1965 tour, which was just been released on DVD.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Rolling Stones perform “The Last Time” in Peter Whitehead’s documentary of a chaotic 1965 tour, which was just been released on DVD.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/multimedia/video-stones/video-stones-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/07/multimedia/video-stones/video-stones-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/07/multimedia/video-stones/video-stones-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/07/multimedia/video-stones/video-stones-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Excerpt: ‘Charlie Is My Darling’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T23:11:20+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'ABKCO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abkco', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/4ea4bd49-650a-596e-89d6-162f098f6893', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/4ea4bd49-650a-596e-89d6-162f098f6893'}, {'abstract': 'A concert meant as a tribute to John Cage was paradoxically, perhaps, wholly devoted to music by Morton Feldman, a Cage associate who died in 1987.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/arts/music/janacek-philharmonic-ostrava-plays-morton-feldman.html', 'snippet': 'A concert meant as a tribute to John Cage was paradoxically, perhaps, wholly devoted to music by Morton Feldman, a Cage associate who died in 1987.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can picture the beatifically amused smile that would crease John Cage’s face, were he somehow able to witness the outpouring of tributes celebrating his 100th birthday this year. Yet as I was waiting to attend the latest event in his honor, at Alice Tully Hall on Monday evening, I was thinking about another American maverick: Elliott Carter, who had died that day at 103, having lived long enough to witness a comparable centenary ballyhoo.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/FELDMAN/FELDMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/FELDMAN/FELDMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/FELDMAN/FELDMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/FELDMAN/FELDMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1222, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrating a Centenary With Works by a Friend', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Celebrating A Centenary With Works By a Friend', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-07T23:12:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/63d15f29-3e9b-5283-9cc0-3c52c49eb999', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63d15f29-3e9b-5283-9cc0-3c52c49eb999'}, {'abstract': 'Gallery owners in Chelsea expect to spend the next several weeks juggling meetings with restoration specialists, contractors and insurance adjusters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/arts/design/chelsea-galleries-face-complexities-of-art-triage.html', 'snippet': 'Gallery owners in Chelsea expect to spend the next several weeks juggling meetings with restoration specialists, contractors and insurance adjusters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At most of the art galleries in Chelsea the water that poured in from the Hudson River during Hurricane Sandy has been pumped out, and the business of sorting out artworks — separating those that survived intact from those that didn’t, figuring out which of the damaged works are reparable — is well under way. Gallery owners no longer sound as despondent as they did last week, when they returned to their businesses in the strip between 10th and 11th Avenues, from 18th to 29th Streets, and found flooded basements, high water marks five feet up their walls, and a loss of art, documentation, catalogs and reference books, to say nothing of physical spaces that will need to be rebuilt. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/CHELSEA/CHELSEA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 581, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/CHELSEA/CHELSEA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 581, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/CHELSEA/CHELSEA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/08/arts/CHELSEA/CHELSEA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth'