", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T01:48:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/666e8191-342b-5842-a15e-ab452aa011ec', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/666e8191-342b-5842-a15e-ab452aa011ec'}, {'abstract': 'America’s changing demographics didn’t seal Obama’s victory. It was his appeal to the middle-class values that matter to most voters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/opinion/obama-won-on-values-not-demographics.html', 'snippet': 'America’s changing demographics didn’t seal Obama’s victory. It was his appeal to the middle-class values that matter to most voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MUCH of the coverage of Tuesday’s results has focused on the strength of Barack Obama’s coalition — minorities, women and young voters. But that analysis misses the real point. The contours of the 2012 presidential race were shaped less by the country’s changing demographics than by the underlying attitudes and values of American voters, who are always far more complex than they appear to pollsters. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Values, Not Demographics, Won the Election', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Values, Not Demographics, Won the Election', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T01:49:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joel Benenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f56454cc-7580-5eb5-9cea-280ae64c8ae0', 'word_count': 1164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f56454cc-7580-5eb5-9cea-280ae64c8ae0'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s task for his second term: inspire confidence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/opinion/can-obama-give-us-confidence.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s task for his second term: inspire confidence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A CLOSE vote by a split electorate has handed President Obama a second term. He steps up, revived and renewed, to preside over a divided nation that often seems to agree on only one thing: today’s children will live less well than their parents. This pervasive loss of confidence, though hard to precisely measure, is of enormous consequence. It’s what sinks civilizations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/opinion/1108OPEDtopos/1108OPEDtopos-jumbo.jpg', 'heig