iginal': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/a81baa82-7b13-56dd-972c-439c3563570b', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a81baa82-7b13-56dd-972c-439c3563570b'}, {'abstract': 'The winners of two state races will not be known at least until absentee ballots are counted, but even if Democrats win, fractures in the party could lead to a Republican running the Senate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/nyregion/new-york-senate-makeup-is-unclear-but-talk-turns-to-which-party-will-lead.html', 'snippet': 'The winners of two state races will not be known at least until absentee ballots are counted, but even if Democrats win, fractures in the party could lead to a Republican running the Senate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Democrats on Wednesday began preparing to lead the New York State Senate after shocking the political establishment with strong performances in a number of contests on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'P', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/nyregion/ALBANY2-1352332924614/ALBANY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 907, 'width': 628, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/nyregion/ALBANY2-1352332924614/ALBANY2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 907, 'width': 628, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Senate Makeup Is Unclear, but Talk Turns to Which Party Will Lead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York Senate Makeup Is Unclear, but Talk Turns to Which Party Will Lead', 'name': None, 'se