ist, persevere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Under a soft, blue sky, a no. 82 public bus rumbled past Tiananmen Square at 7 a.m. on Thursday, windows taped shut. The vast square in the heart of Beijing was sealed off to the public as uniformed security officers and sniffer dogs prowled. Inside the Great Hall of the People, where the 18th Communist Party Congress began at 9 a.m., a security official ran bomb detection equipment over an emergency stretcher – two of the 2,270 appointed delegates to the congress representing China’s 83 million communists have died and the oldest attending delegate is 97. No one was taking any chances with death, natural or unnatural.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/blogs/08rdv-china-congress-didi-roof-star/08rdv-china-congress-didi-roof-star-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/blogs/08rdv-china-congress-didi-roof-star/08rdv-china-congress-didi-roof-star-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Intimate Look Inside the ‘Eighteenth Big’', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T07:10:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'ty