assive” solar performance counts.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/first-things-first-an-efficient-abode/', 'snippet': 'Even solar power advocates say that using solar panels to make electricity is actually the least important part of making a home less dependent on fossil fuels. But “passive” solar performance counts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last few weeks have been a whirlwind of activity at our construction site in Moab as we enter our final month volunteering for the nonprofit group Community Rebuilds. We installed the doors, windows and interior walls and screwed up drywall for the ceiling of the straw bale home we’re building. It’s starting to look like the inside of a real house.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Things First: An Efficient Abode', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heating', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refrigerators', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Windows', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Community Rebuilds (Moab, Utah)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Renewable Energy Laboratory', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moab (Utah)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'nam