55856ca4'}, {'abstract': 'Nineteen other people were injured when scaffolding erected to hold a billboard collapsed.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/woman-killed-in-scaffolding-collapse-at-linkin-park-concert/', 'snippet': 'Nineteen other people were injured when scaffolding erected to hold a billboard collapsed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A woman died and 19 other people were injured when scaffolding collapsed Wednesday night outside a Linkin Park concert in Cape Town, South Africa, the BBC and The Associated Press reported. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woman Killed in Scaffolding Collapse Outside Linkin Park Concert', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scaffolding Collapse at a Linkin Park Concert in South Africa Kills a Woman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GlaxoSmithKline PLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Linkin Park', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cape Town (South Africa)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T14:12:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd121285-6262-5f1f-ad9f-4a4e6fb399eb', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd121285-6262-5f1f-ad9f-4a4e6fb399eb'}, {'abstract': 'Also, the man behind the anti-Islam video that in September ignited bloody protests in the Muslim world is sentenced to prison for violating the terms of his parole.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/the-breakfast-meeting-numbers-crunchers-defeat-pundits-and-sex-film-industry-is-stung/', 'snippet': 'Also, the man behind the anti-Islam video that in September ignited bloody protests in the Muslim world is sentenced to prison for violating the terms of his parole.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While everyone was watching how voters would settle the Obama-Romney contest for the presidency, they also settled, for now, another dispute, Michael Cooper writes: the pundits versus the number crunchers. It was the number crunchers in a landslide, as polls — especially when they had been looked at cumulatively as a so-called “polls of polls” — were quite accurate. The political pundits, including those with a partisan bent — like Karl Rove, Dick Morris and Michael Barone — were far from the mark with their predictions of a big Romney victory.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Numbers-Crunchers Defeat Pundits, and Sex Film Industry Is Stung', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nakoula, Nakoula Basseley', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rove, Karl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T14:19:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlenam