technology has grown more sophisticated, photojournalists have been able to bring us ever closer to its daily realities and to offer new ways of understanding the experience of those who live through it. That’s one lesson of “War/Photography: Images of Armed Conflict and Its Aftermath,” now at the Museum of Fine Arts, Houston, through Feb. 3.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/arts/design/20121111-SUBCOMBAT-slide-UNWZ/20121111-SUBCOMBAT-slide-UNWZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/11/arts/design/20121111-SUBCOMBAT-slide-UNWZ/20121111-SUBCOMBAT-slide-UNWZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/arts/design/20121111-SUBCOMBAT-slide-UNWZ/20121111-SUBCOMBAT-slide-UNWZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/arts/design/20121111-SUBCOMBAT-slide-UNWZ/20121111-SUBCOMBAT-slide-UNWZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/arts/design/20121111-SUBCOMBAT-slide-UNWZ/20121111-SUBCOMBAT-slide-UNWZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/11/arts/design/20121111-SUBCOMBAT-slide-UNWZ/20121111-SUBCOMBAT-slide-UNWZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': 