': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c72b2c33-bfe7-531a-a806-268eab10323c', 'word_count': 1080, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c72b2c33-bfe7-531a-a806-268eab10323c'}, {'abstract': 'New Hampshire’s all-mother congressional delegation and governor is a first, but still just a footnote — and that in itself is a sign of how much things have changed.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/new-hampshires-all-mother-congressional-delegation-and-governor/', 'snippet': 'New Hampshire’s all-mother congressional delegation and governor is a first, but still just a footnote — and that in itself is a sign of how much things have changed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the election of the Democrats Ann McLane Kuster and former Representative Carol Shea-Porter to the House of Representatives, New Hampshire becomes the first state to send an all-female delegation to Congress. (Kuster and Shea-Porter join Senators Jeanne Shaheen, a Democrat, and Kelly Ayotte, a Republican.) And with the election of Maggie Hassan as governor, it becomes the first state that is primarily helmed, politically, by women — and not just women, but mothers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/style/motherlode-nh-women/motherlode-nh-women-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 727, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/style/motherlode-nh-women/motherlode-nh-women-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 727, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/style/motherlode-nh-women/motherlode-nh-women-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/08/style/motherlode-nh-women/motherlode-nh-women-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/style/motherlode-nh-women/motherlode-nh-women-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Hampshire’s All-Mother Congressional Delegation (and Governor)', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ayotte, Kelly A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hassan, Maggie', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuster, Ann McLane', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaheen, Jeanne', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shea-Porter, Carol', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T15:08:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d73628e9-c823-592d-9d0c-851c4e3f0ad5', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d73628e9-c823-592d-9d0c-851c4e3f0ad5'}, {'abstract': 'Orlando Palacios, the owner and hatter of Worth & Worth, dispenses thumbnail wisdom on buying and wearing hats.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/video-shopping-for-a-classic-hat/', 'snippet': 'Orlando Palacios, the owner and hatter of Worth & Worth, dispenses thumbnail wisdom on buying and wearing hats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One autumn night, more years ago than I’d care to remember, I was in a restaurant bathroom and caught a glimpse of the back of my head in a three-way mirror. What I’d thought was a patch of thinning hair was to my amazement completely bald.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Shopping for a Classic Chapeau', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hats and Caps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T15:10:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric V Copage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': 'V <missing Dot>', 'lastname': 'Copage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13a0e406-bdc3-536c-ad97-2990a1708f50', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13a0e406-bdc3-536c-ad97-2990a1708f50'}, {'abstract': 'The chef Laurent Tourondel and the entrepreneur Jimmy Haber have settled litigation from the breakup of their restaurant empire two and a half years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/at-last-a-truce-in-the-blt-battle/', 'snippet': 'The chef Laurent Tourondel and the entrepreneur Jimmy Haber have settled litigation from the breakup of their restaurant empire two and a half years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It wasn’t the Peloponnesian War, or even the Seven Years’ War. The struggle began only two and a half years ago, when Laurent Tourondel, the haute French chef, and Jimmy Haber, the restaurateur and corporate entrepreneur, ended their partnership in the $80 million BLT empire.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Last, a Truce in the BLT Battle', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haber, Jimmy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tourondel, Laurent', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BLT FISH', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T15:25:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c4e74a0-0c5b-55e6-aa57-dbd580a0138a', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c4e74a0-0c5b-55e6-aa57-dbd580a0138a'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/what-were-reading-563/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Post: Being among the many without power after Hurricane Sandy has changed Gov. Andrew Cuomo’s eating habits. Sandra Lee, the Food Network cook who is also the governor’s girlfriend, explains. — Susan Edgerley', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T15:27:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/980a2262-5314-53c8-9614-bacb12d2c6e1', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/980a2262-5314-53c8-9614-bacb12d2c6e1'}, {'abstract': 'The three-party coalition of Prime Minister Antonis Samaras was licking its wounds following the defections of several key members in a crucial vote on austerity measures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/world/europe/defections-shake-greek-coalition.html', 'snippet': 'The three-party coalition of Prime Minister Antonis Samaras was licking its wounds following the defections of several key members in a crucial vote on austerity measures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — The three-party coalition of Prime Minister Antonis Samaras was licking its wounds on Thursday, after the defections of several key members in a crucial vote on austerity measures. The proposals, aimed at keeping the country in the euro zone, passed narrowly but the defections, mostly among Socialist Party members, shook the government’s stability. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Defections Shake Greek Coalition', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Defections Shake Greek Coalition', 'na