ionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/cold-steel-and-crossed-sabers-at-little-washington/', 'snippet': 'How a charismatic rebel cavalryman fought his way across Civil War Virginia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a violent denouement to the enormous set-piece battles of Second Bull Run and Antietam in the summer of 1862, that fall cavalry clashes raged across Northern Virginia. In dozens of farm villages and crossroads communities, roving bands of Union and Confederate horsemen engaged in a series of brief and often bloody skirmishes. One such fight took place near the hamlet of Little Washington on Nov. 8, 1862. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cold Steel and Crossed Sabers at Little Washington', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T17:30:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eedb633a-12b6-59d1-bc37-9ea2c1845cc9', 'word_count': 1726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eedb633a-12b6-59d1-bc37-9ea2c1845cc9'}, {'abstract': 'The government can address the so-called fiscal cliff through more progressive spending, not higher tax rates, the author writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/setting-the-table-for-tax-negotiations/', 'snippet': 'The government can address the so-called fiscal cliff through more progressive spending, not higher tax rates, the author writes.', 'lead_parag