blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/clear-channel-bets-on-electronic-dance-music-signing-up-pete-tong/', 'snippet': 'The British D.J. and radio personality will anchor a new station on iHeartRadio, Clear Channel’s online brand. Also, streaming music keeps growing; a Sony digital executive resigns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Clear Channel Communications is turning to the electronic dance music craze to help build its online brand, iHeartRadio, with a new channel featuring Pete Tong, the British D.J. and radio personality who has been one of the genre’s biggest taste makers for two decades.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clear Channel Bets on Electronic Dance Music, Signing Up Pete Tong', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clear Channel Communications Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T17:37:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/141f468c-1b98-5136-95ce-a4e335a85b2f', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/141f468c-1b98-5136-95ce-a4e335a85b2f'}, {'abstract': 'Two days after his re-election, President Obama had made no public remarks outside his victory speech, and will have few forays into the public eye in the coming week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/us/politics/obamas-quiet-return-to-the-white-house.html', 'snippet': 'Two days after his re-election, President Obama had made no public remarks outside his victory speech, and will have few forays into the public eye in the coming week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — After an intense campaign during which Americans — at least those in swing states — could not walk by their televisions without being assaulted by an ad lauding or pillorying President Obama, the man of the moment has suddenly gone quiet.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/09obama/09obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/09/us/09obama/09obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/09obama/09obama-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/09obama/09obama-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/09obama/09obama-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/09/us/09obama/09obama-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marathon Over, a Muted Return to Washington', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marathon Over, A Muted Return To Washington', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T17:43:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/174254f8-0b18-55b2-b96c-591d33707b78', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/174254f8-0b18-55b2-b96c-591d33707b78'}, {'abstract': 'Sam Sifton, the national editor of The New York Times and the pioneer of Dining’s annual Thanksgiving Help Line, discussed Thanksgiving prep on the “Today” show this morning.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/talking-turkey-on-today/', 'snippet': 'Sam Sifton, the national editor of The New York Times and the pioneer of Dining’s annual Thanksgiving Help Line, discussed Thanksgiving prep on the “Today” show this morning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sam Sifton, the national editor of The New York Times and the pioneer of Dining’s annual Thanksgiving Help Line, appeared on “Today” this morning, talking about best practices for turkey, cranberry sauce and dressing. The video is above, and if you have follow-up questions, don’t fret: the Help Line will go live next week, with Times reporters and editors standing by to offer advice on your Thanksgiving dilemmas in the kitchen and beyond. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talking Turkey on ‘Today’', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sifton, Sam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T18:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14dd4a1f-89dd-5d68-8ba3-c7f4d626f7da', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14dd4a1f-89dd-5d68-8ba3-c7f4d626f7da'}, {'abstract': 'After years of political and legal threats that kept President Obama’s health care law in a state of uncertainty, his re-election all but assures it will survive. The next hurdle is making it work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/health/states-face-tight-health-care-deadlines.html', 'snippet': 'After years of political and legal threats that kept President Obama’s health care law in a state of uncertainty, his re-election all but assures it will survive. The next hurdle is making it work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After nearly three years of legal and political threats that kept President Obama’s health care law in a constant state of uncertainty, his re-election on Tuesday all but guarantees that the historic legislation will survive.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/jp-HEALTH-1/jp-HEALTH-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/09/us/jp-HEALTH-1/jp-HEALTH-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/jp-HEALTH-1/jp-HEALTH-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/jp-HEALTH-1/jp-HEALTH-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_na