ide outpouring of support for their refusal to consider tax increases as part of a deficit-reduction plan.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/who-has-a-mandate/', 'snippet': 'To hear some Republicans tell it, Election Day was a nationwide outpouring of support for their refusal to consider tax increases as part of a deficit-reduction plan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the White House and Congress settle back into their longstanding arguments about taxing and spending, the word “mandate” is in the air. The question, specifically, is whether the president has one or not. To hear some Republicans tell it, Election Day was a nationwide outpouring of support for their refusal to consider tax increases as part of a deficit-reduction plan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Has a Mandate?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cole, Tom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T18:38:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7eba000d-9d4f-5be5-990c-b9f5ad93898d', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7eba000d-9d4f-5be5-990c-b9f5ad93898d'}, {'abstract': 'A closer look at the idea that Hurricane Sandy will finally spur meaningful greenhouse policy.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/will-storms-wall-street-impact