trate almost exclusively on these works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American sculptor Alexander Calder (1898-1976) was blessed with several kinds of genius. He was brilliant at the hands-on part, able to think incisively in several materials. He was innately cosmopolitan, a natural stylist and a bit of a sponge, swift to absorb and make his own the best of both the past and the present. He was an entertainer who aimed to please without pandering, to reconcile modernism and popular art, with assists from folk and what was then called primitive art.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09CALDER_SPAN/09CALDER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09CALDER_SPAN/09CALDER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09CALDER_SPAN/09CALDER_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09CALDER_SPAN/09CALDER_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09CALDER_SPAN/09CALDER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09CALDER_SPAN/09CALDER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09CALDER_SPAN/09CALDER_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Relics of a Sculptor’s Bronze Age', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Relics of a Sculptor’s Bronze Age', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calder, Alexander', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calder Foundation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T21:04:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d0ac18c-9e36-545f-b345-e65d095cefd8', 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d0ac18c-9e36-545f-b345-e65d095cefd8'}, {'abstract': 'The investment in the private media company founded by Peter Chernin would make the Qatar firm one of its two largest financial backers.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/qatar-holdings-said-to-invest-100-million-in-chernin-group/', 'snippet': 'The investment in the private media company founded by Peter Chernin would make the Qatar firm one of its two largest financial backers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The Chernin Group, a private media company founded by a former News Corporation president, Peter Chernin, on Thursday continued to expand its financial support, this time with an equity investment from Qatar Holdings, the group said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Qatar Holdings Is Said to Invest $100 Million in Chernin Group', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chernin, Peter A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chernin Group LLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Providence Equity Partners Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Qatar Investment Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qatar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T21:05:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e115ce63-c35c-5527-97a0-5f52afcd31a5', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e115ce63-c35c-5527-97a0-5f52afcd31a5'}, {'abstract': 'With gas lines in New York City still stubbornly long and no relief for gas shortages in sight, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg imposed an odd-even gas rationing rule that goes into effect at 6 a.m. Friday. Officials in Long Island did the same; there, the rule goes into effect at 5 a.m.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/bloomberg-imposes-odd-even-gas-rationing/', 'snippet': 'With gas lines in New York City still stubbornly long and no relief for gas shortages in sight, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg imposed an odd-even gas rationing rule that goes into effect at 6 a.m. Friday. Officials in Long Island did the same; there,...', 'lead_paragraph': '10:23 p.m. | Updated  A revised version of this article is available here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': N