cob Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0b668aa-b9d7-51c3-a333-6fad98a19a9a', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0b668aa-b9d7-51c3-a333-6fad98a19a9a'}, {'abstract': 'NickMom, a late-night programming block on Nick Jr., speaks to two preoccupations in its intended audience, but little else.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/arts/television/nickmom-a-late-night-programming-block-on-nick-jr.html', 'snippet': 'NickMom, a late-night programming block on Nick Jr., speaks to two preoccupations in its intended audience, but little else.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A plea to all the women out there, especially the mothers: Resist the numbing allure of NickMom, a late-night programming block Nick Jr. began last month. Do not be seduced by its rehashing of mother-child dynamics from drab sitcoms or its relentless focus on penises. Do not allow yourselves to be captured by its I.Q.-lowering gravitational pull. You’ll end up like me. Like us. Like guys.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09NICKMOM_SPAN/09NICKMOM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09NICKMOM_SPAN/09NICKMOM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09NICKMOM_SPAN/09NICKMOM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/