say, the gnashing of teeth and rending of garments on the right comes as a surprise. We knew that they would be upset; but the extent to which they were really, truly unprepared for the obvious possibility that Obama would be reelected is remarkable. I suspect that it comes down to two things: self-definition in terms of always being the people with the power, and the right-wing information bubble, which left them completely unaware of information they didn’t want to hear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Socialism!', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T22:54:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59d0dfa1-78c2-57d3-a603-23f48b99b126', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59d0dfa1-78c2-57d3-a603-23f48b99b126'}, {'abstract': 'A selected, critical guide to comedy shows, festivals and improv in the New York area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/arts/comedy-listings-for-nov-9-15.html', 'snippet': 'A selected, critical guide to comedy shows, festivals and improv in the New York area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Comedy', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comedy Listings for Nov. 9-15', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T23:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': 