and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently. See more here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Security Bug Bounties and Better Translation', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T23:46:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebfbcc74-6dda-515c-900a-eb71183448d1', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebfbcc74-6dda-515c-900a-eb71183448d1'}, {'abstract': 'For many companies, Veterans Day campaigns have evolved from quotidian affairs — sales on cars or mattresses — into programs offering assistance in areas like finding jobs or buying homes.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/more-marketers-hail-veterans-and-try-to-help-them-too/', 'snippet': 'For many companies, Veterans Day campaigns have evolved from quotidian affairs — sales on cars or mattresses — into programs offering assistance in areas like finding jobs or buying homes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Madison Avenue is paying greater attention to those who are serving or have served in the armed forces. It was true last year, and the year before, and for the 2012 Veterans Day holiday the trend is continuing to gain strength.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Marketers Hail Veterans, and Try to Help Them, Too', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans Day (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-08T23:52:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0513643-b9c3-582c-a796-bf01193e0df6', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0513643-b9c3-582c-a796-bf01193e0df6'}, {'abstract': 'Jean-Marc Vallée’s “Café de Flore” follows two stories, one in contemporary Montreal and the other in Paris decades earlier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/movies/cafe-de-flore-by-jean-marc-vallee.html', 'snippet': 'Jean-Marc Vallée’s “Café de Flore” follows two stories, one in contemporary Montreal and the other in Paris decades earlier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ethereal art rock is the aural adhesive connecting two stories set four decades apart on different continents in the Canadian filmmaker Jean-Marc Vallée’s “Café de Flore.” This knotty contemplation of amour fou that transcends time and place is a movie for extreme romantics. ', 'print_section