urricane Sandy relief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first F12 Berlinetta to be sold in the United States will be auctioned by Ferrari, which will donate the proceeds to the American Red Cross to support the organization’s relief efforts after Hurricane Sandy, the automaker said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ferrari to Auction F12 Berlinetta for Hurricane Relief', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN RED CROSS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ferrari SpA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T00:38:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carla Baranauckas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baranauckas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/722a0926-9ebc-5ff3-8bb8-aced2cdaffb2', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/722a0926-9ebc-5ff3-8bb8-aced2cdaffb2'}, {'abstract': 'For one more dose of election night excitement, here are Nate Silver’s appearances on TimesCast, where he discussed results as they came in with The Times’s Megan Liberman.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/election-night-replay/', 'snippet': 'For one more dose of election night excitement, here are Nate Silver’s appearances on TimesCast, where he discussed results as they came in with The Times’s Megan Liberman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The excitement of election night is fading. Although ballots are still being counted, President Obama appears to have carried Florida, the last undecided state, and Republicans are confronting a challenging electoral map.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Election Night Replay', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Nate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T00:42:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micah Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c344d24-46dc-5a3f-9565-55cbbc35344c', 'word_count': 60, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c344d24-46dc-5a3f-9565-55cbbc35344c'}, {'abstract': 'Sears, which sold many Bionic Wrenches last holiday season, is selling a similar product this year — only now it is made in China instead of America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/business/popular-wrench-fights-a-chinese-rival.html', 'snippet': 'Sears, which sold many Bionic Wrenches last holiday season, is selling a similar product this year — only now it is made in China instead of America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Christmas, Sears had a brisk seller in the Bionic Wrench, an award-winning, patented tool with spiffy lime green accents. This holiday season, though, Sears has a special display for its own wrench, in the red and black colors of its house brand, Craftsman.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/business/WRENCH/WRENCH-jumbo-v2.