/giving/girl-scouts-refocus-message-on-leadership.html', 'snippet': 'The Girl Scouts, with corporate help, are focusing on educating girls in leadership after surveys showed they lacked confidence in their abilities to rise to the top.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHO hasn’t heard that girls can have whatever job they want — entrepreneur, chief executive, president of the United States?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Cookie Sales to Lessons in Leadership', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Cookie Sales to Lessons in Leadership', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Girl Scouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T01:10:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Giving', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Olson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de832c89-78ff-5204-99f0-1585aa10d265', 'word_count': 1191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de832c89-78ff-5204-99f0-1585aa10d265'}, {'abstract': 'Bohemia Ecological Preserve in Northern California was created on donated land — now owned by a nonprofit, LandPaths — and it is being maintained by volunteers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/giving/benefactors-create-and-maintain-a-private-park-in-california.html', 'snippet': 'Bohemia Ecological Preserve in Northern California was created on donated land — now owned by a nonprofit, LandPaths — and it is being maintained by volunteers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE waterfall that is the best-known feature of the Bohemia Ecological Preserve is currently nothing more than a picturesque spill of bone-dry rocks. The shaggy grasslands that carpet the preserve’s rolling terrain are a parched golden brown.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/giving/PARKS/PARKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/09/giving/PARKS/PARKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/giving/PARKS/PARKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/giving/PARKS/PARKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/giving/PARKS/PARKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/09/giving/PARKS/PARKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/giving/PARKS/PARKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Not a Public Park, but a ‘People-Powered’ One', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not a Public Park, but a ‘People-Powered’ One', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volunteers and Community Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T01:11:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Giving', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Beato', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beato', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3924d076-65de-5c37-9f12-1fe5af110b6a', 'word_count': 1215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3924d076-65de-5c37-9f12-1fe5af110b6a'}, {'abstract': 'The three vignettes that make up “In Another Country” have Isabelle Huppert’s character dealing with various situations as the only foreigner in an overcast South Korean beach town.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/movies/in-another-country-starring-isabelle-huppert.html', 'snippet': 'The three vignettes that make up “In Another Country” have Isabelle Huppert’s character dealing with various situations as the only foreigner in an overcast South Korean beach town.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like many other films by the sly and prolific South Korean director Hong Sang-soo, “In Another Country” is at once a comedy of manners and an oblique commentary on the power of cinema to expose and alter reality. Its three chapters, each a little under a half-hour long, are scenarios dreamed up by an aspiring young screenwriter (Jung Yumi) in the midst of some vague family trouble. The movies she writes, which we see enacted on the screen (with Ms. Jung as a helpful neighbor), are variations on some of Mr. Hong’s favorite themes: social awkwardness, sexual frustration and the selfishness of Korean men.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'cap