nitiative), legal (the Comic Book Legal Defense Fund) or serving a greater good (We Can Be Heroes).', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/business/COMICS/COMICS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/business/COMICS/COMICS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1318, 'width': 837, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/business/COMICS/COMICS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/09/business/COMICS/COMICS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/business/COMICS/COMICS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Comics World, Needy Have Heroes of Their Own', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Comics World, Needy Have Heroes Of Their Own', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cartoons and Cartoonists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T01:32:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Giving', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fefa8dcb-3358-5d0c-ab52-774005f0bc62', 'word_count': 1061, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fefa8dcb-3358-5d0c-ab52-774005f0bc62'}, {'abstract': 'Lenders are aggravating a storm-related bottleneck by requiring property reinspections in affected zones.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/realestate/mortgages-dealing-with-delayed-closings-after-hurricane-sandy.html', 'snippet': 'Lenders are aggravating a storm-related bottleneck by requiring property reinspections in affected zones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE extensive power failures that have paralyzed the region in the wake of Hurricane Sandy have understandably delayed closings in mortgage deals that had otherwise been buttoned up. But lenders are adding to the logistical bottleneck by requiring that properties in affected areas be reinspected for damage. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/realestate/11mort-graphic/11mort-graphic-articleLarge.png', 'height': 307, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/11/realestate/11mort-graphic/11mort-graphic-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 307}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/realestate/11mort-graphic/11mort-graphic-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/11/realestate/11mort-graphic/11mort-graphic-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dealing With Delayed Closings After Hurricane Sandy', 'kicker': 'Mortgages', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dealing With Delayed Closings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York Metropolitan Area', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T01:35:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Prevost', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prevost', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff1d421d-6d2f-583a-af81-534ae95720db', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff1d421d-6d2f-583a-af81-534ae95720db'}, {'abstract': 'In Lisa Albright’s turgid family drama, Bernadette Peters plays a faded Broadway diva with two daughters who starts life over in a rented, graffiti-scarred shack in Nashua, N.H.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/movies/coming-up-roses-starring-bernadette-peters.html', 'snippet': 'In Lisa Albright’s turgid family drama, Bernadette Peters plays a faded Broadway diva with two daughters who starts life over in a rented, graffiti-scarred shack in Nashua, N.H.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine, if you can, a character like Norma Desmond from “Sunset Boulevard” or Mama Rose from “Gypsy” putting down roots in an impoverished New England town. Then go back and try to figure out how such a thing could be possible. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09ROSES_SPAN/