/', 'snippet': 'In his second term, President Obama can demonstrate that “the choice between our safety and our ideals” is false.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Second Chance on Human Rights', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Second Chance on Human Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T01:50:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric L. Lewis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Lewis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef329cc0-ebdc-51c9-a99d-f4616a998ccf', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef329cc0-ebdc-51c9-a99d-f4616a998ccf'}, {'abstract': 'Female representation matters, but only when there’s parity with men.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/more-women-but-not-nearly-enough/', 'snippet': 'Female representation matters, but only when there’s parity with men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Congress that convenes in January will include a record number of women: 20 senators and at least 81 representatives. Female candidates broke other barriers on Tuesday. New Hampshire will be the first state to send an all-female delegation to Congress. A woman was elected to the South Carolina Senate, currently the only all-male state legislative chamber.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Women, but Not Nearly Enough', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Women, but Not Nearly Enough', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T01:52:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tali Mendelberg and Christopher F. Karpowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tali', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mendelberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Karpowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79be4290-0e20-5e71-ba0e-2efd6f1a1f63', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79be4290-0e20-5e71-ba0e-2efd6f1a1f63'}, {'abstract': 'Perhaps fearing that they would be giving too much power to unions, voters defeated a Constitutional amendment that would have guaranteed the right to collective bargaining.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/business/in-michigan-a-setback-for-unions.html', 'snippet': 'Perhaps fearing that they would be giving too much power to unions, voters defeated a Constitutional amendment that would have guaranteed the right to collective bargaining.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hoping to set a precedent for other states, Michigan’s labor unions spent months pushing a referendum to amend the state’s Constitution to prohibit the legislature from ever enacting a law that would curb the powers of public employee unions.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/business/Labor/Labor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/business/Labor/Labor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/business/Labor/Labor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/09/business/Labor/Labor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/business/Labor/Labor-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Michigan, a Setback for Unions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Michigan, A Setback For Unions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T01:53:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5031c05b-7691-5a75-abae-91f0d1dc37b9', 'word_count': 1040, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5031c05b-7691-5a75-abae-91f0d1dc37b9'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama should hang tough and hold his ground even at the cost of letting his opponents inflict damage on a still-shaky economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/opinion/krugman-lets-not-make-a-deal.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama should hang tough and hold his ground even at the cost of letting his opponents inflict damage on a still-shaky economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To say the obvious: Democrats won an amazing victory. Not only did they hold the White House despite a still-troubled economy, in a year when their Senate majority was supposed to be doomed, they actually added seats.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'