{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5920bb05-e52c-5350-945a-5559bd9a338e', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5920bb05-e52c-5350-945a-5559bd9a338e'}, {'abstract': 'The latest “Dangerous Liaisons” film iteration is a Chinese-language version that retains the story of pretty people behaving badly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/movies/dangerous-liaisons-directed-by-hur-jin-ho.html', 'snippet': 'The latest “Dangerous Liaisons” film iteration is a Chinese-language version that retains the story of pretty people behaving badly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The story and its players look different in the latest screen iteration of “Dangerous Liaisons,” but the venomous passions remain repellently, seductively familiar. Bankrolled by Chinese money and directed by a South Korean filmmaker, Jin-ho Hur, this Chinese-language version of the 18th-century French novel by Pierre Choderlos de Laclos opens in Shanghai in 1931, when the city was known as the Paris of the Orient. (Now it’s just the center of the world.) That year a fighting-trim Mao Zedong helped create the Chinese Soviet Republic, and Japan invaded the Chinese province of Manchuria, setting up a puppet government. The second Sino-Japanese war was six years away. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09DANGEROUS_SPAN/DANGEROUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09DANGEROUS_SPAN/DANGEROUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09DANGEROUS_SPAN/DANGEROUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09DANGEROUS_SPAN/DANGEROUS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 865, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09DANGEROUS_SPAN/DANGEROUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09DANGEROUS_SPAN/DANGEROUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/09DANGEROUS_SPAN/DANGEROUS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cunning Tale Retold in Another Language', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Cunning Tale Retold In Another Language', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Dangerous Liaisons (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhang Ziyi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hur, Jin-ho', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T01:55:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/979e9762-93ec-5b65-b32c-61f5a32e7501', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/979e9762-93ec-5b65-b32c-61f5a32e7501'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans might  rebuild by first listening to those who have come to this land with the very hopes conservatives should want to affirm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/opinion/brooks-the-party-of-work.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans might  rebuild by first listening to those who have come to this land with the very hopes conservatives should want to affirm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American colonies were first settled by Protestant dissenters. These were people who refused to submit to the established religious authorities. They sought personal relationships with God. They moved to the frontier when life got too confining. They created an American creed, built, as the sociologist Seymour Martin Lipset put it, around liberty, individualism, equal opportunity, populism and laissez-faire.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Party of Work', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Party Of Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asian-Americans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T01:55:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c73aa1a-266e-5e7e-aad6-c34bac333524', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c73aa1a-266e-5e7e-aad6-c34bac333524'}, {'abstract': 'More austerity may please the Germans, but it is an unnecessary tragedy for Greece and it won’t pay down its debt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/opinion/greece-drinks-the-hemlock.html', 'snippet': 'More austerity may please the Germans, but it is an unnecessary tragedy for Greece and it won’t pay down its debt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greece’s Parliament did what it had to do on Thursday. Despite some defections from the ruling centrist coalition, lawmakers narrowly approved a $23 billion package of new austerity measures, including further spending cuts to social services, pensions and public salaries, as well as tax increases demanded by Greece’s European lenders. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece Drinks the Hemlock', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece Drinks the Hemlock', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samaras, Antonis', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T01:58:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3363807d-ce2b-5c5d-9ce9-8963228d180f', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3363807d-ce2b-5c5d-9ce9-8963228d180f'}, {'abstract': 'Discredited, I hope.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/deficit-hawks-down-please/', 'snippet': 'Discredited, I hope.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One big question looking forward is whether Obama will once again turn to the Beltway-insider deficit hawks for alleged wisdom. Let’s hope not.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deficit Hawks Down — Please', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T02:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a479587d-5a5f-53d6-bf03-a3eff997261c', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a479587d-5a5f-53d6-bf03-a3eff997261c'}, {'abstract': 'Those who see nothing but decline, loss and failure in Tuesday’s results should take the long view.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/the-great-experiment/', 'snippet': 'Those who see nothing but decline, loss and failure in Tuesday’s results should take the long view.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anyone who still has a smidge of humanity left after our $6 billion electoral argument should consider the symbolism at the top of a ballot now headed for history’s vault. The incumbent’s father is from a race of people first brought to these shores in chains and sold like whiskey barrels at portside auctions. The challenger’s father was born in Mexico, to a family of sexual and religious outlaws who fled the United States. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Great Experiment', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mormons (Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T02:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1f4b6f8-45a3-5cf1-9959-c228b3a5a035', 'word_count': 931, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1f4b6f8-45a3-5cf1-9959-c228b3a5a035'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers said Thursday that they were trying to strike a deal that would avert a fiscal crisis next year when trillions of dollars in tax increases and automatic spending cuts begin to go into force.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/us/politics/congress-sees-rising-urgency-on-fiscal-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers said Thursday that they were trying to strike a deal that would avert a fiscal crisis next year when trillions of dollars in tax increases and automatic spending cuts begin to go into force.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Senior lawmakers said Thursday that they were moving quickly to take advantage of the postelection political atmosphere to try to strike an agreement that would avert a fiscal crisis early next year when trillions of dollars in tax increases and automatic spending cuts begin to go into force.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/us/politics/10obama_image1/10obama_image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', '