s to make it more reliable and inclusive?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/roomfordebate/2012/11/08/does-our-voting-system-need-to-be-fixed/', 'snippet': 'Is our voting system fine as it is, or are there ways to make it more reliable and inclusive?', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Better Way to Vote', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T02:04:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e5c3a92-f3c3-52c5-acd1-39a93b5f4aca', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e5c3a92-f3c3-52c5-acd1-39a93b5f4aca'}, {'abstract': 'Members of a conservation corps came from Washington and other states to help clear fallen trees and storm debris, but found themselves caring for people with special needs in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/nyregion/out-of-town-volunteers-help-run-a-brooklyn-shelter.html', 'snippet': 'Members of a conservation corps came from Washington and other states to help clear fallen trees and storm debris, but found themselves caring for people with special needs in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To keep up with Randy Ladowski, who was carrying about 30 pounds of just-washed clothes in a black trash bag, you had to practically run down South Elliott Place in Fort Greene, Brooklyn. Normally, Mr. Ladowski is in the woods in Washington State, part of a conservation corps working on trails and nature projects.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/nyregion/SUB-ABOUT/SUB-ABOUT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name