e a highway gunman responsible for 24 attacks, which made residents of the Detroit suburb nervously eye each passing car for weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/us/wixom-mich-shooting-suspect-is-arrested.html', 'snippet': 'Police in Wixom, Mich., arrested a suspect they believe to be a highway gunman responsible for 24 attacks, which made residents of the Detroit suburb nervously eye each passing car for weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIXOM, Mich. — He chose his targets with no discernible pattern, firing at Cadillacs, minivans and pickup trucks, at young drivers and older ones, at men on their way to work, fans heading for the ballpark and women picking up their children from school, his shooting attacks stretching through four counties along the Interstate 96 corridor.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/WIXOM-1/WIXOM-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/09/us/WIXOM-1/WIXOM-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/WIXOM-1/WIXOM-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/WIXOM-1/WIXOM-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/WIXOM-1/WIXOM-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/09/us/WIXOM-1/WIXOM-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Held in Shootings That Terrorized Michigan Town', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man Held in Shootings That Terrorized Michigan Town', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wixom (Mich)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T02:17:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Goode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9946a1ff-82c4-5555-8f4c-6ea1c76f9bc8', 'word_count': 1078, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9946a1ff-82c4-5555-8f4c-6ea1c76f9bc8'}, {'abstract': 'Congressional leaders have made clear that the debt ceiling will be part of talks over the so-called fiscal cliff, with many members unwilling to raise the ceiling without a broader deal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/business/debt-ceiling-complicates-fiscal-cliff.html', 'snippet': 'Congressional leaders have made clear that the debt ceiling will be part of talks over the so-called fiscal cliff, with many members unwilling to raise the ceiling without a broader deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Come January, should Congress fail to act, the United States will face more than immense tax increases and spending cuts. It will also run out of room to finance its large running deficits.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/business/09ceiling-pic/09ceiling-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/business/09ceiling-pic/09ceiling-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Debt Ceiling Complicates a Tax Shift', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Debt Ceiling Complicates A Tax Shift', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Ratings and Credit Rating Agencies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cantor, Eric', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T02:21:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e4b76b2-21b8-50d9-9b3f-1f51a11f3e86', 'word_count': 967, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e4b76b2-21b8-50d9-9b3f-1f51a11f3e86'}, {'abstract': 'Voters, in these hard times, agreed to pay more out of their pockets to shore up the state’s tattered public schools and universities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/opinion/californians-say-yes-to-raising-their-taxes.html', 'snippet': 'Voters, in these hard times, agreed to pay more out of their pockets to shore up the state’s tattered public schools and universities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of all the state election results across the nation, few can top the shocking good sense of California voters in approving temporary tax increases to raise $6 billion a year to shore up the state’s tattered public schools and university system. That’s right: There were voters in these hard times agreeing to be taxed despite the “no new taxes” mantra of simplistic conservative politicians. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Californians Say Yes to Taxes', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Californians Say Yes to Taxes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T02:21:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5906551b-633c-5ee8-b4ef-219c51c74678', 'word_count': 330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5906551b-633c-5ee8-b4ef-219c51c74678'}, {'abstract': 'Voters in Florida and Montana sent a message to politicians who might want to attack women’s reproductive rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/opinion/voters-speak-on-abortion-rights.html', 'snippet': 'Voters in Florida and Montana sent a message to politicians who might want to attack women’s reproductive rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Election Day, Florida voters wisely rejected a proposed amendment to the State Constitution that would prohibit abortion coverage as part of health plans for state workers and Medicaid recipients (such coverage is already severely limited by law). Going further, the amendment would have cut back on existing state privacy protections for women by barring the State Supreme Court from granting “broader rights to an abortion than those contained in the United States Constitution.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Voters Speak on Abortion Rights', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Voters Speak on Abortion Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T02:21:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c6bd360-03c0-5321-ab21-a0ace020d778', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c6bd360-03c0-5321-ab21-a0ace020d778'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees can’t do much this off-season until they hear back from the three free agents they’ve made qualifying offers to.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/waiting-to-hear-back/', 'snippet': 'The Yankees can’t do much this off-season until they hear back from the three free agents they’ve made qualifying offers to.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIAN WELLS, Calif. — Brian Cashman shrugged his shoulders several times during his press briefing, since he had few answers to most questions. For the moment, the Yankees’ off-season is on hold until the team finds out whether reliever Rafael Soriano, starting pitcher Hiroki Kuroda and outfielder Nick Swisher will accept their $13.3 million qualifying offers from the team.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Waiting to Hear Back', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cashman, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuroda, Hiroki', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soriano, Rafael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swisher, Nick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T02:25:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jorge Arangure Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jorge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arangure', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fecfdab-4923-56c7-b3de-cfbbc6d226c0', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fecfdab-4923-56c7-b3de-cfbbc6d226c0'}, {'abstract': 'New York City has not done enough to help public housing residents without power or heat or even food.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/opinion/where-hurricane-sandy-still-hurts.html', 'snippet': 'New York City has not done enough to help public housing residents without power or heat or even food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For all the efforts of federal, state and local officials to help people after Hurricane Sandy, unacceptable pockets of suffering remain. Ten days after the hurricane struck, thousands of people in New York City’s public housing are still without heat, water, electricity or food. Many people needed assistance after the storm, but the most vulnerable of the city’s inhabitants seem to be among the last in line to get it. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Hurricane Sandy Still Hurts', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Hurricane Sandy Still Hurts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing Authority (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Outages and Blackouts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public and Subsidized Housing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T02:26:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0a2b11e-5117-5bd5-b080-bd2c9cba8dbe', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0a2b11e-5117-5bd5-b080-bd2c9cba8dbe'}, {'abstract': 'On Day 54 of the National Hockey League lockout, both sides said negotiations would again be conducted Friday, signaling continued progress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/sports/hockey/nhl-labor-talks-continue-with-some-optimism.html', 'snippet': 'On Day 54 of the National Hockey League lockout, both sides said negotiations would again be conducted Friday, signaling continued progress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.H.L. Players’ Association heard responses from the league on a new proposal centering on two key issues Thursday, as bargaining intensified in a third straight day of talks at what had been an unspecified location in Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guarded Optimism as Talks Continue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guarded Optimism As Talks Continue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettman, Gary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fehr, Donald', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "National Hockey League Players' Assn", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T02:30:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c96d3f27-cdd1-56a0-a8b0-e58a2d1d2f29', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c96d3f27-cdd1-56a0-a8b0-e58a2d1d2f29'}, {'abstract': 'M.L.S. Commissioner Don Garber on Thursday night apologized to fans for Wednesday night’s postponement of the Red Bulls-D.C. United playoff match in Harrison, N.J.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/08/m-l-s-commissioner-apologizes-to-fans/', 'snippet': 'M.L.S. Commissioner Don Garber on Thursday night apologized to fans for Wednesday night’s postponement of the Red Bulls-D.C. United playoff match in Harrison, N.J.', 'lead_paragraph': 'M.L.S. Commissioner Don Garber on Thursday night apologized to fans for Wednesday night’s postponement of the Red Bulls-D.C. United playoff match in Harrison, N.J.:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'M.L.S. Commissioner Apologizes to Fans', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garber, Don', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T02:33:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac0b9170-4b20-5453-9d7a-9250eb872068', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac0b9170-4b20-5453-9d7a-9250eb872068'}, {'abstract': 'The national picture of Election Day was one of Democratic victories, but in Texas, Republicans are celebrating another statewide sweep and the state’s first Hispanic United States senator.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/us/gop-dominated-in-texas-on-election-day.html', 'snippet': 'The national picture of Election Day was one of Democratic victories, but in Texas, Republicans are celebrating another statewide sweep and the state’s first Hispanic United States senator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Democratic victories across the nation left Republican voters and activists with the political version of a hangover last week. In the alternate universe known as Texas, they are blaming the Champagne.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/09TTElection1/09TTElection1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/09/us/09TTElection1/09TTElection1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/09TTElection1/09TTElection1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/09TTElection1/09TTElection1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/09TTElection1/09TTElection1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/09/us/09TTElection1/09TTElection1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/us/09TTElection1/09TTElection1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Against the Grain, G.O.P. Dominated on Election Day', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Against the Grain, G.O.P. Dominated On Election Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, State Legislature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Ted', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T02:33:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Root', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Root', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae262193-362b-58e4-912f-291d1016c0a4', 'word_count': 1217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae262193-362b-58e4-912f-291d1016c0a4'}, {'abstract': 'The franchise received plenty of attention for moving to Brooklyn, but a subsequent 1-2 start, including a 30-point loss against the Heat, has not gone unnoticed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/sports/basketball/nets-caught-between-off-season-hype-and-a-slow-start.html', 'snippet': 'The franchise received plenty of attention for moving to Brooklyn, but a subsequent 1-2 start, including a 30-point loss against the Heat, has not gone unnoticed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ORLANDO, Fla. — In a digital era in which judgments are rendered in rapid-fire, 140-character blasts, there is no time for explanation, no room for nuance and little use for patience. So Deron Williams is pretty sure the world is ready to bury the Nets, even if he is willfully ignoring the chatter.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/sports/nets/nets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 784, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/sports/nets/nets-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1567, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/sports/nets/nets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/09/sports/nets/nets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/sports/nets/nets-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nets Are Caught Between Hype and a Slow Start', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nets Are Caught Between Hype and a Slow Start', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Deron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Joe (1981- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T02:35:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a46e5a6-f574-583c-91af-f1ba52356df7', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a46e5a6-f574-583c-91af-f1ba52356df7'}, {'abstract': 'A Palestinian boy was struck in the head by a bullet during clashes between Israeli forces and militants in southeast Gaza on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/world/middleeast/gaza-boy-killed-as-militants-clash-with-israeli-force.html', 'snippet': 'A Palestinian boy was struck in the head by a bullet during clashes between Israeli forces and militants in southeast Gaza on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Palestinian boy was killed during clashes between Israeli forces and militants in southeast Gaza on Thursday. A Gaza medical official said that the boy, Ahmed Abu Dagga, 11, was struck in the head by a bullet and died later in a hospital. Hamas, the Islamic militant group that controls Gaza, said he was killed by Israeli fire. Hamas said that its fighters had set off a bomb against an Israeli force that crossed the border into Gaza with tanks and bulldozers. Israeli tanks and helicopter gunships opened fire during the confrontation, residents said. The Israeli military said that soldiers engaged in routine activity along the border came under fire and fired back, and that it was checking on reports of the boy’s death. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gaza: Boy Killed as Militants Clash With Israeli Force', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gaza: Boy Killed as Militants Clash With Israeli Force', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T02:40:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fares Akram', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fares', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akram', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/caa0fc41-6543-5ea0-830b-016e75e8f008', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/caa0fc41-6543-5ea0-830b-016e75e8f008'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Gromoff, an Eastern Orthodox priest, lost one of his feet, and part of the other, to complications from diabetes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/nyregion/an-eastern-orthodox-priest-is-hobbled-by-diabetes.html', 'snippet': 'Peter Gromoff, an Eastern Orthodox priest, lost one of his feet, and part of the other, to complications from diabetes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty-four years ago, when he was told he had just six months to live, Peter Gromoff went, as he put it, “monastery shopping.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/nyregion/Y-SUB-NEEDIEST/Y-SUB-NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/09/nyregion/Y-SUB-NEEDIEST/Y-SUB-NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/nyregion/Y-SUB-NEEDIEST/Y-SUB-NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/nyregion/Y-SUB-NEEDIEST/Y-SUB-NEEDIEST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType'