 professors, many care deeply about what’s happening and have turned to humor to deal with their frustration at the gap between what they want to know and what the government wants them to know.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Thursday’s theatrical opening in Beijing of the 18th Communist Party Congress, the real action shifted today to behind-the-scenes meetings among kingmakers who will hammer out the deals that decide China’s new leadership. Traditionally, these meetings have taken place in private locations, including hotels like the Xiyuan and the Capital, where delegates are staying.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/blogs/09rdv-china-congress-show-people-shut-out/09rdv-china-congress-show-people-shut-out-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/blogs/09rdv-china-congress-show-people-shut-out/09rdv-china-congress-show-people-shut-out-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1496, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shut Out of Party Congress and Power Transfer, Chinese Citizens Turn to Humor', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T07:18:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', 