'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/business/8-TOOLKIT/8-TOOLKIT-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Respond: Password Hygiene and Headaches', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T11:39:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba81ed75-a9d2-57ac-a402-5edb1c1cbadd', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba81ed75-a9d2-57ac-a402-5edb1c1cbadd'}, {'abstract': 'There’s a big difference between protecting a concept for a new business and protecting a highly differentiated methodology.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/your-ideas-are-worthless-part-2/', 'snippet': 'There’s a big difference between protecting a concept for a new business and protecting a highly differentiated methodology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a recent post, I wrote about my belief that ideas had no value and that it wasn’t worth anyone’s time to protect a business idea. It’s a notion I have been talking about for some time, but it is a controversial concept that often provokes strong disagreement. That disagreement, I think, stems from a misunderstanding of what an idea really is — or at least what I deem an idea to be.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Ideas Are Worthless', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '',