': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tigers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKeon, Howard P', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Loretta', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Fund for Animal Welfare', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zanesville (Ohio)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T12:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nuwer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nuwer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5a20ed1-c791-5ec7-8cf2-2d8169d08157', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5a20ed1-c791-5ec7-8cf2-2d8169d08157'}, {'abstract': 'A multi-stage deal designed to give Diageo control.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/diageo-and-united-spirits-terms-of-the-deal/', 'snippet': 'A multi-stage deal designed to give Diageo control.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Diageo, the British spirits giant, and United Spirits, the Indian liquor company controlled by Vijay Mallya, announced a $2 billion deal Friday expected to give the British company just over half of the Indian company. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Diageo and United Spirits: Terms of the Deal', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T12:56:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0f0bd96-bafd-5c25-8c93-133aeed49201', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0f0bd96-bafd-5c25-8c93-133aeed49201'}, {'abstract': 'Taimoor Shah, a reporter and interpreter for The New York Times, recounts his experience reporting on the Panjwai Massacre.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/days-of-horror-and-grief-reporting-the-panjwai-massacre/', 'snippet': 'Taimoor Shah, a reporter and interpreter for The New York Times, recounts his experience reporting on the Panjwai Massacre.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Taimoor Shah has been a reporter and interpreter for The New York Times in Kabul and southern Afghanistan for more than 10 years, covering some of the most dangerous corners of the war. In March, he was one of the first to see the victims of an American soldier’s rampage through an Afghan village in the Panjwai district of Kandahar, where 16 civilians were killed. This week, the soldier accused in those killings, Staff Sgt. Robert Bales, began his journey through the military justice system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Days of Horror and Grief: Reporting the Panjwai Massacre', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bales, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Panjwai (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T13:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Taimoor Shah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Taimoor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32573af7-0bae-5f81-a572-dae4925a6abb', 'word_count': 1913, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32573af7-0bae-5f81-a572-dae4925a6abb'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/opinion-report-what-voters-want/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: What Voters Want', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T13:07:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d10e76e-0999-5364-a9bf-b81c08eacd5f', 'word_count': 66, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d10e76e-0999-5364-a9bf-b81c08eacd5f'}, {'abstract': 'As a symbol of Englishness, the Anglican Church is, on the face of it, as anachronistic as warm beer, London fogs and the stiff upper lip with Sunday attendance at its 16,000 parish churches falling to less than one million.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/archbishop-ranks-as-englands-top-non-royal-in-one-of-the-worlds-least-religious-countries/', 'snippet': 'As a symbol of Englishness, the Anglican Church is, on the face of it, as anachronistic as warm beer, London fogs and the stiff upper lip with Sunday attendance at its 16,000 parish churches falling to less than one million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — As Queen Elizabeth on Friday ended months of speculation by confirming Bishop Justin Welby, a 56-year-old former oil executive, will be the next head of the Church of England, her increasingly secular subjects might be forgiven for asking what all the fuss was about.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/blogs/rdv-welby/rdv-welby-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/blogs/rdv-welby/rdv-welby-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Archbishop Ranks as England’s Top Non-Royal, in One of the World’s Least Religious Countries', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANGLICAN CHURCHES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Church of England', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T13:12:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cc83242-3c3a-5cc1-beb5-bf7534881fe2', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cc83242-3c3a-5cc1-beb5-bf7534881fe2'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: A veteran of World War II got an unexpected response when he told a young woman about his Army stretch.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/thank-you-for-your-service/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A veteran of World War II got an unexpected response when he told a young woman about his Army stretch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thank You for Your Service', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T13:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Milton Kamen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Milton', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kamen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f7af2e1-635b-5d56-a626-7de6fa7df37d', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f7af2e1-635b-5d56-a626-7de6fa7df37d'}, {'abstract': 'With investors already worried about the fiscal cliff, there’s another wild card that will factor into the debates in Washington: the debt ceiling. | President Obama may be well positioned to push for changes in housing policy. | Kayak Software is being bought by Priceline.com for $1.8 billion in cash and stock. | Groupon is still having difficulty making money.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/more-unknowns-from-washington/', 'snippet': 'With investors already worried about the fiscal cliff, there’s another wild card that will factor into the debates in Washington: the debt ceiling. | President Obama may be well positioned to push for changes in housing policy. | Kayak Software is...', 'lead_paragraph': 'MORE UNKNOWNS FROM WASHINGTON \xa0|\xa0 With investors already worried about the possible tax increases and spending cuts known as the fiscal cliff, there’s another wild card that will factor into the debates in Washington in the coming months: the debt ceiling. A failure to raise the federal borrowing limit in a timely manner could send “financial markets into a panic,” writes Annie Lowrey in The New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Unknowns From Washington', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T13:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bddc40da-262c-51bf-aab3-b68da42dd51b', 'word_count': 1764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bddc40da-262c-51bf-aab3-b68da42dd51b'}, {'abstract': 'Apollo Global Management is the latest private equity firm to prove that the third quarter was a boon to the industry, swinging to a profit from the same time last year as the value of its holdings improved.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/apollo-turns-a-profit-as-portfolios-rise/', 'snippet': 'Apollo Global Management is the latest private equity firm to prove that the third quarter was a boon to the industry, swinging to a profit from the same time last year as the value of its holdings improved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apollo Global Management is the latest private equity firm to prove that the third quarter was a boon to the industry, swinging to a profit from the same time last year as the value of its holdings improved.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apollo Turns a Profit as Portfolios Rise', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Black, Leon D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apollo Global Management', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T13:55:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03041c08-b9a3-51bb-a233-82e70b27f816', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03041c08-b9a3-51bb-a233-82e70b27f816'}, {'abstract': 'The company’s subtle, sophisticated scented detergents now have candles to match.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/clean-burn-the-laundress-candles/', 'snippet': 'The company’s subtle, sophisticated scented detergents now have candles to match.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though the scent of Tide will always have its fans (and there’s a Facebook page to prove it), few laundry detergents can claim the sort of passionate olfactory following enjoyed by the Laundress New York. The company’s subtle, sophisticated scents — more fragrance counter than cleaning aisle — are so addictive that they’ve prompted numerous customers to ask the Laundress co-founders, Lindsey Boyd and Gwen Whiting, to make candles to match. At long last, that wish has come true: The pair has just introduced a trio of candles in their most popular fragrances. Lady has an herbal, citrusy bouquet with notes of amber, lavender and bergamot; No. 247 is a gentle blend of bergamot, thyme, lavender, musk and ylang ylang; and Cedar’s woodsy notes of cedar and sandalwood are balanced out by orange and rose. Like the cleaning products that inspired them, the candles are subtly designed (the artist Daniela Kamiliotis, who drew the Laundress’s signature “Lady,” created the packaging), effective and eco-friendly.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clean Burn | The Laundress Candles', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coin-Op Candles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T14:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy MacDonell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc5ca386-45d0-52a4-a237-ec1e8e5d5c34', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc5ca386-45d0-52a4-a237-ec1e8e5d5c34'}, {'abstract': 'United Spirits, whose biggest shareholder is the millionaire Vijay Mallya, will help London-based Diageo to meet its goal of getting half of its revenue from emerging markets years ahead of its 2015 target.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/diageo-buys-controlling-stake-in-indias-biggest-liquor-company/', 'snippet': 'United Spirits, whose biggest shareholder is the millionaire Vijay Mallya, will help London-based Diageo to meet its goal of getting half of its revenue from emerging markets years ahead of its 2015 target.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI – Diageo, the world’s largest spirits maker, said Friday that it would buy a controlling stake in India’s biggest liquor company for $2 billion, a move that gives it a bigger foothold in this fast-growing market.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Diageo Buys Control of India’s Biggest Liquor Company', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Diageo Buys Control of India’s Biggest Liquor Company', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mallya, Vijay', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Diageo PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kingfisher Airlines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Spirits', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T14:10:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e528f1e1-37e6-56c9-af79-1673945918d5', 'word_count': 923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e528f1e1-37e6-56c9-af79-1673945918d5'}, {'abstract': 'From an unfashionable corner of economically disheveled Spain, Zara has conquered the “fast fashion” market by learning a new way to understand shoppers all over the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/magazine/how-zara-grew-into-the-worlds-largest-fashion-retailer.html', 'snippet': 'From an unfashionable corner of economically disheveled Spain, Zara has conquered the “fast fashion” market by learning a new way to understand shoppers all over the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Galicia, on the Atlantic coast of northern Spain, is the homeland of Generalissimo Francisco Franco, but is otherwise famous for being a place people try to leave. For much of the 20th century, hundreds of thousands of gallegos, as they are called, emigrated to countries as far away as Argentina to escape Galicia’s rural poverty. Today, however, even as Spain teeters on the edge of economic catastrophe, the Galician city La Coruña has attracted notice as the hometown of Amancio Ortega Gaona, the world’s third-richest man — he displaced Warren Buffett this year on the Bloomberg billionaire index — and the founder of a wildly successful fashion company, Inditex, more commonly known by its oldest and biggest brand, Zara.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/magazine/11zara1/11zara1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/11/magazine/11zara1/11zara1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/magazine/11zara1/11zara1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 716, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/magazine/11zara1/11zara1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1049, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/magazine/11zara1/11zara1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/11/magazine/11zara1/11zara1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/magazine/11zara1/11zara1-thu