called “Pain and Gain,” declared that the actor was “awesome.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'He’s played a porn star who turns into a drug addict; a washed-up boxer who turns into a championship boxer; and, in his real life, a rapper and dancer who turns into an underwear model, actor and producer. So why shouldn’t Mark Wahlberg appear in a movie opposite alien robots who turn into vehicles and household appliances?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/transformers/transformers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/transformers/transformers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/transformers/transformers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/transformers/transformers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/transformers/transformers-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mark Wahlberg Will Talk to Robots in ‘Transformers 4’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mark Wahlberg Signs On For ‘Transformers 4’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bay, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaBeouf, Shia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wahlberg, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hasbro Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paramount Pictures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T15:29:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78ac286f-cb41-545a-9f4c-24c1855977bd', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78ac286f-cb41-545a-9f4c-24c1855977bd'}, {'abstract': 'You’re going around minding your business, then comes the letter saying: “Hey! You just turned 50.” As if you didn’t know.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/booming/how-aarp-learns-peoples-birthdays.html', 'snippet': 'You’re going around minding your business, then comes the letter saying: “Hey! You just turned 50.” As if you didn’t know.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may have been lucky enough not to get a draft notice during the Vietnam War, but this is one bullet you younger boomers are almost certainly not going to dodge: the membership invitation that arrives from AARP, seemingly at the stroke of midnight on your 50th birthday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/booming/09question-booming-aarp/09question-booming-aarp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 796, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/booming/09question-booming-aarp/09question-booming-aarp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1593, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'supe