e': '2012-11-09T16:03:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d50ec29f-4d4e-52cb-a55c-05aff700c96e', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d50ec29f-4d4e-52cb-a55c-05aff700c96e'}, {'abstract': 'What’s on view this week in art museums around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/this-week-in-the-global-arts-guide-2/', 'snippet': 'What’s on view this week in art museums around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The juxtaposition of more than 100 photographs with portraits, interiors and urban scenes in “Gustave Caillebotte” at the Schirn Kunsthalle in Frankfurt illustrates how Caillebotte (1848-94) pioneered a quasi-photographic way of seeing and depicting. Hardly known in Germany, according to the organizers of the show, the Impressionist painter was a strong financial supporter of other Impressionists — Renoir and Monet — paying for their studios and acquiring their works. An anecdote: Ill-disposed critics talked about the stench coming from the workers’ sweat when ‘‘The Floor Scrapers, 1875’’ was first shown at the second Impressionist show. The exhibition continues through Jan. 20.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/9rdv-artguidec/9rdv-artguidec-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 312, 'width': 450, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/9rdv-artguidec/9rdv-artguidec-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 312, 'width': 450, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week in the Global Arts Guide', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caillebotte, Gustave', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Frankfurt (Germany)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T16:08:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Hopkins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hopkins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5380c8e-02f4-5928-aab1-f4f68265a10f', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5380c8e-02f4-5928-aab1-f4f68265a10f'}, {'abstract': 'As a reproductive health bill advances in the Philippines, it is peak baby-delivery season, with women and their newborns are sleeping two to a bed at one Manila hospital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/world/asia/10iht-manila10.html', 'snippet': 'As a reproductive health bill advances in the Philippines, it is peak baby-delivery season, with women and their newborns are sleeping two to a bed at one Manila hospital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANILA — In the main ward at Dr. Jose Fabella Memorial Hospital, 171 women and nearly as many newborns share fewer than 100 beds. Dozens more expectant mothers line the street outside, some sleeping on the sidewalk while waiting to get in.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/world/10iht-manila-babies/10iht-manila-babies-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'wi