-81190b48864f'}, {'abstract': 'The N.H.L. and the players union met in New York for a fourth straight day as the talks between the two sides intensified on Day 55 of the lockout.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/sports/hockey/union-says-wide-gap-remains-as-latest-nhl-talks-continue.html', 'snippet': 'The N.H.L. and the players union met in New York for a fourth straight day as the talks between the two sides intensified on Day 55 of the lockout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A leaked internal memorandum from the players union may have caused some damage to the labor negotiations between the N.H.L. and the union Friday.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Leaked Memo Could Complicate the N.H.L. Labor Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Leaked Memo Could Complicate the N.H.L. Labor Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fehr, Donald', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T18:24:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3177431d-8c8e-5499-913c-af711450b9db', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3177431d-8c8e-5499-913c-af711450b9db'}, {'abstract': 'If Griffith Park is to Los Angeles what Central Park is to New York, then the Trails Cafe might be its bare-bones Tavern on the Green.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/edible-selby-happy-trails/', 'snippet': 'If Griffith Park is to Los Angeles what Central Park is to New York, then the Trails Cafe might be its bare-bones Tavern on the Green.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Griffith Park is to Los Angeles what Central Park is to New York, as some Angelenos are wont to say, then the Trails Cafe might be its bare-bones Tavern on the Green. Across the street from one of the park’s most popular trails, which leads up to the Griffith Observatory, the cafe is the pit stop of choice for visitors, most of whom stop in to refuel post-hike. Its owners, Jenny Park and Mickey Petralia, serve Stumptown coffee, savory and sweet pies, avocado sandwiches, chili, scones, cookies and quiches, as well as their ‘‘Snakedog,’’ a pastry-wrapped hot dog. ‘‘I like a rustic, homemade style as opposed to fine-dining type of food,’’ says Park, who is also the pastry chef. The fare fits the surroundings, a rugged network of trails that vein the Santa Monica mountains above Los Feliz. ‘‘People come to escape,’’ she says. ‘‘It’s an oasis away from the main city. And one of the only places in L.A. that doesn’t have parking meters.’’ Go to the interactive slide show >>', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Edible Selby | Happy Trails', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Edible Selby: Happy Trails', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T18:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Todd Selby and Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Todd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Selby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title