ht ratings are looking up thanks to the addition of “Malibu Country” and, more important, the growing success of its fourth-season reality show “Shark Tank.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When ABC announced last spring that its fall schedule would include a Friday-night lineup pairing Reba McEntire’s new show, “Malibu Country,” with Tim Allen’s returning “Last Man Standing,” the plan evoked memories of the “TGIF” family comedy block that drew in a large number of viewers young and old for much of the 1990s. The only problem was that ABC had not been able to replicate that success since.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ABC’s Friday-Night Bet Pays Off', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLEN, TIM', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuban, Mark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McEntire, Reba', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T19:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62d297fc-acd5-5969-907a-35a3fa9fa61b', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62d297fc-acd5-5969-907a-35a3fa9fa61b'}, {'abstract': 'A White House official confirmed the “social” evening, on Friday, after reports surfaced in Boston.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/massachusetts-governor-to-dine-at-the-white-house-friday/', 'snippet': 'A White House official confirmed the “social” evening, on Friday, after reports surfaced in Boston.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The auditions for President Obama’s second-term cabinet are under way, with Gov. Deval Patrick of Massachusetts and his wife heading to Washington on Friday for dinner with Mr. Obama and his wife, Michelle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts Governor to Dine at the White House Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patrick, Deval L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T19:35:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c9e4330-eec9-5ddc-8934-521965cd37c7', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c9e4330-eec9-5ddc-8934-521965cd37c7'}, {'abstract': 'He did not reveal himself as a Kenyan socialist eager to pillage the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/a-first-look-at-second-term-obama/', 'snippet': 'He did not reveal himself as a Kenyan socialist eager to pillage the economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We got our first look today at Second Term Obama and – shock – he did not reveal himself as a Kenyan socialist eager to pillage the economy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A First Look at Second Term Obama', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T19:39:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7186f11-5ea7-524d-94b3-bf0bf44e7ab9', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7186f11-5ea7-524d-94b3-bf0bf44e7ab9'}, {'abstract': 'The politically connected state sector may threaten China’s economy and political stability, but it is unclear whether leaders will take action.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/world/asia/state-enterprises-pose-test-for-chinas-new-leaders.html', 'snippet': 'The politically connected state sector may threaten China’s economy and political stability, but it is unclear whether leaders will take action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Wealthy Chinese carry up to three smartphones, one for each of the state-owned service providers, in the hope that at least one will have enough network capacity to provide reliable e-mail service. Most Chinese factories have heavily polluting diesel generators to cope with blackouts of up to three days a week, because state-owned electricity companies have not added capacity fast enough to meet demand.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/world/asia/10china_image/10china_image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/world/asia/10china_image/10china_image-superJumbo.jpg', '