hat you view these images in full-screen mode.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Life on the Track and in the Stretch', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Horseman Builds Career on His Terms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grandparents', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T20:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor J. Blue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Blue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69f53ac0-9d9f-5c14-8503-779cee02f3d8', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69f53ac0-9d9f-5c14-8503-779cee02f3d8'}, {'abstract': '“The Vandal,” by the actor Hamish Linklater, will open in January at the Flea Theater', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/holly-hunter-to-star-in-new-play-off-broadway/', 'snippet': '“The Vandal,” by the actor Hamish Linklater, will open in January at the Flea Theater', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lights are definitely back on at the Flea Theater in TriBeCa, which like many downtown theaters struggled in the wake of Hurrican Sandy. The Flea announced on Friday that Holly Hunter, an Oscar winner for “The Piano,” will star in the premiere of “The Vandal,” in January.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holly Hunter To Star in New Play Off Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Holly Hunter to Star In Off Broadway Play', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradshaw, Thomas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freed, Amy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunter, Holly', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iskandar, Ed Sylvanus', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Linklater, Hamish', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simpson, Jim', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Flea Theater', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'TriBeCa (NYC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T20:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da334c9b-daaf-5a82-8d00-82cae31cc2c0', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da334c9b-daaf-5a82-8d00-82cae31cc2c0'}, {'abstract': 'A Norwegian artist throws fashion into his mad mix of a show at Luxembourg & Dayan.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/graphic-material-a-proenza-schoulerbjarne-melgaard-mash-up/', 'snippet': 'A Norwegian artist throws fashion into his mad mix of a show at Luxembourg & Dayan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Norwegian artist Bjarne Melgaard considers himself first and foremost as a painter and a writer, though his elaborate installations, which can also involve drawings, photographs, films, furniture, dolls and all manner of ready-made objects, are far from solitary productions. Melgaard brings in a large cast of collaborators and gives them very little direction, an approach, he says, that allows room for surprise. “A New Novel by Bjarne Melgaard,” on view at Luxembourg & Dayan, 64 East 77th Street, through Dec. 22, even has some fashion thrown into the mad, mad mix, thanks to a collaboration with Jack McCollough and Lazaro Hernandez of Proenza Schouler, who designed an evening dress inspired by Melgaard’s paintings, in versions to fit a 50-inch doll and also a 6-foot doll, as well as three men’s ensembles in Melgaard’s size. Proenza Schouler fans might also notice material from the designers’ past collections upholstered onto Melgaard’s hulking, off-kilter furniture and patchworked into a rug on the gallery’s ground floor. “This kind of collaboration is a lot of fun and gives us freedom to play a little outside of our usual system,” said McCollough and Hernandez in an e-mail. “Bjarne is an incredible artist and we are very much honored both to know him and to be a part of his wild ride.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Material | A  Proenza Schouler/Bjarne Melgaard Mash Up', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Lazaro', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCollough, Jack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Melgaard, Bjarne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Luxembourg & Dayan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Proenza Schouler', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T20:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9167e3a6-4210-5e33-9f12-65aa3dd22199', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9167e3a6-4210-5e33-9f12-65aa3dd22199'}, {'abstract': 'Martha Stewart Living Omnimedia is struggling, and the lavish compensation for its founder, Martha Stewart, and her sway over the board may be part of the company’s problem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/business/at-martha-stewart-living-martha-may-be-the-problem.html', 'snippet': 'Martha Stewart Living Omnimedia is struggling, and the lavish compensation for its founder, Martha Stewart, and her sway over the board may be part of the company’s problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among America’s corporate leaders, there are surely few whose interests are more closely aligned with their shareholders’ than the homemaking icon Martha Stewart. She owns 26 million shares and controls nearly 90 percent of the voting rights of Martha Stewart Living Omnimedia. She’s the company’s nonexecutive chairwoman and serves on the board. Martha Stewart, the company, is inseparable from Martha Stewart, the person.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/business/10stewart-pic/10stewart-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/10/business/10stewart-pic/10stewart-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/business/10stewart-pic/10stewart-pic-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/business/10stewart-pic/10stewart-pic-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 