ail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/09/magazine/09-rocket-3/09-rocket-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/magazine/09-rocket-3/09-rocket-3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fathers and Sons and Rocket Ships', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sahre, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T20:46:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arem Duplessis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Duplessis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd13823c-0c70-5264-86ed-b9f254ca0654', 'word_count': 719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd13823c-0c70-5264-86ed-b9f254ca0654'}, {'abstract': 'A bleak report, in the form of a law firm associate’s departure memo, on the state of the upper middle class work-parent juggle.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/an-overwhelmed-mothers-departure-memo/', 'snippet': 'A bleak report, in the form of a law firm associate’s departure memo, on the state of the upper middle class work-parent juggle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The “departure memo” is a fixture at many large employers, and nowhere more so than at big law firms. Departures, particularly of young associates, are built into the business model. Not everyone is supposed to stay, and many never planned to stay, so leaving is often celebrated. Many of the “Departure Memos of the Day” published on Above the Law fall into that category. Excitement at the next opportunity, and a little bit of glee at leaving, is completely acceptable, as is a little thumbing of the nose at the firm. Creativity isn’t unusual.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Overwhelmed Mother’s Departure Memo', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clifford Chance', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T20:50:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f379c50b-3aee-5ea8-a943-d81ecffd3dca', 'word_count': 1415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f379c50b-3aee-5ea8-a943-d81ecffd3dca'}, {'abstract': 'We’ve asked select performers for the New York Comedy Festival to share their best clean joke. Vote for your favorite.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/11/09/arts/nyt-comedy-challenge-2012.html', 'snippet': 'We’ve asked select performers for the New York Comedy Festival to share their best clean joke. Vote for your favorite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’ve asked select performers for the New York Comedy Festival to share their best clean joke. Vote for your favorite.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [