Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/37b44e0b-7435-5939-94f2-830fc51cc44b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/37b44e0b-7435-5939-94f2-830fc51cc44b'}, {'abstract': '“Kingdom of the Snakes” enters the hardcover and paperback lists this week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/graphic-books-best-sellers-lego-toys-in-book-form/', 'snippet': '“Kingdom of the Snakes” enters the hardcover and paperback lists this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Comic books inspired by toys, and vice versa, have a rich history. “Secret Wars,” from Marvel Comics, teamed up a legion of heroes and villains in the deepest regions of space to meet and confront the Beyonder. Among the results: a black costume for Spider-Man and a series of action figures. DC’s “Super Powers,” which had its heroes and villains involved with mega-threat Darkseid, had similar results.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/books/09graphic-books/09graphic-books-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 300, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/books/09graphic-books/09graphic-books-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 300, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/books/09graphic-books/09graphic-books-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/09/books/09graphic-books/09graphic-books-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/books/09graphic-books/09graphic-books-thumbL