mage', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/science/recipehealthkugel/recipehealthkugel-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/science/recipehealthkugel/recipehealthkugel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/06/science/recipehealthkugel/recipehealthkugel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/06/science/recipehealthkugel/recipehealthkugel-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Kugel Challenge', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quinoa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T20:58:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c16de393-e8d8-5970-8b0d-1f4e3a9ebddb', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c16de393-e8d8-5970-8b0d-1f4e3a9ebddb'}, {'abstract': 'An analysis of President Obama’s tough choices on housing. | On Wall Street, its time to mend fences with the president. | Andrew Ross Sorkin said that the election won’t solve all puzzles. | A big bets soured, imperiling a small firm. | A deal maker for Morgan Stanley was eased out. | HSBC may face charges in a laundering inquiry.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/week-in-review-on-wall-street-a-new-tone-with-old-tactics/', 'snippet': 'An analysis of President Obama’s tough choices on housing. | On Wall Street, its time to mend fences with the president. | Andrew Ross Sorkin said that the election won’t solve all puzzles. | A big bets soured, imperiling a small firm. | A deal ma...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A look back on our reporting of the past week’s highs and lows in finance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week in Review: On Wall Street, a New Tone With Old Tactics', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T21:03:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Owles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Owles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68eede50-f9f4-55e7-9925-b2a081746c72', 'word_count': 1047, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68eede50-f9f4-55e7-9925-b2a081746c72'}, {'abstract': 'Over the last year, household formation has been picking up.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/movin-out/', 'snippet': 'Over the last year, household formation has been picking up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost exactly a year ago I wrote an article about how tortoise-slow growth in household formation was hurting the economy. Unemployed new high school and college graduates were staying with their parents rather than moving into homes of their own, thereby depriving the economy of all the spending and hiring that goes along with setting up new digs. Under normal circumstances, each time a household is formed it adds about $145,000 to output that year as the spending ripples through the economy, according to an estimate last year from Mark Zandi, chief economist at Moody’s Analytics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Movin’ Out', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T21:09:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/246ae9e4-d984-5de5-a5ea-958141b74370', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/246ae9e4-d984-5de5-a5ea-958141b74370'}, {'abstract': 'The last of the sought-after trio of penthouse sponsor units has sold at One Thirty West 12, the luxury condominium conversion at a former residence for nurses on the St. Vincent’s Hospital campus,', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/big-ticket-sold-for-8442899/', 'snippet': 'The last of the sought-after trio of penthouse sponsor units has sold at One Thirty West 12, the luxury condominium conversion at a former residence for nurses on the St. Vincent’s Hospital campus,', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last of the sought-after trio of penthouse sponsor units at One Thirty West 12, the wildly popular (and sold-out) luxury condominium conversion at a former residence for nurses on the St. Vincent’s Hospital campus, sold for $8,442,899, the most