rd_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afb026ab-6a17-541b-969b-dc69b3c305c2'}, {'abstract': 'Introducing the second annual New York Times Comedy Challenge.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/exercise-your-vote-again-this-time-in-the-service-of-comedy/', 'snippet': 'Introducing the second annual New York Times Comedy Challenge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Did you know it was New York Comedy Week? No parking rules are suspended, but we’re celebrating anyway — with the second annual New York Times Comedy Challenge. We asked six rising comedians to tell us their best, but cleanest joke. (This is a family newspaper’s Web site, after all.) Now it’s your turn to decide who killed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exercise Your Vote Again, This Time in the Service of Comedy', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Che, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaffigan, Jim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T21:10:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ece40d7b-2c37-5515-84ae-fbcf41890170', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ece40d7b-2c37-5515-84ae-fbcf41890170'}, {'abstract': 'In “Un Ballo in Maschera,” elements of the intensely emotional are juxtaposed with strands of lighter, wryly comic scenes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/arts/music/un-ballo-in-maschera-at-metropolitan-opera.html', 'snippet': 'In “Un Ballo in Maschera,” elements of the intensely emotional are juxtaposed with strands of lighter, wryly comic scenes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The usual reason for a director to update the setting of a serious opera is to bring out the grim, contemporary darkness of the story. The most interesting aspect of David Alden’s disappointing, metaphor-laden new production of Verdi’s “Ballo in Maschera,” at the Metropolitan Opera, which opened on Thursday night, is that he uses an early-20th-century setting and film noir imagery to emphasize not just the work’s darkness but also its strangeness.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/arts/jp-ballo/jp-ballo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/arts/jp-ballo/jp-ballo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1465, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/arts/jp-ballo/jp-ballo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/10/arts/jp-ballo/jp-ballo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/arts/jp-ballo/jp-ballo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Icarus Haunts a Verdi Work Cloaked in Noir', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Icarus Haunts A Verdi Work Cloaked in Noir',