16c'}, {'abstract': 'Oklahoma City has embraced the Thunder to such an extent that even a countercultural icon like they psychedelic rocker Wayne Coyne of the Flaming Lips feels obligated to become a fan.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/this-sunday-oklahoma-city-is-big-league/', 'snippet': 'Oklahoma City has embraced the Thunder to such an extent that even a countercultural icon like they psychedelic rocker Wayne Coyne of the Flaming Lips feels obligated to become a fan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A semi-embarrassing curiosity of mine is obscure professional sports leagues — stuff like arena football, roller hockey, team tennis — and one of the observable phenomenon of these leagues is that when they start pulling their teams out of Chicago and Houston and putting them in places like Tacoma, Rochester and Oklahoma City, it’s usually a sign of their impending doom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/magazine/09-okc-thunder-wayne-coyne/09-okc-thunder-wayne-coyne-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/magazine/09-okc-thunder-wayne-coyne/09-okc-thunder-wayne-coyne-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1289, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/magazine/09-okc-thunder-wayne-coyne/09-okc-thunder-wayne-coyne-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/09/magazine/09-okc-thunder-wayne-coyne/09-okc-thunder-wayne-coyne-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'capt