'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been in several conversations over the past few days with generally reasonable people who are still worried that markets might turn on U.S. bonds any day now. I don’t think they’re right; but even if they are, I’m not clear what they believe would happen next. For the fact is that it’s much harder than most people seem to imagine to tell a Greece-type story about a country with its own currency and a floating exchange rate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Simple Analytics of Invisible Bond Vigilantes (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-09T23:59:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8508d97f-595f-519a-98e7-1ca332fe6ca2', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8508d97f-595f-519a-98e7-1ca332fe6ca2'}, {'abstract': 'The Nature Conservancy on Long Island responds to an Op-Ed article.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/opinion/natures-protective-ways.html', 'snippet': 'The Nature Conservancy on Long Island responds to an Op-Ed article.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nature’s Protective Ways', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nature’s Protective Ways', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wetlands', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subjec