/article/46e6460c-f103-5d19-abed-d635f575c190', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46e6460c-f103-5d19-abed-d635f575c190'}, {'abstract': 'Best wishes, and thanks.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/09/friday-night-music-the-end-of-the-civil-wars/', 'snippet': 'Best wishes, and thanks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fans of The Civil Wars – myself included – have received a terrible shock: the duo has cancelled its tour, and posted a statement about “irreconcilable differences”. Just last month, as you can see from the performance below, they seemed to take just as much joy as ever in making music. So you have to wonder what happened; but then, you never really know what anyone’s life is like from the inside.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: The End of The Civil Wars?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T00:02:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf62a44a-67ef-5553-b607-9fa606f07068', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf62a44a-67ef-5553-b607-9fa606f07068'}, {'abstract': 'At Republic, a boisterous gastropub in Bloomfield, Conn., what unifies the menu’s wild eclecticism is the chef’s decision to take the path of highest calories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/nyregion/a-review-of-republic-in-bloomfield.html', 'snippet': 'At Republic, a boisterous gastropub in Bloomfield, Conn., what unifies the menu’s wild eclecticism is the chef’s decision to take the path of highest calories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I first encountered a wallet-busting truffles-and-foie-gras Kobe burger in Las Vegas, at the burger bar run by Hubert Keller, of Fleur de Lys fame. It used to be that what was eaten in Vegas stayed in Vegas, but no more. That same deluxe burger, priced at $49, anchors the menu at Republic, a boisterous new Bloomfield gastropub whose chef, Steven Wolf, once worked for Mr. Keller. Like Vegas itself, this restaurant serves up good fun that’s bad for you. Salt, fat or sweet: pick your pleasure, select your sin.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/nyregion/11DINCECT1/11DINCECT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/nyregion/11DINCECT1/11DINCECT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2039, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/nyregion/11DINCECT1/11DINCECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/11/nyregion/11DINCECT1/11DINCECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/nyregion/11DINCECT1/11DINCECT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Diverse Menu Unified by Calories', 'kicker': 'Connecticut Dining | Bloomfield', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Diverse Menu Unified by Calories', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republic (Bloomfie