ons, Harold C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Precision Castparts Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Titanium Metals Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T01:04:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f6b0d34-db1f-5c33-920a-c1f3959204e7', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f6b0d34-db1f-5c33-920a-c1f3959204e7'}, {'abstract': 'Gilles Vaillancourt, the mayor of Laval, Quebec, for 23 years, resigned Friday, becoming the second municipal leader in the province to quit this week amid accusations of corruption.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/world/americas/canada-another-mayor-resigns.html', 'snippet': 'Gilles Vaillancourt, the mayor of Laval, Quebec, for 23 years, resigned Friday, becoming the second municipal leader in the province to quit this week amid accusations of corruption.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Gilles Vaillancourt, the mayor of Laval, Quebec, for 23 years, resigned Friday, becoming the second municipal leader in the province to quit this week amid accusations of corruption. On Monday, Gérald Tremblay resigned as Montreal’s mayor after a sweeping inquiry into corruption indicated that he had turned a blind eye to widespread graft in his city. He denied any wrongdoing. The inquiry, which is examining corruption involving municipal officials, contractors and organized crime, has yet to focus on Laval, the province’s third largest city. But last month, a special anticorruption police squad raided Mr. Vaillancourt’s two homes and his office and later seized the contents of several safe deposit boxes. On Friday, Mr. Vaillancourt said that the allegations against him were “without proof.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Another Mayor Resigns', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Another Mayor Resigns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Quebec Province (Canada)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T01:05:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/91085dfd-3ee8-5a2c-99ff-0d960836eb8f', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91085dfd-3ee8-5a2c-99ff-0d960836eb8f'}, {'abstract': 'A small group of victors in House and Senate races this week speak fluidly and abstractly about religion, when they talk about it at all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/us/politics/politicians-who-speak-of-religion-in-unaccustomed-ways.html', 'snippet': 'A small group of victors in House and Senate races this week speak fluidly and abstractly about religion, when they talk about it at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yes, a victory for Mitt Romney on Tuesday would have been the ultimate sign that Americans accept Mormons — that a tradition until recently considered a cult throughout the evangelical world, unable to shake its association with long-discarded polygamous ways, has come to seem pretty normal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Politicians Who Reject Labels Based on Religion', 'kicker': 'Beliefs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Politicians Who Reject Labels Based on Religion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buddhism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mormons (Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T01:09:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Oppenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oppenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d22948b0-8a03-5909-9dc2-8ca0aa4f35b7', 'word_count': 907, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d22948b0-8a03-5909-9dc2-8ca0aa4f35b7'}, {'abstract': 'A study commissioned by the C.I.A. and other agencies says that the acceleration of climate change will place unparalleled strains on the American military and intelligence agencies in coming years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/science/earth/climate-change-report-outlines-perils-for-us-military.html', 'snippet': 'A study commissioned by the C.I.A. and other agencies says that the acceleration of climate change will place unparalleled strains on the American military and intelligence agencies in coming years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Climate change is accelerating, and it will place unparalleled strains on American military and intelligence agencies in coming years by causing ever more disruptive events around the globe, the nation’s top scientific research group said in a report issued Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Climate Change Report Outlines Perils for U.S. Military', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Report Outlines Climate Change Perils', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States National Research Council', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T01:09:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58753492-06ec-5e8f-9739-2e8cff3c075c', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58753492-06ec-5e8f-9739-2e8cff3c075c'}, {'abstract': 'The Bears’ defense, which prompted preseason questions because of the ages of its marquee players, has been terrorizing offenses, piling up turnovers and scoring touchdowns at a rate a modest offense might find impressive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/sports/football/bears-are-scoring-at-will-and-thats-just-the-defense.html', 'snippet': 'The Bears’ defense, which prompted preseason questions because of the ages of its marquee players, has been terrorizing offenses, piling up turnovers and scoring touchdowns at a rate a modest offense might find impressive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAKE FOREST, Ill. — As the Chicago Bears’ defense terrorizes offenses around the N.F.L., piling up turnovers and scoring touchdowns at a rate a modest offense might find impressive, a mantra has emerged at Halas Hall, the team’s practice site. When players and coaches were asked this week who was responsible for what has been a record-setting season for the unit, the answer was always the same: “The star of our defense is the defense.” ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/y-bears/y-bears-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/y-bears/y-bears-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/y-bears/y-bears-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/y-bears/y-bears-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1415, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/y-bears/y-bears-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/y-bears/y-bears-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/y-bears/y-bears-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bears Are Scoring at Will, and That’s Just the Defense', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bears Are Scoring at Will, and That’s Just the Defense', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bears', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T01:11:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de3b295b-2ae2-5761-9445-44a675ae9a1f', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de3b295b-2ae2-5761-9445-44a675ae9a1f'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate on Thursday voted to designate March 19 as a national day of remembrance for the French and Algerian victims of the Algerian war of independence from 1954 to 1962.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/world/europe/france-a-day-for-a-wars-victims.html', 'snippet': 'The Senate on Thursday voted to designate March 19 as a national day of remembrance for the French and Algerian victims of the Algerian war of independence from 1954 to 1962.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Senate on Thursday voted to designate March 19 as a national day of remembrance for the French and Algerian victims of the Algerian war of independence from 1954 to 1962. The measure was originally adopted in 2002 by the lower house of Parliament before being shelved for a decade. President François Hollande, who plans to visit Algeria in December, is hoping to gain Algerian backing for an African-led military intervention in northern Mali, which has been overrun by armed Islamist groups. In October, Mr. Hollande became the first French president to officially acknowledge that scores of Algerian independence protesters were killed by the French police at a rally in Paris in 1961. March 19 was selected as the day of remembrance because it was the date of the cease-fire that ended the fighting in 1962. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: A Day for a War’s Victims', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: A Day for a War’s Victims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALGERIA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T01:16:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7d0cd25-24da-5cba-9761-0f003386b1e9', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7d0cd25-24da-5cba-9761-0f003386b1e9'}, {'abstract': 'Wendell Castle’s creations have blurred the boundaries between art and craft and form and function, challenging traditional notions of how furniture should look and how it should be used.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/nyregion/the-furniture-of-wendell-castle-at-the-aldrich-in-ridgefield.html', 'snippet': 'Wendell Castle’s creations have blurred the bou