inority voters. The justices should uphold the validity of the section, which requires nine states and parts of several others with deep histories of racial discrimination to get permission from the Justice Department or a federal court before making any changes to their voting rules. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Supreme Test on the Right to Vote', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Supreme Test on the Right to Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shelby County (Ala)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T02:25:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d7a4785-a249-5639-bcce-43823a32a981', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d7a4785-a249-5639-bcce-43823a32a981'}, {'abstract': 'Voters softened a law imposing a life sentence for any felony conviction if a defendant had two prior serious convictions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/opinion/a-three-strikes-law-made-fairer-in-california.html', 'snippet': 'Voters softened a law imposing a life sentence for any felony conviction if a defendant had two prior serious convictions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'California’s voters softened one of the nation’s most destructive and unfair sentencing policies this week when they approved a ballot initiative revising the infamous three-strikes law of 1994, which imposes a life sentence for any felony conviction — no matter how minor — if the defendant has two previous serious convictions. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Strikes Made Fairer', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Three Strikes Made Fairer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T02:29:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdf69533-406d-57a8-8219-d36299ddd194', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdf69533-406d-57a8-8219-d36299ddd194'}, {'abstract': 'With many tax cuts set to expire on Dec. 31 and some new taxes scheduled to start with the new year, many Americans’ tax bills will go up next year. Exactly how much is not yet clear, but here is how some of those changes would affect two types of taxpayers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/11/10/business/tax-raises-that-may-come.html', 'snippet': 'With many tax cuts set to expire on Dec. 31 and some new taxes scheduled to start with the new year, many Americans’ tax bills will go up next year. Exactly how much is not yet clear, but here is how some of those changes would affect two types of...', 'lead_paragraph': 'With many tax cuts set to expire on Dec. 31 and some new taxes scheduled to start with the new year, many Americans’ tax bills will go up next year. Exactly how much is not yet clear, but here is how some of those changes would affect two types of taxpayers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tax Raises That May Come', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T02:30:12+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/ade43301-62ef-5f30-9719-061abd13540c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/ade43301-62ef-5f30-9719-061abd13540c'}, {'abstract': 'After a beating last summer that left him with a concussion, Badgers running back Montee Ball is back to being one of the nation’s top players and his team is contending in the Big Ten.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/sports/ncaafootball/montee-ball-and-wisconsin-back-to-their-old-selves.html', 'snippet': 'After a beating last summer that left him with a concussion, Badgers running back Montee Ball is back to being one of the nation’s top players and his team is contending in the Big Ten.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The room was quiet, his teammates hanging on his every word, when Montee Ball apologized for what he had not seen coming. Someone had called his name, he turned, saw a fist, then nothing. He awoke in a hospital bed with a concussion and a face swollen from five men kicking his head.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 