idents of a battered Belle Harbor, on the Rockaway Peninsula, the biggest fear is being forgotten.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday morning, fresh light fell on the continuing miseries wrought by Hurricane Sandy, and Abby Barnett, a city schoolteacher, was entirely grateful for the brilliant sun as she continued to muck out her battered bay-front home in Belle Harbor, on the Rockaway Peninsula. “The looters were right there,” she said, pointing to the backyard of a neighbor who heard them and began screaming, alerting others guarding hearth and home through another cold night of uncertainty. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Search for Words Amid Devastation', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The City Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Search for Words Amid Devastation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockaway Peninsula (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockaway Beach (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'City Life', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T02:42:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f034cd86-87f1-51a5-8c10-774e6e934829', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f034cd86-87f1-51a5-8c10-774e6e934829'}, {'abstract': 'With Rafael Soriano, Nick Swisher and Hiroki Kuroda all declining the team’s one-year, $13.3 million offer, the Yankees will now begin to determine which of the three players, if any, will come back.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/sports/baseball/yankees-rafael-soriano-nick-swisher-and-hiroki-kuroda-turn-down-qualifying-offers.html', 'snippet': 'With Rafael Soriano, Nick Swisher and Hiroki Kuroda all declining the team’s one-year, $13.3 million offer, the Yankees will now begin to determine which of the three players, if any, will come back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIAN WELLS, Calif. — Nobody really wants to believe the Yankees are aiming to become fiscally responsible, relatively speaking, but in making qualifying offers this off-season to Rafael Soriano, Nick Swisher and Hiroki Kuroda, the team showed a reluctance to make a long-term commitment to any player at this point. While they might not be aiming to be as thrifty as the Mets, the Yankees no longer want a bloated budget.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/yankees/yankees-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 642, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/yankees/yankees-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1285, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/yankees/yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/yankees/yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/yankees/yankees-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Surprise: 3 Yankees Turn Down 1-Year Offers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Surprise: 3 Yankees Turn Down 1-Year Offers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swisher, Nick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soriano, Rafael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuroda, Hiroki', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T02:53:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jorge Arangure Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jorge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arangure', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4c83957-2600-5f26-b9cb-7bdb448bad41', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4c83957-2600-5f26-b9cb-7bdb448bad41'}, {'abstract': 'The outcome of several races remained a mystery in Arizona as officials struggled to count a record number of early and provisional ballots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/11/09/us/20121110_BALLOTS.html', 'snippet': 'The outcome of several races remained a mystery in Arizona as officials struggled to count a record number of early and provisional ballots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The outcome of several races remained a mystery in Arizona as officials struggled to count a record number of early and provisional ballo