, Berkeley.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/education/california-historian-named-chancellor.html', 'snippet': 'Nicholas B. Dirks, Columbia University’s executive vice president for arts and sciences and dean of the faculty, has been chosen to be chancellor of the University of California, Berkeley.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Nicholas B. Dirks, Columbia University’s executive vice president for arts and sciences and dean of the faculty, has been chosen to be chancellor of the University of California, Berkeley. The Board of Regents will vote this month on the appointment, made by the University of California’s president, Mark Yudof. Dr. Dirks, 61, an anthropologist and historian who has written three books on India, would succeed Robert J. Birgeneau. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Historian Named Chancellor', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Historian Named Chancellor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dirks, Nicholas B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Berkeley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T04:28:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ca278d0-5bd5-5cbd-b0ee-9e8b243e3212', 'word_count': 68, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ca278d0-5bd5-5cbd-b0ee-9e8b243e3212'}, {'abstract': 'An Iraqi immigrant was arrested on first-degree murder charges in the beating death of his wife, a mother of five whose killing was initially thought to be a hate crime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/us/california-spouse-faces-murder-charge.html', 'snippet': 'An Iraqi immigrant was arrested on first-degree murder charges in the beating death of his wife, a mother of five whose killing was initially thought to be a hate crime.', 'lead_paragraph': ' An Iraqi immigrant was arrested on first-degree murder charges in the beating death of his wife, a mother of five whose killing was initially feared to be a hate crime. Kassim Alhimidi, 48, was arrested on Thursday in the death of Shaima Alawadi, also an Iraqi immigrant, who was found in their home in El Cajon with an anti-Muslim note beside her body, El Cajon police said Friday. The killing shocked members of the city’s large Muslim immigrant community, some of whom feared it had been a hate crime, a possibility Mr. Alhimidi spoke about in the days after his wife’s death. Jim Redman, police chief in El Cajon, said the killing was the result of “a domestic violence incident,” not a hate crime. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Spouse Faces Murder Charge', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Spouse Faces Murder Charge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alhimidi, Kassim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'El Cajon (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alawadi, Shaima', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T04:38:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'o