times.com/2012/11/10/sports/ncaafootball/bill-curry-at-georgia-state-focuses-on-final-win-despite-tug-of-retirement.html', 'snippet': 'Georgia State’s Bill Curry plans to end his nearly 20 years coaching and mentoring players to spend time with his family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — On a gritty downtown block, intense rain and the specter of lightning shooed the Georgia State football team off its practice field Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/y-curry/y-curry-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/y-curry/y-curry-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/y-curry/y-curry-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/y-curry/y-curry-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/y-curry/y-curry-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/y-curry/y-curry-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/sports/y-curry/y-curry-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Focusing on One Last Saturday, Despite the Tug of Retirement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Focusing on One Last Saturday, Despite the Tug of Retirement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curry, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Georgia State University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T05:17:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Tierney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tierney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b0eb01e-ad91-5fcd-9ae1-ebf5d4b38aef', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b0eb01e-ad91-5fcd-9ae1-ebf5d4b38aef'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (DirecTV) THE ROLLING STONES: CHARLIE IS MY DARLING — IRELAND 1965 (2012) In honor of the 50th anniversary of the Rolling Stones, this hourlong documentary — originally directed by Peter Whitehead and produced by Andrew Loog Oldham, and digitally restored for a new version by the director Mick Gochanour and the producer Robin Klein — follows the young band, with Brian Jones on guitar (above left, with Mick Jagger), as it tours Ireland in 1965. “It is both a postcard from an earlier phase of celebrity culture and a glorious mixtape of raucous and memorable songs,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times — among them, “The Last Time,” “Time Is on My Side,” “(I Can’t Get No) Satisfaction” and “a couple of Beatles tunes hummed and strummed by Keith Richards and Mick Jagger in a hotel room” as the men “were still figuring out how to be the opposite of the four lads from Liverpool.” Their answer, he added, “was to be naughtier, more aggressive, more theatrically sexual.” And despite intimations of events to come — Jones’s death, less than five years away, and the lethal mayhem of Altamont in 1969 — mostly, Mr. Scott said, “what you see is the intensity of rock ’n’ roll at a time when it still felt risky and thrilling.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T06:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/c97e41fc-94d4-56a7-a609-a0abee1f5b07', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c97e41fc-94d4-56a7-a609-a0abee1f5b07'}, {'abstract': 'A round-up of news from across India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/newswallah-bharat-edition-63/', 'snippet': 'A round-up of news from across India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jammu and Kashmir: The Jammu and Kashmir High Court held that a Muslim man’s power to divorce his wife is not “unrestricted or unqualified,” Kashmir Live reported. Justice Hasnain Masoodi, in his 23-page judgment, delved into the details of Shariah, or Islamic law, and the Koran, the Muslim holy book, to come to the conclusion that a “husband cannot have 