 worry that the public may be losing privacy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/technology/biometric-data-gathering-sets-off-a-privacy-debate.html', 'snippet': 'Biometric data-gathering — from palm scans to facial-recognition software — is all the rage. But consumer advocates worry that the public may be losing privacy.', 'lead_paragraph': '“PLEASE put your hand on the scanner,” a receptionist at a doctor’s office at New York University Langone Medical Center said to me recently, pointing to a small plastic device on the counter between us. “I need to take a palm scan for your file.”', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-STREAM/11-STREAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 857, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-STREAM/11-STREAM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1714, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-STREAM/11-STREAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-STREAM/11-STREAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-STREAM/11-STREAM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When a Palm Reader Knows More Than Your Life Line', 'kicker': 'Slipstream', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When a Palm Reader Knows More Than Your Life Line', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biometrics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York University Langone Medical Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronic Health Records', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T20:45:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natasha Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natasha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2503c54-8d73-574a-8b0d-3eec244de16a', 'word_count': 1147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2503c54-8d73-574a-8b0d-3eec244de16a'}, {'abstract': 'From 1998 to 2001, Kozmo.com offered free delivery within an hour. Now, some online merchants and their delivery partners are inching back toward that vision.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/technology/online-merchants-again-pursue-same-day-delivery-service.html', 'snippet': 'From 1998 to 2001, Kozmo.com offered free delivery within an hour. Now, some online merchants and their delivery partners are inching back toward that vision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the exhilarating, anything-is-possible days of 1998 to 2001, Kozmo.com offered an online store with a quick  delivery service in a number of American cities. “Free delivery in under an hour” was its motto.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-DIGI/11-DIGI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 988, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption':