” (Nov. 4).', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quickening the Pace of Economic Recovery', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quickening The Pace of Economic Recovery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T21:03:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb10219d-e9a2-52ad-8757-febf5b8c5555', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb10219d-e9a2-52ad-8757-febf5b8c5555'}, {'abstract': 'Let there be lights!', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/power-to-the-people/', 'snippet': 'Let there be lights!', 'lead_paragraph': 'Well, to the Wells/Krugman household, anyway — after 12 days. Still using 4G for internet access. But progress at last.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Power to the People', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T21:04:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44393f66-3f63-5aa3-a72c-87ab37b4467e', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44393f66-3f63-5aa3-a72c-87ab37b4467e'}, {'abstract': 'After devoting much of his early life to hockey, the C.E.O. of Brooks Sports says he needed to pivot and put his energy into business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/jobs/jim-weber-of-brooks-sports-and-the-path-to-running-shoes.html', 'snippet': 'After devoting much of his early life to hockey, the C.E.O. of Brooks Sports says he needed to pivot and put his energy into business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I GREW up in a suburb of St. Paul, one of six children. My family owned a combination bowling alley, restaurant and tavern, and our lives revolved around that business. I was counting change from the vending machines and rolling it into coin sleeves at the age of 7. Among my jobs there was working behind the bowling counter. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-BOSS/11-BOSS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 790, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-BOSS/11-BOSS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1457, 'width': 1124, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-BOSS/11-BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-BOSS/11-BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-BOSS/11-BOSS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ice Skates to Running Shoes', 'kicker': 'The Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ice Skates to Running Shoes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weber, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooks Sports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berkshire Hathaway Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T21:11:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d5e858f-4d89-507f-8c95-4ce5a6bc109c', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d5e858f-4d89-507f-8c95-4ce5a6bc109c'}, {'abstract': 'Many C.E.O.’s lament that recent college graduates lack specific, technical skills, but these employers should realize that a broad education has benefits, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/jobs/bridging-the-hiring-gap-for-college-graduates.html', 'snippet': 'Many C.E.O.’s lament that recent college graduates lack specific, technical skills, but these employers should realize that a broad education has benefits, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANY newly minted college graduates are filled with anxiety, fearing that they won’t find decent jobs despite their knowledge and skills, and that they will never be free of tuition debt. At the same time, executives say they can’t find qualified applicants for a wide range of jobs.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-PRE/11-PRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 967, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-PRE/11-PRE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1484, 'width': 1571, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-PRE/11-PRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-PRE/11-PRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/business/11-PRE/11-PRE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Bridge the Hiring Gap', 'kicker': 'Preoccupations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How To Bridge The Hiring Gap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T21:12:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert W. Goldfarb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Goldfarb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41591d71-64a3-5802-b54d-bc5960fcff33', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41591d71-64a3-5802-b54d-bc5960fcff33'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes a campaign does tell you about fitness to govern.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/unqualified/', 'snippet': 'Sometimes a campaign does tell you about fitness to govern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back during the late unlamented era after the Supremes installed W in the White House, it was common to hear assertions from the Beltway types to the effect that the effectiveness of the Bush political campaign demonstrated that the Bush team had the competence needed to run the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unqualified', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T21:19:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db9ddd79-b507-5498-8e44-801e33a84028', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db9ddd79-b507-5498-8e44-801e33a84028'}, {'abstract': 'More than a week after Hurricane Sandy, Gerritsen Beach in Brooklyn, a seaside enclave of police officers, firefighters and emergency medics, is worse off than all but a few city neighborhoods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/nyregion/gerritsen-beach-home-to-emergency-workers-is-still-reeling-from-the-storm.html', 'snippet': 'More than a week after Hurricane Sandy, Gerritsen Beach in Brooklyn, a seaside enclave of police officers, firefighters and emergency medics, is worse off than all but a few city neighborhoods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If any neighborhood could have been expected to cope smoothly with Hurricane Sandy, it should have been Gerritsen Beach, Brooklyn, which is rich with police officers, firefighters and emergency medics accustomed to dealing with other people’s disasters.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/nyregion/GERRITSEN/GERRITSEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/11/nyregion/GERRITSEN/GERRITSEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/nyregion/GERRITSEN/GERRITSEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/nyregion/GERRITSEN/GERRITSEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/nyregion/GERRITSEN/GERRITSEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/11/nyregion/GERRITSEN/GERRITSEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/nyregion/GERRITSEN/GERRITSEN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Neighborhood That Emergency Workers Call Home Is Still Reeling From Storm', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Neighborhood That Emergency Workers Call Home Is Still Reeling From Storm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'GERRITSEN BEACH (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Outages and Blackouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T21:25:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7e5af26-1df4-5f7e-b95c-30619f7b93fc', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7e5af26-1df4-5f7e-b95c-30619f7b93fc'}, {'abstract': 'Muddled CEOs.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/10/more-on-invisible-bond-vigilantes/', 'snippet': 'Muddled CEOs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I argued yesterday that even if the heretofore invisible bond vigilantes materialize one of these days, their attack won’t have the effects the deficit hawks imagine. Because America has its own currency and a floating exchange rate, a loss of confidence would lead not to a contractionary rise in interest rates but to an expansionary fall in the dollar. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More on Invisible Bond Vigilantes', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-10T21:34:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b4b067a-fdc1-5ef6-893d-1f69de9bb610', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b4b067a-fdc1-5ef6-893d-1f69de9bb610'}, {'abstract': 'George Entwistle stepped down Saturday amid a deepening controversy over BBC news reports on prominent public figures accused of pedophilia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/world/europe/george-entwistle-resigns-as-head-of-bbc.html', 'snippet': 'George Entwistle stepped down Saturday amid a deepening controversy over BBC news reports on prominent public figures accused of pedophilia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — After weeks of turmoil over the BBC’s coverage of a spreading pedophile scandal, the broadcaster’s director general, George Entwistle, resigned on Saturday night, bowing to a wave of condemnation by critics including a longtime BBC television anchor, who depicted him as having lost control of “a rudderless ship heading towards the rocks.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/world/11bbc3/11bbc3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 726, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/world/11bbc3/11bbc3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1452, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/11/world/11bbc3/11bbc3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/11/world/11bbc3/11bbc3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'BBC Director Quits in Furor Over Coverage of Sexual Abuse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'BBC Director Quits in Furor Over Coverage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'org