times.com/2012/11/10/off-script-at-chinas-18th-party-congress/', 'snippet': 'Even at an event as choreographed as the Chinese Community Party’s national congress, taking place in Beijing right now, moments of truth slip out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — As China’s 18th Communist Party Congress moved into the weekend, a key part of the show was in full swing — meetings of party delegations from each province and key groups such as central government bodies. The provincial meetings are normally scripted affairs, attended by some of the men (and the top provincial leaders, like the national ones, are virtually all men,) who will be the future national leaders. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/blogs/10rdv-18th-national-congress-hunan-room/10rdv-18th-national-congress-hunan-room-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/blogs/10rdv-18th-national-congress-hunan-room/10rdv-18th-national-congress-hunan-room-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Off Script at China’s 18th Party Congress', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li Wangyang', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-11T00:25:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bca12ef-a206-54a5-8704-80e8a6343aa2', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bca12ef-a206-54a5-8704-80e8a6343aa2'}, {'abstract': 'If you want to know the Texas Republican Party’s next direction, keep an eye on David Dewhurst and Joe Straus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/us/dewhurst-and-straus-as-a-texas-gop-microcosm.html', 'snippet': 'If you want to know the Texas Republican Party’s next direction, keep an eye on David Dewhurst and Joe Straus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ross Ramsey, the executive editor of The Texas Tribune, writes a column for The Tribune.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '35A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Moves Right, the Other May Be Pushed', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Moves Right, The Other May Be Pushed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dewhurst, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Straus, Joseph R III', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-11T00:33:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Ramsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86c32481-10ba-5c2c-a5d3-e6b8d3a6a697', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86c32481-10ba-5c2c-a5d3-e6b8d3a6a697'}, {'abstract': 'Despite an influx of coal projects, poverty rates remain stubbornly high, raising tough questions about whether Africa’s resource boom can effectively raise the standards of living of its people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/world/africa/as-coal-boosts-mozambique-the-rural-poor-are-left-behind.html', 'snippet': 'Despite an influx of coal projects, poverty rates remain stubbornly high, raising tough questions about whether Africa’s resource boom can effectively raise the standards of living of its people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CATEME, Mozambique — When Augusto Conselho Chachoka and his neighbors heard that the world’s biggest coal mine was to be built on their land, a tantalizing new future floated before them. Instead of scraping by as subsistence farmers, they would earn wages as miners, they thought. The mining company would build them sturdy new houses, it seemed. Finally, a slice of the wealth that has propelled Mozambique from its war-addled past to its newfound status as one of the world’s fastest-growing economies would be theirs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Coal Boosts Mozambique, the Rural Poor Are Left Behind', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Coal Boosts Mozambique, The Rural Poor Are Left Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mozambique', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rural Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-11T00:37:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23bed97f-4d69-58a7-b5d4-a163658625e7', 'word_count': 1479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23bed97f-4d69-58a7-b5d4-a163658625e7'}, {'abstract': 'New gas and coal deals rarely create large numbers of jobs or foster local entrepreneurship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/11/10/world/africa/20121111-MOZAMBIQUE.html', 'snippet': 'New gas and coal deals rarely create large numbers of jobs or foster local entrepreneurship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New gas and coal deals rarely create large numbers of jobs or foster local entrepreneurship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/world/africa/20121111-MOZAMBIQUE-slide-63DS/20121111-MOZAMBIQUE-slide-63DS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1021, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/world/africa/20121111-MOZAMBIQUE-slide-63DS/20121111-MOZAMBIQUE-slide-63DS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2043, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/10/world/africa/20121111-MOZAMBIQUE-slide-63DS/20121111-MOZAMBIQUE-slide-63DS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/10/world/africa/20121111-MOZAMBIQUE-slide-63DS/20121111-MOZAMBIQUE-slide-63DS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {