'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14dd1aeb-0279-59aa-85f1-3897c0d4f6a1', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14dd1aeb-0279-59aa-85f1-3897c0d4f6a1'}, {'abstract': 'How do they condemn too much deficit reduction?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/squirming-hawks/', 'snippet': 'How do they condemn too much deficit reduction?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fiscal cliff poses an interesting problem for self-styled deficit hawks. They’ve been going on and on about how the deficit is a terrible thing; now they’re confronted with the possibility of a large reduction in the deficit, and have to find a way to say that this is a bad thing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Squirming Hawks', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-11T15:19:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af0d40f7-5158-57b4-95f3-a0c750e36f13', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af0d40f7-5158-57b4-95f3-a0c750e36f13'}, {'abstract': 'At a time when we can see video shot by a robot on Mars and when we can deposit checks on our smartphones without going to a bank, why do most people still have to go to a polling place to vote?', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/disruptions-casting-a-ballot-by-smartphone/', 'snippet': 'At a time when we can see video shot by a robot on Mars and when we can deposit checks on our smartphones without going to a bank, why do most people still have to go to a polling place to vote?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Tuesday, millions of Americans stood in long lines to cast their votes. While they waited, sometimes for several hours, many used their smartphones to pass the time.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/technology/12bits-voting/12bits-voting-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/technology/12bits-voting/12bits-voting-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1288, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/technology/12bits-voting/12bits-voting-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/12/technology/12bits-voting/12bits-voting-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/technology/12bits-voting/12bits-voting-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disruptions: Casting a Ballot by Smartphone', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Voting Booth In the Hands Of Everyone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {