ing close to 40,000 theatergoers last year. “Gnit” by Mr. Eno (“Middletown”), a cautionary tale about laziness, is to run March 15 to April 7; “Appropriate” by Mr. Jacobs-Jenkins (“Neighbors”), about a sibling feud over a newly discovered inheritance, is slated for March 5 to April 7; and “The Delling Shore,” the new play be Mr. Marks (“Brack’s Last Bachelor Party”), about an author’s strange evening at a rival’s lake house, is set for Feb. 27 to April 7. For the complete lineup, see actorstheatre.org.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Humana Festival Sets Lineup', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Humana Festival Lineup Announced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eno, Will', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs-Jenkins, Branden', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marks, Sam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACTORS THEATER OF LOUISVILLE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-11T17:23:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aba578c3-9b1d-512b-9ebc-78c55cf40b18', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aba578c3-9b1d-512b-9ebc-78c55cf40b18'}, {'abstract': 'Chinese officials tried to allay concerns on Sunday that the country was allowing its banking system to grow at a reckless pace as a way to sustain short-term economic growth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/business/global/chinas-banking-leaders-seek-to-calm-concerns-over-revived-growth.html', 'snippet': 'Chinese officials tried to allay 