6f-9993882e33b1'}, {'abstract': "The officials are unlikely to sign off on a long-delayed tranche of aid for Greece until they receive a report on the country's progress in meeting its fiscal goals.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/business/global/euro-zone-finance-ministers-to-wrestle-with-greek-debt.html', 'snippet': "The officials are unlikely to sign off on a long-delayed tranche of aid for Greece until they receive a report on the country's progress in meeting its fiscal goals.", 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — Finance ministers from euro area countries were scheduled to gather here on Monday evening to confront a Greek debt that still threatened to torpedo the European monetary union after three years of unbroken crisis. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro Zone Finance Ministers to Wrestle With Greek Debt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'European Officials to Meet on Greek Debt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samaras, Antonis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-11T21:32:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Kanter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a53c5e65-6694-540c-82af-beac1ab54a50', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a53c5e65-6694-540c-82af-beac1ab54a50'}, {'abstract': 'The Giants’ loss was their second in a row and left them in the unenviable position of stewing about their poor play for two weeks before facing the Packers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/sports/football/giants-appear-listless-in-loss-to-bengals.html', 'snippet': 'The Giants’ loss was their second in a row and left them in the unenviable position of stewing about their poor play for two weeks before facing the Packers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CINCINNATI — Early last week, as the Giants began to prepare for Sunday’s game against the Cincinnati Bengals, it was a challenge for the players to keep from thinking ahead. It was not that they were looking past the Bengals to another opponent; rather, the Giants studied for the Bengals game while trying to fend off dreams of an impending vacation.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1406, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking Forward to Resting, the Giants Get an Early Start', 'kicker': 'Bengals 31, Giants 13', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking Forward to Resting, The Giants Get an Early Start', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cincinnati Bengals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalton, Andy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-11T21:50:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eeecdd0b-1255-52c6-bc5c-7c9cb1b5bd14', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eeecdd0b-1255-52c6-bc5c-7c9cb1b5bd14'}, {'abstract': 'A festival made up of countless small-scale impressions, Jazz & Colors featured 30 ensembles performing the same set list, at the same time, throughout Central Park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/arts/music/30-bands-perform-in-jazz-colors-at-central-park.html', 'snippet': 'A festival made up of countless small-scale impressions, Jazz & Colors featured 30 ensembles performing the same set list, at the same time, throughout Central Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cornetist Kirk Knuffke was playing music for an idyll at midafternoon on Saturday: “Skating in Central Park,” an elegant waltz composed by John Lewis for the Modern Jazz Quartet. There were no skaters in sight, but the scene felt otherwise right. Mr. Knuffke and his band mates, in winter coats, set up beside a footpath at the park’s northeast corner, facing the glassy surface of the Harlem Meer. A stone’s throw behind them buses moved unhurriedly along Duke Ellington Circle; on an adjacent park bench someone busily filled in Mr. Knuffke’s image on a sketch pad, complete with hat and beard. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/jpjazz2/jpjazz2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 294, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/jpjazz2/jpjazz2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 294}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/jpjazz2/jpjazz2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 503, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/jpjazz2/jpjazz2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1005, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/jpjazz2/jpjazz2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/jpjazz2/jpjazz2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/jpjazz2/jpjazz2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Backbeats, Footpaths and Meer', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Backbeats, Footpaths And Meer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CENTRAL PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-11T22:14:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf9d4e2a-40d5-582c-8c12-acc3e15a5628', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf9d4e2a-40d5-582c-8c12-acc3e15a5628'}, {'abstract': 'Two studies by the NPD Group seemed to show conflicting data on the effects of streaming music services like Pandora and Spotify on users’ spending and listening.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/studies-offer-a-complex-view-of-music-consumers-habits/', 'snippet': 'Two studies by the NPD Group seemed to show conflicting data on the effects of streaming music services like Pandora and Spotify on users’ spending and listening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the growth of streaming music services like Pandora and Spotify, which let people listen to millions of songs free or by subscription, a critical question for the industry is how these habits will affect users’ spending and listening habits. Yet the more the issue is studied, the more complicated the answer.', 'print_section': '