ww.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/us/politics/first-republicans-must-find-common-ground-among-themselves.html', 'snippet': 'While some leaders argued that the party must find new ways to talk about key issues, others blamed losses on poor candidates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For four years, the leader most capable of unifying the fractious Republican Party has been Barack Obama.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Strains to Define How to Close Gap With Voters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republicans’ First Challenge: Find Common Ground Among Themselves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-11T22:49:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Sack and Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f565cc0-74c1-566a-942f-2ecade1093a6', 'word_count': 1497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f565cc0-74c1-566a-942f-2ecade1093a6'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/arts/television/whats-on-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (Investigation Discovery) I DIDN’T DO IT Chris Noth narrates this new series, which takes viewers through cases in which innocent people were sent to jail while the guilty parties roamed free. First up: Ronald Cotton, left, who spent more than a decade imprisoned for raping Jennifer Thompson before DNA tests exonerated him. Ms. Thompson and Mr. Cotton are now friends, campaigning together to prevent flawed eyewitness testimony.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-11T22:49:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/aad6a0da-0ced-505f-9242-6d6589eb8afc', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aad6a0da-0ced-505f-9242-6d6589eb8afc'}, {'abstract': 'A modified version of “Catfish” the documentary, about the deceptions of online relationships, surfaces as a reality show on MTV.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/arts/television/catfish-the-tv-show-with-nev-schulman-exposes-deceit.html', 'snippet': 'A modified version of “Catfish” the documentary, about the deceptions of online relationships, surfaces as a reality show on MTV.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the documentary “Catfish” was released in 2010, its depiction of a relationship built on Internet trickery drew critical praise as well as questions about authenticity and exploitation. The film’s successor, a series called “Catfish: The TV Show” beginning Monday on MTV, generates the same questions but with easier answers. The series is both more obviously real and more routinely, prosaically exploitative than the film. It’s the reality-TV dividend.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'There’s Always a Catch', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'There’s Always A Catch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Catfish (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-11T22:57:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/843cd431-4cf0-5d4b-9b84-c684ddf35338', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/843cd431-4cf0-5d4b-9b84-c684ddf35338'}, {'abstract': 'Advantage Democrats, but can they keep it?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/organization/', 'snippet': 'Advantage Democrats, but can they keep it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Fallows says something I’ve been thinking, too:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Organization', 'kicke