alue': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T02:47:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2191f786-0539-598d-bec1-2e19bf91d204', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2191f786-0539-598d-bec1-2e19bf91d204'}, {'abstract': 'The deficit scolds have discredited themselves with arguments that are wrong and also dishonest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/opinion/krugman-hawks-and-hypocrites.html', 'snippet': 'The deficit scolds have discredited themselves with arguments that are wrong and also dishonest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in 2010, self-styled deficit hawks — better described as deficit scolds — took over much of our political discourse. At a time of mass unemployment and record-low borrowing costs, a time when economic theory said we needed more, not less, deficit spending, the scolds convinced most of our political class that deficits rather than jobs should be our top economic priority. And now that the election is over, they’re trying to pick up where they left off.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hawks and Hypocrites', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hawks And Hypocrites', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowles, Erskine B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T02:49:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fab5343a-7206-5d31-b2b2-a6e598e7b2d4', 'word_count': 820, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fab5343a-7206-5d31-b2b2-a6e598e7b2d4'}, {'abstract': 'We are now in that postelection respite, when you can almost see the green and red landing lights up ahead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/opinion/after-the-returns-november-returns.html', 'snippet': 'We are now in that postelection respite, when you can almost see the green and red landing lights up ahead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that the election is over, it feels as though we’ve been cleared for our approach to the holidays. You can almost see the green and red landing lights up ahead, guiding us over a forest of balsam and fir and into the heart of a gift-giving season almost no one is prepared to think about yet. November has been handed back to us, to do with it what we will. Among the things we can be thankful for, when Thanksgiving comes, is the fact that voting occurs so early in the month. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After the Returns, November Returns', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After the Returns, November Returns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autumn (Season)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T02:49:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/536a1491-406b-5f62-991d-47f98ffd30ed', 'word_c