urity initiatives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/opinion/president-obamas-foreign-policy-agenda.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama has a new chance to carry out national security initiatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'National security didn’t play heavily in the presidential election. But President Obama’s legacy, and the country’s future, will be shaped as much by the foreign policy and defense decisions he makes over the next four years as by those on the domestic side. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Foreign Policy Agenda', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Foreign Policy Agenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T03:19:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0327bdb-09a7-5229-b617-31799a8dde7d', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0327bdb-09a7-5229-b617-31799a8dde7d'}, {'abstract': 'Owners and the union have drawn close to a deal that would end the lockout, but they remain far apart on when players can become free agents, among other contractual matters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/sports/hockey/nhl-contract-issues-are-final-hurdle-in-talks.html', 'snippet': 'Owners and the union have drawn close to a deal that would end the lockout, but they remain far apart on when players can become free agents, among other contractual matters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a week of negotiations, the N.H.L. and its players association have drawn close to agreement on several key issues, remaining far apart in only one main area: players’ contract rights. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/hockey/12hockey-2/12hockey-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/hockey/12hockey-2/12hockey-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1468, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/hockey/12hockey-2/12hockey-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/hockey/12hockey-2/12hockey-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/hockey/12hockey-2/12hockey-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Contract Issues Emerge as Final Hurdle in N.H.L. Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Contract Issues Emerge as Final Hurdle in N.H.L. Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T03:28:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9bb88e9-ec04-5da9-8911-4e1f06520597', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9bb88e9-ec04-5da9-8911-4e1f06520597'}, {'abstract': 'The misery of Hurricane Sandy has created a fleeting moment of political will, a chance to assure the survival of our greatest metropolis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/opinion/keller-a-new-manhattan-project.html', 'snippet': 'The misery of Hurricane Sandy has created a fleeting moment of political will, a chance to assure the survival of our greatest metropolis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the monster storm struck, my colleagues at The Times’s Room for Debate desk asked an array of experts whether New York should build protective barriers against the next one. The answers covered, pardon the expression, the waterfront: Do something big! (“Worth the Investment”) Do something small! (“Big Projects, Big Problems”) Do nothing much! (“Low on the List of Life-Saving Ideas”) Think about doing, well, something! (“A Wake-Up Call to Consider the Options”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 350, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller