ph': '// ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cutler Knockout, and Penalties That Aren’t Equal', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cutler, Jay', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steratore, Gene', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bears', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Texans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T12:42:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Bretherton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bretherton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b92965e-66e4-50d4-93a9-23773de4587c', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b92965e-66e4-50d4-93a9-23773de4587c'}, {'abstract': 'A commercial property owner in California will be able to avoid large upfront costs by paying regular installments on a utility bill. In a twist, the payments will continue even if the property changes hands.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/a-new-way-to-foot-efficiency-upgrades/', 'snippet': 'A commercial property owner in California will be able to avoid large upfront costs by paying regular installments on a utility bill. In a twist, the payments will continue even if the property changes hands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For commercial property owners in California looking to finance energy efficiency upgrades for their buildings, the process should be a bit easier and cheaper come early next year, thanks to a new pilot program approved last week by the state’s Public Utilities Commission.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Way to Foot Efficiency Upgrades', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T12:45:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Witkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d796233-fdcb-5538-b66b-a16415cb244b', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d796233-fdcb-5538-b66b-a16415cb244b'}, {'abstract': 'With the widespread and growing desire to study abroad, an industry of agents (some ethical, some not) has sprung up to provide services to students and their families. Do you want an overseas education so much that you would pay an agent?', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/using-agents-on-quests-for-admissions-abroad/', 'snippet': 'With the widespread and growing desire to study abroad, an industry of agents (some ethical, some not) has sprung up to provide services to students and their families. Do you want an overseas education so much that you would pay an agent?', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG—Lara Farrar reports from Shanghai that China is seeking public comment on a proposal to crack down on the education agents who charge students to help them get to overseas schools. While there are some reputable private counselors and education consultants, many agents in China engage in unethical behavior: falsifying academic records, applications and essays and making false promises to clients that they can “guarantee” admissions. (The reality is that no guarantee from an agent can get you into a top school if you don’t have the test scores or grades to qualify. Diploma mills are another matter.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Using Agents on Quests for Admissions Abroad', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T12:48:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Lau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50652dcf-8061-5b32-9130-2b80f02786f4', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50652dcf-8061-5b32-9130-2b80f02786f4'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/opinion-report-support-the-m-t-a/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: Support the M.T.A.', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T13:02:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 