, 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec8f9abd-177b-57f2-bbd6-c91b0b5d7bcd', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec8f9abd-177b-57f2-bbd6-c91b0b5d7bcd'}, {'abstract': 'U.S. Coach Jurgen Klinsmann named 20 players to his roster for a friendly match Wednesday at Russia.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/klinsmann-picks-20-to-face-russia/', 'snippet': 'U.S. Coach Jurgen Klinsmann named 20 players to his roster for a friendly match Wednesday at Russia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jurgen Klinsmann, the coach of the United States national team, released a 20-man training camp roster on Monday ahead of Wednesday’s match against Russia at Kuban Stadium in Krasnodar (10 a.m. Eastern, ESPN2, ESPN3 and Univision).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Klinsmann Picks 20 to Face Russia', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T15:54:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67ac761c-56d0-59a4-8728-00ffd2a9e5a2', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67ac761c-56d0-59a4-8728-00ffd2a9e5a2'}, {'abstract': 'Fears that the architectural jewel in Barcelona might be put up for sale were allayed by the creation of a special foundation.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/gaudis-casa-mil-gets-reprieve/', 'snippet': 'Fears that the architectural jewel in Barcelona might be put up for sale were allayed by the creation of a special foundation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BARCELONA — With the economic crisis roiling Europe, fears have been growing among cultural observers that cash-strapped countries like Greece, Spain and Italy could sell cultural treasures to avert financial insolvency. In Spain these concerns were fanned in recent weeks after it emerged that Catalunya Caixa, a struggling savings bank that owns the Antoni Gaudi Barcelona masterpiece Casa Milà, could be forced to put that architectural jewel up for sale. There were even rumors that a Russian billionaire wanted to buy the building. But those fears have been allayed after the bank, which was temporarily taken over by the state after going bankrupt, announced last week that it would set up a special foundation to administer Casa Milà and to assure that it would not go to auction. Catalan culture officials said the foundation would have a budget of about 35 million euros, a big chunk of that derived from ticket sales to Casa Milà, a popular tourist destination.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gaudi’s Casa Mila Gets Reprieve', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaudi, Antoni', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Barcelona (Spain)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T15:55:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9620e6f-672e-5ad7-a2e2-41d4b2db5d00', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9620e6f-672e-5ad7-a2e2-41d4b2db5d00'}, {'abstract': 'Religion looms large in Cologne, but its less pious passions — from art to beer — are just as abundant.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/grand-teuton/', 'snippet': 'Religion looms large in Cologne, but its less pious passions — from art to beer — are just as abundant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '77', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grand Teuton', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grand Teuton', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cologne (Germany)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T16:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Lewis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcd9f057-466d-55b7-be46-df1c097b0613', 'word_count': 2235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcd9f057-466d-55b7-be46-df1c097b0613'}, {'abstract': 'Military duty in particular — but also other professions that require people to travel a lot or work away from home for long periods of time— can put serious strains on marriages and family life. If you or your spouse is in such a role, how do you make your family life work?', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/when-a-spouse-is-posted-abroad/', 'snippet': 'Military duty in particular — but also other professions that require people to travel a lot or work away from home for long periods of time— can put serious strains on marriages and family life. If you or your spouse is in such a role, how do you...', 'lead_paragraph': '7:07 p.m. | Updated David H. Petraeus and his wife, Holly, and their two grown children had “long been viewed by military families as an inspiration, a model for making a marriage work despite the separation and hardship of long deployments overseas,” write Scott Shane and Sheryl Gay Stolberg in an article about the rise and fall of Gen. Petraeus, who resigned as director of the Central Intelligence Agency on Friday after admitting to an extramarital affair. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/12rdv-expat/12rdv-expat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/12rdv-expat/12rdv-expat-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1343, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When a Spouse Is Posted Abroad', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petraeus, David H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T16:01:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/448d57ad-3c3d-5b70-8c3e-b44a1f09d7a4', 'word_count': 3