}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a800894-9686-501e-827e-4f099ddf9410', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a800894-9686-501e-827e-4f099ddf9410'}, {'abstract': 'As an ant starts a trip across a rubber band, the band begins to stretch. Will the ant ever reach the other end?', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/ant/', 'snippet': 'As an ant starts a trip across a rubber band, the band begins to stretch. Will the ant ever reach the other end?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our puzzle this week comes from a frequent contributor, Marco Moriconi, who has this to say about the challenge:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ant on a Rubber Band Puzzle', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T17:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3da7974-1f8e-5b10-8d25-45d1561622e7', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3da7974-1f8e-5b10-8d25-45d1561622e7'}, {'abstract': 'The 88-year-old speakeasy that closed this year is being reopened as an elegant restaurant and bar.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/bills-begins-its-new-life-in-a-week/', 'snippet': 'The 88-year-old speakeasy that closed this year is being reopened as an elegant restaurant and bar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John DeLucie has a penchant for renovating venerable restaurant locations, including the Lion in Greenwich Village, and the town house on East 81st Street that has become Crown. Now, having taken over what was Bill’s Gay Nineties — the 88-year-old speakeasy that closed this year — he has taken an elegant dark paintbrush to the paneled walls in the ground-floor bar, the second-floor dining room and the third-floor private room. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill’s Begins Its New Life Next Monday', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeLucie, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Bill's (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T17:07:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bf2f70f-595a-5671-ae12-54ac36a0d126', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bf2f70f-595a-5671-ae12-54ac36a0d126'}, {'abstract': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/walkabout-1112-fewer-planes-in-spain-and-captains-aboard/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spanish Airline Shrinks The parent company of Iberia announced a sweeping restructuring that will eliminate at least 4,500 jobs and cut capacity by 15 percent. (New York Times)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walkabout — 11/12: Fewer Planes in Spain and Captains Aboard', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T17:10:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1414cda-2b07-5ddc-8996-4869f4769ede', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1414cda-2b07-5ddc-8996-4869f4769ede'}, {'abstract': 'In many of the states where the campaigns focused most of their attention, more people voted than in 2008. Turnout is likely to have declined in many non-battleground states, however.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/turnout-steady-in-swing-states-and-down-in-others-but-many-votes-remain-uncounted/', 'snippet': 'In many of the states where the campaigns focused most of their attention, more people voted than in 2008. Turnout is likely to have declined in many non-battleground states, however.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Initial accounts of last Tuesday’s presidential election contemplated what seemed to be a significant decline in turnout from 2008. Those reports may have been premature, at least in part. Some states, particularly those where much balloting is conducted by mail, have yet to finish counting their returns. It is likely that there are several million votes left to be counted in California, for example. Nonetheless, it seems probable that we will see something of a split in the number of people who turned out to vote in 2012.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turnout Steady in Swing States and Down in Others, But Many Votes Remain Uncounted', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T17:15:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9584c6a2-ffc8-55e1-b035-f952f11824f7', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9584c6a2-ffc8-55e1-b035-f952f11824f7'}, {'abstract': 'Every fall, Well goes vegetarian, offering delicious no-meat recipes for your holiday table from some of your favorite chefs and cookbook authors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/11/12/health/20121111_vegetarian-thanksgiving.html', 'snippet': 'Every fall, Well goes vegetarian, offering delicious no-meat recipes for your holiday table from some of your favorite chefs and cookbook authors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every fall, Well goes vegetarian, offering delicious no-meat recipes for your holiday table from some of your favorite chefs and cookbook authors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/health/well_veggie_food/well_veggie_food-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 256, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/health/well_veggie_food/well_veggie_food-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 256, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/health/well_veggie_food/well_veggie_food-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/21/health/well_veggie_foo