akes he made in trying to manage stars’ egos while with the Knicks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/sports/basketball/mike-dantoni-is-not-in-phoenix-anymore.html', 'snippet': 'Mike D’Antoni, who will be the Lakers’ new coach, will face the challenge of learning from mistakes he made in trying to manage stars’ egos while with the Knicks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mike D’Antoni resigned from the Knicks eight months ago, after an apparent work slowdown by Carmelo Anthony, it was easy to dump all the blame on Anthony for not being on board with the emergence of Jeremy Lin.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/sports/basketball/13araton-pic/13araton-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/13/sports/basketball/13araton-pic/13araton-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/sports/basketball/13araton-pic/13araton-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/sports/basketball/13araton-pic/13araton-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1526, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/sports/basketball/13araton-pic/13araton-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/13/sports/basketball/13araton-pic/13araton-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/sports/basketball/13araton-pic/13araton-pic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'D’Antoni Is Not in Phoenix Anymore', 'kicker': 'On Basketball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Coach’s Adjustments Must Start From Within', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Lakers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "D'Antoni, Mike", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T17:37:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/306316e9-b5e0-5c33-acbe-1dcef5c08811', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/306316e9-b5e0-5c33-acbe-1dcef5c08811'}, {'abstract': 'A video message from Malala Yousafzai’s father, Ziauddin, released by the hospital in Birmingham, England, where she is recovering, includes footage of the young activist.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/malala-yousafzais-father-thanks-supporters-from-her-hospital-room/', 'snippet': 'A video message from Malala Yousafzai’s father, Ziauddin, released by the hospital in Birmingham, England, where she is recovering, includes footage of the young activist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ziauddin Yousafzai, the Pakistani educator whose 15-year-old daughter, Malala, survived an assassination attempt by Taliban militants, thanked “all peace-loving well-wishers,” for their support in a video statement released on Monday by the hospital in England where she is recovering. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistani Girl’s Father Thanks Supporters From Her Hospital Room', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yousafzai, Malala', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T17:39:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5dcdb1f-7464-5bd7-aff0-4f5bf3eaf754', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5dcdb1f-7464-5bd7-aff0-4f5bf3eaf754'}, {'abstract': 'You’re the Boss is looking for businesses who will be affected by the president’s plan to increase taxes on the wealthy.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/will-higher-taxes-affect-small-businesses-you-tell-us/', 'snippet': 'You’re the Boss is looking for businesses who will be affected by the president’s plan to increase taxes on the wealthy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama may have won a decisive reelection victory, but it is John Boehner, the Republican speaker of the House, who is making the rounds and claiming a mandate. And everywhere he goes, he’s talking about what would happen to small businesses if the Bush-era tax cuts on the wealthiest Americans are allowed to expire. To ABC News’s Diane Sawyer, Mr. Boehner said, “Raising taxes on small-business people is the wrong prescription given where our economy is.” He told USA Today, “Raising taxes on small businesses will kill jobs in America. It is as simple as that.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Higher Taxes Affect Small Businesses? You Tell Us', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Research Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T17:44:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8666fdc-2fd9-51ea-a2e8-0bf7a50a0134', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8666fdc-2fd9-51ea-a2e8-0bf7a50a0134'}, {'abstract': 'Checking in on the second annual New York Times Comedy Challenge, where readers can vote on the rising comedian they find the funniest.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/the-comedy-polls-are-open-late/', 'snippet': 'Checking in on the second annual New York Times Comedy Challenge, where readers can vote on the rising comedian they find the funniest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Comedy Festival ended on Sunday, but The New York Times Comedy Challenge is going the distance. We asked six comics to tell us their best, but cleanest, joke and it’s up to you to decide who killed. Leading the vote is Andrew Santino with his lightning-fast riff on a pickup attempt. But only a hundred or so votes separate Mr. Santino, whom you might have seen on “The Office” last week, from Carmen Lynch, who was a semifinalist on the NBC show “Last Comic Standing.” And there are four other rising stars you might find funnier — Kate Berlant, David Agyekum, Jim Tews and Chris Distefano. Vote here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Comedy Polls Are Open Late', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T17:45:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c833bae-03d3-57cc-90ee-0d723ab43193', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c833bae-03d3-57cc-90ee-0d723ab43193'}, {'abstract': 'There was a clear winner in Tuesday’s presidential election, and it was the statisticians who collectively parsed the polls far better than the old-style pundits. But those polls are getting more expensive and less reliable, as the country moves from landlines to cellphones. Are Internet polls the answer?', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/how-cellphones-complicate-polling/', 'snippet': 'There was a clear winner in Tuesday’s presidential election, and it was the statisticians who collectively parsed the polls far better than the old-style pundits. But those polls are getting more expensive and less reliable, as the country moves f...', 'lead_paragraph': ' With this election, math again messed with the magic* in a media stalwart. Television pundits, usually with the authority left over from past political victories, turned out to be inferior seers compared to fast-moving analysts armed with a raft of polling data. The Times’s own Nate Silver appears to be the biggest winner of all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/technology/09bits-polls/09bits-polls-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 286, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/09/technology/09bits-polls/09bits-polls-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 286}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/technology/09bits-polls/09bits-polls-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 306, 'width': 643, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/technology/09bits-polls/09bits-polls-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 306, 'width': 643, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/technology/09bits-polls/09bits-polls-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/09/technology/09bits-polls/09bits-polls-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/technology/09bits-polls/09bits-polls-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Cellphones Complicate Polling', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'c