e lung and colon cancer often don’t realize that chemotherapy will not cure them, a new study finds.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/what-chemo-cant-do/', 'snippet': 'Patients with late-stage lung and colon cancer often don’t realize that chemotherapy will not cure them, a new study finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s start with a simple medical fact: Chemotherapy doesn’t cure people who have very advanced Stage 4 lung or colon cancer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Misunderstanding Chemo', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chemotherapy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colon and Colorectal Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lung Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T17:52:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb82a8dc-dac1-54b3-99f5-ca07982db3bb', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb82a8dc-dac1-54b3-99f5-ca07982db3bb'}, {'abstract': 'Parsons the New School for Design announced plans to reopen a branch in the French capital.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/parsons-to-reestablish-presence-in-paris/', 'snippet': 'Parsons the New School for Design announced plans to reopen a branch in the French capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — When the doors open next fall the Paris campus of Parsons the New School for Design, the program will be both the oldest and newest overseas branch of an American university. Frank Alvah Parsons, the director of what was then known as the New York School of Fine and Applied Art, initiated a Paris program in 1921. (The school was renamed for him in 1941.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parsons to Re-Establish Presence in Paris', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Americans Abroad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Van Zandt, David E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New School for Social Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parsons the New School for Design', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T17:52:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By D. D. Guttenplan', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cee5e3a-963f-54bb-bee0-a8f31f198366', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cee5e3a-963f-54bb-bee0-a8f31f198366'}, {'abstract': 'The latest inquiry of HSBC, one involving accounts in the island tax haven Jersey, raises questions about whether the bank can settle all the investigations it faces at a reasonable price.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/hsbcs-multiplying-legal-issues/', 'snippet': 'The latest inquiry of HSBC, one involving accounts in the island tax haven Jersey, raises questions about whether the bank can settle all the investigations it faces at a reasonable price.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It went from bad to worse for HSBC last week. The bank added $800 million to its reserves to help address potential money-laundering charges. And it is also confronting more trouble after a whistle-blower pointed to questionable accounts at its subsidiary in Jersey, a tax haven. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'HSBC’s Multiplying Legal Issues', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Money Laundering', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HSBC Holdings PLC.', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T17:53:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2f73d45-9f04-564e-b028-021d535f0519', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2f73d45-9f04-564e-b028-021d535f0519'}, {'abstract': 'For years, a Michigan inmate gathered evidence he said cast doubt on his murder conviction, but there is no assurance that he will be able to present it in court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/us/post-trial-evidence-is-issue-in-supreme-court-case.html', 'snippet': 'For years, a Michigan inmate gathered evidence he said cast doubt on his murder conviction, but there is no assurance that he will be able to present it in court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Supreme Court has a complicated relationship with evidence of innocence that arrives late in the game.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Case Asks When New Evidence Means a New Trial', 'kicker': 'Sidebar', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Question for Justices: When Does New Evidence Require a New Trial?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mich