.com/2012/11/13/sports/erik-weihenmayer-a-blind-adventurer-prepares-to-challenge-colorado-river-in-a-kayak.html', 'snippet': 'Erik Weihenmayer, the first person without sight to summit Mount Everest, will next attempt to descend the Colorado River through the Grand Canyon in a kayak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. — Erik Weihenmayer stood on a concrete berm above a gushing crest of white water and cocked his head slightly. “Sounds gnar,” he said. He was referring to the ear-bone-rattling roar surrounding him, the sound of 536,000 gallons of water spewing each second through six industrial pumps at the U.S. National Whitewater Center. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/13kayak-cnd/11132012Kayak-slide-G21Q-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/13kayak-cnd/11132012Kayak-slide-G21Q-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/13kayak-cnd/11132012Kayak-slide-G21Q-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/13kayak-cnd/11132012Kayak-slide-G21Q-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1389, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/13kayak-cnd/13kayak-cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/13kayak-cnd/13kayak-cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/13kayak-cnd/13kayak-cnd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blind Adventurer Trains for His Scariest Challenge Yet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paddling Blind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weihenmayer, Erik', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blindness', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kayaks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado River', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Grand Canyon (Ariz)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T18:11:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Olsen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d418b36-8d75-52c4-9bf7-d9b9ae42330a', 'word_count': 1108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d418b36-8d75-52c4-9bf7-d9b9ae42330a'}, {'abstract': 'If you’re searching for a meatless main dish that will please a crowd, skip the processed turkey substitutes and consider a hearty dish with the rich flavors and textures of Greek cuisine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/health/giant-beans-with-spinach-tomatoes-and-feta-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'If you’re searching for a meatless main dish that will please a crowd, skip the processed turkey substitutes and consider a hearty dish with the rich flavors and textures of Greek cuisine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The recent feature\xa0 in The New York Times Magazine about Ikaria, the island in Greece renowned for the longevity of its population, brought back wonderful memories of a two-week stay on that island, where I studied its cuisine and the cuisines of many of the other regions of Greece with the prolific Greek-American food writer Diane Kochilas. Diane’s family comes from Ikaria. She was born and raised in Queens, but during one of her many summer stays on the familial island, she fell in love with an Ikarian artist and photographer, Vassilis Stenos (you can see his amazing photography in her latest book, “The Country Cooking of Greece”), and eventually she moved to Greece. She and her family divide their time between Athens and Ikaria, and Diane spends a lot of time in New York, where she is the consulting chef at the Greek restaurants Boukies and Pylos. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/12recipehealth/12recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/13/science/12recipehealth/12recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/12recipehealth/12recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/12recipehealth/12recipehealth-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/12recipehealth/12recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/13/science/12recipehealth/12recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/12recipehealth/12recipehealth-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Thanksgiving, Why Not Go Greek?', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T18:11:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea359808-55a2-5acb-be88-c7447f221232', 'word_count': 913, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea359808-55a2-5acb-be88-c7447f221232'}, {'abstract': 'Law enforcement officials and legal experts said the citizen complaint about unwanted e-mails was handled “on the merits” but that it was more intriguing because the e-mails showed an inside knowledge of the C.I.A. director’s activities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/us/timeline-shows-fbi-discovered-petraeus-affair-in-summer.html', 'snippet': 'Law enforcement officials and legal experts said the citizen complaint about unwanted e-mails was handled “on the merits” but that it was more intriguing because the e-mails showed an inside knowledge of the C.I.A. director’s activities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Is a string of angry e-mails really enough, in an age of boisterous online exchanges, to persuade the F.B.I. to open a cyberstalking investigation?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/world/PETRAEUS/PETRAEUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/world/PETRAEUS/PETRAEUS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1475, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/world/PETRAEUS/PETRAEUS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Motives Questioned in F.B.I. Inquiry of Petraeus E-Mails', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.B.I. Inquiry Into E-Mails Raises Questions on Motives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petraeus, David H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelley, Jill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broadwell, Paula', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULTERY', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T18:16:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane and Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5efff39-da2f-5e70-80d0-218b06a26239', 'word_count': 1103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5efff39-da2f-5e70-80d0-218b06a26239'}, {'abstract': 'The Times reported thoroughly on its incoming president and chief executive without producing a smoking gun.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/as-mark-thompson-starts-new-job-the-bbcs-implosion-is-felt-in-new-york/', 'snippet': 'The Times reported thoroughly on its incoming president and chief executive without producing a smoking gun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mark Thompson started his job on Monday as president and chief executive of The New York Times Company, a British television network was there to capture the moment. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Mark Thompson Starts New Job, the BBC’s Implosion Is Felt in New York', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T18:17:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/258250b4-41a1-5671-a1e8-b6cf95d8ff8e', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/258250b4-41a1-5671-a1e8-b6cf95d8ff8e'}, {'abstract': 'The United States has won re-election to its seat on the U.N. Human Rights Council, a body that can be a critic of Israel but lenient on countries like Sri Lanka, Sudan and Zimbabwe.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/voting-for-u-n-rights-council-puts-focus-on-records-of-panels-member-states/', 'snippet': 'The United States has won re-election to its seat on the U.N. Human Rights Council, a body that can be a critic of Israel but lenient on countries like Sri Lanka, Sudan and Zimbabwe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Those who criticize the United Nations as a toothless and dysfunctional organization often point to the membership of the Human Rights Council to make their case. China, Cuba, Saudi Arabia and Russia all held seats last year. The body has been a vocal and reliable critic of Israel, but has been lenient on countries like Sri Lanka, Sudan and Zimbabwe. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Voting for U.N. Rights Council Puts Focus on Records of Panel’s Member States', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kazakhstan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T18:21:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elias E. Lopez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elias', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Lopez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9ce05a6-0e61-5567-8a8b-0f6c444c5595', 'word_count': 911