umbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/nyregion/12cityroom-eagles/12cityroom-eagles-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/nyregion/12cityroom-eagles/12cityroom-eagles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/13/nyregion/12cityroom-eagles/12cityroom-eagles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/nyregion/12cityroom-eagles/12cityroom-eagles-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Eagle Pushes Students Onto the Stage at the Beacon', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Student Songwriters Pushed by an Eagle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frey, Glenn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eagles, The (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T18:43:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b12ad3d-4f60-5301-ab40-5044ae65088f', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b12ad3d-4f60-5301-ab40-5044ae65088f'}, {'abstract': 'Melissa Clark plans to skip the brine this year, flavoring her turkey with this fiery compound butter.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/hot-chili-butter-brings-flavor-to-the-bird/', 'snippet': 'Melissa Clark plans to skip the brine this year, flavoring her turkey with this fiery compound butter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Melissa Clark will share a Thanksgiving tip, recipe or idea every day until the holiday arrives. Follow @goodappetite on Twitter so you don’t miss a #DailyTGiving tweet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hot Chile Butter Brings Flavor to the Bird', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Turkeys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T18:45:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f537742-d3d4-5e00-b43a-f1ac522440a1', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f537742-d3d4-5e00-b43a-f1ac522440a1'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists have discovered that fairywren mothers teach their unborn chicks a unique begging call to differentiate them from cuckoos invading her nest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/science/australian-fairywren-teaches-chicks-a-password-call.html', 'snippet': 'Scientists have discovered that fairywren mothers teach their unborn chicks a unique begging call to differentiate them from cuckoos invading her nest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some species of cuckoo are known as brood parasites for their devious tactic of laying their eggs in other species’ nests so those birds can care for the cuckoos’ young. Now scientists have discovered that an Australian bird called the fairywren has evolved a way around this tactic: The mothers teach their unborn chicks a unique begging call — a sort of password. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13OBWREN/13OBOX3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13OBWREN/13OBOX3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13OBWREN/13OBWREN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13OBWREN/13OBWREN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13OBWREN/13OBWREN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Birds Learn ‘Password’ to Sing for Their Supper', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Birds Learn ‘Password’ To Sing for Their Supper', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Current Biology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T18:45:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ccdf1f6-50a2-5f1d-bd08-5c4918d20f92', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ccdf1f6-50a2-5f1d-bd08-5c4918d20f92'}, {'abstract': 'Even the Weekly Standard editor wonders why the G.O.P. “is gonna fall on its sword to defend a bunch of millionaires.”', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/bill-kristol-go-ahead-raise-taxes/', 'snippet': 'Even the Weekly Standard editor wonders why the G.O.P. “is gonna fall on its sword to defend a bunch of millionaires.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When even Bill Kristol, the severely conservative Weekly Standard editor, says Republicans should agree to raise taxes on the richest Americans, you have to wonder if the G.O.P. has thought through its post-election, hold-the-line strategy. “It won’t kill the country if Republicans raise taxes a little bit on millionaires,” Mr. Kristol said on Fox News on Sunday. “It really won’t, I don’t think.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Kristol: Go Ahead, Raise Taxes', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cole, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T18:46:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d83f6faf-8089-5a91-a43b-6956eb6ef5b1', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d83f6faf-8089-5a91-a43b-6956eb6ef5b1'}, {'abstract': 'A new campaign, with advertising, marketing and retail elements, seeks to reintroduce the Babar brand to American children and their parents and grandparents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/business/media/this-campaign-wants-us-never-to-forget-babar-the-elephant-king.html', 'snippet': 'A new campaign, with advertising, marketing and retail elements, seeks to reintroduce the Babar brand to American children and their parents and grandparents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Republican Party may have had a tough night last week, but elephants wearing golden crowns will soon be a common sight around the country: Babar, king of the elephants, and his queen, Celeste, are the stars of an elaborate promotional campaign that is now under way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/business/media/13adnewsletter/13adnewsletter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 824, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/business/media/13adnewsletter/13adnewsletter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1663, 'width': 1338, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/business/media/13adnewsletter/13adnewsletter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/13/business/media/13adnewsletter/13adnewsletter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/business/media/13adnewsletter/13adnewsletter-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Coronation for the King of the Elephants', 'kicker': 'Campaign Spotlight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Campaign Wants Us Never to Forget an Elephant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trademarks and Trade Names', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T18:48:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f7e2d7a-464a-54dd-b6c4-f4c46467e215', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f7e2d7a-464a-54dd-b6c4-f4c46467e215'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Peck’s world premiere will replace a previously announced world premiere by the company’s ballet master in chief, Peter Martins.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/a-new-justin-peck-work-for-new-york-city-ballet/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Peck’s world premiere will replace a previously announced world premiere by the company’s ballet master in chief, Peter Martins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Justin Peck, who at 25 is one of the youngest choreographers ever commissioned by the New York City Ballet, is creating a new ballet for the company’s annual “New Combinations Evening” on Jan. 31, the company announced. Mr. Peck’s world premiere, set to “Sinfonietta LaJolla” by the Czech composer Bohuslav Martinu, will replace a previously announced world premiere by the company’s ballet master in chief, Peter Martins.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Justin Peck Work for New York City Ballet', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Justin Peck Work For New York City Ballet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peck, Justin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T18:48:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42af9572-8f4f-5eff-803a-b7a4717a94c8', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42af9572-8f4f-5eff-803a-b7a4717a94c8'}, {'abstract': 'Why not all floating currencies are the same.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/when-confidence-hurts/', 'snippet': 'Why not all floating currencies are the same.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A skeptical correspondent asks whether I really truly believe what I’m saying in my post about how an attack by the bond vigilantes is actually expansionary when you have your own floating currency. How does this jibe with the experience of the Asian financial crisis of the 1980s, he asks? And do I really believe that Japan would be better off if markets became less confident in the value of its bonds?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Confidence Hurts', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T18:51:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e37020e3-29d0-5a04-8a42-9260fe590113', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e37020e3-29d0-5a04-8a42-9260fe590113'}, {'abstract': 'The AdvoCare 500 in Phoenix erupted in a brawl after Jeff Gordon crashed into Clint Bowyer.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/motorsports-monday-keselowski-builds-sprint-cup-lead/', 'snippet': 'The AdvoCare 500 in Phoenix erupted in a brawl after Jeff Gordon crashed into Clint Bowyer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sixth-place finisher Brad Keselowski escaped Sunday’s wild Nascar race at Phoenix, which he described as “borderline ridiculous at times,” with a commanding although not insurmountable lead over Jimmie Johnson, with one race to go in the Chase for the Nascar Sprint Cup championship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Motorsports Monday: Keselowski Builds Sprint Cup Lead', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Motorcycles, Motor Bikes and Motorscooters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nascar Sprint Cup Series', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Jimmie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keselowski, Brad', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N