he diet probably does not help prevent hot flashes and night sweats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many women add soy and fiber to their diet in hopes of preventing the vasomotor symptoms of menopause — hot flashes and night sweats. But a new study suggests it probably does not help.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/health/well_aging/well_aging-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 211, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/health/well_aging/well_aging-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 211, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/health/well_aging/well_aging-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/04/health/well_aging/well_aging-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/health/well_aging/well_aging-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Doubt on Soy and Fiber as Menopause Aid', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vital Signs | Aging: Doubt on Soy and Fiber as Menopause Aid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fiber (Dietary)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Menopause', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soybeans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T19:16:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1d8dbc4-27f1-5539-84df-74198a2643d1', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1d8dbc4-27f1-5539-84df-74198a2643d1'}, {'abstract': 'In 2007, about 1.3 million unemployed adult children were living in their parents’ homes. This year, the total has risen to 2.5 million.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/bundled-households/', 'snippet': 'In 2007, about 1.3 million unemployed adult children were living in their parents’ homes. This year, the total has risen to 2.5 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I wrote on Friday, lots of young Americans are finally moving out of their parents’ basements and forming their own households now that the economy is picking up. But the bundled-household phenomenon remains large, and Mark Zandi, chief economist at Moody’s Analytics, has just shared some interesting data showing its extent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bundled Households', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T19:19:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96099571-8fd5-5ada-bfc3-72efe8af5697', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96099571-8fd5-5ada-bfc3-72efe8af5697'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans: same as they ever were?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/death-by-epistemology/', 'snippet': 'Republicans: same as they ever were?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Josh Marshall is having an interesting discussion — partly with his readers, but also with himself — about the Great Republican Polling Debacle. It seems hard to believe even now, but all the stories indicate that the whole GOP went into last Tuesday in a state of complete delusion. It wasn’t just the Fox News viewers; it wasn’t just the Romney people; the whole party, base and establishment both, believed that it knew a truth hidden from almost every nonpartisan polling outfit, and that a big victory was virtually assured.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death by Epistemology', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T19:19:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/948aa0f1-d11c-525d-b112-c2d535635ad2', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/948aa0f1-d11c-525d-b112-c2d535635ad2'}, {'abstract': 'Nathan Gunn and Kelli O’Hara will play the lovers Billy Bigelow and Julie Jordan in a new staged production of the Rodgers and Hammerstein musical for the New York Philharmonic. The cast will also feature Stephanie Blythe as Nettie Fowler and Alexander Gemignani as Enoch Snow.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/new-york-philharmonic-finds-its-stars-for-carousel/', 'snippet': 'Nathan Gunn and Kelli O’Hara will play the lovers Billy Bigelow and Julie Jordan in a new staged production of the Rodgers and Hammerstein musical for the New York Philharmonic. The cast will also feature Stephanie Blythe as Nettie Fowler and Alex...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kelli O’Hara and Nathan Gunn will be among the latest stars to take a spin on the Rodgers and Hammerstein musical “Carousel” in a new staged production for the New York Philharmonic, it was announced on Monday. The Philharmonic said that Mr. Gunn, the baritone, and Ms. O’Hara, the star of Broadway musicals like “Nice Work If You Can Get It” and “South Pacific,” will play the carousel barker Billy Bigelow and his lover, Julie Jordan; the cast will also feature Stephanie Blythe, the mezzo-soprano, in the role of Nettie Fowler, and Alexander Gemignani (of “Les Misérables” and “Sweeney Todd”) as Enoch Snow.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Philharmonic Finds Its Stars for ‘Carousel’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'O’Hara and Gunn To Star in ‘Carousel’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blythe, Stephanie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Rob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gemignani, Alexander', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gunn, Nathan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hammerstein, Oscar II', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Hara, Kelli", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rando, John', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodgers, Richard', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 11, 