thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/dining/14TURKEY/14TURKEY-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jacques Pépin’s Steam-Powered Turkey', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Tricks? No Sweat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Turkeys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pepin, Jacques', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T19:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Gordinier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordinier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e512ab06-c186-5ce4-9e72-4d6ad748ce0a', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e512ab06-c186-5ce4-9e72-4d6ad748ce0a'}, {'abstract': 'For the French master chef Jacques Pépin, the fourth Thursday in November is a gourmand holiday, and the food has to be plentiful and bountiful, with all the marvelous products of the fall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/dining/jacques-pepins-thanksgiving-love-story.html', 'snippet': 'For the French master chef Jacques Pépin, the fourth Thursday in November is a gourmand holiday, and the food has to be plentiful and bountiful, with all the marvelous products of the fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I ARRIVED in New York in September 1959, ready to conquer this exciting and exhilarating new world after working for several years in the classic restaurants of Paris. Within 48 hours, I had landed a job as the sauce chef at the venerable Pavillon, a temple of haute cuisine on 57th Street and Park Avenue, where Pierre Franey was the chef. And just two months later, I was introduced to the lore and traditions of Thanksgiving at Pierre and Betty Franey’s home on Long Island.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Thanksgiving Love Story', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Thanksgiving Love Story', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T19:31:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacques Pépin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacques', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pépin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/334a8994-6492-55dc-b970-4b6cc84279d9', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/334a8994-6492-55dc-b970-4b6cc84279d9'}, {'abstract': 'Capitol Records is promoting the release of new vinyl versions of the Beatles’ music with pop-up stores in New York and Los Angeles.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/pop-up-stores-to-offer-beatles-vinyl-reissues/', 'snippet': 'Capitol Records is promoting the release of new vinyl versions of the Beatles’ music with pop-up stores in New York and Los Angeles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The reissue of the Beatles’ original albums on vinyl, on Tuesday, restores the music to the 12-inch LP format that thrived when the discs were first released, between 1963 and 1970. But one crucial thing has changed: back in the day, one of the joys of collecting was turning up at a record shop the day a new album was released and getting your hands on a fresh, shrink-wrapped copy. But now brick and mortar record stores are few and far between.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/12artsbeat-beatles/12artsbeat-beatles-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/12artsbeat-beatles/12artsbeat-beatles-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2047, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/12artsbeat-beatles/12artsbeat-beatles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/12artsbeat-beatles/12artsbeat-beatles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/12artsbeat-beatles/12artsbeat-beatles-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pop-Up Stores to Offer Beatles’ Vinyl Reissues', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop-Up Stores and Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beatles, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Capitol Records', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T19:33:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b40d18f-3baf-50f2-bb37-8f94787f123a', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b40d18f-3baf-50f2-bb37-8f94787f123a'}, {'abstract': 'A new annotated and illustrated edition of James Watson’s book “The Double Helix” adds interesting details about the rivalries in the race to decode the structure of DNA.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/science/the-double-helix-review-twists-in-the-tale-of-the-great-dna-discovery.html', 'snippet': 'A new annotated and illustrated edition of James Watson’s book “The Double Helix” adds interesting details about the rivalries in the race to decode the structure of DNA.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anyone seeking to understand modern biology and genomics could do much worse than start with the discovery of the structure of DNA, on which almost everything else is based. The classic account of the discovery, “The Double Helix,” by James D. Watson, was first published in 1968 and has now been reissued in an annotated and illustrated edition.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13BOOKS/13SCIB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1023, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13BOOKS/13SCIB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2045, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Twists in the Tale of the Great DNA Discovery', 'kicker': 'Books on Science', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Twists in the Tale of the Great DNA Discovery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watson, James D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crick, Francis H C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T19:35:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Wade', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wade', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c89c8b9-7013-5f91-bc8f-2998a698de20', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c89c8b9-7013-5f91-bc8f-2998a698de20'}, {'abstract': 'In countries around the world, text-message traffic has been shrinking because Internet-powered alternatives are becoming so widely used. American carriers have fought off the decline — until now. For the first time, the American wireless market saw a decline in messages sent, according to a report by an independent mobile analyst.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/text-messaging-declines-united-states/', 'snippet': 'In countries around the world, text-message traffic has been shrinking because Internet-powered alternatives are becoming so widely used. American carriers have fought off the decline — until now. For the first time, the American wireless market s...', 'lead_paragraph': '3:21 p.m. | Updated Adding text-messaging statistics among corporate customers. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/technology/12bits-texting/12bits-texting-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/technology/12bits-texting/12bits-texting-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/technology/12bits-texting/12bits-texting-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/12/technology/12bits-texting/12bits-texting-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/technology/12bits-texting/12bits-texting-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Text Messaging Declines in U.S. for First Time, Report Says', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Text Messaging\r\nSlips in U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T19:36:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f550bf49-ba06-5b9e-9138-5f7697d94678', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f550bf49-ba06-5b9e-9138-5f7697d94678'}, {'abstract': 'Congress may get a push from the courts to decide whether a site in the Nevada desert is suitable.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/will-a-lame-duck-congress-confront-nuclear-waste/', 'snippet': 'Congress may get a push from the courts to decide whether a site in the Nevada desert is suitable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Congress returns to Washington on Tuesday, it has a very long “to do” list. One item, probably not near the top, is figuring out what to do with nuclear waste, given that President Obama killed a proposed repository in Nevada in March 2010. This summer, a blue-ribbon commission advised that the process of seeking a storage site be restarted. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will a Lame Duck Congress Confront Nuclear Waste?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Wastes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nuclear Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yucca Mountain (Nev)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T19:49:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'sect