tes who survived the tsunami last year wrote essays about the disaster and the healing power of sports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the once-in-a-millennium tsunami struck northeastern Japan on March 11, 2011, it killed thousands of people and destroyed vast stretches of a rugged coastline. As the survivors in Fukushima, Miyagi and Iwate Prefectures started putting their lives back together, they came to rely on each other more than ever.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/belson1/belson1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/belson1/belson1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/belson1/belson1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/belson1/belson1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/belson1/belson1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/belson1/belson1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/sports/belson1/belson1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Tsunami, Grief and the Joy of Basketball', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Tsunami, Grief and the Joy of Basketball', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T20:37:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1116d4f-562a-5bed-8fb1-64853c3dc0b4', 'word_count': 1275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1116d4f-562a-5bed-8fb1-64853c3dc0b4'}, {'abstract': 'The Anschutz Entertainment Group, a major sports and concert company that operates more than 100 sites, has agreed to have StubHub operate its resale market. Also, a study finds that record labels have continued to invest in new talent.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/digital-notes-new-deal-gives-stubhub-a-greater-role-in-concert-sales/', 'snippet': 'The Anschutz Entertainment Group, a major sports and concert company that operates more than 100 sites, has agreed to have StubHub operate its resale market. Also, a study finds that record labels have continued to invest in new talent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the latest sign that ticket scalping has gone mainstream, the Anschutz Entertainment Group, a major sports and concert company that operates more than 100 sites and arenas around the world, has agreed to have StubHub become the resale market for many of its events, the companies said on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Digital Notes: New Deal Gives StubHub a Greater Role in Concert Sales', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ticket Scalping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANSCHUTZ ENTERTAINMENT GROUP', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'eBay Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of the Phonographic Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Live Nation Entertainment Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'StubHub', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ticketmaster', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T20:41:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/159d182b-7be4-5b2f-a2ef-4016249d2721', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/159d182b-7be4-5b2f-a2ef-4016249d2721'}, {'abstract': 'Randall Sullivan’s “Untouchable” chronicles Michael Jackson’s over-the-top fame in a book that feels as though it was constructed out of recycled materials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/books/untouchable-michael-jacksons-life-by-randall-sullivan.html', 'snippet': 'Randall Sullivan’s “Untouchable” chronicles Michael Jackson’s over-the-top fame in a book that feels as though it was constructed out of recycled materials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He was the consummate performer, the ultimate showman. The creator of the biggest-selling album of all time, who three decades ago crashed through racial barriers on the music charts, ushered in the music video age and remade the pop music landscape. A song-and-dance man who took soul, funk, R&B, rock and disco and turned them into a sound distinctively his own, just as seamlessly as he drew upon the work of James Brown, Jackie Wilson and Fred Astaire to create otherworldly dance moves never before seen on this planet. An entertainer who would imprint the imaginations of several generations of fans and shape the work of performers from Justin Timberlake to Beyoncé to Usher. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 757, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/book/book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1514, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/book/book-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Just In: He Was the King of Pop', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Just In: He Was the King of Pop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Untouchable: The Strange Life and Tragic Death of Michael Jackson (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Randall', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T20:43:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b604dc13-513f-5c59-b4b0-373c5cb885fc', 'word_count': 1231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b604dc13-513f-5c59-b4b0-373c5cb885fc'}, {'abstract': 'Hunting tools from 71,000 years ago found in South Africa suggest modern humans with a well-developed capacity for abstract thought and a grasp of complex technologies, a new study concludes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/science/evidence-of-persistent-modern-human-behavior-in-africa.html', 'snippet': 'Hunting tools from 71,000 years ago found in South Africa suggest modern humans with a well-developed capacity for abstract thought and a grasp of complex technologies, a new study concludes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a rock shelter on a coastal cliff in South Africa, scientists have found an abundance of advanced stone hunting tools with a tale to tell of the evolving mind of early modern humans at least 71,000 years ago.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13TOOL1_SPAN/13TOOL1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarg