ions', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T21:03:07+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'Mac William Bishop, Channon Hodge and Pedro Rosado', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mac', 'middlename': 'William', 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Channon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Pedro', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosado', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/7ac6d4bc-1b4e-5b97-8eb0-6b1ab4bb7472', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/7ac6d4bc-1b4e-5b97-8eb0-6b1ab4bb7472'}, {'abstract': 'Pinchas Zukerman and Edo de Waart will play with St. Paul Chamber Orchestra and Minnesota Orchestra, respectively, as the ensembles find themselves locked in a bitter lockout.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/classical-music-big-names-head-to-twin-cities-amid-contract-disputes/', 'snippet': 'Pinchas Zukerman and Edo de Waart will play with St. Paul Chamber Orchestra and Minnesota Orchestra, respectively, as the ensembles find themselves locked in a bitter lockout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pinchas Zukerman and the St. Paul Chamber Orchestra? Edo de Waart and the Minnesota Orchestra? For followers of these two fine ensembles in the Twin Cities, the pairings echo clearly. Mr. Zukerman used to be music director of the chamber orchestra and Mr. de Waart held the same position at the Minnesota ensemble. And both men will soon be back their former podiums, but this time as bit players in labor battles. The managements of the two orchestras have locked out the musicians amid bitter contract disputes and cancelled concerts through the end of the year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Classical Music Big Names Head to Twin Cities Amid Contract Disputes', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Waart, Edo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zukerman, Pinchas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Orchestra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Paul Chamber Orchestra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T21:11:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d478811f-7c57-565b-9ac5-287478302ed1', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d478811f-7c57-565b-9ac5-287478302ed1'}, {'abstract': 'Celebrating the Hindu festival of lights.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/happy-diwali/', 'snippet': 'Celebrating the Hindu festival of lights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Diwali, the Hindu festival of lights, is celebrated by hundreds of millions of people in India and tens of millions more around the world on November 13. India Ink wishes you and your family a Happy Diwali. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Happy Diwali!', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diwali (Hindu Festival)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T21:14:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_