person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maynard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f1470c3-e92b-58bc-bd6c-3c83e4f57843', 'word_count': 2674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f1470c3-e92b-58bc-bd6c-3c83e4f57843'}, {'abstract': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Monday’s selection includes Amazon Web Services expanding in Australia, YouTube preparing to renew its financing for some of its programming and police in Belize saying they want to talk to John McAfee of antivirus fame about a homicide.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/todays-scuttlebot-police-hunt-mcafee-and-youtube-shows/', 'snippet': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Monday’s selection includes Amazon Web Services expanding in Australia, YouTube preparing to renew its financing for some of its programming...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently. See more here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Police Hunt McAfee, and YouTube Shows', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T22:03:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7737ca3-a8f3-522d-8f5f-fc61482f73b1', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7737ca3-a8f3-522d-8f5f-fc61482f73b1'}, {'abstract': 'Though observers feared the worst after Hurricane Sandy, biologists say there is remarkably little evidence that birds suffered mass casualties.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/science/birds-have-natural-ability-to-survive-storms.html', 'snippet': 'Though observers feared the worst after Hurricane Sandy, biologists say there is remarkably little evidence that birds suffered mass casualties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the wake of Hurricane Sandy and the spiteful me-too northeaster, much of the East Coast looked so battered and flooded, so strewed with toppled trees and stripped of dunes and beaches, that many observers feared the worst. Any day now, surely, the wildlife corpses would start showing up — especially birds, for who likelier to pay when a sky turns rogue than the ones who act as if they own it?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13ANGI_SPAN/13ANGI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 279, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13ANGI_SPAN/13ANGI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 279}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13ANGI_SPAN/13ANGI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13ANGI_SPAN/13ANGI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13ANGI_SPAN/13ANGI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13ANGI_SPAN/13ANGI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13ANGI_SPAN/13ANGI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Birds, Storm Survival Is Only Natural', 'kicker': 'Basics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Birds, Storm Survival Is Only Natural', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Migration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T22:03:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalie Angier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Angier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3afc532e-fbe0-5ce2-aa07-ac915884494e', 'word_count': 1420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3afc532e-fbe0-5ce2-aa07-ac915884494e'}, {'abstract': 'History presents a 12-hour mini-series, “Mankind: The Story of All of Us,” which uses figures from the academic and popular-culture fields to trace human history, with an emphasis on warfare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/arts/television/mankind-the-story-of-all-of-us-on-history.html', 'snippet': 'History presents a 12-hour mini-series, “Mankind: The Story of All of Us,” which uses figures from the academic and popular-culture fields to trace human history, with an emphasis on warfare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you run a documentary-oriented television channel, apparently you are periodically overcome with an irresistible urge to go for the everything program: a program, usually a mini-series, that tries to capture the totality of an impossibly big subject. The BBC and the Discovery Channel had the acclaimed “Planet Earth,” followed a few years later by “Life.” The National Geographic Channel has had projects like the sumptuous “Great Migrations.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/mankind/mankind-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/mankind/mankind-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/mankind/mankind-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {