sCast Media+Tech: When Memes Become Reality TV', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T22:15:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b8c447b-31fc-5635-af49-7bf222915317', 'word_count': 28, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b8c447b-31fc-5635-af49-7bf222915317'}, {'abstract': 'The governor said utility companies had restored power to almost all intact homes, but when a home is damaged, it is dangerous to introduce electricity.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/cuomo-says-most-homes-still-without-power-are-too-damaged-for-electricity/', 'snippet': 'The governor said utility companies had restored power to almost all intact homes, but when a home is damaged, it is dangerous to introduce electricity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While about 80,000 homes in New York remain without power, most are dark because they are damaged and utilities cannot safely restore power to them — not because of any delays on the utilities’ part, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo said Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo Says Most Homes Still Without Power Are Too Damaged for Electricity', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T22:17:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce538887-9530-5304-9a15-a616ce65aad4', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce538887-9530-5304-9a15-a616ce65aad4'}, {'abstract': 'A team of social scientists gave advice on how to counter rumors, portray rivals effectively and get out the vote.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/health/dream-team-of-behavioral-scientists-advised-obama-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'A team of social scientists gave advice on how to counter rumors, portray rivals effectively and get out the vote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late last year Matthew Barzun, an official with the Obama campaign, called Craig Fox, a psychologist in Los Angeles, and invited him to a political planning meeting in Chicago, according to two people who attended the session.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13PSYC_SPAN/13PSYC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13PSYC_SPAN/13PSYC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13PSYC_SPAN/13PSYC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/science/13PSYC_SPAN/13PSYC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1384, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption