ges his works in Washington with her troupe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Every season of the Suzanne Farrell Ballet is also a season about George Balanchine. Suzanne Farrell, who danced from the 1960s to the 1980s, was that choreographer’s most celebrated muse. Her company has presented annual seasons at the Kennedy Center here since 2001. In these, she never ceases to address diverse facets of her master’s genius, reviving different — often rare — ballets every year. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/altFARRELL/altFARRELL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/altFARRELL/altFARRELL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1401, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/altFARRELL/altFARRELL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/altFARRELL/altFARRELL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/altFARRELL/altFARRELL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Staging Balanchine Classics as His Muse Provides a Link to the Source', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Staging Balanchine Classics as His Muse Provides a Link to the Source', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Farrell, Suzanne, Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T23:09:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/36bd248b-8b91-520c-a64d-bb7b883c7a8e', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36bd248b-8b91-520c-a64d-bb7b883c7a8e'}, {'abstract': 'Susanne Daniels previously worked at Lifetime, where she presided over hits like “Army Wives” and the WB network, which had culture-defining hits like “Buffy the Vampire Slayer” and “Gilmore Girls.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/mtv-hires-new-president-of-programming/', 'snippet': 'Susanne Daniels previously worked at Lifetime, where she presided over hits like “Army Wives” and the WB network, which had culture-defining hits like “Buffy the Vampire Slayer” and “Gilmore Girls.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'MTV made a significant management change Monday, naming Susanne Daniels, an experienced television executive, to the position of president of programming.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'MTV Hires New President of Programming', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daniels, Susanne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Toffler, Van', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lifetime Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WB Television Network', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T23:11:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66af0669-b420-556a-beef-23f52e80816e', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66af0669-b420-556a-beef-23f52e80816e'}, {'abstract': 'Larry Lederman, author of “Magnificent Trees of the New York Botanical Garden,” returned to the garden last week to see how the trees had fared after Hurricane Sandy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/garden/evaluating-a-storms-damage-to-a-beloved-garden.html', 'snippet': 'Larry Lederman, author of “Magnificent Trees of the New York Botanical Garden,” returned to the garden last week to see how the trees had fared after Hurricane Sandy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHILE Larry Lederman was working on his book, “Magnificent Trees of the New York Botanical Garden,” published by Monacelli Press, he spent years traversing the 50-acre forest along the banks of the Bronx River. Mr. Lederman returned to the garden last week, to see how his beloved trees had survived Hurricane Sandy. Accompanied by Todd Forrest, vice president of horticulture at the garden, and co-author of the book, he walked through the cultivated grounds of the garden, and through the native Thain Family Forest. Mr. Lederman, a lawyer by training and a photographer by passion, talked to a reporter about his visit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/garden/12qnapic/12qnapic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 765, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/garden/12qnapic/12qnapic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1296, 'width': 968, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/garden/12qnapic/12qnapic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/12/garden/12qnapic/12qnapic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/garden/12qnapic/12qnapic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Evaluating a Storm’s Damage to a Beloved Garden', 'kicker': 'Currents | Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Botanical Garden', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lederman, Larry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T23:19:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maria Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e95924b-1619-5456-a570-f21ad6f5dad1', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e95924b-1619-5456-a570-f21ad6f5dad1'}, {'abstract': 'Jamie Moyer, Vinny Testaverde and a prince all get older this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/booming/long-playing-athletes-and-other-boomer-birthdays.html', 'snippet': 'Jamie Moyer, Vinny Testaverde and a prince all get older this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, three great athletes have birthdays, two who made the most of their skills and one who underperformed much of his career. Plus a man who has waited 64 years so far to be king and a politician who may be under more pressure than anyone else in Washington at the moment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Long-Playing Athletes and Other Boomer Birthdays', 'kicker': 'One Year Older', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Testaverde, Vinny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Charles, Prince of Wales', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T23:24:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Winerip', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winerip', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e3e83aa-be3e-53d6-8a70-e1f99bfdb52c', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e3e83aa-be3e-53d6-8a70-e1f99bfdb52c'}, {'abstract': 'The total death toll from the storm is at least 119; causes have included drowning, hypothermia and injuries from falling trees.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/storms-death-toll-climbs-in-new-jersey/', 'snippet': 'The total death toll from the storm is at least 119; causes have included drowning, hypothermia and injuries from falling trees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The death toll in New Jersey from Hurricane Sandy has climbed to 33, The Associated Press reported on Monday, citing information from the New Jersey State Police. A week earlier, the count stood at 23. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Storm’s Death Toll Climbs in New Jersey', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-12T23:27:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f26fb99-78e6-5a7a-ac9d-24ae26f8a365', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f26fb99-78e6-5a7a-ac9d-24ae26f8a365'}, {'abstract': 'Alexandra Wallace, a senior vice president of NBC News, will be the first woman ever put in charge of “Today,” the longtime first-place morning show that slid to second place this year.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/nbc-moves-to-shake-up-today-leadership/', 'snippet': 'Alexandra Wallace, a senior vice president of NBC News, will be the first woman ever put in charge of “Today,” the longtime first-place morning show that slid to second place this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NBC is completing a plan to change the leadership at the “Today” show, the longtime first-place morning show that slid to second place this year during the controversial removal of Ann Curry.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NBC Moves to Shake Up ‘Today’ Le