ct', 'value': 'Tutors and Tutoring', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T01:17:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff1973d0-8104-597d-9339-f627a17d0afe', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff1973d0-8104-597d-9339-f627a17d0afe'}, {'abstract': 'A new group of militant Irish nationalists calling themselves “the I.R.A.” has claimed responsibility for killing a prison officer in Northern Ireland on Nov. 1.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/world/europe/northern-ireland-group-says-it-killed-prison-officer.html', 'snippet': 'A new group of militant Irish nationalists calling themselves “the I.R.A.” has claimed responsibility for killing a prison officer in Northern Ireland on Nov. 1.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A new group of militant Irish nationalists calling themselves “the I.R.A.” has claimed responsibility for killing a prison officer in Northern Ireland on Nov. 1. In a statement sent Monday to The Irish News, a Belfast-based newspaper, the group said the shooting was linked to a dispute over conditions inside Maghaberry Prison, where 41 dissident republicans now being held object to strip-searches by guards. The group, which claims to be the legitimate successor to the disbanded Irish Republican Army, said an “active service unit of the I.R.A. executed” the guard, David Black, 52, “to protect and defend” jailed militants. After Mr. Black’s death, the police arrested and questioned four men but all have been released without charges. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Northern Ireland: Group Says It Killed Prison Officer', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Northern Ireland: Group Says It Killed Prison Officer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belfast (Northern Ireland)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Irish Republican Army', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northern Ireland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T01:21:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Dalby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dalby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c0dc4fe-84f9-5e9b-93a3-ae17c2a7ab0e', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c0dc4fe-84f9-5e9b-93a3-ae17c2a7ab0e'}, {'abstract': 'Buoyed by victories in four states, advocates of same-sex-marriage rights plan to press their cause in Delaware, Hawaii, Illinois, Rhode Island, Minnesota, New Jersey and Oregon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/us/advocates-of-gay-marriage-extend-their-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'Buoyed by victories in four states, advocates of same-sex-marriage rights plan to press their cause in Delaware, Hawaii, Illinois, Rhode Island, Minnesota, New Jersey and Oregon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORTLAND, Me. — Elated by their first ballot victories, in four states, advocates of same-sex marriage rights plan to push legislatures in half a dozen more states toward legalization as they also press their cause in federal courts. They are also preparing for what they hope will be another milestone: the electoral reversal of a constitutional amendment defining marriage as solely between a man and a woman, in Oregon in 2014.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/us/jp-SAMESEX-1/jp-SAMESEX-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/13/us/jp-SAMESEX-1/jp-SAMESEX-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/us/jp-SAMESEX-1/jp-SAMESEX-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/us/jp-SAMESEX-1/jp-SAMESEX-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/us/jp-SAMESEX-1/jp-SAMESEX-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Push Expands for Legalizing Same-Sex Marriage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Push Expands For Legalizing Gay Marriage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T01:21:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm',