ation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Valerie Eliot, who married the poet T. S. Eliot near the end of his life and steadfastly guarded his literary legacy for nearly half a century, died on Friday in London. She was 86.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/ELIOT-obit/ELIOT-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/ELIOT-obit/ELIOT-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/ELIOT-obit/ELIOT-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 928, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/ELIOT-obit/ELIOT-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1857, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/ELIOT-obit/ELIOT-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/ELIOT-obit/ELIOT-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/ELIOT-obit/ELIOT-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Valerie Eliot, Poet’s Wife and Defender, Dies at 86', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Valerie Eliot, Wife and Editor of T. S. Eliot, Dies at 86', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eliot, Valerie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eliot, Thomas Stearns', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T01:47:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/5478bc64-8c0a-5f70-8b43-afa40ff86866', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5478bc64-8c0a-5f70-8b43-afa40ff86866'}, {'abstract': 'A suit, shoes and shirts for job interviews became possible for a young man with help from The Neediest Cases Fund.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/opinion/dont-give-up.html', 'snippet': 'A suit, shoes and shirts for job interviews became possible for a young man with help from The Neediest Cases Fund.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tyrone Norfleet was 15 years old when his daughter was born in February 2008. He went straight to school from the hospital, his “mind racing, just thinking,” he recalled. To help support his daughter, he worked part time at Kmart. After graduating from New Dorp High School on Staten Island in 2010, he needed a full-time job.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/opinion/12norfleet/12norfleet-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/opinion/12norfleet/12norfleet-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Give Up', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Give Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T01:48:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/569132ed-39c1-5567-8fbf-d2ac550db168', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/569132ed-39c1-5567-8fbf-d2ac550db168'}, {'abstract': 'In clucking over the David Petraeus-Paula Broadwell affair, we’re casting roles and assigning blame with our usual chauvinism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/opinion/bruni-the-siren-and-the-spook.html', 'snippet': 'In clucking over the David Petraeus-Paula Broadwell affair, we’re casting roles and assigning blame with our usual chauvinism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were remarks galore about her unusually toned arms and the way she dressed to show them off. I even spotted a comment about how much of her armpits one of her outfits revealed, as if underarm exhibitionism were some sort of sexual sorcery, some aphrodisiac, the key to it all.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':