ri': 'nyt://article/7c26ce89-835e-5c46-ad71-9cdb93ac771b'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors say Anthony Chiasson and Todd Newman were part of a conspiracy that made about $68 million illegally trading the shares of Dell and Nvidia.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/trial-to-open-in-68-million-insider-trading-case/', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors say Anthony Chiasson and Todd Newman were part of a conspiracy that made about $68 million illegally trading the shares of Dell and Nvidia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the sharp-elbowed world of Wall Street, Anthony Chiasson and Todd Newman stood out as two of the good guys.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trial to Open in $68 Million Insider Trading Case', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trial to Open in $68 Million Insider Trading Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chiasson, Anthony', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newman, Todd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dell Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Level Global Investors', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NVIDIA Corporation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SAC Capital Advisors', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T01:52:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb911442-096a-5dee-9674-dcfe965bd6a8', 'word_count': 1103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb911442-096a-5dee-9674-dcfe965bd6a8'}, {'abstract': 'A larger and feistier Democratic majority could finally spell an end to filibuster abuse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/opinion/a-new-chance-for-the-senate.html', 'snippet': 'A larger and feistier Democratic majority could finally spell an end to filibuster abuse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In May, Harry Reid, the Senate majority leader, was furious at yet another obstructionist filibuster by Senate Republicans. He admitted then that he was wrong in 2011 not to change the Senate’s rules when he had a chance.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Chance for the Senate', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Chance for the Senate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Udall, Tom', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkley, Jeffrey A (1956- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T01:53:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/20ad61e5-c2d6-5feb-b1e2-f5e23f461069', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20ad61e5-c2d6-5feb-b1e2-f5e23f461069'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Transportation Authority said it would not provide refunds to riders who purchased 30-day or 7-day unlimited MetroCards before Hurricane Sandy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/nyregion/no-refunds-for-unlimited-metrocards-bought-before-hurricane.html', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Transportation Authority said it would not provide refunds to riders who purchased 30-day or 7-day unlimited MetroCards before Hurricane Sandy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the Metropolitan Transportation Authority worked to repair historic damage to the subway system after Hurricane Sandy, the question of whether holders of unlimited MetroCards would get any credit for the service disruptions seemed somewhat trivial, if not churlish. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'MetroCards After Storm: M.T.A. Says No Refunds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'MetroCards After Storm: M.T.A. Says No Refunds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'MetroCard (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Straphangers Campaign', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T01:54:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b85a9547-46cc-5b98-a4eb-3228ddebf874', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b85a9547-46cc-5b98-a4eb-3228ddebf874'}, {'abstract': 'The firm, Ameridose, has some of the same owners as the pharmacy whose tainted steroid caused a nationwide outbreak of fungal meningitis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/health/safety-problems-found-at-firm-tied-to-meningitis-linked-pharmacy.html', 'snippet': 'The firm, Ameridose, has some of the same owners as the pharmacy whose tainted steroid caused a nationwide outbreak of fungal meningitis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal inspection has turned up a long list of unsanitary conditions and unsafe practices at Ameridose, a drug supplier with some of the same owners as the pharmacy whose tainted steroid caused a nationwide outbreak of fungal meningitis that has killed 32 people and sickened more than 400 others. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Finds Safety Problems at Company Supplying Drugs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.D.A. Finds Safety Problems At Company Supplying Drugs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Compounding Center', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ameridose LLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meningitis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T01:56:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denise Grady and Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grady', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db5b9182-a020-5297-9c20-0cf07b1eaa3b', 'word_count': 659, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db5b9182-a020-5297-9c20-0cf07b1eaa3b'}, {'abstract': 'To build a great middle-class economy, President Obama  must isolate those who distract with their partisan incentives and instead present a clear offer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/opinion/brooks-obama-the-dealmaker.html', 'snippet': 'To build a great middle-class economy, President Obama  must isolate those who distract with their partisan incentives and instead present a clear offer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During his first term, President Obama faced a wicked problem: How do you govern in a highly polarized, evenly divided country with House Republicans who seem unwilling to compromise? Obama never really solved that one, and he was forced to pass his agenda on partisan lines (during the first two years) or not pass it at all (the final two).', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama the Dealmaker', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama The Dealmaker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T01:57:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/747ebbb0-b0b1-5e07-a9e9-a2c958fb6957', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/747ebbb0-b0b1-5e07-a9e9-a2c958fb6957'}, {'abstract': 'As a new collection of essays on hate speech makes clear, there is no completely satisfying way to deal with the topic.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/12/going-in-circles-with-hate-speech/', 'snippet': 'As a new collection of essays on hate speech makes clear, there is no completely satisfying way to deal with the topic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No topic is more frequently debated with less resolution than hate speech. This is made abundantly clear in a new collection of essays written by some of the leading contributors to the debate. The volume is called “The Content and Context of Hate Speech: Rethinking Regulation and Responses,” and it is edited by Michael Herz and Peter Molnar. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Going in Circles With Hate Speech', 'kicker': 'Stanley Fish', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herz, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Molnar, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T02:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Fish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/331d56fa-7ae4-5936-9d62-8ebacfd602a5', 'word_count': 2070, 'uri': 'nyt://article/331d56fa-7ae4-5936-9d62-8ebacfd602a5'}, {'abstract': 'Sloan-Kettering shows how a refusal to pay and public pressure can force a big drug company to bring down the cost of an overpriced cancer drug.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/opinion/incredible-prices-for-cancer-drugs.html', 'snippet': 'Sloan-Kettering shows how a refusal to pay and public pressure can force a big drug company to bring down the cost of an overpriced cancer drug.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An unusually bold stand by doctors at the Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center in New York has forced a big drug company to reduce the cost of an overpriced drug for treating colorectal cancer that was no better than a cheaper competitor and did almost nothing to extend a patient’s life. It is a heartening sign that alert and aggressive physicians can potentially play a major role in helping to reduce the escalating costs of health care for treatments of marginal value. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Incredible Prices for Cancer Drugs', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Incredible Prices for Cancer Drugs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colon and Colorectal Cancer', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Regeneron Pharmaceuticals Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sanofi SA', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T02:04:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7f4263f-a498-5630-9be3-76de80d18eed', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7f4263f-a498-5630-9be3-76de80d18eed'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court should reverse conspiracy convictions on the grounds that they violate the Fifth Amendment’s right to due process.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/opinion/the-burden-of-proof-in-conspiracy.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court should reverse conspiracy convictions on the grounds that they violate the Fifth Amendment’s right to due process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Calvin Smith was convicted of two murders and two counts of conspiracy in 2005 as part of an organized drug enterprise in Washington. He is serving 25 years to life for his part in those crimes, but he is appealing the conspiracy convictions. The Supreme Court, which heard oral argument on this case last week, should reverse the conspiracy convictions on the ground that they violate Mr. Smith’s Fifth Amendment right to due process. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Burden of Proof in Conspiracy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Burden of Proof in Conspiracy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fifth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Calvin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T02:04:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa6e4031-8c24-57c6-ac39-8f9316a35905', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa6e4031-8c24-57c6-ac39-8f9316a35905'}, {'abstract': 'Even as finance ministers from euro zone countries extended the deadline for Greece to make budget cuts, there were signs of continuing disagreement over details of the bailout.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/business/global/europe-gives-greece-two-more-years-for-budget-cuts.html', 'snippet': 'Even as finance ministers from euro zone countries extended the deadline for Greece to make budget cuts, there were signs of continuing disagreement over details of the bailout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — Finance ministers from euro zone countries meeting here late on Monday praised reforms taken by Greece and gave the country two more years to make budget cuts, a concession that is expected to require additional funding of nearly 33 billion euros, or $42 billion. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/business/global/13eurozone/13eurozone-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/business/global/13eurozone/13eurozone-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Gives Greece More Time for Budget Cuts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe Gives Greece More Time for Budget Cuts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samaras, Antonis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Juncker, Jean-Claude