 whose film career peaked around the time Lancôme was introduced in the 1930s: Betty Boop.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/business/Adco/Adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/business/Adco/Adco-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1399, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/13/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/business/Adco/Adco-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Turning to a Screen Siren to Introduce a Mascara', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turning to a Screen Siren To Introduce a Mascara', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cartoons and Cartoonists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "L'Oreal SA", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lancome', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T02:33:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Adam Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Adam', 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a6c8316-69cd-5c92-a1cb-068d82ee886b', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a6c8316-69cd-5c92-a1cb-068d82ee886b'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Collins, Sean Patrick Maloney, Hakeem Jeffries and Grace Meng in New York, and Elizabeth H. Esty of Connecticut, represent an ideological mix.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/nyregion/new-faces-in-us-house-from-new-york-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Chris Collins, Sean Patrick Maloney, Hakeem Jeffries and Grace Meng in New York, and Elizabeth H. Esty of Connecticut, represent an ideological mix.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One is a millionaire businessman who unseated a rising Democratic star. Another is an openly gay man who has worked for Gov. Eliot Spitzer and President Bill Clinton. Another jokes that she began her career in politics as “an angry PTA mom.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/nyregion/NEWFACES/NEWFACES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/13/nyregion/NEWFACES/NEWFACES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/nyregion/NEWFACES/NEWFACES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/nyregion/NEWFACES/NEWFACES-sup