t’s unusual for a Tuesday puzzle, but it might have just been me. Depending on how you look at it, the payoff in this grid is either smack in the middle of the puzzle and I should have caught it, or it’s buried in the middle of the puzzle and I simply missed it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spirit in a Blue Bottle', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T03:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db788dcb-3972-5526-bf88-0828ab2fe597', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db788dcb-3972-5526-bf88-0828ab2fe597'}, {'abstract': '“Vanya and Sonia and Masha and Spike” turns out to be a loving rejection of pretty much everything Chekhov stands for in the popular imagination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/theater/reviews/vanya-and-sonia-and-masha-and-spike-at-lincoln-center.html', 'snippet': '“Vanya and Sonia and Masha and Spike” turns out to be a loving rejection of pretty much everything Chekhov stands for in the popular imagination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you want to know what’s in a name, you could do worse than ask the title characters of “Vanya and Sonia and Masha and Spike,” Christopher Durang’s sunny new play about gloomy people. Nomenclature would seem to be fate, cruel fate, for the insecure inhabitants of this gentle, rambling farce, which opened on Monday night at the Mitzi E. Newhouse Theater at Lincoln Center with a cast featuring some big names of its own, notably David Hyde Pierce and Sigourney Weaver.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/13VANYA/13VANYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/13VANYA/13VANYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/13VANYA/13VANYA-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/13VANYA/13VANYA-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1312, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/13VANYA/13VANYA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/13VANYA/13VANYA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/arts/13VANYA/13VANYA-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Insecure Namesakes With a Gloomy Worldview', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Insecure Namesakes With a Gloomy Worldview', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Vanya and Sonia and Masha and Spike (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':