ght after an election.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, Nov. 13', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T05:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/c87f2700-fa7e-56d3-b638-53b87d1379f9', 'word_count': 49, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c87f2700-fa7e-56d3-b638-53b87d1379f9'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 340 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/word-of-the-day-transient/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 340 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'transient •\\ˈtran(t)-sh(e-)ənt; ˈtran-ze-ənt, ˈtran(t)-se-; ˈtran-zhənt, -jənt\\• adjective and noun', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | transient', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T05:04:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc5cb690-b06a-5b70-9594-6fb3b5229f3a', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc5cb690-b06a-5b70-9594-6fb3b5229f3a'}, {'abstract': 'Despite rising controversy over their prominent role, China’s princelings are emerging as a class that has an increasingly important say in ruling the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/world/asia/chinas-princelings-wield-influence-to-shape-politics.html', 'snippet': 'Despite rising controversy over their prominent role, China’s princelings are emerging as a class that has an increasingly important say in ruling the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — When Maoists were trying to keep control of China in the 1970s, a powerful general from the south came to the aid of moderates, helping to arrest the radicals and throw them in jail. The bold actions of the general, Ye Jianying, paved the way for the country’s move to a more market-oriented economy, and created a political dynasty that still plays kingmaker, able to influence national policy and protect its sprawling business empire in southern China long after his death.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/world/JP-CHINA-1/JP-CHINA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 848, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/world/JP-CHINA-1/JP-CHINA-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1887, 'width': 1563, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/world/JP-CHINA-1/JP-CHINA-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/14/world/JP-CHINA-1/JP-CHINA-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/world/JP-CHINA-1/JP-CHINA-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dynasty of Different Order Is Reshaping China', 'kicker': 'Changing of the Guard', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dynasty of Different Order Is Reshaping China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deng Xiaoping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang Yang (1955- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li Keqiang', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T05:21:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Series', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a19136f-2bca-58a8-abf0-97a78715f780', 'word_count': 1410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a19136f-2bca-58a8-abf0-97a78715f780'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/arts/television/whats-on-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:30 P.M. (13); 10 P.M. (49) THE SUICIDE PLAN In Oregon and Washington those with incurable illnesses may openly ask a doctor for help in ending their lives. But in the rest of the United States people who want to die must rely on friends, family and underground organizations. “Frontline” explores the world of assisted suicide, where the line between legality and criminal behavior blurs in cases like those of Hunt Williams, who was charged with manslaughter for helping a friend shoot himself, and Joan Butterstein (above left, with her daughter Kathleen), a lung cancer patient who turned to Compassion & Choices, a nonprofit counseling and referral organization on end-of-life care, for advice on obtaining a lethal combination of medications that she could administer herself. This episode of “Frontline” also shows a training session for the Final Exit Network, one of the country’s most controversial right-to-die organizations. “When you’re dealing with areas this complex, you’re so much better off with an open system than a secret system,” says Dr. Timothy Quill, a palliative-care physician and leading right-to-die advocate. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T06:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/8673ea2f-fc58-50de-a3c6-d22556fe86e6', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8673ea2f-fc58-50de-a3c6-d22556fe86e6'}, {'abstract': 'Gen. John R. Allen is under investigation for “inappropriate communication” with Jill Kelley, the Tampa, Fla., woman linked to the Petraeus affair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/us/top-us-commander-in-afghanistan-is-linked-to-petraeus-scandal.html', 'snippet': 'Gen. John R. Allen is under investigation for “inappropriate communication” with Jill Kelley, the Tampa, Fla., woman linked to the Petraeus affair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Conflicting portrayals of e-mails written by Gen. John R. Allen, the top American and NATO commander in Afghanistan, emerged Tuesday after it was disclosed that the general was under investigation for what the Pentagon called “inappropriate communication” with the woman whose complaint to the F.B.I. set off the scandal involving David H. Petraeus’s extramarital affair. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/us/13pentagon_cnd/13pentagon_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/us/13pentagon_cnd/13pentagon_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1445, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Another General Is Tied to the Petraeus Inquiry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another General Is Tied to the Petraeus Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petraeus, David H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panetta, Leon E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelley, Jill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allen, John R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broadwell, Paula', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULTERY', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T06:19:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.'