y The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd1908fb-3c32-5ab4-9009-298ac6a9ade8', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd1908fb-3c32-5ab4-9009-298ac6a9ade8'}, {'abstract': 'Osram Sylvania has introduced a bulb whose shape mimics that of a traditional incandescent.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/a-new-bid-for-the-100-watt-light-bulb-market/', 'snippet': 'Osram Sylvania has introduced a bulb whose shape mimics that of a traditional incandescent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the phaseout of incandescent bulbs takes effect, more efficient substitutes are coming to market. Osram Sylvania has announced that it is now selling a light-emitting-diode bulb that emits light equivalent to a 100-watt incandescent. While 100-watt-equivalent L.E.D. spotlights have already been introduced, this is apparently the first bulb-shaped omnidirectional light to enter American stores.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Bid for the 100-Watt Light Bulb Market', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Compact Fluorescent Light Bulbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light Bulbs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Light-Emitting Diodes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lighting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Osram Sylvania', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T12:30:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'ro