y’s long-term forecast that the United States would exceed Saudi Arabia in production led to a clash between the OPEC secretary general, Abdalla El-Badri, and the executive director of the agency, Maria Van der Hoeven, at the Oil and Money Conference in London on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. and Iraq Called Game Changers in Oil Supply', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shale', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Energy Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T13:32:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Reed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3abf7c1-dedb-57a6-ad6d-bcd85433cba6', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3abf7c1-dedb-57a6-ad6d-bcd85433cba6'}, {'abstract': 'The state is trying to restore through an act of Congress a lease sale for energy exploration that President Obama canceled in 2010 after the BP oil spill in the Gulf of Mexico.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/business/energy-environment/after-years-of-waiting-virginia-wants-to-make-its-name-in-oil.html', 'snippet': 'The state is trying to restore through an act of Congress a lease sale for energy exploration that President Obama canceled in 2010 after the BP oil spill in the Gulf of Mexico.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — When Doug Domenech looks out at the Atlantic Ocean, he sees oil and natural gas and jobs and revenue. Standing between him and those prizes are President Obama, the Navy and whales. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/business/energy-environment/14iht-ren-atlantic-sf/14iht-ren-atlantic-sf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/14/business/energy-environment/14iht-ren-atlantic-sf/14iht-ren-atlantic-sf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/business/energy-environment/14iht-ren-atlantic-sf/14iht-ren-atlantic-sf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/business/energy-environment/14iht-ren-atlantic-sf/14iht-ren-atlantic-sf-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/business/energy-environment/14iht-ren-atlantic-sf/14iht-ren-atlantic-sf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/14/business/energy-environment/14iht-ren-atlantic-sf/14iht-ren-atlantic-sf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/business/energy-environme