 the digital archive service.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/for-tablet-users-who-crave-pen-and-paper/', 'snippet': 'Livescribe has created the Sky smartpen, a writing tool that records notes written on special microdot paper. The notes are stored in the cloud through a partnership with Evernote, the digital archive service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anyone who has tried to take notes on a tablet knows how tricky it can be. Your choices are often limited to hunting and pecking on a digital keyboard or fiddling with a clunky stylus.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Tablet Users Who Crave Pen and Paper', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tool for Tablet Users Who Crave Pen and Paper', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Evernote Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Livescribe Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T16:58:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d465d4bf-4919-52e9-a2ba-e2c3d89e9621', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d465d4bf-4919-52e9-a2ba-e2c3d89e9621'}, {'abstract': 'The Victoria’s Secret model in a sexy day dress by Victoria Beckham.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/look-of-the-moment-miranda-kerr/', 'snippet': 'The Victoria’s Secret model in a sexy day dress by Victoria Beckham.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Look: Luck Be a Lady. A sexy day dress worn with dusty rose shoes, tortoiseshell shades, a tightly cinched belt and a tan is anything but a gamble.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Look of The Moment | Miranda Kerr', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Look of the Moment | Miranda Kerr', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerr, Miranda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T17:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4da01f79-9362-55d6-b1b9-4aaf3765b4c8', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4da01f79-9362-55d6-b1b9-4aaf3765b4c8'}, {'abstract': 'Kevin Powers and Ben Fountain, National Book Award nominees, discuss how they approached writing acclaimed novels about war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/books/kevin-powers-and-ben-fountain-national-book-award-nominees.html', 'snippet': 'Kevin Powers and Ben Fountain, National Book Award nominees, discuss how they approached writing acclaimed novels about war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two of the nominees in the fiction category for this year’s National Book Awards, to be handed out Wednesday night, chronicle America’s most recent wars through very different lenses. Kevin Powers, the author of “The Yellow Birds,” served with the United States Army in Iraq in 2004 and 2005, and his novel closely follows one soldier through his traumatic experience on the ground and his subsequent troubles adjusting to life back home. “Billy Lynn’s Long Halftime Walk,” by Ben Fountain, takes place over the course of a few hours at a Dallas Cowboys game on Thanksgiving, where a decorated group of Iraq war soldiers are bewildered participants in a raucous halftime show.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/books/14fountain-4/14fountain-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 660, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/books/14fountain-4/14fountain-4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1321, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/books/14fountain-4/14fountain-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/14/books/14fountain-4/14fountain-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/books/14fountain-4/14fountain-4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Writing Differently About War, but Drawing From the Same Rich Vein', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A WORD WITH: KEVIN POWERS AND BEN FOUNTAIN: Writing Differently About War, While Drawing From the Same Vein', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Yellow Birds (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Book Awards', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fountain, Ben', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Billy Lynn's Long Halftime Walk (Book)", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powers, Kevin C (1980- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T17:17:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fb58eee-84d9-5deb-815c-6cf147387b0b', 'word_count': 1630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fb58eee-84d9-5deb-815c-6cf147387b0b'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Paul D. Ryan of Wisconsin blamed Democratic turnout in “urban areas” for the loss by the Republican presidential ticket last week, saying he was surprised that he and Mitt Romney did not do better in the nation’s big cities.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/ryan-surprised-by-voters-in-urban-areas/', 'snippet': 'Representative Paul D. Ryan of Wisconsin blamed Democratic turnout in “urban areas” for the loss by the Republican presidential ticket last week, saying he was surprised that he and Mitt Romney did not do better in the nation’s big cities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Paul D. Ryan of Wisconsin on Monday blamed Democratic turnout in “urban areas” for the loss by the Republican presidential ticket last week, saying he was surprised that he and Mitt Romney did not do better in the nation’s big cities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryan Surprised by Voters in ‘Urban Areas’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T17:23:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dc5c9d7-61d9-53b0-8fdc-6ad275b0c097', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dc5c9d7-61d9-53b0-8fdc-6ad275b0c097'}, {'abstract': 'How the rage for clipping newspapers helps us interpret what everyday people thought about the conflict.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/scrapbooking-the-civil-war/', 'snippet': 'How the rage for clipping newspapers helps us interpret what everyday people thought about the conflict.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Soon after the Civil War began, a Savannah, Ga., resident named Henrietta Emanuel Solomons – or someone in her household – began to clip items from newspapers. She pasted her clippings over the sheets of a used-up ledger from the family grocery business until sometime in 1863, when she ran out of space. When she finished, they covered 483 large pages. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'