back in the smartphone market, but the company is preparing to share its mapping data with its competitors Apple and Google.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Nokia still hasn’t found its way to a successful comeback in the smartphone market. But the company is hoping to get its tentacles into competitors’ phones through mapping applications, a move it hopes will help it improve its maps. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/technology/13bits-nokia/13bits-nokia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/technology/13bits-nokia/13bits-nokia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/technology/13bits-nokia/13bits-nokia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/13/technology/13bits-nokia/13bits-nokia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/technology/13bits-nokia/13bits-nokia-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nokia to Offer Its Maps for iPhones and Android Phones', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nokia Oyj', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T18:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35933737-31dd-5521-aaf8-76c4a47a3567', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35933737-31dd-5521-aaf8-76c4a47a3567'}, {'abstract': 'At a soundstage in Santa Monica, some of Patti Smith’s fans gathered to hear the understated rock legend in an intimate performance for NPR.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/l-a-p-o-v-because-the-night/', 'snippet': 'At a soundstage in Santa Monica, some of Patti Smith’s fans gathered to hear the understated rock legend in an intimate performance for NPR.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The west-side industrial loftlike neighborhood in southeast Santa Monica, usually abandoned by nighttime, was quietly hopping. Two gorgeous 20-year-olds in short skirts and tall boots were standing up against the wall of a building, a small but dignified line of people down the sidewalk waiting to get in, as on the other side of the street a Mercedes pulled into a parking spot, a Prius made a silent U-turn and slipped into a place, as well. The list at the door was so small and well-vetted, I actually convinced the bouncer not to stamp my hand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'L.A. P.O.V. | Because the Night …', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Patti', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T18:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Ephron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ephron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebc9624d-927b-5b6a-ae8f-320747dbcad7', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebc9624d-927b-5b6a-ae8f-320747dbcad7'}, {'abstract': 'At the annual Glamour Magazine Women of the Year Awards at Carnegie Hall on Monday, the mood was set when Lauren Hutton strolled out to give an award to Jenna Lyons, minutes after a emotional tribute to the Oscar winning director of “Saving Face.”', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/a-night-of-glamour-and-of-seriousness/', 'snippet': 'At the annual Glamour Magazine Women of the Year Awards at Carnegie Hall on Monday, the mood was set when Lauren Hutton strolled out to give an award to Jenna Lyons, minutes after a emotional tribute to the Oscar winning director of “Saving Face.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'What can you say about an evening in which Selena Gomez shared the stage with Ruth Bader Ginsburg, Chelsea Handler thanked her fellow presenter Chelsea Clinton for bringing respectability back to their shared first name, and jokes about Honey Boo Boo and Jennifer Lopez’s derrière were followed by scenes from a harrowing film showing the scarred faces of Pakistani women whose husbands had doused them with acid?', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Night of Glamour, and of Seriousness', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'True Beauty, Inside and Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Chelsea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douglas, Gabby', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunham, Lena', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ginsburg, Ruth Bader', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Handler, Chelsea', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hutton, Lauren', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leibovitz, Annie', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obaid-Chinoy, Sharmeen', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Glamour (Magazine)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T18:02:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Emmrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Emmrich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38dd1d56-4df1-55c7-b090-f57c50b9324f', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38dd1d56-4df1-55c7-b090-f57c50b9324f'}, {'abstract': 'Several Chelsea galleries are reopening after flooding, as costs continue to be tallied.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/amid-recovery-reports-of-sandys-damage-to-art-institutions-keep-coming/', 'snippet': 'Several Chelsea galleries are reopening after flooding, as costs continue to be tallied.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We’re beginning to see progress,” Linda Blumberg, the executive director of the Art Dealers Association of America, said on Tuesday morning. “Galleries are reopening, albeit sometimes in raw states, but they are rebuilding, and putting their best foot forward. We’re determined to bring this community back and get people down there.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3'