raised.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal prosecutor in Brazil is seeking a court order to force the central bank to replace the nation’s entire supply of paper currency with bills that do not display the phrase “God Be Praised,” the newspaper Folha de São Paulo reported on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/world/americas/13lede_brazil/13lede_brazil-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 311, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/world/americas/13lede_brazil/13lede_brazil-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 311, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/world/americas/13lede_brazil/13lede_brazil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/13/world/americas/13lede_brazil/13lede_brazil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/world/americas/13lede_brazil/13lede_brazil-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 148, 'width': 148, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil’s Banknotes Still Praise God, for Now', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T23:03:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey and Taylor Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Taylor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50426757-b982-5d06-8314-cb2e80928d86', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50426757-b982-5d06-8314-cb2e80928d86'}, {'abstract': '“The Law in These Parts” is a documentary investigation into the justice of the legal system in the occupied West Bank and Gaza Strip.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/movies/the-law-in-these-parts-raanan-alexandrowiczs-documentary.html', 'snippet': '“The Law in These Parts” is a documentary investigation into the justice of the legal system in the occupied West Bank and Gaza Strip.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By keeping its focus admirably tight, the sober and sobering Israeli documentary “The Law in These Parts” presents a devastating case against the occupation of the West Bank and the Gaza Strip. Investigating the legal system in the occupied territories, the film is fundamentally an inquiry into justice. It makes a forceful argument: Justice and the occupation are incompatible.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawyers and the Seasoning of Justice in Israel’s Occupied Territories', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Law in These Parts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Alexandrowicz, Ra'anan", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T23:03:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/07dc5c91-6b79-568b-924b-be98d6153272', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07dc5c91-6b79-568b-924b-be98d6153272'}, {'abstract': 'The Shanghai Quartet played Mozart, Bright Sheng (with the pianist Peter Serkin) and Dvorak’s in a passionate performance on Sunday at the 92nd Street Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/arts/music/perter-serkin-and-the-shanghai-quartet-at-the-92nd-street-y.html', 'snippet': 'The Shanghai Quartet played Mozart, Bright Sheng (with the pianist Peter Serkin) and Dvorak’s in a passionate performance on Sunday at the 92nd Street Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even Mozart, the composer of some of the most profound, sublime music ever written, churned out a few works that are merely genial. Like an overlong exchange of pleasantries, his “Hunt” Quartet in B flat (K. 458), almost 30 minutes long, outstays its welcome, even in an excellent performance like that of the Shanghai Quartet on Sunday afternoon at the 92nd Street Y.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/14PETER/14PETER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 810, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/14PETER/14PETER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1621, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/14PETER/14PETER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/14PETER/14PETER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/14PETER/14PETER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sherpas Lead Way to a Feverish Finish', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sherpas Lead Way to a Feverish Finish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Serkin, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheng, Bright', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shanghai String Quartet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T23:12:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/51afdbeb-0aa8-5c79-8d28-aab77f6a3227', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51afdbeb-0aa8-5c79-8d28-aab77f6a3227'}, {'abstract': 'Thomas Pasatieri’s opera “The Martyrs” features two piano monodramas, both using love and incarceration as story points.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/arts/music/the-martyrs-at-the-dicapo-opera-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Thomas Pasatieri’s opera “The Martyrs” features two piano monodramas, both using love and incarceration as story points.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The small, resourceful Dicapo Opera has asserted a new identity for itself in recent seasons. Beyond a steady flow of conventional, standard-repertory items, the company has ventured increasingly into unexamined corners of the global canon.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/martyrs/martyrs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/martyrs/martyrs-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1339, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/martyrs/martyrs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/martyrs/martyrs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/martyrs/martyrs-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Love That Goes to Great Lengths', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Love That Goes to Great Lengths', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dicapo Opera Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pasatieri, Thomas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-13T23:13:31+0000', 'document