d in Park Slope, is another Brooklyn enterprise crossing the river, opening in Manhattan on Wednesday. A new feature at this branch, the fourth and one of the largest in this chain of high-end supermarkets, is a more elaborate prepared-foods department, offering dishes like Dominican pork roast, porchetta-style leg of lamb, brisket meatloaf, roasted cauliflower and (since this is a market from Brooklyn) sautéed kale.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/dining/14STUFF_MARKET/14STUFF_MARKET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/14/dining/14STUFF_MARKET/14STUFF_MARKET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/dining/14STUFF_MARKET/14STUFF1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/dining/14STUFF_MARKET/14STUFF1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/dining/14STUFF_MARKET/14STUFF_MARKET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/14/dining/14STUFF_MARKET/14STUFF_MARKET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/dining/14STUFF_MARKET/14STUFF_MARKET-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For This Market, It’s All About the Preparation', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For This Market, It’s All About The Preparation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets and Grocery Stores', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T00:33:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6942615-3ed8-5291-aeca-9db5709f11c0', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6942615-3ed8-5291-aeca-9db5709f11c0'}, {'abstract': '“Blood Potato,” by James McManus, is a family drama of three brothers on the edge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/theater/reviews/james-mcmanuss-blood-potato-by-apothecary-theater-company.html', 'snippet': '“Blood Potato,” by James McManus, is a family drama of three brothers on the edge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like its brutal and angry characters, “Blood Potato” sometimes falters. But almost every moment it’s onstage, this play is alive. That intensity, consistent and bitter, usually makes up for its mistakes. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/artsspecial/14BLOOD/14BLOOD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/artsspecial/14BLOOD/14BLOOD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/artsspecial/14BLOOD/14BLOOD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/artsspecial/14BLOOD/14BLOOD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/artsspecial/14BLOOD/14BLOOD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/artsspecial/14BLOOD/14BLOOD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/artsspecial/14BLOOD/14BLOOD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Family Stretched by Tensions and Drugs', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Family Tensions, Fueled by Drugs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McManus, James', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flanagan, Dennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kittle, Kevin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apothecary Theater Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T00:39:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Jaworowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jaworowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c036c5f-1d7a-5337-b81d-a2f807d729f9', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c036c5f-1d7a-5337-b81d-a2f807d729f9'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Jesse L. Jackson Jr. has left the Mayo Clinic in Minnesota after treatment there for bipolar disorder, officials at the medical facility said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/us/illinois-jackson-leaves-clinic.html', 'snippet': 'Representative Jesse L. Jackson Jr. has left the Mayo Clinic in Minnesota after treatment there for bipolar disorder, officials at the medical facility said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Jesse L. Jackson Jr., a Democrat who won re-election last week despite a lengthy absence from Congress and virtually no campaigning, has left the Mayo Clinic in Minnesota after treatment there for bipolar disorder, officials at the medical facility said on Tuesday. Aides to Mr. Jackson, who entered the clinic shortly before Election Day after earlier treatment there, provided no more details. Federal agents are investigating Mr. Jackson for possible misuse of campaign funds, a federal authority confirmed last month. Last week, Mr. Jackson won 63 percent of the vote in his Democratic-leaning district on Chicago’s South Side and its southern suburbs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illinois: Jackson Leaves Clinic', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illinois: Jackson Leaves Clinic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Jesse L Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mayo Clinic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T00:44:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ef30906-5421-5d50-9a9c-85de19f00dff', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ef30906-5421-5d50-9a9c-85de19f00dff'}, {'abstract': 'The nation’s Roman Catholic bishops voted unanimously Tuesday to support the cause of sainthood for Dorothy Day, who helped to found the Catholic Worker movement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/us/bishops-support-dorothy-day-for-sainthood.html', 'snippet': 'The nation’s Roman Catholic bishops voted unanimously Tuesday to support the cause of sainthood for Dorothy Day, who helped to found the Catholic Worker movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nation’s Roman Catholic bishops, in Baltimore at their semiannual meeting, voted unanimously Tuesday to support the cause of sainthood for Dorothy Day, a Catholic convert and an advocate for the poor who helped to found the Catholic Worker movement and to advance the church’s teaching on social justice. Meanwhile, a statement of hope for Americans in a difficult economy, written by a bishops’ committee, was defeated after failing to win a two-thirds vote. Some bishops said the document did not sufficiently emphasize Catholic teaching on social justice, the structural causes of economic inequality and the rights of workers to unionize. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bishops Support Dorothy Day for Sainthood', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Religion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bishops Support Dorothy Day For Sainthood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Day, Dorothy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beatifications and Canonizations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T00:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie Goodstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a5888b6-0bfc-5ab7-bdc5-677a83001d9b', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a5888b6-0bfc-5ab7-bdc5-677a83001d9b'}, {'abstract': 'The support for victims of Hurricane Sandy highlights how charity plays in our social contract — we Americans view ourselves as generous, yet we mistrust the government to help those in need.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/business/charitys-role-in-america-and-its-limits.html', 'snippet': 'The support for victims of Hurricane Sandy highlights how charity plays in our social contract — we Americans view ourselves as generous, yet we mistrust the government to help those in need.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anyone doubting Americans’ charity should visit the Rockaways in Queens. Volunteers from all over the city and beyond have descended upon the devastated communities, providing cash, supplies and assistance to locals marooned in waterlogged homes without food or power. They are helping to fill a void in the government’s sometimes plodding response to the disaster wrought by Hurricane Sandy.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-thumbLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Charity’s Role in America, and Its Limits', 'kicker': 'Economic Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Role,\r\nAnd Limits,\r\nOf Charity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T00:57:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eduardo Porter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eduardo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Porter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cddb4b4c-f705-5dcf-b28e-4d18b8c6b82b', 'word_count': 1233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cddb4b4c-f705-5dcf-b28e-4d18b8c6b82b'}, {'abstract': 'In Gregory S. Moss’s new play, “Billy Witch,” teenage summer campers comically experience sexual awakening.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/theater/reviews/billy-witch-onstage-in-queens.html', 'snippet': 'In Gregory S. Moss’s new play, “Billy Witch,” teenage summer campers comically experience sexual awakening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his gleeful romp “Billy Witch,” Gregory S. Moss (“punkplay”) takes familiar ingredients of high school horror — summer camp, a lake, a forest, ghost stories — and hurls them into a whirlwind of comic sexual awakening. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/theater/14billy-web/14billy-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/theater/14billy-web/14billy-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1086, 'width': 723, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': '