ted by the voice of Sue Raney at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency on Thursday evening, I was reminded that for certain singers there is no better description than the quaint euphemism “songbird.” Ms. Raney, who was playing her first New York engagement in 25 years, may be 72, but her voice is young, her singing infused with hope.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Part Tribute, Part Torch, a Voice Goes All Out', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Part Tribute, Part Torch, a Voice Goes All Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T01:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd1196af-9796-5b96-8466-637091541309', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd1196af-9796-5b96-8466-637091541309'}, {'abstract': 'An all-electric Spark will join a growing list of all-electric production cars in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/chevrolet-spark-e-v-to-have-debut-at-los-angeles-auto-show/', 'snippet': 'An all-electric Spark will join a growing list of all-electric production cars in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since the Chevrolet Spark first appeared in 2009, the nameplate of that gas-powered minicar has seemed a bit misleading. Chevrolet will take a big step toward solving that problem later this month at the Los Angeles auto show, where it will introduce an all-electric Spark that will go on sale next year. The Spark EV will join a short but growing list of all-electric production cars in the United States, including the Nissan Leaf and 2013 Ford Focus Electric.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chevrolet Spark E.V. to Have Debut at Los Angeles Auto Show', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Los Angeles Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T01:13:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Schembari', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schembari', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2e87aa2-1454-5d1d-93f9-bd6f19c2baa5', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2e87aa2-1454-5d1d-93f9-bd6f19c2baa5'}, {'abstract': 'An auction will formally open California’s cap-and-trade system, intended to reduce carbon dioxide emissions by issuing allowances to polluters, then trading them in a market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/business/energy-environment/california-to-hold-auction-of-greenhouse-gas-emissions.html', 'snippet': 'An auction will formally open California’s cap-and-trade system, intended to reduce carbon dioxide emissions by issuing allowances to polluters, then trading them in a market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — California’s fledging market-based system for reducing greenhouse gas emissions makes its formal debut on Wednesday with its auction of state-issued pollution allowances.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Market in Emissions Is Set to Open in California', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Market In Emissions Is Set to Open In California', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T01:13:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2c18f36-32d5-5868-9a73-2ed040bcbcba', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2c18f36-32d5-5868-9a73-2ed040bcbcba'}, {'abstract': 'With this trip, the president is following through on his pledge to pivot American foreign policy away from the frustrations of the Middle East and toward Asia’s promising future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/opinion/obamas-subtle-game-will-impress-asians.html', 'snippet': 'With this trip, the president is following through on his pledge to pivot American foreign policy away from the frustrations of the Middle East and toward Asia’s promising future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS President Obama heads to Myanmar, Cambodia and Laos this week and next, intent on reversing China’s drive to tighten its grasp on Southeast Asia, he is exercising an uncannily Asian-style diplomacy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Impress Asia, Leave the Drama Home', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Impress Asia, Leave the Drama Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T01:17:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lewis M. Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lewis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdccce69-d59e-5d20-a5a6-8f04c32d2e60', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdccce69-d59e-5d20-a5a6-8f04c32d2e60'}, {'abstract': 'A pilot anti-malaria initiative in Africa has shown great promise. So why are those financing it so bent on killing it?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/opinion/saving-a-malaria-program-that-saves-lives.html', 'snippet': 'A pilot anti-malaria initiative in Africa has shown great promise. So why are those financing it so bent on killing it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stanford, Calif.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saving a Program That Saves Lives', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saving a Program That Saves Lives', 'name': None, 'seo': None,