tus, which would shield it from alterations and demolition for three years. The home’s owners, Steve Sells and John Hoffman, have said the restrictions would “significantly diminish” their ability to market the property, which is priced at $2.379 million. They said they did not find out about the effort to turn the house into a historic landmark until after they had closed on its purchase. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arizona: No Deal for Wright House', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arizona: No Deal For Wright House', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Frank Lloyd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Phoenix (Ariz)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T01:18:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f24ed4e8-b745-5f65-9cb8-4ff5c1e56f17', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f24ed4e8-b745-5f65-9cb8-4ff5c1e56f17'}, {'abstract': 'Praise for Senator Olympia Snowe’s comments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/opinion/for-civility-in-politics.html', 'snippet': 'Praise for Senator Olympia Snowe’s comments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Civility in Politics', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Civility