uthor’s Talk on Zionism, and Uproar Follows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beinart, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Fairs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zionism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T01:54:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Severson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26052875-af2e-5652-b980-b6ea02dc5e99', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26052875-af2e-5652-b980-b6ea02dc5e99'}, {'abstract': 'Can the world expect a real change in policy at a time of daunting domestic and international challenges?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/opinion/will-chinas-new-leaders-offer-real-change.html', 'snippet': 'Can the world expect a real change in policy at a time of daunting domestic and international challenges?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The unveiling of China’s new leadership this week and the government transition that follows will be enormously important for the United States and the world. When Xi Jinping replaces Hu Jintao as the Communist Party’s general secretary on Thursday at the end of the 18th Party Congress, he will take control of a country that has made tremendous strides in the last decade but also faces daunting domestic and international challenges.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Leadership in China', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Leadership in China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T01:54:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/23ad9503-14d6-56ca-a2e0-89ed811d7a5f', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23ad9503-14d6-56ca-a2e0-89ed811d7a5f'}, {'abstract': 'An appellate court ruling that denies American citizens who are tortured by the American military the right to sue for damages ignores an important Supreme Court precedent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/opinion/getting-away-with-torture.html', 'snippet': 'An appellate court ruling that denies American citizens who are tortured by the American military the right to sue for damages ignores an important Supreme Court precedent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a decision that ignored a 41-year-old precedent and American obligations under international law, a United States appeals court has ruled that American civilians who are tortured by the American military cannot recover damages from the people responsible.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Away With Torture', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Getting Away With Torture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rumsfeld, Donald H', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T01:54:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/44aa10ff-c6ca-58bc-a088-3eb6133514fe', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44aa10ff-c6ca-58bc-a088-3eb6133514fe'}, {'abstract': 'Forget the “fiscal cliff.” What about the smoldering Syria?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/opinion/friedman-obamas-nightmare.html', 'snippet': 'Forget the “fiscal cliff.” What about the smoldering Syria?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The scandal engulfing two of our top military and intelligence officers could not be coming at a worse time: the Middle East has never been more unstable and closer to multiple, interconnected explosions. Virtually every American president since Dwight Eisenhower has had a Middle Eastern country that brought him grief. For Ike, it was Lebanon’s civil war and Israel’s Sinai invasion. For Lyndon Johnson, it was the 1967 Six-Day War. For Nixon, it was the 1973 war. For Carter, it was the Iranian Revolution. For Ronald Reagan, it was Lebanon. For George H.W. Bush, it was Iraq. For Bill Clinton, it was Al Qaeda and Afghanistan. For George W. Bush, it was Iraq and Afghanistan. For Barack Obama’s first term, it was Iran and Afghanistan, again. And for Obama’s second term, I fear that it could be the full nightmare — all of them at once. The whole Middle East erupts in one giant sound and light show of civil wars, states collapsing and refugee dislocations, as the keystone of the entire region — Syria — gets pulled asunder and the disorder spills across the neighborhood. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Nightmare', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama’s Nightmare', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T01:59:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbf4dace-10bf-5a0a-afa6-c427b1df4af8', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbf4dace-10bf-5a0a-afa6-c427b1df4af8'}, {'abstract': 'The Pentagon needs clear rules on misconduct, and they should apply to all serving personnel, regardless of rank or gender.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/opinion/one-lesson-from-the-david-petraeus-scandal.html', 'snippet': 'The Pentagon needs clear rules on misconduct, and they should apply to all serving personnel, regardless of rank or gender.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The scandal unfolding around the resignation of David Petraeus as the director of the Central Intelligence Agency after an adulterous affair raises many questions that need to be answered — from the unusual role played by the Federal Bureau of Investigation in what seems to have begun as a routine investigation of harassing e-mails to whether and when Congressional intelligence committees should have been notified that the leader of the C.I.A. had come under an F.B.I. investigation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Lesson From a Messy Scandal', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Lesson From a Messy Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petraeus, David H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULTERY', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T01:59:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/72506b15-fe4e-559f-8ff1-267cab168a28', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72506b15-fe4e-559f-8ff1-267cab168a28'}, {'abstract': 'Demonstrators burned tires, smashed traffic lights and blocked roads in an unparalleled show of anger at a government proposal to increase fuel prices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/world/middleeast/jordan-faces-protests-after-gas-price-proposal.html', 'snippet': 'Demonstrators burned tires, smashed traffic lights and blocked roads in an unparalleled show of anger at a government proposal to increase fuel prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Violent protests broke out across Jordan on Tuesday night after the government announced an increase in fuel prices, inciting what appeared to be an unparalleled show of anger directed at the king after months of mounting tension in the strategically important and politically fragile king