is car had been vandalized. So when the mayor of the small Black Forest town of Rickenbach reported that he had been the victim of a criminal assault, it at first seemed plausible.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a German Town, Court Finds That Mayor Cried Wolf', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Finds That a Mayor Cried Wolf', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rickenbach (Germany)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moosmann, Norbert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T02:13:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Cottrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cottrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b39ddd2-6b9c-5ba9-b83b-00ef6d947118', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b39ddd2-6b9c-5ba9-b83b-00ef6d947118'}, {'abstract': 'An internal review of how the United Nations handled the bloody final months of Sri Lanka’s civil war in 2009 has concluded that the response was “a grave failure of the U.N.”', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/leaked-report-on-sri-lanka-critical-of-u-n/', 'snippet': 'An internal review of how the United Nations handled the bloody final months of Sri Lanka’s civil war in 2009 has concluded that the response was “a grave failure of the U.N.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'An internal review of how the United Nations handled the bloody final months of Sri Lanka’s civil war in 2009, when as many as 40,000 civilians were killed, has concluded that the response was “a grave failure of the U.N.,” according to a leaked draft of the report. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leaked Report on Sri Lanka Critical of U.N.', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sri Lanka', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T02:19:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c1e4b33-c194-59c0-8ca2-89a912ed2255', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c1e4b33-c194-59c0-8ca2-89a912ed2255'}, {'abstract': 'The Downtown Market, a 130,000-square-foot center for commerce in culinary arts and fresh local food is expected to attract 500,000 visitors a year and spur development.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/realestate/commercial/grand-rapids-mich-bets-on-a-food-market-for-growth.html', 'snippet': 'The Downtown Market, a 130,000-square-foot center for commerce in culinary arts and fresh local food is expected to attract 500,000 visitors a year and spur development.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GRAND RAPIDS, Mich. — The idea of building a year-round public market to tie the city’s skilled chefs to the region’s big complement of young farmers had already attained an air of inevitability by the time this Midwestern city held its first Restaurant Week three summers ago.', 'print_sec