, 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cdafad3-40f7-5224-86b1-acb3b8d91cdc', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cdafad3-40f7-5224-86b1-acb3b8d91cdc'}, {'abstract': 'The authorities said two brothers, Andy Ashkar, 34, and Nayel Ashkar, 36, had tricked the actual winner, a customer at their parents’ convenience store.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/nyregion/syracuse-area-brothers-charged-in-plot-to-steal-5-million-lottery-payout.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities said two brothers, Andy Ashkar, 34, and Nayel Ashkar, 36, had tricked the actual winner, a customer at their parents’ convenience store.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They waited until shortly before the $5 million winning ticket in a scratch-off lottery game would have been worthless. Then, when two brothers from the Syracuse area went to claim the prize, they made an unusual offer: They told state lottery officials that they would be happy to take home less than the full amount if they could avoid a news conference.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Upstate Brothers Are Charged in Plot to Steal a $5 Million New York Lottery Ticket', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Charged in Plot to Steal $5 Million Lottery Payout', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashkar, Andy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syracuse (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashkar, Nayel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T02:24:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a59fc27-70b9-52a3-b104-e8348eb8fbcb', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a59fc27-70b9-52a3-b104-e8348eb8fbcb'}, {'abstract': 'In the past decade, motivated citizens initiating creative solutions to social problems have changed the humanitarian landscape.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/the-rise-of-social-entrepreneur/', 'snippet': 'In the past decade, motivated citizens initiating creative solutions to social problems have changed the humanitarian landscape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recently, I wrote a column suggesting that, in the field of social change, we’re getting smarter. I went so far as to say that we may even be going through a new Enlightenment. I mentioned three ways we’re improving — employing new understandings about human behavior to get better results, using evidence more regularly to assess and guide problem-solving, and constructing integrated solutions to social problems. I also promised to highlight some other advances.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rise of the Social Entrepreneur', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T02:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualif