ork Philharmonic has established a four-year partnership with the Shanghai Symphony Orchestra that will include a residency in China and a stake in an orchestra training program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China long ago emerged as a kind of promised land for classical music, and two of America’s great orchestras are wading in with big projects and very different approaches. You could call one the Philadelphia flier and the other the Big Apple plod.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/13ORCHESTRA/13ORCHESTRA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 619, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/13ORCHESTRA/13ORCHESTRA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1803, 'width': 1090, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/13ORCHESTRA/13ORCHESTRA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/13ORCHESTRA/13ORCHESTRA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/13ORCHESTRA/13ORCHESTRA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Philharmonic Establishes Partnership With Shanghai', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Philharmonic Establishes Partnership With Shanghai', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Orchestra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shanghai Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T03:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07afa2c6-a9be-584f-9544-37d8124cad89', 'word_count': 1194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07afa2c6-a9be-584f-9544-37d8124cad89'}, {'abstract': 'In “Golden Child,” a rural Chinese household’s fragile equilibrium, kept in place by tradition, is threatened when a husband returns from abroad with new ideas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/theater/reviews/golden-child-at-the-signature-center.html', 'snippet': 'In “Golden Child,” a rural Chinese household’s fragile equilibrium, kept in place by tradition, is threatened when a husband returns from abroad with new ideas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The encroaching of Western ideals upon Chinese tradition brings both liberation and loss in David Henry Hwang’s “Golden Child,” a drama with piquant comic overtones set primarily in Fujian, China, in the second decade of the 20th century. First produced by the Public Theater in 1996 and later seen briefly on Broadway, the play is a smart choice to inaugurate the Signature Theater Company’s season devoted to the work of Mr. Hwang. Throughout his career this talented American playwright has returned to themes explored in this gentle-spirited domestic drama: the cost of assimilation for Asians entering into the turbulent flow of the West, the confusions that result from the clash of cultures, the pressure brought to bear on the individual by the family. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/golden/golden-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/golden/golden-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1308, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/golden/golden-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/golden/golden-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/golden/golden-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Ideas Endanger Household Harmony', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Ideas Endanger Household Harmony', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Signature Theater Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maher, Matthew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hwang, David Henry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lim, Jennifer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soelistyo, Julyana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silverman, Leigh', 'rank'