ion': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32db39f0-d346-5667-97cc-23dd75b85c69', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32db39f0-d346-5667-97cc-23dd75b85c69'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Chris Christie, a Republican who has pushed aggressively to cut taxes during his three years in office, said rebuilding New Jersey has to be paid for and “there’s no magic money tree.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/nyregion/chris-christie-reverses-stand-on-tax-hikes-after-storm.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Chris Christie, a Republican who has pushed aggressively to cut taxes during his three years in office, said rebuilding New Jersey has to be paid for and “there’s no magic money tree.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie, a Republican who has pushed aggressively for cutting and capping taxes in New Jersey during his three years in office, said Tuesday that people who lived in towns destroyed by Hurricane Sandy were likely to pay higher taxes to help rebuild.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Christie Reverses Stand on Tax Increases After Storm', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Christie Reverses Stand on Tax Increases in Face of Rebuilding Storm-Ravaged New Jersey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Property Taxes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T03:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Zernike', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zernike', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1df839a0-7a59-5283-b855-3e9ca11f9ca7', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1df839a0-7a59-5283-b855-3e9ca11f9ca7'}, {'abstract': 'The widening scandal threatens to tarnish the reputation of Gen. John R. Allen, the top American commander in Afghanistan, as The New York Times’s Eric Schmitt and Elisabeth Bumiller report.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/top-u-s-general-is-ensnared-in-petraeus-inquiry/', 'snippet': 'The widening scandal threatens to tarnish the reputation of Gen. John R. Allen, the top American commander in Afghanistan, as The New York Times’s Eric Schmitt and Elisabeth Bumiller report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times’s Eric Schmitt and Elisabeth Bumiller reported on the widening Petraeus scandal that threatens to tarnish the reputation of Gen. John R. Allen, the top American commander in Afghanistan. The general is under investigation for what the Pentagon called “inappropriate communication” with Jill Kelley, the woman who was seen by Paula Broadwell, Mr. Petraeus’s lover, as a rival for his attentions and whose complaint to the F.B.I. set off the inquiry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top U.S. General Is Ensnared in Petraeus Inquiry', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLEN, JOAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petraeus, David H', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T03:24:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name':