rl': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/sports/basketball/knicks-beat-magic-and-climb-to-5-0.html', 'snippet': 'Despite trailing in the fourth quarter for the first time, the Knicks forced seven turnovers in the period, holding Orlando to 13 points as they moved to 5-0 for the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ORLANDO, Fla. — Many Knicks looked up at scoreboard inside the Amway Center on Tuesday night and quickly recognized the anomaly. For the first time this season, they trailed in the fourth quarter, and looked vulnerable against an unlikely opponent, the Orlando Magic, who lost to the Brooklyn Nets by 39 points last week.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/sports/subKNICKS/subKNICKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/sports/subKNICKS/subKNICKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1406, 'width': 1882, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/sports/subKNICKS/subKNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/14/sports/subKNICKS/subKNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/sports/subKNICKS/subKNICKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Challenged Late, the Knicks Remain Undefeated', 'kicker': 'Knicks 99, Magic 89', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Challenged Late, the Knicks Climb to 5-0', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orlando Magic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T03:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eca99291-a1e1-5069-bfbf-7d96825f5639', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eca99291-a1e1-5069-bfbf-7d96825f5639'}, {'abstract': 'In a multiplayer trade, the Marlins sent five players, including shortstop Jose Reyes and the starting pitchers Mark Buehrle and Josh Johnson, to the Blue Jays for a group of prospects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/sports/baseball/in-multiplayer-trade-with-blue-jays-marlins-pull-the-plug-again.html', 'snippet': 'In a multiplayer trade, the Marlins sent five players, including shortstop Jose Reyes and the starting pitchers Mark Buehrle and Josh Johnson, to the Blue Jays for a group of prospects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was all a shimmering mirage. The new character of the rebranded Miami Marlins, big shots with thick wallets in a dazzling postmodern ballpark, did not even last 12 months. The Marlins are world-class schemers, forever reaffirming the skepticism of their fans.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/sports/baseball/14trade/14trade-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'artic