ner gets his annual health care renewal rates — along with a rundown of the many changes to come.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/for-business-owners-the-health-care-details-begin-to-emerge/', 'snippet': 'A business owner gets his annual health care renewal rates — along with a rundown of the many changes to come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, before the election, I received a fat envelope from Independence Blue Cross with our health insurance renewal rates for 2013. This happens about this time each fall, and it is not something I look forward to.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Business Owners, the Health Care Details Begin to Emerge', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paul Downs Cabinetmakers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T12:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7b0563a-57c5-5208-9514-ecd2e5ff0e23', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7b0563a-57c5-5208-9514-ecd2e5ff0e23'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s links: Internet sentience; ignorance and democratic legitimacy; Peter Sloterdjik’s philosophical merits, and more.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/stone-links-collective-consciousness/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s links: Internet sentience; ignorance and democratic legitimacy; Peter Sloterdjik’s philosophical merits, and more.', 'lead_paragraph': ' At Rationally Speaking, Massimo Pagliucci weighs in on questions addressed in a roundtable discussion at Slate: Since the number of transistors in the networked computers worldwide is three orders of magnitude greater than the number of synapses in the human brain, might the Internet be conscious? Put another way, is there qualitatively something it is like to be the Internet? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stone Links: Collective Consciousness', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romano, Carlin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Alan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T12:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark de Silva', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Silva', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd9b322e-edc0-56d6-b502-065c012a06d2', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd9b322e-edc0-56d6-b502-065c012a06d2'}, {'abstract': 'Corals use chemical communication to recruit fish to help control menacing seaweed, researchers say.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/a-reef-in-distress-gobies-to-the-rescue/', 'snippet': 'Corals use chemical communication to recruit fish to help control menacing seaweed, researchers say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the waters surrounding the Fiji Islands, the coral reef has vigilant defenders. Researchers have discovered that when alerted by chemical signals transmitted by corals, two resident species of the goby fish will swing into action and limit a growth of seaweed that contributes to the bleaching of precious reefs. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Reef in Distress? Gobies to the Rescue', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T12:25:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma Bryce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bryce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17111311-fbb1-5efa-ae68-b43e3dba3e73', 'word_count': 657, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17111311-fbb1-5efa-ae68-b43e3dba3e73'}, {'abstract': 'The Samsung Galaxy Note II is either a really big phone or really small tablet, with so many features your contract will run out before you learn to use them all.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/samsungs-biggest-phone-or-smallest-tablet/', 'snippet': 'The Samsung Galaxy Note II is either a really big phone or really small tablet, with so many features your contract will run out before you learn to use them all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are the kind of person who likes to pore over a good owner’s manual (or in this case, owner’s Web page) you will love the Samsung Galaxy Note II.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Samsung’s Biggest Phone, or Smallest Tablet', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'majo