ole': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06b749fd-d9ca-5f7f-bf25-ab1afbd9cc2c', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06b749fd-d9ca-5f7f-bf25-ab1afbd9cc2c'}, {'abstract': 'Critics agree that the iPad Mini is a perfect form-factor, but argue that the iPad Biggie, the larger version with the retina display, is the perfect screen resolution. So which one do you buy?', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/the-ipad-mini-vs-the-ipad-biggie/', 'snippet': 'Critics agree that the iPad Mini is a perfect form-factor, but argue that the iPad Biggie, the larger version with the retina display, is the perfect screen resolution. So which one do you buy?', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s trouble in Pixeltown.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/technology/bits-ipadminiv/bits-ipadminiv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/technology/bits-ipadminiv/bits-ipadminiv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/technology/bits-ipadminiv/bits-ipadminiv-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/13/technology/bits-ipadminiv/bits-ipadminiv-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/technology/bits-ipadminiv/bits-ipadminiv-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The iPad Mini vs. the iPad Biggie', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APPLES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T12:34:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9761cfa-ec03-5725-8bbb-9f689df06705', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9761cfa-ec03-5725-8bbb-9f689df06705'}, {'abstract': 'A one- or two-word search in some search engines brings instant answers about local sunrise and sunset times.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/tip-of-the-week-sunrise-sunset-%e2%80%94-at-a-glance/', 'snippet': 'A one- or two-word search in some search engines brings instant answers about local sunrise and sunset times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the year winds down, sunset arrives earlier in the day. If you want to see just when darkness will fall next, just type the word “sunset” and your current ZIP code into the search box on the Google or Yahoo home page and hit the Enter key to see the time of the next sunset displayed at the top of the results page. Typing “sunrise” brings up the time of the next day’s first light. If your browser is set to use your computer or mobile device’s location data, you do not even need to include your ZIP code in the search box because the search engine already knows where you are.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Sunrise, Sunset — at a Glance', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T12:36:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.D. BIERSDORFER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c624825-8f3c-5511-8e9b-1f05ccdc5c8f', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c624825-8f3c-5511-8e9b-1f05ccdc5c8f'}, {'abstract': 'The husband-and-wife team talk about their collaboration on Mr. Apatow’s new comedy, “This Is 40,” in which Ms. Mann and Paul Rudd reprise their roles as a married couple not unlike Mr. Apatow and Ms. Mann.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/strange-bedfellows-judd-apatow-and-leslie-mann-on-the-making-of-this-is-40/', 'snippet': 'The husband-and-wife team talk about their collaboration on Mr. Apatow’s new comedy, “This Is 40,” in which Ms. Mann and Paul Rudd reprise their roles as a married couple not unlike Mr. Apatow and Ms. Mann.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Some couples throw themselves into their work so they can spend more time apart from each other, and then there are collaborators like Judd Apatow and Leslie Mann. This husband-and-wife team has become increasingly intertwined over the course of films like “Knocked Up” and “Funny People,” which Mr. Apatow wrote and directed and in which Ms. Mann played supporting characters. That partnership reaches a culmination of sorts in Mr. Apatow’s new movie, “This Is 40,” in which Ms. Mann and Paul Rudd reprise their “Knocked Up” roles as a married couple — not unlike Ms. Mann and Mr. Apatow — beset by problems at their workplaces and in their family. The film, which Universal will release on Dec. 21, also features Mr. Apatow and Ms. Mann’s daughters, Maude and Iris Apatow, who once again play the children of Ms. Mann and Mr. Rudd’s characters. All of which must make things interesting when the Apatow family goes home at the end of the day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/apatow/apatow-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/apatow/apatow-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/apatow/apatow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/apatow/apatow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/arts/apatow/apatow-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Strange Bedfellows: Judd Apatow and Leslie Mann on  ‘This Is 40’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'APATOW, JUDD', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mann, Leslie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T13:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed3cb957-0f9d-5b0d-9edb-071487bd295c', 'word_count': 1383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed3cb957-0f9d-5b0d-9edb-071487bd295c'}, {'abstract': 'In “This Is 40” Mr. Apatow is at the helm, his wife, Leslie Mann, and their daughters are in the cast, and the characters have grown up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/movies/judd-apatows-life-as-art-in-this-is-40.html', 'snippet': 'In “This Is 40” Mr. Apatow is at the helm, his wife, Leslie Mann, and their daughters are in the cast, and the characters have grown up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18APATOW_SPAN/18APATOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 287, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18APATOW_SPAN/18APATOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 287}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18APATOW_SPAN/18APATOW_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 490, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18APATOW_SPAN/18APATOW_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 980, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18APATOW_SPAN/18APATOW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18APATOW_SPAN/18APATOW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnail