nt years, the football player Tim Tebow is to be announced on Wednesday morning as the new “brand ambassador” for TiVo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tebow, Meet TiVo … TiVo, Meet Tebow', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebow, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TiVo Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T13:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9753374-411d-5ddb-b7a3-50000456cccb', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9753374-411d-5ddb-b7a3-50000456cccb'}, {'abstract': 'For the past week, hundreds of military veterans from across the nation have flocked to Far Rockaway, summoned by a beacon from Team Rubicon, a nonprofit created by veterans to help other veterans through a therapy known as disaster relief.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/hundreds-of-veterans-help-sandy-victims-and-each-other/', 'snippet': 'For the past week, hundreds of military veterans from across the nation have flocked to Far Rockaway, summoned by a beacon from Team Rubicon, a nonprofit created by veterans to help other veterans through a therapy known as disaster relief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They have come from as far as Alaska to tear down water-damaged walls and clear debris from flood-ravaged yards. They have been assigned team leaders and given marching orders. They have been asked to work in the rain, sleep on a gym floor and eat military Meals Ready to Eat. If that all sounds like a military humanitarian mission, well, that’s sort of the idea.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hundreds of Veterans Help Sandy Victims and Each Other', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far Rockaway (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockaway Beach (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T13:05:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ade3579f-9c40-5537-9070-8ecd384692d9', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ade3579f-9c40-5537-9070-8ecd384692d9'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/opinion-report-military-standards/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: Military Standards', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T13:07:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1757c849-4b05-5faa-855c-4c4354573e67', 'word_count': 67, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1757c849-4b05-5faa-855c-4c4354573e67'}, {'abstract': 'According to several current and former Microsoft executives, several run-ins with other company leaders led to Steven Sinofsky’s departure, reports Nick Wingfield in The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/daily-report-sinofskys-abrasive-nature/', 'snippet': 'According to several current and former Microsoft executives, several run-ins with other company leaders led to Steven Sinofsky’s departure, reports Nick Wingfield in The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steven Sinofsky’s abrasive style was a source of discord within Microsoft, and he and Steven A. Ballmer, Microsoft’s chief executive, agreed that it was time for him to leave, reports Nick Wingfield in The New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: Sinofsky’s Abrasive Nature', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sinofsky, Steven', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T13:13:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07fbd0b4-cd88-5a6a-81ec-d843b8aeb6c5', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07fbd0b4-cd88-5a6a-81ec-d843b8aeb6c5'}, {'abstract': 'Why are Chinese coming to Japan, an expensive country they are raised to dislike, with an economy that’s shrinking while China’s is expanding?', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/the-new-japanese-worker-is-chinese/', 'snippet': 'Why are Chinese coming to Japan, an expensive country they are raised to dislike, with an economy that’s shrinking while China’s is expanding?', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — These days Japan’s newsstands are filled with shrill, hyperbolic and sometimes nationalistic titles about China. “The China Risk.” “The End of China.” “China: Withdraw or Stay the Course.” Such headlines reflect the anxiety of a declining nation that fears its rising neighbor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New Japanese Worker is Chinese', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Workers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Part-Time Employment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T13:14:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Harney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dbbd118-0c6b-5db4-91fa-9dd25b7265f1', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dbbd118-0c6b-5db4-91fa-9dd25b7265f1'}, {'abstract': 'The S.E.C. is being pressed to adopt new rules for money market funds. | Lawyers for two former hedge fund managers in an insider trading case are trying to discredit government witnesses. | About 804 million Facebook shares are becoming eligible to be sold. | Costco, Walmart and Home Depot are giving new meaning to the term “retail bank.”', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/new-push-for-money-fund-rules/', 'snippet': 'The S.E.C. is being pressed to adopt new rules for money market funds. | Lawyers for two former hedge fund managers in an insider trading case are trying to discredit government witnesses. | About 804 million Facebook shares are becoming eligible ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'After heavy lobbying by the industry, the Securities and Exchange Commission failed earlier this year to adopt new rules designed to protect money market funds. Now, regulators are aggressively demanding action. The top regulators who are part of the Financial Stability Oversight Council voted on Tuesday on three proposed rule changes to bring to the S.E.C. If the changes are not adopted, the council could impose its own oversight on money market funds, Edward Wyatt reports in The New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Push for Money Fund Rules', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T13:19:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c58a7f5a-3c8d-5962-9949-e341f0830906', 'word_count': 1565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c58a7f5a-3c8d-5962-9949-e341f0830906'}, {'abstract': 'Foaming rivers, in Nairobi now and New York a few short decades ago.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/no-river-should-be-doing-that/', 'snippet': 'Foaming rivers, in Nairobi now and New York a few short decades ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just over a week ago, M. Sanjayan, the lead scientist for the Nature Conservancy, posted photos of a “suds tsunami” rising from a polluted river in Nairobi and spilling over a highway. He’s added this video snippet, in which you can here him say, “No river should be doing that. Mountains of foam, in Nairobi.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘No River Should Be Doing That’', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HUDSON RIVER', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature Conservancy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beacon (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fishkill (NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T13:24:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55ed9d2b-cdee-57eb-a5e8-04b1d87ebec6', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55ed9d2b-cdee-57eb-a5e8-04b1d87ebec6'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: A young man’s compliment to an 86-year-old woman started a chain reaction.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/beaut