roduction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Erbil (Iraq)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevron Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Total SA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Exxon Mobil Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T14:07:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Reed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7646ab6-128a-51bb-8831-41c58b57d137', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7646ab6-128a-51bb-8831-41c58b57d137'}, {'abstract': 'On Thursday, the American League will announce the winner of its Most Valuable Player award. It is likely to be Miguel Cabrera, the Detroit Tigers star who won the league’s triple crown. But most statistically minded fans favor another player.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/the-statistical-case-against-cabrera-for-m-v-p/', 'snippet': 'On Thursday, the American League will announce the winner of its Most Valuable Player award. It is likely to be Miguel Cabrera, the Detroit Tigers star who won the league’s triple crown. But most statistically minded fans favor another player.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, the American League will announce the recipient of its Most Valuable Player award. The winner is likely to be Miguel Cabrera, the Detroit Tigers star who won the league’s triple crown by leading in batting average (.330), home runs (44) and runs batted in (139).', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Statistical Case Against Cabrera for M.V.P.', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'M.V.P. Debate Goes Beyond The Numbers in a Box Score', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statistics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cabrera, Miguel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trout, Mike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Angels of Anaheim', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T14:13:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5ba1556-d38c-5f84-bf82-395da8db4698', 'word_count': 1466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5ba1556-d38c-5f84-bf82-395da8db4698'}, {'abstract': 'A much better term than “fiscal cliff”.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/the-austerity-bomb/', 'snippet': 'A much better term than “fiscal cliff”.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brian Beutler of Talking Points Memo seems to have been the first to use the phrase “austerity bomb” for what’s scheduled to happen at the end of the year. It’s a much better term than “fiscal cliff”. The cliff stuff makes people imagine that it’s a problem of excessive deficits when it’s actually about the risk that the deficit will be too small; also and relatedly, the fiscal cliff stuff enables a bait and switch in which people say “so, this means that we need to enact Bowles-Simpson and raise the retirement age!” which have nothing at all to do with it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Austerity Bomb', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T14:22:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28ec6080-299c-524f-ad26-43b8f5480d07', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28ec6080-299c-524f-ad26-43b8f5480d07'}, {'abstract': 'U.S. lineup for Wednesday’s friendly international at Russia.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/u-s-lineup-vs-russia/', 'snippet': 'U.S. lineup for Wednesday’s friendly international at Russia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is the starting lineup, and substitutes, for the United States for its friendly international match against Russia in Krasnodar on Wednesday (ESPN2, ESPN3, Univision Deportes; 10 a.m. Eastern).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Lineup vs. Russia', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T14:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d4bbd82-ea9a-5674-9007-c43a5dd07d44', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d4bbd82-ea9a-5674-9007-c43a5dd07d44'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Nancy Pelosi of California has decided to stay in Congress and serve as House Democratic leader for another two years, an aide said Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/pelosi-to-remain-in-congress-and-continue-as-democratic-leader/', 'snippet': 'Representative Nancy Pelosi of California has decided to stay in Congress and serve as House Democratic leader for another two years, an aide said Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:42 p.m. | Updated  A revised version of this post appears here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pelosi Will Remain Democratic Leader in House; Few Changes in Leadership', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelosi, Nancy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T14:36:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer and John H. Cushman Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Cushman', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/757cdda2-c70f-5f59-8c20-f60a9590c118', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/757cdda2-c70f-5f59-8c20-f60a9590c118'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/what-were-reading-567/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vulture: MTV is shooting a culinary talk show; now we KNOW the 18-to-24-year-olds are into food. Even if the host is Vinny from “Jersey Shore.” — Julia Moskin', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T14:40:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8196f9dc-205e-5543-b333-a56b7a238634', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8196f9dc-205e-5543-b333-a56b7a238634'}, {'abstract': 'Pat Robertson speaks.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/all-about-the-patriarchy/', 'snippet': 'Pat Robertson speaks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a strand of thought — I identify it especially with Corey Robin, although he’s not alone — that says that conservatism isn’t really about the things it claims to be about. It isn’t really about free markets and moral values; it’s about authority — the authority of bosses over workers, of men over women, of whites over Those People.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'All About the Patriarchy', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T14:44:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5f8f024-d516-56b8-9fc5-7631af74651e', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5f8f024-d516-56b8-9fc5-7631af74651e'}, {'abstract': 'Participants in a training program in the South Bronx gain something beyond job skills.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/when-a-green-job-is-more-than-a-green-job/', 'snippet': 'Participants in a training program in the South Bronx gain something beyond job skills.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can a community like the South Bronx, which\xa0 suffers from\xa0 high unemployment, underinvestment and so-called environmental injustice, fit into the green economy? In 2010 a union-backed training initiative took on the question, enrolling unemployed\xa0 residents, including many who had served time in prison, in a green jobs certification program.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When a Green Job Is More Than a Green Job', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vocational Training', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T14:44:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Crean', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crean', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/232a4136-50d8-50ef-86c4-15973268ff9a', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/232a4136-50d8-50ef-86c4-15973268ff9a'}, {'abstract': 'Also, The Washington Post brings in a new top editor, Martin Baron of The Boston Globe, to succeed its current editor, Marcus Brauchli.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/the-breakfast-meeting-petraeuss-lost-privacy-and-colberts-disappearing-super-pac/', 'snippet': 'Also, The Washington Post brings in a new top editor, Martin Baron of The Boston Globe, to succeed its current editor, Marcus Brauchli.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The prominent people — including two generals atop the nation’s security apparatus — swept up in the investigation of a private conflict between two women illustrate the threat to privacy when law enforcement officials begin examining online communications, Scott Shane reports. “It’s a particular problem with cyberinvestigations — they rapidly become open-ended because there’s such a huge quantity of information available and it’s so easily searchable,” said Marc Rotenberg, executive director of the Electronic Privacy Information Center in Washington, adding, “If the C.I.A. director can get caught, it’s pretty much open season on everyone else.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Petraeus’s Lost Privacy, and Colbert’s Disappearing ‘Super PAC’', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baron, Martin D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brauchli, Marcus W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broadwell, Paula', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clash, Kevin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colbert, Stephen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weymouth, Katharine Bouchage', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sesame Workshop', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post Company', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T14:53:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b29c089-8ad5-5b3a-8447-4db359cb19d3', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b29c089-8ad5-5b3a-8447-4db359cb19d3'}, {'abstract': 'The Rev. Stephen S. Garmey, the vicar of Calvary Episcopal Church, died last month at 79, and he was too consummate a New York character to let go so easily.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/an-episcopal-vicar-who-loved-avant-garde-russian-art/', 'snippet': 'The Rev. Stephen S. Garmey, the vicar of Calvary Episcopal Church, died last month at 79, and he was too consummate a New York character to let go so easily.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:09 p.m. | Updated There is no way to say this but sheepishly: the death of the Rev. Stephen S. Garmey on Oct. 4 went unrecorded in the news columns of The New York Times, and he was too consummate a New York character to let go so easily.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Episcopal Vicar Who Loved Avant-Garde Russian Art', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garmey, Jane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calvary Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gramercy Park (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T14:53:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f436d669-6ee3-51f2-ac91-cdf05542efae', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f436d669-6ee3-51f2-ac91-cdf05542efae'}, {'abstract': 'Troubles in the euro zone and rising prices may send the British economy back into contraction in the fourth quarter, the governor of the Bank of England said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/business/global/bank-of-england-offers-somber-assessment-of-uk-economy.html', 'snippet': 'Troubles in the euro zone and rising prices may send the British economy back into contraction in the fourth quarter, the governor of the Bank of England said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The British economy might shrink again in the fourth quarter as troubles in the euro zone and rising prices take their toll on a fragile recovery, Mervyn A. King, the governor of the Bank of England, said on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 