 a streak capped by a trip to the Western Conference finals in 2004. But that run has been followed by eight consecutive seasons without a playoff appearance, currently the longest drought in the N.B.A.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: Looking Into the Timberwolves’ Fast Start', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T15:42:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By JUSTIN KUBATKO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KUBATKO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b31960d5-a584-5b77-97b2-5eff585f8e47', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b31960d5-a584-5b77-97b2-5eff585f8e47'}, {'abstract': 'Astronomers and stargazers mourn growing light pollution in India’s capital city.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/delhis-disappearing-night-sky/', 'snippet': 'Astronomers and stargazers mourn growing light pollution in India’s capital city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You could be pardoned for thinking that light pollution is someone’s idea of a Diwali joke.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Delhi’s Disappearing Night Sky', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Astronomy and Astrophysics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diwali (Hindu Festival)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lighting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stars and Galaxies', 'r