name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b1c226a-a6f8-5dc7-9483-ce85820a0600', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b1c226a-a6f8-5dc7-9483-ce85820a0600'}, {'abstract': 'In David H. Petraeus’s state of residence, Virginia, as in 22 others, adultery remains a criminal act, a vestige of the way the law has tried to anchor sexual activity within marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/us/adultery-an-ancient-crime-still-on-many-books.html', 'snippet': 'In David H. Petraeus’s state of residence, Virginia, as in 22 others, adultery remains a criminal act, a vestige of the way the law has tried to anchor sexual activity within marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When David H. Petraeus resigned as director of the C.I.A. because of adultery he was widely understood to be acknowledging a misdeed, not a crime. Yet in his state of residence, Virginia, as in 22 others, adultery remains a criminal act, a vestige of the way American law has anchored legitimate sexual activity within marriage. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/world/adultery/adultery-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 623, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/world/adultery/adultery-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1246, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Adultery, an Ancient Crime That Remains on Many Books', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Adultery, an Ancient Crime That Remains on Many Books', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petraeus, David H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULTERY', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T15:55:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae798263-07ab-559f-8cf3-80af1b68d726', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae798263-07ab-559f-8cf3-80af1b68d726'}, {'abstract': 'Adam Silverman, a Los Angeles ceramics artist, will have a show of works opening this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/13/garden/adam-silverman-ceramics-show-opens-nov-17.html', 'snippet': 'Adam Silverman, a Los Angeles ceramics artist, will have a show of works opening this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adam Silverman’s latest pots, which will be on view in Los Angeles beginning this weekend, seem to have emerged from a volcano: they are intensely colored, craggily textured and in some cases evoke the flow of lava.Mr. Silverman, a ceramics artist who lives in Los Angeles, was trained as an architect at the Rhode Island School of Design. A few years ago, he decided to devote himself full time to making pottery. From 2010 to 2012, he created pieces for the Kimbell Art Museum in Fort Worth, using only materials unearthed at the site of the Renzo Piano-designed pavilion that will complement the existing Louis Kahn building. \xa0Those works are smooth, large and monotone, the colors reminiscent of hard soil, arid greenery and excavated concrete.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/garden/13eventspic/13eventspic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 576, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/garden/13eventspic/13eventspic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1950, 'width': 1097, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/garden/13eventspic/13eventspic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/13/garden/13eventspic/13eventspic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/13/garden/13eventspic/13eventspic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Functional Pots With Decorative Expression', 'kicker': 'Currents | Events', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Functional Pots With Decorative Expression', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T15:57:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maria Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e28473b2-f2aa-5f58-9114-3324505bbd82', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e28473b2-f2aa-5f58-9114-3324505bbd82'}, {'abstract': 'A new show at the Vitra Design Museum in Germany examines the influence of pop culture on everyday life.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/now-showing-pop-art-design/', 'snippet': 'A new show at the Vitra Design Museum in Germany examines the influence of pop culture on everyday life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Showing | Pop Art Design', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T16:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f948b98e-bb83-591d-abfe-371f4080986a', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f948b98e-bb83-591d-abfe-371f4080986a'}, {'abstract': 'Sportswriters spared no outrage for the Marlins owner Jeffrey Loria after the team’s latest fire sale left even his remaining players venting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/sports/the-marlins-no-1-problem.html', 'snippet': 'Sportswriters spared no outrage for the Marlins owner Jeffrey Loria after the team’s latest fire sale left even his remaining players venting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We would like to take this opportunity to congratulate the Marlins owner Jeffrey Loria because it is no small feat these days to emerge as the most deplorable person in sports. The competition is extraordinarily tough. Just to win Tuesday’s battle of reprobates, Loria had to nose out the former football star Jerramy Stevens, his rapsheet long enough to reach Jupiter, who was arrested on charges of assaulting his fiancée, the soccer player Hope Solo, a day before their planned wedding day. And both needed to edge ahead of the N.H.L., which is insulting each and every one of its fans with its “Save Us From Ourselves!” player lockout stretching into Month 2.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/baseball/15leadingpic/15leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/baseball/15leadingpic/15leadingpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1295, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/baseball/15leadingpic/15leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/baseball/15leadingpic/15leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/baseball/15leadingpic/15leadingpic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trading Away the Marlins’ Dignity', 'kicker': 'Leading Of