oyotas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Toyota is recalling 670,000 of its 2004-9 Prius hybrids in the United States to fix problems involving the loss of steering and the hybrid powertrain shutting down, the automaker has told the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toyota Recalling 670,000 Prius Hybrids in U.S.', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Toyota Recalls Priuses in U.S. To Fix Steering and Pumps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T16:34:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd846925-db25-5e0a-91c0-afcc6023db44', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd846925-db25-5e0a-91c0-afcc6023db44'}, {'abstract': 'The Dave Matthews Band announced that the profits of its Nov. 30 concert in New Jersey will go to help with recovery efforts after Hurricane Sandy.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/dave-matthews-concert-to-benefit-hurricane-recovery/', 'snippet': 'The Dave Matthews Band announced that the profits of its Nov. 30 concert in New Jersey will go to help with recovery efforts after Hurricane Sandy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Dave Matthews Band announced on Wednesday that it would devote the proceeds of its next arena concert in New Jersey to help with the recovery efforts after Hurricane Sandy, The Associated Press reported.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/14artsbeat-matthews/14artsbeat-matthews-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/14artsbeat-matthews/14artsbeat-matthews-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/14artsbeat-matthews/14artsbeat-matthews-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/14artsbeat-matthews/14artsbeat-matthews-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/14artsbeat-matthews/14artsbeat-matthews-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dave Matthews Concert to Benefit Hurricane Recovery', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dave Matthews Concert to Benefit Storm Recovery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dave Matthews Band', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Izod Center (East Rutherford, NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T16:39:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/549fea8c-b48b-54db-8690-b6c857d97d0b', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/549fea8c-b48b-54db-8690-b6c857d97d0b'}, {'abstract': 'All the talk of China taking over the world will remain just talk until Beijing can allow its people to function as normal during big events like the Party Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/china-party-paranoia/', 'snippet': 'All the talk of China taking over the world will remain just talk until Beijing can allow its people to function as normal during big events like the Party Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — As if by clockwork, last week the Internet in Beijing slowed to a crawl. Google and gmail would not open. My V.P.N., an essential tool to circumvent the Great Firewall, stopped working.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Party Paranoia', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T16:40:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clarissa Sebag-Montefiore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clarissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sebag-Montefiore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95e3e879-5429-5572-a208-823d7a18d1c8', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95e3e879-5429-5572-a208-823d7a18d1c8'}, {'abstract': 'In an improvisational exercise with friends, the choreographer and visual artist Simone Forti presented her new work, “That Fish Is Broke,” for Danspace Project’s series Judson Now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/arts/dance/simone-fortis-that-fish-is-broke-at-danspace-project.html', 'snippet': 'In an improvisational exercise with friends, the choreographer and visual artist Simone Forti presented her new work, “That Fish Is Broke,” for Danspace Project’s series Judson Now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thursday evening a woman walked into St. Mark’s Church and began telling the sparse crowd assembled there about her trip from California. As the woman, who looked to be in her 70s, talked serenely and informally, she traveled back and forth on a diagonal, her gesticulations exaggerating those that normally accompany speech. Her musings turned to the Moon, to the center of the Earth. As she related a Hopi folk tale about staying open to the universe as you make a name for yourself, her gestures mocked, as gently as possible, the notion of becoming famous.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/forti/forti-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 714, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/forti/forti-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1429, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/forti/forti-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/forti/forti-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/arts/forti/forti-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Improvisational Motion Can Lead to Cuddling', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Improvisational Motion Can Lead to Cuddling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Forti, Simone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T16:41:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a7c82f9-6bc3-5ae7-abc5-0da8e4a2f411', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a7c82f9-6bc3-5ae7-abc5-0da8e4a2f411'}, {'abstract': 'Sales of medications that target symptoms of normal aging are soaring, according to data recently released at the American Public Health Association’s annual meeting.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/fighting-off-age-at-the-pharmacy-counter/', 'snippet': 'Sales of medications that target symptoms of normal aging are soaring, according to data recently released at the American Public Health Association’s annual meeting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We wrinkle. We have night sweats. We forget names and wake, with brittle, unwanted consciousness, in the middle of the night. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting Off Age at the Pharmacy Counter', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Public Health Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Express Scripts Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T16:42:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith Graham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9280bd57-cb8b-5982-af24-8497676e19fa', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9280bd57-cb8b-5982-af24-8497676e19fa'}, {'abstract': 'Children’s Day celebrated across India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/image-of-the-day-nov-14/', 'snippet': 'Children’s Day celebrated across India.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: Nov. 14', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T16:45:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/adc5bc59-b3e1-5c37-8118-29