209-99fc93b1b34f'}, {'abstract': 'The story of the Corinth camp, where thousands of slaves found freedom — and heartbreak.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/grants-contraband-conundrum/', 'snippet': 'The story of the Corinth camp, where thousands of slaves found freedom — and heartbreak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lincoln administration may not have gone to war in 1861 to end slavery, but no one bothered to tell that to the slaves. Within six weeks of the firing on Fort Sumter, Gen. Benjamin Butler was forced to decide what to do with three slaves who escaped to Fortress Monroe on the north shore of Virginia’s James River. Butler, certainly no abolitionist, nonetheless refused to return the three to their owner, labeling them “contrabands of war.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grant’s Contraband Conundrum', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T17:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Beard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a52707d-991e-591e-a158-5515604f2807', 'word_count': 1585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a52707d-991e-591e-a158-5515604f2807'}, {'abstract': 'National oil companies are trying to translate ownership of massive reserves into a much more important position in the industry and the world.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/in-power-shift-national-oil-companies-gain-on-western-big-oil/', 'snippet': 'National oil companies are trying to translate ownership of massive reserves into a much more important position in the industry and the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Those of us attending the Oil and Money conference convened by the IHT and Energy Intelligence will likely take away two big themes. The more obvious one is the comeback of the North American oil and gas industry thanks to shale gas and oil. Shale plays are likely to turn the U.S. into both a natural gas and oil exporter, said Adam Sieminski, administrator of the U.S. Energy Information Administration, the U.S. government’s data repository.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/blogs/14rdv-oil-and-money-sinopec-station/14rdv-oil-and-money-sinopec-station-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/blogs/14rdv-oil-and-money-sinopec-station/14rdv-oil-and-money-sinopec-station-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1311, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Power Shift, National Oil Companies Gain on Western ‘Big Oil’', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shale', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rosneft', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sinopec Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Total SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T17:34:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World'