'snippet': 'In recent years, big corporations have used their size to rewrite the rules for paying the small businesses that supply them. In many cases, terms have gone from 30 days to 90 days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We have just published an article exploring what appears to be a burgeoning trend among big businesses: helping small businesses — with loans, mentoring, new opportunities and sometimes a combination of all three. While the story focuses on the efforts of Boston Beer Company, large companies across the commercial spectrum, including financial giants and national retailers, have joined in.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'There’s a Great Way Big Businesses Could Help Small Businesses', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Beer Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Beer Company Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T18:12:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b94000d8-f7e2-5a02-815a-52f1f9489107', 'word_count': 883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b94000d8-f7e2-5a02-815a-52f1f9489107'}, {'abstract': 'If MOOCs are determined to be close enough to traditional college courses, they could make higher education more affordable and accessible.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/mooc-college-credit/', 'snippet': 'If MOOCs are determined to be close enough to traditional college courses, they could make higher education more affordable and accessible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the prevalence of massive open online courses, or MOOCs, gain momentum, the American Council on Education has announced a new project that would determine whether these MOOCs should be eligible for college credit. Our colleague Tamar Lewin reports:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should MOOCs Be Eligible for College Credit?', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewin, Tamar', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN COUNCIL ON EDUCATION', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T18:15:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/771e581c-7c44-54ea-a083-1e5c9a05c6c4', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/771e581c-7c44-54ea-a083-1e5c9a05c6c4'}, {'abstract': 'Japanese high school athletes who survived the tsunami last year wrote essays about the devastation — and the healing power of sports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/sports/after-the-disaster-a-miraculous-canoe.html', 'snippet': 'Japanese high school athletes who survived the tsunami last year wrote essays about the devastation — and the healing power of sports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the once-in-a-millennium tsunami struck northeastern Japan on March 11, 2011, it killed thousands of people and destroyed vast stretches of a rugged coastline. As the survivors in Fukushima, Miyagi and Iwate Prefectures started putting their lives back together, they came to rely on each other more than ever.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/belson2/belson2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1021, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/belson2/belson2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1021, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/belson2/belson2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/belson2/belson2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/belson2/belson2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After the Disaster, a Miraculous Canoe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After the Disaster, a Miraculous Canoe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Canoes and Canoeing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 