tion-of-a-brilliantly-negative-restaurant-review/', 'snippet': 'The critic Pete Wells gave his first “poor” restaurant rating in The Times — and he did it memorably.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since Pete Wells took over the restaurant critic’s job in November 2011, he has never – until Wednesday — written a review that comes not only with no stars, but also with the label “poor.” (He has given only one four-star review, to Le Bernardin.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Question of a (Brilliantly) Negative Restaurant Review', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T19:12:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d3a26e9-f629-5e0e-a8d1-691a1d9a0f18', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d3a26e9-f629-5e0e-a8d1-691a1d9a0f18'}, {'abstract': 'The new investors joined Goldman Sachs in a new round of financing that values the streaming music service at $3 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/spotify-attracts-investments-from-coca-cola-and-fidelity/', 'snippet': 'The new investors joined Goldman Sachs in a new round of financing that values the streaming music service at $3 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Coca-Cola is becoming a minority investor in Spotify, as part of a new round of financing that will bring in $100 million and value the streaming music service at about $3 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spotify Attracts Investments From Coca-Cola and Fidelity', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coca-Cola Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fidelity Investments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Spotify', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T19:17:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario and Andrew Ross Sorkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c3f5745-84a3-58c7-bfd3-dd4417f2c81f', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c3f5745-84a3-58c7-bfd3-dd4417f2c81f'}, {'abstract': 'Rating the performance of U.S. players in an international friendly against Russia on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/player-ratings-russia-2-u-s-2/', 'snippet': 'Rating the performance of U.S. players in an international friendly against Russia on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States snatched an uneven tie against Russia in Krasnodar on Wednesday thanks to a goal in second-half injury time by Mix Diskerud. The match was the final one on the U.S. schedule this year as it looks ahead to the final round of regional World Cup qualifying matches that begin at Honduras on Feb. 6.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Player Ratings: Russia (2), U.S. (2)', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T19:24:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41dcf853-0374-5132-b978-3938fc06d060', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41dcf853-0374-5132-b978-3938fc06d060'}, {'abstract': 'Stacy Lewis, the first United States-born winner of the L.P.G.A. Player of the Year award since 1994, will get to take golf’s version of a victory lap at the Titleholders tournament in Naples, Fla.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/sports/golf/stacy-lewis-writes-her-own-ending-to-player-of-the-year-story.html', 'snippet': 'Stacy Lewis, the first United States-born winner of the L.P.G.A. Player of the Year award since 1994, will get to take golf’s version of a victory lap at the Titleholders tournament in Naples, Fla.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An hour before last year’s L.P.G.A. player of the year announcement, Stacy Lewis was in a hotel room working on the recipient’s speech. Yani Tseng of Taiwan, with seven tour victories, was the repeat winner and had asked Lewis for help putting her thoughts down on paper. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/lewis/lewis-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/lewis/lewis-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'c