day published a tape-recording of the famous, 1981 comments on race and the Republican party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republicans bristled with indignation during the 2012 campaign any time someone suggested that there might be a racial undertone (or overtone, or just a tone) to attacks on President Obama. You know, that he was a Kenya–born socialist Muslim just passing himself off as an American. There was no racial intent there, no “dog whistle.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lee Atwater’s ‘Southern Strategy’ Interview', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Atwater, Lee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T19:31:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d3390cf-5e55-51e9-8aea-7077691396aa', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d3390cf-5e55-51e9-8aea-7077691396aa'}, {'abstract': 'Black and white dresses from resort collections are rolling into stores now; gloves from Causse Gantier; and a nail polish that comes packaged as little pills inside a bottle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/11/15/fashion/20121115-BROWSING.html', 'snippet': 'Black and white dresses from resort collections are rolling into stores now; gloves from Causse Gantier; and a nail polish that comes packaged as little pills inside a bottle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Black and white dresses from resort collections are rol