 machines.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/an-afterlife-for-the-electric-car/', 'snippet': 'A prototype tests the potential for providing a market for past-their-prime batteries and providing storage for energy from intermittent sources like solar panels and wind machines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Advocates of electric cars and renewable energy have talked for years about repackaging the battery packs built for cars as home energy storage devices once they can no longer hold enough charge to run a vehicle. On Wednesday,  ABB and General Motors announced that they were trying out just that idea with the battery packs of five Chevy Volts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Afterlife for the Electric Car', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Batteries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABB LTD', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IMG Worldwide', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T20:12:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5ebaa83-c621-586b-ae42-180d98fd3f56', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5ebaa83-c621-586b-ae42-180d98fd3f5