-question-are-the-tigers-the-new-yankees/', 'snippet': 'For the second straight year, the Tigers made a big free agency splash by signing Torii Hunter for $26 million over two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to find anyone in baseball who doesn’t like Torii Hunter. He has been a remarkably productive and affable player over his 15-year major league career, bringing power and speed and a flair for playing the outfield to both the Twins and the Angels. Now the Tigers have made the winning bid to be Hunter’s third team, signing him to a two-year, $26 million deal, after the Angels decided that Hunter, at age 37, wasn’t worth re-signing with a $13.3 million qualifying offer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hunter Signing Prompts Question: Are the Tigers the New Yankees?', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dombrowski, Dave', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fielder, Prince', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunter, Torii', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martinez, Victor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Delmon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T20:39:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d23fb27a-b595-5381-9b02-b160e9ccbc69', 'w