n of the film “The Color Purple” on Saturday as part of a new initiative to feature celebrated films on socially responsible themes four times a year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'USA Network to Air ‘The Color Purple’ and Other Socially Responsible Films', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hammer, Bonnie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Network', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T21:51:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32206146-723f-544f-9c17-e62c1bffc02c', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32206146-723f-544f-9c17-e62c1bffc02c'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s copy chief loves Fitzgerald and Sedaris but thinks everyone should start with Garner’s Dictionary of Modern American Usage.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/how-to-read-like-a-magazine-language-cop/', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s copy chief loves Fitzgerald and Sedaris but thinks everyone should start with Garner’s Dictionary of Modern American Usage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rob Hoerburger is the chief of the magazine’s copy desk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/magazine/09-rob-hoerburger-books/09-rob-hoerburger-books-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'im