e': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3632a98f-45ef-578b-8259-869f68d77638', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3632a98f-45ef-578b-8259-869f68d77638'}, {'abstract': 'The president, Mr. Romney said in a call with donors, won by “giving targeted groups a big gift.”', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/romney-blames-loss-on-obama-gifts/', 'snippet': 'The president, Mr. Romney said in a call with donors, won by “giving targeted groups a big gift.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now we know that Mitt Romney did not “misspeak” when he whined to a big-money crowd that 47 percent of Americans mooch off government and “believe they are victims.” He meant precisely what he said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Blames Loss on Obama ‘Gifts’', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T23:17:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By ANDREW ROSENTHAL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ROSENTHAL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c6960bc-30ca-5f1e-b8fc-282b5f6c80f4', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c6960bc-30ca-5f1e-b8fc-282b5f6c80f4'}, {'abstract': 'Lawrence Wright’s book, “Going Clear: Scientology, Hollywood and the Prison of Belief,” is based on an article that appeared in The New Yorker.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/knopf-to-publish-pulitzer-prize-winners-investigation-of-scientology/', 'snippet': 'Lawrence Wright’s book, “Going Clear: Scientology, Hollywood and the Prison of Belief,” is based on an article that appeared in The New Yorker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawrence Wright, who won the Pulitzer Prize for general nonfiction in 2007 for his last book, “The Looming Tower: Al Qaeda and the Road to 9/11,” has written an investigation of the Church of Scientology, the Alfred A. Knopf publishing house announced Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knopf to Publish Pulitzer Prize Winner’s Investigation of Scientology', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In January, Knopf to Publish Investigation of Scientology', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Lawrence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Church of Scientology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knopf, Alfred A, Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T23:19:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e887099b-ce26-57a3-b83c-b88cdb8f543e', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e887099b-ce26-57a3-b83c-b88cdb8f543e'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers and bankers are suggesting that Greece offer a buyback of its debt, and possibly invoke clauses in its bond contracts to put pressure on debt holders to accept the offer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/business/global/greece-looks-at-offering-creditors-a-buyback-to-lower-its-debt.html', 'snippet': 'Lawyers and bankers are suggesting that Greece offer a buyback of its debt, and possibly invoke clauses in its bond contracts to put pressure on debt holders to accept the offer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — As Greece’s creditors bicker over the terms of its bailout, the government is examining a more radical approach that could reduce the country’s escalating debt pile in one fell swoop.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/business/global/15greekdebt/15greekdebt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/business/global/15greekdebt/15greekdebt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/business/global/15greekdebt/15greekdebt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/15/business/global/15greekdebt/15greekdebt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/business/global/15greekdebt/15greekdebt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece Examines a Debt Buyback as One Way to Reduce Its Burden', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece Examines a Debt Buyback as One Way to Reduce Its Burden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-14T23:21:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Landon Thomas Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Landon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ecd9875-6006-5165-90d1-ace8aa44edff', 'word_count': 1399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ecd9875-6006-5165-90d1-ace8aa44edff'}, {'abstract': 'Christopher Plummer reprises his stage role in “Barrymore,” about a hypothetical John Barrymore comeback.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/movies/barrymore-stars-christopher-plummer-erik-canuel-directs.html', 'snippet': 'Christopher Plummer reprises his stage role in “Barrymore,” about a hypothetical John Barrymore comeback.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A one-man spectacle, “Barrymore” doesn’t involve that blond charmer, Drew, she of the sunburst smiles and a production company called Flower Films to go with it. No, this Barrymore is her paternal grandfather, John (1882-1942), a theater star turned silent-screen Great Profile turned — depending on who tells the tale — legend, boozy washout or self-defeating tragedy. In 1963 Orson Welles, who knew of the burdens of fame, said that Barrymore’s Hamlet was the greatest he had seen, characterizing it as “a man of genius who happened to be a prince” and was “tender and virile and witty and dangerous.” The movies, alas, only gave us a screen test for that Hamlet.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/arts/15BARRY/15BARRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/15/arts/15BARRY/15BARRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/arts/15BARRY/15BARRY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 566, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/arts/15BARRY/15BARRY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1133, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/arts/15BARRY/15BARRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/15/arts/15BARRY/15BARRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/arts/15BARRY/15BARRY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Profile of a Great Has-Been Granted One Last Chance', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Profile of a Great Has-Been Granted One Last Chance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Plummer, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':