no one would call or bother me. Sometimes, in the middle of the night, I would go out for a short walk around my block. I was surprised to find that homeless people were sleeping inside a bank, lying between A.T.M.’s. In my travels, I’ve noticed this seems to be a growing phenomenon throughout Europe, a result of the economic crisis. When the producers of the “Why Poverty?” project invited me to contribute, I decided to make a short film to show what happens in these banks — the sleeping homeless people and the various reactions of those who encounter them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/opinion/video-opdoc-lullaby/video-opdoc-lullaby-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/14/opinion/video-opdoc-lullaby/video-opdoc-lullaby-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/opinion/video-opdoc-lullaby/video-opdoc-lullaby-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/14/opinion/video-opdoc-lullaby/video-opdoc-lullaby-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Lullaby’', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Lullaby’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T01:39:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Kossakovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kossakovsky', 'qualif