nytimes.com/2012/11/15/world/americas/canada-ruling-says-towers-windows-caused-deaths-of-900-birds-in-toronto.html', 'snippet': 'Judge William G. Turtle  dismissed charges against the building’s former owner after concluding that provincial laws were not intended to cover inadvertent deaths caused by glass.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A justice of the peace ruled Wednesday that the windows of a Toronto office tower killed 900 birds from 2008 to 2009. But William G. Turtle, the judge, dismissed charges against the building’s former owner after concluding that provincial laws were not intended to cover inadvertent deaths caused by glass. Albert Koehl, a lawyer at Ecojustice, the group that brought the prosecution, said an appeal was possible. New owners of the building, Consilium Place, recently installed a pattern over its windows to mitigate bird strikes. Another judge is to issue a decision in a case against owners of another Toronto building next month. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Ruling Says Tower’s Windows Caused Deaths of 900 Birds in Toronto', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Ruling Says Tower’s Windows Caused Deaths of 900 Birds in Toronto', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glass', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buildings (Structures)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T04:22:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/02ebf81b-ee15-53dc-b6dd-e55780c77299', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02ebf81b-ee15-53dc-b6dd-e55780c77299'}, {'abstract': 'Louise Erdrich won the fiction award for her novel “The Round House,” while other awards were given for nonfiction, poetry, young people’s literature and American letters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/us/louise-erdrichs-novel-the-round-house-wins-national-book-award.html', 'snippet': 'Louise Erdrich won the fiction award for her novel “The Round House,” while other awards were given for nonfiction, poetry, young people’s literature and American letters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beating out an unusually competitive field, Louise Erdrich won the National Book Award for fiction on Wednesday night for “The Round House,” a novel about a teenage boy’s effort to investigate an attack on his mother on a North Dakota reservation, and his struggle to come to terms with the violence in their culture.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/us/AWARDS/AWARDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/us/AWARDS/AWARDS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/us/AWARDS/AWARDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/15/us/AWARDS/AWARDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth'