None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Christie's", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T04:36:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d81c2359-e459-5ebe-9fb1-1b56b8de9b08', 'word_count': 820, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d81c2359-e459-5ebe-9fb1-1b56b8de9b08'}, {'abstract': 'Armed groups executed more than 250 civilians, including 83 children, in one area of the Democratic Republic of Congo this year, according to a United Nations report.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/world/africa/congo-un-report-cites-slaughter.html', 'snippet': 'Armed groups executed more than 250 civilians, including 83 children, in one area of the Democratic Republic of Congo this year, according to a United Nations report.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Armed groups executed more than 250 civilians, including 83 children, in one area of the Democratic Republic of Congo this year, according to a United Nations report published Wednesday. It said that rebels in North Kivu Province, along the border with Rwanda, killed the civilians between April and September. “The systematic human rights violations committed by these armed groups, including the slaughter of so many children, are the most serious we have seen in recent times” in Congo, said the United Nations high commissioner for human rights, Navi Pillay. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congo: U.N. Report Cites Slaughter', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Congo: U.N. Report Cites Slaughter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Congo, Democratic Republic of (Congo-Kinshasa)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T04:38:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e96a95c-cf97-505b-b156-13352266eb2a', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e96a95c-cf97-505b-b156-13352266eb2a'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Kumalo used his journalism experience to become a chronicler of the cruelties of apartheid and South Africa’s eventual emergence as a biracial democracy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/world/africa/alf-kumalo-south-african-photographer-of-apartheid-dies-at-82.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Kumalo used his journalism experience to become a chronicler of the cruelties of apartheid and South Africa’s eventual emergence as a biracial democracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alf Kumalo was an unlikely candidate to become one of South Africa’s leading documentary photographers. He had no formal training with a camera and began using one in the 1950s only because the newspaper he worked for as court reporter was so small that he was expected to take the photographs for his own articles. ', 'print_section': 'B'