t round of the N.C.A.A. men’s Division I soccer tournament.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An N.Y./N.J. N.C.A.A. Derby', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Soccer Championships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fairleigh Dickinson University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "St John's University", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T05:01:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Strauch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2af7e02f-13de-567d-b556-637e4399e740', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2af7e02f-13de-567d-b556-637e4399e740'}, {'abstract': 'An Australian reporter was repeatedly called on to ask questions during the Communist Party Congress, an event where foreign journalists are routinely stonewalled. How did she manage it?', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/a-foreign-reporter-serves-up-softballs-in-beijing/', 'snippet': 'An Australian reporter was repeatedly called on to ask questions during the Communist Party Congress, an event where foreign journalists are routinely stonewalled. How did she manage it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Before the Chinese Communist Party concluded its landmark congress on Thursday with a new roster of leaders, a mild furor broke out among the foreign press corps when an Australian journalist was allowed to ask questions at several official gatherings where overseas reporters are almost pathologically ignored. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 