mes.com/2012/11/16/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-assault.html', 'snippet': 'Israel on Friday said it was prepared to pause its assault during a visit by Egypt’s prime minister, a day after Palestinian militants fired hundreds of rockets and Israeli tanks rumbled toward the Gaza border.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIRYAT MALACHI, Israel — Israel and Hamas brushed aside international calls for restraint on Thursday and escalated their lethal conflict over Gaza, where Palestinian militants launched hundreds of rockets into Israeli territory, targeting Tel Aviv for the first time, and Israel intensified its aerial assaults and sent armored vehicles rumbling toward the Gaza border for a possible invasion.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/world/Gaza-1/Gaza-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/16/world/Gaza-1/Gaza-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/world/Gaza-1/Gaza-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/world/Gaza-1/Gaza-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/world/Gaza-1/Gaza-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/16/world/Gaza-1/Gaza-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/world/Gaza-1/Gaza-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel and Hamas Step Up Air Attacks in Gaza Clash', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel and Hamas Step Up Air Attacks in Gaza Clash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T07:33:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb638869-323e-56c7-b047-d7b327ec8b5f', 'word_count': 1353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb638869-323e-56c7-b047-d7b327ec8b5f'}, {'abstract': 'In the first session of the 2012 IHT Luxury Conference: The Promise of Africa, The Power of the Mediterranean, I talked with Simone Cipriani, the driving force behind the UN’s the Ethical Fashion Initiative, and designer IIlaria Venturini Fendi, about how fashion is helping alleviate poverty and empower African women.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/iht-luxury-conference-live-empowering-african-artisans/', 'snippet': 'In the first session of the 2012 IHT Luxury Conference: The Promise of Africa, The Power of the Mediterranean, I talked with Simone Cipriani, the driving force behind the UN’s the Ethical Fashion Initiative, and designer IIlaria Venturini Fendi, a...', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Not until I was standing knee deep in mud in the giant Kibera slum in Nairobi, or watched women in a female collective making bags for Stella McCartney in Kenya’s Great Rift Valley, did I really get what Simone Cipriani does. The dynamic Italian, part of a United Nations anti-poverty effort, the Ethical Fashion Initiative, is harnessing the creativity of African artisans to create true modern luxury touched by human hands. Ilaria Venturini Fendi from the famous Italian leather company plays her role by making bags with the slogan: Not Charity! Just Work!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'IHT Luxury Conference 2012: Empowering African Artisans', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T07:59:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Suzy Menkes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Suzy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Menkes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/288b2573-7a12-5047-9da5-3d3b30203032', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/288b2573-7a12-5047-9da5-3d3b30203032'}, {'abstract': 'The Shiv Sena leader’s death could spark riots among his supporters, many fear.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/with-bal-thackeray-on-life-support-mumbai-braces-for-violence/', 'snippet': 'The Shiv Sena leader’s death could spark riots among his supporters, many fear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rightist Hindu leader Bal Thackeray is on life support, a spokesman said, and reports that the 86-year old politician is near death brought Mumbai to a virtual standstill on Thursday, as businesses closed and\xa0 residents cleared the streets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Bal Thackeray on Life Support, Mumbai Braces for Violence', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vandalism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachchan, Amitabh', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shiv Sena', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T09:10:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6276eeab-02bb-5df1-ad89-505394ed2f8d', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6276eeab-02bb-5df1-ad89-505394ed2f8d'}, {'abstract': 'Differences have grown greater than similarities, author says, though there is always cricket.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/in-india-cross-border-bengali-pride-fades-with-a-new-generation/', 'snippet': 'Differences have grown greater than similarities, author says, though there is always cricket.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You know what the problem with you kids today is,” one of our Bengali teachers in school would say, his anger barely controlled. “You don’t value your culture, your heritage.” And then his finger would point in the direction we assumed was the east. “Unlike our brothers across the border.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In India, Cross-Border Bengali Pride Fades With a New Generation', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identification Devices', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Anthems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tagore, Rabindranath', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Calcutta (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bengal (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T09:18:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arnab Ray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arnab', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb8a35ad-ea38-5fad-adf3-43b27c893da8', 'word_count': 872, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb8a35ad-ea38-5fad-adf3-43b27c893da8'}, {'abstract': 'Although tragically separated, the countries should forge a new relationship, not dwell on nostalgia, author says.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/in-bangladesh-stranded-on-the-borders-of-two-bengals/', 'snippet': 'Although tragically separated, the countries should forge a new relationship, not dwell on nostalgia, author says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every time I am in Kolkata for work, something very specific happens at dinner. My host takes me aside, wanting to tell me about their family home in pre-1947 East Bengal. Often that home is in Chittagong, Comilla, Sylhet or Faridpur district, but it can be many other places as well. They will invariably talk about what was left behind– a well-ordered, bucolic life. Sensing both longing and reproach in these encounters, I always hesitate in my response.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Bangladesh, Stranded on the Borders of Two Bengals', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gandhi, Indira', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rahman, Mujibur', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tagore, Rabindranath', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of India (Marxist)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ayodhya (India)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kolkata (India)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bengal (India)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T09:20:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Naeem Mohaiemen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Naeem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohaiemen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dedf602-e517-505b-9570-4ddabb26a247', 'word_count': 1156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dedf602-e517-505b-9570-4ddabb26a247'}, {'abstract': 'Can you choose the word pair that best completes the sentences from the article?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/test-yourself-english-nov-15-2012/', 'snippet': 'Can you choose the word pair that best completes the sentences from the article?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the Sunday Magazine article “Robert De Niro: In Conversation.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, Nov. 15, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T09:31:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7304250d-b4c2-5a38-a947-5d29b1ee1010', 'word_count': 47, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7304250d-b4c2-5a38-a947-5d29b1ee1010'}, {'abstract': 'Austerity programs were likely to be scrutinized in light of the data, which pointed toward a recession continuing well into next year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/business/global/daily-euro-zone-watch.html', 'snippet': 'Austerity programs were likely to be scrutinized in light of the data, which pointed toward a recession continuing well into next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — The euro zone economy shrank for a second consecutive quarter, according to official data released Thursday, eliminating any doubt about whether the region is in recession and signaling that a long road to recovery remains.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4'