N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bair, Sheila C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T10:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2faa0645-2c7f-58da-b0fe-d3bd2bf95247', 'word_count': 1265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2faa0645-2c7f-58da-b0fe-d3bd2bf95247'}, {'abstract': 'Susannah Ray’s photos of the surfing community of Rockaway Beach in Queens were to her, for a time, a kind of love song. Now, in the aftermath of Hurricane Sandy, “They’re almost like a dirge.”', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/recalling-the-right-coast-before-the-storm/', 'snippet': 'Susannah Ray’s photos of the surfing community of Rockaway Beach in Queens were to her, for a time, a kind of love song. Now, in the aftermath of Hurricane Sandy, “They’re almost like a dirge.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Susannah Ray loves surfing, but she does not miss it. She misses home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recalling the ‘Right Coast,’ Before the Storm', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surfing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockaway Beach (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockaway Peninsula (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T10:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72d35154-c51a-5aa4-acbe-2920199cd371', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72d35154-c51a-5aa4-acbe-2920199cd371'}, {'abstract': 'How careful are you about what you post on social media or say in instant or text messages or in e-mail?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/how-careful-are-you-online/', 'snippet': 'How careful are you about what you post on social media or say in instant or text messages or in e-mail?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The director of the C.I.A., David H. Petraeus, resigned last week after the Federal Bureau of Investigation discovered he was having an extramarital affair. The F.B.I. began by investigating a civilian e-mail harassment case, but, as the bureau reviewed thousands of pages of private e-mails, the scandal widened — to General Petraeus and others. While this scandal raises many questions about ethics, it also raises questions about online privacy and expectations of privacy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/world/ASSESS-LN/ASSESS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/14/world/ASSESS-LN/ASSESS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/world/ASSESS-LN/ASSESS-jumbo.j