s imprint. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Two-Book Deal for ‘Gone Girl’ Author Gillian Flynn', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Random House’s 2-Book Deal For ‘Gone Girl’ Author', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flynn, Gillian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Delacorte Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Random House', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T13:41:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f4770d6-f5dd-5469-ae68-e9448e93a15c', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f4770d6-f5dd-5469-ae68-e9448e93a15c'}, {'abstract': 'From months-long photographic exposures of the construction and destruction of Berlin to a show of images by Dennis Hopper, the city is currently a veritable candy store of photography.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/history-in-pictures-all-over-berlin/', 'snippet': 'From months-long photographic exposures of the construction and destruction of Berlin to a show of images by Dennis Hopper, the city is currently a veritable candy store of photography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — In the basement of a gallery on the Pariser Platz — where Mickey Mouse and fake Soviet officers are often seen posing in front of the Brandenburg Gate — a photography exhibition is devoted to events in a different part of the world. “Cairo: Open City – New Testimonies from an Ongoing Revolution,” addresses how current history is being documented. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/arts/15rdv-palast/15rdv-palast-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 537, 'width': 750, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/arts/15rdv-palast/15rdv-palast-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 537, 'width': 750, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'History in Pictures, All Over Berlin', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hopper, Dennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newman, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Germany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T13:57:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher F. Schuetze', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Schuetze', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a341e90-581b-563d-a9f0-a8205b3180de', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a341e90-581b-563d-a9f0-a8205b3180de'}, {'abstract': 'A family pilgrimage to Italy puts the past in a new light.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/back-to-bernalda/', 'snippet': 'A family pilgrimage to Italy puts the past in a new light.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My grandfather Agostino Coppola came to America from the southern Italian village of Bernalda, in the region now known as Basilicata. An irascible character known for his stories, he had seven sons, who all tended to imitate him and to whom he passed his stories. Of those seven sons, only two are left (my father, Carmine, died in 1991): my 98-year-old uncle Mikey, who is my godfather, and my uncle Anton, a noted composer and conductor still working at the age of 95. In the past 12 years he’s written an opera, “Sacco and Vanzetti”; rewritten the libretto of Puccini’s only failure, “Edgar;” and done extensive revisions for “The Merry Widow.” Anton became known to us as Uncle Kiki, so named because my brother, as a child, had a friend named Dickie and called everyone “Kiki.” The name stuck.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '145', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Back to Bernalda', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back To Bernalda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T14:01:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis Ford Coppola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'Ford', 'lastname': 'Coppola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63865697-de6d-596a-a819-ea54cbf709b5', 'word_count': 1438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63865697-de6d-596a-a819-ea54cbf709b5'}, {'abstract': 'You’re all takers.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/the-moocher-majority/', 'snippet': 'You’re all takers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lots of people having fun with Mitt Romney’s post-election diagnosis, which is that President Obama played dirty: he won peoples’ votes by — horrors — actually making their lives better:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Moocher Majority', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T14:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e813109-5807-5bc5-b950-c7737fe9e4e5', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e813109-5807-5bc5-b950-c7737fe9e4e5'}, {'abstract': 'A bill that is intended to shore up the nation’s electronic defenses failed to advance in the Senate on Wednesday, after a motion to force a vote fell short of the 60 votes needed to pass. That could lead President Obama to sign an executive order on the issue.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/daily-report-cybersecurity-bill-stalls/', 'snippet': 'A bill that is intended to shore up the nation’s electronic defenses failed to advance in the Senate on Wednesday, after a motion to force a vote fell short of the 60 votes needed to pass. That could lead President Obama to sign an executive order...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bill that is intended to shore up the nation’s electronic defenses failed to advance in the Senate on Wednesday. That could lead President Obama to sign an executive order on the issue. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-rep