 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Earvin', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebow, Tim', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Price, David Taylor', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T16:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42f18011-cb3c-5c7e-afb0-3a9ffbec5d8a', 'word_count': 834, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42f18011-cb3c-5c7e-afb0-3a9ffbec5d8a'}, {'abstract': 'Radical activity from the 1960s and beyond, as well as the aftermath of Sept. 11, led David Mamet to write his new play, “The Anarchist,” now in previews and starring Patti LuPone and Debra Winger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/theater/david-mamet-on-his-inspirations-for-the-anarchist.html', 'snippet': 'Radical activity from the 1960s and beyond, as well as the aftermath of Sept. 11, led David Mamet to write his new play, “The Anarchist,” now in previews and starring Patti LuPone and Debra Winger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON the morning of Sept. 11, 2001, I was in a hotel in Toronto. The morning paper had a reprint of a Chicago Tribune interview, run that Sunday, with Bill Ayers, a member of the radical Weather Underground in the 1960s. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18ANARCHIST1_SPAN/18ANARCHIST1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name