 be open to outside students accepted to the program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Starting next fall, 10 prominent universities, including Duke, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill and Northwestern, will form a consortium called Semester Online, offering about 30 online courses to both their students — for whom the classes will be covered by their regular tuition — and to students elsewhere who would have to apply and be accepted and pay tuition of more than $4,000 a course. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'University Consortium to Offer Small Online Courses for Credit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'University Consortium to Offer Small Online Courses for Credit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duke University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of North Carolina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Northwestern University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T16:43:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hannah Seligson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seligson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a2d5181-bd69-50ed-8445-67fea7001891', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a2d5181-bd69-50ed-8445-67fea7001891'}, {'abstract': 'As soon as a patient is described as noncompliant, doctor shorthand for patients who don’t take their medication or follow medical recommendations, it’s as though a black mark is branded on the chart.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/when-the-patient-is-noncompliant/', 'snippet': 'As soon as a patient is described as noncompliant, doctor shorthand for patients who don’t take their medication or follow medical recommendations, it’s as though a black mark is branded on the chart.', 'lead_paragraph': '“A 63-year-old man with hypertension, elevated cholesterol and diabetes,” the intern recited as he presented the case to me in clinic. He read the list of seven medications the patient was prescribed. “But he’s noncompliant,” the intern added.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/health/08well_ofri/08well_ofri-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 455, 'width': 446, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/health/08well_ofri/08well_ofri-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 455, 'width': 446, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/health/08well_ofri/08well_ofri-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/08/health/08well_ofri/08well_ofri-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/08/health/08well_ofri/08well_ofri-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Patient Is ‘Noncompliant’', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T16:44:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Ofri, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ofri', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d88d09f2-bd45-55d0-b658-bc1ed4abf69d', 'word_count': 834, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d88d09f2-bd45-55d0-b658-bc1ed4abf69d'}, {'abstract': 'A $5 million donation will lead to a state-of-the-art screening room for Columbia’s new arts center.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/columbia-to-get-a-state-of-the-art-screening-room/', 'snippet': 'A $5 million donation will lead to a state-of-the-art screening room for Columbia’s new arts center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Katharina Otto-Bernstein, a filmmaker and graduate of Columbia University, is donating $5 million to create a state-of-the art screening room in the university’s new arts building, Columbia University officials announced.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Columbia to Get a State-of-the-Art Screening Room', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Columbia Grad Contributes To New Screening Room', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattanville (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T16:50:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28e8ce96-47dd-5191-8c59-226812611786', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28e8ce96-47dd-5191-8c59-226812611786'}, {'abstract': 'This special edition Jeep pays tribute to the members of the United States military by donating $250 to military charities for every model sold.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/jeep-patriot-freedom-edition-has-charity-link/', 'snippet': 'This special edition Jeep pays tribute to the members of the United States military by donating $250 to military charities for every model sold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeeps got their start as military vehicles in the 1940s, and even though they’ve ended up in countless civilian driveways, the company likes to remind us of its red, white and blue connection. That’s why exactly nobody was surprised at the announcement this week of the Jeep Patriot Freedom Edition. This special edition Jeep pays tribute to the members of the United States military by donating $250 to military charities for every model sold. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeep Patriot Freedom Edition Has Charity Link', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jeep Division of Chrysler', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T16:57:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Schembari', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schembari', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5002a18-53ed-5b50-a97a-5402c3b0dbe4', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5002a18-53ed-5b50-a97a-5402c3b0dbe4'}, {'abstract': 'Lovers of animation of all kinds are highly encouraged to head over to the New Museum on November 17 for a one-time screening of 20 new cutting-edge short films.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/cartoon-network-aboveground-animation-at-the-new-museum/', 'snippet': 'Lovers of animation of all kinds are highly encouraged to head over to the New Museum on November 17 for a one-time screening of 20 new cutting-edge short films.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lovers of animation of all kinds are highly encouraged to head over to the New Museum on Nov. 17 for “Aboveground Animation,” a one-time screening of 20 new cutting-edge animated short films. The screening is curated by the artist Casey Jane Ellison, who started an online archive and exhibition platform when she was a student at the Art Institute of Chicago. “I wanted to create awareness for animation,” explains Ellison, whose hilarious alter ego, Case Case, is the anchor of the online pop culture journal Status Update. “So rather than people uploading their work individually on YouTube, I thought it was important to create a more curated context.” The selection of films will run the gamut from digital to analog — full-on C.G.I. to hand-drawn or stop-motion animation. Participating artists include Robert Bittenbender, Cody Critcheloe, Erin Dunn, Steve Emmons, Lauren Gregory, Ryan Whittier Hale, Rhett LaRue, Jacolby Satterwhite, Monira Al Qadiri and Lale Westvind, as well as Ellison herself, who will moderate a post-screening discussion. So what made her get into animation in the first place? “When I was little, I watched an episode of ‘The Sopranos’ featuring a dream sequence in which Tony is interacting with an animated fish,” Ellison says, laughing. “I remember being really affected by the emotion conveyed in that scene, and the element of surprise. That’s when animation is really good — when you don’t know where it’s coming from.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cartoon Network | ‘Aboveground Animation’ at the New Museum', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T17:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felix Burrichter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burrichter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64ac7f30-580d-591d-b3bb-93e35de8eeff', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64ac7f30-580d-591d-b3bb-93e35de8eeff'}, {'abstract': 'In a Times Magazine profile from 19 years ago, the actor said there was tension between him and his father, who was an artist, over who would “overshadow” whom.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/past-forward-robert-de-niro-the-son/', 'snippet': 'In a Times Magazine profile from 19 years ago, the actor said there was tension between him and his father, who was an artist, over who would “overshadow” whom.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/magazine/14-deniro/14-deniro-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/14/magazine/14-deniro/14-deniro-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1285, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'super