aption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/nyregion/16hernandez/16hernandez-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspect in Patz Case Will Plead Not Guilty, Lawyer Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suspect in Patz Case Will Plead Not Guilty, Lawyer Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Confessions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patz, Etan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Pedro (1961- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T17:20:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Russ Buettner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Russ', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buettner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f9dd75f-7022-5ec2-8037-ae16c99a363a', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f9dd75f-7022-5ec2-8037-ae16c99a363a'}, {'abstract': 'My father was dying back home in New York. Across the country in Los Angeles, nothing seemed as real to me.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/hollywood-dreams/', 'snippet': 'My father was dying back home in New York. Across the country in Los Angeles, nothing seemed as real to me.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The summer I moved to Los Angeles, leaving New York City behind for good, a mix of disorientation and doubt crept over me. The tiny but cheap Hollywood sublet I’d arranged over the Internet for my husband and me might turn out to be a scam. Same with the job I’d found just before the move, sealed with a 15-minute phone conversation, no paperwork signed — I was sure I’d show up the first day to a blank stare, murmurs about a misunderstanding. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hollywood Dreams', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dreams', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T17:21:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Levin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Levin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7bdc975-6d99-5e37-913b-eda536c00646', 'word_count': 1376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7bdc975-6d99-5e37-913b-eda536c00646'}, {'abstract': 'As he plans a climate education push, President Obama says emission plans still have to mesh with economic priorities.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/with-economy-still-trumping-emissions-obama-plans-an-education-push-on-climate/', 'snippet': 'As he plans a climate education push, President Obama says emission plans still have to mesh with economic priorities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In case you missed President Obama’s first long discussion of human-driven global warming in recent memory, which came near the end of his news conference on Wednesday, here’s the brunt of it, as summarized on Twitter by  Will Oremus of Slate (found via Stephen Lacey):', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Economy Still Trumping Emissions, Obama Plans an Education Push on Climate', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cheney, Dick', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hansen, James E', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T17:27:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10b6d520-fe2e-5ef1-ac6f-ac7d14940d91', 'word_count': 1271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10b6d520-fe2e-5ef1-ac6f-ac7d14940d91'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/arts/television/whats-on-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (HBO) CROSSFIRE HURRICANE (2012) The director Brett Morgen culls from more than 1,000 hours of film, 500 hours of audio and 80 hours of new interviews to chronicle the 50-year history of the Rolling Stones and their transformation from, as Mick Jagger says, “the band everybody hated to the band everybody loves.” What sets the band apart from the rest? “A chemical reaction seems to have happened,” says Keith Richards (above, second from left, with his band mates Charlie Watts, left, Bill Wyman, Mr. Jagger and Ronnie Wood). “You can’t really stop the Rolling Stones. You know when that sort of avalanche is facing you, you just get out of the way.” Among the documentary’s highlights are depictions of the chaos that accompanied the band’s early tours; the birth of the Jagger-Richards songwriting partnership; the death of the guitarist Brian Jones in 1969 and the terror later that year at the Altamont Festival, where four people died; and Mr. Richards’s 1977 drug arrest in Toronto, which threatened to break up the band. In a recent interview with Jon Pareles in The New York Times, Mr. Richards pronounced himself amazed at the band’s longevity. “There is a certain magnetic glue that pulls us all together, that overrides any other peripheral things,” he said. “Once we get behind our instruments, there’s something bigger. The sum is greater than the parts. There’s just a feeling that we were meant to do this, we have to do this, and we’re just following the trail.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T17:31:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/86978fd0-8a2a-58b5-9a04-b97b0f84e1fc', 'word_count': 740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86978fd0-8a2a-58b5-9a04-b97b0f84e1fc'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Santino is the winner of the second annual New York Times Comedy Challenge, in which more than 8,000 readers decided which of six rising comedians killed.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/the-new-york-times-comedy-challenge-and-the-winner-is/', 'snippet': 'Andrew Santino is the winner of the second annual New York Times Comedy Challenge, in which more than 8,000 readers decided which of six rising comedians killed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 8,000 readers weighed in on our second annual New York Times Comedy Challenge, in which six rising comedians shared their best — but cleanest! — bit and we asked you to decide which one killed. Though the vote was close (fewer than 300 votes separated the front-runners), no one asked for a recount and we can declare a winner: Andrew Santino, with his lightning-fast riff on what is and isn’t in his dreams. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New York Times Comedy Challenge: And the Winner Is …', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T17:33:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be327b6f-6985-5ebf-aed9-d39af11febf7', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be327b6f-6985-5ebf-aed9-d39af11febf7'}, {'abstract': 'Investigations come after alle