url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/booming/why-do-i-feel-colder-as-i-get-older.html', 'snippet': 'Physiological changes or medical problems can make people more sensitive to cold as they age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As he turned to go on, he spat speculatively. There was a sharp, explosive crackle that startled him. He spat again. And again, in the air, before it could fall to the snow, the spittle crackled. He knew that at fifty below spittle crackled on the snow, but this spittle had crackled in the air. Undoubtedly it was colder than fifty below—how much colder he did not know.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/booming/15question-booming-cold/15question-booming-cold-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 228, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/15/booming/15question-booming-cold/15question-booming-cold-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 228}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/booming/15question-booming-cold/15question-booming-cold-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/booming/15question-booming-cold/15question-booming-cold-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 954, 'width': 1553, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/booming/15question-booming-cold/15question-booming-cold-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/15/booming/15question-booming-cold/15question-booming-cold-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/booming/15question-booming-cold/15question-booming-cold-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Am I So Cold?', 'kicker': 'Question Mark', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temperature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T18:08:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec6c8ea5-957a-5537-b899-e258d0f9b394', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec6c8ea5-957a-5537-b899-e258d0f9b394'}, {'abstract': 'Why does finding the precise word matter? In this lesson, students consider the advantages and disadvantages of using a thesaurus. Then, they choose from a variety of activities to go further in experimenting with word choice in writing.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/thank-you-thesaurus-experimenting-with-the-right-word-vs-the-almost-right-word/', 'snippet': 'Why does finding the precise word matter? In this lesson, students consider the advantages and disadvantages of using a thesaurus. Then, they choose from a variety of activities to go further in experimenting with word choice in writing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | Why use a thesaurus? Why does finding the precise word matter? In this lesson, students will explore the difference between the right word and the almost-right word and consider the advantages and disadvantages of using a thesaurus. Then, they choose from a variety of activities to go further in experimenting with word choice in writing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/opinion/draft-thesaurus-LN/draft-thesaurus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/opinion/draft-thesaurus-LN/draft-thesaurus-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1650, 'width': 1350, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/opinion/draft-thesaurus-LN/draft-thesaurus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/12/opinion/draft-thesaurus-LN/draft-thesaurus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/12/opinion/draft-thesaurus-LN/draft-thesaurus-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thank You, Thesaurus: Experimenting With the Right Word vs. the Almost-Right Word', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T18:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Christy Brown and Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': 'Christy', 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce801635-2f76-5cf3-b4fb-9d8467b11d09', 'word_count': 1943, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce801635-2f76-5cf3-b4fb-9d8467b11d09'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/14/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (Spike TV) EDDIE MURPHY: ONE NIGHT ONLY Thirty years after the release of “48 Hrs.,” the movie that made Mr. Murphy a star, Arsenio Hall, Samuel L. Jackson, Jeffrey Katzenberg, Martin Lawrence, Tracy Morgan, Charlie Murphy, Nick Nolte, Brett Ratner, Chris Rock and Stevie Wonder (above top, with Mr. Murphy) pay tribute to their friend and colleague in this two-hour special taped on Nov. 3 at the Saban Theater in Los Angeles. The house band is the Roots. Two of Mr. Murphy’s films lead in: “Coming to America” (1988), at 2:10 and 7:15 p.m., and “Beverly Hills Cop” (1984), at 4:50.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T18:16:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/00b922e3-5ffc-5696-a66d-98acce6c4133', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00b922e3-5ffc-5696-a66d-98acce6c4133'}, {'abstract': 'A new resource guide on the Foreign Corrupt Practices Act highlights the benefits to companies that voluntarily disclose potential violations and take remedial actions, but it leaves plenty of uncertainty.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/in-bribery-law-the-watchword-is-uncertainty/', 'snippet': 'A new resource guide on the Foreign Corrupt Practices Act highlights the benefits to companies that voluntarily disclose potential violations and take remedial actions, but it leaves plenty of uncertainty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department and the Securities and Exchange Commission on Wednesday released eagerly awaited guidance on the Foreign Corrupt Practices Act, a law that has become a bane to many multinationals. Enforcement of the statute has increased in the last few years, and is now a centerpiece in government efforts to police corporations with overseas operations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Bribery Law, the Watchword Is Uncertainty', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Corrupt Practices Act (1977)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T18:29:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f3431fd-db4f-573d-96de-c767613961f9', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f3431fd-db4f-573d-96de-c767613961f9'}, {'abstract': 'A lawyer representing San Francisco nudists has filed a class action lawsuit to overturn a city ordinance making it illegal to be nude in public.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/11/16/us/san-francisco-nudist-ban-lawsuit.html', 'snippet': 'A lawyer representing San Francisco nudists has filed a class action lawsuit to overturn a city ordinance making it illegal to be nude in public.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lawyer representing San Francisco nudists has filed a class action lawsuit to overturn a city ordinance making it illegal to be nude in public.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Class Action Complaint on San Francisco Nudity Ban', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nudism and Nudity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T18:31:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/ae88461c-dbb8-5ae7-9437-53ad79a2db3c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/ae88461c-dbb8-5ae7-9437-53ad79a2db3c'}, {'abstract': 'Bricks unleashed by the storm plunged through the roof of the Argosy Book Store in Manhattan, allowing rainwater to soak historic documents, including acts of Congress signed by Thomas Jefferson.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/storms-damage-extends-to-nations-history/', 'snippet': 'Bricks unleashed by the storm plunged through the roof of the Argosy Book Store in Manhattan, allowing rainwater to soak historic documents, including acts of Congress signed by Thomas Jefferson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a freezer in a building on East 59th Street, steps from Lexington Avenue, far from where Hurricane Sandy inflicted the most pain, are some papers. The temptation is to say that they are old and they are cold, and they are — that is true. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/nyregion/15cityroom-bookstore/15cityroom-bookstore-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/nyregion/15cityroom-bookstore/15cityroom-bookstore-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/nyregion/15cityroom-bookstore/15cityroom-bookstore-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/16/nyregion/15cityroom-bookstore/15cityroom-bookstore-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/nyregion/15cityroom-bookstore/15cityroom-bookstore-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Storm’s Damage Extends to Nation’s History', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pieces of History Suffer In Wind and Rain’s Wake', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Argosy Book Store', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T18:31:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6505aa29-1b0e-544b-8a16-f4618a4743cc', 'word_count': 779, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6505aa29-1b0e-544b-8a16-f4618a4743cc'}, {'abstract': 'The unemployment rate in New York City dropped in October but the figure does not reflect the effects of Hurricane Sandy.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/citys-unemployment-rate-dipped-in-october/', 'snippet': 'The unemployment rate in New York City dropped in October but the figure does not reflect the effects of Hurricane Sandy.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Before Hurricane Sandy roared through, New York City was adding jobs and its unemployment rate was declining, the State Labor Department reported on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City’s Unemployment Rate Dipped in October', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labor Department (NYS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T18:37:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Mc