ill return on newsprint in December at a cost of $5 an issue.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/a-counterculture-totem-to-return-as-a-leaner-magazine/', 'snippet': 'The influential music magazine Arthur, which in its earlier incarnation had a circulation of 40,000 as a free publication, will return on newsprint in December at a cost of $5 an issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From 2002 to 2008, Arthur was music’s version of a literary-minded “little magazine.” Distributed free in record stores and coffee shops, it celebrated underground culture of all kinds and attracted writers like Alan Moore (“Watchmen”), Douglas Rushkoff and even Thurston Moore of Sonic Youth, who wrote a reviews column with the critic Byron Coley.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Counterculture Totem to Return as a Leaner Magazine', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coley, Byron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Alan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Thurston', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rushkoff, Douglas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T18:45:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/356441ab-9ff8-55ab-b4c7-8e9dbd7513cf', 'word_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/356441ab-9ff8-55ab-b4c7-8e9dbd7513cf'}, {'abstract': 'Christiana Fisher, the former director of social service agencies that Assemblyman Vito J. Lopez controlled, admitted she had allowed inaccurate documents about a salary increase to be delivered to a grand jury.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/nyregion/christiana-fisher-director-with-ties-to-lopez-to-plead-guilty.html', 'snippet': 'Christiana Fisher, the former director of social service agencies that Assemblyman Vito J. Lopez controlled, admitted she had allowed inaccurate documents about a salary increase to be delivered to a grand jury.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The former longtime director of the network of social service agencies that for decades was controlled by Assemblyman Vito J. Lopez of Brooklyn pleaded guilty on Thursday to a federal criminal contempt charge stemming from inaccurate documents that appeared to justify an outsize salary increase she received.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Director of Agencies Controlled by Lopez Pleads Guilty to Contempt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Director of Agencies Controlled by Lopez Pleads Guilty to Contempt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Vito J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ridgewood-Bushwick Senior Citizens Council', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Christiana M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T18:45:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser and William K. Rashbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organizati