hannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Vijai', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Pedro', 'middlename': 'Rafael', 'lastname': 'Rosado', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/a2bdddaa-15bc-5de3-8b20-60c4692382a0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/a2bdddaa-15bc-5de3-8b20-60c4692382a0'}, {'abstract': 'The 101st campaign of The New York Times Neediest Cases Fund has begun. If your family is doing something creative to raise money for the fund, we want to hear from you.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/neediest-cases-the-youngest-donors/', 'snippet': 'The 101st campaign of The New York Times Neediest Cases Fund has begun. If your family is doing something creative to raise money for the fund, we want to hear from you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 101st campaign of The New York Times Neediest Cases Fund has begun. Every year, donors from all across the country open their hearts and wallets to help those who have fallen on hard times. If your child or family is\xa0 using creative techniques to raise money for this year’s campaign, we want to hear from you. Drop us a line on Facebook or Twitter or leave a comment below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Neediest Cases: The Youngest Donors', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T19:16:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efaaa49e-4ed4-51fe-8e0b-01ada5e1fc79', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efaaa49e-4ed4-51fe-8e0b-01ada5e1fc79'}, {'abstract': 'The Senator who wants to hold Watergate-style hearings about Benghazi missed a classified briefing about…Benghazi.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/john-mccains-scheduling-error/', 'snippet': 'The Senator who wants to hold Watergate-style hearings about Benghazi missed a classified briefing about…Benghazi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Poor John McCain. The senior senator from Arizona, former presidential candidate and general Republican big-man-in-Washington was so busy on Wednesday complaining about President Obama’s handling of the Benghazi mission killings that he just didn’t have time to do his actual job and attend a hearing on the Benghazi mission killings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'John McCain’s Scheduling Error', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Benghazi (Libya)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T19:17:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a486aae7-19e1-5f42-a379-c27d7c8368b0', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a486aae7-19e1-5f42-a379-c27d7c8368b0'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama and Mitt Romney won roughly an equal number of votes among straight voters, but the president carried the gay vote three to one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/us/politics/gay-vote-seen-as-crucial-in-obamas-victory.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama and Mitt Romney won roughly an equal number of votes among straight voters, but the president carried the gay vote three to one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While President Obama’s lopsided support among Latino and other minority voters has been a focus of postelection analysis, the overwhelming support he received from another growing demographic group — Americans who identify as gay, lesbian or bisexual — has received much less attention.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/us/GAY/GAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/16/us/GAY/GAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/us/GAY/GAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/us/GAY/GAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1285, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/us/GAY/GAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/16/us/GAY/GAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i