’s critically acclaimed memoir “Oddly Normal,” talks about himself, the book and life as a gay teen.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/learning-that-odd-is-normal/', 'snippet': 'In a new video, Joe Schwartz, the subject of his father’s critically acclaimed memoir “Oddly Normal,” talks about himself, the book and life as a gay teen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few months ago, I was at home reading a review copy of “Oddly Normal” by my colleague John Schwartz. The book begins with the suicide attempt of John’s then 13-year-old son, Joe, who had recently told his classmates he was gay. It goes on to explain how Joe’s parents struggled with a school system that didn’t always understand their son, and how Joe eventually found the path to self acceptance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Learning That Odd Is Normal', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T20:03:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c6a561e-e01f-5dea-8825-d63f61105cd3', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c6a561e-e01f-5dea-8825-d63f61105cd3'}, {'abstract': 'Now that R.A. Dickey has knuckled his way to a Cy Young Award, could others be far behind? Phil Niekro would like to find out.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/phil-niekro-godfather-of-knucklers-is-ready-to-help/', 'snippet': 'Now that R.A. Dickey has knuckled his way to a Cy Young Award, could others be far behind? Phil Niekro would like to find out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before his first game as a knuckleball pitcher, in 2006, R.A. Dickey had a 16-18 career record with a 5.55 earned run average. The advanced metric Wins Above Replacement scored him a 0.0, as calculated by Baseball-Reference.com. Essentially, Dickey was contributing no more or less value than any player who could be plucked from Class AAA.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/sports/baseball/16niekro/16niekro-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/sports/baseball/16niekro/16niekro-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/sports/baseball/16niekro/16niekro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/16/sports/baseball/16niekro/16niekro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/sports/baseball/16niekro/16niekro-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Phil Niekro, Godfather of Knucklers, Is Ready to Help', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickey, R A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Niekro, Phil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T20:04:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/536aae1b-11a6-5134-995a-343b42660e35', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/536aae1b-11a6-5134-995a-343b42660e35'}, {'abstract': 'Woody Johnson said he was not happy with the Jets’ performance this season, and refused to evaluate the performances of Mark Sanchez, Rex Ryan and Mike Tannenbaum.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/no-votes-of-confidence-from-jets-owner/', 'snippet': 'Woody Johnson said he was not happy with the Jets’ performance this season, and refused to evaluate the performances of Mark Sanchez, Rex Ryan and Mike Tannenbaum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. — The staggering Jets have lost five of their last six games to drop to 3-6, and a loss Sunday could have the organization considering an overhaul before Thanksgiving arrives. Yet the talk on Thursday had little to do with that critical game, at St. Louis.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/football/15woody/15woody-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 710, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/football/15woody/15woody-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1421, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/football/15woody/15woody-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/football/15woody/15woody-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/football/15woody/15woody-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Votes of Confidence From Jets Owner', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jets Keep Eye on Rams, When It’s Not on Tebow Or Ryan or the Owner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Woody', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T20:12:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Pedulla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pedulla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c85e283a-74a0-5584-81b8-81b8fa45b73e', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c85e283a-74a0-5584-81b8-81b8fa45b73e'}, {'abstract': 'In this capital city, you’ll find castles and culture, local wine and creative cuisine, homegrown fashion and textured history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/travel/36-hours-in-ljubljana-slovenia.html', 'snippet': 'In this capital city, you’ll find castles and culture, local wine and creative cuisine, homegrown fashion and textured history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SLOVENIA’S first city, Ljubljana, has its fair share of charming Old World plazas, baroque churches and dramatic castles. But this walkable capital (population 280,000) also has a rich cultural scene that would be impressive in a city twice its size. In the last few years, Ljubljana has seen several notable museum openings, a new public bike-rental program and a major renovation of its Hapsburg-era opera house. With the country surrounded by Italy, Austria, Hungary and Croatia, the national cuisine is infused with a cornucopia of influences; the capital’s latest restaurants are bypassing novelty and getting creative with traditional Slovenian fare. There are also surprisingly offbeat facets of the city, like Metelkova City, a cluster of clubs and galleries that opened inside a complex of former military buildings after Slovenia declared independence, in 1991. Elsewhere, remnants of a Roman wall built around A.D. 15 share a block with boxy Communist office buildings and Art Nouveau mansions from Austro-Hungarian times. Such juxtapositions contribute to the city’s distinctive character.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/travel/18HOURS1_SPAN-sf/18HOURS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 456, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/18/travel/18HOURS1_SPAN-sf/18HOURS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 456}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/travel/18HOURS1_SPAN-sf/18HOURS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 778, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_n