BP under federal environmental laws.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/opinion/criminality-in-the-gulf-spill.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama Administration must pursue further penalties against BP under federal environmental laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two and a half years after the massive gulf oil spill, BP has agreed to plead guilty to 14 criminal charges brought by the Justice Department and cough up $4.5 billion in fines and other payments. This is not the first financial penalty the British oil giant has paid for its careless and destructive behavior, nor should it be the last. Still to come are multibillion-dollar settlements under various environmental laws. The Justice Department must be no less diligent in pressing these claims and should not settle for anything less than what the gulf coast, its battered environment and its residents need to address the long-term consequences of this disaster. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Criminality in the Gulf Spill', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Criminality in the Gulf Spill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico Oil Spill (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Water Act', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Commission on the BP Deepwater Horizon Oil Spill and Offshore Drilling', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf Coast (US)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T20:38:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/890a1232-442f-5f14-916b-c1b7e005ff08', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/890a1232-442f-5f14-916b-c1b7e005ff08'}, {'abstract': 'Signs of a middle class with aspirations to more than the basics have encouraged major luxury brands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/business/global/fashion-houses-take-notice-of-africas-rise.html', 'snippet': 'Signs of a middle class with aspirations to more than the basics have encouraged major luxury brands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Has Africa’s golden moment arrived? For the gurus of the luxury world, the answer is a resounding yes — at least as a source of inspiration for design trends that are rippling through the fashion industry.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/business/Luxury1/Luxury1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/business/Luxury1/Luxury1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1599, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fashion Weighs a Deeper Investment in Africa', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fashion Weighs a Deeper Investment in Africa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject',