r to winding down one of the longer-running takeover sagas in recent memory, as the rental car company said on Thursday that it had won regulatory approval for its $2.3 billion takeover of the Dollar Thrifty Automotive Group.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hertz Wins F.T.C. Approval of Its Deal for Dollar Thrifty', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dollar Thrifty Automotive Group Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Trade Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hertz Global Holdings Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T21:39:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cf63ffd-0587-55ee-8129-98fd40f1b41c', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cf63ffd-0587-55ee-8129-98fd40f1b41c'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama and Mitt Romney won roughly an equal number of votes among straight voters nationwide, exit polls showed.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/gay-vote-seen-as-crucial-in-obamas-victory/', 'snippet': 'President Obama and Mitt Romney won roughly an equal number of votes among straight voters nationwide, exit polls showed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While President Obama’s lopsided support among Latino and other minority voters has been a focus of postelection analysis, the overwhelming support he received from another growing demographic group — Americans who identify as gay, lesbian or bisexual — has received much less attention.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gay Vote Seen as Crucial in Obama’s Victory', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T21:40:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micah Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5556b361-59f1-5e9d-965e-b8c788db1eae', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5556b361-59f1-5e9d-965e-b8c788db1eae'}, {'abstract': 'The estimate called into question whether the United States would have the resources to act quickly to thwart the movement of such weapons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/world/middleeast/pentagon-sees-seizing-syria-chemical-arms-as-vast-task.html', 'snippet': 'The estimate called into question whether the United States would have the resources to act quickly to thwart the movement of such weapons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Pentagon has told the Obama administration that any military effort to seize Syria’s stockpiles of chemical weapons would require upward of 75,000 troops, amid increasing concern that the militant group Hezbollah has set up small training camps close to some of the chemical weapons depots, according to senior American officials.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pentagon Says 75,000 Troops Might Be Needed to Seize Syria Chemical Arms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pentagon Says 75,000 Troops Might Be Needed to Seize Syria Chemical Arms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hezbollah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T21:54:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David E. Sanger and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Sanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d67aada-3e60-5725-ab67-6638ec5057f2', 'word_count': 1242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d67aada-3e60-5725-ab67-6638ec5057f2'}, {'abstract': 'Having bet their entire policy agenda on the defeat of President Obama, the G.O.P. now seems lost.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/republicans-adrift/', 'snippet': 'Having bet their entire policy agenda on the defeat of President Obama, the G.O.P. now seems lost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having bet their entire policy agenda on the defeat of President Obama, Congressional Republicans seem adrift. Their efforts to cast the president as a failure by stalling the economy didn’t work. Their furious and false denunciations of health-care reform came to nothing. Their promises that tax cuts for the wealthy would spur economic growth were disbelieved.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Adrift', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords'