al': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/86bbd013-43bb-5031-9caf-e5074093f115', 'word_count': 1496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86bbd013-43bb-5031-9caf-e5074093f115'}, {'abstract': 'The Pride of the Ocean film festival aboard the Celebrity Summit cruise offers a rich diversity of subject matter.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/out-at-sea/', 'snippet': 'The Pride of the Ocean film festival aboard the Celebrity Summit cruise offers a rich diversity of subject matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first gay-themed film that I remember thoroughly enjoying was “The Adventures of Priscilla, Queen of the Desert.” It was funny, had a great soundtrack and the characters all seemed confident in their identities. Before that, my experience with gay cinema was a mix of self-loathing screeds (“The Boys in the Band”), cautionary tales (“Longtime Companion”) and blink-and-you’ll-miss it crumbs (“Pump Up the Volume”).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out at Sea', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T22:21:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebbeb8c7-9bbe-52fb-abfa-fb07998bf002', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebbeb8c7-9bbe-52fb-abfa-fb07998bf002'}, {'abstract': 'A reluctant gay cruiser finds the right mix of culture and camaraderie — and still gets to sleep by midnight.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/all-aboard-2/', 'snippet': 'A reluctant gay cruiser finds the right mix of culture and camaraderie — and still gets to sleep by midnight.', 'lead