ks as both communities seek to alert the world to their grief.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palestinians and Israelis Share Images of Dead and Wounded Children', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T22:31:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e4e3c7b-1bbb-5afa-aea9-7160ce8962ba', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e4e3c7b-1bbb-5afa-aea9-7160ce8962ba'}, {'abstract': 'An updated interactive map of the forests of Cameroon reveals a complicated mix of land use below the green canopy.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/mapping-cameroons-motley-canopy/', 'snippet': 'An updated interactive map of the forests of Cameroon reveals a complicated mix of land use below the green canopy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From above, the forests of Cameroon seem to sweep across the land in an unending carpet of green. The forested swath is the second-largest in Africa, with tens of thousands of people at its fringes and nestled in its lush depths, dependent on what appears to be a continuous canopy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mapping Cameroon’s Motley Canopy', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'ran