', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/25ab7150-180c-51df-8699-3bcdc47738ab', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/25ab7150-180c-51df-8699-3bcdc47738ab'}, {'abstract': 'Federal investigators have accused a Queens foundry owner of trying to sell an unauthorized copy of a Jasper Johns sculpture on which he forged the artist’s signature.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/15/authorities-cast-queens-foundry-owner-as-forger/', 'snippet': 'Federal investigators have accused a Queens foundry owner of trying to sell an unauthorized copy of a Jasper Johns sculpture on which he forged the artist’s signature.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Brian Ramnarine’s foundry in Long Island City was so well-known among artists for its excellent work that Jasper Johns entrusted the owner in 1990 to make a wax cast of the mold for his famous 1960 metallic collage “Flag.” On Thursday, Mr. Ramnarine, 58, was indicted on charges he used Mr. Johns’s mold to surreptitiously make a bronze sculpture that he attributed to Mr. Johns and tried to sell for $11 million, according to the United States attorney in Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Authorities Cast Queens Foundry Owner as Forger', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Queens Foundry Owner Accused of Forgery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forgery', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johns, Jasper', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-15T23:48:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Co