70 students, is still second.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More international students attended United States colleges and universities in the 2011-12 school year than ever before, making it the sixth consecutive year in which international student enrollment has increased, according to the annual “Open Doors” report from the Institute of International Education.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China and India Top List of International Students Attending U.S. Colleges', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Students (in US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Study and Teaching', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute of International Education', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Michigan State University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Northeastern University', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ohio State University', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Purdue University', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Illinois', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Michigan', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Southern California', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T00:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b683945b-bc18-5ba1-b989-6aac951460dd', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b683945b-bc18-5ba1-b989-6aac951460dd'}, {'abstract': '“The Comedy,” by Rick Alverson, is about a young man with too much time and money on his hands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/movies/the-comedy-by-rick-alverson-stars-tim-heidecker.html', 'snippet': '“The Comedy,” by Rick Alverson, is about a young man with too much time and money on his hands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Swanson, the lump of humanity at the center of “The Comedy,” has money and privilege, but no class. As he waits for his rich father to die, Swanson (Tim Heidecker) spends his days hanging out with his pals, drinking, riding his bike, working at menial jobs — more out of boredom than economic necessity — and luring women back to the sailboat he keeps moored in the waters off New York City. What appeals to these women? The film does not bother to say, or even to give them names. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/movies/comedy-span/comedy-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/15/movies/comedy-span/comedy-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight':