 White House and the halls of Congress, and whose subjects included 20th-century Southern political leaders, President Richard M. Nixon’s daughters and William Faulkner, died on Monday in Memphis. He was 89.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/Bouldin3/Bouldin3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/Bouldin3/Bouldin3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/Bouldin3/Bouldin3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/Bouldin3/Bouldin3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1292, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/Bouldin3/Bouldin3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/Bouldin3/Bouldin3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marshall J. Bouldin III, Painter of Politicians, Dies at 89', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marshall J. Bouldin III, 89; Painted Political Portraits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bouldin, Marshall J III', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T00:51:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Vitello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vitello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c3b387c-8171-5bdb-9910-c8b63dc2e1db', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c3b387c-8171-5bdb-9910-c8b63dc2e1db'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Bradna was a star of the Folies Bergère touring company before she won movie roles in Hollywood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/movies/olympe-bradna-stage-and-screen-actress-dies-at-92.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Bradna was a star of the Folies Bergère touring company before she won movie roles in Hollywood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Olympe Bradna, a French-born dancer and actress who charmed Broadway as a child star of Paris’s touring Folies Bergère and appeared in Hollywood films opposite Gary Cooper and Ronald Reagan before trading stardom for life as a wife and mother, died on Nov. 5 in Stockton, Calif. She was 92. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/Bradna1/Bradna1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/Bradna1/Bradna1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/Bradna1/Bradna1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJum