s back as the ball looped into the goal from an almost unthinkable distance.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ibrahimovic’s Goal: Best Ever?', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Goooooooal for the Ages. But Is It the Best Ever?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibrahimovic, Zlatan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T00:58:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b459687-47ee-51c9-8f30-978ffdbbd6ab', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b459687-47ee-51c9-8f30-978ffdbbd6ab'}, {'abstract': 'After posting their first winning record in more than a decade last season, the Hoyas have been forced to use four quarterbacks in 2012, including a freshman.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/sports/ncaafootball/georgetown-trying-to-get-football-program-righted.html', 'snippet': 'After posting their first winning record in more than a decade last season, the Hoyas have been forced to use four quarterbacks in 2012, including a freshman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In his first offensive series of the season, the Georgetown Hoyas’ senior quarterback and captain, Isaiah Kempf, took off running on a third-and-9 from the team’s 25-yard line. He gained 18 yards but sustained a concussion that sidelined him indefinitely.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'im