2012/11/16/nyregion/rivals-vie-for-wood-from-storm-torn-rockaway-boardwalk.html', 'snippet': 'Various groups are vying for the wood that once made up the Rockaway Boardwalk so they can recycle or transform it into other products as a way to generate local revenue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Near Beach 114th Street, loose piles of planks from the once-proud Rockaway Boardwalk — a hardwood hodgepodge of Angelique, teak, pine, ipe, Cumaru and greenheart — lie sprawled on the beach. Mangled street lamps and, of all relics, a phone booth, are still bolted to the upturned wood. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/nyregion/WOOD2-sub/WOOD2-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/16/nyregion/WOOD2-sub/WOOD2-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/nyregion/WOOD2-sub/WOOD2-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/nyregion/WOOD2-sub/WOOD2-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1146, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/nyregion/WOOD2-sub/WOOD2-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/16/nyregion/WOOD2-sub/WOOD2-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 