d by Matt Ross, is an impressively executed acting exercise for Chris Messina and Marin Ireland. Playing an unnamed couple whose long-running, clandestine affair begins with a one-night stand after they meet in a hotel bar, these attractive actors spend much of the movie unclothed as they explore the shifting dynamics of a relationship that exists in a bubble. In movie-pitch language it might be described as “Same Time, Next Year” meets “Up in the Air” but with a French twist. That twist has to do with the film’s mood and austere visual style.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/twentyeight-span/twentyeight-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/twentyeight-span/twentyeight-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/twentyeight-span/twentyeight-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/twentyeight-span/twentyeight-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/twentyeight-span/twentyeight-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/twentyeight-span/twentyeight-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/twentyeight-span/twentyeight-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Check-In, Check-Out Affair', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Check-In, Check-Out Affair', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ireland, Marin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ross, Matt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Messina, Chris', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T01:39:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a3c69c9-6749-5a18-bff3-ba1d4a0819ac', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a3c69c9-6749-5a18-bff3-ba1d4a0819ac'}, {'abstract': 'Commissioner Roger Goodell told an audience at the Harvard School of Public Health that the N.F.L. was working hard to combat serious injuries, including those from hits to the head.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/sports/football/roger-goodell-nfl-commissioner-speaks-on-concussions.html', 'snippet': 'Commissioner Roger Goodell told an audience at the Harvard School of Public Health that the N.F.L. was working hard to combat serious injuries, including those from hits to the head.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — N.F.L. Commissioner Roger Goodell said Thursday that the league was doing more than ever to combat serious injuries, including those from hits to the head that can cause brain trauma, but that a cultural shift was needed to change the “warrior mentality” of players unwilling to disclose when they are hurt.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goodell Speaks of Changes Needed in N.F.L. Culture', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Goodell Speaks of Changes Needed in N.F.L. Culture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodell, Roger', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard School of Public Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T01:40:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c807d8e-4478-5211-8b4a-1b079febc45e', 'word_count': 622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c807d8e-4478-5211-8b4a-1b079febc45e'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge on Thursday upheld a South Carolina law allowing police officers to check the immigration status of suspects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/us/south-carolina-federal-court-delivers-mixed-verdict-on-immigration-measure.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge on Thursday upheld a South Carolina law allowing police officers to check the immigration status of suspects.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A federal judge on Thursday upheld a South Carolina law allowing police officers to check the immigration status of suspects. But the judge, Richard M. Gergel of Federal District Court in Charleston, continued to block other provisions of the state’s immigration crackdown. South Carolina is one of several states, along with Arizona, Georgia and Alabama, that have passed so-called show-me-your-papers laws. In June, the Supreme Court upheld Arizona’s 2010 law, and since then lower courts have issued similar rulings in Alabama and Georgia. Judge Gergel continued to block a provision of South Carolina’s law that would make it a crime to harbor or transport an illegal immigrant. He also said the police may not detain a person solely to check his immigration status. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Carolina: Federal Court Delivers Mixed Verdict on Immigration Measure', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Carolina: Federal Court Delivers Mixed Verdict On Immigration Measure ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T01:43:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robbie Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robbie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a723c28-8493-527c-9391-c5145466d56a', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a723c28-8493-527c-9391-c5145466d56a'}, {'abstract': 'The United States is seeking a security agreement authorizing a presence after Afghan forces assume responsibility for the war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/world/asia/us-in-talks-with-afghans-on-presence-after-2014.html', 'snippet': 'The United States is seeking a security agreement authorizing a presence after Afghan forces assume responsibility for the war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The United States and Afghanistan began talks on Thursday on a security agreement that would authorize an American troop presence in Afghanistan after 2014, when Afghan forces are to assume responsibility for the war. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. in Talks With Afghans on Presence After 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. in Talks With Afghans On Presence After 2014', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Status of Forces Agreements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T01:45:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07e2fb69-2989-5afb-8111-31e25c997e32', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07e2fb69-2989-5afb-8111-31e25c997e32'}, {'abstract': 'Why are some immigrants and their descendants considered simply "American," while others are still thought of as "outsiders"?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/roomfordebate/2012/11/15/how-immigrants-come-to-be-seen-as-americans/', 'snippet': 'Why are some immigrants and their descendants considered simply "American," while others are still thought of as "outsiders"?', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "Crossing the Line Between 'Immigrant' and 'American'", 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T01:47:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ac61a45-3700-5631-be09-9b2669695110', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ac61a45-3700-5631-be09-9b2669695110'}, {'abstract': 'The groundbreaking contract that Newark and its teachers’ union have hammered out offers reason for hope that the quality of teaching will improve.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/opinion/school-reform-in-newark-with-a-new-teachers-contract.html', 'snippet': 'The groundbreaking contract that Newark and its teachers’ union have hammered out offers reason for hope that the quality of teaching will improve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Newark and its teachers’ union deserve praise for the groundbreaking contract that the two sides have hammered out. The relatively calm negotiations that led up to the union’s ratification vote this week stood in sharp contrast to the vitriol that surrounded a similar agreement earlier this year in Chicago that led to a polarizing strike. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'School Reform in Newark', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'School Reform in Newark', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Evaluations (Labor)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T01:47:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/25c57d70-d3bf-57ed-a29d-b9c435f3a8d2', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25c57d70-d3bf-57ed-a29d-b9c435f3a8d2'}, {'abstract': 'No party, including the Democrats, should benefit from a defective political system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/opinion/the-tarnish-of-the-electoral-college.html', 'snippet': 'No party, including the Democrats, should benefit from a defective political system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the late-1960s through the ’80s, Republicans were convinced that they had a permanent lock on the Electoral College. The Sun Belt was rising, traditionally Democratic states were losing population, and Republicans won five of six presidential elections beginning in 1968. Democrats complained that this archaic system was a terrible and undemocratic way to choose the country’s executive. They were right, but they were ignored.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Tarnish of the Electoral College', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Tarnish of the Electoral College', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electoral College', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Elections (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T01:47:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/32abc55a-c428-5bbe-9499-dea3002b4bf0', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32abc55a-c428-5bbe-9499-dea3002b4bf0'}, {'abstract': 'The authorities say the train slammed into a parade float headed to an event honoring wounded veterans in Midland, Tex.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/us/texas-four-are-killed-and-17-injured-when-train-hits-veterans-parade-float.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities say the train slammed into a parade float headed to an event honoring wounded veterans in Midland, Tex.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four people were killed in Midland, Tex., on Thursday evening after a train crashed into a parade float at an event honoring veterans, the authorities said. At least 17 others were injured in the crash, which took place at a railroad crossing in the West Texas city about 4:30 p.m., according to the police chief, Price Robinson. Many of the injured appeared to be veterans and their spouses, he said. The parade on Thursday, led by a local group called Show of Support, was supposed to take the veterans through the city before ending at a planned banquet. The group provides outdoor opportunities to wounded service members and sponsors a whitetail deer hunt for them, according to the group’s Web site. Two people died at the scene and two later at a local hospital, Chief Robinson said. At least 10 others are in critical condition and seven are in stable condition at Midland Memorial Hospital, he said. The crash is being investigated, the police said. It took place at the railroad crossing at Garfield Street and Industrial Avenue, in the city of about 113,000 people. The Show of Support Web site lists 25 service members as its “2012 Heroes.” Their profiles describe the members’ deployments in Iraq and Afghanistan and how many were wounded in attacks involving improvised explosive devices. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: Four Are Killed and 17 Injured When Train Hits Veterans Parade Float', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: Four Are Killed and 17 Injured When Train Hits Veterans Parade Float ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T01:54:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma G. Fitzsimmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Fitzsimmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f774befa-b18b-53cf-8e05-fa64c9d4b402', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f774befa-b18b-53cf-8e05-fa64c9d4b402'}, {'abstract': 'Midnight the Dog fetched food and water across Washington Street to people marooned in the Westbeth apartment block during Hurricane Sandy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/nyregion/a-dog-named-midnight-is-a-west-village-hero-after-the-storm.html', 'snippet': 'Midnight the Dog fetched food and water across Washington Street to people marooned in the Westbeth apartment block during Hurricane Sandy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Midnight the Dog, a noble, slobbering beast, trotted down Bethune Street in the West Village one morning this week with a plastic grocery bag clenched in his teeth, cargo swinging inches above the sidewalk. He moved with a sureness of step that suggested his canine ancestors might have been let off the ark by Noah at the first D’Agostino’s they saw. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bottled Water Delivery! (Pardon the Slobber)', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bottled Water Delivery! (Pardon the Slobber)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Village (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T02:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43ed2e02-f1da-5688-8f22-7a11f5d2e601', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43ed2e02-f1da-5688-8f22-7a11f5d2e601'}, {'abstract': 'At least four people were killed and 17 others injur