975d2-19c9-5c24-b9c3-65acde4c6bed'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Hankin’s documentary “16 Acres” plots the machinations in the 11-year effort to redevelop the World Trade Center site.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/movies/16-acres-from-richard-hankin.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Hankin’s documentary “16 Acres” plots the machinations in the 11-year effort to redevelop the World Trade Center site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who was going to build what at ground zero, and when, became so convoluted so quickly that a lot of people no doubt gave up trying to follow the machinations years ago. Richard Hankin does a fine job of making it all coherent again in “16 Acres,” a documentary that features forthright interviews with major players and gives a good sense of the infighting and pettiness without getting bogged down in it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Collisions at Ground Zero', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '16 Acres', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T03:02:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/42bdea53-8253-5b33-8dc3-3e3050c8fcaf', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42bdea53-8253-5b33-8dc3-3e3050c8fcaf'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Normals,” directed by Kevin Connors, a jobless man in his 20s agrees to take an experimental antipsychotic drug to escape debt collectors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/movies/the-normals-starring-bryan-greenberg.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Normals,” directed by Kevin Connors, a jobless man in his 20s agrees to take an experimental antipsychotic drug to escape debt collectors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “The Normals” Billy Schine, in his 20s, unemployed and not sure what to do with his life, avoids a debt collector by entering a two-week clinical trial of an antipsychotic treatment at a drug-testing center in Queens. Between the taking of pills, the drawing of blood, the poking and prodding and interviews, he and his fellow “normals” — among them a professional “trial-tester”; an egomaniacal actor; a troubled, confused Bible reader; an attractive, provocative young woman — battle tedium and irritate one another. It’s like high school, without the dance.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/16RDP_NORMALS_SPAN/16RDP_NORMALS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/16RDP_NORMALS_SPAN/16RDP_NORMALS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/16RDP_NORMALS_SPAN/16RDP_NORMALS_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/16RDP_NORMALS_SPAN/16RDP_NORMALS_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 878, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/a