mmy performances; her rendition of the national anthem at Super Bowl XXV in 1991; and her first national television appearance, on “The Merv Griffin Show,” on April 29, 1985.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7cae3a8-a8eb-5414-b338-393baafebc85', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7cae3a8-a8eb-5414-b338-393baafebc85'}, {'abstract': 'The duo won four trophies, including best song and best recording for their hit single “Corre!” while the Colombian rocker Juanes won album of the year for his “MTV Unplugged” release.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/jesse-joy-are-big-winners-at-latin-grammys/', 'snippet': 'The duo won four trophies, including best song and best recording for their hit single “Corre!” while the Colombian rocker Juanes won album of the year for his “MTV Unplugged” release.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jesse & Joy, the sweet-singing, brother-and-sister pop duo from Mexico, were the big winners at the 13th Annual Latin Grammy Awards in Las Vegas on Thursday night, walking away with four trophies, including best song and best recording for their hit single, “Corre!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jesse & Joy Are Big Winners at Latin Grammys', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo