 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T08:15:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df946c70-d468-5d7d-b58a-9374c9416c13', 'word_count': 1202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df946c70-d468-5d7d-b58a-9374c9416c13'}, {'abstract': 'The Frenchman Franck Ribery has been the heart and soul of Bayern Munich’s recent run of success.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/ribery-at-the-heart-of-bayern-munichs-record-breaking-start/', 'snippet': 'The Frenchman Franck Ribery has been the heart and soul of Bayern Munich’s recent run of success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the hustle and bustle of the boisterously-famed Bundesliga crowd at the equally impressive Allianz Arena on Saturday afternoon, you’d be forgiven for finding your attention unfaithfully encouraged away from the action on the field in favor of the splendor that surrounded it. This was in part down to the spectacle that accompanies each home tie with Bayern Munich; the backdrop of varying colors from the red and white patterned crowd to the swishing multi-colored advertising boards, all set to the soundtrack of passionate Bavarian fans, but it was mostly to with the poor spectacle on the grass – a drab 2-0 win over Eintracht Frankfurt. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ribery at the Heart of Bayern Munich’s Record-Breaking Run', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ribery, Franck', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayern Munich (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T08:25:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stefan Bienkowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stefan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bienkowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fc6c866-b4a1-596d-ab8a-0592641b2f40', 'word_count': 822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fc6c866-b4a1-596d-ab8a-0592641b2f40'}, {'abstract': 'I sat down with Renzo Rosso, founder of Diesel, Ali Hewson and her husband Bono, founder of Edun, and Erastus Kibugu of Technoserve.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/iht-luxury-conference-live-bono-on-sustainable-fashion/', 'snippet': 'I sat down with Renzo Rosso, founder of Diesel, Ali Hewson and her husband Bono, founder of Edun, and Erastus Kibugu of Technoserve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Fashion to the rescue! Renzo Rosso, the founder of Diesel and its desirable denim, lives up to his company’s flagship name: Only the Brave. The executive on a motorbike puts his energy into a foundation to help social enterprises in Mali and other parts of Africa. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'IHT Luxury Conference 2012: Bono on ‘Sustainable Fashion’', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosso, Renzo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Diesel Jeans Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Edun', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T08:48:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Suzy Menkes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Suzy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Menkes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df6b0dc0-4b67-5d03-8790-89174b00a2b3', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df6b0dc0-4b67-5d03-8790-89174b00a2b3'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Gandhi will be the main campaign strategist as well as lead candidate for India’s 2014 elections.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/rahul-gandhi-gets-a-new-job/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Gandhi will be the main campaign strategist as well as lead candidate for India’s 2014 elections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rahul Gandhi has finally taken a power position, Congress Party leaders and political analysts said Friday, after his mother Sonia, the party’s president, created an “election co-ordination committee” Thursday evening to prepare for upcoming national elections in 2014.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rahul Gandhi Gets a New Job', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gandhi, Rahul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian National Congress', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T09:08:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sruthi Gottipati', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sruthi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gottipati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5682e1cc-f4e5-5241-81f0-ae89ad28df12', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5682e1cc-f4e5-5241-81f0-ae89ad28df12'}, {'abstract': 'Pakistan just passed a law guaranteeing free education for children. But the move may be more of a political calculation than a true commitment.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/pakistans-new-education-bill-is-more-old-politics-than-new-policy/', 'snippet': 'Pakistan just passed a law guaranteeing free education for children. But the move may be more of a political calculation than a true commitment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Pakistan’s National Assembly has unanimously passed the Right to Free and Compulsory Education Bill 2012, guaranteeing free education for all children between the ages of five and 16. This right was already enshrined in the Constitution, but it took this bill to articulate how it would be delivered. Under the new law, passed on Tuesday, parents who refuse to send their children to school can be fined and imprisoned for three months, and employers who hire school-age children face fines and up to six months in prison.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ghost Education', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illiteracy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Millennium Development Goals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reading and Writing Skills', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yousafzai, Malala', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T09:18:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Huma Yusuf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Huma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yusuf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fe5591f-27af-513d-ae68-1d9b821e075b', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fe5591f-27af-513d-ae68-1d9b821e075b'}, {'abstract': 'What award did R. A. Dickey win?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/knuckleballer-wins-cy-young-award/', 'snippet': 'What award did R. A. Dickey win?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Funny Pitch No More: Mets’ Knuckleballer Wins League Honors,” Tyler Kepner writes about R. A. Dickey winning baseball’s Cy Young Award. Read the article to answer the questions below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/15kepner_337-LN/15kepner_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 894, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/15kepner_337-LN/15kepner_337-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1787, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/15kepner_337-LN/15kepner_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/15kepner_337-LN/15kepner_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/sports/15kepner_337-LN/15kepner_337-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Knuckleballer Wins Cy Young Award', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T09:45:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/347a4f0f-cd61-52b0-8843-1e0f4462c483', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/347a4f0f-cd61-52b0-8843-1e0f4462c483'}, {'abstract': 'The awards show, in its 13th year, was broadcast from Las Vegas, where the Latin Grammys have settled congenially into an environment of spectacle and showgirls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/arts/music/at-latin-grammy-awards-a-whirl-of-styles-on-display.html', 'snippet': 'The awards show, in its 13th year, was broadcast from Las Vegas, where the Latin Grammys have settled congenially into an environment of spectacle and showgirls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 13th annual Latin Grammy Awards on Thursday night anointed a new favorite for the Latin Academy of Recording Arts and Sciences: Jesse & Joy, Mexican siblings whose heartbroken ballad “¡Corre!” (“Run!”) was named song of the year (an award for the songwriters) and record of the year (for the recorded single), stealing the spotlight from frequent Latin Grammy winners.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/16l