icle/bbf4be78-362f-5453-b900-3f3e54483ab7', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbf4be78-362f-5453-b900-3f3e54483ab7'}, {'abstract': 'With so much changing in the rest of India, Kolkata’s constancy feels like a regression.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/oh-kolkata-my-second-goodbye-to-home/', 'snippet': 'With so much changing in the rest of India, Kolkata’s constancy feels like a regression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late in June, I moved back to my hometown, Kolkata, after eight years in Delhi and one in New York. As I looked to kick off my freelance career, Kolkata was the obvious choice for a base – there, I did not have to pay for rent or food (thanks, mom) and I thought I would rediscover the city that knew all my firsts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oh Kolkata! My Second Goodbye to Home', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banerjee, Mamata', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kolkata (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bengal (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T11:36:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sambuddha Mitra Mustafi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sambuddha', 'middlename': 'Mitra', 'lastname': 'Mustafi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/738