ain': 'App Smart Extra: More Apps for Android Tablets', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T12:02:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kit Eaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7146ce94-e029-5eb0-9f56-0785b26553f0', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7146ce94-e029-5eb0-9f56-0785b26553f0'}, {'abstract': 'The Giants quarterback’s interceptions and errors come from the same mentality that produces his daring successes, an analyst says.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/the-foolish-brilliance-of-eli-manning/', 'snippet': 'The Giants quarterback’s interceptions and errors come from the same mentality that produces his daring successes, an analyst says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few links for your consideration, with not a single mention of the Jets’ backup quarterback:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Foolish Brilliance of Eli Manning', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodell, Roger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T12:23:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c4876ea-1d76-566c-9f15-db3b0af88e40', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c4876ea-1d76-566c-9f15-db3b0af88e40'}, {'abstract': 'What’s on view this week in art museums around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/this-week-in-the-global-arts-guide-3/', 'snippet': 'What’s on view this week in art museums around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 100 paintings by Gauguin and other artists figure in “Gauguin and the Voyage to the Exotic,” on view at the Museo Thyssen-Bornemisza in Madrid. Hoping he could live in ‘‘ecstasy, calm and art,’’ Gauguin departed for Tahiti in 1892. With his new life, came a new idiom that shed exotic stereotypes about the symbiosis between man and nature. That theme was pursued by other artists such as Rousseau, Franz Marc, Matisse, Kandinsky and Nolde, whose depictions of the jungle were worlds away from the academic, the urban and the bourgeois. Through Jan. 13.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/16rdv-artsguide/16rdv-artsguide-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/16rdv-artsguide/16rdv-artsguide-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1485, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week in the Global Arts Guide', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T12:37:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Hopkins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hopkins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30b54f84-d872-57f9-9900-e8097bdf2bc3', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30b54f84-d872-57f9-9900-e8097bdf2bc3'}, {'abstract': 'Deleting unwanted programs from a Mac OS X system is usually not as hard — nor as thorough — as it may seem.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/qa-removing-programs-on-a-mac/', 'snippet': 'Deleting unwanted programs from a Mac OS X system is usually not as hard — nor as thorough — as it may seem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Removing Programs on a Mac', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Desktop Computers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T12:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3736f473-16af-5dd2-a91d-3e0f6c942dc0', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3736f473-16af-5dd2-a91d-3e0f6c942dc0'}, {'abstract': 'By charging individuals, the government is signaling a return to the practice of prosecuting officers and managers rather than a company alone, scholars say.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/on-our-radar-the-bp-indictments/', 'snippet': 'By charging individuals, the government is signaling a return to the practice of prosecuting officers and managers rather than a company alone, scholars say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deception on the flow rate, negligence in pressure tests, misinterpretation of data, a failure to consult: a look at the charges against BP officials indicted in the 2010 Deepwater Horizon disaster, which killed 11 men and spewed five million barrels’ worth of oil into the gulf. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: The BP Indictments', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T12:48:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5962291f-ff09-52bd-8df3-6ed4e2415436', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5962291f-ff09-52bd-8df3-6ed4e2415436'}, {'abstract': 'The “fiscal cliff” explained, learning that odd is normal, the best options for wireless tethering and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/friday-reading-the-fiscal-cliff-explained/', 'snippet': 'The “fiscal cliff” explained, learning that odd is normal, the best options for wireless tethering and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Reading: The ‘Fiscal Cliff,’ Explained', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T12:52:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/448d71f7-b4b3-5a14-b0dc-58d41317dfe7', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/448d71f7-b4b3-5a14-b0dc-58d41317dfe7'}, {'abstract': 'The 7th edition of the Rome Film Festival is in progress this week and for once, even if you’re not a movie star, you are welcome to be a part of it — via the Inernet.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/at-the-rome-film-festival-a-virtual-red-carpet/', 'snippet': 'The 7th edition of the Rome Film Festival is in progress this week and for once, even if you’re not a movie star, you are welcome to be a part of it — via the Inernet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 7th edition of the Rome Film Festival is in progress this week and for once, even if you’re not a movie star, you are welcome to be a part of it. Marco Mueller, director of the festival, has changed the rules of the game by using the Internet. Viewers can register and follow festival events online, from the red carpet, to press conferences to movie presentations, taking the festival outside the usual boundaries of roped-off stages, VIP passes and the insider atmosphere. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/arts/15rdv-romefesta/15rdv-romefesta-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 716, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/arts/15rdv-romefesta/15rdv-romefesta-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1432, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At the Rome Film Festival, a Virtual Red Carpet', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web-Original Programming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coppola, Roman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tarantino, Quentin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verhoeven, Paul', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Django Unchained (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Tricked (Movie)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T12:54:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Saskia de Rothschild', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Saskia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Rothschild', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6acf80da-08e8-5cc8-aa31-9b3774b07fc7', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6acf80da-08e8-5cc8-aa31-9b3774b07fc7'}, {'abstract': 'A year with more than its shares of disasters can change a person’s perspective.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/booming/what-are-you-thankful-for-this-thanksgiving.html', 'snippet': 'A year with more than its shares of disasters can change a person’s perspective.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We have gone through some hard times this past year: The hurricane in the East, the drought in the Midwest and terrible forest fires in the West. Living through disaster has a tendency to alter a person’s perspective about what matters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Are You Thankful for This Thanksgiving?', 'kicker': 'The Friday Question', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T12:58:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Winerip', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winerip', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/577859ce-ea8b-597b-931f-3f5973a41c5d', 'word_count': 67, 'uri': 'nyt://article/577859ce-ea8b-597b-931f-3f5973a41c5d'}, {'abstract': '“Taking My Time,” a Joel Meyerowitz retrospective book, puts bodies of his work in one place for the first time and is likely to go a long way toward redefining the career of the groundbreaking artist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/arts/design/joel-meyerowitz-in-new-book-and-at-howard-greenberg-gallery.html', 'snippet': '“Taking My Time,” a Joel Meyerowitz retrospective book, puts bodies of his work in one place for the first time and is likely to go a long way toward redefining the career of the groundbreaking artist.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I CALL it the Zen bell,” the photographer Joel Meyerowitz was saying recently, sitting in the sunshine in his Upper West Side apartment and studio, describing a nagging compulsion to begin a long-term project about banks in the wake of the Great Recession. “I’m not getting any ding from anywhere else right now, and I keep hearing it ringing. So I’m going to pay attention.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18MEYEROWITZ_SPAN/18JPMEYEROWITZ2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18MEYEROWITZ_SPAN/18JPMEYEROWITZ2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18MEYEROWITZ_SPAN/18JPMEYEROWITZ2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18MEYEROWITZ_SPAN/18JPMEYEROWITZ2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1385, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18MEYEROWITZ_SPAN/18JPMEYEROWITZ2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18MEYEROWITZ_SPAN/18JPMEYEROWITZ2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18MEYEROWITZ_SPAN/18JPMEYEROWITZ2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Restless Lifetime of Paying Attention', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Restless Lifetime of Paying Attention', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meyerowitz, Joel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Phaidon Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T13:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article'