_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/on-witness-stand-former-analyst-describes-insider-trading-scheme/', 'snippet': 'Jesse Tortora, a former stock analyst, testified at the criminal trial of his one-time boss at Diamondback, Todd Newman, and Anthony Chiasson, the co-founder of the hedge fund Level Global.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2008, Jesse Tortora, a junior tech-stock analyst, made $2.25 million, his best year at the hedge fund Diamondback Capital Management.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Witness Stand, Former Analyst Describes Insider Trading Scheme', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chiasson, Anthony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newman, Todd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Richard J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T13:40:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3fa5301-3026-5dc8-a20a-3aef2df626d1', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3fa5301-3026-5dc8-a20a-3aef2df626d1'}, {'abstract': 'While a bidding war over Schiff Nutrition International plays out, Hertz’s acquisition of Dollar Thrifty appears to be wrapping up. | The hunt for yield continues. The latest target: European bank debt. | A fight between Bank of America and MBIA moved to the bond market. | It’s not a happy time to be Mark Pincus, the chief executive of Zynga.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/rival-bid-for-schiff-as-hertz-deal-wraps-up/', 'snippet': 'While a bidding war over Schiff Nutrition International plays out, Hertz’s acquisition of Dollar Thrifty appears to be wrapping up. | The hunt for yield continues. The latest target: European bank debt. | A fight between Bank of America and MBIA m...', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIVAL BID FOR SCHIFF, AS HERTZ DEAL WRAPS UP \xa0|\xa0 Schiff Nutrition International, a vitamin and nutritional supplement company, is the prize in a bidding war that broke out on Thursday. The Reckitt Benckiser Group made a rival offer for Schiff of $1.4 billion, trumping the $1.2 billion deal with the German pharmaceutical giant Bayer, which was announced on Oct. 30, DealBook’s Michael J. de la Merced reports. Reckitt Benckiser, a consumer products giant, is looking to use the acquisition to break into the market for vitamin and nutritional supplements. Reckitt’s chief executive, Rakesh Kapoor, described his offer as superior and “substantially similar” to the rival deal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rival Bid for Schiff, as Hertz Deal Wraps Up', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T13:56:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cab04501-8add-585e-8928-ae9ba27bcbcb', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cab04501-8add-585e-8928-ae9ba27bcbcb'}, {'abstract': 'The songs from “Ghost Brothers of Darkland County,” a musical by Stephen King and John Mellencamp, will be released on an album in the spring.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/king-and-mellencamps-musical-comes-back-to-life/', 'snippet': 'The songs from “Ghost Brothers of Darkland County,” a musical by Stephen King and John Mellencamp, will be released on an album in the spring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stephen King and John Mellencamp plan to release the soundtrack from their musical “Ghost Brothers of Darkland County” next spring, and they have recruited a list of prominent musicians to record the songs, including Elvis Costello, Sheryl Crow, Taj Mahal and Kris Kristofferson, Rolling Stone magazine reported on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'King and Mellencamp’s Musical Comes Back to Life', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'King-Mellencamp Musical Comes Back to Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Stephen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mellencamp, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T14:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b32449d-0f05-5316-ae1b-3c206190b29d', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b32449d-0f05-5316-ae1b-3c206190b29d'}, {'abstract': 'Nicaragua has long been an unplugged paradise. What happens when the jet set arrives? Karlie Kloss tests the waters.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/a-delicate-balance/', 'snippet': 'Nicaragua has long been an unplugged paradise. What happens when the jet set arrives? Karlie Kloss tests the waters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See the interactive slide show >>', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '139', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Delicate Balance | Nicaragua', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Delicate Balance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kloss, Karlie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGinley, Ryan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nicaragua', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T14:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Felsenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Felsenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/660b6cf4-0431-5ff3-ab57-c750fb6a8f33', 'word_count': 2047, 'uri': 'nyt://article/660b6cf4-0431-5ff3-ab57-c750fb6a8f33'}, {'abstract': 'We’re the least worst!', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/the-halt-and-the-lame-2/', 'snippet': 'We’re the least worst!', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ryan Avent reminds us just how poor economic performance has been since the crisis, all across the advanced world:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Halt and the Lame', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T14:01:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9c7bf04-1279-5c4b-ac50-aa15466692d3', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9c7bf04-1279-5c4b-ac50-aa15466692d3'}, {'abstract': 'A gorgeous restoration of a stained-glass window bearing the image of Peter Stuyvesant cannot mask the fact that Stuyvesant, the leader of New Amsterdam, looks like a man not to be crossed.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/peter-stuyvesant-now-glowing-but-still-glowering/', 'snippet': 'A gorgeous restoration of a stained-glass window bearing the image of Peter Stuyvesant cannot mask the fact that Stuyvesant, the leader of New Amsterdam, looks like a man not to be crossed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brighter? Definitely. Clearer? Without question. Vibrant? Dazzlingly so. Warmer and fuzzier? Never.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peter Stuyvesant, Now Glowing but Still Glowering', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T14:16:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/206266ba-b337-5659-b31b-331936e3414c', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/206266ba-b337-5659-b31b-331936e3414c'}, {'abstract': 'Congressional leaders left a meeting expressing confidence that the two parties will reach a deal on tax increases and spending cuts by the end of the year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/us/politics/obama-meeting-top-lawmakers-in-tough-deficit-talks.html', 'snippet': 'Congressional leaders left a meeting expressing confidence that the two parties will reach a deal on tax increases and spending cuts by the end of the year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Democratic and Republican leaders of Congress emerged from their first budget meeting with President Obama at the White House at midday Friday and, in a rare show of bipartisan bonhomie, jointly expressed confidence that the two parties will reach an agreement before the end of the year to avert economy-rattling tax increases and across-the-board spending cuts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/us/politics/17obama_image1/17obama_image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/17/us/politics/17obama_image1/17obama_image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/us/politics/17obama_image1/17obama_image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 557, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/us/politics/17obama_image1/17obama_image1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1115, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/us/politics/17obama_image1/17obama_image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/17/us/politics/17obama_image1/17obama_image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/us/politics/17obama_image1/17obama_image1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At White House, Top Lawmakers Say They Expect Budget Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Meeting Top Lawmakers in Tough Deficit Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T14:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e465a7c-8f3f-5688-8eef-f6f61a218f5e', 'word_count': 1446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e465a7c-8f3f-5688-8eef-f6f61a218f5e'}, {'abstract': 'We’d like to think Redd Foxx would approve.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/the-big-one-alan-gilbert-conducts-the-sanford-and-son-theme-for-30-rock/', 'snippet': 'We’d like to think Redd Foxx would approve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even if — especially if? — you are Alan Gilbert, you don’t get to appear on a show like “30 Rock” without getting pulled down to its silly, satirical level. On Thursday night’s episode of that NBC comedy, Mr. Gilbert, the music director of the New York Philharmonic, found himself an unknowing pawn in a battle between the characters played by Tracy Morgan and Alec Baldwin (who in real life is an enthusiastic patron of the Philharmonic and a member of its board). That feud culminates in the above scene, which finds Mr. Gilbert conducting an orchestral arrangement of Quincy Jones’s composition “The Streetbeater” — better known to us big dummies as the theme to “Sanford and Son.” We’d like to think that Redd Foxx would approve.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Big One: Alan Gilbert Conducts the ‘Sanford and Son’ Theme For ’30 Rock’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baldwin, Alec', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbert, Alan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T14:30:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85dbb8c1-249b-5b25-981b-382cf894071a', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85dbb8c1-249b-5b25-981b-382cf894071a'}, {'abstract': 'Online advertising shifts to follow consumers online, the BBC’s legal woes mount, and how both sides in the conflict over Gaza are using social networks.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/the-breakfast-meeting-targeted-ads-reshape-online-media-and-gaza-conflict-on-the-internet/', 'snippet': 'Online advertising shifts to follow consumers online, the BBC’s legal woes mount, and how both sides in the conflict over Gaza are using social networks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Online advertising is shifting toward “programmatic buying,” a system that allows advertisers to follow individual consumers online, Tanzina Vega writes. It is a different method for reaching an online audience, one that gives less value to the context (that is, the writing, photos and video surrounding the ad) than to the individual who happens to visiting that particular site. Advertisers like Nike, Comcast, Progressive and Procter & Gamble are using programmatic buying and it is punishing traditional online publishers who are receiving a smaller share of ad dollars as marketers can buy across a broader range of sites.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Targeted Ads Reshape Online Media, and Gaza Conflict on the Internet', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Mark John (1957- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T14:41:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24cb5e2c-b9f2-5330-9fa1-c68a087f5706', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24cb5e2c-b9f2-5330-9fa1-c68a087f5706'}, {'abstract': 'On Friday, The Lede is providing updates on the conflict in Gaza as events unfold.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/latest-updates-on-the-gaza-conflict/', 'snippet': 'On Friday, The Lede is providing updates on the conflict in Gaza as events unfold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday, The Lede followed the conflict in Gaza as events unfolded. Updates below mixed breaking news reports with the accounts of eyewitnesses posted online — including text, audio, video and photographs uploaded to the Web by journalists and bloggers in the region, as well as participants in the fighting. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nov. 16 Updates on the Gaza Conflict', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T14:57:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c07b3d34-46d2-53c9-8fcf-f71b5ae3b1f8', 'word_count': 3577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c07b3d34-46d2-53c9-8fcf-f71b5ae3b1f8'}, {'abstract': 'A revised version of the 2000 musical “Bare,” about teenagers wrestling with religion and sexuality, is getting a new Off Broadway revival at New World Stages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/theater/bare-revived-at-new-world-stages.html', 'snippet': 'A revised version of the 2000 musical “Bare,” about teenagers wrestling with religion and sexuality, is getting a new Off Broadway revival at New World Stages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOMETIME in the early 2000s the composer Damon Intrabartolo enrolled himself in a camp for self-described ex-gay Christians as a kind of agent provocateur. With the pretense of seeking to cure his homosexuality, he intended to suss out, and possibly lightly sabotage, the program.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18BARE_SPAN/18BARE_SPARE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18BARE_SPAN/18BARE_SPARE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18BARE_SPAN/18BARE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18BARE_SPAN/18BARE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1339, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18BARE_SPAN/18BARE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18BARE_SPAN/18BARE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18BARE_SPAN/18BARE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Musical Makes Changes as Closets Open', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Musical Makes Changes As Closets Open', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARIMA, STAFFORD', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T15:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Weinert-Kendt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weinert-Kendt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29d70533-4cc9-5a8e-a4d7-eef67f791d0d', 'word_count': 1112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29d70533-4cc9-5a8e-a4d7-eef67f791d0d'}, {'abstract': 'Britain’s armed forces are quickly heading toward their lowest levels in a century. France, which was the first European country to openly back the Syrian opposition, will shrink its forces 7 percent in 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/can-europes-shrinking-military-back-up-its-commitments-to-syrias-rebels/', 'snippet': 'Britain’s armed forces are quickly heading toward their lowest levels in a century. France, which was the first European country to openly back the Syrian opposition, will shrink its forces 7 percent in 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Great Britain on Thursday became the latest European country to throw its support behind the nascent Syrian rebel opposition movement. Foreign Secretary William Hague of Britain, who will host Syrian representatives in London on Friday to discuss cooperation going forward, said the time may have come for Western help in establishing a no-fly zone. “We are not excluding any option in the future because,” he said, “the Syrian crisis is getting worse and worse all the time.” (In February, Mr. Hague had ruled out military intervention.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/blogs/16rdv-syria-brtain-hague/16rdv-syria-brtain-hague-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/blogs/16rdv-syria-brtain-hague/16rdv-syria-brtain-hague-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1415, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Europe’s Shrinking Military Back up Its Commitments to Syria?', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'No-Fly Zones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T15:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e53d7c94-ad73-5666-98a3-1b569e605451', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e53d7c94-ad73-5666-98a3-1b569e605451'}, {'abstract': 'I spoke with Frida Giannini, creative director of Gucci, and Giambattista Valli live from Rome on Friday, Nov 15, the final day of the 2012 IHT Luxury Conference about “their Rome.”', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/iht-luxury-conference-live-what-makes-rome-eternal-for-designers/', 'snippet': 'I spoke with Frida Giannini, creative director of Gucci, and Giambattista Valli live from Rome on Friday, Nov 15, the final day of the 2012 IHT Luxury Conference about “their Rome.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'They are modern Romans with global reach. Frida Giannini, the creative mind behind Gucci, has made the eternal city her home. Giambattista Valli is also Roman — but chooses to work out of Paris. Together they explore the appeal of ‘’Mia Roma,’’ my Rome, from its spirit to its shops. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'IHT Luxury Conference 2012: What Makes Rome Eternal for Designers', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T15:09:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Suzy Menkes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Suzy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Menkes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee83e410-960c-5577-86a7-95d39b68c41a', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee83e410-960c-5577-86a7-95d39b68c41a'}, {'abstract': 'The Dutch shipping company TNT Express agreed on Friday to sell its airline operations as the European company looks to win regulatory support for its proposed 5.2 billion euros ($6.6 billion) takeover by United Parcel Service.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/tnt-express-to-sell-airline-unit-ahead-of-u-p-s-takeover/', 'snippet': 'The Dutch shipping company TNT Express agreed on Friday to sell its airline operations as the European company looks to win regulatory support for its proposed 5.2 billion euros ($6.6 billion) takeover by United Parcel Service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The Dutch shipping company TNT Express agreed on Friday to sell its airline operations as the European company looks to win regulatory support for its proposed 5.2 billion euros ($6.6 billion) takeover by United Parcel Service.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TNT Express to Sell Airline Unit Ahead of U.P.S. Takeover', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T15:18:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1197d5d7-3479-5eea-8b91-8c0433ed1eb0', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1197d5d7-3479-5eea-8b91-8c0433ed1eb0'}, {'abstract': 'Nike announced on Friday that it had reached an agreement to sell its Cole Haan unit to the private equity firm Apax Partners for $570 million.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/nike-to-sell-cole-haan-to-apax-partners-for-570-million/', 'snippet': 'Nike announced on Friday that it had reached an agreement to sell its Cole Haan unit to the private equity firm Apax Partners for $570 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nike announced on Friday that it had reached an agreement to sell its Cole Haan unit to the private equity firm Apax Partners for $570 million.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nike to Sell Cole Haan to Apax Partners for $570 Million', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nike to Sell Cole Haan for $570 Million', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APAX PARTNERS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NIKE Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TPG Capital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T15:20:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf0f85ac-c9c8-5f6e-b600-88e69c0b94ef', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf0f85ac-c9c8-5f6e-b600-88e69c0b94ef'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of events this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/arts/nov-18-24.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of events this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SIX years ago, when BOB DYLAN played the first New Orleans Jazz & Heritage Festival after Hurricane Katrina, his set list pointedly featured “High Water (For Charley Patton),” a harrowingly vivid portrait of flooding, death and exodus. As is often the case, he was working as much with myth as reality, but that didn’t lessen the catharsis. Mr. Dylan, who recently released his 35th studio album, “Tempest” (Columbia), understands more than anyone how carefully his words are parsed. So there may be reason to anticipate a similar gesture at the new Barclays Center in Brooklyn on Wednesday. During recent stops on his Never Ending Tour, he has played “The Levee’s Gonna Break,” his liberal revision of “When the Levee Breaks,” a blues account of the Great Mississippi Flood of 1927.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18GUIDE3_SPAN/18GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18GUIDE3_SPAN/18GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/18GUIDE3_SPAN/18GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo',