are bed-and-breakfasts or small hotels that include dinner. I enjoyed meeting fellow travelers at mealtime.Karolina DryjanskaNew York, N.Y.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Editor', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Solo But Not Alone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T15:33:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/39456374-64ae-5982-bfbf-0ad5c8e68aa7', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39456374-64ae-5982-bfbf-0ad5c8e68aa7'}, {'abstract': 'Investors anxious about automatic tax increases on Dec. 31, should President Obama and Congress fail to agree on a plan to avoid them, should exercise prudence in trying to minimize exposure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/your-money/taxes/advisers-caution-against-hasty-decisions-in-advance-of-tax-changes.html', 'snippet': 'Investors anxious about automatic tax increases on Dec. 31, should President Obama and Congress fail to agree on a plan to avoid them, should exercise prudence in trying to minimize exposure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH all the ominous talk of tax increases and a “fiscal cliff” if President Obama and Congressional leaders can’t agree on a plan to avert automatic tax increases on Dec. 31, some investors may be tempted to act soon to take advantage of the current tax rates.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/business/Wealth/Wealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': 