organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02c084cd-2fc8-545a-a1ea-4a81390da0d0', 'word_count': 1244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02c084cd-2fc8-545a-a1ea-4a81390da0d0'}, {'abstract': 'Kostas Vaxevanis, a magazine owner, was acquitted after publishing a list of Greeks who held Swiss bank accounts, but the prosecutor has appealed the verdict, calling it “legally mistaken.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/world/europe/kostas-vaxevanis-cleared-of-privacy-violations-to-be-retried.html', 'snippet': 'Kostas Vaxevanis, a magazine owner, was acquitted after publishing a list of Greeks who held Swiss bank accounts, but the prosecutor has appealed the verdict, calling it “legally mistaken.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — A Greek magazine publisher and editor who was cleared of violating privacy laws this month after he published the names of more than 2,000 Greeks with Swiss bank accounts is to face trial again, a court official said Friday, after the prosecutor appealed the verdict. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greek Publisher, Cleared of Privacy Violations, Faces Retrial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greek Publisher, Cleared of Privacy Violations, Faces Retrial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vaxevanis, Kostas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T16:54:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0413e570-d78b-50c6-b942-f1e6219eb4ee', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0413e570-d78b-50c6-b942-f1e6219eb4ee'}, {'abstract': 'A selective compendium of DVD releases, divided into seasonal themes, new releases, repackaged favorites and movies for cinephiles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/movies/homevideo/a-dvd-gift-guide-for-the-holidays.html', 'snippet': 'A selective compendium of DVD releases, divided into seasonal themes, new releases, repackaged favorites and movies for cinephiles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Blu-ray players continue to drop in price and rise in popularity, many distributors are returning to their libraries to create newly restored and remastered editions of enduring classics and popular favorites. The price tag on some of this year’s gift box collections may seem a bit stiff, but per title, the sets can still represent a genuine bargain, particularly given the heavy discounts available at online retailers. (All prices given below are the manufacturer’s suggested retail; in most cases you’ll be able to find markdowns of 30 to 40 percent.) And a well-produced Blu-ray, like Sony’s new edition of “Lawrence of Arabia,” offers a quality of sound and image that none of the streaming services — with their highly compressed digital files — can come close to matching. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/23dvd-image/23dvd-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/23dvd-image/23dvd-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/23dvd-image/23dvd-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/23dvd-image/23dvd-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/23dvd-image/23dvd-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/23dvd-image/23dvd-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/23dvd-image/23dvd-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dreaming of a Blu-ray Christmas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dreaming of a Blu-ray Christmas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DVD (Digital Versatile Disc)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T16:54:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'DVD', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Kehr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kehr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cb99b42-95a6-53ce-90b7-035b091bae71', 'word_count': 1262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cb99b42-95a6-53ce-90b7-035b091bae71'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/weekend-fare-storm-fund-raisers-and-holiday-markets/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several Hurricane Sandy benefits are taking place this weekend at restaurants and markets across the city:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare: Storm Fund-Raisers and Holiday Markets', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T16:59:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba1f30d9-3f87-555a-96ea-940c843f2e54', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba1f30d9-3f87-555a-96ea-940c843f2e54'}, {'abstract': 'The Port Authority of New York and New Jersey has released a video of floodwater gushing into the Hoboken and Exchange Place PATH stations, which are still off line.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/video-path-stations-being-flooded-during-storm/', 'snippet': 'The Port Authority of New York and New Jersey has released a video of floodwater gushing into the Hoboken and Exchange Place PATH stations, which are still off line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Port Authority of New York and New Jersey has released a video (see above or click here), spliced together from security-camera footage, of floodwater gushing into and burying the Hoboken and Exchange Place PATH stations on Oct. 29.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: PATH Stations Being Flooded During Storm', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hoboken (NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T17:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e01b3f5-abe1-509c-939d-1d8a0de2a0e1', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e01b3f5-abe1-509c-939d-1d8a0de2a0e1'}, {'abstract': 'New collections of shows as varied as “All in the Family” and “Doctor Who” are available for viewers who can’t get enough of their favorite characters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/arts/television/tv-boxed-sets-whole-series-and-seasons.html', 'snippet': 'New collections of shows as varied as “All in the Family” and “Doctor Who” are available for viewers who can’t get enough of their favorite characters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the person who still likes to take a television series down off the shelf — rather than just clicking online — the home entertainment industry continues to offer doorstopping boxed sets of DVDs, and this holiday season brings complete collections of TV landmarks like “All in the Family” and “The Fugitive.” To sweeten the pot in the contest against video streaming, some of these boxes include extras like a “Doctor Who” sonic screwdriver or a “Game of Thrones” dragon’s egg that you won’t get from Hulu or Amazon.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/gift-tvdvd/gift-tvdvd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/gift-tvdvd/gift-tvdvd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1520, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/gift-tvdvd/gift-tvdvd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/gift-tvdvd/gift-tvdvd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/gift-tvdvd/gift-tvdvd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Holiday Guests From Archie Bunker to Doctor Who', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Holiday Guests From Archie Bunker to Doctor Who', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DVD (Digital Versatile Disc)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T17:02:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2f8bd37-1354-590e-82b6-6cc3fabf014d', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2f8bd37-1354-590e-82b6-6cc3fabf014d'}, {'abstract': 'At the latest hearing, Republicans were more interested in political theater than in actually addressing substantive issues.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/the-benghazi-circus/', 'snippet': 'At the latest hearing, Republicans were more interested in political theater than in actually addressing substantive issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are still unanswered questions about the Benghazi mission killings–remaining fine details about what happened that day, what the intelligence community knew (or didn’t know) before the attack, whether better security around American diplomats could have prevented the tragedy. It’s not surprising that, directly after the incident, there was some confusion as to what, exactly, had taken place. Just as it’s not surprising that questions remain two months later. At least it’s not surprising to serious people with a background in military and intelligence matters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Benghazi Circus', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Susan E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T17:09:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbfbf563-79ee-5970-985f-302ff7a5421d', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbfbf563-79ee-5970-985f-302ff7a5421d'}, {'abstract': 'The Wii U, the first major video game console to hit the market in six years, is likely to be the biggest gift for gamers this season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/arts/video-games/the-wii-u-featuring-a-touch-screen-controller.html', 'snippet': 'The Wii U, the first major video game console to hit the market in six years, is likely to be the biggest gift for gamers this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s really only one gift for the gamer in your life this season: the WII U, Nintendo’s follow-up to its blockbuster Wii and the first major video game console to hit the market in six years. As with all new hardware, it’s difficult to predict what the software developers who make games — including those at Nintendo — are going to create for the Wii U over the next several years. But setting it up for the first time gave me a little of that Christmas morning feeling: at last, something new.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/gift-video/gift-video-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/gift-video/gift-video-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1420, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/gift-video/gift-video-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/16/arts/gift-video/gift-video-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Gamers, One Big Thing and Many Smaller', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Gamers, One Big Thing and Many Smaller', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wii (Video Game System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nintendo Co Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T17:12:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Video Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Suellentrop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suellentrop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17f51a00-299c-5639-996c-153097fe4dd5', 'word_count': 909, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17f51a00-299c-5639-996c-153097fe4dd5'}, {'abstract': 'If you own any of the key injured quarterbacks this week, taking a chance on the Eagles’ Nick Foles could pay off. But he’s not among our favorable matchup picks for Week 11.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/week-11-in-fantasy-football-favorable-and-unfavorable-matchups-2/', 'snippet': 'If you own any of the key injured quarterbacks this week, taking a chance on the Eagles’ Nick Foles could pay off. But he’s not among our favorable matchup picks for Week 11.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jason and Justin Sablich will provide fantasy football advice and analysis throughout the season on this blog and on Twitter @5thDownFantasy. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week 11 in Fantasy Football: Favorable and Unfavorable Matchups', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Personnel File', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cutler, Jay', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foles, Nick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newton, Cameron J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roethlisberger, Ben', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vick, Michael', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub