oe Wright, the director of “Anna Karenina,” narrates a scene from the film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the director Joe Wright, all the world, or at least all of “Anna Karenina,” is a stage. The filmmaker uses a theatrical concept in adapting Leo Tolstoy’s classic novel for the screen. Here, he narrates a scene that includes the characters Levin (Domhnall Gleeson), Oblonsky (Matthew Macfadyen) and Kitty (Alicia Vikander). He discusses how filming inside a theater allowed him the opportunity to compress transitional moments, as well as amplify emotion. Read A. O. Scott’s review here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anatomy of a Scene: ‘Anna Karenina’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T17:26:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c706d65-8655-5325-b9f7-16174a690e20', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c706d65-8655-5325-b9f7-16174a690e20'}, {'abstract': 'Japanese high school athletes who survived the devastating tsunami last year wrote essays about the disaster — and the healing power of sports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/sports/swimming-against-the-storm.html', 'snippet': 'Japanese high school athletes who survived the devastating tsunami last year wrote essays about the disaster — and the healing power of sports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the once-in-a-millennium tsunami struck northeastern Japan on March 11, 2011, it killed thousands of people and destroyed vast stretches of a rugged coastline. As the survivors in Fukushima, Miyagi and Iwate Prefectures started putting their lives back together, they came to rely on one another more than ever.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/belson3/belson3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1021, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/belson3/belson3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1021, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/belson3/belson3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/belson3/belson3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/belson3/belson3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Swimming Against the Storm', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Swimming Against the Storm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interscholastic Athletics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T17:27:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2775bc57-19bf-56eb-b30f-148381701e63', 'word_count': 1185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2775bc57-19bf-56eb-b30f-148381701e63'}, {'abstract': 'Thursday’s agreement is another step in the company’s struggle to improve its image, but it was not the comprehensive settlement that the company and investors were hoping for.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/business/global/despite-accord-spill-aftermath-shadows-bp.html', 'snippet': 'Thursday’s agreement is another step in the company’s struggle to improve its image, but it was not the comprehensive settlement that the company and investors were hoping for.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The deal that BP reached Thursday with the United States is another step toward removing the doubt that has hung over the company and its stock price since the explosion that killed 11 people on the Deepwater Horizon rig in 2010. But it is not the comprehensive settlement that the company and investors were hoping for.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/business/BP/BP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/business/BP/BP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Accord, Spill Aftermath Shadows BP', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite U.S. Settlement, BP Faces Billions in Fines for Clean Water Act Violations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico Oil Spill (2010)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T17:29:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Reed and Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a56d80a-6bd4-504b-a287-88de9574b536', 'word_count': 1058, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a56d80a-6bd4-504b-a287-88de9574b536'}, {'abstract': 'How a transcendentalist minister took charge of the first official black regiment.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/captain-higginson-takes-command/', 'snippet': 'How a transcendentalist minister took charge of the first official black regiment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Capt. Thomas Wentworth Higginson spent the fall of 1862 whipping raw recruits for the Massachusetts 51st into fighting shape. After declining an officer’s commission in the early months of the Civil War, the 38-year-old Transcendentalist minister had decided that if “antislavery men” expected to influence the conduct and settlement of the conflict, then they “must take part in it.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Captain Higginson Takes Command', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Military)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Higginson, Thomas Wentworth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T17:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan J. Kytle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Kytle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26bbb6eb-09da-5337-a754-abb0842acaf0', 'word_count': 1850, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26bbb6eb-09da-5337-a754-abb0842acaf0'}, {'abstract': 'My 8-year-old son and his friend spent untold hours playing a massively multiplayer online game over the past summer — and I didn’t care.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/four-hours-of-screen-time-no-problem/', 'snippet': 'My 8-year-old son and his friend spent untold hours playing a massively multiplayer online game over the past summer — and I didn’t care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This past summer, I came home from work to find my son and his friend M. playing Roblox, a massively multiplayer online game that lets you construct virtual worlds and customize an avatar to explore it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Four Hours of Screen Time? No Problem', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T17:34:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diane Mehta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mehta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4649c14e-9178-50bb-923a-34468a60a94e', 'word_count': 881, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4649c14e-9178-50bb-923a-34468a60a94e'}, {'abstract': 'In Germany and in the euro zone as a whole, industrial production has slowed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/11/16/business/World-Production-Stagnates.html', 'snippet': 'In Germany and in the euro zone as a whole, industrial production has slowed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Germany and in the euro zone as a whole, industrial production has slowed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Charts: World Production Stagnates', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Production', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T17:37:56+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/e210e024-bdea-52eb-a7a4-49352e5eca58', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/e210e024-bdea-52eb-a7a4-49352e5eca58'}, {'abstract': 'A man was killed in a street in Gaza City, witnesses said, and a poster hung on his body accusing him of collaborating with the Israelis in the killing of 15 Palestinian leaders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/world/middleeast/suspected-collaborator-with-israel-executed-in-gaza.html', 'snippet': 'A man was killed in a street in Gaza City, witnesses said, and a poster hung on his body accusing him of collaborating with the Israelis in the killing of 15 Palestinian leaders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GAZA — Masked gunmen in Gaza killed a man here on Friday as a suspected collaborator with Israel on the third day of its deadly aerial bombardments, shooting him multiple times and leaving his body beneath a billboard featuring a Hamas fighter holding a rocket.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/world/middleeast/17execute_image1/17execute_image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/17/world/middleeast/17execute_image1/17execute_image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/world/middleeast/17execute_image1/17execute_image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/world/middleeast/17execute_image1/17execute_image1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspected Collaborator With Israel Killed on Gaza Street', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suspected Collaborator With Israel Killed on Gaza Street', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T17:38:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren and Fares Akram', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Fares', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akram', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a37d8510-959b-5b71-b8f5-c50bc6fb950e', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a37d8510-959b-5b71-b8f5-c50bc6fb950e'}, {'abstract': 'To stock the ideal bathroom library, here’s a list of 11 titles from the books of 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/books/best-bathroom-books-of-2012.html', 'snippet': 'To stock the ideal bathroom library, here’s a list of 11 titles from the books of 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month in The New York Times, I called “The Hungry Ear: Poems of Food & Drink,” Kevin Young’s anthology, “easily the best bathroom book of 2012, no small praise.” I stand by that observation and by my only slightly tongue-in-cheek suggestion that the National Book Awards establish a prize in this category. If I had to pick 10 more titles from this year to stock the ideal bathroom library, they’d be as follows:', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '37', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/books/23garner-1/23garner-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/books/23garner-1/23garner-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/books/23garner-1/23garner-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/23/books/23garner-1/23garner-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/books/23garner-1/23garner-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stories, Essays and Poems for the Powder Room', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stories, Essays and Poems for the Powder Room', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T17:51:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e144f19b-6f96-5fbd-ad19-27809399f167', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e144f19b-6f96-5fbd-ad19-27809399f167'}, {'abstract': 'World War II intrigue, an audacious heist, misfits of science, an anthology of gay and lesbian comics and superheroes are on the bill in these graphic novels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/books/graphic-novels-from-batgirl-to-wrinkle-in-time.html', 'snippet': 'World War II intrigue, an audacious heist, misfits of science, an anthology of gay and lesbian comics and superheroes are on the bill in these graphic novels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Outer-space adventures, the mysteries of the oceans, 20-something angst, World War II intrigue, an audacious heist, misfits of science, an anthology of gay and lesbian comics and, oh yes, superheroes. Even the finickiest of readers will find something to enjoy in this selection of graphic novels.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/books/23graphic-SUB/23graphic-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 942, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/books/23graphic-SUB/23graphic-SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1885, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy'