lactic future, but she has mixed feelings about the distractions of modern technology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'O CAPTAIN: The prolific science fiction writer Lois McMaster Bujold has won four best-novel Hugo Awards in her career so far. That’s more than anyone except the great Robert A. Heinlein, who won five — though one of his should by rights take an asterisk, since it was awarded 50 years retroactively. Now Bujold can claim another of Heinlein’s achievements: With “Captain Vorpatril’s Alliance” hitting the hardcover fiction list this week at No. 16 (it’s the latest entry in her comic Vorkosigan Saga series, set some thousand years in the future), she’s finally broken into the print edition of the New York Times best-\xadseller list.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/books/18list-img/18list-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 223, 'width': 220, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/books/18list-img/18list-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 223, 'width': 220, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/books/18list-img/18list-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/18/books/18list-img/18list-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/books/18list-img/18list-img-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'k