ings for FX.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/american-horror-storys-cheery-ratings-tale/', 'snippet': 'Though the concept was drastically changed this season, “American Horror Story” has continued to do well in the ratings for FX.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A corrupt mental institution may not sound like viewer catnip, but it has proved just that for the FX show “American Horror Story,” which continues to be a ratings hit. The second season’s first five episodes\xa0 have averaged close to three million total viewers for their initial broadcasts, which led to FX’s announcement on Thursday that the show would be renewed for a third season.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘American Horror Story’s’ Cheery Ratings Tale', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Cheery Ratings Tale: ‘American Horror Story’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Falchuk, Brad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Ryan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX (TV Network)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T19:40:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dea945a3-6bae-5f2a-a45b-3021859321f6', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dea945a3-6bae-5f2a-a45b-3021859321f6'}, {'abstract': 'An effort to retrieve family photos lost in Hurricane Sandy reflects the significance of prints in a