orge Vecsey does not think the Mets should trade R.A. Dickey.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/why-the-mets-should-keep-dickey/', 'snippet': 'George Vecsey does not think the Mets should trade R.A. Dickey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Vecsey has heard the rumblings about the possibility the Mets might trade pitcher R.A. Dickey, who just won the National League Cy Young Award, and asks, “Is there some impulse for self-destruction among New York teams?” The full essay is at georgevecsey.com. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why the Mets Should Keep Dickey', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickey, R A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vecsey, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T20:04:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56598305-458d-5c24-986c-3fb5a4c7f7ee', 'word_count': 44, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56598305-458d-5c24-986c-3fb5a4c7f7ee'}, {'abstract': 'The agency rejected requests from several states to relax the ethanol mandate because of a sharp decline in the corn crop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/business/energy-environment/epa-upholds-ethanol-standard-on-use-in-gasoline.html', 'snippet': 'The agency rejected requests from several states to relax the ethanol mandate because of a sharp decline in the corn crop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Environmental Protection Agency declined on Friday to relax its requirement on the use of corn ethanol in gasoline, rejecting a request from several states related to a steep decline in the nation’s corn production.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.P.A. Upholds Federal Mandate for Ethanol in Gasoline', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'E.P.A. Upholds Federal Mandate for Ethanol in Gasoline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethanol', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T20:04:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/604c9269-d68c-5711-addb-be63fa17343a', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/604c9269-d68c-5711-addb-be63fa17343a'}, {'abstract': 'One of the most frustrating experiences with using Apple TV, Xbox and other Internet-connected boxes is text entry. That’s why Xbox SmartGlass, a new app that lets users control their game consoles from touch screen devices, seems so exciting. Unfortunately, the app is flawed.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/smartglass-app-for-controlling-your-xbox-has-a-few-holes/', 'snippet': 'One of the most frustrating experiences with using Apple TV, Xbox and other Internet-connected boxes is text entry. That’s why Xbox SmartGlass, a new app that lets users control their game consoles from touch screen devices, seems so exciting. Unf...', 'lead_paragraph': ' One of the most frustrating experiences with using Apple TV, Xbox and almost any other Internet-connected set-top box is text entry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'SmartGlass App for Controlling Your Xbox Has a Few Holes', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Xbox (Video Game System)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T20:05:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccbef8e8-84a6-5d26-af6a-a7f636dd7fa9', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccbef8e8-84a6-5d26-af6a-a7f636dd7fa9'}, {'abstract': 'The Afghans were on their way to a wedding in western Afghanistan when their van hit a roadside bomb, and most of the dead were women and children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/world/asia/bomb-kills-civilians-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'The Afghans were on their way to a wedding in western Afghanistan when their van hit a roadside bomb, and most of the dead were women and children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — A roadside bomb killed 17 civilians, most of them women and children, on Friday as they traveled to a wedding in western Afghanistan. It was the third time in less than 10 days that a bomb claimed the lives of civilians. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bomb Kills 17 Civilians in Afghanistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Roadside Bomb Kills 17 Civilians in Afghanistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T20:10:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin and Taimoor Shah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Taimoor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c9a352c-d25b-5f4e-b62b-03a821817c86', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c9a352c-d25b-5f4e-b62b-03a821817c86'}, {'abstract': 'For guys who find accessorizing intimidating, the jewelry designer Yuvi Alpert offers a foolproof system online.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/site-to-be-seen-menincities-com/', 'snippet': 'For guys who find accessorizing intimidating, the jewelry designer Yuvi Alpert offers a foolproof system online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For guys who find accessorizing intimidating — the stress of picking cuff links that complement the thumb ring, for example, being just too much to bear — the jewelry designer Yuvi Alpert has created a foolproof system. It begins with how you buy things. On his new Web site, MenInCities.com, which goes live this week, a limited-edition collection of no more and no less than nine distinct but coordinating accessories is released each month. Everything, from worn-in leather wallets to antique-inspired beaded bracelets, is priced at $39.99. “I love that you can see the entirety of every collection on one page,” Alpert says. “I want our customers to be able to shop without distractions and just focus on the designs in front of them.” Pulling from previous experience as the designer for the boho jewelry line Ruby Kobo, Alpert’s first collection for Men In Cities is filled with easy, simple pieces that are enough to wear to the office (think muted silver cuffs and a deep blue bracelet with a small skull pendant). “I wanted everything to be straightforward. I design items that I feel work well together,” he says. “My personal style is T-shirt, jeans, accessories. But If you feel like a rock star and want to wear 10 bracelets at a time, go for it. We want men to be able to add character to their own look, just a touch of formality with a cravat or tie clip.” Men In Cities also offers styling tips, via illustrated guides. “The idea’s to introduce men to a new way of thinking,” he says. “There’s no right or wrong — it’s what you feel comfortable with.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Site to Be Seen | MenInCities.com', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T20:15:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Frank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a651f85e-8651-562a-b865-b451d5797890', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a651f85e-8651-562a-b865-b451d5797890'}, {'abstract': 'This 2012-13 Knicks recall the Mavericks team that won the N.B.A. title in 2011, and not just because Jason Kidd and Tyson Chandler are on the roster.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/how-the-knicks-mirror-the-2010-11-champion-mavericks/', 'snippet': 'This 2012-13 Knicks recall the Mavericks team that won the N.B.A. title in 2011, and not just because Jason Kidd and Tyson Chandler are on the roster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mythology of the 2010-11 Dallas Mavericks was that they were considered underdogs in every playoff series they won on their way to becoming N.B.A. champions. In reality, although they were widely dismissed as they entered the playoffs, the Mavs hardly came out of nowhere. Dallas began the season a blistering 24-5 before Dirk Nowitzki was hurt and Dallas dropped 9 of their next 11 games.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/sports/basketball/16kidd/16kidd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 809, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/sports/basketball/16kidd/16kidd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1618, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/sports/basketball/16kidd/16kidd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/16/sports/basketball/16kidd/16kidd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/sports/basketball/16kidd/16kidd-thumbLarg