emselves into something to talk about by signing outfielder Melky Cabrera to a free-agent contract.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/who-woke-up-the-blue-jays/', 'snippet': 'For the second time in the still-young hot stove season, the Blue Jays have turned themselves into something to talk about by signing outfielder Melky Cabrera to a free-agent contract.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the second time in the still-young hot stove season, the Blue Jays have turned themselves into something to talk about by signing the former Giants and Yankees outfielder Melky Cabrera to a free-agent contract. This time, the talk might not be quite as complimentary as when the Jays took advantage of the Marlins’ fire sale to acquire Jose Reyes, Josh Johnson, Emilio Bonifacio, John Buck and Mark Buehrle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/sports/baseball/16cabrera_batsblog/16cabrera_batsblog-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/sports/baseball/16cabrera_batsblog/16cabrera_batsblog-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/sports/baseball/16cabrera_batsblog/16cabrera_batsblog-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/16/sports/baseball/16cabrera_batsblog/16cabrera_batsblog-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/sports/baseball/16cabrera_batsblog/16cabrera_batsblog-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Woke Up the Blue Jays?', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steroids', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Testosterone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cabrera, Melky', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Josh', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Jose', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Blue Jays', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T20:40:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/166676b5-656f-5877-9b42-fc7e7890a9cf', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/166676b5-656f-5877-9b42-fc7e7890a9cf'}, {'abstract': 'While once reporting on a vintage-car rally, I spent a day in three Alfa Romeos. The effect was intoxicating, and I vowed to get one. It took a trip to Rome and then a long boat ride for the car, but a Giulia 1300 TI is now in my garage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/automobiles/collectibles/it-followed-me-home-can-i-keep-it.html', 'snippet': 'While once reporting on a vintage-car rally, I spent a day in three Alfa Romeos. The effect was intoxicating, and I vowed to get one. It took a trip to Rome and then a long boat ride for the car, but a Giulia 1300 TI is now in my garage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — In April 2010, while reporting on the California Mille, a vintage-car rally, I spent a memorable day riding in three Alfa Romeos: a 1928 6C 1500 Sport Zagato, a 1959 Giulietta Sprint Veloce and an innocent-looking 1967 Giulia Super sedan.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/automobiles/18ALFA1/18ALFA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/18/automobiles/18ALFA1/18ALFA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/automobiles/18ALFA1/18ALFA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 560, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/automobiles/18ALFA1/18ALFA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1120, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/automobiles/18ALFA1/18ALFA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/18/automobiles/18ALFA1/18ALFA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/automobiles/18ALFA1/18ALFA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It Followed Me Home. Can I Keep It?', 'kicker': 'Collecting', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It Followed Me Home. Can I Keep It?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub'