are International Airport (Chicago)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Airlines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hostess Brands', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T22:36:17+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c44fb55d-7dce-5917-99bd-156801112e57', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c44fb55d-7dce-5917-99bd-156801112e57'}, {'abstract': 'Judy Smith is a rescue artist for people mired in scandal, including Monica Lewinsky and now Jill Kelley, the Tampa socialite who touched off the sex scandal surrounding Gen. David Petraeus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/fashion/judy-smith-enters-the-petraeus-spotlight.html', 'snippet': 'Judy Smith is a rescue artist for people mired in scandal, including Monica Lewinsky and now Jill Kelley, the Tampa socialite who touched off the sex scandal surrounding Gen. David Petraeus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUDY SMITH’S calling to crisis management came early. \xa0Her story went like this: \xa0The “It” couple in her middle-school class had broken up. Rumor had it that despite the boy’s staunch denials, he had kissed another girl. Where others saw\xa0heartbreak, 11-year-old Judy saw opportunity. “After hearing his side, I was convinced he was telling the truth,” Ms. Smith wrote in her recent self-help memoir, “Good Self, Bad Self: Transforming Your Worst Qualities Into Your Biggest Assets.”\xa0She persuaded the girl of the boyfriend’s trustworthiness, prompting Ms. Smith’s own tween epiphany: if an emotionally uninvolved third party believed and argued for someone’s innocence, the wronged party was more likely to believe it, too. And thus a career was born.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 's