cation that has washed north of East 96th Street has by no means been wholesale. But the signs of evolution are evident.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/realestate/east-harlem-living-in-more-small-dogs-and-big-home-prices.html', 'snippet': 'The latest wave of gentrification that has washed north of East 96th Street has by no means been wholesale. But the signs of evolution are evident.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN his 1995 memoir “Dreams From My Father,” Barack Obama described the Yorkville walk-up on 94th Street near First Avenue where he had lived in the 1980s as “part of the shifting border between East Harlem and the rest of Manhattan.” Over the last several years, as the latest wave of gentrification has washed north of East 96th Street, breaching a traditional dividing line sometimes called the Wall by East Harlem residents, that boundary has blurred even further.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/realestate/SUB-2-LIVING-IN/SUB-2-LIVING-IN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/18/realestate/SUB-2-LIVING-IN/SUB-2-LIVING-IN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/realestate/SUB-2-LIVING-IN/SUB-2-LIVING-IN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/realestate/SUB-2-LIVING-IN/SUB-2-LIVING-IN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image