sworth, Stephen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Juilliard School', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T23:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b594879-0f51-5277-9928-30009ca70296', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b594879-0f51-5277-9928-30009ca70296'}, {'abstract': 'The image of China’s most enduring pop-folk icon, Peng Liyuan, has been made over since Xi Jinping was set on the path to being party secretary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/world/asia/peng-liyuan-first-lady-of-china-dimmed-her-star.html', 'snippet': 'The image of China’s most enduring pop-folk icon, Peng Liyuan, has been made over since Xi Jinping was set on the path to being party secretary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Peng Liyuan, China’s most enduring pop-folk icon, is beloved for her glass-cracking soprano and her ability to take on such roles as a coquettish Tibetan yak herder, a lovelorn imperial courtesan, even a stiff-lipped major general — which in fact she is.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/world/china/china-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/world/china/china-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/world/china/china-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/17/world/china/china-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/world/china/china-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Star in China Both Rises and Sets', 'kicker': 'The Saturday Profile', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Star In China Both Rises And Sets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peng Liyuan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T23:02:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Biography', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f72f2ae-cc77-5beb-af43-85e2c67aec21', 'word_count': 1350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f72f2ae-cc77-5beb-af43-85e2c67aec21'}, {'abstract': 'More good stuff from the middle of the Atlantic.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/friday-night-music-king-and-lionheart/', 'snippet': 'More good stuff from the middle of the Atlantic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m always fascinated by the strange chemistry that makes a great band appear — the way the right good musicians become something much greater if they happen to hook up. Still grieving for the troubles, whatever they are, of The Civil Wars; but these young Icelanders have the magic, too:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: King and Lionheart', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-16T23:05:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5186106a-adce-5360-a843-d2646aec65e1', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5186106a-adce-5360-a843-d2646aec65e1'}, {'abstract': 'Madison Square Garden, which has not been home to an N.C.A.A. men’s basketball tournament game since 1961, will host the East Regional in 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/sports/ncaabasketball/ncaa-tournament-returning-to-madison-square-garden.html', 'snippet': 'Madison Square Garden, which has not been home to an N.C.A.A. men’s basketball tournament game since 1961, will host the East Regional in 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jerry West had fouled out, having scored only 10 points, and watched as West Virginia, with its 26-1 record, was defeated in the first round of the 1958 N.C.A.A. tournament. As a Manhattan College player missed a meaningless free throw, fans spilled onto the Madison Square Garden court, throwing hats without care and cheering the hometown team.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/ncaabasketball/17garden-1/17garden-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/ncaabasketball/17garden-1/17garden-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/ncaabasketball/17garden-1/17garden-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/ncaabasketball/17garden-1/17garden-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1576, 'width': 1984, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/ncaabasketball/17garden-1/17garden-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/ncaabasketball/17garden-1/17garden-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/ncaabasketball/17garden-1/17garden-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Garden Memories, Faded by Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Garden Memories, Faded By Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Basketball Championships (Men)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National I