not an extraordinary number, both historical precedent in midterm election years and a deeper examination of this year’s results would argue strongly against Democrats being able to gain that many seats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Democrats did not have as strong a performance in races for the United States House of Representatives last week as they did in the contests for the Senate and the presidency. Instead, Republicans retained control of the chamber.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Unlikely to Regain House in 2014', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T00:17:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dc225be-f62e-5b6e-848e-2c0fe977671f', 'word_count': 1035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dc225be-f62e-5b6e-848e-2c0fe977671f'}, {'abstract': 'Kurt Masur conducted the New York Philharmonic in a Brahms program at Avery Fisher Hall on Thursday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/arts/music/kurt-masur-and-new-york-philharmonic.html', 'snippet': 'Kurt Masur conducted the New York Philharmonic in a Brahms program at Avery Fisher Hall on Thursday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brahms has long been a specialty of Kurt Masur, both during his tenure as music director of the New York Philharmonic from 1991 to 2002 and for a quarter-century at the Leipzig Gewandhaus and on recordings. In a return to the Philharmonic this fall he is taking part in a survey of Brahms’s complete symphonies and concertos, which began on Nov. 7. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/17PHIL/17PHIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/17PHIL/17PHIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/17PHIL/17PHIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/17PHIL/17PHIL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/17PHIL/17PHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/17PHIL/17PHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/17PHIL/17PHIL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Austria and Autumn, in Works by Brahms', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Austria and Autumn, in Works by Brahms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brahms, Johannes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Masur, Kurt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T00:23:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1a39f18-e1bf-522a-b699-39b61274559f', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1a39f18-e1bf-522a-b699-39b61274559f'}, {'abstract': 'The menu at Restaurante El Mariachi lists almost 40 items, but its little plates outshine the rest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/nyregion/a-review-of-restaurante-el-mariachi-in-trenton.html', 'snippet': 'The menu at Restaurante El Mariachi lists almost 40 items, but its little plates outshine the rest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On its menu, Restaurante El Mariachi calls itself Mexican, but I went to this establishment in Trenton because I had learned online that it served pupusas. These Salvadoran-style, saucer-size corn cakes are delicious; grilled so that the exterior enhances the crisp, tender morsels of pork rind filling, they play nicely against curtido, a pickled cabbage and carrot slaw served on the side. They were equally satisfying filled with melted cheese and loroco, an edible flower, usually pickled, with a taste between asparagus and green bean. When I had almost eaten my fill of these popular snacks, I stayed for the tacos and the seafood soup.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18DINENJ1/18DINENJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18DINENJ1/18DINENJ1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18DINENJ1/18DINENJ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18DINENJ1/18DINENJ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18DINENJ1/18DINENJ1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Tacos Make Room for Pupusas', 'kicker': 'New Jersey Dining | Trenton', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Tacos Make Room for Pupusas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Trenton (NJ)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Restaurante El Mariachi (Trenton, NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T00:23:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Cook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cook', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/81aea185-ce2f-5d38-a579-2990f002e0b2', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81aea185-ce2f-5d38-a579-2990f002e0b2'}, {'abstract': 'The Dining staff is answering your pressing Thanksgiving questions.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/16/have-a-thanksgiving-quandary-ask-the-help-line/', 'snippet': 'The Dining staff is answering your pressing Thanksgiving questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Dining section staff is answering your pressing Thanksgiving questions on the annual Help Line, addressing topics like brining the bird, how far ahead you can make pumpkin pie, how best to cook a wild turkey, whether it’s rude for vegetarians to bring along their own dishes for dinner, and how old is too old for the kids table. (Answers to questions about Jacques Pépin’s steamed and roasted turkey can be found there; Denise Landis, The Times’s recipe tester, has also answered several questions about the recipe in the comments thread on this blog post.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Have a Thanksgiving Quandary? Ask the Help Line.', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T00:25:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c1fe287-f751-51a9-bec2-c9508d1286bc', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c1fe287-f751-51a9-bec2-c9508d1286bc'}, {'abstract': 'Leslie Uggams explains away an unusual performance, years ago, and includes a tribute to Marvin Hamlisch in her show at 54 Below.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/arts/music/leslie-uggams-in-classic-uggams-at-54-below.html', 'snippet': 'Leslie Uggams explains away an unusual performance, years ago, and includes a tribute to Marvin Hamlisch in her show at 54 Below.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Classic Uggams,” her bright, spunky new show at 54 Below, Leslie Uggams recalls what happened several years ago when she flubbed the lyrics to “June Is Bustin’ Out All Over,” a song she barely knew, during a live, televised outdoor performance in Washington, and was heard spouting nonsensical filler. The night before, it had rained, she said on Wednesday evening. During her performance, the assistant holding the cue cards in front of her as she strode down the aisle, singing, slipped on the wet grass and fell, scattering the cards, and she had to improvise. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/SUB-17UGGAMS/SUB-17UGGAMS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/SUB-17UGGAMS/SUB-17UGGAMS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1997, 'width': 1437, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/SUB-17UGGAMS/SUB-17UGGAMS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/SUB-17UGGAMS/SUB-17UGGAMS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/arts/SUB-17UGGAMS/SUB-17UGGAMS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'She Who Once Improvised at the Drop of a Cue Card', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'She Who Once Improvised At the Drop of a Cue Card', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Uggams, Leslie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '54 Below (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T00:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bc3a7cb-336a-5982-97eb-537f6188eb1f', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bc3a7cb-336a-5982-97eb-537f6188eb1f'}, {'abstract': 'A United Nations appeals court on Friday unexpectedly overturned the war crimes convictions of two Croatian generals involved in an offensive that resulted in the death of hundreds of Serbian civilians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/world/europe/hague-court-overturns-convictions-of-2-croatian-generals.html', 'snippet': 'A United Nations appeals court on Friday unexpectedly overturned the war crimes convictions of two Croatian generals involved in an offensive that resulted in the death of hundreds of Serbian civilians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A United Nations appeals court in The Hague on Friday unexpectedly overturned the war crimes convictions of two Croatian generals who led a 1995 campaign that helped end the wars involving Serbia, Bosnia and Croatia but also left several hundred Serbian civilians dead and drove more than 150,000 from their homes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/world/hague/hague-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/wor