 'nyt://article/d1b6e754-9302-5176-8a7b-4e90942ca4c9', 'word_count': 1164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1b6e754-9302-5176-8a7b-4e90942ca4c9'}, {'abstract': '“Stones in His Pockets,” by Marie Jones, at Hudson Stage, depicts villagers hoping their bleak lives will benefit from a film.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/nyregion/a-review-of-stones-in-his-pockets-at-hudson-stage.html', 'snippet': '“Stones in His Pockets,” by Marie Jones, at Hudson Stage, depicts villagers hoping their bleak lives will benefit from a film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So a Hollywood movie company goes to County Kerry, Ireland, and almost everybody in town gets a job as an extra. Young men who already saw their futures as hopeless, finding themselves surrounded by high-powered industry types every day, have the reality of their own bleak lives rubbed in their faces. In the process, though, they soldier on, trying to act dispossessed enough or jubilant enough to satisfy the assistant director. And trying to get extra desserts at the craft services table. One of them even becomes the leading lady’s object of desire, though she may want to sleep with him only to get her character’s accent right. As an assistant director explains tactfully, “Miss Giovanni has a habit of going ethnic.”', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18ARTSWE1_SPAN/18ARTSWE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18ARTSWE1_SPAN/18ARTSWE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18ARTSWE1_SPAN/18ARTSWE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {