ent an innocent man to prison for 15 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge chastised the Brooklyn district attorney, Charles J. Hynes, on Friday for defending and promoting a prosecutor in his office whose illegal tactics sent an innocent man to prison for 15 years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top Prosecutor in Brooklyn Is Rebuked by U.S. Judge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Top Prosecutor In Brooklyn Is Rebuked By U.S. Judge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'District Attorneys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hynes, Charles J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Jabbar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T03:45:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b38d4e9-c526-5f42-b0d8-0b9a0599e220', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b38d4e9-c526-5f42-b0d8-0b9a0599e220'}, {'abstract': 'Absent Congressional action, the country faces more than half a trillion dollars in tax increases and spending cuts next year, and semantic debate has sprung up alongside the policy debate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/us/fiscal-cliff-slope-debtpocalypse-it-means-austerity.html', 'snippet': 'Absent Congressional action, the country faces more than half a trillion dollars in tax increases and spending cuts next year, and semantic debate has sprung up alongside the policy debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Come January, the United States might careen off the fiscal cliff. Or start rolling down the fiscal slope. Or, in a worst-case scenario, find itself staggering amid the hot ashes of a debtpocalypse.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whether ‘Fiscal Cliff’ or Debtpocalypse, by Any Name, It Spells Austerity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Whether ‘Fiscal Cliff’ or Debtpocalypse, by Any Name, It Spells Austerity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slang', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T03:46:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a726964-9da1-5b19-a1e3-5c6154d2886e', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a726964-9da1-5b19-a1e3-5c6154d2886e'}, {'abstract': 'Books on Emma Goldman and Alexander Berkman; the jazz guitarist John Pizzarelli; and the ecology of New York Harbor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/nyregion/books-on-emma-goldman-a-jazz-guitarist-and-new-york-harbor.html', 'snippet': 'Books on Emma Goldman and Alexander Berkman; the jazz guitarist John Pizzarelli; and the ecology of New York Harbor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THEY were born in Russia, immigrated to the United States as teenagers and met in a coffee shop in 1889 on the Lower East Side. “They became fast friends, briefly lovers and then loyal comrades, their lives and destinies forever intertwined,” Paul and Karen Avrich write in “Sasha and Emma: The Anarchist Odyssey of Alexander Berkman and Emma Goldman” (Belknap Press, $35). Goldman went on to become an advocate for women’s rights and an author of anarchist philosophy. She founded the anarchist journal Mother Earth, which Berkman would edit. The two idealists also became darkly entangled in political violence.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18BOOK/18BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18BOOK/18BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1369, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Friends, Lovers and Anarchists', 'kicker': 'Bookshelf', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Friends, Lovers And Anarchists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldman, Emma', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldman, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pizzarelli, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York Harbor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_