zation': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84df2ed4-2dc3-5e25-b1c9-fbf959dc817c', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84df2ed4-2dc3-5e25-b1c9-fbf959dc817c'}, {'abstract': 'The United States Embassy in Athens on Friday warned of the risk of violent attacks against visitors “perceived to be foreign migrants” after a rise in racially motivated assaults in Greece.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/world/europe/us-issues-travel-warning-for-greece.html', 'snippet': 'The United States Embassy in Athens on Friday warned of the risk of violent attacks against visitors “perceived to be foreign migrants” after a rise in racially motivated assaults in Greece.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United States Embassy in Athens on Friday warned of the risk of violent attacks against visitors “perceived to be foreign migrants” after a rise in racially motivated assaults in Greece, where far-right sentiment is on the rise. In a message on its Web site, the embassy noted that American citizens of African, Asian, Hispanic or Middle Eastern descent were most at risk. The warning follows an increase in violent attacks against immigrants living in Greece and foreign visitors, mostly by members or supporters of Golden Dawn, a neo-Nazi political party. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece: U.S. Issues Travel Warning', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece: U.S. Issues Travel Warning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T04:49:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c8eb51b-cf52-5d08-9e7c-788ef8127997', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c8eb51b-cf52-5d08-9e7c-788ef8127997'}, {'abstract': 'Flood insurance is expensive and homeowners of modest means are at the mercy of their insurers, whereas the wealthy can just rebuild after a storm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/nyregion/paying-to-rebuild-after-the-storm-now-and-in-the-future.html', 'snippet': 'Flood insurance is expensive and homeowners of modest means are at the mercy of their insurers, whereas the wealthy can just rebuild after a storm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To walk toward Jacob Riis Park on the western end of the Rockaway Peninsula in Queens, through the beaches of Belle Harbor and Neponsit, is to wonder whether severe weather has its own particular taste, its own logic for exempting certain belongings from its animosity. While Hurricane Sandy buried some of the area’s large oceanfront houses in the sand or split them in two, smashing sport utility vehicles into living rooms, other structures suffered a more artful destruction. These might be called, for the purposes of a perverse disaster tourism, the doll houses — places where the facades were ripped off to reveal rooms with collapsed flooring from which still-made beds dangled and cable boxes hung in the air from their cords; a tableau of total obliteration save for a preserved Oriental vase or an intact fireplace mantel.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18BIGCITY1_SPAN/18BIGCITY1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18BIGCITY1_SPAN/18BIGCITY1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18BIGCITY1_SPAN/18JPBIGCITY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18BIGCITY1_SPAN/18JPBIGCITY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18BIGCITY1_SPAN/18BIGCITY1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18BIGCITY1_SPAN/18BIGCITY1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18BIGCITY1_SPAN/18BIGCITY1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Paying to Rebuild, and Rebuild Again', 'kicker': 'Big City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paying to Rebuild, And Rebuild Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T04:49:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97d62e25-1e18-58a0-b0ef-2236426c5295', 'word_count': 897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97d62e25-1e18-58a0-b0ef-2236426c5295'}, {'abstract': 'Hostess Brands announced plans to wind down operations and sell off its brands. Test your knowledge of Hostess and the cakes it is known for.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/11/17/business/17hostess-quiz.html', 'snippet': 'Hostess Brands announced plans to wind down operations and sell off its brands. Test your knowledge of Hostess and the cakes it is known for.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hostess Brands announced plans to wind down operations and sell off its brands. Test your knowledge of Hostess and the cakes it is known for.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quiz: Hostess and Its Cakes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hostess Brands', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T04:52:27+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/f1cc214b-265c-565f-a96b-96869d1764e1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/f1cc214b-265c-565f-a96b-96869d1764e1'}, {'abstract': 'A Greek magazine publisher and editor who was cleared of violating privacy laws this month after he published the names of more than 2,000 Greeks with Swiss bank accounts is to face trial again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/world/europe/greek-publisher-of-hot-doc-to-be-tried-again.html', 'snippet': 'A Greek magazine publisher and editor who was cleared of violating privacy laws this month after he published the names of more than 2,000 Greeks with Swiss bank accounts is to face trial again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Greek magazine publisher and editor who was cleared of violating privacy laws this month after he published the names of more than 2,000 Greeks with Swiss bank accounts is to face trial again, a court official said Friday, after the prosecutor appealed. Kostas Vaxevanis who owns and edits Hot Doc, a respected investigative magazine, was acquitted of misdemeanor charges by a judge on Nov. 1 after publishing the list. The case shined a light on the Greek authorities’ failure to effectively crack down on widespread tax evasion and fueled a debate over media freedom and personal privacy laws. Mr. Vaxevanis is to be retried in a higher-level misdemeanor court on the same charges, and faces a two-year prison sentence if he is found guilty.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/world/briefs-vaxevanis/briefs-vaxevanis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 653, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/world/briefs-vaxevanis/briefs-vaxevanis-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1036, 'width': 661, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece: A 2nd Trial for Naming Names', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece: A 2nd Trial for Naming Names', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hot Doc (Magazine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vaxevanis, Kostas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T04:53:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/83ec61e9-ce5e-5f71-978f-858f4c19d0f0', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83ec61e9-ce5e-5f71-978f-858f4c19d0f0'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Garrett was an authority on decorative arts and known to the public as an appraiser on the PBS series “Antiques Roadshow.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/us/wendell-d-garrett-decorative-arts-expert-on-antiques-roadshow-dies-at-83.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Garrett was an authority on decorative arts and known to the public as an appraiser on the PBS series “Antiques Roadshow.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wendell D. Garrett, an authority on American decorative arts known to public-television viewers for his long, professorial presence as an appraiser on “Antiques Roadshow,” died on Wednesday in Williston, Vt. He was 83.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/us/GARRETT-obit/GARRETT-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cr