/a7f7905c-f0fd-5107-822a-8f11e1bcd159', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7f7905c-f0fd-5107-822a-8f11e1bcd159'}, {'abstract': 'How engraving and photography concealed, and revealed, the vital role African-Americans played in the Civil War railroad.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/the-civil-wars-brother-artists/', 'snippet': 'How engraving and photography concealed, and revealed, the vital role African-Americans played in the Civil War railroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In March and April 1862, a handful of photographers, some employed by Mathew Brady, set out from Washington to record the scenes surrounding the Army of the Potomac and to view the destruction left in Northern Virginia in the wake of the Confederate retreat to Richmond. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Civil War’s ‘Brother Artists’', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Mathew', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T05:27:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By William G. Thomas and Leslie Working', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Working', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b53f97b-419d-54ab-afa0-115eeb8a6b11', 'word_count': 1782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b53f97b-419d-54ab-afa0-115eeb8a6b11'}, {'abstract': 'At last count, officials were attributing 97 deaths to Hurricane Sandy and its aftermath within a 65-mile radius of New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/nyregion/hurricane-sandys-deadly-toll.html', 'snippet': 'At last count, officials were attributing 97 deaths to Hurricane Sandy and its aftermath within a 65-mile radius of New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At last count, officials were attributing 97 deaths to Hurricane Sandy and its aftermath within a 65-mile radius of New York City, in an area that stretched across New York, New Jersey and Connecticut, from Burlington County in New Jersey to Suffolk County on Long Island to North Salem, N.Y., in Westchester County, where Jack Baumler, 11, and Michael Robson, 13, died Oct. 29 when a tree struck Jack’s family home.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18deaths/18deaths-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18deaths/18deaths-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18deaths/18deaths-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/18deaths/18deaths-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1398, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/201