s of Diwali greeting cards, boxes of sweets and colorful e-mails, here’s some other ways of people have sent holiday cheer:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Diwali Greetings From Near and Far', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diwali (Hindu Festival)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colbert, Stephen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mukherjee, Pranab', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T06:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malavika Vyawahare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malavika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vyawahare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e51f8dc-1cdf-531d-847d-3f0b45ae9081', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e51f8dc-1cdf-531d-847d-3f0b45ae9081'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks’ perfect start came to an end in Memphis against the team with the best record in the Western Conference.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/sports/basketball/knicks-unbeaten-record-too-good-to-last.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks’ perfect start came to an end in Memphis against the team with the best record in the Western Conference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEMPHIS — The two coaches stood on the opposite sides\xa0 of the court on Friday, each one believing their style of play was superior. On one end stood Mike Woodson, who in a short period this season has transformed the Knicks into a team that plays small, relying on ball movement and strong perimeter defense. The\xa0Memphis Grizzlies’ coach, Lionel Hollins, preaches interior defense, low-post scoring and rebounding.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/basketball/17knicks-2/17knicks-2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/basketball/17knicks-2/17knicks-2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/basketball/17knicks-2/17knicks-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 756, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/basketball/17knicks-2/17knicks-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1513, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/basketball/17knicks-2/17knicks-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/17/sports/basketball/17knicks-2/17knicks-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Grizzlies Knock Knicks Off Their Roost', 'kicker': 'Grizzlies 105, Knicks 95', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grizzlies Knock Knicks Off Their Roost', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Memphis Grizzlies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T06:01:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05a60800-cf38-59c5-957b-377c8e4b1635', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05a60800-cf38-59c5-957b-377c8e4b1635'}, {'abstract': 'In the British theater a production of one celebrated title by no means precludes another following hot on its heels. Sometimes the one seems almost to be stalking the other. But how much is too much, even of a good thing?', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/chekhov-again-uncle-vanya-and-the-instant-replay/', 'snippet': 'In the British theater a production of one celebrated title by no means precludes another following hot on its heels. Sometimes the one seems almost to be stalking the other. But how much is too much, even of a good thing?', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you don’t like the “Uncle Vanya” you’re seeing, at the moment — or “Henry V” or “The Duchess of Malfi” or (fill in the classic play of your choice) — just wait a minute: another will be along in a sec.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/15/arts/15rdv-wolfb/15rdv-wolfb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None