: 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0963c9aa-7817-5cfc-ad64-65fd8def0c99', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0963c9aa-7817-5cfc-ad64-65fd8def0c99'}, {'abstract': 'Formula One has tried and tried again to find a permanent home for the United States Grand Prix. Finally, it has settled on what might seem like the weirdest place: Austin, Texas.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/f1-races-into-america-and-austin-keeps-it-weird/', 'snippet': 'Formula One has tried and tried again to find a permanent home for the United States Grand Prix. Finally, it has settled on what might seem like the weirdest place: Austin, Texas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUSTIN, Texas — There is something that feels a little unreal about this weekend in Austin. Or maybe the better word is that there is something that feels a little weird. That is, of course, good news for this city, a blueberry in the middle of Texas’s tomato soup — or whatever metaphor the cab driver used while driving to the Circuit of the Americas this morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/blogs/16rdv-austin-track/16rdv-austin-track-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/blogs/16rdv-austin-track/16rdv-austin-track-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'F1 Races Into America and Austin Keeps It Weird', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T12:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0238a079-4eb2-539f-b7d2-0b3f2dd58659', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0238a079-4eb2-539f-b7d2-0b3f2dd58659'}, {'abstract': 'After several weeks of illness, divisive politician dies.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/bal-thackeray-extremist-hindu-leader-dies-in-mumbai/', 'snippet': 'After several weeks of illness, divisive politician dies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The founder of the extremist Hindu group Shiv Sena, Bal K. Thackeray, 86, died in Mumbai on Saturday afternoon, doctors who were treating him told reporters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bal Thackeray, Extremist Hindu Leader, Dies in Mumbai', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T13:06:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eef18519-d0c5-5763-badf-feb5b761c6ca', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eef18519-d0c5-5763-badf-feb5b761c6ca'}, {'abstract': 'For vegetarian main courses, look to Greece for inspiration, writes Martha Rose Shulman in this week’s Recipes for Health.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/