e newly formed Syrian opposition council as the “sole representative” of the Syrian people, President François Hollande of France met with its leaders in Paris on Saturday and agreed to install a new Syrian ambassador in France.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/world/europe/18france_image1/18france_image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/18/world/europe/18france_image1/18france_image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/world/europe/18france_image1/18france_image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/world/europe/18france_image1/18france_image1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1349, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/world/europe/18france_image1/18france_image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/18/world/europe/18france_image1/18france_image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/world/europe/18france_image1/18france_image1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'France to Let Syria Council Establish Ambassador', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France to Let Syria Council Establish Ambassador', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T16:50:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0eddd46c-879f-5a00-913f-58025e4b6d6d', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0eddd46c-879f-5a00-913f-58025e4b6d6d'}, {'abstract': 'Time for another Acrostic from Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/variety-an-otherworldly-acrostic/', 'snippet': 'Time for another Acrostic from Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SECOND SUNDAY PUZZLE — I don’t know about you, but I’m a space geek. I love books, movies, and even puzzles about outer space. One of my favorites, “2001: A Space Odyssey,” was written by Arthur C. Clarke, the author of today’s acrostic quote.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: An Otherworldly Acrostic', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acrostic Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T17:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05e70d32-8a50-5378-bd8b-063c96dcd5ac', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05e70d32-8a50-5378-bd8b-063c96dcd5ac'}, {'abstract': 'Victories with long putters by Ernie Els at the British Open and Guan Tianlang, 14, at the Asia-Pacific Amateur Championship have fueled debate over a possible ban.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/sports/golf/notable-wins-with-long-putters-fuel-debate-on-possible-ban.html', 'snippet': 'Victories with long putters by Ernie Els at the British Open and Guan Tianlang, 14, at the Asia-Pacific Amateur Championship have fueled debate over a possible ban.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A golfer in his 40s and another in his teens qualified for the Masters 105 days apart, their generation gap bridged by a broomstick shaft. The belly putters used by 43-year-old Ernie Els in his victory at the British Open in July and by 14-year-old Guan Tianlang in his win at the Asia-Pacific Amateur Championship this month are the pokers stirring the game’s hottest controversy, one that has smoldered for decades.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/sports/putters/putters-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 635, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/sports/putters/putters-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1271, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/sports/putters/putters-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/18/sports/putters/putters-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/sports/putters/putters-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Golf Club to Divide Them', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Golf Club To Divide Them', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Golf Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Professional Golfers Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal and Ancient Golf Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Els, Ernie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tianlang, Guan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PGA Tour Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T17:15:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f91b88ff-0075-594a-9abf-fbe8ce9bb010', 'word_count': 1610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f91b88ff-0075-594a-9abf-fbe8ce9bb010'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama is making his first overseas trip after the election to China’s backyard as the United States tries to increase its influence in the region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/world/obamas-road-to-myanmar-is-paved-with-new-asia-intentions.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama is making his first overseas trip after the election to China’s backyard as the United States tries to increase its influence in the region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — On the stump this fall, President Obama boasted that he had “brought more trade cases against China” than his predecessor had. In an ad, he asserted that his challenger “never stood up to China.” During a debate, Mr. Obama said he expanded trade with other Asian nations “so that China starts feeling more pressure” to play by the rules.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/world/bull-diplo2/bull-diplo2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/18/world/bull-diplo2/bull-diplo2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/world/bull-diplo2/bull-diplo2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/world/bull-diplo2/bull-diplo2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/world/bull-diplo2/bull-diplo2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/1