essing smartly for work doesn’t have to mean spending tons of money on a huge wardrobe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/jobs/in-a-work-wardrobe-the-best-accessory-may-be-confidence.html', 'snippet': 'Dressing smartly for work doesn’t have to mean spending tons of money on a huge wardrobe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. You’ve been putting off buying new work clothes, but your wardrobe is showing signs of wear — and some of the items are outdated. You are on a tight budget, so what should you buy?', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/business/18-CAREER/18-CAREER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/business/18-CAREER/18-CAREER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1797, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/business/18-CAREER/18-CAREER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/18/business/18-CAREER/18-CAREER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/business/18-CAREER/18-CAREER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mix, Match and Add a Layer of Confidence', 'kicker': 'Career Couch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mix, Match And Add A Layer of Confidence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discount Selling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T18:29:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eilene Zimmerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eilene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/e299cedc-df9e-5adf-b35e-f892d48fb5b4', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e299cedc-df9e-5adf-b35e-f892d48fb5b4'}, {'abstract': 'The president of Keurig, the single-serve brewing business, says she twice took herself out of the corporate race, and emerged a better leader as a result.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/jobs/keurigs-president-on-stepping-back-to-lead-better.html', 'snippet': 'The president of Keurig, the single-serve brewing business, says she twice took herself out of the corporate race, and emerged a better leader as a result.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY parents both emigrated from France and met each other while living in New York City. My father served in the United States Army in World War II and later became an importer of exotic hardwoods. My mother, a fashion designer, stayed home to raise me.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/business/18-BOSS/18-BOSS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 587, 'width': 453, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cre