20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suit Contests Limits\r\non Online Activities\r\nof Sex Offenders', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suit Says New Law Violates Sex Offenders’ Rights Online', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T19:43:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Norimitsu Onishi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Norimitsu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Onishi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07377456-401b-5370-a9be-2211ba1492a0', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07377456-401b-5370-a9be-2211ba1492a0'}, {'abstract': 'Congress, an always-pokey institution, has become a civics-class horror show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/opinion/sunday/suggestions-for-filibuster-reform.html', 'snippet': 'Congress, an always-pokey institution, has become a civics-class horror show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE item likely to be on the 113th Congress’s agenda — the Senate majority leader, Harry Reid, has hinted as much — is filibuster reform. Over the last three Congresses, the number of filibusters introduced by minority Republicans has hit record levels, and an always-pokey institution has become a civics-class horror show, a legislative abattoir where perky, fresh-faced bills go not to become law but to die protracted, agonizing deaths, less “Schoolhouse Rock” than “Saw.” ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talking, Cured', 'kicker': 'Loose Ends', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Talking, Cured', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T19:44:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Handy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Handy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7017a6b-88d0-58a0-ab37-7252e6fdf272', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7017a6b-88d0-58a0-ab37-7252e6fdf272'}, {'abstract': 'In split-second auctions, companies are jockeying for the chance to buy online ads geared to your specific tastes. But consumer advocates see a risk of a computer-generated class system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/technology/your-online-attention-bought-in-an-instant-by-advertisers.html', 'snippet': 'In split-second auctions, companies are jockeying for the chance to buy online ads geared to your specific tastes. But consumer advocates see a risk of a computer-generated class system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YOU can be sold in seconds. '