s,” died on Nov. 8 in Costa Mesa, Calif. She was 96.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/dog-BLISS-obit/dog-BLISS-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 184, 'width': 128, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/dog-BLISS-obit/dog-BLISS-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 184, 'width': 128, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/dog-BLISS-obit/dog-BLISS-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/dog-BLISS-obit/dog-BLISS-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/dog-BLISS-obit/dog-BLISS-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lucille Bliss, Voice of Crusader Rabbit and Smurfette, Dies at 96', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lucille Bliss, 96, Voice of Crusader Rabbit and Smurfette', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cartoons and Cartoonists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Smurfs (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T20:20:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/28dba942-b40e-574e-8f3a-403e075f6111', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28dba942-b40e-574e-8f3a-403e075f6111'}, {'abstract': 'If life has become an endless series of sarcastic jokes and pop references, a competition to see who can care the least, we’ve made a collective misstep.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/how-to-live-without-irony/', 'snippet': 'If life has become an endless series of sarcastic jokes and pop references, a competition to see who can care the least, we’ve made a collective misstep.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If irony is the ethos of our age — and it is — then the hipster is our archetype of ironic living.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Live Without Irony', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How To Live Without Irony', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T20:24:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christy Wampole', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wampole', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b9e1554-d238-53fc-823b-ca6c0ad80804', 'word_count': 1847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b9e1554-d238-53fc-823b-ca6c0ad80804'}, {'abstract': 'I wanted church-going parents. Instead, books and wine were our grace.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/the-prayer-of-an-unconventional-family/', 'snippet': 'I wanted church-going parents. Instead, books and wine were our grace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thank you, God, or whatever you call yourself, if you are really there at all, and if you have a nice sense of humor (on which I am banking), for the family you gave me.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Prayer of an Unconventional Family', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Prayer of an Unconventional Family', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T20:25:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Lamott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lamott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fd43f2c-98dc-5d8d-a49d-474c01dc6c19', 'word_count': 1261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fd43f2c-98dc-5d8d-a49d-474c01dc6c19'}, {'abstract': 'Far-right ultranationalist groups are exploiting old enmities and new fears across Europe, inflaming xenophobia and violence against immigrants and minorities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/opinion/sunday/europes-new-fascists.html', 'snippet': 'Far-right ultranationalist groups are exploiting old enmities and new fears across Europe, inflaming xenophobia and violence against immigrants and minorities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE evening in September 2011, Ali Rahimi, a 27-year-old Afghan asylum seeker, was hanging around with friends outside his building in central Athens when more than a dozen Greeks approached. Several men set upon Mr. Rahimi, one with a knife. Panicked, he fled into his apartment and fought back, managing to push the men out the door. He found blood gushing from just above his heart, one of five stab wounds in his back and chest. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/sunday-review/18GREECE1/18GREECE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/18/sunday-review/18GREECE1/18GREECE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/sunday-review/18GREECE1/18GREECE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/sunday-review/18GREECE1/18GREECE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/sunday-review/18GREECE1/18GREECE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/18/sunday-review/18GREECE1/18GREECE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/sunday-review/18GREECE1/18GREECE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe’s New Fascists', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe’s New Fascists', 'name': None, 'se