on_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0b93072-d494-52dc-b23a-6ce60a86ec16', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0b93072-d494-52dc-b23a-6ce60a86ec16'}, {'abstract': 'Even Mayor Bloomberg, a genuine fighter for health, gives out chips.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/the-high-cost-of-free-office-snacks/', 'snippet': 'Even Mayor Bloomberg, a genuine fighter for health, gives out chips.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TECHNOLOGY companies are famous for providing free food for their employees. Office areas stocked with snacks are great for morale and promote random interactions that often generate new ideas.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The High Cost of Free Office Snacks', 'kicker': 'Ezekiel J. Emanuel', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The High Cost Of Free Office Snacks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snack Foods', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T22:33:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ezekiel J. Emanuel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ezekiel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Emanuel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5137e036-34c1-53ef-9d8a-4776e7b849fa', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5137e036-34c1-53ef-9d8a-4776e7b849fa'}, {'abstract': 'A lovely puzzle by Timothy Polin.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/star-crossed-lovers/', 'snippet': 'A lovely puzzle by Timothy Polin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — Well, this is nifty. Six movies and their star-crossed lovers, plus the actors who starred in them, adorn today’s puzzle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Star-Crossed Lovers', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T23:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b256682e-63f4-50bf-bd23-60092ede1a57', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b256682e-63f4-50bf-bd23-60092ede1a57'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my column from inside Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/when-our-policies-in-syria-have-failed/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my column from inside Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column is from Syria, trying to capture some of the humanitarian catastrophe unfolding there. Partly because it’s a civil war, partly because it’s hard to get the story, it has faded somewhat from the headlines. It’s an interesting contrast with the Gaza, which deservedly is a huge international story — but so is Syria, where about 1,000 times as many have died. Indeed, one of my concerns is that the Israeli strikes on Gaza (and a ground invasion if, God forbid, it happens) play into Assad’s hands by distracting the world from his brutality.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Our Policies in Syria Have Failed…', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T23:03:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71298041-b380-5739-86cd-2732c9893623', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71298041-b380-5739-86cd-2732c9893623'}, {'abstract': 'The police said the three men killed over the past four months were all shop owners of Middle Eastern descent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/nyregion/same-22-caliber-pistol-used-to-kill-three-brooklyn-merchants-police-say.html', 'snippet': 'The police said the three men killed over the past four months were all shop owners of Middle Eastern descent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first killing took place days after the Fourth of July inside Valentino Fashion in Bay Ridge, Brooklyn, where the proprietor was found shot in the neck.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/GUN-sub2/GUN-sub2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 200, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/nyregion/GUN-sub2/GUN-sub2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Same .22-Caliber Pistol Was Used to Kill Three Merchants in Brooklyn, Police Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Same .22-Caliber Pistol Was Used to Kill Three Merchants in Brooklyn, Police Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kadare, Isaac', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gebeli, Mohamed', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-17T23:13:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan and Christopher Maag', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maag', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfbfcc01-1657-5746-bcfa-c143f8451ed8', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfbfcc01-1657-5746-bcfa-c143f8451ed8'}, {'abstract': 'Phillip Johnson overcame isolation, psychological problems and homelessness and now is the life of a dance event he runs at the service center where he gets therapy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/nyregion/emerging-from-a-bleak-life-to-become-fabulous-phil.html', 'snippet': 'Phillip Johnson overcame isolation, psychological problems and homelessness and now is the life of a dance event he runs at the service center where he gets therapy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, Phillip Johnson was caught in what seemed like an endless trench of bad luck. He was fired from a job, exp