have for the first time given Hamas the ability to strike as far as Tel Aviv and Jerusalem.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/world/jp-gaza/jp-gaza-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/18/world/jp-gaza/jp-gaza-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/world/jp-gaza/jp-gaza-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/world/jp-gaza/jp-gaza-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/world/jp-gaza/jp-gaza-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/18/world/jp-gaza/jp-gaza-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/world/jp-gaza/jp-gaza-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Longer Reach, Rockets Bolster Hamas Arsenal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Longer Reach,\r\nRockets Bolster\r\nHamas Arsenal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-18T02:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d655f89-6c1a-5455-8ff4-274284a0c8b7', 'word_count': 1124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d655f89-6c1a-5455-8ff4-274284a0c8b7'}, {'abstract': 'After cruising to easy victories in the first round of the Women’s World Championship, Hou Yifan and Humpy Koneru, the top two seeds, lost their next matches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/crosswords/chess/chess-hou-yifan-loses-at-womens-championship.html', 'snippet': 'After cruising to easy victories in the first round of the Women’s World Championship, Hou Yifan and Humpy Koneru, the top two seeds, lost their next matches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There will soon be a new women’s world champion. And after an incredible series of upsets on Thursday and Friday in the second round of the Women’s World Championship tournament in Khanty-Mansiysk, Russia, it will not be one of the favorites. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/crosswords/chess/18chess/18chess-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 190, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/crosswords/chess/18chess/18chess-superJumbo.jpg', 'height