eludes-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The French pianist Pierre-Laurent Aimard performed the second book of Debussy’s “Préludes” with his own remarkably clear and varied textures but little sensuality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The past week briefly put to rest justifiable fears that Debussy’s 150th birthday would continue to be ignored by New York’s major cultural institutions.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debussy, With Rigor and Elegance', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Debussy, With Rigor And Elegance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AIMARD, PIERRE-LAURENT', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Debussy, Claude', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-18T20:26:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d978e07-c6b2-57eb-a759-ad138e710ee6', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d978e07-c6b2-57eb-a759-ad138e710ee6'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks topped the undermanned Pacers in a mostly sluggish Sunday afternoon game at Madison Square Garden, bouncing back from their first loss of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/sports/basketball/knicks-behind-raymond-felton-and-carmelo-anthony-upend-pacers.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks topped the undermanned Pacers in a mostly sluggish Sunday afternoon game at Madison Square Garden, bouncing back from their first loss of the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Raymond Felton, the player the Knicks chose over Jeremy Lin this off-season, has been an integral and intriguing piece of this veteran Knicks team. Unlike some of his teammates, the 28-year-old Felton is still in his prime. And although much of the pressure is on Carmelo Anthony to make the Knicks’ offense work, Felton understands he shares in the responsibility of making the Knicks successful.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/sports/basketball/19knicks-4/19knicks-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 784, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/sports/basketball/19knicks-4/19knicks-4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1568, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/sports/basketball/19knicks-4/19knicks-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/19/sports/basketball/19knicks-4/19knicks-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/sports/basketball/19knicks-4/19knicks-4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Felton Driving Offense, Knicks Rebound at Garden', 'kicker': 'Knicks 88, Pacers 76', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Felton Driving Offense, Knicks Rebound at Garden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Felton, Raymond', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indiana Pacers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-18T20:28:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdbfd1ff-460e-5255-9d4d-ce2c2d7e89d0', 'word_count': 936, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdbfd1ff-460e-5255-9d4d-ce2c2d7e89d0'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/17/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) SAFE HOUSE (2012) Tobin Frost (Denzel Washington, above), a rogue superspy formerly with the Central Intelligence Agency and called “the black Dorian Gray,” is held for debriefing in a Cape Town safe house by an untested rookie, Matt Weston (Ryan Reynolds), after dodging a gun-toting gang and slipping into the American Embassy in this thriller about the very bad things that operatives sometimes do in the name of country and company. Despite cutting among as many as four action scenes at a time, the director, Daniel Espinosa, “maintains a visually coherent, narratively rational sense of time and space, no matter how fast the story shifts about, which it does with increasing speed when that same heavily armed horde that had been chasing Frost breaches the safe house, slaughtering most of the American operatives and sending Frost and Weston running,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. The story, written by David Guggenheim, “ebbs into more familiar cynicism rather than building toward political complexity,” she added. Still, “\xa0‘Safe House’ is essentially and very effectively a rollicking smash-and-crash chase movie that happens to be surprisingly well acted.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-18T20:50:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/debfe2ea-a41f-573e-a114-e690c01fe6c6', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/debfe2ea-a41f-573e-a114-e690c01fe6c6'}, {'abstract': 'Television schedule for Sunday, Nov. 18.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/arts/television/television-schedule-for-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television schedule for Sunday, Nov. 18.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (13, 49) THE DUST BOWL Ken Burns uses film footage, photographs, the songs of Woody Guthrie and interviews with 26 survivors to chronicle the worst environmental disaster caused by humanity in American history. With a script from Dayton Duncan, voiced by Patricia Clarkson, Kevin Conway, Amy Madigan and Carolyn McCormick and narrated by Peter Coyote, this two-part documentary, starting with this episode, “The Great Plow Up,” explores the farming practices that, throughout the 1930s, destroyed the Great Plains farmland and turned prairies into deserts by unleashing huge, deadly dust storms. (Above, wearing goggles in Lakin, Kan., in 1935.) “Mr. Burns has two aces up his sleeve in ‘The Dust Bowl,’\xa0” Mike Hale wrote in The New York Times. “One is the copious supply of photographs and film of the dust storms themselves, awesome and apocalyptic images he can put on screen whenever we need a visual jolt. The other is his cast of living witnesses.”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "What's on Sunday", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "What's On Sunday", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-18T20:50:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6e315e3-b85b-53e2-8281-41a2cd943aa3', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6e315e3-b85b-53e2-8281-41a2cd943aa3'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/arts/television/whats-on-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (Nickelodeon) THE TEENICK 2012 HALO AWARDS Nick Cannon hosts this fourth annual ceremony, which was taped Saturday at the Hollywood Palladium and honors teenagers committed to public service by pairing them with celebrities who share their causes. The honorees are Allyson Ahlstrom, who founded Threads for Teens, which collects and distributes clothing to disadvantaged girls while giving them a boutique-shopping experience, and who is matched with Tyra Banks; Matt Ferguson, who created Matt’s Chemo Bags, filled with items that bring relief to cancer patients, and who is paired with Emma Stone; Kylie Lan Tumiatti (above, with Mr. Cannon), who brings books to life through performances and audio recordings, and who is matched with Justin Bieber; and Taylor Waters, a volunteer with the American Red Cross who is paired with Josh Duhamel.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-18T20:51:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7a315f6-c0a7-5490-b140-5616c8552dd2', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7a315f6-c0a7-5490-b140-5616c8552dd2'}, {'abstract': 'The Jets ended a three-game slide and improved to 4-6 with a pummeling of the Rams behind a brilliant performance by Mark Sanchez and a defense that forced three turnovers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/sports/football/mark-sanchez-and-jets-top-rams-ending-a-three-game-skid.html', 'snippet': 'The Jets ended a three-game slide and improved to 4-6 with a pummeling of the Rams behind a brilliant performance by Mark Sanchez and a defense that forced three turnovers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — Every defeat for the Jets has accelerated a potential overhaul, increased the discomfort, intensified the scrutiny. Their owner, Woody Johnson, called this season a “miserable experience,” adding that he did not “sign up” for such gloom. He put on notice the coach, Rex Ryan, who vowed to reverse the team’s fortunes or “die trying,” and the general manager, Mike Tannenbaum, who in a radio interview insisted that the Jets had been making “meaningful progress.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/sports/football/19jets-pic/19jets-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/19/sports/football/19jets-pic/19jets-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/sports/football/19jets-pic/19jets-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/sports/football/19jets-pic/19jets-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1425, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/sports/football/19jets-pic/19jets-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/19/sports/football/19jets-pic/19jets-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/sports/football/19jets-pic/19jets-pic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sanchez and Jets End Skid, Changing the Conversation, at Least for Now', 'kicker': 'Jets 27, Rams 13', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jets Savor Their Feel-Good Afternoon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Rams', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradford, Sam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Mark', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sparano, Tony', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-18T21:39:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d53c2358-d17e-57f1-9611-cff3bd78d907', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d53c2358-d17e-57f1-9611-cff3bd78d907'}, {'abstract': 'Cusi Cram’s “Radiance” suggests a story rich in compelling conflict. But that story is resistant to being told in theatrical form.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/theater/reviews/radiance-by-labyrinth-at-bank-street-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Cusi Cram’s “Radiance” suggests a story rich in compelling conflict. But that story is resistant to being told in theatrical form.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The set designer David Meyer’s facsimile of a 1950s dive bar off Hollywood Boulevard is so meticulously detailed that you might be tempted, before the performance of “Radiance” starts, to climb up on one of the tattered bar stools and order a bourbon, perhaps even dropping a couple of coins in the cigarette machine for a pack of Luckies. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/theater/19radiance-web/19radiance-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'wid