-series-on-own.html', 'snippet': 'The television series “Married to the Army: Alaska” focuses on seven soldiers’ wives who are terrified about what their husbands are facing and also kept in the dark about the worst aspects of it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Typically on the Oprah Winfrey Network a chewy center of titillation and raw candor is wrapped inside a puff pastry of warmth and good intention. The channel wants it both ways: to transgress without being fully complicit, to nod at sensationalism while snuggling under the cover of purposefulness.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/arts/submarried/submarried-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 905, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/arts/submarried/submarried-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1809, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/arts/submarried/submarried-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/19/arts/submarried/submarried-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/arts/submarried/submarried-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Home Front: The Kisses Are M.I.A.', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Home Front: The Kisses Are M.I.A.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oprah Winfrey Network', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-18T22:21:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9f4a145-940f-5f76-951b-8cba2ac9ef99', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9f4a145-940f-5f76-951b-8cba2ac9ef99'}, {'abstract': 'For the mezzo-soprano Bernarda Fink, somber themes dominated the evening at Alice Tully Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/arts/music/bernarda-fink-at-alice-tully-hall.html', 'snippet': 'For the mezzo-soprano Bernarda Fink, somber themes dominated the evening at Alice Tully Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'She had sung the last word of Mahler’s “Ich Bin der Welt Abhanden Gekommen,” and the pianist Anthony Spiri was playing the sober final bars. The mezzo-soprano Bernarda Fink looked out, over and past the audience at Alice Tully Hall, as if she had seen something in the far distance that she could not identify.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/arts/FINK/FINK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/arts/FINK/FINK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1515, 'width': 1090, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank