45-59ed-545c-aee5-818e2af465d7'}, {'abstract': 'The giant media company is on the verge of acquiring up to 49 percent of YES, the channel that carries Yankee games and perhaps the most valuable regional sports network in the country.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/news-corporations-bid-for-a-stake-in-yes-would-value-channel-at-3-billion/', 'snippet': 'The giant media company is on the verge of acquiring up to 49 percent of YES, the channel that carries Yankee games and perhaps the most valuable regional sports network in the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'News Corporation is on the verge of acquiring up to 49 percent of the YES Network from the Yankees and their partners, according to three people familiar with the negotiations. The purchase price for the noncontrolling stake is based on a valuation of the channel at slightly more than $3 billion.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Corporation’s Bid for a Stake in YES Would Value Channel at $3 Billion', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'News Corp. Said to Be Near Deal for Up to 49% of YES', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carey, Chase', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, James R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinbrenner, George M 3d', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinbrenner, Hal', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YES Network', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-18T22:33:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir and Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0f035ab-db13-5a25-849a-cae26aae6460', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0f035ab-db13-5a25-849a-cae26aae6460'}, {'abstract': 'The company will perform in New York for the first time in eight years as part of the Joyce Theater Foundation’s spring gala.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/arts/dance/nederlands-dans-theater-to-perform-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'The company will perform in New York for the first time in eight years as part of the Joyce Theater Foundation’s spring gala.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Nederlands Dans Theater will perform in New York for the first time in eight years as part of the Joyce Theater Foundation’s spring gala on April 10 at the David H. Koch Theater at Lincoln Center, the organizations are to announce on Monday. The company will remain at the Koch Theater to present two New York premieres on April 11 and 12 created by its artistic director, Paul Lightfoot, and the choreographer Sol León, who recently collaborated on the “Shutters Shut” duet at City Center. The dance company will also perform at Carolina Performing Arts at the University of North Carolina, Chapel Hill; the Music Center in Los Angeles; and Zellerbach Hall at the University of California, Berkeley.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nederlands Dans Theater to Perform in New York', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nederlands Dans Theater To Perform in New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nederlands Dans Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joyce Theater Foundation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-18T22:39:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdb3dad9-dd3e-525e-854f-7a1cb5205968', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdb3dad9-dd3e-525e-854f-7a1cb5205968'}, {'abstract': 'Government reports will include existing home sales and the consumer sentiment index for November, and Best Buy and Hewlett-Packard are among companies reporting earnings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/business/economy/economic-reports-for-the-week-of-nov-19.html', 'snippet': 'Government reports will include existing home sales and the consumer sentiment index for November, and Best Buy and Hewlett-Packard are among companies reporting earnings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ECONOMIC REPORTS Data scheduled to be released include existing home sales for Octoberhousing starts for October (Tuesday); and weekly jobless claimsthe Thomson Reuters/University of Michigan consumer sentiment index for Novemberleading economic indicators for October (Wednesday).', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economic Reports for the Week Ahead', 'kicker': 'Looking Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Economic Reports for the Week Ahead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-18T22:41:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/cda43172-ce59-5a21-8161-53098ae5c157', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cda43172-ce59-5a21-8161-53098ae5c157'}, {'abstract': 'The following tax-exempt fixed-income issues are scheduled for pricing this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/business/treasury-auctions-set-for-the-week-of-nov-19.html', 'snippet': 'The following tax-exempt fixed-income issues are scheduled for pricing this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Treasury’s schedule of financing this week includes Monday’s regular weekly auction of new three- and six-month bills and an auction of four-week bills on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Auctions Set for This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasury Auctions Set for This Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-18T22:43:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/834ef8de-d0b1-596c-a782-f85f6d1a3408', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/834ef8de-d0b1-596c-a782-f85f6d1a3408'}, {'abstract': 'The author Andrew Solomon explains how “Far From the Tree,” his new book, developed from his own experiences as a child and a parent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/books/andrew-solomon-far-from-the-tree-parents-and-children.html', 'snippet': 'The author Andrew Solomon explains how “Far From the Tree,” his new book, developed from his own experiences as a child and a parent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrew Solomon’s enormous new book, “Far From the Tree: Parents, Children, and the Search for Identity,” is about children who are born or who grow up in ways their parents never expected. It’s a subject Mr. Solomon knows from experience. He was dyslexic as a child and struggled to learn to read. As he described in “The Noonday Demon,” which won a National Book Award in 2001, he once suffered from crippling, suicidal depressions. And Mr. Solomon is gay, which made his parents so uncomfortable that as a teenager he visited sexual surrogates in the hopes of “curing” himself. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/arts/19SOLOMON/19SOLOMON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/19/arts/19SOLOMON/19SOLOMON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/arts/19SOLOMON/19SOLOMON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 610, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/arts/19SOLOMON/19SOLOMON-super