hotography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T01:16:28+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Obituaries', 'section_name': 'Obituaries', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/067d514d-9d1e-536b-905a-ade829af019c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/067d514d-9d1e-536b-905a-ade829af019c'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Lucas combined his patience, talent for lighting and large cameras to create memorable images of subjects like Marlene Dietrich, Lauren Bacall and Gregory Peck.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/arts/cornel-lucas-photographer-whose-portraits-defined-film-stars-dies-at-92.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Lucas combined his patience, talent for lighting and large cameras to create memorable images of subjects like Marlene Dietrich, Lauren Bacall and Gregory Peck.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cornel Lucas, a British portrait photographer who created defining images of Brigitte Bardot, Katharine Hepburn, Gregory Peck and a host of other celebrities during the 1950s and ’60s, when publicity photos were the lifeblood of the star-making process, died on Nov. 8 in London. He was 92. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/dog-LUCAS2-obit/dog-LUCAS2-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/dog-LUCAS2-obit/dog-LUCAS2-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1361, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/dog-LUCAS2-obit/dog-LUCAS2-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/dog-LUCAS2-obit/dog-LUCAS2-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/18/arts/dog-LUCAS2-obit/dog-LUCAS2-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cornel Lucas, Photographer Whose Portraits Defined Film Stars, Dies at 92', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cornel Lucas, 92; Created Portraits of Actors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lucas, Cornel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T01:16:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Vitello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vitello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac9e2fd2-91c2-5e2a-bcd9-8f30fccfc17a', 'word_count': 691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac9e2fd2-91c2-5e2a-bcd9-8f30fccfc17a'}, {'abstract': 'The popular public radio show gets a new lease on life after its last original episode was taped in October.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/18/siriusxm-to-broadcast-car-talk/', 'snippet': 'The popular public radio show gets a new lease on life after its last original episode was taped in October.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Public radio’s “Car Talk” car-repair, brainteaser and relationship-advice show may have an even bigger life in reruns than in its successful 25-year national run.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'SiriusXM to Broadcast Car Talk', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'SiriusXM to Broadcast ‘Car Talk’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Magliozzi, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Public Radio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sirius XM Radio Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T01:19:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00d3a5c2-9b4f-57d4-a99d-11a91a47412e', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00d3a5c2-9b4f-57d4-a99d-11a91a47412e'}, {'abstract': 'The real threat to our long-term prosperity is wealth inequality, so we need a progressive wealth tax.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/opinion/to-reduce-inequality-tax-wealth-not-income.html', 'snippet': 'The real threat to our long-term prosperity is wealth inequality, so we need a progressive wealth tax.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHETHER you’re in the 99 percent, the 47 percent or the 1 percent, inequality in America may threaten your future. Often decried for moral or social reasons, inequality imperils the economy, too; the International Monetary Fund recently warned that high income inequality could damage a country’s long-term growth. But the real menace for our long-term prosperity is not income inequality — it’s wealth inequality, which distorts access to economic opportunities. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Reduce Inequality, Tax Wealth, Not Income', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Reduce Inequality, Tax Wealth, Not Income', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T01:19:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Altman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Altman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/50fbd55b-3c90-5c8a-8296-0d5ea1cda08e', 'word_count': 1228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50fbd55b-3c90-5c8a-8296-0d5ea1cda08e'}, {'abstract': 'Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac owe the American taxpayer a huge debt. Why won’t anybody in Washington demand our money back?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/opinion/a-140-billion-iou.html', 'snippet': 'Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac owe the American taxpayer a huge debt. Why won’t anybody in Washington demand our money back?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHO says Democrats and Republicans can’t agree on anything? When it comes to fixing the government’s troubled and costly relationship with the private mortgage market, bipartisanship is very much alive. Politicians in both parties have reached consensus over the past four years to simply do nothing.', 'source': 'The New York Time