enewed push as a win-win solution. The contention is that they more fully serve the goal of diversity in higher education and provide a progressive way to resolve an enduring conflict that has now returned to the Supreme Court in a case about race-conscious admissions at the University of Texas at Austin. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Class-Based vs. Race-Based Admissions', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Class-Based vs. Race-Based Admissions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AFFIRMATIVE ACTION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Texas at Austin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T02:31:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9f49dba-4480-5365-bbd4-8c0527baec87', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9f49dba-4480-5365-bbd4-8c0527baec87'}, {'abstract': 'At 2, Elijah Rodriguez has already logged a lot of hours at the emergency room, a homeless shelter and Rikers Island.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/201