', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/nyregion/19winerip-booming-thanksgiving/19winerip-booming-thanksgiving-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 938, 'width': 938, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/nyregion/19winerip-booming-thanksgiving/19winerip-booming-thanksgiving-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/19/nyregion/19winerip-booming-thanksgiving/19winerip-booming-thanksgiving-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/nyregion/19winerip-booming-thanksgiving/19winerip-booming-thanksgiving-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thankful for a Red Sky at Dusk', 'kicker': 'Our Generation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T13:06:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Winerip', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winerip', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccae8a0b-12bf-5f77-880d-3d5a1b76362f', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccae8a0b-12bf-5f77-880d-3d5a1b76362f'}, {'abstract': 'The merger between Glencore and Xstrata looks on track to win approval on Tuesday. | With Hostess planning to close, Twinkies, Ho Hos and other iconic products will likely be on the block. | Cisco Systems is buying Meraki for about $1.2 billion. | Jamie Dimon of JPMorgan Chase is having discussions with the president on ways to avoid the so-called fiscal cliff.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/glencore-xstrata-deal-goes-to-a-vote/', 'snippet': 'The merger between Glencore and Xstrata looks on track to win approval on Tuesday. | With Hostess planning to close, Twinkies, Ho Hos and other iconic products will likely be on the block. | Cisco Systems is buying Meraki for about $1.2 billion. |...', 'lead_paragraph': 'After months of negotiations, the merger between the trading firm Glencore International and the mining company Xstrata looks on track to win investor approval. Shareholders are set to vote on Tuesday on the $32 billion merger, and on retention bonuses potentially worth more than $200 million. Last week, the sovereign wealth fund Qatar Holding, which had opposed the initial offer, voiced its support. While shareholders seem ready to approve the deal, it is less clear how they will view the retention bonuses for executives, which are subject to a separate vote. Qatar Holding, which has a 12 percent stake in Xstrata, said it would abstain from that vote, citing “the sensitivities concerning governance issues in the U.K.” It is also unclear what may happen if the merger is approved but the retention bonuses are rejected. “There is a chance the combination may backfire,” Bloomberg News writes. Xstrata’s managers might, in theory, walk away — “an unsettling thought to some longtime followers of the company.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Glencore-Xstrata Deal Set for a Vote', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T13:13:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/791234ac-fa01-5c01-92e6-bc39171c4251', 'word_count': 2004, 'uri': 'nyt://article/791234ac-fa01-5c01-92e6-bc39171c4251'}, {'abstract': 'Julian Edelman wound up stealing the show against the Colts, but as always, it’s Tom Brady who makes the Patriots go.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/week-11-quick-hits-tom-brady-and-patriots-versatility/', 'snippet': 'Julian Edelman wound up stealing the show against the Colts, but as always, it’s Tom Brady who makes the Patriots go.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy Benoit takes a tour through Sunday’s Week 11 games. Share your thoughts:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week 11 Quick Hits: Tom Brady and Patriots’ Versatility', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T13:15:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4956aced-63ee-5779-9ef7-67a12b31565e', 'word_count': 1729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4956aced-63ee-5779-9ef7-67a12b31565e'}, {'abstract': 'The blunt remarks by Xi Jinping were made Saturday at a meeting of the Politburo, which announced a turnover of 15 members last week during the change in leadership.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/world/asia/new-communist-party-chief-in-china-denounces-corruption.html', 'snippet': 'The blunt remarks by Xi Jinping were made Saturday at a meeting of the Politburo, which announced a turnover of 15 members last week during the change in leadership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — In his first speech to the Chinese Communist Party’s elite Politburo, Xi Jinping, the new party chief, denounced the prevalence of corruption and said officials needed to guard against its spread or it would “doom the party and the state.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/world/CHINA/CHINA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/world/CHINA/CHINA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1603, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/world/CHINA/CHINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/20/world/CHINA/CHINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/world/CHINA/CHINA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Communist Party Chief in China Denounces Corruption in Speech', 'kicker': 'Changing of the Guard', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Communist Party Chief in China Denounces Corruption in Speech', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T13:15:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85567d45-99df-57be-a19e-f3ae50c50bd0', 'word_count': 941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85567d45-99df-57be-a19e-f3ae50c50bd0'}, {'abstract': 'A woman’s Facebook comment about a shutdown in Mumbai following the death of a religious leader, and her friend’s support, land them in jail.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/women-arrested-in-mumbai-for-complaining-on-facebook/', 'snippet': 'A woman’s Facebook comment about a shutdown in Mumbai following the death of a religious leader, and her friend’s support, land them in jail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MUMBAI—For over 30 hours following the death of the Shiv Sena leader Bal Thackeray on Saturday, stores throughout Mumbai closed their shutters and taxis and auto-rickshaws stayed off the streets. While analysts throughout Mumbai debated whether the citywide shutdown following the death of Mr. Thackeray was inspired by fear or respect, one 21-year-old woman and her friend were arrested for raising a similar question.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Women Arrested in Mumbai for Complaining on Facebook', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mistry, Rohinton', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shiv Sena', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T13:15:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani and Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/592e0d41-575b-52e4-92ab-8cb8b71fcca3', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/592e0d41-575b-52e4-92ab-8cb8b71fcca3'}, {'abstract': 'Creating bespoke vacations, meatless main dishes for a holiday table, Medicare premiums to rise by $5 a month and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/monday-reading-creating-bespoke-vacations/', 'snippet': 'Creating bespoke vacations, meatless main dishes for a holiday table, Medicare premiums to rise by $5 a month and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: Creating Bespoke Vacations', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T13:19:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a6db85a-9edd-5530-af0c-4054e3891814', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a6db85a-9edd-5530-af0c-4054e3891814'}, {'abstract': 'The Galaxy and the Dynamo, who were among the last teams to earn places in the M.L.S. playoffs, will meet for the title on Dec. 1.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/m-l-s-playoffs-also-rans-and-title-runs/', 'snippet': 'The Galaxy and the Dynamo, who were among the last teams to earn places in the M.L.S. playoffs, will meet for the title on Dec. 1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was probably some hand-wringing and pearl-clutching among soccer purists last week when it became clear that the teams with the eighth- and ninth-best records in Major League Soccer this season were on track to face off in this season’s championship game. On Sunday night, that matchup was confirmed: Houston finished off D.C. United in the Eastern Conference finals, and Los Angeles did the same to Seattle in the West. Each team won on aggregate, 4-2, after a convincing victory in the first leg.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'M.L.S. Playoffs: Also-Rans and Title Runs', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T13:23:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76c1a095-171d-515d-a9c8-6a2124b3841a', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76c1a095-171d-515d-a9c8-6a2124b3841a'}, {'abstract': 'Bad history, worse economics.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/the-europe-in-rubble-excuse/', 'snippet': 'Bad history, worse economics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whenever I point out how well America did with strong unions and highly progressive taxation after World War II, I can count on conservatives trying to resolve their cognitive dissonance by saying “but it was easy then — all our competitors were in ruins!” You can see this all over the comments on today’s column.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Europe-in-Rubble Excuse', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T13:56:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49fefe82-3bff-5696-b985-69047bc58954', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49fefe82-3bff-5696-b985-69047bc58954'}, {'abstract': 'Heavy shelling and gunfire on Monday broke a tense standoff between Congolese rebels on the outskirts of the eastern city of Goma and government soldiers backed by United Nations troops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/world/africa/rebels-issue-ultimatum-to-congo-forces-in-goma.html', 'snippet': 'Heavy shelling and gunfire on Monday broke a tense standoff between Congolese rebels on the outskirts of the eastern city of Goma and government soldiers backed by United Nations troops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KAMPALA, Uganda — Heavy shelling and gunfire on Monday broke a tense standoff between Congolese rebels on the outskirts of the eastern Congolese city of Goma and government soldiers backed by United Nations troops who were hunkered down inside, as fears also rose of a direct military confrontation between the Democratic Republic of Congo and its neighbor Rwanda.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/global-home/20congo-image/20congo-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/global-home/20congo-image/20congo-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/global-home/20congo-image/20congo-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/20/global-home/20congo-image/20congo-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/global-home/20congo-image/20congo-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Congo Forces and Rebels Resume Fight for Goma', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Congo Forces And Rebels Resume Fight For Goma', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'March 23 Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Congo, Democratic Republic of (Congo-Kinshasa)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rwanda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T13:57:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Kron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f105aa6c-fb18-50b9-9d3f-39c7e52a3145', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f105aa6c-fb18-50b9-9d3f-39c7e52a3145'}, {'abstract': 'For Lily, 18 and fresh out of high school, destiny comes down to genetics: she is following in the stilettoed footsteps of her mother, the model Kristen McMenamy.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/styled-to-a-t-lily-mcmenamy/', 'snippet': 'For Lily, 18 and fresh out of high school, destiny comes down to genetics: she is following in the stilettoed footsteps of her mother, the model Kristen McMenamy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Girl ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '61', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Styled To a T | Lily McMenamy', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Styled to a T', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T14:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}