t': 'The author of this week’s cover article answers questions on Ashlyn Blocker’s lack of physical pain and how doctors might use her case to treat the opposite condition — chronic pain.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/behind-the-cover-story-justin-heckert-on-learning-about-pain-from-a-girl-who-feels-none/', 'snippet': 'The author of this week’s cover article answers questions on Ashlyn Blocker’s lack of physical pain and how doctors might use her case to treat the opposite condition — chronic pain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Justin Heckert, a writer in Indianapolis, is the author of\xa0this week’s cover article\xa0about Ashlyn Blocker, a 13-year-old who is physically incapable of feeling pain because of a genetic mutation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/magazine/16-justin-heckert/16-justin-heckert-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/magazine/16-justin-heckert/16-justin-heckert-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 810, 'width': 1080, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/magazine/16-justin-heckert/16-justin-heckert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/16/magazine/16-justin-heckert/16-justin-heckert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/16/magazine/16-justin-heckert/16-justin-heckert-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Cover Story: Justin Heckert on Learning About Pain From a Girl Who Feels None', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Senses and Sensation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T15:52:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18e9003f-1032-5792-bc79-dd3bb73f5ddf', 'word_count': 1091, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18e9003f-1032-5792-bc79-dd3bb73f5ddf'}, {'abstract': 'The French jewelry designer Annelise Michelson likes to meld odd ingredients — lace, chain and glass — into her bijoux.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/cuff-love-annelise-michelson/', 'snippet': 'The French jewelry designer Annelise Michelson likes to meld odd ingredients — lace, chain and glass — into her bijoux.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The French jewelry designer Annelise Michelson graduated from the prestigious fashion academy École de la Chambre Syndicale de la Couture Parisienne and went on to work for Hermès and Vanessa Bruno. She only discovered bijoux after Carine Roitfeld, the former French Vogue editor-in-chief, asked her to design accessories for a shoot. For that Michelson melded odd ingredients — lace, chain and glass — and realized that, when it came to jewelry, “there was a whole new world of things not yet being done.” For her latest collection, she has made gilded bronze cuffs ($1,950; annelisemichelson.com) that were inspired by draped si