id': 'nyt://article/6a39ae09-e527-5a7c-9ff2-e9ef4af1e8b1', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a39ae09-e527-5a7c-9ff2-e9ef4af1e8b1'}, {'abstract': 'The Hopi argue in a federal lawsuit that artificial snow made from sewage effluent would spread from an Arizona ski area and threaten the San Francisco peaks groundsel.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/snow-sewage-and-a-fragile-alpine-plant/', 'snippet': 'The Hopi argue in a federal lawsuit that artificial snow made from sewage effluent would spread from an Arizona ski area and threaten the San Francisco peaks groundsel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Weeks before the snow guns at the Arizona Snowbowl ski area are set to begin blowing artificial snow made from sewage effluent — a focus of a 10-year legal battle — the Hopi tribe has mounted a new challenge, arguing that the plan could jeopardize the survival of a fragile plant.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Snow, Sewage and a Fragile Alpine Plant', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sewers and Sewage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Forest Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T16:53:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Macmillan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macmillan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b486cff5-3744-59c4-827c-f977693df56f', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b486cff5-3744-59c4-827c-f977693df56f'}, {'abstract': 'On the Rockaway Peninsula, Buildings Department inspectors have the enormous task of determining whether houses are safe, fixable or broken beyond repair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/nyregion/in-queens-deciding-fate-of-homes-damaged-by-hurricane-sandy.html', 'snippet': 'On the Rockaway Peninsula, Buildings Department inspectors have the enormous task of determining whether houses are safe, fixable or broken beyond repair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joanne Brand stepped gingerly through the front door of her beach house last week and headed down a narrow hallway to look for her grandmother’s silver, heavy, old-fashioned cutlery dotted with delicate flowers. She managed just a few small steps toward the living room, and then she stumbled right into the wall.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/nyregion/20appraisal-1/20appraisal-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/20/nyregion/20appraisal-1/20appraisal-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/nyregion/20appraisal-1/20appraisal-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/nyregion/20appraisal-1/20appraisal-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty