imes', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tough Times? You Wouldn’t Know at Party for Private Equity Titan', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tough Times? You Wouldn’t Know at Party for Private Equity Titan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birthdays', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bonderman, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TPG Capital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T17:32:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14d5957a-49a0-5bfd-b4e2-0adf5ad11645', 'word_count': 691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14d5957a-49a0-5bfd-b4e2-0adf5ad11645'}, {'abstract': 'Conservation groups praise a commission for renewing fishing limits on the bluefin tuna but fault it for failing to protect sharks.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/bluefin-fishing-quota-will-rise-only-slightly/', 'snippet': 'Conservation groups praise a commission for renewing fishing limits on the bluefin tuna but fault it for failing to protect sharks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The international commission responsible for the conservation of the Atlantic and Mediterranean bluefin tuna agreed Monday to hold the 2013 fishing quota close to this year’s number despite modest signs of an improvement in stocks of the bluefin, the world’s most valuable fish.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bluefin Fishing Quota Will Rise Only Slightly', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Commission for the Conservation of Atlantic Tunas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Union for Conservation of Nature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oceana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Environment Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mediterranean Sea', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T17:38:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17417a32-4ff7-5ed2-80e3-178084320413', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17417a32-4ff7-5ed2-80e3-178084320413'}, {'abstract': 'Cirque du Soleil will appear in a parking lot at Citi Field in March.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/a-circus-at-citi-field-and-its-not-the-mets/', 'snippet': 'Cirque du Soleil will appear in a parking lot at Citi Field in March.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cirque du Soleil is bringing its newest big-top show, “Totem,” to a parking lot at Citi Field in March, a new location for its New York premiere of a show that deploys the company’s signature visual and acrobatic language for an ironic look at human evolution. The limited engagement begins on March 14 with tickets on sale for performances through April 7 (although an extension is possible). Tickets will be available on Tuesday for Cirque Club members and on Nov. 30 to the general public.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Circus at Citi Field (and It’s Not the Mets)', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Big Top Comes To the Baseball Field', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACROBATS AND ACROBATICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lepage, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cirque du Soleil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citi Field (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T17:42:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ea4f3ff-8754-5433-b430-cc7fb44c7355', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ea4f3ff-8754-5433-b430-cc7fb44c7355'}, {'abstract': 'The new locations include several of the busiest hubs along Manhattan’s West Side, including Times Square, Rockefeller Center and Columbus Circle.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/cellphone-and-wireless-service-coming-to-more-subway-stations/', 'snippet': 'The new locations include several of the busiest hubs along Manhattan’s West Side, including Times Square, Rockefeller Center and Columbus Circle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a year after underground Wi-Fi and cellphone service first came to a handful of subway station platforms, officials said Monday that 30 more stations would be connected by “the end of the first quarter of 2013.”', 'source': 'The New York Times',