e, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Q. and A. With Stuart Elliott', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Macy's Inc", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T18:12:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3e51103-b48a-5970-8c59-c361699a6eac', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3e51103-b48a-5970-8c59-c361699a6eac'}, {'abstract': 'Xi Jinping has a different style than his predecessors, that is clear. What isn’t clear yet is whether he will be much of a reformer. What DealBook readers need to know about China this week.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/welcome-to-the-xi-jinping-era/', 'snippet': 'Xi Jinping has a different style than his predecessors, that is clear. What isn’t clear yet is whether he will be much of a reformer. What DealBook readers need to know about China this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China has entered the Xi Jinping era. The transition to Mr. Xi from Hu Jintao appears to have been messy, given both the Bo Xilai scandal and the machinations of former leader Jiang Zemin, but Mr. Hu no longer has any formal party positions and the handover was, at least on paper, the cleanest in the history of the People’s Republic of China. It was also the first to occur in the Internet age, so we may have just been more aware of the plotting, scheming and infighting. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Welcome to the Xi Jinping Era', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'valu