, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/753c8075-4cbc-5c79-92cc-7c1474b5bb6e', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/753c8075-4cbc-5c79-92cc-7c1474b5bb6e'}, {'abstract': 'In 2012 books about the lives of acts like Fleetwood Mac and Rod Stewart have increased the canon of music bios and memoirs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/books/rock-n-roll-and-write.html', 'snippet': 'In 2012 books about the lives of acts like Fleetwood Mac and Rod Stewart have increased the canon of music bios and memoirs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Neil Young said it best: Writing books is a great thing for a musician to do. It’s a way to make money without having to play and sing all the time. If, like Mr. Young, the musician has broken a toe, given up marijuana, had trouble writing songs or otherwise begun needing a change of pace, the rock book answers prayers. Mostly publishers’ prayers. Since sales of Keith Richards’s “Life” went through the roof two years ago, these bios and memoirs have begun turning up everywhere.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/books/23maslin-img/23maslin-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/books/23maslin-img/23maslin-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/books/23maslin-img/23maslin-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/23/books/23maslin-img/23maslin-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/books/23maslin-img/23maslin-img-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Stars’ Year to Rock ’n’ Write', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Stars’ Year to Rock ’n’ Write', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Rod', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Neil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T21:59:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a3adefa-bacd-55a8-bf76-c1bc50c84575', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a3adefa-bacd-55a8-bf76-c1bc50c84575'}, {'abstract': 'A senior Egyptian official told foreign correspondents that the West was blaming the victims, which he said were the Palestinians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/world/middleeast/egypt-advocates-for-palestinians-while-brokering-truce-talks.html', 'snippet': 'A senior Egyptian official told foreign correspondents that the West was blaming the victims, which he said were the Palestinians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — While holding itself out as an honest broker for truce talks between Israel and Hamas over the Gaza conflict, Egypt’s new government sought on Monday to plunge into the battle over international public opinion on behalf of the Palestinian cause — an arena where the Israelis, more experienced in the world of the free press and democratic politics, have historically dominated.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'While Trying to Mediate, Egypt Blames Israel for Gaza Conflict', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'While Trying to Mediate, Egypt Blames Israel for Gaza Conflict', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T22:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d490248-cbdb-5179-8649-36c7bfd93c26', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d490248-cbdb-5179-8649-36c7bfd93c26'}, {'abstract': 'A Norwegian shares her secret to year-round, outdoor play: comfortable knitwear.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/new-kids-label-alert-ellas-wool/', 'snippet': 'A Norwegian shares her secret to year-round, outdoor play: comfortable knitwear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year ago, Vibeke Kvan Johansen noticed that in the span of two weeks her local Brooklyn playground went from teeming with about 200 children to having just 5 or so on its jungle gyms. The weather, of course, had become cold. But the emptiness was still strange to her; in Johansen’s native Norway, where “a warm day is 30 Fahrenheit,” children frolic outside all year long. The secret: a layer of not-at-all-itchy merino wool under their clothing (right against the skin). Johansen, a former hair and makeup artist and mother to Ella, 4, and Mikkel, 17 months, asked nannies and parents in her neighborhood what their little ones had on beneath their outerwear, and not one said wool. So, she’s made it her mission to spread the woolly word, bringing Nordic knitwear brands to the United States and selling their bodysuits, leggings, hats and more on her Web site, ellaswool.com. Why wool? It’s a heat regulating material, absorbs 30 percent of its weight in moisture before feeling wet, is softer than cotton and is better for those with allergies or sensitive skin. But perhaps its best benefit is that it allows children to play outdoors when the temperature drops, which, if you’re a parent is always a good thing. (Active children eat all their dinner and go right to bed!) “It’s my mission to have as many kids as possible outside to play all year long — with style,” Johansen says. “I already see myself as the wool queen,” she adds with a laugh. “Maybe not of the U.S. yet, but at least of Park Slope.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New (Kids) Label Alert | Ella’s Wool', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Warmth From Brooklyn’s Wool Queen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T22:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Kane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/228c118a-9f7d-5fe2-8037-0a5a975a76c8', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/228c118a-9f7d-5fe2-8037-0a5a975a76c8'}, {'abstract': 'The choreographer Juliette Mapp paid tribute to what she called “a wildness of possibility,” which electrified Judson artists of the early 1960s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/arts/dance/nature-and-its-discontents-juliette-mapp-at-danspace.html', 'snippet': 'The choreographer Juliette Mapp paid tribute to what she called “a wildness of possibility,” which electrified Judson artists of the early 1960s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nature is perhaps not the first thing that comes to mind when you think of the experimental Judson Dance Theater of the early 1960s. This was an urban movement, after all. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/arts/20MAPP1/20MAPP1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 739, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/arts/20MAPP1/20MAPP1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1477, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where the Wild Things Are Unexpected', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where the Wild Things Are Unexpected', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenblit, Jen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Judson Dance Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gries, Lance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lieber, Molly', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mapp, Juliette', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Eleanor (Dancer)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date':