eeking to educate Web users, a group of privacy pros is trying to translate obtuse privacy policies into graphic icons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Web site privacy policies are usually long, vague and notoriously neglected by most of us. Or as Alex Fowler, chief privacy officer at Mozilla, put it, “We have long upheld that privacy policies suck.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/technology/19bits-icons/19bits-icons-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 81, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/technology/19bits-icons/19bits-icons-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 81, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/technology/19bits-icons/19bits-icons-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/19/technology/19bits-icons/19bits-icons-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/technology/19bits-icons/19bits-icons-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Building an Iconography for Digital Privacy', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T22:50:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57f7bda0-3473-5dee-8688-b43b1c0b8bc6', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57f7bda0-3473-5dee-8688-b43b1c0b8bc6'}, {'abstract': 'Michel Kouakou’s dances, performed at the Joyce SoHo on Saturday, contain echoes and themes of his native Ivory Coast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/arts/dance/michel-kouakous-choreography-has-echoes-of-ivory-coast.html', 'snippet': 'Michel Kouakou’s dances, performed at the Joyce SoHo on Saturday, contain echoes and themes of his native Ivory Coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Vilcek Prize for Creative Promise honors foreign-born professionals working in the United States. Michel Kouakou, this year’s winner in dance, was born in Ivory Coast. Since he left Africa in 1999, his studies have taken him to Brussels, Japan, Prague and New York. Now living in Los Angeles, he has spoken of his desire to build an “artistic bridge” between his homeland and his adopted country. Daara Dance, the company he formed in 2003, is global in vision. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/arts/VILCEK/VILCEK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/20/arts/VILCEK/VILCEK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/arts/VILCEK/VILCEK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': Non