//www.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/opinion/how-obama-can-use-pressure-to-bring-peace.html', 'snippet': 'It’s time for President Obama to test Egypt’s and Turkey’s ability to lead in the Middle East.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOUR years ago, when Israel invaded Gaza and around 1,300 Palestinians and 13 Israelis were killed — the very model of a pointless war — Washington did nothing to offer a creative or positive path to the combatants. George W. Bush was the lamest of lame ducks, and although Barack Obama, after he was inaugurated, vowed to push for Middle East peace, he was too distracted by America’s domestic problems.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Obama Can Use Pressure to Bring Peace', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Obama Can Use Pressure to Bring Peace', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erdogan, Recep Tayyip', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T23:16:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Raviv and Yossi Melman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raviv', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Yossi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Melman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'r