cellation of three vacation days from the weeklong February break to make up for days lost to damage and delays from Hurricane Sandy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Storm Prompts New York City’s Schools to Cancel 3 Days Off', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winter Break Cut by 3 Days In City Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T23:32:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenny Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/251ef434-7e53-576f-b764-9195729f5fcf', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/251ef434-7e53-576f-b764-9195729f5fcf'}, {'abstract': 'Two men buried $10,000 in coins as something of a publicity stunt. They left clues, but after three years, the treasure was still not found. Recently, they dug up the treasure and donated it to a hurricane recovery effort.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/buried-treasure-unburied-for-a-greater-good/', 'snippet': 'Two men buried $10,000 in coins as something of a publicity stunt. They left clues, but after three years, the treasure was still not found. Recently, they dug up the treasure and donated it to a hurricane recovery effort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an adventure about buried treasure (real), pirates (made up) and clues (too complicated, it turned out), the temptation is to talk like a matey and tell the world: The cap’n says to quit yer foolish searching because the booty’s not there now. The laddies who put it in the ground dug it up and gave it away. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/nyregion/19cityroom-gold/19cityroom-gold-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/nyregion/19cityroom-gold/19cityroom-gold-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/nyregion/19cityroom-gold/19cityroom-gold-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/20/nyregion/19cityroom-gold/19cityroom-gold-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/nyregion/19cityroom-gold/19cityroom-gold-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Buried Treasure, Unburied for a Greater Good', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Unfound Treasure Is Unburied for a Cause', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-19T23:42:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'titl