ml', 'snippet': 'A former Notre Dame star, Justin Tuck of the Giants is keeping quiet about his alma mater’s chances of winning the national title.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — At first, Justin Tuck pleaded superstition when it came to questions about Notre Dame. Tuck is the Giants’ defensive captain and almost surely the most visible Fighting Irish product in the N.F.L., but he immediately became leery Monday when a conversation turned toward his alma mater’s No. 1 ranking and seemingly clear path to the national championship game.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1557, 'width': 1595, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/20/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuck Trying His Hardest to Avoid Jinxing the Irish', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tuck Tries To Avoid Jinxing The Irish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tuck, Justin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Superstitions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Notre Dame', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T01:41:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea6cfdab-40ae-5a1f-bc99-b132fba9eaa4', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea6cfdab-40ae-5a1f-bc99-b132fba9eaa4'}, {'abstract': 'David Beckham has announced that the M.L.S. Cup championship game would be his last for the Los Angeles Galaxy.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/beckham-will-leave-galaxy-after-m-l-s-cup/', 'snippet': 'David Beckham has announced that the M.L.S. Cup championship game would be his last for the Los Angeles Galaxy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Beckham announced Monday that he would leave the Los Angeles Galaxy after the M.L.S. Cup championship Dec. 1, ending a six-year run in Major League Soccer that raised the league’s profile and also its level of play.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beckham Will Leave Galaxy After M.L.S. Cup', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beckham, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Galaxy (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T01:47:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc15145d-9f2b-543b-ade8-72bf04c7ffc8', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc15145d-9f2b-543b-ade8-72bf04c7ffc8'}, {'abstract': 'The decision to charge a powerful religious leader in the death of two followers is viewed by many as a sign that President Macky Sall may pursue previously untouchable figures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/world/africa/murder-case-against-cheikh-bethio-thioune-tests-senegals-new-government.html', 'snippet': 'The decision to charge a powerful religious leader in the death of two followers is viewed by many as a sign that President Macky Sall may pursue previously untouchable figures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAKAR, Senegal — The singsong chanting wafted over the seaside neighborhood all night, and during the day the poor flocked to the edge of the religious leader’s compound to share sumptuous open-air banquets, feasting on giant pots of rice, five steers barbecued whole, camels, couscous and other delicacies. Leading politicians courted the leader, and thousands followed his word.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/world/SENEGAL/SENEGAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 983, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':