 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/sports/baseball/mlb-roundup-marlins-blue-jays-trade-approved.html', 'snippet': 'Major League Baseball approved a trade in which Miami sent high-priced players — Jose Reyes, Josh Johnson and Mark Buehrle — to Toronto for promising young players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Commissioner Bud Selig formally approved a 12-player trade Monday that sent five veterans from the Miami Marlins to the Toronto Blue Jays last week. The need for a review, even if it was only a formality, underscored the charged emotions that accompanied the deal.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/sports/BASE/BASE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/sports/BASE/BASE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1647, 'width': 1140, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Selig Approves Miami-Toronto Deal, Saying Judgment Involved Is ‘Plausible’', 'kicker': 'M.L.B. Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Selig Approves Miami-Toronto Deal, Saying Judgment Involved Is ‘Plausible’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Marlins', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Selig, Bud', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Blue Jays', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trades (Sports)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T02:12:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db62046d-6731-5b5a-b7fe-14b725b636ca', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db62046d-6731-5b5a-b7fe-14b725b636ca'}, {'abstract': 'Warmth and gratitude greeted volunteers who did their part to help clean up in Coney Island.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/opinion/day-laborers-offer-help-after-hurricane-sandy.html', 'snippet': 'Warmth and gratitude greeted volunteers who did their part to help clean up in Coney Island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 50 or so people gathered outside a storm-ruined taco restaurant on Saturday morning in Coney Island, on a backstreet behind the Boardwalk near the Wonder Wheel. They were day laborers, Hispanic men and women who have been spending weekends as a volunteer brigade, helping other people chip away at the mountains of debris and accepting nothing in return except work gloves, face masks and safety information cards from the Occupational Safety and Health Administration. They came from all over the region, including a day labor hiring center in Bensonhurst, Brooklyn, that Hurricane Sandy had washed away. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Day Laborers, Helping Hands', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Day Laborers, Helping Hands', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Day Laborers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CONEY ISLAND (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'su