-nov-20-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Tuesday, Nov. 20, 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Within three weeks, I had more feedback on my sociological ideas than I’d had in my whole teaching career. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, Nov. 20, 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T02:36:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/069bce7d-98c4-547e-acff-cd39de61c393', 'word_count': 43, 'uri': 'nyt://article/069bce7d-98c4-547e-acff-cd39de61c393'}, {'abstract': 'What a politician’s non-answer says about the GOP and American Christianity.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/marco-rubio-and-the-age-of-the-earth/', 'snippet': 'What a politician’s non-answer says about the GOP and American Christianity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There has been some attention paid, predictably enough, to Florida Senator Marco Rubio’s response to a GQ interviewer’s question about the age of the Earth. Here are the remarks themselves:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Marco Rubio and the Age of the Earth', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T02:39:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8577d3