ct', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Aurora (Colo)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bank Robberies', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T03:53:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Frosch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frosch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/167b526a-f399-520e-92db-95dec519d2b9', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/167b526a-f399-520e-92db-95dec519d2b9'}, {'abstract': 'For all of Roger Penske’s success, including 15 Indianapolis 500 titles, he had yet to win a Sprint Cup championship. Then Brad Keselowski came along.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/sports/autoracing/for-roger-penske-sprint-cup-title-tastes-sweet.html', 'snippet': 'For all of Roger Penske’s success, including 15 Indianapolis 500 titles, he had yet to win a Sprint Cup championship. Then Brad Keselowski came along.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOMESTEAD, Fla. — Roger Penske and Brad Keselowski are hardly the ideal match — Penske with his starched white shirts and stoic, reserved demeanor next to the swaggering, outspoken and occasionally outlandish Keselowski.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Penske, Cup Title Tastes Sweet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quest Completed: Title Is Sweet Taste for Penske', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Penske, Roger', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keselowski, Brad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nascar Sprint Cup Series', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Stock Car Auto Racing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Penske Racing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T03:58:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Auto Racing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Viv Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Viv', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a31f436-66b4-585d-95ce-1a8b61d17ff5', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a31f436-66b4-585d-95ce-1a8b61d17ff5'}, {'abstract': 'The International Court of Justice in The Hague gave Nicaragua control of a large area of the Caribbean Sea, but ruled that group of seven tiny islands should remain under Colombian control.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/world/americas/a-mixed-ruling-for-a-caribbean-dispute.html', 'snippet': 'The International Court of Justice in The Hague gave Nicaragua control of a large area of the Caribbean Sea, but ruled that group of seven tiny islands should remain under Colombian control.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The International Court of Justice in The Hague on Monday gave Nicaragua control of a large area of the Caribbean Sea that had long been part of the territorial waters of Colombia. But the court ruled that a group of seven tiny islands sought by Nicaragua should remain under Colombian control. The ruling was meant to close a long-running case filed by Nicaragua. The court ruled in 2007 that three larger islands belonged to Colombia. The group of smaller islands is much closer to the coast of Nicaragua than to Colombia, and the ruling could expand Nicaragua’s access to oil and gas deposits. Both countries have proposed drilling in the seabed around the islands, although environmentalists have raised concerns. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Mixed Ruling for a Caribbean Dispute', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Mixed Ruling for a Caribbean Dispute', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Court of Justice (UN)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nicaragua', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Caribbean Area', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T03:58:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8765eaf-a34b-549b-8819-ca94365f3da1', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8765eaf-a34b-549b-8819-ca94365f3da1'}, {'abstract': 'Officials in Bugarach will temporarily bar access to the town’s mountain to prevent it from being overrun by visitors looking for a haven ahead of Dec. 21, 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/world/europe/france-no-refuge-for-the-apocalypse.html', 'snippet': 'Officials in Bugarach will temporarily bar access to the town’s mountain to prevent it from being overrun by visitors looking for a haven ahead of Dec. 21, 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Local officials in Bugarach, in southwestern France, will temporarily bar access to the town’s mountain to prevent it from being overrun by visitors looking for a haven in the event of an apocalypse that some people believe will occur on Dec. 21, 2012, based on a particular interpretation of the Mayan calendar. About a hundred police officers and firefighters will block access to the mountain from Dec. 19 to Dec. 23 for “safety reasons” and to ensure that “any festive gathering of people, including rave parties and massive highly alcoholic street parties, will be banned,” according to a news release issued by Éric Freysselinard, the local prefect. \xa0Last year, the mayor of Bugarach, a tiny village at the foot of the mountain, alerted the local authorities after he read on Internet forums that some people planned to take refuge on the mountain next month. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: No Refuge for the Apocalypse', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: No Refuge for the Apocalypse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doomsday', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pic de Bugarach (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T04:06:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maïa de la Baume', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maïa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de la Baume', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a1ace48-e4f5-56f7-81c2-8c154eec1a5c', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a1ace48-e4f5-56f7-81c2-8c154eec1a5c'}, {'abstract': 'New economic bonds between Cuba and the United States have formed, creating new challenges, new possibilities — and a more complicated debate over the 50-year-old American trade embargo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/11/19/world/americas/20121120-CUBA.html', 'snippet': 'New economic bonds between Cuba and the United States have formed, creating new challenges, new possibilities — and a more complicated debate over the 50-year-old American trade embargo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New economic bonds between Cuba and the United States have formed, creating new challenges, new possibilities — and a more complicated debate over the 50-year-old American trade embargo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/world/americas/20121120-CUBA-slide-2CK8/20121120-CUBA-slide-2CK8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/world/americas/20121120-CUBA-slide-2CK8/20121120-CUBA-slide-2CK8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/19/world/americas/20121120-CUBA-slide-2CK8/20121120-CUBA-slide-2CK8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/19/world/americas/20121120-CUBA-slide-2CK8/20121120-CUBA-slide-2CK8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '