 the organization’s leader, Ales Belyatsky, who was sentenced to prison for tax evasion last year. Mr. Belyatsky says that he is not guilty; Western governments have criticized his prosecution as politically motivated. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Belarus: Rights Activists Face Eviction', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Belarus: Rights Activists Face Eviction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evictions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belyatsky, Ales', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vyasna Human Rights Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T04:13:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea85a258-a072-5bfe-8fc6-9bf39caf27f9', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea85a258-a072-5bfe-8fc6-9bf39caf27f9'}, {'abstract': 'Jean-François Copé was declared the winner of the leadership of France’s main conservative party on Monday night by a very narrow margin, more than 24 hours after results had been expected.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/world/europe/jean-francois-cope-becomes-french-opposition-leader.html', 'snippet': 'Jean-François Copé was declared the winner of the leadership of France’s main conservative party on Monday night by a very narrow margin, more than 24 hours after results had been expected.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Jean-François Copé, 48, was declared the winner of the leadership of France’s main conservative party on Monday night by a very narrow margin, more than 24 hours after results had been expected. Mr. Copé, right, beat the favored former prime minister, François Fillon, by 50.03 percent to 49.97 percent — only 98 votes — according to official results. The campaign was bitter, with charges of fraud, and will do little to improve the image of the party, the Union for a Popular Movement, which lost the presidential election in May and the legislature in June. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: New Leader for the Opposition', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: New Leader for the Opposition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Union for a Popular Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cope, Jean-Francois', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T04:17:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b172d4f8-3b87-5c8f-9c14-a5ad48a822ad', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b172d4f8-3b87-5c8f-9c14-a5ad48a822ad'}, {'abstract': 'The success of the Agra-Lucknow expressway could be a key factor in the chief minister of U.P.’s career.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/19/akhilesh-yadavs-big-highway-bet/', 'snippet': 'The success of the Agra-Lucknow expressway could be a key factor in the chief minister of U.P.’s career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sept. 26, the Uttar Pradesh cabinet approved construction on the Agra-Lucknow Access Controlled Expressway, the chief minister Akhilesh Yadav’s ambitious, 270-kilometer (168-mile) highway project that promises to connect two of the state’s most populous cities in nearly half the time it currently takes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Akhilesh Yadav’s Big Highway Bet', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AGRA (INDIA)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uttar Pradesh State (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T04:23:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Edison Hayden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'Edison', 'lastname': 'Hayden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d04ee6f2-6e82-5997-8b43-ab6991b46fe9', 'word_count': 947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d04ee6f2-6e82-5997-8b43-ab6991b46fe9'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 900 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/word-of-the-day-censor/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 900 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'censor •\\ˈsen(t)-sər\\• noun and verb', 'source': 'The