name': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e44f8053-b398-5e68-9e30-3308826894a8', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e44f8053-b398-5e68-9e30-3308826894a8'}, {'abstract': 'There was a time when the wizards of the Times photo studio created whole tableaux to situate the dishes they photographed, unlike the food photographers of today. “We tried to show a whole menu.”', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/set-the-stage-then-the-table/', 'snippet': 'There was a time when the wizards of the Times photo studio created whole tableaux to situate the dishes they photographed, unlike the food photographers of today. “We tried to show a whole menu.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'These are golden times for seductive food imagery. Open a newspaper or magazine, and prepare to be titillated by otherworldly close-ups of dew-moistened figs glistening on pillowy beds of sheep’s milk ricotta.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Set the Stage, Then the Table', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T10:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland and Darcy Eveleigh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Darcy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eveleigh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/950eb915-8a22-513b-afda-296a0d03ae64', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/950eb915-8a22-513b-afda-296a0d03ae64'}, {'abstract': 'Candice Childress, a high school senior in Las Vegas, has “very little pity for a school with a $100 million endowment that wants to burrow its way into the forefront of my consciousness by bragging about its Frisbee golf team.”', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/envelope-please-candice-childress-3/', 'snippet': 'Candice Childress, a high school senior in Las Vegas, has “very little pity for a school with a $100 million endowment that wants to burrow its way into the forefront of my consciousness by bragging about its Frisbee golf team.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'November is halfway over; teacher recommendation letters, last-minute transcript amendments and sanitized personal statements about “what a college education means to me” are all coming down the pipeline for most prospective students in this country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/education/envpls13-candice/envpls13-candice-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 408, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/education/envpls13-candice/envpls13-candice-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 408, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/education/envpls13-candice/envpls13-candice-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/03/education/envpls13-candice/envpls13-candice-thumb