it and the Burden: Tax Reform – Why We Need It and What It Will Take.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New Republican Tax Policy', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T11:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebeb5b43-1585-59eb-863b-0f8ee1067a2f', 'word_count': 1057, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebeb5b43-1585-59eb-863b-0f8ee1067a2f'}, {'abstract': 'Quarterback Josh Freeman is having a breakout year after Tampa Bay’s general manager changed coaches and rebuilt the offense, signing receiver Vincent Jackson and drafting running back Doug Martin.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/how-the-bucs-rebuilt-and-built-up-josh-freeman/', 'snippet': 'Quarterback Josh Freeman is having a breakout year after Tampa Bay’s general manager changed coaches and rebuilt the offense, signing receiver Vincent Jackson and drafting running back Doug Martin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chase Stuart writes about the historical and statistical side of football at his site, FootballPerspective.com', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Freeman Excels in Bucs’ Remade Offense', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Do