ey call home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For her 60th birthday, my mom cooked steak, but my dad had trouble chewing and five weeks later, at 59, he was dead, and she was facing a lonely house in Miami.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/booming/20children-booming-inlaws/20children-booming-inlaws-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/20/booming/20children-booming-inlaws/20children-booming-inlaws-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/booming/20children-booming-inlaws/20children-booming-inlaws-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/booming/20children-booming-inlaws/20children-booming-inlaws-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/booming/20children-booming-inlaws/20children-booming-inlaws-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/20/booming/20children-booming-inlaws/20children-booming-inlaws-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/booming/20children-booming-inlaws/20children-booming-inlaws-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Life-Saving Bond Between In-Laws', 'kicker': 'From Our Children', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T12:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathan Deuel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Deuel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db9b7b53-07bf-510b-b2cf-721ad1fcfb10', 'word_count': 1017, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db9b7b53-07bf-510b-b2cf-721ad1fcfb10'}, {'abstract': 'If the merchant cash advance companies can get money to businesses in a few days, couldn’t the banks do the same?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/what-the-s-b-a-could-learn-from-the-alternative-lenders/', 'snippet': 'If the merchant cash advance companies can get money to businesses in a few days, couldn’t the banks do the same?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last weekend, my family and I packed our car full of supplies and drove to a fire station in New Jersey to deliver goods to an area that had been hit hard by Hurricane Sandy. Like tens of millions of other Americans, we tried to make our small contribution. The experience was eye-opening for my children. They saw the devastation firsthand. And they got to see the volunteers organizing supplies and the Red Cross van delivering food to whomever needed it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What the Banks and the S.B.A. Could Learn From Silicon Valley', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Small Business Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T12:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ami Kassar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ami', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kassar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1a1d8b4-56c5-584d-9b18-1a5a3cf36204', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1a1d8b4-56c5-584d-9b18-1a5a3cf36204'}, {'abstract': 'Meatpacking of racehorses should be illegal, and the sale of horse meat should be banned.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/opinion/global/protecting-the-noble-racehorse.html', 'snippet': 'Meatpacking of racehorses should be illegal, and the sale of horse meat should be banned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was gratifying to read Joe Drape’s excellent article on the tragic plight of unwanted racehorses. To learn that 138,000 horses were sent to Canada and Mexico to be slaughtered in 2010 alone is shocking. This encapsulates the horrible end for so many older horses that are not put out to grass when their working days are over. Meatpacking of this noble animal should be illegal and the sale of horse meat should be banned. And our yet wild herds of horses in America must be protected from the whims of politicians.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protecting a Noble Animal', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T12:09:45+0000', 'docume