rl': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/signing-up-to-help-fight-alzheimers/', 'snippet': 'A registry of people willing to participate in Alzheimer’s studies was formed. Its goal: to provide information, raise public awareness, debunk nonsense and help accelerate the pace of research.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I just signed up online for the new Alzheimer’s Prevention Registry. It took about three minutes: I entered my name, birth date, gender, ethnicity, e-mail address and answered a few questions about whether I had received a diagnosis of mild cognitive impairment or dementia or had a family history. (I will resist the urge to crack nervous jokes about car keys or whether I will remember the username and password I just created.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Signing Up to Help Fight Alzheimer’s', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clinical Trials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T12:26:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc05f71a-6f1e-5af3-8a6c-17acd82b34fd', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc05f71a-6f1e-5af3-8a6c-17acd82b34fd'}, {'abstract': 'There is one simple, but drastic, solution, experts say.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/how-to-steer-clear-of-indias-strict-internet-laws/', 'snippet': 'There is one simple, but drastic, solution, experts say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The arrest of two women in Mumbai for a Facebook post is the latest heavy-handed move by India’s government to curb what Indian citizens say on the Internet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Steer Clear of India’s Strict Internet Laws', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tamil Nadu (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T12:27:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sangeetha Rajeesh and Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sangeetha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rajeesh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d51afcbc-23a6-5a52-8ad2-7ae400189d72', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d51afcbc-23a6-5a52-8ad2-7ae400189d72'}, {'abstract': '49ers Coach Jim Harbaugh left open the possibility of a quarterback change after Colin Kaepernick dazzled against the Bears while an injured Alex Smith watched.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/49ers-harbaugh-invites-quarterback-controversy/', 'snippet': '49ers Coach Jim Harbaugh left open the possibility of a quarterback change after Colin Kaepernick dazzled against the Bears while an injured Alex Smith watched.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the N.F.C. title game last season in San Francisco, it sometimes seemed that the 49ers were playing with one hand tied behind their back. They had no deep passing game with their wideouts; they barely had an intermediate one. Alex Smith completed one pass to a wide receiver in an overtime loss to the Giants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '49ers’ Harbaugh Invites Quarterback Controversy', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harbaugh, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaepernick, Colin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Alex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T12:34:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/540326e8-18fe-5e01-9589-9e857bd5d01b', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/540326e8-18fe-5e01-9589-9e857bd5d01b'}, {'abstract': 'A third exploratory drilling operation fails to yield bounty.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/on-our-radar-cubas-oil-hunt/', 'snippet': 'A third exploratory drilling operation fails to yield bounty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cuba’s third attempt to drill a deepwater oil well has ended without success. Underlining the dimensions of the country’s energy challenge, the $750 million oil rig that spent much of this year plumbing the Straits of Florida and Gulf of Mexico was the only deepwater platform in the world that can drill in Cuban waters without running afoul of American sanctions. [National Geographic]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Cuba’s Oil Hunt', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T12:38:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b00400df-ae9d-53ac-a843-770535d7d42e', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b00400df-ae9d-53ac-a843-770535d7d42e'}, {'abstract': 'Moody’s has downgraded France’s valued AAA sovereign debt rating. The bad news for President Hollande comes on the heels of what was seen as an irksome piece of France-bashing by The Economist magazine.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/french-downgrade-focuses-on-failure-to-compete/', 'snippet': 'Moody’s has downgraded France’s valued AAA sovereign debt rating. The bad news for President Hollande comes on the heels of what was seen as an irksome piece of France-bashing by The Economist magazine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — The French can always blame their latest bit of financial bad news on the Curse of The Economist.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/blogs/rdv-france/rdv-france-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/blogs/rdv-france/rdv-france-