ds': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Congo, Democratic Republic of (Congo-Kinshasa)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'March 23 Movement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T14:35:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman and Josh Kron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb94a36c-1656-5ef6-be7c-99ca0d0e4a12', 'word_count': 1033, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb94a36c-1656-5ef6-be7c-99ca0d0e4a12'}, {'abstract': 'Also, a documentary about David Geffen, to be shown on PBS, depicts a mogul’s life both familiar and not.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/the-breakfast-meeting-news-corp-awakens-and-when-publicity-photos-mattered/', 'snippet': 'Also, a documentary about David Geffen, to be shown on PBS, depicts a mogul’s life both familiar and not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rupert Murdoch’s News Corporation is becoming more active in the media world after a year on its heels as the phone-hacking scandal sapped resources and energy, Amy Chozick reports. The widening scandal with the BBC, which has been a frequent jousting target for the Murdochs, has offered a rare bit of schadenfreude. The first acquisition by News Corporation could be a 49 percent stake in the Yes Network, the cable TV home of the New York Yankees, which would fit into the company’s plans to expand in regional sports. Meanwhile, the plan to divide News Corp.’s entertainment and publishing assets has freed Mr. Murdoch to look to acquire businesses like The Los Angeles Times, without displeasing investors more interested in cable and broadcast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: News Corp. Awakens, and When Publicity Photos Mattered', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bardot, Brigitte', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Rebekah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geffen, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANTI-DEFAMATION LEAGUE', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T14:43:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0edf94f-fab4-504c-a4d5-f2a7e0abf5c5', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0edf94f-fab4-504c-a4d5-f2a7e0abf5c5'}, {'abstract': 'Bayer walked away from a deal to buy the nutritional supplement company Schiff Nutrition International for $1.2 billion, after Reckitt Benckiser made a $1.4 billion offer.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/bayer-drops-bid-for-schiff-nutrition/', 'snippet': 'Bayer walked away from a deal to buy the nutritional supplement company Schiff Nutrition International for $1.2 billion, after Reckitt Benckiser made a $1.4 billion offer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The German pharmaceutical company Bayer on Tuesday walked away from a deal to buy the nutritional supplement company Schiff Nutrition International for $1.2 billion.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bayer Drops Bid for Schiff Nutrition', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'DealBook Online: Abandoning A Bid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reckitt Benckiser', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T14:58:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50164261-b17d-5266-a170-6166bb957d66', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50164261-b17d-5266-a170-6166bb957d66'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Susan Kellogg, a Drexel medical-school professor, is prepared to answer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/booming/ask-an-expert-on-female-sexuality.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Susan Kellogg, a Drexel medical-school professor, is prepared to answer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s Ask the Expert features Dr. Susan Kellogg, who will answer questions related to female sexuality. She is a professor of obstetrics and gynecology at Drexel University College of Medicine in Philadelphia; a professor of human sexuality at Widener University in Chester, Pa.; and a clinical associate faculty member at the University of Pennsylvania and Thomas Jefferson University. Dr. Kellogg is also the co-founder of The Pelvic and Sexual Health Institute of Philadelphia, where she is the director of Vulvar and Sexual Medicine and a member of the editorial board of The Journal of Sexual Medicine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/booming/21expertplea-booming-sex/21expertplea-booming-sex-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 731, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/booming/21expertplea-booming-sex/21expertplea-booming-sex-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1463, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/booming/21expertplea-booming-sex/21expertplea-booming-sex-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/21/booming/21expertplea-booming-sex/21expertplea-booming-sex-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/booming/21expertplea-booming-sex/21expertplea-booming-sex-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Have Questions on Female Sexuality?', 'kicker': 'Ask an Expert', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T15:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Winerip', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winerip', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/023cc2e0-66ec-5b0d-927c-08fafa87f081', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/023cc2e0-66ec-5b0d-927c-08fafa87f081'}, {'abstract': 'The Web lapped newspapers as a primary source of coverage in 2012, but a fair amount of that online traffic went to, you guessed it, newspaper sites.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/election-audience-votes-and-web-clobbers-print/', 'snippet': 'The Web lapped newspapers as a primary source of coverage in 2012, but a fair amount of that online traffic went to, you guessed it, newspaper sites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elections are full of real-time data and rapid twists and turns, so it’s no surprise that audiences flocked to the Web in the recent election and seemed to use newspapers as a secondary source on election matters. In the great unpacking of the 2012 election, the Pew Research Center took a look at how and where voters got their news.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Election Audience Votes, and Web Clobbers Print', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T15:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f11fde9a-c08b-5215-ae41-1c51a8da2c89', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f11fde9a-c08b-5215-ae41-1c51a8da2c89'}, {'abstract': 'After