 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/559a98be-20cf-5685-bd81-ed07c8e756c9'}, {'abstract': 'In Maryland and Rutgers, the Big Ten added two schools that were successes at running up budget deficits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/sports/is-a-bigger-big-ten-better-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'In Maryland and Rutgers, the Big Ten added two schools that were successes at running up budget deficits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you were sitting around recently thinking, gosh, it has been a little slow in the world of college conference money-grubbing expansion moves, the Big Ten has ridden to your rescue. Yes, it had been a whole 15 minutes since college sports reminded everyone with a bullhorn that it is really all about television revenue and getting bigger and badder and muscling out the competition and hoarding more schools that people might have heard of and holding news conferences to tell everyone you are bigger and badder and yes, money trumps all. So thanks, Big Ten, we really needed that reminder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/sports/ncaafootball/21leadingpic/21leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/sports/ncaafootball/21leadingpic/21leadingpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1438, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/sports/ncaafootball/21leadingpic/21leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/21/sports/ncaafootball/21leadingpic/21leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth':