potentially affect criminal cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Police Commissioner Raymond W. Kelly said Tuesday that facilities used for storing evidence in criminal cases suffered flooding during Hurricane Sandy. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Say Storm Damaged Evidence', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flooding Damages Evidence Stored At Police Facilities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Raymond W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T17:44:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88a7c85e-7b88-5613-9c7b-6b7a5c00e0ba', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88a7c85e-7b88-5613-9c7b-6b7a5c00e0ba'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a rock thing.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/how-we-know-the-earth-is-old/', 'snippet': 'It’s a rock thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One thing that kind of tickles me about Marco Rubio’s age of the planet stuff is that it leads right to one of my favorite examples of science — the founding of modern geology by James Hutton, part of the Scottish Enlightenment. (Another figure in that Enlightenment, David Hume, created what I consider the first true economic model. Hume also wrote some philosophy, I hear — and was friends with a guy named Adam Smith). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How We Know The Earth Is Old', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T17:45:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4bf1b95-d1f6-5ad8-9a4d-965930447e18', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4bf1b95-d1f6-5ad8-9a4d-965930447e18'}, {'abstract': 'An exotic use for turkey leftovers: biryani, a rice dish rich with fragrant spices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/dining/biryani-a-fragrant-rice-dish-perfect-for-thanksgiving-leftovers.html', 'snippet': 'An exotic use for turkey leftovers: biryani, a rice dish rich with fragrant spices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BIRYANI, the fragrant, festive rice dish, is found all over India and Pakistan, but is popular in the Middle East and Southeast Asia as well. Of course, it is also served in the United States in restaurants and private homes, and sold from street carts.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/dining/21KITCH_SPAN/21KITCH_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/21/dining/21KITCH_SPAN/21KITCH_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/dining/21KITCH_SPAN/21KITCH_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption':