ntum diversions, like thrillers and crime novels, though occasionally the serious stuff intrudes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/magazine/20-hugo-books/20-hugo-books-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/magazine/20-hugo-books/20-hugo-books-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1463, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/magazine/20-hugo-books/20-hugo-books-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/20/magazine/20-hugo-books/20-hugo-books-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/20/magazine/20-hugo-books/20-hugo-books-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Read Like a Person Who Has Way Too Much to Read', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-20T19:55:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugo Lindgren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindgren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60fdbf1f-aa07-5c48-bcd6-6400ed3e54ff', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60fdbf1f-aa07-5c48-bcd6-6400ed3e54ff'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers for an 80-year-old widow of a veteran are asking the United States Supreme Court to empower the Court of Appeals for Veterans Claims to issue fewer remands and simply issue final decisions on its own.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/a-case-that-could-unhinge-a-veterans-benefits-hamster-wheel/', 'snippet': 'Lawyers for an 80-year-old widow of a veteran are asking the United States Supreme Court to empower the Court of Appeals for Veterans Claims to issue fewer remands and simply issue final decisions on its own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there is one thing more frustrating, complicated and time-consuming than applying for veterans disability benefits, it may well be appealing the decisions made by the Department of Veterans Affairs on those very claims. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Case That Could Unhinge a Veterans Benefits ‘Hamster Wheel’', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Widows and Widowers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fox, William F', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dickinson School of Law', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 10, 'major