38b3442', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8008e4d3-5737-56dc-b08b-d917238b3442'}, {'abstract': '“Thomas Jefferson: The Art of Power,” a new biography, devotes much attention to the statesman’s view of the republic as being engaged in a long, partly undeclared war with Britain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/books/thomas-jefferson-the-art-of-power-by-jon-meacham.html', 'snippet': '“Thomas Jefferson: The Art of Power,” a new biography, devotes much attention to the statesman’s view of the republic as being engaged in a long, partly undeclared war with Britain.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Self-evident” is one of the most meaningful words in the Declaration of Independence, a document drafted by Thomas Jefferson but edited by some of his fellow founding fathers. According to  Walter Isaacson, author of a biography of Benjamin Franklin, Jefferson’s original version used the phrase “We hold these truths to be sacred & undeniable.” It was Franklin who deemed those same truths “self-evident,” to convey that they were rooted in rationality, not religion.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/arts/21BOOK/21BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/arts/21BOOK/21BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1361, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/arts/21BOOK/21BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/21/arts/21BOOK/21BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight':