r and related operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense has identified 2,141 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations. It confirmed the deaths of the following Americans recently:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T00:15:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaa1bf2b-6c4c-55e5-b0f3-b1d94516763e', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaa1bf2b-6c4c-55e5-b0f3-b1d94516763e'}, {'abstract': 'In Belgium, a small European nation struggling with ethnic rivalries, the national soccer team has put to one side the political and linguistic differences that have crippled society.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/sports/soccer/in-divided-belgium-sons-of-immigrants-unite-on-soccer-field.html', 'snippet': 'In Belgium, a small European nation struggling with ethnic rivalries, the national soccer team has put to one side the political and linguistic differences that have crippled society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — In opposite corners of the press room, deep inside King Baudouin Stadium, two packs of journalists crowded around their subjects. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype':