obama-in-cambodia-sidesteps-the-ghosts-of-history.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s visit did not address the tumultuous events of the 1970s, when American warplanes carpet-bombed the impoverished country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHNOM PENH, Cambodia — Four decades after American warplanes carpet-bombed this impoverished country, an American president came to visit for the first time. He came not to defend the past, nor to apologize for it. In fact, he made no public mention of it whatsoever.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/world/CAMBODIA/CAMBODIA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/21/world/CAMBODIA/CAMBODIA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/world/CAMBODIA/CAMBODIA-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/world/CAMBODIA/CAMBODIA-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/world/CAMBODIA/CAMBODIA-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/21/world/CAMBODIA/CAMBODIA-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/world/CAMBODIA/CAMBODIA-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama, in Cambodia, Sidesteps Ghosts of American Wartime Past', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama, in Cambodia, Sidesteps Ghosts of American Wartime Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Asean', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambodia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hun Sen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T00:44:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e91819d-4e5c-54f3-a4ea-e22ebbf4aa14', 'word_count': 1127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e91819d-4e5c-54f3-a4ea-e22ebbf4aa14'}, {'abstract': 'A medical student in India complained on Facebook about the attention a political leader’s death was getting, and she and a friend were charged.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/world/asia/india-police-arrest-student-over-facebook-post.html', 'snippet': 'A medical student in India complained on Facebook about the attention a political leader’s death was getting, and she and a friend were charged.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — When the right-wing Hindu political leader Bal K. Th