e41c803'}, {'abstract': 'Hiroki Kuroda, who will turn 38 next year, agreed Tuesday to a one-year, $15 million contract to pitch for the Yankees again next season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/sports/baseball/hiroki-kuroda-signs-one-year-deal-with-yankees.html', 'snippet': 'Hiroki Kuroda, who will turn 38 next year, agreed Tuesday to a one-year, $15 million contract to pitch for the Yankees again next season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hiroki Kuroda turns 38 years old on Feb. 10, right around the time he will report to spring training for his 17th professional season. Most of those were spent in Japan, where he might finish his career someday. For now, he is staying with the Yankees, with a one-year, $15 million contract that helps them in two ways.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/sports/cityREFERyankees/cityREFERyankees-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/21/sports/cityREFERyankees/cityREFERyankees-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/sports/cityREFERyankees/cityREFERyankees-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/sports/cityREFERyankees/cityREFERyankees-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 815, 'width': 1903, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/sports/cityREFERyankees/cityREFERyankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/21/sports/cityREFERyankees/cityREFERyankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/sports/cityREFERyankees/cityREFERyankees-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kuroda Re-Signs With Yanks for a Year', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kuroda Re-Signs With Yanks For a Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuroda, Hiroki', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T01:15:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f782b847-8ba2-58e7-a3c2-aa6da685a294', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f782b847-8ba2-58e7-a3c2-aa6da685a294'}, {'abstract': 'A report by the Food and Drug Administration found flaws in the company’s testing and oversight of a product known as the Durata.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/business/report-raises-concerns-over-st-jude-heart-device.html', 'snippet': 'A report by the Food and Drug Administration found flaws in the company’s testing and oversight of a product known as the Durata.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A report on an inspection of a St. Jude Medical facility released Tuesday by federal officials found significant flaws in the company’s testing and oversight of a controversial heart device component, a copy of the document shows. The report may also raise questions about how St. Jude executives recently depicted the inspection’s contents to investors and others.\xa0', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Report Raises Concerns Over St. Jude Heart Device', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Report Raises Concerns\r\nOver Heart Device Maker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heart', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Implants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Devices', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Jude Medical Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defibrillators', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T01:16:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Thomas and Barry Meier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d383d06-ab05-54fe-86fe-0cda9ad800a4', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d383d06-ab05-54fe-86fe-0cda9ad800a4'}, {'abstract': 'Roy Bourgeois, a Roman Catholic priest who became an outspoken advocate for the ordination of women, has been excommunicated and defrocked by the Vatican.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/us/religion-priest-excommunicated-for-ordaining-a-woman.html', 'snippet': 'Roy Bourgeois, a Roman Catholic priest who became an outspoken advocate for the ordination of women, has been excommunicated and defrocked by the Vatican.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roy Bourgeois, a Roman Catholic priest who became an outspoken advocate for the ordination of women, has been excommunicated and defrocked by the Vatican and dismissed from the Maryknoll Fathers and Brothers. Mr. Bourgeois, 73, was a Maryknoll priest for 40 years, serving in El Salvador and leading protests at the United States Army School of the Americas in Georgia. In 2008, after he participated in an ordination ceremony for a woman, the Vatican told him to recant or face excommunication. Its doctrinal office ordered his dismissal on Oct. 4, but Mr. Bourgeois, who said he believed he was in the midst of negotiations with his superiors, did not learn about it until Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Religion: Priest Excommunicated for Ordaining a Woman', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Religion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Priest Excommunicated For Ordaining a Woman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bourgeois, Roy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Excommunication', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T01:17:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie Goodstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c473c85-aa9a-52b5-9751-48422ece9217', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c473c85-aa9a-52b5-9751-48422ece9217'}, {'abstract': 'Bucking the trend of travel services shutting down in the face of online competition, Liberty Travel has opened a 10,000-square-foot store on Madison Avenue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/realestate/commercial/liberty-travel-opens-a-flagship-in-midtown-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'Bucking the trend of travel services shutting down in the face of online competition, Liberty Travel has opened a 10,000-square-foot store on Madison Avenue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While popular travel Web sites have led many brick-and-mortar travel agencies across the United States to shut down in recent years, FC USA, part of the global Australian travel company that owns Liberty Travel, chose to buck that trend and last month opened a 10,000-square-foot storefront on Madison Avenue in Midtown Manhattan. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/business/TRAVEL/TRAVEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/business/TRAVEL/TRAVEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1315, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/business/TRAVEL/TRAVEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/21/business/TRAVEL/TRAVEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/business/TRAVEL/TRA