5903-9739-94f13a9f1894', 'word_count': 655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/084f9130-617c-5903-9739-94f13a9f1894'}, {'abstract': 'Employees said a warning from the company that “there could be consequences” for not reporting to work constituted an illegal threat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/business/wal-mart-workers-file-complaint-with-us-labor-board.html', 'snippet': 'Employees said a warning from the company that “there could be consequences” for not reporting to work constituted an illegal threat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A union-backed group of Wal-Mart workers, OUR Walmart, said on Tuesday that it had filed a complaint with the National Labor Relations Board, asserting that Wal-Mart was making illegal threats to deter its employees from participating in protests scheduled for Black Friday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wal-Mart Workers File Complaint With U.S. Labor Board', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wal-Mart Workers File Complaint With U.S. Labor Board', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wal-Mart Stores Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Labor Relations Board', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Friday and Cyber Monday (Shopping)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T01:48:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebee4fd4-ceba-5269-9095-b268e1a59f06', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebee4fd4-ceba-5269-9095-b268e1a59f06'}, {'abstract': 'Hewlett-Packard contends that Autonomy, the British software firm it acquired for $10 billion last year, misclassified revenue, including sales of hardware with sales of software licenses.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/h-p-claim-highlights-a-gray-area-in-software-sales/', 'snippet': 'Hewlett-Packard contends that Autonomy, the British software firm it acquired for $10 billion last year, misclassified revenue, including sales of hardware with sales of software licenses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hewlett-Packard’s accusations of “serious accounting improprieties” at Autonomy are eerily reminiscent of accounting missteps uncovered over a decade ago at software firms like MicroStrategy, Computer Associates and Lernout & Hauspie.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'H.P. Claim Highlights a Gray Area in Software Sales', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'H.P. Claim Highlights a Gray Area in Software Sales', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lesjak, Catherine A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Michael Richard (1965- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitman, Margaret C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Autonomy Corp PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hewlett-Packard Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T01:48:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8fd2bf5-c521-5815-848a-8a94bc2021a7', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8fd2bf5-c521-5815-848a-8a94bc2021a7'}, {'abstract': 'The sex-and-e-mail affair that forced out the C.I.A. director, David H. Petraeus, has now ripened to the image management stage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/us/act-ii-of-a-scandal-cue-the-superlawyers-and-the-spinmasters.html', 'snippet': 'The sex-and-e-mail affair that forced out the C.I.A. director, David H. Petraeus, has now ripened to the image management stage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In every scandal that roils this capital, the opening phase of shocking revelations and wall-to-wall news coverage soon gives way to Phase 2: the spinning. The sex-and-e-mail affair that forced out the C.I.A. director and embroiled the top American commander in Afghanistan has now ripened to the image management stage, and a venerable Washington cottage industry has been fully engaged. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/us/SCANDAL-1/SCANDAL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/21/us/SCANDAL-1/SCANDAL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/us/SCANDAL-1/SCANDAL-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/us/SCANDAL-1/SCANDAL-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1336, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/us/SCANDAL-1/SCANDAL-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/21/us/SCANDAL-1/SCANDAL-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/us/SCANDAL-1/SCANDAL-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Second Act of a Scandal: Cue the Superlawyers and the Spinmasters', 'kicker': 'Washington Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Second Act of a Scandal: Cue the Superlawyers and the Spinmasters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petraeus, David H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Muse, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khawam, Natalie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowell, Abbe D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelley, Jill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Myers, Dee Dee', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broadwell, Paula', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULTERY', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barnett, Robert B', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T01:49:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16562505-1ad0-5b81-a68b-9c9c14135c05', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16562505-1ad0-5b81-a68b-9c9c14135c05'}, {'abstract': 'Despite several faulty provisions, the Obama administration is endorsing a bill to increase access to public lands for hunting and fishing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/opinion/dangerous-sport-in-lawmaking.html', 'snippet': 'Despite several faulty provisions, the Obama administration is endorsing a bill to increase access to public lands for hunting and fishing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to Congress, the term “sportsmen” can mask a multitude of sins. Witness the Sportsmen’s Act of 2012, a bipartisan collection of proposals to increase access to public lands for hunting, fishing and the nation’s “shooting heritage,” as the Obama administration put it in endorsing the measure despite several faulty provisions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dangerous Sport in Lawmaking', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dangerous Sport in Lawmaking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunting and Trapping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wilderness Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polar Bears', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lead', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Sport', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T01:49:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d6f37ff-d491-5d0d-9e94-c20a3d011968', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d6f37ff-d491-5d0d-9e94-c20a3d011968'}, {'abstract': 'In a sound ruling, a federal appellate court struck down the state’s ban on race-conscious affirmative action policies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/opinion/michigans-burdensome-amendment.html', 'snippet': 'In a sound ruling, a federal appellate court struck down the state’s ban on race-conscious affirmative action policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a persuasive ruling last week, a majority of the United States Court of Appeals for the Sixth Circuit struck down Michigan’s ban on race-conscious affirmative action policies. The ban violated the United States Constitution’s equal protection clause by placing an unfair burden on racial minorities seeking to change those policies. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan’s Burdensome Amendment', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Michigan’s Burdensome Amendment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AFFIRMATIVE ACTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T01:59:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ed53305-5f02-5bd1-a617-d422189af488', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ed53305-5f02-5bd1-a617-d422189af488'}, {'abstract': 'If you didn’t take the sweet potato for granted, you’d be giving thanks for it.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/all-hail-the-sweet-potato/', 'snippet': 'If you didn’t take the sweet potato for granted, you’d be giving thanks for it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For more than 30 consecutive Thanksgivings — including this one — I’ve written about turkey in all of its guises. Occasionally I’ve protested, pleading with editors that although the bird in its wild form may be traditional and is indisputably indigenous, whether the one you buy is free-range, wild, natural, organic, pumped up with antibiotics or even injected with “butter,” it’s just about the worst piece of meat you can roast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'All Hail the Sweet Potato', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sweet Potatoes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Turkeys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T02:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e08abd1e-dc07-5e13-8c66-6af2ffb4ac96', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e08abd1e-dc07-5e13-8c66-6af2ffb4ac96'}, {'abstract': 'From Senator Richard G. Lugar’s foreign policy expertise to Senator Kent Conrad’s bichon frisé, the expiring Congress has left its mark in ways large, small and weird.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/us/politics/members-of-the-112th-congress-depart-quirks-in-tow.html', 'snippet': 'From Senator Richard G. Lugar’s foreign policy expertise to Senator Kent Conrad’s bichon frisé, the expiring Congress has left its mark in ways large, small and weird.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Oh, how much will be missed on Capitol Hill next year, when more than 80 current members depart, half of them involuntarily. Say goodbye to the foreign policy expertise of Senator Richard G. Lugar of Indiana, to the institutional knowledge of many in the California delegation and, perhaps most sadly of all, to Senator Kent Conrad’s bichon frisé.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/us/CONGRESS-2/CONGRESS-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/us/CONGRESS-2/CONGRESS-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1447, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/us/CONGRESS-2/CONGRESS-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/21/us/CONGRESS-2/CONGRESS-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/us/CONGRESS-2/CONGRESS-2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Members of the 112th Congress Depart, Taking Their Quirks Along', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Me