': 'The artist draws things he saw in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/20/things-i-saw-no-43/', 'snippet': 'The artist draws things he saw in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Suggestions for what you’d like Jason to see and draw may be sent to thingsisaw@nytimes.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Things I Saw — No. 43', 'kicker': 'Things I Saw', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T02:02:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Polan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0683fff-f11d-507a-97b5-d7ee6596df64', 'word_count': 21, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0683fff-f11d-507a-97b5-d7ee6596df64'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey received the ridicule of fellow Republicans because he stood up for his state and praised President Obama after Hurricane Sandy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/opinion/duty-before-party-for-gov-chris-christie.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey received the ridicule of fellow Republicans because he stood up for his state and praised President Obama after Hurricane Sandy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New Jersey coastline was a shambles, hundreds of thousands of houses in the state were dark and cold, and entire towns were largely homeless. The state needed federal help, and Gov. Chris Christie did what he had to do to get it, including praising President Obama for delivering aid and comfort. For that, he was pilloried by a Republican Party that places blind loyalty above emergency.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Duty Before Party', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Duty Before Party', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T02:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f7104b4-2910-541d-aedc-3144a705d524', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f7104b4-2910-541d-aedc-3144a705d524'}, {'abstract': 'Turkey has found itself largely shut out of the central and defining Arab-Israeli conflict in Gaza.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/world/europe/turkey-with-anti-israel-stance-sidelined-as-mideast-broker.html', 'snippet': 'Turkey has found itself largely shut out of the central and defining Arab-Israeli conflict in Gaza.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — After prayers on Friday, Prime Minister Recep Tayyip Erdogan stepped outside a mosque on the banks of the Bosporus here and dismissed a suggestion that Turkey should talk directly with a onetime ally, Israel, to attempt to resolve the crisis unfolding in Gaza.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkey Finds It Is Sidelined as Broker in Mideast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': Non