basketball/knicks-defeat-hornets-to-move-to-8-1.html', 'snippet': 'Carmelo Anthony scored 29 points in 28 minutes, including 19 points in the first quarter, as the Knicks cruised to a victory over the Hornets on Tuesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — This was the world Carmelo Anthony envisioned when he joined the Knicks two seasons ago, where defenders have the best view in the arena to watch him light up the scoreboard.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 937, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1874, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fast Start for Anthony and 8-1 Start for Knicks', 'kicker': 'Knicks 102, Hornets 80', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fast Start For Anthony And 8-1 Start For Knicks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Orleans Hornets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T04:53:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/937de0f0-f025-5da6-81a1-4d1ebd464af6', 'word_count': 852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/937de0f0-f025-5da6-81a1-4d1ebd464af6'}, {'abstract': 'The 45-year-old suspect, described by the authorities as a xenophobic nationalist, was accused of plotting to detonate a homemade four-ton car bomb.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/world/europe/poland-scientist-is-held-in-plot-to-blow-up-parliament-building.html', 'snippet': 'The 45-year-old suspect, described by the authorities as a xenophobic nationalist, was accused of plotting to detonate a homemade four-ton car bomb.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A scientist at Krakow’s Agricultural University has been arrested on charges that he planned to bomb the Parliament building in Warsaw, prosecutors said Tuesday. The 45-year-old suspect, described by the authorities as a xenophobic nationalist, was accused of plotting to detonate a homemade four-ton car bomb. According to Prime Minister Donald Tusk, the suspect apparently drew inspiration from the Norwegian Anders Behring Breivik, who killed 77 people last year in a shooting spree and bombing. He added that the suspect, who was arrested in Krakow on Nov. 9 but has not been publicly identified, had access to campus laboratories, built and tested homemade bombs, and had explosives, remote-control detonators and guns. He also had “carried out reconnaissance in the neighborhood of the Sejm,” the Parliament, a prosecutor said. Mr. Tusk called on the people of Poland to relinquish the highly partisan and “aggressive language, language of hatred” that has characterized much of the public discourse in Poland for the past several years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poland: Scientist Is Held in Plot to Blow Up Parliament Building', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Poland: Scientist Is Held in Plot To Blow Up Parliament Building', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Krakow (Poland)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T04:53:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kulish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3c2872e-87f8-5045-8b7c-46e2f39b34e6', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3c2872e-87f8-5045-8b7c-46e2f39b34e6'}, {'abstract': 'The brain hormone oxytocin facilitates the ability to read other people’s emotions and deepens bonds between group members. It is also almost certainly an essential, if unacknowledged, player in most sports competitions.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/the-love-hormone-as-sports-enhancer/', 'snippet': 'The brain hormone oxytocin facilitates the ability to read other people’s emotions and deepens bonds between group members. It is also almost certainly an essential, if unacknowledged, player in most sports competitions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is playing football like falling in love? That question, which would perhaps not occur to most of us watching hours of the bruising game this holiday season, is the focus of a provocative and growing body of new science examining the role of oxytocin in competitive sports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': 