protests, which rippled across the country, were led by Hugo Moyano, the leader of a powerful labor federation and a onetime government ally. He is also the father of Pablo Moyano, the leader of the drivers’ union. The protesters demanded a reduction in federal taxes for workers to compensate for an inflation rate private economists estimate to be 25 percent. With its main arteries blockaded by demonstrators, Buenos Aires had the air of a holiday, with parts of the public transit system shut down, above, businesses closed and normally bustling avenues all but empty. Mrs. Kirchner was re-elected last year, but her support has plummeted as the economy has slowed. Appearing on television on Tuesday night, she called the strike “extortion.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/21/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Argentina: General Strike Is Challenge to President', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Argentina: General Strike Is Challenge to President', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Buenos Aires (Argentina)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T05:03:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Schmall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c3acb52-b431-5fd7-a3a6-9534471c2696', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c3acb52-b431-5fd7-a3a6-9534471c2696'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (13) MY LIFE AS A TURKEY Joe Hutto can “talk turkey,” a result of having spent more than a year as a full-time parent to a clutch of wild hatchlings. In this Emmy Award-winning film, “Nature” listens as Mr. Hutto, a wildlife artist and environmentalist, recounts his efforts to bond with turkey poults the way their mother would, as viewers watch Jeff Palmer, above, a photographer and actor, recreate the experience by bonding with a brood of his own. The next thing Mr. Hutto knew, he was rearing 16 chicks, becoming especially fond of Sweet Pea, a snuggler, and Turkey Boy, the bold rascal of the bunch. He wrote about the experience in his book “Illumination in the Flatwoods.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'conte