)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T06:45:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b0dbc16-8777-5d99-93b0-0eaa3db59793', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b0dbc16-8777-5d99-93b0-0eaa3db59793'}, {'abstract': 'The attack, deep in the main diplomatic neighborhood of Kabul, killed three security guards and wounded two civilians, according to police officials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/world/asia/afghan-suicide-bomber-kills-3-near-us-embassy.html', 'snippet': 'The attack, deep in the main diplomatic neighborhood of Kabul, killed three security guards and wounded two civilians, according to police officials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — The Afghan government executed six Taliban prisoners on Wednesday, just days after welcoming Pakistan’s release of other Taliban prisoners, illustrating the tightrope that President Hamid Karzai is trying to walk: reaching out to the Taliban politically while demonstrating his opposition to their terrorist acts. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghanistan Executes Six in Gesture on Taliban', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghanistan Executes Six In Gesture On Taliban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'v