alf-century career takes up a massive two-volume book, and an exhibition. Elaisha Stokes, a freelance videographer for The New York Times, shadowed Mr. Conrad taking Mr. Meyerowitz’s portrait in his studio on the Upper West Side to accompany\xa0an article by Randy Kennedy. Lens also recently published a post\xa0by Mr. Meyerowitz on his approach to color and black-and-white photography.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Assignment: Photographing the Photographer', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meyerowitz, Joel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T10:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a17af423-87df-55b4-ab2b-7d29dae3ce16', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a17af423-87df-55b4-ab2b-7d29dae3ce16'}, {'abstract': 'The archbishop of Canterbury, the Most Rev. Rowan Williams, said the church had lost credibility with the vote, and Prime Minister David Cameron urged it to find a way to resolve church-state relations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/world/europe/church-of-england-rejects-appointing-female-bishops.html', 'snippet': 'The archbishop of Canterbury, the Most Rev. Rowan Williams, said the church had lost credibility with the vote, and Prime Minister David Cameron urged it to find a way to resolve church-state relations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — In a sign of deepening crisis in the Church of England after it rejected the appointment of women as bishops, its spiritual leader said Wednesday that the church had “undoubtedly lost a measure of credibility” and had a “lot of explaining to do” to 