se peaked in Week 5 against Cleveland and has been in a\xa0relatively consistent decline\xa0since. The Giants’ worst outing was their most recent one, against Cincinnati. This has spurred theories of a tired arm for quarterback Eli Manning because of an accumulation of instances with a high number of pass attempts, like 51 against Tampa Bay, 42 against Philadelphia, 40 against Washington and 46 against the Bengals. But this is the worst kind of post-hoc analysis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week 12 N.F.L. Game Probabilities, and a Tired Theory', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T11:03:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7f48eb5-e9c4-5053-98f7-a1b2fd4e645c', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7f48eb5-e9c4-5053-98f7-a1b2fd4e645c'}, {'abstract': 'The execution of the lone surviving gunman from the 2008 terror attacks in Mumbai was welcomed by survivors.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/what-they-said-families-of-2611-victims-react-to-kasabs-execution/', 'snippet': 'The execution of the lone surviving gunman from the 2008 terror attacks in Mumbai was welcomed by survivors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The relatives of those killed in the November 2008 terror attacks expressed relief over the execution of Ajmal Kasab, the lone surviving gunman, who was hanged by the Indian authorities Wednesday morning in Yerwada jail. Justice has finally been delivered, many said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What They Said: Families of Mumbai Terror Victims React to Gunman’s Execution', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kasab, Mohammed Ajmal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T11:05:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77166119-6891-53ed-803f-fff6874d2463', 'word_count': 73, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77166119-6891-53ed-803f-fff6874d2463'}, {'abstract': 'Muddy Waters Research says Olam International, an agricultural commodities company partly owned by the Singaporean sovereign wealth fund Temasek Holdings, is “at risk of collapsing.” Olam has responded with a lawsuit.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/muddy-waters-turns-its-focus-on-singapore/', 'snippet': 'Muddy Waters Research says Olam International, an agricultural commodities company partly owned by the Singaporean sovereign wealth fund Temasek Holdings, is “at risk of collapsing.” Olam has responded with a lawsuit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Carson C. Block made a name for himself and his company, Muddy Waters Research, by betting big against the shares of Chinese companies that were listed in North America. Now he is setting his sights on Singapore.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Singapore Company Sues a Vocal Critic', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Singapore Company Sues a Vocal Critic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Short Selling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muddy Waters Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Singapore', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T11:23:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Gough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/911cde8a-7659-5fc6-8b4b-e2ef25f8dbb2', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/911cde8a-7659-5fc6-8b4b-e2ef25f8dbb2'}, {'abstract': 'For the writer, trips to the Lower East Side for special family foods are a decades-long tradition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/booming/lox-and-cream-cheese-for-thanksgiving.html', 'snippet': 'For the writer, trips to the Lower East Side for special family foods are a decades-long tradition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the summer, in the Catskills resort community where I grew up during the ’50s, getting great Jewish food was not a problem. The hotels on our side of the mountains in Fleischmanns, N.Y., were dying, but there were still enough city people that it was not hard to find smoked fish and salamis and decent rye bread.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/booming/21wadler-booming-thanksgiving2/21wadler-booming-thanksgiving2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subTyp