es.com/2012/11/21/a-murder-ballad-playlist/', 'snippet': 'Juliana Nash offers a selection of some of the murder ballads and songs that she loves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I learned to play guitar at summer camp by singing traditional folk songs around a campfire. Something about the haunting, story-driven nature of those songs engaged me in a deep way, at an early age. But it wasn’t until long past my formal musical training and a career as songwriter, rhythm guitarist and lead singer for the band Talking to Animals that I was introduced to the genre of the murder ballad. Julia Jordan, a playwright and friend, approached me to collaborate on a new musical inspired by this old, musical form. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A ‘Murder Ballad’ Playlist', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Insider’s Choice Of Killer Songs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T15:43:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliana Nash', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nash', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe51ee02-79ef-501c-82af-ac6b32089a77', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe51ee02-79ef-501c-82af-ac6b32089a77'}, {'abstract': 'A retired physics professor in Tamil Nadu, on the front lines of a growing battle.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/fighting-for-free-speech-online-in-india/', 'snippet': 'A retired physics professor in Tamil Nadu, on the front lines of a growing battle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marx Anthonisamy is a 63-year-old retired physics professor, \xa0a Tamil literature critic and author who lives in Chennai, where he pens books on politics, Hindutva, Buddhism and Islam.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting for Free Speech Online in India', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tamils (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chidambaram, P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'India Against Corruption', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T15:56:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sangeetha Rajeesh and Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sangeetha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rajeesh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d54ceb9-abdb-537c-9323-c6c90cf8103b', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d54ceb9-abdb-537c-9323-c6c90cf8103b'}, {'abstract': 'The death of the security official, Faraj Mohammed al-Drissi, is the latest in a series of mysterious killings that have raised fears about Libya’s precarious postwar security.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/world/africa/benghazi-security-director-is-assassinated-libyan-officials-say.html', 'snippet': 'The death of the security official, Faraj Mohammed al-Drissi, is the latest in a series of mysterious killings that have raised fears about Libya’s precarious postwar security.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — A senior Libyan security official was assassinated outside his home in the eastern city of Benghazi, officials said Wednesday, the same city where the United States ambassador and three other Americans were killed at their diplomatic compound in September. The Libyan official’s death was the latest in a series of mysterious killings that have raised fears about the country’s precarious postwar security. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Security Chief in Benghazi Assassinated, Libyan Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Security Chief In Benghazi Assassinated, Libyan Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Benghazi (Libya)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T15:56:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c8d6667-8caf-5fc5-b491-8fc34f33c487', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c8d6667-8caf-5fc5-b491-8fc34f33c487'}, {'abstract': 'Consumers still can’t find Garth Brooks or Tool on iTunes. And Def Leppard is only offering “forgeries” of its own work. Who should be Apple’s next priority in bringing to the iTunes store? What act have you searched for in vain at iTunes?', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/now-that-acdcs-there-whos-still-missing-from-itunes/', 'snippet': 'Consumers still can’t find Garth Brooks or Tool on iTunes. And Def Leppard is only offering “forgeries” of its own work. Who should be Apple’s next priority in bringing to the iTunes store? What act have you searched for in vain at iTunes?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apple’s iTunes has added the AC/DC catalog and closed one of the few significant gaps in its music store. But gaps remain at the service, which will turn 10 years old in a few months and has sold more than 20 billion songs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now That AC/DC’s There, Who’s Still Missing From iTunes?', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T15:59:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91b62e10-f7ff-5c29-81f1-044dfa7e1e0a', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91b62e10-f7ff-5c29-81f1-044dfa7e1e0a'}, {'abstract': 'Are see-through clothes ever really wearable? This season, they are.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/sheer-luck/', 'snippet': 'Are see-through clothes ever really wearable? This season, they are.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What can seem daunting about sheer is that, well, it’s sheer. While these peekaboo fabrics look all airy and ethereal parading down a runway on a reed-thin 17-year old-model, knowing how to wear any of them in real life isn’t exactly obvious. Thankfully, this season, designers have hit on ways that a woman can incorporate transparency into her style, and not one of them requires a bee-sting bust or an exhibitionist swagger.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '68', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sheer Luck', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sheer Luck', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costa, Francisco', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCartney, Stella', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Philo, Phoebe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Celine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T16:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By SARAH HARRIS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'HARRIS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e74846b2-c096-5233-8fe4-52749638ac63', 'word_count': 691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e74846b2-c096-5233-8fe4-52749638ac63'}, {'abstract': 'Not where you think.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/stifling-destructive-bureaucracy/', 'snippet': 'Not where you think.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a story about anti-Obamacare deadenders, Talking Points Memo runs this picture:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stifling, Destructive Bureaucracy', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T16:01:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3048357f-0e06-5518-9edb-2d0d888fe8e0', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3048357f-0e06-5518-9edb-2d0d888fe8e0'}, {'abstract': 'Martial arts warriors from Orissa perform in the state capital of Bhubaneshwar.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/image-of-the-day-nov-21/', 'snippet': 'Martial arts warriors from Orissa perform in the state capital of Bhubaneshwar.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: Nov. 21', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Martial Arts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T16:06:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14bf8ff3-2c76-5859-8d9e-1856701a35fc', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14bf8ff3-2c76-5859-8d9e-1856701a35fc'}, {'abstract': 'Salvatore Perrone, of Staten Island, was charged in three killings, and the police commissioner said Mr. Perrone had been seeking more victims.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/nyregion/gun-found-in-apartment-tied-to-man-linked-to-merchant-killings.html', 'snippet': 'Salvatore Perrone, of Staten Island, was charged in three killings, and the police commissioner said Mr. Perrone had been seeking more victims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The search for a suspect in the recent deaths of three Brooklyn shopkeepers ended on Wednesday with the arrest of a clothing dealer whom Police Commissioner Raymond W. Kelly described as a “serial killer” intent on finding more victims.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/nyregion/SERIAL1-sub/SERIAL1-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/22/nyregion/SERIAL1-sub/SERIAL1-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/nyregion/SERIAL1-sub/SERIAL1-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/nyregion/SERIAL1-sub/SERIAL1-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1316, 'width': 1974, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/nyregion/SERIAL1-sub/SERIAL1-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/22/nyregion/SERIAL1-sub/SERIAL1-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image