', 'snippet': 'The second biopic about the famed director had its premiere Sunday night at the Ziegfeld Theater in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVEN in death, Alfred Hitchcock has accomplished something that few Hollywood icons can claim: to have not one, but two somewhat unflattering biographical films made about him in the same year. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/fashion/22SCENE_SPAN/22SCENE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/22/fashion/22SCENE_SPAN/22SCENE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/fashion/22SCENE_SPAN/22SCENE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/fashion/22SCENE_SPAN/22SCENE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/fashion/22SCENE_SPAN/22SCENE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/22/fashion/22SCENE_SPAN/22SCENE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/fashion/22SCENE_SPAN/22SCENE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hitchcock ‘Psycho’ Drama', 'kicker': 'Scene City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Hitchcock ‘Psycho’ Drama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johansson, Scarlett', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ziegfeld Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biel, Jessica', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hopkins, Anthony', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T17:32:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacob Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56f3da1e-7313-5d39-a912-a7af24270b8f', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56f3da1e-7313-5d39-a912-a7af24270b8f'}, {'abstract': 'The rules on real estate mortgage investment conduits are designed to prevent operating companies from avoiding corporate tax. Banks and other financial institutions that originate mortgages should pay that tax. Passive conduits should not.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/why-a-tax-crackdown-is-not-needed-on-mortgage-backed-securities/', 'snippet': 'The rules on real estate mortgage investment conduits are designed to prevent operating companies from avoiding corporate tax. Banks and other financial institutions that originate mortgages should pay that tax. Passive conduits should not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Capitol Hill is poking around for tax revenue. One sleeping dog to let lie is the tax treatment of real estate mortgage investment conduits, or Remics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why a Tax Crackdown Is Not Needed on Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T17:33:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Fleischer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fleischer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01b70088-024b-5c21-8720-93e6ad184208', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01b70088-024b-5c21-8720-93e6ad184208'}, {'abstract': 'It is unforgivable that those we trust to take care of us, our doctors and our government — and for some, our church — repeatedly and even fatally fail women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/opinion/an-antiquated-abortion-law-in-ireland.html', 'snippet': 'It is unforgivable that those we trust to take care of us, our doctors and our government — and for some, our church — repeatedly and even fatally fail women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN late October, Savita Halappanavar, a 31-year-old dentist who was 17 weeks pregnant, was admitted to a hospital in Galway, Ireland, in severe pain. Doctors acknowledged that she was having a miscarriage, but over the course of three days, they reportedly refused to terminate the pregnancy and end her suffering because they could detect a fetal heartbeat. Citing Roman Catholic Ireland’s near-total ban on abortion as the reason, the physicians denied Dr. Halappanavar a procedure that most likely would have saved her life. She died Oct. 28.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Antiquated Abortion Law in Ireland', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Antiquated Abortion Law in Ireland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halappanavar, Savita', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University Hospital Galway', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T17:37:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethel Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5681218b-06e1-5441-b1c9-6b3c76a7686a', 'word_count': 746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5681218b-06e1-5441-b1c9-6b3c76a7686a'}, {'abstract': 'The Lede is following events in the Middle East, where Egypt’s foreign minister announced that a cease-fire in the Gaza conflict is scheduled to begin on Wednesday night at 9 p.m. local time.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/latest-updates-on-the-gaza-conflict-3/', 'snippet': 'The Lede is following events in the Middle East, where Egypt’s foreign minister announced that a cease-fire in the Gaza conflict is scheduled to begin on Wednesday night at 9 p.m. local time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lede is following events in the Middle East, where Egypt’s foreign minister announced that a cease-fire in the Gaza conflict is scheduled to begin on Wednesday night at 9 p.m. local time (2 p.m. Eastern Time).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nov. 21 Updates on the Gaza Conflict', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T17:38:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6857a767-ca95-5727-99d7-f57a0ae71ccd', 'word_count': 3055, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6857a767-ca95-5727-99d7-f57a0ae71ccd'}, {'abstract': 'A performance artist who campaigns against overconsumption preaches about “sharing, not shopping.”', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/a-preacher-of-the-gospel-of-sharing-not-shopping/', 'snippet': 'A performance artist who campaigns against overconsumption preaches about “sharing, not shopping.”', 'lead_paragraph': '2:13 p.m. | Updated below |From the first days of this blog in 2007, a focal point has been the word “enough.” How much is enough? Can we learn to reach for an apple when we crave a cookie? Can we make something instead of buying something? Which good life do you seek — the Vegas version or Plato’s?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A ‘Preacher’ of the Gospel of Sharing, Not Shopping', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T17:41:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae453083-fa3e-5595-bbb7-17f617d1c053', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae453083-fa3e-5595-bbb7-17f617d1c053'}, {'abstract': 'Backup quarterbacks — and in some cases, third-stringers — came to the fore after injuries to a bunch of starters, but the odds are almost always stacked against them.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/quirks-of-the-game-the-third-string-quarterback/', 'snippet': 'Backup quarterbacks — and in some cases, third-stringers — came to the fore after injuries to a bunch of starters, but the odds are almost always stacked against them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'And down they go. A rash of injuries to big-name quarterbacks — Ben Roethlisberger, Jay Cutler, Michael Vick and Alex Smith — thrust a bunch of backups to the fore last week, with very mixed results. But while Byron Leftwich, Jason Campbell, Nick Foles and Colin Kaepernick were all in the spotlight, the shifting situation also meant new roles for football’s least glamorous players, third-string quarterbacks. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/sports/football/21batch/21batch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype'