piration when you do not feel like typing or looking for a notepad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A voice recorder app for your smartphone is one way to quickly capture sudden thoughts on a device you are likely to have with you when inspiration strikes. Some phones have built-in recorders; the Voice Memos app in Apple’s iOS system for the iPhone lets you record, edit and e-mail your dictated thoughts as sound clips. If your phone does not include a voice or sound recorder with the operating system, you can find several third-party programs (like Evernote, which may include more features than a default system app) in your phone’s app store. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Have Your Phone Take a Memo', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recording Equipment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Evernote Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T18:03:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09e5228d-6d0c-5b6e-a43e-85ec269deddb', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09e5228d-6d0c-5b6e-a43e-85ec269deddb'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors file charges against a former portfolio manager at the hedge fund SAC Capital Advisors, directly involving the billionaire Steven A. Cohen, the fund’s founder.', 'web_url': 