news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily S. Rueb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rueb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3679005-5a31-5dbb-af61-fe457925f91d', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3679005-5a31-5dbb-af61-fe457925f91d'}, {'abstract': 'On the 67th day of the N.H.L. lockout, the union offered concessions, but the league said they didn’t go far enough.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/sports/hockey/nhl-players-offer-new-proposal-to-owners.html', 'snippet': 'On the 67th day of the N.H.L. lockout, the union offered concessions, but the league said they didn’t go far enough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.H.L. on Wednesday rejected the latest players union proposal despite significant concessions from the union 67 days into the lockout. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.H.L. Rejects Union Offer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.H.L. Rejects Union Offer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fehr, Donald', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "National Hockey League Players' Assn", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T18:23:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4054277a-505a-51b3-8ee5-2fe325e4951a', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4054277a-505a-51b3-8ee5-2fe325e4951a'}, {'abstract': 'A scheduled program turns into a benefit concert.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/improvising-a-sandy-benefit-at-le-possion-rouge/', 'snippet': 'A scheduled program turns into a benefit concert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The composers Sxip Shirey and Danielle Eva Schwob had just started rehearsals with the Syzygy New Music ensemble for a Nov. 30 collaborative show at Le Poisson Rouge when Hurricane Sandy hit New York. In the storm’s aftermath Mr. Shirey and Ms. Schwob decided that the show should go on, but not quite as originally planned. Instead of a straightforward program of Mr. Shirey’s quirky instrumental and vocal works and Ms. Schwob’s hard-edged pop songs, the composers and Syzygy are presenting Danielle and Sxip’s Hour of Charm: Hurricane Relief – a benefit concert for which they have assembled a starry alt classical cast.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Improvising a Sandy Benefit at Le Poisson Rouge', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Improvising a Benefit At Le Poisson Rouge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reynolds, Todd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rothenberg, Ned', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shirey, Sxip', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Poisson Rouge', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T18:24:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Ko