dia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jackson Letter of Resignation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Jesse L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T20:23:16+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/baba357c-e42f-5250-a298-2c9e0d0c5c77', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/baba357c-e42f-5250-a298-2c9e0d0c5c77'}, {'abstract': 'In annual White House tradition, President Obama pardons the annual Thanksgiving turkey.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/no-fighting-over-these-drumsticks/', 'snippet': 'In annual White House tradition, President Obama pardons the annual Thanksgiving turkey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cobbler, go in peace.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Fighting Over These Drumsticks', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T20:25:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f23e83f1-b00e-5ed7-8e1e-66e2baabb91e', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f23e83f1-b00e-5ed7-8e1e-66e2baabb91e'}, {'abstract': 'While the recent blackouts were sobering, advances in battery technology are more driven by the issue of how the grid will absorb solar and wind power.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/after-the-storm-a-solar-reckoning/', 'snippet': 'While the recent blackouts were sobering, advances in battery technology are more driven by the issue of how the grid will absorb solar and wind power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I reported this week in The Times, many homeowners with solar panels on their roofs found themselves without electricity along with their conventionally powered neighbors when Hurricane Sandy knocked out power along the coasts of New Jersey, Queens, Brooklyn and Long Island. But in Bayonne, N.J., a school with an unusual coupling of a solar array and a backup diesel generator found itself chugging along through the storm and its aftermath, allowing more than 50 residents to spend the night that Sandy hit on cots in a heated, dry and well-lighted community room.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.:  In a Blackout, Solar Exceptions', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T20:25:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diane Cardwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cardwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05c3c264-3896-5fc3-9850-537c4d7c32b6', 'word_count': 1257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05c3c264-3896-5fc3-9850-537c4d7c32b6'}, {'abstract': 'While Thanksgiving gas prices in the United States are higher than a year ago and at a record level, oil experts say plentiful global supplies will help prevent a jump in prices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/business/energy-environment/despite-the-rise-in-mideast-violence-oil-prices-stay-steady.html', 'snippet': 'While Thanksgiving gas prices in the United States are higher than a year ago and at a record level, oil experts say plentiful global supplies will help prevent a jump in prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — American drivers filling their tanks for the Thanksgiving weekend can forget the impact of the Middle East on oil prices for a day or two.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/business/OIL/OIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/business/OIL/OIL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Oil Prices Stay Steady Despite Mideast Conflict', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oil Prices Stay Steady Despite Mideast Conflict', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T20:25:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aebbc1cf-096c-57dd-b2d4-f289d841e9cf', 'word_count': 961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aebbc1cf-096c-57dd-b2d4-f289d841e9cf'}, {'abstract': 'A response to Paul Krugman on economic security and social disintegration.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/can-we-be-sweden/', 'snippet': 'A response to Paul Krugman on economic security and social disintegration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My colleague Paul Krugman has written an interesting response to my Sunday column, which pushed back against “winning the future” triumphalism on the left by noting the emergent Democratic majority’s roots in what I described as “social disintegration” and “economic fear.” Krugman agrees with the second half of that description, but argues that the economic factors vastly oughtweigh the social ones:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can We Be Sweden?', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T20:27:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76f73fab-9284-5c7f-8d3d-cbaf600b53af', 'word_count': 1247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76f73fab-9284-5c7f-8d3d-cbaf600b53af'}, {'abstract': 'The Times’ Ed Ou reports on Palestinian refugees who have sought safety in shelters organized by the United Nations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/middleeast/100000001916850/a-refuge-amid-the-strikes.html', 'snippet': 'The Times’ Ed Ou reports on Palestinian refugees who have sought safety in shelters organized by the United Nations.', 'l