e couch, are becoming a worthy alternative to jeans and chinos in the limited industry of men’s bottoms. Designers like Sacai, J.Crew and Kolor showed them in their spring 2013 presentations. They’re the foundation of Alexander Wang’s lifestyle line T –– a pair running for about $250 mixes easily on racks alongside the label’s luxurious knits and leather jackets. The Club Monaco pair on Hedi Slimane’s muse du jour Gryphon O’Shea ($90; clubmonaco.com), seen here, are as suitable with an Outlier anorak as they are with a deconstructed blazer. Click through our interactive slideshow for more tips on how to wear the season’s sweats with style. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Wear | The Statement Sweat Pant', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Loose Fit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-21T21:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Rider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d7ee301-c60f-59e5-bd49-fa84288a409c', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d7ee301-c60f-59e5-bd49-fa84288a409c'}, {'abstract': 'Salvatore Sciarrino’s soundscape “Cerchio Tagliato dei Suoni” (“Cutting the Circle of Sounds”), a piece for 104 flutists, had its United States premiere at the Guggenheim.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/arts/music/cerchio-tagliato-dei-suoni-at-the-guggenheim-museum.html', 'snippet': 'Salvatore Sciarrino’s soundscape “Cerchio Tagliato dei Suoni” (“Cutting the Circle of Sounds”), a piece for 104 flutists, had its United States premiere at the Guggenheim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Salvatore Sciarrino, a self-taught Italian composer who ranks among the world’s foremost avant-gardists, has an affinity for the flute: a point proved by “Fabbrica degli incantesimi,” an entrancing 2011 CD of his unaccompanied flute music as performed by Roberto Fabbriciani. Employing an instrument known for its pure tone and associated with tuneful merriment, Mr. Sciarrino fashions mysterious, evocative and atmospheric soliloquies enhanced by unorthodox playing techniques.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22FLUTES/22FLUTES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22FLUTES/22FLUTES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22FLUTES/22FLUTES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22FLUTES/22FLUTES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1387, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22FLUTES/22FLUTES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22FLUTES/22FLUTES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22FLUTES/22FLUTES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': 