usic and books, than for creating content. So while they are useful for e-mail, it can be a challenge to use one as a machine for work — although it can be done.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/technology/29gw-tablets/29gw-tablets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/technology/29gw-tablets/29gw-tablets-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/technology/29gw-tablets/29gw-tablets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/technology/29gw-tablets/29gw-tablets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/technology/29gw-tablets/29gw-tablets-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Choose a Tablet, First Choose an Operating System', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T01:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdde5581-2312-5fbe-b444-0afc5aa7aa38', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdde5581-2312-5fbe-b444-0afc5aa7aa38'}, {'abstract': 'New documents show that the Food and Drug Administration  threatened to use its full authority on the Massachusetts company implicated in the outbreak only to back away, citing lack of jurisdiction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/health/documents-show-fdas-failures-in-meningitis-outbreak.html', 'snippet': 'New documents show that the Food and Drug Administration  threatened to use its full authority on the Massachusetts company implicated in the outbreak only to back away, citing lack of jurisdiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Newly released documents add vivid detail to the emerging portrait of the Food and Drug Administration’s ineffective and halting efforts to regulate a Massachusetts company implicated in a national meningitis outbreak that has sickened nearly 500 people and killed 34. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oversight Failures Documented in Meningitis Outbreak', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oversight Failures Documented in Meningitis Outbreak', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Compounding Center', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meningitis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steroids', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cadden, Barry J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T01:05:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack and Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2e7e393-1e0a-5e71-b8ec-2dc9818afc96', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2e7e393-1e0a-5e71-b8ec-2dc9818afc96'}, {'abstract': 'Residents of Maloula, an oasis of tolerance, have vowed not to succumb to sectarianism and be dragged into the chaos in other parts of the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/world/middleeast/maloula-is-a-diverse-haven-from-syrias-horrors.html', 'snippet': 'Residents of Maloula, an oasis of tolerance, have vowed not to succumb to sectarianism and be dragged into the chaos in other parts of the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MAALOULA, Syria — In a country clouded by conflict, where neighbors and families are now divided by sectarian hatred, this mountaintop town renowned for its spiritual healing qualities and restorative air is an oasis of tolerance. Residents of the ancient and mainly Christian town — one of the last places where Western Aramaic, the language of Jesus Christ, is still spoken — vowed at the beginning of the Syrian conflict 20 months ago not to succumb to sectarianism and be dragged into the chaos.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/world/maloula/maloula-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 693, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/world/maloula/maloula-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1387, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/world/maloula/maloula-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/22/world/maloula/maloula-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/world/maloula/maloula-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mountaintop Town Is a Diverse Haven From Syria’s Horrors', 'kicker': 'Maaloula Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mountaintop Town Is a Diverse Haven From Syria’s Horrors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunni Muslims', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T01:19:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janine di Giovanni', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cfbb080-497e-57e9-855c-ebb9ea781542', 'word_count': 1157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cfbb080-497e-57e9-855c-ebb9ea781542'}, {'abstract': 'In his early years at The Times, Mr. Blair reported on both local and national news. He also worked in the United Nations bureau before becoming a foreign correspondent in 1956.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/business/william-g-blair-new-york-times-reporter-dies-at-87.html', 'snippet': 'In his early years at The Times, Mr. Blair reported on both local and national news. He also worked in the United Nations bureau before becoming a foreign correspondent in 1956.', 'lead_paragraph': 'William G. Blair, a former reporter and foreign bureau chief for The New York Times and public relations director for its parent company, died on Monday in Manhattan. He was 87.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/business/BLAIR/BLAIR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/business/BLAIR/BLAIR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1878, 'width': 1300, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/business/BLAIR/BLAIR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/22/business/BLAIR/BLAIR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/business/BLAIR/BLAIR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'mai