 '_id': 'nyt://article/43194ea7-efdd-5ac7-a366-c137ce161d62', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43194ea7-efdd-5ac7-a366-c137ce161d62'}, {'abstract': 'A bizarre legal tale took a turn when the first assistant United States attorney was exposed for participating under an alias in the rancorous comments section of a local news Web site.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/us/in-new-orleans-comments-by-assistants-imperil-job-of-federal-prosecutor.html', 'snippet': 'A bizarre legal tale took a turn when the first assistant United States attorney was exposed for participating under an alias in the rancorous comments section of a local news Web site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — It is not at all unusual for the goings-on at the United States attorney’s office to be a prime subject of conversation here, where corruption has a long and well-chronicled history. What is unusual is that the office itself, and not one of the politicians it is prosecuting, is the focus of all the talk. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/us/NEWORLEANS/NEWORLEANS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/us/NEWORLEANS/NEWORLEANS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1293, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In New Orleans, Comments by Assistants Imperil Job of Federal Prosecutor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Comments by Assistants Imperil Job of Prosecutor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 2, 'majo