 Shiites as they observed a major religious holiday killed at least 26 people and wounded dozens on Wednesday, heightening fears of further bloodshed in the coming days.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/world/pakistan/pakistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 419, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/22/world/pakistan/pakistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 419}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/world/pakistan/pakistan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/world/pakistan/pakistan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1425, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/world/pakistan/pakistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/22/world/pakistan/pakistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/world/pakistan/pakistan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Day of Suicide Attacks Heightens Fears in Pakistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: Bombers Attack Shiites', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rawalpindi (Pakistan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Karachi (Pakistan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lashkar-e-Jhangvi', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T04:08:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Declan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4a96ec3-a129-55c7-9889-62c4809b4a0c', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4a96ec3-a129-55c7-9889-62c4809b4a0c'}, {'abstract': 'The 1984 cult film “Red Dawn” had Soviet troops invading the United States. A remake of the movie replaced the Soviets with Chinese invaders, but with China now the world’s second-largest film market, the producers have digitally transformed the bad guys into North Koreans.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/21/remake-of-red-dawn-changes-its-political-hue/', 'snippet': 'The 1984 cult film “Red Dawn” had Soviet troops invading the United States. A remake of the movie replaced the Soviets with Chinese invaders, but with China now the world’s second-largest film market, the producers have digitally transformed the b...', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — There are essentially two versions of North Korea available to cartoonists, filmmakers, political analysts and Jon Stewart. The first is the Acme-rocket, Wile E. Coyote kind of place where the leisure-suited, bouffant-haired dictator receives daily injections of the blood of young virgins and makes a dozen holes-in-one during his first-ever round of golf. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remake of ‘Red Dawn’ Changes Its Political Hue', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Milius, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Red Dawn (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Cheat (Movie)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T04:28:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/802132f0-1869-5dd5-935a-1e2d4fc3668b', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/802132f0-1869-5dd5-935a-1e2d4fc3668b'}, {'abstract': 'Carmelo Anthony missed a potential game-winning shot after the Knicks, who lost their second game of the season, had rallied from a double-digit deficit in the fourth quarter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/sports/basketball/carmelo-anthony-misses-shot-as-mavericks-beat-knicks.html', 'snippet': 'Carmelo Anthony missed a potential game-winning shot after the Knicks, who lost their second game of the season, had rallied from a double-digit deficit in the fourth quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS — The ball came to Carmelo Anthony in the game’s final moments. Coach Mike Woodson drew up the play for Anthony, his best player. When Anthony dribbled to his left, he was open for a moment. Anthony rose for a game-winning baseline jumper — the shot he and Woodson wanted — to beat the Dallas Mavericks. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/sports/knicks-1/knicks-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 721, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/sports/knicks-1/knicks-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1442, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/sports/knicks-1/knicks-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/22/sports/knicks-1/knicks-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/sports/knicks-1/knicks-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crucial Shot and Late Rally Fall Short for Knicks in Dallas', 'kicker': 'Mavericks 114, Knicks 111', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crucial Shot and Late Rally Fall Short for Knicks in Dallas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T04:46:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36d15817-c51d-5e63-b9b1-5d18c88c48b6', 'word_count': 1019, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36d15817-c51d-5e63-b9b1-5d18c88c48b6'}, {'abstract': 'With defensive principles stressed by Coach Mike Woodson in training camp, the Knicks have become one of the toughest teams to score against in the N.B.A.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/sports/basketball/knicks-focus-on-defense-is-accounting-for-their-success.html', 'snippet': 'With defensive principles stressed by Coach Mike Woodson in training camp, the Knicks have become one of the toughest teams to score against in the N.B.A.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS — The first sign that told Tyson Chandler the Knicks could be a dominant team on defense was in training camp. Chandler had asked Coach Mike Woodson after last season to think about what he wanted the team’s principles to be on defense.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/sports/knicks/knicks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 906, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/sports/knicks/knicks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1811, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Knicks’ Focus on Defense Is Accounting for Their Success', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knicks&#8217; Focus on Defense Is Accounting for Their Success', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodson, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chandler, Tyson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T04:54:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a679ab11-3ea0-554d-b9bc-67f1446657fc', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a679ab11-3ea0-554d-b9bc-67f1446657fc'}, {'abstract': 'The government responded Wednesday to criticism that the Persian Gulf monarchy is intensifying its repression of dissidents, and abandoning reforms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/world/middleeast/bahrain-government-defends-changes.html', 'snippet': 'The government responded Wednesday to criticism that the Persian Gulf monarchy is intensifying its repression of dissidents, and abandoning reforms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The government responded Wednesday to criticism by Amnesty International and others who have charged that the Persian Gulf monarchy is intensifying its repression of dissidents, and abandoning reforms it promised after cracking down on a popular uprising last year. The government cited progress on several fronts, saying it had worked toward overhauling its security services and had reinstated workers who were fired for political reasons. Amnesty and other groups have cited recent moves by the government, including banning protests and stripping 31 dissidents of their citizenship, as evidence of an intensifying crackdown. The government drew fresh criticism on Wednesday, when a court sentenced 23 medical workers to three months in prison on the charge of “illegal gathering,” according to Physicians for Human Rights. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bahrain Government Defends Changes', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bahrain: Responding to Criticism, Government Defends Changes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Persian Gulf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahrain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T05:04:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/689d5ad1-d33d-5dc3-af95-bb955d3a7122', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/689d5ad1-d33d-5dc3-af95-bb955d3a7122'}, {'abstract': 'The top security official for São Paulo State resigned as authorities grappled with a spree of execution-style killings of police officers and a broader surge in homicides.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/world/americas/brazil-security-official-resigns-after-deaths-of-police-officers.html', 'snippet': 'The top security official for São Paulo State resigned as authorities grappled with a spree of execution-style killings of police officers and a broader surge in homicides.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The top security official for São Paulo State resigned as authorities grappled with a spree of execution-style killings of police officers and a broader surge in homicides. The resignation of Antonio Ferreira Pinto, announced Wednesday by Gov. Geraldo Alckmin, came amid criticism of Mr. Ferreira Pinto’s handling of security policies. So far this year, more than 90 police officers have been killed in São Paulo. That is a sharp rise from 2011, pointing to a resurgence of a powerful organized crime organization, the First Capital Command, or P.C.C., as the group is known by its Portuguese initials. Mr. Ferreira Pinto had played down the influence of the group, which operates largely from within São Paulo’s prison system. A prominent judicial official, Fernando Grella, was named to replace Mr. Ferreira Pinto. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil: Security Official Resigns After Deaths of Police Officers', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brazil: Security Official Resigns After Deaths of Police Officers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T05:05:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8cd3c95-a1f8-506e-a3f1-a634d08e3451', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8cd3c95-a1f8-506e-a3f1-a634d08e3451'}, {'abstract': 'The United States Embassy in Paris denied Wednesday that the United States carried out a cyberattack to read files on computers in the Élysée Palace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/world/europe/france-us-denies-spying-report.html', 'snippet': 'The United States Embassy in Paris denied Wednesday that the United States carried out a cyberattack to read files on computers in the Élysée Palace.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United States Embassy in Paris denied Wednesday that the United States carried out a cyberattack to read files on computers in the Élysée Palace during the administration of President Nicolas Sarkozy, as reported in Wednesday’s edition of L’Express, a French weekly. The magazine quoted an unnamed source as saying that a computer worm had been introduced into Élysée computers in May and suggesting that the worm was similar to Flame, a virus aimed at Iran and presumed to be the work of the United States and Israel. In a statement, the embassy said that the story was untrue and that the charge against Washington was based on “a bundle of assumptions.” One American official said that it was as if, after a car accident, anyone who had a car would be blamed. The embassy statement said, “We categorically refute the allegations” that the United States “participated in a cyberattack against the French government.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: U.S. Denies Spying Report', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: U.S. Denies Spying Report', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T05:07:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/925ab2a4-e209-563e-9164-05c8e42dba2a', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/925ab2a4-e209-563e-9164-05c8e42dba2a'}, {'abstract': 'Once respected and revered, Indian teachers are now criticized for their fashion sense.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/in-bangalore-a-what-not-to-wear-for-teachers/', 'snippet': 'Once respected and revered, Indian teachers are now criticized for their fashion sense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGALORE—When a Bangalore school, part of India’s largest school chain called Delhi Public School, or D.P.S., recently surveyed 300 teenage students in an anonymous review called “Loving Your Teacher,” the authorities were staggered by the barrage of criticism about teachers’ appearances.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Bangalore, a ‘What Not to Wear’ for Teachers', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangalore (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T05:54:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Saritha Rai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Saritha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f64491b7-2398-5544-a3e9-800b664de1d9', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f64491b7-2398-5544-a3e9-800b664de1d9'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/arts/television/whats-on-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 A.M. (NBC) MACY’S THANKSGIVING DAY PARADE Matt Lauer, Savannah Guthrie and Al Roker host this 86th installment of the parade, with appearances by Kareem Abdul-Jabbar, Trace Adkins, the Big Apple Circus, Colbie Caillat, Jimmy Fallon and the Roots, Flo Rida, Whoopi Goldberg, Carly Rae Jepsen, Don McLean, the Muppets and cast of “Sesame Street,” and the Olympic gymnasts Gabby Douglas, McKayla Maroney, Aly Raisman, Kyla Ross and Jordyn Wieber. The Broadway casts of “Annie,” “Bring It On,” “Cinderella,” “Elf” and “Nice Work If You Can Get It” will perform, along with the Radio City Rockettes. This year’s ballon brigade features Buzz Lightyear, Charlie Brown, Hello Kitty, Kermit the Frog, Kung Fu Panda, Pikachu, Sailor Mickey, Sonic the Hedgehog, Spider-Man and SpongeBob SquarePants. Above, a scene from last year’s parade.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T06:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9d5f49d-1a63-598c-a79f-f7e265d1f835', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9d5f49d-1a63-598c-a79f-f7e265d1f835'}, {'abstract': 'Now that it has almost as many users as the population of China, Facebook proposes to end a system of voting on policy changes because it says it has grown too big.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/facebook-seeks-user-feedback-on-plan-to-end-voting-system/', 'snippet': 'Now that it has almost as many users as the population of China, Facebook proposes to end a system of voting on policy changes because it says it has grown too big.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Democracy can be difficult, especially for a multibillion dollar public company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook Seeks User Feedback on Plan to End Voting System', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T06:03:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26f8b5cd-4c18-5908-8a90-ba229e72b16a', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26f8b5cd-4c18-5908-8a90-ba229e72b16a'}, {'abstract': 'A day after giving their all against the Lakers, the Nets got off to a fast start against the Warriors and then wilted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/sports/basketball/nets-fall-flat-against-warriors-as-energy-wanes.html', 'snippet': 'A day after giving their all against the Lakers, the Nets got off to a fast start against the Warriors and then wilted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OAKLAND, Calif. — A day after giving their all against the star-studded Los Angeles Lakers, the Nets got off to a fast start against the Golden State Warriors and then wilted, a bad second quarter followed by a disastrous third. The Nets’ regression after they sprinted to a 30-18 first-quarter lead came slowly, methodically, as they failed to sustain the energy necessary to sink shots and rotate defensively on shooters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/sports/basketball/22netsgamer-1/22netsgamer-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 823, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/sports/basketball/22netsgamer-1/22netsgamer-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1645, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/sports/basketball/22netsgamer-1/22netsgamer-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/22/sports/basketball/22netsgamer-1/22netsgamer-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/sports/basketball/22netsgamer-1/22netsgamer-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nets Fall Flat as Energy Wanes', 'kicker': 'Warriors 102, Nets 93'