ouse Burning: The Founding Fathers, Our National Debt, and Why It Matters to You.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mary Miller vs. Neil Barofsky for the S.E.C.', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barofsky, Neil M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T10:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42e859c0-4b29-5d0f-9d7e-80fb9eb89699', 'word_count': 1187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42e859c0-4b29-5d0f-9d7e-80fb9eb89699'}, {'abstract': 'The Sands Street gatehouses at the Brooklyn Navy Yard have been restored to their original 1896 design.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/realestate/streetscapes-brooklyn-navy-yard-gatehouses-shed-barnacles.html', 'snippet': 'The Sands Street gatehouses at the Brooklyn Navy Yard have been restored to their original 1896 design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE venerable Brooklyn Navy Yard is a 300-acre industrial complex of vintage factory structures and shiny new modern buildings. But the latest work there is a careful re-creation of the two little 1896 castles known as the Sands Street gatehouses, through which millions of workers poured to build the battleships Arizona and Missouri, among others.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'cap