 and the media is lionizing polarizing figures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Supreme Court lawyer, Karuna Nundy, spoke to India Ink to take stock of the recent arrest of two young women for their Facebook activity, the laws that were used to justify their arrest, and the way to resolve this case. Ms. Nundy, 36, has worked on a number of civil liberties cases and also advises governments of various countries on their compliance with local constitutions and international law. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An ‘Oppressive’ Regime Limits Free Speech in India, Civil Liberties Expert Says', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thackeray, Balasaheb K', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T10:26:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sruthi Gottipati', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sruthi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gottipati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea719aa7-e941-5549-9834-595e527adc34', 'word_count': 901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea719aa7-e941-5549-9834-595e527adc34'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/the-early-word-an-unlikely-partnership/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Today’s Times:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: An Unlikely Partnership', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T11:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31d17317-90f5-59dc-8aa6-f4eb73942784', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31d17317-90f5-59dc-8aa6-f4eb73942784'}, {'abstract': 'When you’re faced with the choice between fresh and dried mushrooms, the answer is easy: Both.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/magazine/mushroom-magic.html', 'snippet': 'When you’re faced with the choice between fresh and dried mushrooms, the answer is easy: Both.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the word “mushroom” conjures for you white buttons in little supermarket tubs, you’re not alone. But there is a big world of mushrooms out there, and you don’t have to be a forager to live in it. Wild mushrooms can be found in spring, summer and fall, but farmed mushrooms, grown mostly in the dark, are always around and a little easier to find than the ones hiding in the woods. So are dried mushrooms, which may be domesticated or truly wild and which are among the most flavorful ingredients you can keep in your pantry.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/magazine/25eat1/25eat1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width