 challenge ever to the received wisdom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/magazine/oliver-stone-rewrites-history-again.html', 'snippet': 'The filmmaker mounts his biggest challenge ever to the received wisdom.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Come on, that’s such a canard, you know that,” Oliver Stone said. “ ‘The Greatest Generation?’ That was the biggest publishing hoax of all. It’s to sell books.” This seemingly sacrosanct term was coined by Tom Brokaw for his 1998 book of the same title, in which he recounted the lives of ordinary, World War II-era Americans. “I was in Vietnam with the Greatest Generation. They were master sergeants, generals, colonels. They had arrogance beyond belief. The hubris that allowed Henry Kissinger to say North Vietnam is a fourth-rate power we will break. The hubris of that!”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/magazine/25stone/25stone-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/25/magazine/25stone/25stone-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 719}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/magazine/25stone/mag-25Stone-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 846, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/magazine/25stone/mag-25Stone-t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1239, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/magazine/25stone/25stone-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name':