 authorities.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/glencore-wins-antitrust-approval-for-xstrata-deal/', 'snippet': 'Glencore International gained regulatory approval for its $32 billion takeover of Xstrata after it agreed to sell assets and reduce its operations to appease European antitrust authorities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Glencore International gained European regulatory approval on Thursday for its $32 billion takeover of the mining company Xstrata, after agreeing to sell assets and reduce its operations in Europe to satisfy antitrust concerns.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Glencore Wins European Approval for Xstrata Deal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Conditions, Europe Approves Xstrata Takeover', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Glencore International AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T13:10:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/517c67d8-2ec8-592f-8be0-c45ee2e4c881', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/517c67d8-2ec8-592f-8be0-c45ee2e4c881'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: Three days after Hurricane Sandy landed, Midtown Manhattan seemed calm and, in places, virtually untouched. But something seemed different, and the differences kept accumulating.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/overheard-in-hurricane-sandys-wake/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: Three days after Hurricane Sandy landed, Midtown Manhattan seemed calm and, in places, virtually untouched. But something seemed different, and the differences kept accumulating.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Overheard in Hurricane Sandy’s Wake', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T13:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Solow Holzman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': 'Solow', 'lastname': 'Holzman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79f704b5-9d20-5a84-840c-bb1c5d15bc56', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79f704b5-9d20-5a84-840c-bb1c5d15bc56'}, {'abstract': 'Now that Moody’s has reduced the debt rating of France, the zone’s second-largest guarantor, the ratings of two organizations handling euro zone bailouts are expected to be reduced in turn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/business/global/daily-euro-zone-watch.html', 'snippet': 'Now that Moody’s has reduced the debt rating of France, the zone’s second-largest guarantor, the ratings of two organizations handling euro zone bailouts are expected to be reduced in turn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — France’s loss of its prime debt rating from Moody’s Investors Service this week poses a challenge for the euro zone’s bailout funds, which now face their own potential downgrades and higher borrowing costs as a result.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'French Downgrade Complicates Life for Bailout Funds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Downgrade Of France Entangles Euro Funds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Corporation", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Investors Service Inc", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Ratings and Credit Rating Agencies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Stability Mechanism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T13:31:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1047ceb-457d-58ea-8cbb-a585267fbd31', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1047ceb-457d-58ea-8cbb-a585267fbd31'}, {'abstract': 'Charles Dickens lived with a secret that overlaps with the mystery in his last, unfinished novel, “The Mystery of Edwin Drood.” The musical based on that tale is back on Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/theater/mystery-of-edwin-drood-dickenss-unfinished-novel.html', 'snippet': 'Charles Dickens lived with a secret that overlaps with the mystery in his last, unfinished novel, “The Mystery of Edwin Drood.” The musical based on that tale is back on Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLES DICKENS, a lifelong ham, would have loved Rupert Holmes’s “Mystery of Edwin Droo