ital in Texas in October.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/lil-wayne-taking-seizure-medication/', 'snippet': 'The rapper told MTV that he’s been taking medication since he became ill and was rushed to a hospital in Texas in October.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rapper Lil Wayne told MTV he has been taking medication to prevent seizures since last month, when he became ill aboard his private jet and was rushed to a hospital in Texas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22artsbeat-wayne/22artsbeat-wayne-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22artsbeat-wayne/22artsbeat-wayne-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1335, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22artsbeat-wayne/22artsbeat-wayne-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22artsbeat-wayne/22artsbeat-wayne-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22artsbeat-wayne/22artsbeat-wayne-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lil Wayne Taking Seizure Medication', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seizures (Medical)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lil Wayne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T16:32:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7df28bca-bcc0-58e3-8cd2-80a16eb20f04', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7df28bca-bcc0-58e3-8cd2-80a16eb20f04'}, {'abstract': 'An all-star roster of players is expected to appear in the Operation Hat Trick charity game at Boardwalk Hall in Atlantic City on Saturday night.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/perhaps-the-best-n-h-l-game-this-season/', 'snippet': 'An all-star roster of players is expected to appear in the Operation Hat Trick charity game at Boardwalk Hall in Atlantic City on Saturday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Operation Hat Trick charity game at Boardwalk Hall in Atlantic City on Saturday night will have a star-laden lineup. All proceeds go to families affected by Hurricane Sandy. The captains, Brad Richards of the Rangers and Scott Hartnell of the Philadelphia Flyers, will lead teams expected to include the following locked-out N.H.L. players who have committed to appear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Perhaps the Best N.H.L. Game This Season', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Brad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlantic City (NJ)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T16:41:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/712596b2-361a-549c-a19a-9beef683b732', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/712596b2-361a-549c-a19a-9beef683b732'}, {'abstract': 'The singer said surgery to remove a polyp on her vocal cords was successful.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/bjork-undergoes-throat-surgery/', 'snippet': 'The singer said surgery to remove a polyp on her vocal cords was successful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Björk has undergone a successful surgery to remove a polyp on her vocal cords that doctors discovered several years ago. In a note posted on her Web site on Wednesday, the Icelandic singer said she had tried for more than four years to manage the problem with dietary changes and exercises to stretch her vocal cords, but decided this year to undergo laser surger, after being forced to cancel some performances of her “Biophilia” show in April.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22artsbeat-bjork/22artsbeat-bjork-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 814, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22artsbeat-bjork/22artsbeat-bjork-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1627, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22artsbeat-bjork/22artsbeat-bjork-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22artsbeat-bjork/22artsbeat-bjork-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/22/arts/22artsbeat-bjork/22artsbeat-bjork-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Björk Undergoes Throat Surgery', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Björk Recovering From Throat Surgery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bjork', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T16:50:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/553aac35-7618-58fe-a42d-eca4d007ba15', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/553aac35-7618-58fe-a42d-eca4d007ba15'}, {'abstract': 'A performer who entertains troops overseas discusses the pleasures of celebrating Thanksgiving with the military.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/in-the-army-theres-a-place-at-the-thanksgiving-table-for-everyone/', 'snippet': 'A performer who entertains troops overseas discusses the pleasures of celebrating Thanksgiving with the military.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I circled the Ralph’s parking lot for several minutes looking for a place to park. Finally, I decided to abandon the parking lot and find a place on the street. I crossed four lanes of traffic and made my way into the grocery store, which was brimming with shoppers filling their carts with turkeys, pecans, green beans, alcohol and yams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Army, There’s a Place at the Thanksgiving Table for Everyone', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bosnia and Herzegovina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kosovo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T16:58:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Rawlings', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rawlings', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f96cb83-9875-5deb-af1b-c5de1e282261', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f96cb83-9875-5deb-af1b-c5de1e282261'}, {'abstract': 'Local politicians and feminist groups had objected to the performance.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/chris-brown-concert-canceled-in-guyana/', 'snippet': 'Local politicians and feminist groups had objected to the performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The singer Chris Brown has canceled a concert in Guyana after local politicians and feminist groups mounted protests because he was convicted of beating up his former girlfriend Rihanna in 2009, The Associated Press reported.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/