“Lincoln,” has created a self-guided route that highlights film locations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tourism agencies have recently started capitalizing on the credits at the end of movies that thank city, state and foreign film commissions for allowing on-location shoots, building tourism campaigns timed to film releases.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Its ‘Lincoln’ Tour, Virginia Is for Moviegoers', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Its ‘Lincoln’ Tour, Virginia Is for Moviegoers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T18:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3123b5d3-8336-5526-a058-cc7f1d4b5b19', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3123b5d3-8336-5526-a058-cc7f1d4b5b19'}, {'abstract': 'A publicity campaign in Lecompton, Kan., seeks national recognition of the tiny town’s crucial role in the election of President Lincoln and in the Civil War.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/us/lecompton-kansas-promotes-role-in-lincolns-rise.html', 'snippet': 'A publicity campaign in Lecompton, Kan., seeks national recognition of the tiny town’s crucial role in the election of President Lincoln and in the Civil War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LECOMPTON, Kan. — Cloaked in a top hat, frock coat, pleated shirt and cravat, Paul Bahnmaier is on a frenetic campaign to thrust his 625-person hometown into the spotlight by heralding its seismic yet little-known place in antebellum history: The first step toward Abraham Lincoln’s election as president took place here.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/us/LINCOLN-1/LINCOLN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/23/us/LINCOLN-1/LINCOLN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/us/LINCOLN-1/LINCOLN-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 621, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/us/LINCOLN-1/LINCOLN-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1242, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/us/LINCOLN-1/LINCOLN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/23/us/LINCOLN-1/LINCOLN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Kansas Town Seeks Fame as a Chapter in Lincoln’s Rise', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Kansas Town Seeks Fame as a Chapter in Lincoln’s Rise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lecompton (Kan)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Lincoln (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T18:10:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2ecee2d-e1f6-560e-b368-543113e257d4', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2ecee2d-e1f6-560e-b368-543113e257d4'}, {'abstract': 'After getting a range of bills passed in the last legislative session, anti-abortion groups have an even more ambitious agenda for the Legislature in 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/us/anti-abortion-groups-push-new-round-of-abortion-rules-in-texas.html', 'snippet': 'After getting a range of bills passed in the last legislative session, anti-abortion groups have an even more ambitious agenda for the Legislature in 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anti-abortion groups championed a string of successful measures during the 2011 Texas legislative session — including a law that requires physicians to perform a sonogram 24 hours in advance of an abortion. For the 2013 session, they are trying to do even more to restrict abortions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/us/23TTFetalpain1/23TTFetalpain1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/23/us/23TTFetalpain1/23TTFetalpain1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/us/23TTFetalpain1/23TTFetalpain1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo'