 {'abstract': 'Readers respond to an article about chocolate in the Caribbean.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/travel/letters-to-the-editor.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to an article about chocolate in the Caribbean.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Caribbean Chocolate', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Editor', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To the Editor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chocolate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Caribbean Area', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T18:51:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/dadb8134-0433-52a4-9d1f-d75270330a53', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dadb8134-0433-52a4-9d1f-d75270330a53'}, {'abstract': 'From her secluded salon in the Beverly Hills Neiman Marcus, Catherine Bloom helps create fashion’s next big things.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/secret-sharer/', 'snippet': 'From her secluded salon in the Beverly Hills Neiman Marcus, Catherine Bloom helps create fashion’s next big things.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Los Angeles isn’t really a pedestrian sort of town. On Wilshire Boulevard’s department store row, you park you car or hand it off to a valet, then enter through the back door — which gives you an instant air of entitlement and belonging, like a backstage pass to a magical world. At Neiman Marcus, there’s somewhere even more hidden — what I call the secret inside the secret — up the escalator to the second floor, in a five-room suite set behind the Valentino boutique: the workplace of Catherine Bloom, Neiman’s personal shopper extraordinaire.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '76', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Secret Sharer', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Secret Sharer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-22T19:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Ephron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ephron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/516077d3-19be-5155-90b3-43093701bf79', 'word_count': 1095, 'uri': 'nyt://article/516077d3-19be-5155-90b3-43093701bf79'}, {'abstract': 'Tommy Tune, in his cabaret show “Taps, Tunes and Tall Tales,” breezes through 20 songs stitched together by amusing, heartfelt anecdotes and brief tap routines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/arts/music/tommy-tune-at-feinsteins-at-loews-regency.html', 'snippet': 'Tommy Tune, in his cabaret show “Taps, Tunes and Tall Tales,” breezes through 20 songs stitched together by amusing, heartfelt anecdotes and brief tap routines.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Honored and ancient.” That is how Tommy Tune — on Sunday evening at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency — described his feelings about having been designated a living landmark three years ago by the New York Landmarks Conservancy. If physical monumentality is a prerequisite for landmark status, no entertainer is more qualified. Mr. Tune, who stands 6-foot-6 and wore a scarlet vested suit for his show, “Taps, Tunes and Tall Tales,” is larger than life. And his handsomely styled silver mane contributed to the statuesque image. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u