, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e8e31b5-5720-5351-bb51-afef7a546249'}, {'abstract': 'Banks need more policing so tough new standards for modifying loans and processing foreclosures are followed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/opinion/more-questions-on-mortgage-relief.html', 'snippet': 'Banks need more policing so tough new standards for modifying loans and processing foreclosures are followed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In February, when five big banks settled with government officials over evidence of foreclosure fraud, the deal was greeted with skepticism. The banks agreed to provide $25 billion in mortgage relief to hard-pressed borrowers, $17 billion of it from reducing the principal on troubled loans. The government considered that a victory, because banks resist principal reductions, but banks have a reputation for promising amends that never seem to get made. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Questions on Mortgage Relief', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Questions on Mortgage Relief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T01:15:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9174fe23-2666-5a7a-ab5d-4bb094f9beec', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9174fe23-2666-5a7a-ab5d-4bb094f9beec'}, {'abstract': "What are the core issues confronting Xi Jinping's leadership, and what can we expect to see?", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/roomfordebate/2012/11/22/dawn-of-a-new-china/', 'snippet': "What are the core issues confronting Xi Jinping's leadership, and what can we expect to see?", 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dawn of a New China?', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T01:19:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a124c780-6faf-53a8-ac92-9f328b1734b4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a124c780-6faf-53a8-ac92-9f328b1734b4'}, {'abstract': 'The nation needs the European Union as much as the union needs it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/opinion/britains-place-in-europe.html', 'snippet': 'The nation needs the European Union as much as the union needs it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Euro-skepticism has remained a current in British politics, long after Britain put aside centuries of anti-European sentiment to join the Common Market in 1973 and to become a member of the more highly integrated European Union 20 years later. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain’s Place in Europe', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain&#8217;s Place in Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-