pg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/23/nyregion/LIDO1/LIDO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/nyregion/LIDO1/LIDO1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Towers, Rich in History, Await Rebirth After Storm', 'kicker': 'Lido Beach Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Towers, Rich in History, Await Rebirth After Storm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lido Beach (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T01:31:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Applebome', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Applebome', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bc1bebe-813e-556d-8b02-eb934bd94be1', 'word_count': 960, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bc1bebe-813e-556d-8b02-eb934bd94be1'}, {'abstract': 'Arrests for possession of small amounts of marijuana do not serve public safety.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/opinion/an-ineffective-way-to-fight-crime.html', 'snippet': 'Arrests for possession of small amounts of marijuana do not serve public safety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a year has passed since Commissioner Raymond Kelly of the New York Police Department issued a memorandum ordering officers to follow a 1977 state law that bars them from arresting people with small amounts of marijuana unless the drug is being publicly displayed. Even so, a lawsuit filed by the Legal Aid Society in June and pending in state court makes the case that the police are still arresting people illegally in clear violation of both the commissioner’s directive and the state law. More than 50,000 possession arrests were made last year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Ineffective Way to Fight Crime', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Ineffective Way to Fight Crime', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Raymond W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T01:33:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5341aaad-e7f0-5658-8f56-d728db5f9338', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5341aaad-e7f0-5658-8f56-d728db5f9338'}, {'abstract': 'As Salvatore Perrone was ordered held without bail in the killings of Brooklyn shopkeepers, details emerged of a man prone to both combativeness and exuberance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/nyregion/salvatore-perrone-suspect-in-3-murders-faced-financial-troubles.html', 'snippet': 'As Salvatore Perrone was ordered held without bail in the killings of Brooklyn shopkeepers, details emerged of a man prone to both combativeness and exuberance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the day a traveling salesman described by the police as a serial killer was ordered held without bail on charges that he murdered three Brooklyn shopkeepers, more details of his life began to emerge. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/nyregion/SERIAL2-color/SERIAL2-color-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 462, 'width': 327, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/nyregion/SERIAL2-color/SERIAL2-color-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 462, 'width': 327, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/nyregion/SERIAL2-color/SERIAL2-color-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/23/nyregion/SERIAL2-color/SERIAL2-color-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/nyregion/SERIAL2-color/SERIAL2-color-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspect in Three Killings Faced Financial Troubles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suspect in Three Killings Faced Financial Troubles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kadare, Isaac', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vahudupour, Rahmatollah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'n