_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Appleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/952f9cfa-23d1-5338-8f04-106b71232024', 'word_count': 1201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/952f9cfa-23d1-5338-8f04-106b71232024'}, {'abstract': 'After a blaze in Yonkers forced Carolyn Cobbs and her three young children from their home, bringing sleepless nights and disrupting her education, the family is trying to get back on track.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/nyregion/mother-and-3-children-find-stability-after-a-fire-even-without-furniture.html', 'snippet': 'After a blaze in Yonkers forced Carolyn Cobbs and her three young children from their home, bringing sleepless nights and disrupting her education, the family is trying to get back on track.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That August day was shaping up to be one that a busy mother, who held down a job and attended classes, cherishes with her children. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/23/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/23/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Family Finds Stability, but No Furniture, After a Fire', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Family Finds Stability, but No Furniture, After a Fire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Westchester Jewish Community Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UJA-Federation of New York', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T03:41:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ee8aac6-ad85-5771-ac39-e1a784f83c0f', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ee8aac6-ad85-5771-ac39-e1a784f83c0f'}, {'abstract': 'Former President Nicolas Sarkozy was put under caution as a witness who could face charges related to accusations that his 2007 election campaign received illegal donations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/world/europe/france-sarkozy-questioned-over-campaign-funds.html', 'snippet': 'Former President Nicolas Sarkozy was put under caution as a witness who could face charges related to accusations that his 2007 election campaign received illegal donations.', 'lead_paragraph': ' After more than 10 hours of questioning by an investigative judge in Bordeaux on Thursday, former President Nicolas Sarkozy was put under caution as a witness who could face charges related to accusations that his 2007 election campaign received illegal donations from one of France’s richest people, Liliane Bettencourt, the L’Oréal heiress. Mr. Sarkozy was not formally indicted but questioned as a witness under caution, meaning that evidence obtained could be used against him in a future prosecution, the Bordeaux prosecutor told French news agencies. The accusations stem from Mr. Sarkozy’s first presidential campaign; no longer president, he has lost his legal immunity. Mr. Sarkozy denies that he took any money from Ms. Bettencourt, now 90, or that his campaign benefited from any illegal fund-raising. Ms. Bettencourt’s former accountant told the police that she handed over 150,000 euros (about $192,000) in cash and was told the money would go to the Sarkozy campaign. Mr. Sarkozy’s party, the center-right Union for a Popular Movement, is in the midst of a prolonged and bitter leadership fight. A Sarkozy protégé, Jean-François Copé, and a former prime minister, François Fillon, both claim victory in an internal party vote. Reports on Thursday said Alain Juppé, a former prime minister and foreign minister who helped found the party, would serve as a mediator. Mr. Sarkozy’s own popularity has been rising again. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Sarkozy Questioned Over Campaign Funds', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Sarkozy Questioned Over Campaign Funds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettencourt, Liliane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T03:49:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6d56e9e-14ff-5bbb-af8f-4d54df3196b3', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6d56e9e-14ff-5bbb-af8f-4d54df3196b3'}, {'abstract': 'Spain announced that it would grant automatic citizenship to Jews of Sephardic descent as a further gesture of reconciliation after their ancestors were expelled more than five centuries ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/world/europe/spain-citizenship-process-eased-for-sephardic-jews.html', 'snippet': 'Spain announced that it would grant automatic citizenship to Jews of Sephardic descent as a further gesture of reconciliation after their ancestors were expelled more than five centuries ago.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Spain announced Thursday that it would grant automatic citizenship to Jews of Sephardic descent as a further gesture of reconciliation after their ancestors were expelled more than five centuries ago. Sephardic Jews already benefit from a preferential naturalization procedure that requires them to live in Spain for only two years before claiming citizenship, but the change means that Jews will have to present only a certificate confirming their ancestry to claim a Spanish passport. The government did not say how many Jews it expected to apply for citizenship, but it noted that a large number of Sephardic Jews lived in Turkey and across Latin America. While estimates differ, the number of Jews living in Spain — 25,000 to 45,000 people in a population of 47 million — is only a fraction of the number who lived in the country before 1492, when Jews were told to convert to Christianity or go into exile. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spain: Citizenship Process Eased for Sephardic Jews', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spain: Citizenship Process Eased for Sephardic Jews', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T03:52:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1101eba8-542d-54e2-97b8-728a0251d563', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1101eba8-542d-54e2-97b8-728a0251d563'}, {'abstract': 'Indian experts discuss the low rates of conviction and execution for terrorism.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/22/why-are-few-terrorists-executed-in-india/', 'snippet': 'Indian experts discuss the low rates of conviction and execution for terrorism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'India has faced terrorism for more than the last five decades, practically since the country was created. The northeast states, central and east India, Punjab and Jammu and Kashmir have been particularly affected, but almost no state has been free from terror incidents in that time. At least 90,000 people have lost their lives in India in terrorism-related incidents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Are Few Terrorists Executed in India?', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kasab, Mohammed Ajmal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Punjab (Pakistan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T03:53:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c0d8c69-1553-5f6b-9f85-0cc2d0f2348c', 'word_count': 1173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c0d8c69-1553-5f6b-9f85-0cc2d0f2348c'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and C