ive years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kohlberg Kravis Roberts agreed on Friday to buy Alliant Insurance Services, an insurance brokerage firm, from the Blackstone Group. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'K.K.R. to Buy Alliant Insurance From Blackstone', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alliant Insurance Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'The Blackstone Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T14:14:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/387521a8-af6a-5f81-ba27-9bf2a346daf4', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/387521a8-af6a-5f81-ba27-9bf2a346daf4'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands of protesters chanted for the downfall of President Mohamed Morsi’s government in Cairo, while others ransacked the offices of the president’s former party in other cities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/24/world/middleeast/amid-protest-egypts-leader-defends-his-new-powers.html', 'snippet': 'Thousands of protesters chanted for the downfall of President Mohamed Morsi’s government in Cairo, while others ransacked the offices of the president’s former party in other cities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Protests erupted across Egypt on Friday, as opponents of President Mohamed Morsi clashed with his supporters over a presidential edict that gave him unchecked authority and polarized an already divided nation while raising a specter, the president’s critics charged, of a return to autocracy. \xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/world/jp-egypt1/jp-egypt1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/24/world/jp-egypt1/jp-egypt1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/world/jp-egypt1/jp-egypt1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/world/jp-egypt1/jp-egypt1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/world/jp-egypt1/jp-egypt1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/24/world/jp-egypt1/jp-egypt1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/world/jp-egypt1/jp-egypt1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clashes Break Out After Morsi Seizes New Power in Egypt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Violent Protests in Egypt As Leader Expands Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T14:34:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim and David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebff0851-b7bc-586c-9f2f-1cf3c9ab63e3', 'word_count': 1244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebff0851-b7bc-586c-9f2f-1cf3c9ab63e3'}, {'abstract': 'Also, the German offshoot of The Financial Times decides to stop publishing, and Quebec orders big United States retailers to translate their names into French.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/the-breakfast-meeting-bbc-tries-to-reset-again-and-a-close-to-linsanity/', 'snippet': 'Also, the German offshoot of The Financial Times decides to stop publishing, and Quebec orders big United States retailers to translate their names into French.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British Broadcasting Corporation on Thursday named a new general director, Tony Hall, who it hopes will restore order to the organization, which has been overwhelmed by scandal related to botched reporting of sexual abuse, John F. Burns and Alan Cowell reported. He replaces George Entwistle, who resigned this month after less than two months in the job. Mr. Hall began his career as a news trainee at the BBC, but for the last 11 years has run the Royal Opera House in London. In the late 1990s, when Mr. Hall was the BBC’s news chief, he was passed over for the director general’s post; the man who beat him was Greg Dyke, who quit in 2004 amid a scandal related to reporting of the Iraq war.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: BBC Tries to Reset Again, and a Close to ‘Linsanity’', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lin, Jeremy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Quebec Province (Canada)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T14:35:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4714f891-f377-5b49-83ac-f9ea90d1d2bb', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4714f891-f377-5b49-83ac-f9ea90d1d2bb'}, {'abstract': 'A 20-room co-op, with 12,000 square feet of interior space, was sold by the socialite Denise Rich to David Geffen, a founder of DreamWorks.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/big-ticket-sold-for-54-million/', 'snippet': 'A 20-room co-op, with 12,000 square feet of interior space, was sold by the socialite Denise Rich to David Geffen, a founder of DreamWorks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The opulent 20-room penthouse at 785 Fifth Avenue where the socialite and songstress Denise Rich reigned as the hostess supreme has sold for $54 million, the biggest sale of the week according to city records. The duplex was reputed to be one of the largest apartments in New York City, with 12,000 square feet of interior space and 5,000 square feet of wraparound terraces and roof gardens overlooking Central Park.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/realestate/ticket/ticket-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 603, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/realestate/ticket/ticket-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1206, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/realestate/ticket/ticket-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/25/realestate/ticket/ticket-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/realestate/ticket/ticket-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Ticket | Sold for $54 Million', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Ticket: $54,000,000', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geffen, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rich, Denise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CENTRAL PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T14:43:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f258aed0-7ad1-572a-b121-d1c88e16996a', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f258aed0-7ad1-572a-b121-d1c88e16996a'}, {'abstract': 'At a sugar plantation in Brazil, a company will use genetically modified algae that eats carbon dioxide from sugar and excretes ethanol.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/another-path-to-biofuels-two-actually/', 'snippet': 'At a sugar plantation in Brazil, a company will use genetically modified algae that eats carbon dioxide from sugar and excretes ethanol.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week I wrote about two companies that are racing to be first in commercial-scale production of motor fuel from nonfood sources. A large group of other companies is pursuing various other strategies, one or two steps behind. One of those companies is planning to use algae.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Path to Biofuels', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALGAE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biofuels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethanol', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sugar', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'ran