 Robinson will do something she has done more times — in front of more people, in more cities of the world — than she can easily calculate. This time, though, will be the last: the last time as a member of Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater that she holds the white parasol above the baptism scene in “Revelations,” the last time she and her yellow dress help turn the whole theater into a rocking church. Ms. Robinson is retiring.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/arts/25RENEE_SPAN/25RENEE4_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/25/arts/25RENEE_SPAN/25RENEE4_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/arts/25RENEE_SPAN/25RENEE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 839, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/arts/25RENEE_SPAN/25RENEE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1677, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/arts/25RENEE_SPAN/25RENEE4_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/25/arts/25RENEE_SPAN/25RENEE4_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/arts/25RENEE_SPAN/25RENEE4_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Choreography of Goodbye', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Choreography of Goodbye', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, Renee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AILEY, ALVIN, AMERICAN DANCE THEATER', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T15:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59ace046-f223-573c-8fec-30adc42debd4', 'word_count': 1190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59ace046-f223-573c-8fec-30adc42debd4'}, {'abstract': 'Psychotherapy’s struggle to sell itself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/magazine/psychotherapys-image-problem-pushes-some-therapists-to-become-brands.html', 'snippet': 'Psychotherapy’s struggle to sell itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the summer of 2011, after I completed six years of graduate school and internship training and was about to start my psychotherapy practice, I sat down with my clinical supervisor in the Los Angeles office we’d be sharing. It had been a rigorous six years, transitioning from my role as a full-time journalist always on tight deadlines to that of a therapist whose world was broken into slow, thoughtful hours listening and trying to help people come to a deeper understanding of their lives. My supervisor went over the filing systems, billing procedures and ethical quandaries like whether to take referrals from current clients, but we never discussed how I would get these clients. I fully assumed, in what now seems like an astounding fit of naïveté, that I’d send out an e-mail announcement and network with doctors, and to paraphrase “Field of Dreams,” if I built it, they would come.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/magazine/25therapist1/25therapist1-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/25/magazine/25therapist1/25therapist1-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/magazine/25therapist1/mag-25Therapist-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/magazine/25therapist1/mag-25Therapist-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/magazine/25therapist1/25therapist1-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/25/magazine/25therapist1/25therapist1-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/magazine/25therapist1/25therapist1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Brand Is Your Therapist?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Branding Cure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub':