ervations of the dwarf planet Makemake indicate that it lacks a significant atmosphere and reflects about as much sunlight as dirty snow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/science/space/makemake-dwarf-planet-beyond-pluto-has-no-atmosphere-study-suggests.html', 'snippet': 'Recent observations of the dwarf planet Makemake indicate that it lacks a significant atmosphere and reflects about as much sunlight as dirty snow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not much is known about Makemake, a dwarf planet that circles the Sun beyond Pluto. But scientists got a closer glimpse of it last year, when it passed briefly in front of a star (an event called an occultation), and they report their findings in the current issue of the journal Nature. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/27planet_observatory/27observatory-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/27planet_observatory/27observatory-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 1280, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/27planet_observatory/27planet_observatory-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/27/science/27planet_observatory/27planet_observatory-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/27planet_observatory/27planet_observatory-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dwarf Planet Lacks Atmosphere, Glimpse Suggests', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dwarf Planet Lacks Atmosphere, Glimpse Suggests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Astronomy and Astrophysics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Makemake (Dwarf Planet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Planets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T15:53:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb3d5a7b-938a-544e-844d-068f6aee4675', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb3d5a7b-938a-544e-844d-068f6aee4675'}, {'abstract': 'A Dutch shoe designer and his Italian girlfriend find inspiration for their men’s collections in Hemingway and the art of Florence.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/sole-mates/', 'snippet': 'A Dutch shoe designer and his Italian girlfriend find inspiration for their men’s collections in Hemingway and the art of Florence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Dutch shoe designer Louis Leeman first crossed paths with his girlfriend and collaborator, Erica Pelosini, in her home town of Florence, Italy, while he was a student at the Polimoda fashion school. “We are the complete opposites in so many things,” said Pelosini, who got her start as a fashion journalist. “It can be tricky, but in the end that’s what makes it work.” They hatched a plan to make men’s shoes after a day spent looking at Canaletto paintings at the Museo Bellini in Florence. (They’re pictured above in the museum.) In 2010, they moved to Paris and, while Leeman moonlighted for established fashion houses, the pair began making handcrafted kicks that soon ended up on the shelves at Bergdorf Goodman. Leeman said his shoes are targeted at footloose dandies who value old-fashioned construction. His latest collection, he said, channels “The Sun Also Rises,” with matador-inspired slippers (above) and soft suede moccasins. Playing with cultural references is one of Leeman’s favorite parts of fashion. “There’ll always be some influence from poetry, music, painting or literature,” he said. ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '66', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sole Mates', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sole Mates', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T16:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Tudela', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tudela', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a8864bd-6784-59b7-864c-e6d45a89d35f', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a8864bd-6784-59b7-864c-e6d45a89d35f'}, {'abstract': 'Retailers are using apps to try to lure shoppers away from the Internet and back to stores, Stephanie Clifford and Claire Cain Miller report on Friday in The New York Times. As bait, retailers are using technological tools that will make shopping on the busiest day of the year a little more sane.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/daily-report-using-apps-to-lure-shoppers-into-stores/', 'snippet': 'Retailers are using apps to try to lure shoppers away from the Internet and back to stores, Stephanie Clifford and Claire Cain Miller report on Friday in The New York Times. As bait, retailers are using technological tools that will make shopping ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Retailers are using apps to try to lure shoppers away from the Internet and back to stores, Stephanie Clifford and Claire Cain Miller report on Friday in The New York Times. As bait, retailers are using technological tools that will make shopping on the busiest day of the year a little more sane — and give shoppers an edge over their competition.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: Using Apps to Lure Shoppers Into Stores', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T16:04:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/093ed9c7-d1a3-53bd-b064-88077a9c3676', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/093ed9c7-d1a3-53bd-b064-88077a9c3676'}, {'abstract': 'A procession to mark Muharram, the first month of the Islamic calendar, in Amroha, Uttar Pradesh.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/image-of-the-day-nov-23/', 'snippet': 'A procession to mark Muharram, the first month of the Islamic calendar, in Amroha, Uttar Pradesh.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: Nov. 23', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uttar Pradesh State (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T16:04:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://a