; and what to wear the first day of a new job.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/fashion/the-same-old-song-societys-child.html', 'snippet': 'What to say when people comment on your beau’s race; when the plus-one turns out to be someone not welcome; and what to wear the first day of a new job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am a white woman and have recently started dating a man who is Asian. The last man I dated was also Asian, and the problem is that, so far, every person I’ve introduced him to has made a comment insinuating that I have some sort of Asian fetish or desire to replace my last boyfriend. I know that if I dated two white men in a row, nobody would even notice, let alone say anything. How should I respond? ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Society’s Child', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Society’s Child', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T18:33:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/f51d4a39-68ed-505b-b09c-09c3e3c9a483', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f51d4a39-68ed-505b-b09c-09c3e3c9a483'}, {'abstract': 'Borussia Mönchengladbach has struggled to keep pace with the top teams in Germany’s Bundesliga.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/23/what-happened-to-borussia-barcelona-monchengladbach/', 'snippet': 'Borussia Mönchengladbach has struggled to keep pace with the top teams in Germany’s Bundesliga.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From part-time trialists to seasoned pros, Germany’s Bundesliga teams have taken to this season’s UEFA Champions League like it was their god given right. From Manchester mavericks Borussia Dortmund, to the evergreen European contenders Bayern Munich, to Arsenal’s Gelsenkirchen assassins Schalke, the Bundesliga’s top three have taken no prisoners in their march to European domination. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Happened to Borussia (Barcelona) Mönchengladbach?', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Borussia Monchengladbach (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'German Bundesliga', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T18:38:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stefan Bienkowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stefan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bienkowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/000568e6-4b03-5938-a728-ad5854d541a1', 'word_count': 1016, 'uri': 'nyt://article/000568e6-4b03-5938-a728-ad5854d541a1'}, {'abstract': 'Ahn Cheol-soo, a computer software mogul who was widely seen as a top contender for the presidency, threw his support behind a fellow liberal who has championed aggressive engagement with North Korea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/24/world/asia/ahn-cheol-soo-unexpectedly-quits-south-koreas-presidential-race.html', 'snippet': 'Ahn Cheol-soo, a computer software mogul who was widely seen as a top contender for the presidency, threw his support behind a fellow liberal who has championed aggressive engagement with North Korea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — The millionaire software mogul who was widely seen as a top contender in South Korea’s presidential election in December unexpectedly withdrew his candidacy on Friday, throwing his support behind the candidate of the main opposition party who has championed more engagement with North Korea and “balanced diplomacy” with Washington and Beijing. South Korea’s diplomatic policy is currently weighted more toward the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/world/korea/korea-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 725, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/world/korea/korea-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1432, 'width': 1014, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/world/korea/korea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/24/world/korea/korea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/world/korea/korea-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'South Korea Is Surprised by Departure of Candidate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Korea Is Surprised By Departure Of Candidate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moon Jae-in', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahn Cheol-soo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Park Chung-hee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea'