st.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the director Joe Wright sees it, everything in a film is choreographed. In his unconventional take on “Anna Karenina,” he pushes this idea to the limit by removing the imaginary line between an actor’s movement and dance. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/arts/24ANNA/24ANNA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/arts/24ANNA/24ANNA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1458, 'width': 1093, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/arts/24ANNA/24ANNA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/24/arts/24ANNA/24ANNA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/arts/24ANNA/24ANNA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Words Dance on Screen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making Words Dance On Screen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Anna Karenina (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cherkaoui, Sidi Larbi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '