', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Count Continues, Reassessing Pennsylvania', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-23T21:57:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4de990fa-ca4d-50d3-aeec-57a141b72081', 'word_count': 1283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4de990fa-ca4d-50d3-aeec-57a141b72081'}, {'abstract': 'The fatal shooting by Israeli soldiers of a Palestinian man did not fracture the cease-fire that ended eight days of fighting between Hamas and Israel. But it did showcase the confusion that remains over the deal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/11/23/world/middleeast/20121123-GAZA-GOBIG.html', 'snippet': 'The fatal shooting by Israeli soldiers of a Palestinian man did not fracture the cease-fire that ended eight days of fighting between Hamas and Israel. But it did showcase the confusion that remains over the deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fatal shooting by Israeli soldiers of a Palestinian man did not fracture the cease-fire that ended eight days of fighting between Hamas and Israel. But it did showcase the confusion that remains over the deal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/world/middleeast/2012112