': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public and Subsidized Housing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Outages and Blackouts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing Authority (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T00:14:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79058cb5-3630-574d-8db1-a9da57865a4d', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79058cb5-3630-574d-8db1-a9da57865a4d'}, {'abstract': 'In many neighborhoods around New York City that are currently weighing school rezoning proposals, passions have been running high.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/nyregion/brooklyn-school-rezoning-touches-off-a-border-war.html', 'snippet': 'In many neighborhoods around New York City that are currently weighing school rezoning proposals, passions have been running high.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two hours ticked by slowly in the John Jay High School auditorium as, one after another, Park Slope residents presented data about diversity, detailed unsafe crossings along Fourth Avenue and recounted how far they would have to travel to get to school if a plan to rezone two of the most popular schools in the Brooklyn neighborhood were enacted.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/nyregion/25REZONE_SPAN/25REZONE_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'x