d once it all ended.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/nyregion/CLOWN/CLOWN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/nyregion/CLOWN/CLOWN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1467, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/nyregion/CLOWN/CLOWN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/24/nyregion/CLOWN/CLOWN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/nyregion/CLOWN/CLOWN-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Couple Seeking to Draw Smiles at Parade, Annual Clown Ritual Turns Tragic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Couple Seeking to Draw Smiles at Parade, Annual Clown Ritual Turns Tragic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blasetti, Irene', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blasetti, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clowns', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T01:59:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By N. R. Kleinfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'N.', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Kleinfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c5c512b-0722-5124-bc13-f9b24a1e4f9e', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c5c512b-0722-5124-bc13-f9b24a1e4f9e'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama now has the freedom to take on the issue that politicians shun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/24/opinion/promises-on-gun-control.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama now has the freedom to take on the issue that politicians shun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s fleeting mention of the need for stronger gun controls at a presidential debate last month was hardly the kind of forceful political statement needed to address the scourge of gun violence in this country. Even his tepid remark was considered by the nation’s gun owners as a threat to take away their firearms. In what amounts to a buyers’ panic, they are again ramping up gun and ammunition sales as they did four years ago, convinced that Mr. Obama intends a gun-control crackdown. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Promises on Gun Control', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Promises on Gun Control', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feinstein, Dianne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T02:02:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/403473ac-ed97-5e8c-b686-c289bad046a3', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/403473ac-ed97-5e8c-b686-c289bad046a3'}, {'abstract': 'If you can’t find something to please your palate on the Woodland Restaurant’s three-page menu, you must not be trying.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/nyregion/a-review-of-the-woodland-restaurant-in-lakeville.html', 'snippet': 'If you can’t find something to please your palate on the Woodland Restaurant’s three-page menu, you must not be trying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an economy that sees restaurants opening and closing within months, the Woodland Restaurant in Lakeville is one of those rarities that have been around for decades — since 1983, in fact. There is no secret behind its longevity, simply an adherence to the old dictum about giving the customer what he or she wants.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/nyregion/25DINECT1/25DINECT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 823, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/nyregion/25DINECT1/25DINECT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1645, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/nyregion/25DINECT1/25DINECT1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', '