hold the big guys accountable.” Now, some bankers, their lobbyists and their Republican allies on the Senate banking committee reportedly would like nothing better than to keep Ms. Warren off the powerful bank panel — where she could do the most harm to the status quo, and the most good for the country. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Their Problem With Elizabeth Warren', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Their Problem With Elizabeth Warren', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T02:11:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a609e8c6-527b-5330-a45b-75b8bbf76a21', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a609e8c6-527b-5330-a45b-75b8bbf76a21'}, {'abstract': 'Readers in the United States knew Mr. Courtenay mainly for his first novel, “The Power of One,” but he sold more than 20 million copies of 21 books in all. His last novel came out this month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/24/books/bryce-courtenay-australian-novelist-dies-at-79.html', 'snippet': 'Readers in the United States knew Mr. Courtenay mainly for his first novel, “The Power of One,” but he sold more than 20 million copies of 21 books in all. His last novel came out this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bryce 