s', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T02:13:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f004ce1b-0866-512f-8330-5240587bf815', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f004ce1b-0866-512f-8330-5240587bf815'}, {'abstract': 'The government of Prime Minister John Key has linked its fortunes to some of Hollywood’s biggest pictures, creating a grand experiment in the fusion of film and government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/24/business/media/new-zealand-wants-a-hollywood-put-on-its-map.html', 'snippet': 'The government of Prime Minister John Key has linked its fortunes to some of Hollywood’s biggest pictures, creating a grand experiment in the fusion of film and government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WELLINGTON, New Zealand — Standing by his desk in New Zealand’s distinctive round Parliament building, known locally as the Beehive, Prime Minister John Key proudly brandished an ornately engraved sword. It was used, he said, by Frodo Baggins, the protagonist of the “Lord of the Rings” trilogy, and in the films it possesses magical powers that cause it to glow blue in the presence of goblins.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/business/media/HOBBIT-slide-QOGP/HOBBIT-slide-QOGP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/24/business/media/HOBBIT-slide-QOGP/HOBBIT-slide-QOGP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/