count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4094824d-78e4-5198-a5fe-ceb3e5b22c2d'}, {'abstract': 'The election of François Hollande, the first French president from the left in 17 years, has sparked a shuffling of the news media ranks, along with potential conflicts of interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/24/world/europe/in-france-in-bed-with-media-can-be-taken-more-literally.html', 'snippet': 'The election of François Hollande, the first French president from the left in 17 years, has sparked a shuffling of the news media ranks, along with potential conflicts of interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The nation’s leading conservative newspaper ousted its top editor, apparently hoping to ingratiate itself with the new government. A cultural magazine brought in a new editor as well, opting for the partner of a newly minted government minister. The man she replaced took a job working for the new president. The springtime election of François Hollande, the first French president from the left in 17 years, has brought about a shuffling of the news media ranks, along with a host of potential conflicts of interest.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/world/FRANCE1/FRANCE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/world/FRANCE1/FRANCE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1604, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/24/world/FRANCE1/FRANCE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/24/world/FRANCE1/FR