m bustling Vancouver in British Columbia to quaint Nova Scotia are locked on the broadcast of the Grey Cup, the Canadian Football League’s championship game. Not only is the Grey Cup considered Canada’s Super Bowl, but it also practically doubles as the country’s alternate Independence Day. Understanding the significance of this game is a true test of patriotism. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sports/grey-1/grey-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 585, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sports/grey-1/grey-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1170, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sports/grey-1/grey-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/25/sports/grey-1/grey-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sports/grey-1/grey-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada’s Big Game Goes Beyond Super', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada’s Big Game Goes Beyond Super', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Canadian Football League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Argonauts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calgary Stampeders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T16:47:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerald Narciso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerald', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Narciso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b085dbc-0910-52f4-97a7-0a087f97d395', 'word_count': 863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b085dbc-0910-52f4-97a7-0a087f97d395'}, {'abstract': 'Jeffrey Harris’s cryptic crossword is wrapped in a riddle that’s wrapped in an enigma.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/24/variety-cryptic-wrapped-in-an-enigma/', 'snippet': 'Jeffrey Harris’s cryptic crossword is wrapped in a riddle that’s wrapped in an enigma.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SECOND SUNDAY PUZZLE — We all know the feeling of waiting and waiting for a bus to come, only to see two arrive at the same time. That’s the way a lot of crossword solvers feel about Sundays, when they’re bombarded with The Big Sunday as well as a variety puzzle. It can be overwhelming at times. But this week we’ve got a cryptic crossword, courtesy of Jeffrey Harris, that’s worth your wait because you’ll be scratching your head over it for quite a while. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Cryptic Wrapped in an Enigma', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T17:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Gaffney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ga