ded.html', 'snippet': 'Teams are turning to advanced statistics that can show the probability of success of plays and players, provide real-time analysis, and even suggest practice regimens after injuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeff Dominitz grew up rooting for the Washington Redskins during their glory years under Joe Gibbs. So when an N.F.L. team called him in 2006 about a job doing statistical research and analysis for the scouting department, he could not say no. He left his teaching position at Carnegie Mellon and, temporarily, his family and wound up living alone near the team’s headquarters.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More N.F.L. Teams Hire Statisticians but Their Use Remains Mostly Guarded', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More N.F.L. Teams Use Statisticians, but League Acceptance Is Not Mode', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statistics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T17:32:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bac934f3-fae5-5a6e-ba13-376bcc2649b2', 'word_count': 1395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bac934f3-fae5-5a6e-ba13-376bcc2649b2'}, {'abstract': 'A good quarterback controversy has at least five stages. The 