://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/business/nottingham-spirks-co-presidents-on-cultivating-new-ideas.html', 'snippet': 'The leaders of an innovation consulting firm say they often tell their client companies to narrow down their project teams — to include only those who own the idea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This interview with  John Nottingham and  John Spirk, co-presidents of Nottingham Spirk, an innovation consulting firm based in Cleveland, was conducted and condensed by  Adam Bryant. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/business/25-CORNER/25-CORNER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 290, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/business/25-CORNER/25-CORNER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 290, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/business/25-CORNER/25-CORNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/25/business/25-CORNER/25-CORNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Idea Kitchen, Too Many Cooks Can Spoil the Broth', 'kicker': 'Corner Office | John Nottingham and John Spirk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Idea Kitchen, Too Many Cooks Can Spoil the Broth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nottingham, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nottingham Spirk', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spirk, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T18:51:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Bryant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bryant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/47817dc5-67db-55e5-98ff-e21bdc42eb49', 'word_count': 1074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47817dc5-67db-55e5-98ff-e21bdc42eb49'}, {'abstract': 'The artist draws things he saw in Michigan and New York.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/24/things-i-saw-no-44/', 'snippet': 'The artist draws things he saw in Michigan and New York.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Suggestions for what you’d like Jason to see and draw may be sent to thingsisaw@nytimes.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Things I Saw — No. 44', 'kicker': 'Things I Saw', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T19:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Polan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3e92311-e061-5fb7-bbfb-8dd6968acdb8', 'word_count': 21, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3e92311-e061-5fb7-bbfb-8dd6968acdb8'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court barred mandatory life sentences without parole for young people, forcing states to rethink criminal penalties.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/opinion/sunday/juvenile-injustice-and-the-states.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court barred mandatory life sentences without parole for young people, forcing states to rethink criminal penalties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Step by step, the Supreme Court has been trying to reshape the way the American criminal justice system deals with those under the age of 18. In Miller v. Alabama this June, it ruled that a mandatory life sentence without parole for a juvenile is cruel and unusual punishment, even when the crime is homicide. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Juvenile Injustice', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Juvenile Injustice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mandatory Sentencing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kagan, Elena', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T19:02:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6924e3b5-612f-5ff1-918b-9e4291cdc572', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6924e3b5-612f-5ff1-918b-9e4291cdc572'}, {'abstract': 'The Giants faithfully (and a bit comically) practice a play called the Flood Tip — Coach Tom Coughlin’s version of the last-second heave to the end zone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/sports/football/giants-have-a-design-for-desperation-heave-into-end-zone-jump-hold-breath.html', 'snippet': 'The Giants faithfully (and a bit comically) practice a play called the Flood Tip — Coach Tom Coughlin’s version of the last-second heave to the end zone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Every Saturday morning before every Sunday game, the Giants gather at the team’s training center and take part in a walk-through. They do not wear pads, just team sweats, but the walk-through is designed to simulate situations the players may encounter and to reinforce exactly where each player should be.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1548, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/25/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants’ Design for Desperation: Heave Into End Zone, Jump, Exhale', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giants’ Design for Desperation: Heave Into End Zone, Jump, Exhale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords':