n': [{'firstname': 'Maureen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dowd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/231e5bdc-8d54-53ce-99c5-611946ad5233', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/231e5bdc-8d54-53ce-99c5-611946ad5233'}, {'abstract': 'The stories of Dale Curtis Gaines and other prisoners reveal how the most vulnerable and helpless suffered the most from a harsh law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/opinion/sunday/california-horror-stories-and-the-3-strikes-law.html', 'snippet': 'The stories of Dale Curtis Gaines and other prisoners reveal how the most vulnerable and helpless suffered the most from a harsh law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Californians brought a close to a shameful period in the state’s history when they voted this month to soften the infamous “three strikes” sentencing law. The original law was approved by ballot initiative in 1994, not long after a parolee kidnapped and murdered a 12-year-old girl. It was sold to voters as a way of getting killers, rapists and child molesters off the streets for good.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sunday-review/1125editorial/1125editorial-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sunday-review/1125editorial/1125editorial-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1535, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sunday-review/1125editorial/1125editorial-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/25/sunday-review/1125editorial/1125editorial-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sunday-review/1125editorial/1125editorial-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'California Horror Stories and the 3-Strikes Law', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Sunday Observer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California Horror Stories And the 3-Strikes Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Retardation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T19:05:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brent Staples', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staples', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ddffd14-f2ff-5fd9-b595-218f85e7c35a', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ddffd14-f2ff-5fd9-b595-218f85e7c35a'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans can start to repair their standing among women, gay and immigrant voters by agreeing on a bill that would help protect all victims of domestic violence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/opinion/sunday/the-gop-and-violence-against-women.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans can start to repair their standing among women, gay and immigrant voters by agreeing on a bill that would help protect all victims of domestic violence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Republicans are serious about repairing their party’s standing among women, gay and Hispanic voters, they need to adjust some policies and stop sending hostile messages. A good place to start would be for Republicans in the House to stop blocking reauthorization of the Violence Against Women Act over provisions deemed too protective of gay and immigrant victims of domestic violence and sexual assault. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The G.O.P. and Violence Against Women', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The G.O.P. and Violence Against Women', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T19:05:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a94f93a-60d2-56ff-b51e-9e89f5b088ae', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a94f93a-60d2-56ff-b51e-9e89f5b088ae'}, {'abstract': 'The criticism of a new restaurant in Times Square was delicious, even if the food was not.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/opinion/sunday/reviews-by-times-critics-with-all-guns-blazing.html', 'snippet': 'The criticism of a new restaurant in Times Square was delicious, even if the food was not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Times’s culture editor, Jonathan Landman, calls them “exuberant pans” — reviews so energetically negative that they seem to achieve liftoff. They blast into the media world with cosmic force. Everyone wants to talk about them in a “did you see that?” way. Sometimes, they become instant classics. And, it goes almost without saying, the critic’s fun is inversely proportional to how it feels on the receiving end. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/public-editor/MSullivan-2/MSullivan-2-articleLarge.png', 'height': 895, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/04/public-editor/MSullivan-2/MSullivan-2-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 895}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/public-editor/MSullivan-2/MSullivan-2-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 913, 'width': 612, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/public-editor/MSullivan-2/MSullivan-2-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 913, 'width': 612, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/public-editor/MSullivan-2/MSullivan-2-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/04/public-editor/MSullivan-2/MSullivan-2-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/public-editor/MSullivan-2/MSullivan-2-thumbLarge-v3.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviews With ‘All Guns Blazing’', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reviews With ‘All Guns Blazing’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wells, Pete', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fieri, Guy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Editor (Times Column)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T19:05:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbbcca25-ae18-547b-ba69-a68f99263a7f', 'word_count': 1010, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbbcca25-ae18-547b-ba69-a68f99263a7f'}, {'abstract': 'The latest Israeli-Hamas conflict was as much a test for Egypt as anyone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/opinion/sunday/friedman-morsis-moment.html', 'snippet': 'The latest Israeli-Hamas conflict was as much a test for Egypt as anyone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Israeli-Hamas miniwar last week was the first test of the post-Arab awakening order in the Middle East. Hamas, by getting embroiled in a missile duel with Israel and then calling on Arab countries for support, particularly Egypt, was testing Cairo as much as Israel. And the question Hamas was posing to Egyptians was simple: Did Egypt have a democratic revolution last year to become more like Iran or more like China? In other words, is Egypt ready to sacrifice the Camp David peace, U.S. aid and economic development to support Hamas’s radical, pro-Iranian agenda, or not?', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Morsi’s Moment', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Morsi’s Moment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Jordan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T19:05:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed3e36dd-ea0b-5786-8cd2-f49f7b3270fc', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed3e36dd-ea0b-5786-8cd2-f49f7b3270fc'}, {'abstract': 'Both parties should do everything they can to make the payroll tax holiday permanent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/opinion/sunday/douthat-our-enemy-the-payroll-tax.html', 'snippet': 'Both parties should do everything they can to make the payroll tax holiday permanent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WE have two political parties in America, runs a saying that conservatives like to quote. One is stupid, the other is evil. And when they join forces to do something that’s both stupid and evil — well, that’s what we call “bipartisanship.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Enemy, the Payroll Tax', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Our Enemy, the Payroll Tax', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payroll Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Security (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T19:06:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fb328a2-4600-51f0-a582-ca550f7a503a', 'word_count': 779, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fb328a2-4600-51f0-a582-ca550f7a503a'}, {'abstract': 'The Giants acknowledge that one of the main reasons they were able to defeat Green Bay in the playoffs last January was the sustained pressure they put on quarterback Aaron Rodgers.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/24/matchup-packers-7-3-at-giants-6-4/', 'snippet': 'The Giants acknowledge that one of the main reasons they were able to defeat Green Bay in the playoffs last January was the sustained pressure they put on quarterback Aaron Rodgers.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:20 p.m. Eastern, NBC', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Matchup: Packers (7-3) at Giants (6-4)', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Packers (7-3) at Giants (6-4)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodgers, Aaron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tuck, Justin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T19:08:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54356fde-fc43-5975-a6c0-a708ba3075ce', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54356fde-fc43-5975-a6c0-a708ba3075ce'}, {'abstract': 'Millions of American citizens on the island have spoken. Now, Washington must act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/opinion/sunday/will-puerto-rico-be-americas-51st-state.html', 'snippet': 'Millions of American citizens on the island have spoken. Now, Washington must act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE of the little-noticed results of the Nov. 6 elections was a plebiscite held in Puerto Rico on the island’s relationship with the United States. The outcome was murky, much like the last century’s worth of political history between Washington and San Juan, and the mainland’s confused or disinterested attitude toward Puerto Rico that abetted it. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sunday-review/25PUERTORICO/25PUERTORICO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 844, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sunday-review/25PUERTORICO/25PUERTORICO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1688, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sunday-review/25PUERTORICO/25PUERTORICO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/25/sunday-review/25PUERTORICO/25PUERTORICO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/sunday-review/25PUERTORICO/25PUERTORICO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Puerto Rico Be America’s 51st State?', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Will Puerto Rico Be America’s 51st State?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puerto Ricans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Munoz Marin, Luis (1898-1980)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Munoz Rivera, Luis (1859-1916)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Puerto Rico', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T19:11:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Royston Patterson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'Royston', 'lastname': 'Patterson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bb542dc-7e24-5377-94b7-e41bb99d2efc', 'word_count': 1538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bb542dc-7e24-5377-94b7-e41bb99d2efc'}, {'abstract': 'An enlightened approach already being used in several states gives patients more say in the medical interventions they want.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/opinion/sunday/end-of-life-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'An enlightened approach already being used in several states gives patients more say in the medical interventions they want.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three years ago, at the height of the debate over health care reform, there was an uproar over a voluntary provision that encouraged doctors to discuss with Medicare patients the kinds of treatments they would want as they neared the end of life. That thoughtful provision was left out of the final bill after right-wing commentators and Republican politicians denounced it falsely as a step toward euthanasia and “death panels.” ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Care at the End of Life', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Care at the End of Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Living Wills and Health Care Proxies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gundersen Lutheran Health System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wisconsin Medical Society', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T19:12:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/14ab5c23-f2ec-5a56-91ed-653456cfea7e', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14ab5c23-f2ec-5a56-91ed-653456cfea7e'}, {'abstract': 'I found myself in a sort of Paradise. But I was quickly exiled by my own mind.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/24/the-snake-in-the-garden/', 'snippet': 'I found myself in a sort of Paradise. But I was quickly exiled by my own mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once upon a time a friend told me about a retreat house in the hills of California. I drove three hours north from my mother’s home and came upon an 800-acre spread, with golden pampas grass tumbling down to a great expanse of blue 1,200 feet below. The place was radiantly silent — save for bells tolling three or four times a day — and I was so far from telephone and laptop that I could lose myself for hours in anything at all, or nothing. At dusk, deer stepped into my private garden to graze; an hour later, I stepped out of my room and found myself under an overturned saltshaker of stars.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Snake in the Garden', 'kicker': 'Anxiety', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Snake in the Garden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T19:15:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pico Iyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pico', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Iyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/317228dc-0959-51b1-b9cf-9c851f1abcf8', 'word_count': 1300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/317228dc-0959-51b1-b9cf-9c851f1abcf8'}, {'abstract': 'Jeremy Lin faced the Knicks, the team with whom he became a sudden star, and found ways to contribute beyond scoring on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/24/lin-plays-a-different-role-with-the-rockets/', 'snippet': 'Jeremy Lin faced the Knicks, the team with whom he became a sudden star, and found ways to contribute beyond scoring on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — The Rockets have the biggest center-hung indoor video scoreboard in the United States, unveiling it at Toyota Center this month. The two sideline-facing screens are 58 feet long, stretching between the free-throw lines, and offer production videos, live action and replays.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Like Address, Lin’s Game Has Changed', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lin, Jeremy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Rockets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T19:17:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6825883-c09d-56ff-b9d2-c46cfe9fe8ab', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6825883-c09d-56ff-b9d2-c46cfe9fe8ab'}, {'abstract': 'Even with subsidized premiums, many homeowners drop their flood insurance, thinking it’s a bad investment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/opinion/sunday/paying-for-future-catastrophes.html', 'snippet': 'Even with subsidized premiums, many homeowners drop their flood insurance, thinking it’s a bad investment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Philadelp