ddlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yezzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c9e461d-edac-548e-8e50-33c908effab8', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c9e461d-edac-548e-8e50-33c908effab8'}, {'abstract': 'An economist imagines a debate between two President Obamas — one liberal, one moderate — as Washington aims to avoid hitting a fiscal wall at year-end.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/business/a-liberal-obama-vs-a-moderate-obama-in-the-fiscal-debate.html', 'snippet': 'An economist imagines a debate between two President Obamas — one liberal, one moderate — as Washington aims to avoid hitting a fiscal wall at year-end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THROUGHOUT Washington, policy makers are debating \xa0how\xa0to avoid hitting a wall on Jan. 1, when\xa0large and abrupt tax\xa0increases and spending cuts\xa0will take effect automatically unless Congress acts. The debate is perhaps no more fervent than it is inside the head of our newly re-elected president, who must now decide what kind of policy leader he will become, both in this confrontation and throughout\xa0 his second term.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/business/25-VIEW/25-VIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/business/25-VIEW/25-VIEW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/business/25-VIEW/25-VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType