 Chen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — The title of today’s puzzle should give you a decent tip-off about the theme, but it’ll become apparent soon after you start solving. A good sign that you’ve stumbled onto a theme answer is that the letters that fit will feel incomplete and frustrating. Take that as a positive development. Your frustration will quickly turn to satisfaction, because once you topple the first one, the rest will fall like dominoes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Little Extra', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T23:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Gaffney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gaffney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/525c0d0d-a1f6-5b75-b2f5-87e087f2c16d', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/525c0d0d-a1f6-5b75-b2f5-87e087f2c16d'}, {'abstract': 'Preparing for the 50th anniversary of John F. Kennedy’s assassination, Dallas plans to recreate the art exhibition that was hung in the president and the first lady’s Fort Worth hotel suite in 1963.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/us/the-artworks-john-f-kennedy-saw-in-texas-on-nov-21-1963.html', 'snippet': 'Preparing for the 50th anniversary of John F. Kennedy’s assassination, Dallas plans to recreate the art exhibition that was hung in the president and the first lady’s Fort Worth hotel suite in 1963.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In November 1963, in anticipation of President John F. Kennedy’s visit to Texas, a group of Fort Worth cultural leaders hatched a plan to both honor the president and upend their city’s reputation as a sleepy, unsophisticated backwater. They brought together a collection of locally owned artwork and mounted a mini-exhibit inside the president’s suite at the Hotel Texas in downtown Fort Worth, where he spent the night on Nov. 21, 1963. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/us/25TTCulture/25TTCulture-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 698, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/us/25TTCulture/25TTCulture-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1396, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Girding for Anniversary of Tragedy in Dallas', 'kicker': 'Texas Monthly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Girding for Anniversary Of Tragedy in Dallas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dallas (Tex)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, John Fitzgerald', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-24T23:27:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Kelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3cbfedf-3a88-5313-baa2-a58371f6667c', 'word_count': 889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3cbfedf-3a88-5313-baa2-a58371f6667c'}, {'abstract': 'Between 2000 and 2004, five companies affiliated with Cheng Yu-tung and his New World Group acquired 20 percent of Ping An’s stock.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/business/global/another-big-stake-in-ping-an-hidden-in-a-hong-kong-investment.html', 'snippet': 'Between 2000 and 2004, five companies affiliated with Cheng Yu-tung and his New World Group acquired 20 percent of Ping An’s stock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The main connection to Ping An for relatives of Wen Jiabao was through their stakes in a company based in the prime minister’s hometown, Tianjin, in northern China. But there was also apparently a Hong Kong connection.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/world/china-sidebar/china-sidebar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 893, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/world/china-sidebar/china-sidebar-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1388, 'width': 1211, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/world/china-sidebar/china-sidebar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/25/world/china-sidebar/china-sidebar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/25/world/china-sidebar/china-sidebar-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Big Stake in Ping An, Hidden in a Hong Kong Investment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline'