'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b414e00b-28e3-5a80-83c5-79eb83052eea', 'word_count': 858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b414e00b-28e3-5a80-83c5-79eb83052eea'}, {'abstract': 'The jet was put into service in September after years of construction work and is seen by many as a symbol of China’s military modernization.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/world/asia/china-lands-jet-on-its-first-aircraft-carrier.html', 'snippet': 'The jet was put into service in September after years of construction work and is seen by many as a symbol of China’s military modernization.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — The Chinese military has successfully landed a fighter jet on the Liaoning, China’s first aircraft carrier, according to a report on Sunday by Xinhua, the state news agency.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Regional Tensions Rise, China Lands Jet on First Carrier', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Regional Tensions Rise, China Lands Jet on First Carrier', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xinhua', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aircraft Carriers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-25T22:44:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92462834-ffbd-5a74-b375-caa6e7d52daa', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92462834-ffbd-5a74-b375-caa6e7d52daa'}, {'abstract': 'Production will soon move ahead for a fourth season, to consist of eight new episodes and a Christmas special, the BBC reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/arts/television/theres-no-stopping-downton-abbey.html', 'snippet': 'Production will soon move ahead for a fourth season, to consist of eight new episodes and a Christmas special, the BBC reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fans of the popular British drama “Downton Abbey,” who are anticipating Season 3 premiere on Jan. 6 in the United States, now have even more Crawley family intrigues to look forward to (below, Dan Stevens as Matthew Crawley and Michelle Dockery as Lady Mary). Production will soon move ahead for a fourth season, to consist of eight new episodes and a Christmas special, the BBC reported. The British television channel ITV confirmed the news on Friday, and Gareth Neame, an executive producer, said that some characters would return, although he did not specify. Filming will begin in February with a scheduled premiere for the fall in Britain. PBS, which carries the show in the United States, has not said when the fourth season will be shown.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'There’s No Stopping ‘Downton Abbey’', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'There’s No Stopping ‘Downton Abbey’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Downton Abbey (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-25T22:50:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/54c956e2-b346-5c56-ab1c-6c1a2f8b44b0', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54c956e2-b346-5c56-ab1c-6c1a2f8b44b0'}, {'abstract': 'Rebels claimed to have seized three crucial installations and 11 mobile antiaircraft guns, demonstrating their ability to advance in areas around the capital despite facing aerial attacks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/world/middleeast/syrian-rebels-said-to-have-seized-military-airport.html', 'snippet': 'Rebels claimed to have seized three crucial installations and 11 mobile antiaircraft guns, demonstrating their ability to advance in areas around the capital despite facing aerial attacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Syrian rebels said they seized an important military airport and an air defense base just outside Damascus on Sunday, adding to a monthlong string of tactical successes — capturing bases, disrupting supply routes and seizing weaponry — that demonstrate their ability to erode the government’s dominance despite facing withering aerial attacks. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/world/middleeast/26syria/26syria-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 322, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/world/middleeast/26syria/26syria-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 322, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rebels Claim They Seized Air Bases in Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rebels Claim They Seized Air Bases In Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Skype Technologies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Bases and Installations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-25T22:50:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard and C. J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b9cd2ed-ff68-5679-b8e1-80a1dda8007d', 'word_count': 1149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b9cd2ed-ff68-5679-b8e1-80a1dda8007d'}, {'abstract': 'The Times is starting a new online feature Monday to follow the talks between President Obama and Congressional leaders over the so-called fiscal cliff.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/debt-reckoning-the-fiscal-deadline-in-washington/', 'snippet': 'The Times is starting a new online feature Monday to follow the talks between President Obama and Congressional leaders over the so-called fiscal cliff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times is starting a new online feature on Monday to follow the talks between President Obama and Congressional leaders over the so-called fiscal cliff. In the weeks ahead we will use this space to track developments from the White House and Capitol Hill, explain the major economic and fiscal issues, examine public opinion and analyze the options that the parties are considering, among other things. Follow along at Debt Reckoning: The Fiscal Deadline in Washington. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debt Reckoning: The Fiscal Deadline in Washington', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-25T22:52:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08960978-1419-5d4a-b41c-1fc212e3765a', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08960978-1419-5d4a-b41c-1fc212e3765a'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Corden has agreed to play the lead role in “School for Santas,” a Christmas movie to begin shooting in New York and London early next year.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/a-starring-role-for-james-corden/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Corden has agreed to play the lead role in “School for Santas,” a Christmas movie to begin shooting in New York and London early next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s truly no resting on his laurels for the British actor James Corden. Following his Tony Award-winning turn on Broadway in the comedy “One Man, Two Guvnors,” Mr. Corden, 34, has agreed to play the lead role in “School for Santas,” a Christmas movie to begin shooting in New York and London early next year. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Starring Role for James Corden', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Starring Role For James Corden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bean, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corden, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-25T22:58:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/866c84c1-c8c9-5a4d-a739-88c1677467fd', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/866c84c1-c8c9-5a4d-a739-88c1677467fd'}, {'abstract': 'The ad from the Human Rights Campaign enlists the actor Morgan Freeman, hoping to capitalize on recent victories at the polls for same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/after-success-on-same-sex-marriage-gay-rights-group-uses-ad-to-keep-pressure-on/', 'snippet': 'The ad from the Human Rights Campaign enlists the actor Morgan Freeman, hoping to capitalize on recent victories at the polls for same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What do you do when, after more than 30 defeats in a row, you win four votes, all on the same Election Day? The answer for an organization seeking equality for gay men and lesbians is to run a television commercial that celebrates the victories while at the same time looking beyond them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Success on Same-Sex Marriage, Gay Rights Group Uses Ad to Keep Pressure On', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freeman, Morgan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Campaign', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-25T22:59:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70cfca61-44e1-5f3d-99c6-8cc70cc7c03b', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70cfca61-44e1-5f3d-99c6-8cc70cc7c03b'}, {'abstract': 'A scrumptious Monday from Ed Sessa.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/25/to-your-health/', 'snippet': 'A scrumptious Monday from Ed Sessa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONDAY’S PUZZLE — Hope you came hungry for this culinary-themed Monday puzzle by Ed Sessa, which feels like comfort food after a set of challenging weekend puzzles. The grid contains numerous clues and answers pertaining to a smorgasbord of foods. Dig in.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Your Health!', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-2