uhammad, No Regret', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Benghazi (Libya)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Innocence of Muslims (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nakoula, Nakoula Basseley', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T02:03:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Serge F. Kovaleski and Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Serge', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Kovaleski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77009e10-8737-51df-a241-ff944824904f', 'word_count': 2421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77009e10-8737-51df-a241-ff944824904f'}, {'abstract': 'Owls always appear as a shape, a swift, peripheral presence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/opinion/the-owlish-night.html', 'snippet': 'Owls always appear as a shape, a swift, peripheral presence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m driving in the last of the dusk, bare trees on both sides of the road. A bird form slants silently across the highway, just above the arc of the headlights. Impossible to say what color it is, but it is an owl. It is all I ever see of owls up around my farm, that swift, peripheral, ghosting drift across an opening in the trees. Every time I see one I remember the great gray owl that I saw years ago above a hilly dirt road just before dawn in southern Montana. It was as though a cumulonimbus cloud had been compressed into bird shape and given stern yellow eyes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Owlish Night', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The Rural Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Owlish Night', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Owls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T02:07:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verlyn Klinkenborg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verlyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klinkenborg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e0587a7-3eb4-59c4-8b6e-9ac24e0fe639', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e0587a7-3eb4-59c4-8b6e-9ac24e0fe639'}, {'abstract': 'Sooner or later, the Knicks of New York and the Nets of Brooklyn will do something worth chanting about.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/sports/basketball/knicks-nets-will-turn-into-a-rivalry-to-join-new-yorks-rich-past.html', 'snippet': 'Sooner or later, the Knicks of New York and the Nets of Brooklyn will do something worth chanting about.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Is Brooklyn still in the league?” — Bill Terry, manager, New York Giants, 1934', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 's