1-2-billion-in-barclays-warrants/', 'snippet': 'Qatar Holding had acquired the warrants, which are financial instruments that can be exchanged for stock, during the 2008 financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The sovereign wealth fund Qatar Holding said on Monday that it had sold its remaining warrants in Barclays in a deal that has led to a $1.2 billion share sale in the British bank.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Qatar Holding Sells Barclays Warrants Worth $1.2 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sovereign Wealth Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Qatar Investment Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T12:13:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ab3b8de-156f-533a-b4df-f8eb19f7c5fb', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ab3b8de-156f-533a-b4df-f8eb19f7c5fb'}, {'abstract': 'The idea of hospice care in one’s home is overwhelming, but it can bring its own rewards, too.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/turning-a-home-into-a-hospital/', 'snippet': 'The idea of hospice care in one’s home is overwhelming, but it can bring its own rewards, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At age 96, my mother moved to New York City to live with me and my family in our two-bedroom Manhattan apartment after becoming increasingly isolated while living alone in Florida. She moved into my sons’ bedroom surrounded by all manner of adolescent paraphernalia, including every style of trendy sneakers, a giant papier-mâché statue of Michael Jordan and a poster of Bob Marley.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turning a Home Into a Hospital', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospice Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T12:55:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda G. Beeler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Beeler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d20d5caf-ddbf-5760-81a9-c2e247b29f4b', 'word_count': 1206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d20d5caf-ddbf-5760-81a9-c2e247b29f4b'}, {'abstract': 'One proposal being floated as an alternative to raising the top marginal rate would place its heaviest tax burden on the somewhat wealthy as opposed to the very wealthy.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/congressional-proposal-could-create-bubble-in-tax-code/', 'snippet': 'One proposal being floated as an alternative to raising the top marginal rate would place its heaviest tax burden on the somewhat wealthy as opposed to the very wealthy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The coming Congressional debate over fiscal policy is sure to feature a wide array of proposals, some of which would hit certain taxpayers harder than others.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congressional Proposal Could Create ‘Bubble’ in Tax Code', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Congressional Proposal Could Create ‘Tax Bubble’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T13:10:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15e3e9e0-808c-5ac6-a428-a1fe0657dce9', 'word_count': 1373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15e3e9e0-808c-5ac6-a428-a1fe0657dce9'}, {'abstract': 'The Onex Corporation of Canada agreed on Monday to buy USI, an insurance brokerage firm, from a Goldman Sachs private equity fund for $2.3 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/onex-to-buy-usi-an-insurance-broker-for-2-3-billion/', 'snippet': 'The Onex Corporation of Canada agreed on Monday to buy USI, an insurance brokerage firm, from a Goldman Sachs private equity fund for $2.3 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Onex Corporation of Canada agreed on Monday to buy USI, an insurance brokerage firm, from a Goldman Sachs private equity fund for $2.3 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Onex to Buy USI, an Insurance Broker, for $2.3 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Onex Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T13:14:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0f7716e-751c-5ce3-97fc-07b8da75c9df', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0f7716e-751c-5ce3-97fc-07b8da75c9df'}, {'abstract': 'Focusing on perpetual Jets failure makes for a great narrative, and it’s certainly an easy one, but there’s one problem: the history and the reality don’t support it.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/debunking-the-same-old-jets-myth/', 'snippet': 'Focusing on perpetual Jets failure makes for a great narrative, and it’s certainly an easy one, but there’s one problem: the history and the reality don’t support it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s the season for the “Same Old Jets” remarks. Focusing on failure makes for a great narrative, especially after a loss of the magnitude of Thursday’s 49-19 shellacking by New England. As critics sharpen their knives, they will search for new ways to characterize the “hapless”\xa0 J-E-T-S, or\xa0 “Just End The Season,”\xa0 as they might say. It all sounds smarmy and smart, except for one thing: the history and the reality don’t support it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debunking the ‘Same Old Jets’ Myth', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T13:15:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Bretherton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bretherton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22661051-671c-50ae-981c-95df812fe3d1', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22661051-671c-50ae-981c-95df812fe3d1'}, {'abstract': 'The latest alumnus of SAC Capital Advisors is set to appear in federal court in Manhattan on Monday. | How the family of China’s prime minister grew wealthy from an investment in Ping An Insurance. | A trading loss at UBS has led to a fine of £29.7 million. | Qatar Holding has sold its remaining warrants in Barclays.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/former-sac-trader-to-appear-in-court/', 'snippet': 'The latest alumnus of SAC Capital Advisors is set to appear in federal court in Manhattan on Monday. | How the family of China’s prime minister grew wealthy from an investment in Ping An Insurance. | A trading loss at UBS has led to a fine of £29....', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mathew Martoma, the latest alumnus of SAC Capital Advisors to be accused of breaking the law, is set to appear in Federal District Court in Manhattan on Monday morning. The insider trading case against him “represents a watershed moment” in the government’s investigation of SAC Capital, as it links the hedge fund’s founder, Steven A. Cohen, to trading activity the government says was illegal, DealBook’s Peter Lattman reports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former SAC Trader to Appear in Court', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T13:22:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', '