hout her media empire, which includes a magazine, a cable TV network and an XM satellite radio channel, Christine Haughney writes. As Ms. Winfrey put it in an interview: “Obviously, the show was helping in ways that you know I hadn’t accounted for.” Still, there are signs of stability at the network. A new focus for Ms. Winfrey has been to lead her magazine — O, The Oprah Magazine — to a younger audience. Introduced in 2000, the magazine took off immediately, but its median audience age of 49 is significantly higher than some other women’s magazines.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Oprah Attempts to Right the Ship, and Libel Comes to Twitter', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clash, Kevin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McAlpine, Alistair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nakoula, Nakoula Basseley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Martha', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winfrey, Oprah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'O: The Oprah Magazine', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T14:46:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/191f283c-fe79-5158-a44d-9e24ce449331', 'word_count': 656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/191f283c-fe79-5158-a44d-9e24ce449331'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/what-were-reading-573/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GQ: “I reached for the cool-looking pinkish drink on the table and took a deep gulp, only to remember it was a michelada made of Bud Light spiked with smoked-clam juice, chile oil and a rim of more crushed chiles and Sichuan peppercorns,” writes Brett Martin in this great, gonzo profile of Danny Bowien from Mission Chinese Food. “I felt like a Looney Tunes character trying to quench the fire of a jalapeño with a nice draught of Tabasco. Peeling myself off the ceiling, I came down face-to-face with a leering bright-yellow forty-foot dragon.” … — Jeff Gordinier ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T14:47:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85759fc6-28d2-5110-bf92-c693a81575c1', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85759fc6-28d2-5110-bf92-c693a81575c1'}, {'abstract': 'McGraw-Hill agreed on Monday to sell its education division to Apollo Global Management for about $2.5 billion, completing the publisher’s transformation into a provider of high-end financial information.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/mcgraw-hill-to-sell-education-unit-to-apollo-for-2-5-billion/', 'snippet': 'McGraw-Hill agreed on Monday to sell its education division to Apollo Global Management for about $2.5 billion, completing the publisher’s transformation into a provider of high-end financial information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'McGraw-Hill agreed on Monday to sell its education division to Apollo Global Management for about $2.5 billion, completing the publisher’s transformation into a provider of high-end financial information.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McGraw-Hill to Sell Education Unit to Apollo for $2.5 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apollo Global Management', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McGraw-Hill Companies Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T15:07:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b09df369-a7fd-5e8e-ae71-822740987bcd', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b09df369-a7fd-5e8e-ae71-822740987bcd'}, {'abstract': 'Mary L. Schapiro announced on Monday that she was stepping down as chairwoman of the Securities and Exchange Commission. She will leave the agency better than she found it.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/schapiro-head-of-s-e-c-to-announce-departure/', 'snippet': 'Mary L. Schapiro announced on Monday that she was stepping down as chairwoman of the Securities and Exchange Commission. She will leave the agency better than she found it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mary L. Schapiro spent four years at the Securities and Exchange Commission trying to shake the regulator’s past.