 'snippet': 'Martha Rose Shulman provides five salads substantial enough to stand in for a main course.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanksgiving is over, the holiday season is close upon us and a week of salads for dinner is probably a good idea. If you still have leftover Thanksgiving turkey or vegetables in need of a home, composed salads fit that bill nicely. I began working on this week’s recipes with leftover turkey in mind, though I tested the recipes that call for it with chicken breast tenders that I cooked in my wok: I seasoned the chicken with kosher salt, heated the wok over high heat, added a little canola oil – about a tablespoon -- and cooked the chicken tenders for about 3 to 4 minutes a side. When they were cool I shredded them and used them in a November Recipes for Health rendition of a Cobb salad (no bacon, and carrots instead of tomatoes). I also used the chicken in a spinach salad and made it optional in a sweet potato and kale salad.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/26recipehealth/26recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/27/science/26recipehealth/26recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/26recipehealth/26recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/26recipehealth/26recipehealth-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1278, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/26recipehealth/26recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/27/science/26recipehealth/26recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/26recipehealth/26recipehealth-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Feast, Salads Take Center Stage', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T16:29:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba85b95a-af08-5a98-acec-f3a87eb09771', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba85b95a-af08-5a98-acec-f3a87eb09771'}, {'abstract': 'Angel Haze shares lyrical quirks and aesthetic tics with the indie rappers of the moment, but the 21-year-old is already transcending those ranks.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/timely-native-voice/', 'snippet': 'Angel Haze shares lyrical quirks and aesthetic tics with the indie rappers of the moment, but the 21-year-old is already transcending those ranks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Angel Haze shares lyrical quirks and aesthetic tics with the indie rappers of the moment: Azealia Banks, Sasha Go Hard, Zebra Katz. But the 21-year-old Raee’n Wahya (her Cherokee name) is already transcending those ranks. If anything she’s more like Nicki Minaj, with her big ambitions and knack for rhyme, although Wahya decided early on she wouldn’t rely on gimmicks or a hypersexualized image. She rants against misogyny, trumpets her heritage and is honest about herself — nearly to a fault. In late October she released “Cleaning Out My Closet,” divulging details of her childhood sexual abuse, which she survived in part by taking inspiration from Eminem, to whom the song is a brilliant tribute. Next year, Wahya will begin an international tour, release several EPs and videos — including one for her biggest hit, “New York” — and cut her first full album, which will be more melodic. “I’m not a rapper, I’m a rock star,” she says. “I just wanna work hard. Taylor Swift’s my archnemesis.” Really? “Nah, I love her. I wanna be like her.” ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '166', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Timely | Native Voice', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Native Voice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haze, Angel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T16:35:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacob Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b27efe0-985f-50ce-82ae-b82dab332396', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b27efe0-985f-50ce-82ae-b82dab332396'}, {'abstract': 'United States military planners are drawing up broad outlines of a force that would remain in Afghanistan after 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/asia/100000001923189/americas-future-role-in-afgha