or greater TV ratings – by changing up its rules regularly, most notably by allowing up to 10 best-picture nominees in recent years. This season, the Academy also saw fit to move up the dates for nominations: voting will now start Dec. 17, instead of later in the month as before, and the choices will be announced on Jan. 10, nearly two weeks earlier than normal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the New Oscar Schedule Is Reshaping Campaigns', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hooper, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACADEMY OF MOTION PICTURE ARTS AND SCIENCES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PricewaterhouseCoopers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T17:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0e9ddb2-333c-5265-8c91-63a407973a2f', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0e9ddb2-333c-5265-8c91-63a407973a2f'}, {'abstract': 'Can you find the elegant solution to this puzzle from award-winning mathematician Steven Strogatz’s new book “The Joy of x”?', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/joy-of-x/', 'snippet': 'Can you find the elegant solution to this puzzle from award-winning mathematician Steven Strogatz’s new book “The Joy of x”?', 'lead_paragraph': 'We have a special treat this week and next: puzzles from Steven Strogatz‘s “The Joy of x,” the recently-released book based on Dr. Strogatz’s popular New York Times Opinionator Series “The Elements of Math.” (“The Elements of Math,” in case you missed it, is Dr. Strogatz’ 15-part series on mathematics from “the basic to the baffling” that ran back in early 2010.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steven Strogatz and The Joy of x', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strogatz, Steven', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T17:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3793e71c-f68d-5651-a99f-01d61f03a77b', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3793e71c-f68d-5651-a99f-01d61f03a77b'}, {'abstract': 'Some exercises, like hyperventilation-reduction techniques and yoga breathing exercises, can help asthmatics, a comprehensive review finds.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/really-breathing-exercises-can-relieve-asthma/', 'snippet': 'Some exercises, like hyperventilation-reduction techniques and yoga breathing exercises, can help asthmatics, a comprehensive review finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE FACTS', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 529, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo'