hip/', 'snippet': 'The event, which takes a cue from the “upfronts” for TV, will be administered by the Interactive Advertising Bureau, reducing the role of the digital advertising agency Digitas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Interactive Advertising Bureau, a trade organization for the digital advertising industry, announced on Monday that it would lead the second annual Digital Content Newfronts in April. The conference takes its cue from the television “upfronts” in May, when broadcast and cable networks show off their new offerings to advertisers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Digital ‘Upfronts’ to Be Given New Leadership', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Upfronts (Television)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Digitas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interactive Advertising Bureau', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T19:02:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d99c880-1c5d-5fdb-b403-fa58b30abfa7', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d99c880-1c5d-5fdb-b403-fa58b30abfa7'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers found that subjects with low blood levels of vitamin D were more likely to develop diabetes than those with higher levels.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/low-vitamin-d-level-tied-to-type-1-diabetes/', 'snippet': 'Researchers found that subjects with low blood levels of vitamin D were more likely to develop diabetes than those with higher levels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new study has found a strong correlation between low vitamin D blood levels and Type 1 diabetes.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/21/health/well_patterns/well_patterns-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/21/health/well_patterns/well_patterns-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/21/health/well_patterns/well_patterns-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/05/21/health/well_patterns/well_patterns-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/21/health/well_patterns/well_patterns-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Low Vitamin D Level Tied to Type 1 Diabetes', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Patterns: Low Vitamin D Level Tied to Type 1 Diabetes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vitamin D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T19:03:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8f2e879-beb1-5fba-a0d7-7f2bb43da69a', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8f2e879-beb1-5fba-a0d7-7f2bb43da69a'}, {'abstract': 'Judges generally don’t like it when they are described as political creatures, but there is no getting around it: the party of the president who appoints them is a good predictor of how they will rule.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/us/judges-rulings-follow-partisan-lines.html', 'snippet': 'Judges generally don’t like it when they are described as political creatures, but there is no getting around it: the party of the president who appoints them is a good predictor of how they will rule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A couple of weeks ago, a federal appeals court ruled that voters in Michigan could not ban racial preferences in admissions to the state’s public universities. The ruling struck some people as curious (“a state does not deny equal treatment by mandating it,” a dissenting judge wrote), but that is not today’s topic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/us/BAR1/BAR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 629, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/us/BAR1/BAR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 629, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/us/BAR1/BAR1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 1