k': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Brennan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brennan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f8ea705-d4e8-50d4-89d9-d8ee56a905cf', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f8ea705-d4e8-50d4-89d9-d8ee56a905cf'}, {'abstract': 'With five games to go in the regular season, no division is tied and the leaders of five of the eight divisions have at least a three-game cushion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/sports/football/parity-takes-a-break-in-division-races.html', 'snippet': 'With five games to go in the regular season, no division is tied and the leaders of five of the eight divisions have at least a three-game cushion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Ray Rice caught a dump-off pass just a few steps past the line of scrimmage Sunday and turned it into the greatest display of individual effort this season — crossing the field and then lunging to convert on fourth-and-29 in the fourth quarter — he did more than power the Baltimore Ravens’ come-from-behind victory over the San Diego Chargers. He essentially slammed the door on two division races at once, siphoned most of the drama from the A.F.C. and cast doubt on the idea that parity is still the primary underpinning of the N.F.L.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/sports/football/27forward-pic/27forward-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/27/sports/football/27forward-pic/27forward-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/sports/football/27forward-pic/27forward-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/sports/football/27forward-pic/27forward-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1426, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/sports/football/27forward-pic/27forward-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/27/sports/football/27forward-pic/27forward-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/sports/football/27forward-pic/27forward-pic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Division Races, Parity Takes a Holiday, for Now', 'kicker': 'N.F.L. Fast Forward', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Division Races, Parity Takes a Holiday, for Now', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaepernick, Colin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Diego Chargers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Ray', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Ravens', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T19:20:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b54cdec-098e-5b5c-9d4f-1b9c5ab2b9be', 'word_count': 1161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b54cdec-098e-5b5c-9d4f-1b9c5ab2b9be'}, {'abstract': 'Should universities be government-funded basic services, like roads and hospitals? Or should they be market driven? If so, will only big-name, elite schools draw moneyed donors and rich students?', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/universities-ponder-accounting-101-how-to-balance-the-books/', 'snippet': 'Should universities be government-funded basic services, like roads and hospitals? Or should they be market driven? If so, will only big-name, elite schools draw moneyed donors and rich students?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s considered an impolite topic in some scholarly circles, where academics would rather talk about resources or funding than say the “m” word. But the reality is that academia needs money to survive. Whatever a school’s goals are—giving a chance to poor students, encouraging better teaching, driving great research—someone has to pay.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Universities Ponder Accounting 101: How to Balance the Books', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University College London', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T19:29:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Lau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/975301e0-8fb9-5916-bb5f-056a48a8effc', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/975301e0-8fb9-5916-bb5f-056a48a8effc'}, {'abstract': 'The documentary is scheduled to be shown on Feb. 16.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/hbo-buys-revealing-film-about-beyonc-made-by-beyonc/', 'snippet': 'The documentary is scheduled to be shown on Feb. 16.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HBO has bought the rights to a documentary about the pop star Beyoncé Knowles directed and produced by none other than … Beyoncé Knowles. No wonder, then, that it’s being billed as “intimate” and “revealing,” with “unprecedented access,” as a news release from the cable network put it on Monday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'HBO Buys ‘Revealing’ Film about Beyoncé, Made by Beyoncé', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beyoncé on Beyoncé: HBO Buys Documentary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knowles, Beyonce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T19:33:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d3d53ea-9b17-5834-a699-1b5c144fab08', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d3d53ea-9b17-5834-a699-1b5c144fab08'}, {'abstract': 'The agenda at Doha will focus on firming up pledges that had been negotiated in the summit meetings of the past few years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/business/energy-environment/un-climate-talks-promise-little-drama.html', 'snippet': 'The agenda at Doha will focus on firming up pledges that had been negotiated in the summit meetings of the past few years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The last three United Nations climate change summit meetings have been disorderly affairs, marked by brinkmanship, breakdowns and a weary sense that there has to be a better way to address the intensifying challenge of a simmering planet.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/business/energy-environment/27iht-rbog-cop/27iht-rbog-cop-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/27/business/energy-environment/27iht-rbog-cop/27iht-rbog-cop-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/business/energy-environment/27iht-rbog-cop/27iht-rbog-cop-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/business/energy-environment/27iht-rbog-cop/27iht-rbog-cop-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1347, 'width': 2048, 'su