n': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3549f553-d9dc-5aac-84bd-3b57f8ecc8d7', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3549f553-d9dc-5aac-84bd-3b57f8ecc8d7'}, {'abstract': 'As President Obama and Congress scrape for ways to raise tax revenue without hurting middle-income families or pushing up rates, the mortgage interest deduction may be part of the discussion.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/mortgage-interest-deduction-once-a-sacred-cow-is-seen-as-vulnerable/', 'snippet': 'As President Obama and Congress scrape for ways to raise tax revenue without hurting middle-income families or pushing up rates, the mortgage interest deduction may be part of the discussion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A tax break that has long been untouchable could soon be in for some serious scrutiny.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mortgage Interest Deduction, Once a Sacred Cow, Is Under Scrutiny', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tax Break Once Sacred Is Now Seen As Vulnerable', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Realtors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T19:46:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55e2761a-dc76-590a-907d-d43982c92a10', 'word_count': 1119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55e2761a-dc76-590a-907d-d43982c92a10'}, {'abstract': 'The parade of discarded coaches includes Gene Chizik of Auburn, Colorado’s Jon Embree, North Carolina State’s Tom O’Brien and Boston College’s Frank Spaziani and Danny Hope of Purdue.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/firing-season-claims-auburns-chizik-two-years-from-championship/', 'snippet': 'The parade of discarded coaches includes Gene Chizik of Auburn, Colorado’s Jon Embree, North Carolina State’s Tom O’Brien and Boston College’s Frank Spaziani and Danny Hope of Purdue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s tempting to compare college football with its professional counterpart on an average day, but the gap just got a little bit smaller on Sunday when Auburn pulled the plug on Coach Gene Chizik. Yes, Chizik’s team went 3-9 and lost to Georgia and Alabama by a combined score of 87-0. But two years ago, he was also hoisting the crystal trophy as the Bowl Championship Series winner, riding the talents of quarterback Cam Newton to the highest spot in his sport.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/sports/ncaafootball/26gene/26gene-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/sports/ncaafootball/26gene/26gene-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/sports/ncaafootball/26gene/26gene-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'l