by the beautiful, eerie world of Dare Wright. I loved her books and the uneasy feeling they gave me.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/haunted-by-the-lonely-doll/', 'snippet': 'As a child, I was fascinated by the beautiful, eerie world of Dare Wright. I loved her books and the uneasy feeling they gave me.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Then one morning Edith looked into the garden and there stood two bears!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Haunted by ‘The Lonely Doll’', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Symbols and Symbolism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Dare', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T19:52:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89e7fa16-623a-5c88-9270-c06f372c5379', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89e7fa16-623a-5c88-9270-c06f372c5379'}, {'abstract': 'The right pot, a small pit, some rocks and a lot of time combine to make baked beans with a big flavor payoff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/dining/who-needs-an-oven-just-bury-your-beans.html', 'snippet': 'The right pot, a small pit, some rocks and a lot of time combine to make baked beans with a big flavor payoff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE morning a couple of months ago, my friend and frequent co-author Chris Schlesinger called me. “You have to come look at my new bean hole,” he said.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/dining/28BEANS1_SPAN/28BEANS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/28/dining/28BEANS1_SPAN/28BEANS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/dining/28BEANS1_SPAN/1128-BEANS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/dining/28BEANS1_SPAN/1128-BEANS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/dining/28BEANS1_SPAN/28BEANS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/28/dining/28BEANS1_SPAN/28BEANS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/dining/28BEANS1_SPAN/28BEANS1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Needs an Oven? Just Bury Your Beans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Needs an Oven? Just Bury Your Beans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T19:58:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Willoughby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Willoughby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bffbbc92-749c-525e-a05d-10e4ceb795f9', 'word_count': 1158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bffbbc92-749c-525e-a05d-10e4ceb795f9'}, {'abstract': 'A great salad to make with leftover roasted sweet potatoes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/health/roasted-sweet-potato-and-crispy-kale-salad-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'A great salad to make with leftover roasted sweet potatoes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is a great salad to make with leftover roasted sweet potatoes but you can also roast them just to make the salad. The trick to succeeding with crispy kale is to make sure it is completely dry before you put it in the oven. If you are using bunched kale I recommend that you stem and wash it, spin it twice in a salad spinner, then set the leaves in single layers on a few layers of paper towels and roll them up. You can then refrigerate for up to a day or two. Once the salad is assembled, the portion of kale that you toss with the sweet potatoes will soften, and the kale that surrounds the sweet potatoes will remain crispy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/29recipehealth/29recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/27/science/29recipehealth/29recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/29recipehealth/29recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/29recipehealth/29recipehealth-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1345, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/29recipehealth/29recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/27/science/29recipehealth/29recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/29recipehealth/29recipehealth-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Roasted Sweet Potato and Crispy Kale Salad With Roquefort Dressing', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T20:03:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/510c30eb-c648-5756-80dc-5919e83c926d', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/510c30eb-c648-5756-80dc-5919e83c926d'}, {'abstract': 'Bonuses for associates at the big law firm ranged from $10,000 for first-year associates to $60,000 for senior associates, according to a memo obtained by DealBook. Those numbers are a big bump from last year.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/cravath-announces-bonuses-for-its-associates/', 'snippet': 'Bonuses for associates at the big law firm ranged from $10,000 for first-year associates to $60,000 for senior associates, according to a memo obtained by DealBook. Those numbers are a big bump from last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year around this time, the heads of the country’s largest law firms weigh the size of year-end bonuses for their junior lawyers. And almost all ask the same question: What will Cravath pay?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cravath Sets the Tone for Law Firm Bonuses', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cravath Swaine & Moore', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T20:08:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f7a8b86-2cb5-5266-b253-06f6fef9f4f6', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f7a8b86-2cb5-5266-b253-06f6fef9f4f6'}, {'abstract': 'With the retirement of Senator Joseph I. Lieberman in January, John McCain and Lindsey Graham will lose the veneer of bipartisanship that helped their policy goals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/us/politics/liebermans-retirement-is-end-of-three-amigos.html', 'snippet': 'With the retirement of Senator Joseph I. Lieberman in January, John McCain and Lindsey Graham will lose the veneer of bipartisanship that helped their policy goals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — For over a decade, the bipartisan trio of senators traveled the world together, from war-torn Iraq to security conferences in Germany to the remote kingdom of Bhutan. Their hawkish world views often placed them at odds with their respective parties, but together they secured a place at the center of every major foreign policy debate.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/us/AMIGOS/AMIGOS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/us/AMIGOS/AMIGOS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/us/AMIGOS/AMIGOS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/27/us/AMIGOS/AMIGOS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/us/AMIGOS/AMIGOS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Foreign Policy’s Bipartisan Trio Becomes Republican Duo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Foreign Policy’s Bipartisan Trio Becomes Republican Duo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lieberman, Joseph I', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Lindsey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T20:09:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1fc9ddb-68e3-5964-8d2b-bf4fdd61d23c', 'word_count': 1267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1fc9ddb-68e3-5964-8d2b-bf4fdd61d23c'}, {'abstract': 'An important mystery.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/whats-the-matter-with-italy/', 'snippet': 'An important mystery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sorry about radio silence — real life intruded. Also, working on longer-term projects; including one that had me looking at a pretty big puzzle that isn’t getting much attention, namely, what is going on with Italy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s The Matter With Italy?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T20:12:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41794e53-2413-5fa8-b464-a60db87e03e9', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41794e53-2413-5fa8-b464-a60db87e03e9'}, {'abstract': 'Served with baked tofu “fingers,” this salad can hold all the leftover vegetables from your Thanksgiving feast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/health/asian-chopped-salad-with-seasoned-tofu-fingers-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'Served with baked tofu “fingers,” this salad can hold all the leftover vegetables from your Thanksgiving feast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I like to serve the baked seasoned tofu “fingers” warm on top of the salad. They are delicious cold, too; it is worth making up a separate batch for the refrigerator. If you have an assortment of vegetables leftover from Thanksgiving dinner, throw them in!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/30recipehealth/30recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/27/science/30recipehealth/30recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/30recipehealth/30recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/30recipehealth/30recipehealth-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1316, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/30recipehealth/30recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/27/science/30recipehealth/30recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg