he Muslim Brotherhood canceled plans for a large demonstration in his support, signaling a chance to calm an escalating battle that has paralyzed a divided nation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeming Retreat by Egypt Leader on New Powers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeming Retreat By Egypt Leader On New Powers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T20:15:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick and Mayy El Sheikh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b474452c-e7a6-51d1-a512-1be9c841e63c', 'word_count': 1486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b474452c-e7a6-51d1-a512-1be9c841e63c'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. John J. Ross, a Harvard physician, has written a gripping and instructive collection of 10 medico-literary biographical sketches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/health/woe-is-syphilis-and-other-afflictions-of-famous-writers.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. John J. Ross, a Harvard physician, has written a gripping and instructive collection of 10 medico-literary biographical sketches.', 'lead_paragrap