own-ahmad-bradshaws-59-yard-screen/', 'snippet': 'In a big game against Green Bay, the play increased the Giants’ win probability from 55 percent to 67 percent in the blink of an eye.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With a game against the rejuvenated Washington Redskins on tap in Week 13, the Giants’ Sunday night matchup with the Green Bay Packers was quietly a huge game. A loss would have sent them reeling to 6-5 — just a game ahead of the Redskins and Dallas Cowboys in the division. Instead, the Giants dominated the Packers, maintaining a two-game lead in the division.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking Down Ahmad Bradshaw’s 59-Yard Screen', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradshaw, Ahmad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T20:27:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Bales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10c5b6a8-5bf6-5e95-8737-ae1999bbcb6e', 'word_count': 569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10c5b6a8-5bf6-5e95-8737-ae1999bbcb6e'}, {'abstract': 'Style may course through the veins of this Milan-based executive (her mother, Consuelo Castiglioni, is the designer of Marni), but she’s no fussy fashionista.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/profile-in-style-caroline-castiglioni/', 'snippet': 'Style may course through the veins of this Milan-based executive (her mother, Consuelo Castiglioni, is the designer of Marni), but she’s no fussy fashionista.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Style may course through the veins of this Milan-based executive (her mother, Consuelo Castiglioni, is the designer of Marni), but she’s no fussy fashionista. “I don’t like to follow the runway look,” she says. “I prefer to personalize it and make it my own.” Castiglioni, Marni’s director of special projects, applies the same individualistic aesthetic to the airy house she shares with her partner, Federico Ferrari, and their son, Filippo. A former ceramics factory in the Corso Magenta area, the whitewashed space serves as a neutral backdrop for the couple’s collection of midcentury furniture and objects. “When we renovated, our idea was to create a modern, clean environment for our favorite pieces.” And, of course, generous storage space for her extensive wardrobe, which contains mostly Marni (surprise!), with some Comme des Garçons and Vionnet thrown in for good measure.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '86', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Profile in Style | Carolina Castiglioni', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Carolina Castiglioni', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T20:35:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandra Ballentine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ballentine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccf5d03d-dfc2-57a5-9de6-7656b47d0625', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccf5d03d-dfc2-57a5-9de6-7656b47d0625'}, {'abstract': 'Nearly a quarter of survey respondents said their financial situation had improved this year.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/the-people-who-are-spending-more-this-season/', 'snippet': 'Nearly a quarter of survey respondents said their financial situation had improved this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Cyber Monday unfolds, consumers seem a bit more comfortable with spending this holiday season, according to an annual survey.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The People Who Are Spending More This Season', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T20:36:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f75c4e6a-541c-5f4c-ac37-b7282623ddbe', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f75c4e6a-541c-5f4c-ac37-b7282623ddbe'}, {'abstract': 'A 4-year-old girl at NewYork-Presbyterian Hospital got a new liver, flown in just in time as Hurricane Sandy hit the region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/health/amid-hurricane-sandy-a-race-to-get-a-liver-transplant.html', 'snippet': 'A 4-year-old girl at NewYork-Presbyterian Hospital got a new liver, flown in just in time as Hurricane Sandy hit the region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the best possible news, at the worst possible time.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/science/27TRAN_SPAN/27TRAN_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/27/science/27TRAN_SPAN/27TRAN_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xl