, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T20:43:24+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'Fritzie Andrade', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fritzie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Andrade', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/ede4d3e1-cdcf-593e-a395-87a59c076853', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/ede4d3e1-cdcf-593e-a395-87a59c076853'}, {'abstract': 'It’s common knowledge that Florida cut back on early voting in 2011 to reduce the turnout of blacks and other groups likely to vote for Democrats. But it’s refreshing to see that former top Republicans in the state are now saying so out loud.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/why-florida-really-changed-its-voting-rules/', 'snippet': 'It’s common knowledge that Florida cut back on early voting in 2011 to reduce the turnout of blacks and other groups likely to vote for Democrats. But it’s refreshing to see that former top Republicans in the state are now saying so out loud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s common knowledge that Florida cut back on early voting in 2011 to reduce the turnout of blacks and other groups likely to vote for Democrats. But it’s refreshing to see that former top Republicans in the state are now saying so out loud.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Florida Really Changed Its Voting Rules', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida’s Fake Fraud Claims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T20:46:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aca72feb-e66a-5beb-a236-156e7dbc6a45', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aca72feb-e66a-5beb-a236-156e7dbc6a45'}, {'abstract': 'Distinguished Concerts International New York performed Handel’s “Messiah”at Avery Fisher Hall on Sunday in an orchestration that led to a 40-year dispute.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/arts/music/messiah-a-perennial-returns-in-a-rare-form.html', 'snippet': 'Distinguished Concerts International New York performed Handel’s “Messiah”at Avery Fisher Hall on Sunday in an orchestration that led to a 40-year dispute.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Thanksgiving behind us, it is not just the shopping season that has commenced at full gush: “Messiah” season has arrived as well. It is nearly impossible to track every performance of this splendid, celebrated 1741 Handel oratorio in New York during a given year, but as far as I can tell, credit for the first arrival of 2012 goes to Distinguished Concerts International New York, a producing organization known for mounting choral extravaganzas with singers from around the world.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/arts/MESSIAH/MESSIAH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/arts/MESSIAH/MESSIAH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/arts/MESSIAH/MESSIAH-thumbStandard