ldy legacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week: psychiatrists rewrite their diagnostic bible, but still have problems with the personality disorder entries, and Superstorm Sandy’s moldy legacy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Science Times Podcast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mold', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychiatry and Psychiatrists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-26T20:52:03+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/a6eb7182-a64e-50ca-9a1f-943e266f5e1f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/a6eb7182-a64e-50ca-9a1f-943e266f5e1f'}, {'abstract': 'With “Jimmy’s End,” the world gets to watch the Watchman work.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/26/watchlist-alan-moore-tries-his-hand-at-an-on-screen-original/', 'snippet': 'With “Jimmy’s End,” the world gets to watch the Watchman work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alan Moore has been a big cheese in the comics world for 30 years, going back to his work on “Swamp Thing” and his creation of “V for Vendetta” in the early 1980s. But recently he’s been known less for his writing than for his carping: to the moviegoing public, at least, he’s the guy who’s never happy with the films made from his books. (Of James McTeigue’s “V for Vendetta”: “It’s a thwarted and frustrated and largely impotent American liberal fantasy.” Of Zack Snyder’s “Watchmen”: “The ‘Watchmen’ film sounds like more regurgitated worms.”)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headli