': 'nyt://article/43297d7c-1cb4-51eb-97ef-5d992ee09dac', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43297d7c-1cb4-51eb-97ef-5d992ee09dac'}, {'abstract': 'The Nets ground their way through four quarters and overtime to defeat the Knicks at Barclays Center in the teams’ first meeting. The intracity rivals are now tied for first place in their division.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/sports/basketball/nets-beat-knicks-in-overtime-in-first-meeting-as-intracity-rivals.html', 'snippet': 'The Nets ground their way through four quarters and overtime to defeat the Knicks at Barclays Center in the teams’ first meeting. The intracity rivals are now tied for first place in their division.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York turned on itself Monday night, its basketball loyalties divided and contorted and scattered about, its sanity tested and every breath exhausted until one word reverberated in the air.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nets Take First Meeting of New York City Teams', 'kicker': 'Nets 96, Knicks 89 (Overtime) ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Rivalry Comes To Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T03:34:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a99c820c-d083-5e8f-b28d-02b5bd7e12c3', 'word_count': 1156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a99c820c-d083-5e8f-b28d-02b5bd7e12c3'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on November 27, 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/pageoneplus/corrections-november-27-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on November 27, 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: November 27, 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T03:35:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72012918-c51a-5abf-9842-8ac74afa43b8', 'word_count': 765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72012918-c51a-5abf-9842-8ac74afa43b8'}, {'abstract': 'The unusual court order relates to $3,150 that Mayor Rob Ford solicited while a city councilor from lobbyists and corporations  for a private children’s football charity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/world/americas/judge-orders-toronto-mayor-to-leave-office.html', 'snippet': 'The unusual court order relates to $3,150 that Mayor Rob Ford solicited while a city councilor from lobbyists and corporations  for a private children’s football charity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A judge ordered Rob Ford, the mayor of Toronto, to step down on Monday after finding that he violated conflict of interest laws. The unusual court order against the mayor of Canada’s largest city relates to $3,150 that Mr. Ford solicited while a city councilor from lobbyists and corporations for a private children’s football charity that he operates. Mr. Ford subsequently voted in favor of a successful motion striking down an order requiring him to return the money. The court order is suspended for 14 days and Mr. Ford, who attributed the ruling to “left wing politics,” will ask the court it delay it pending an appeal. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Orders Toronto Mayor to Leave Office', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Judge Orders Toronto Mayor to Leave Office', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Rob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T03:37:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/eafbf7c2-f27f-5b76-8240-d954122645a4', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eafbf7c2-f27f-5b76-8240-d954122645a4'}, {'abstract': 'Top public officials apparently tried to undermine investment professionals like Tarrus Richardson, who supported legislation to open doors for blacks, Latinos and women in the nearly all-white world of finance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/nyregion/after-effort-to-open-doors-for-others-a-capitalist-is-locked-out.html', 'snippet': 'Top public officials apparently tried to undermine investment professionals like Tarrus Richardson, who supported legislation to open doors for blacks, Latinos and women in the nearly all-white world of finance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a child in Chicago, Tarrus Richardson clipped newspaper articles about Reginald Lewis, a financier who would become the first African-American to run a billion-dollar business. Mr. Richardson’s father, a Vietnam veteran, started a popcorn business, and made Tarrus a shareholder at age 8. Mr. Richardson went on to Harvard Business School, and with his friend, Willie Woods, opened an investment firm, ICV Capital Partners, specializing in inner-city companies, in 1998. They were among the firms chosen during the past decade to invest a portion of New York State’s $250 billion pension fund assets. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/nyregion/GOTHAM/GOTHAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/nyregion/GOTHAM/GOTHAM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/nyregion/GOTHAM/GOTHAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/27/nyregion/GOTHAM/GOTHAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/nyregion/GOTHAM/GOTHAM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Effort to Open Doors for Others, a Capitalist Is Locked Out', 'kicker': 'Gotham', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Effort to Open Doors for Others, a Capitalist Is Locked Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiNapoli, Thomas P', 'rank': 2, '