ield.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEL AVIV — It was late Saturday evening when I caught up with the Knesset member Amir Peretz, the former Israeli defense minister, former head of the Labor Party and former chairman of Israel’s trade union organization. It had been a very busy Saturday for him: Peretz is running, yet again, in the primaries of the Labor Party, which are scheduled for Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Iron Man', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peretz, Amir', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labour Party (Israel)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T08:44:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20af43bd-638e-5505-9feb-5722aa806d2e', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20af43bd-638e-5505-9feb-5722aa806d2e'}, {'abstract': 'The math of controlling climate change could get even trickier as scientists begin to factor in emissions of carbon that is expected to be released from the melting of permafrost.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/grappling-with-the-permafrost-problem/', 'snippet': 'The math of controlling climate change could get even trickier as scientists begin to factor in emissions of carbon that is expected to be released from the melting of permafrost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The greatest single uncertainty about climate change is how much the warming of the planet will feed on itself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grappling With the Permafrost Problem', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Doha (Qatar)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T09:01:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e681d38e-72c1-5d74-8a87-96bd90c6e441', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e681d38e-72c1-5d74-8a87-96bd90c6e441'}, {'abstract': 'Can you choose the best synonym for “bulwark” as it is used in the article?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/test-yourself-english-nov-27-2012/', 'snippet': 'Can you choose the best synonym for “bulwark” as it is used in the article?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the article “Where Pilgrims Landed, Thanksgiving Is Kept at Table, Not Mall.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, Nov. 27, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T09:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'sectio