heir discharge program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the past, the only thing a patient was sure to get after a hospital stay was a bill. But as Medicare cracks down on high readmission rates, hospitals are dispatching nurses, transportation, culturally specific diet tips, free medications and even bathroom scales to patients deemed at risk of relapsing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Efforts to Close Hospitals’ Revolving Doors', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T10:21:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jordan Rau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jordan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/507c40cb-0b4e-52e3-a98d-ad1516aea5d2', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/507c40cb-0b4e-52e3-a98d-ad1516aea5d2'}, {'abstract': 'Chandler Buckingham, a student at Rogers High School in Rogers, Ark., has already heard decisions from three out of the four colleges to which she applied.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/envelope-please-chandler-buckingham-4/', 'snippet': 'Chandler Buckingham, a student at Rogers High School in Rogers, Ark., has already heard decisions from three out of the four colleges to which she applied.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On television, it is common to see the image of a high school senior worried about getting accepted into college. The senior talks to his or her parents and the three of them are worried, but hopeful.', 'source': 'The New York 