 and be clear and accessible to all readers. But we should also take care to avoid lapses that would lead expert readers to question our reporting or our attention to detail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I asked my colleague Jim Dao, who has done great reporting on the armed forces and military life, for suggestions on avoiding some common missteps in military references.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tips on Military Usage', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T13:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip B. Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/772730e4-437b-5745-ad72-c8c8bbfc27f0', 'word_count': 1345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/772730e4-437b-5745-ad72-c8c8bbfc27f0'}, {'abstract': 'As the first foreigner in three centuries was named to head the Bank of England, the British press said appointing Mark Carney was a bit like having an outsider run the national soccer team.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/canadian-welcomed-as-team-england-bank-boss/', 'snippet': 'As the first foreigner in three centuries was named to head the Bank of England, the British press said appointing Mark Carney was a bit like having an outsider run the national soccer team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Britain’s press reached for the soccer analogy to explain why a foreigner had been picked to head the Bank of England, the country’s central bank.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/blogs/rdv-carney/rdv-carney-jumbo.jp