and canary yellow tuxedo shirt, Rudd plays air guitar to “Hound Dog” and helps the 13-year-old belle of the ball, in all her pink-ruffled glory, to cheat at limbo, raising one end of the bar so she can slip under it. When a child off camera protests — “Not fair!” — Rudd half-croons, “Hey, pal, it’s her gig.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '99', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leap of Faith', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leap of Faith', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudd, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T14:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10572671-6aa8-5462-b2c7-aa8afdf7b143', 'word_count': 776, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10572671-6aa8-5462-b2c7-aa8afdf7b143'}, {'abstract': 'Kirk Hammett, the lead guitarist for the band Metallica, talks about his collection of horror-themed memorabilia, much of which is featured in a new coffee table book.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/movies-memorabilia-and-metallica/', 'snippet': 'Kirk Hammett, the lead guitarist for the band Metallica, talks about his collection of horror-themed memorabilia, much of which is featured in a new coffee table book.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kirk Hammett, the lead guitarist for the band Metallica, was 6 years old when an older brother got a model of Frankenstein and painted it, to Mr. Hammett’s dismay, in a rainbow of psychedelic colors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Movies, Memorabilia and Metallica', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'p