reds of thousands of people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/world/middleeast/egypt-morsi.html', 'snippet': 'President Mohamed Morsi’s attempt to soften his edict did little to constrain the crowd, which some estimates put at hundreds of thousands of people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Tens of thousands of people filled the central Tahrir Square on Tuesday afternoon in an outpouring of rage at President Mohamed Morsi’s attempt to claim expansive new powers and at the role in politics played by his party, the Muslim Brotherhood.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/world/28egypt-HP/20121127_Egypt_ss-slide-3QIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 563, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/world/28egypt-HP/20121127_Egypt_ss-slide-3QIC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1125, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/world/28egypt-HP/28egypt-HP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/27/world/28egypt-HP/28egypt-HP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt Protesters Gather to Denounce Morsi in Scenes Recalling Uprising', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt Protesters Gather to Denounce Morsi in Scenes Recalling Uprising', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T14:47:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim and David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe2d7a42-9d85-5658-ac62-ef53ad0b45f8', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe2d7a42-9d85-5658-ac62-ef53ad0b45f8'}, {'abstract': 'Also, the head of the trust that supervises the British Broadcasting Corporation said a recent BBC report that wrongly implicated a former Conservative Party politician in sexual abuse showed “appalling editorial judgment.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/the-breakfast-meeting-a-new-russian-tv-star-and-the-joy-of-a-critics-pan/', 'snippet': 'Also, the head of the trust that supervises the British Broadcasting Corporation said a recent BBC report that wrongly implicated a former Conservative Party politician in sexual abuse showed “appalling editorial judgment.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Svetlana Kuritsyna, a 20-year-old woman from an impoverished rural region of Russia, has become a media star on the basis of an innocent, somewhat inarticulate video interview in which she praises President Vladimir V. Putin. She can be seen as the polar opposite of Pussy Riot, the anti-Putin feminist punk band, three of whose members are now in prison, Sophia Kishkovsky writes. Ms. Kuritsyna is now the star of her own trashy reality show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: A New Russian TV Star, and the Joy of a Critic’s Pan', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ai Weiwei', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fieri, Guy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'John, Elton', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pussy Riot', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T14:49:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1029ad8-f5a2-5d51-9b44-135db0b5e2e1', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1029ad8-f5a2-5d51-9b44-135db0b5e2e1'}, {'abstract': 'The Gotham Independent Film Awards didn’t offer a lot of surprises but there were tidbeats to be gleaned, and many about Jared Leto.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/things-we-learned-at-the-gothams-jared-leto-edition/', 'snippet': 'The Gotham Independent Film Awards didn’t offer a lot of surprises but there were tidbeats to be gleaned, and many about Jared Leto.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were few surprises at the Gotham Awards on Monday evening, no best-picture ties or debuts of future comedy duos. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Things We Learned at the Gothams, Jared Leto Edition', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gotham Independent Film Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Birbiglia, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blunt, Emily', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeWitt, Rosemarie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duplass, Mark', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leto, Jared', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConaughey, Matthew', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ray, Bingham', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zeitlin, Benh', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '30 Seconds to Mars (Music Group)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EMI Group PLC', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T15:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e7dae4d-28ef-5e3a-a65b-3e3dad94dffd', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e7dae4d-28ef-5e3a-a65b-3e3dad94dffd'}, {'abstract': 'Katie Roiphe’s new essay collection is lean and literate in the way it argues, among other points, that we’ve grown pretty dull and conservative, more interested in being parents than in being adults.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/books/in-praise-of-messy-lives-essays-by-katie-roiphe.html', 'snippet': 'Katie Roiphe’s new essay collection is lean and literate in the way it argues, among other points, that we’ve grown pretty dull and conservative, more interested in being parents than in being adults.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many people have cultivated a dislike for Katie Roiphe’s books, essays, reviews and persona. She has been called “an uncomfortablist” and (long ago in The New Yorker) a “self-proclaimed bad girl and sexual rebel.” Gawker takes aim at her on what seems like a weekly basis, in blog posts with understated headlines like “Shut Up, Katie Roiphe.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/28book-2/28book-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 724, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/28book-2/28book-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1447, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/28book-2/28book-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/28book-2/28book-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/28book-2/28book-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Defending the Unruly Realm', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Call To Embrace Life’s Unruly Realms', '