on-sale-dec-14/', 'snippet': 'Sam played it; now it’s is being auctioned by Sotheby’s. The piano from “Casablanca,” that is.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These may be tough times for many beloved pianos, but one famous set of keys has so much sentimental value – and Hollywood cachet – that it is expected to fetch a million-dollar price at Sotheby’s on Dec. 14. The piano that was used to play “As Time Goes By” in the 1942 movie “Casablanca” is being offered for sale by a Japanese collector, with Sotheby’s estimating that it will go for up to $1.2 million, according to The Associated Press.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'You Must Remember This: ‘Casablanca’ Piano on Sale Dec. 14', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergman, Ingrid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bogart, Humphrey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Casablanca (Morocco)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T15:31:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/095e03c0-7b09-570d-9e02-b2c4386236de', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/095e03c0-7b09-570d-9e02-b2c4386236de'}, {'abstract': 'For a child, getting their own Facebook is a sign that they are now officially a teenager, but they must be made aware of the consequences of their online actions. Here are some tips to help your child join the social network without regret.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/putting-a-13-year-old-child-safely-on-facebook/', 'snippet': 'For a child, getting their own Facebook is a sign that they are now officially a teenager, but they must be made aware of the consequences of their online actions. Here are some tips to help your child join the social network without regret.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An e-mail in my inbox Monday morning from my editor had a scary subject line: “Help!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/theater/bits-fbteens/bits-fbteens-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 230, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/theater/bits-fbteens/bits-fbteens-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 230, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/theater/bits-fbteens/bits-fbteens-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/26/theater/bits-fbteens/bits-fbteens-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/theater/bits-fbteens/bits-fbteens-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting a 13-Year-Old Child Safely on Facebook', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T15:42:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14b18002-9a0e-560d-a9ee-0b45f6fd6b4b', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14b18002-9a0e-560d-a9ee-0b45f6fd6b4b'}, {'abstract': 'Rona Fairhead’s departure follows the announcement that Pearson’s chief executive, Marjorie Scardino, would be leaving her post. Their exits are likely to fuel speculation that Pearson will look to sell The Financial Times.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/head-of-financial-times-group-to-step-down/', 'snippet': 'Rona Fairhead’s departure follows the announcement that Pearson’s chief executive, Marjorie Scardino, would be leaving her post. Their exits are likely to fuel speculation that Pearson will look to sell The Financial Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:48 a.m. | Updated Rona Fairhead, chief executive of Pearson PLC’s Financial Times Group and a member of Pearson’s board of directors, will step down in April, the company said Tuesday. She will be the second high-level executive in recent months to leave Pearson, the London-based media conglomerate.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Head of Financial Times Group to Step Down', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Second Executive Announces Departure From Pearson', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fairhead, Rona', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fallon, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scardino, Marjorie M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Times', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Times Group', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pearson PLC', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T15:48:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfe228a8-5b5b-5e7a-a437-589238f758f3', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfe228a8-5b5b-5e7a-a437-589238f758f3'}, {'abstract': 'This moment was a long time coming. The ground-to-air war (and the likely government retaliation for this hit) can be expected to be bloodier from here.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/videos-from-syria-appear-to-show-first-confirmed-hit-of-aircraft-by-surface-to-air-missile/', 'snippet': 'This moment was a long time coming. The ground-to-air war (and the likely government retaliation for this hit) can be expected to be bloodier from here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These two videos (in order) are freshly moving online. The first shows a Syrian Air Force helicopter of the Mi-8 line clearly being hit by a fast-moving projectile as it makes its way through a slow left turn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Videos From Syria Appear to Show First Confirmed Hit of Aircraft by Surface-to-Air Missile', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T15:54:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12b05816-0d16-5e04-8822-a3033ac0efb7', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12b05816-0d16-5e04-8822-a3033ac0efb7'}, {'abstract': 'By building the Major League Baseball Players Association into a force that revolutionized the game, Mr. Miller became one of the most influential figures in the sport’s history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/sports/baseball/marvin-miller-union-leader-who-changed-baseball-dies-at-95.html', 'snippet': 'By building the Major League Baseball Players Association into a force that revolutionized the game, Mr. Miller became one of the most influential figures in the sport’s history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marvin Miller, an economist and labor leader who became one of the most important figures in baseball history by building the major league players union into a force that revolutionized the game and ultimately transformed all of professional sports, died on Tuesday at his home in Manhattan. He was 95.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/sports/baseball/27miller-pic2/27miller-pic2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/s