le/c521eab0-c245-52f6-a504-b427a1cbc48f'}, {'abstract': 'Memorable moments from the Gothams included Matt Damon’s likening himself to Sarah Palin wolf-hunting and the host Mike Birbiglia crowd-sourcing his jokes.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/things-we-learned-at-the-gothams-crowdsourcing-edition/', 'snippet': 'Memorable moments from the Gothams included Matt Damon’s likening himself to Sarah Palin wolf-hunting and the host Mike Birbiglia crowd-sourcing his jokes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the Gotham Independent Film Awards on Monday, we learned a few things, mostly about Jared Leto. But there were other educational tidbits:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Things We Learned at the Gothams, Crowdsourcing Edition', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gotham Independent Film Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Birbiglia, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Bradley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Damon, Matt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilman, Jared', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leto, Jared', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Russell, David O', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calvin Klein Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internet Movie Database', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T16:15:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/889c7180-25bf-5bf1-92bd-7701062db4f8', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/889c7180-25bf-5bf1-92bd-7701062db4f8'}, {'abstract': 'Fans of a Romanian soccer team took up a collection to pay players’ wages.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/as-transylvania-goes-so-goes-romania/', 'snippet': 'Fans of a Romanian soccer team took up a collection to pay players’ wages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid rumors of their club folding, players from Universitatea Cluj of Romania’s Liga 1 were paid for the first time in four months on Saturday. After a 2-1 derby loss to UEFA Champions League participant CFR Cluj, a small amount of cash found its way into U Cluj’s locker room — not from the owner’s checkbook, but from the fans’ pockets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Transylvania Goes So Goes Romania', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Romania', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T16:20:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liviu Bird', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liviu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bird', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dbfe33a-7ea0-5e8d-8043-b03da976d26c', 'word_count': 1046, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dbfe33a-7ea0-5e8d-8043-b03da976d26c'}, {'abstract': 'Among other things, “Far from the Tree” is a tribute to parents who live the daily grind, who celebrate incremental victories, and who avoid reading books about their child’s diagnosis until they’re ready.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/far-from-the-tree-and-the-literature-of-autism/', 'snippet': 'Among other things, “Far from the Tree” is a tribute to parents who live the daily grind, who celebrate incremental victories, and who avoid reading books about their child’s diagnosis until they’re ready.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent road trip, my son, Jonah, and I outvoted my wife, Cynthia, winning the right to listen to Steely Dan’s “Greatest Hits.” This provided Cynthia with time to fashion a pointed critique of the songs Jonah and I were happily singing along to.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Far From the Tree’ and the Literature of Autism', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Solomon, Andrew', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T16:22:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joel Yanofsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yanofsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99256939-9ed5-5a50-9cce-1f8ee83b08ee', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99256939-9ed5-5a50-9cce-1f8ee83b08ee'}, {'abstract': 'The year’s notable fiction, poetry and nonfiction, selected by the editors of The New York Times Book Review.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/books/review/100-notable-books-of-2012.html', 'snippet': 'The year’s notable fiction, poetry and nonfiction, selected by the editors of The New York Times Book 