': 'nyt://article/acc8d47c-0d40-5aab-915a-6462ceb180ff', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acc8d47c-0d40-5aab-915a-6462ceb180ff'}, {'abstract': 'Add sea salt by the handful into your bath to release toxins, soften skin and add immeasurably to the sum of well-being in the world.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/the-samurai-shopper-all-wet/', 'snippet': 'Add sea salt by the handful into your bath to release toxins, soften skin and add immeasurably to the sum of well-being in the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s been so much uninvited salt water in New York lately that it’s probably tragic irony that the Samurai Shopper just wants to soak in a warm bath with a few capfuls of aromatic bath salts to relax my muscles and soothe my nerves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Samurai Shopper | All Wet', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T16:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By S.S. Fair', 'person': [{'firstname': 'S.', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Fair', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/688395a8-bd9b-5d9e-b7bb-cca0c6e6211e', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/688395a8-bd9b-5d9e-b7bb-cca0c6e6211e'}, {'abstract': 'How a Republican Senator’s proposed grand bargain differs from Romney’s agenda, and why it matters.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/bob-corker-and-the-romney-road-not-taken/', 'snippet': 'How a Republican Senator’s proposed grand bargain differs from Romney’s agenda, and why it matters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Bob Corker, Republican of Tennessee, has earned a round of media attention this week for sketching out a potential tax reform/entitlement reform compromise in the Washington Post. Here’s the meat of his proposed grand bargain:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bob Corker and the Romney Road Not Taken', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T16:34:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1878170c-49da-5de8-97a7-05b0690522c6', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1878170c-49da-5de8-97a7-05b0690522c6'}, {'abstract': 'Virtue was not rewarded.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/twenties-tales/', 'snippet': 'Virtue was not rewarded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 1920s — when several of the victorious Allies emerged from World War I with large debts in their own currencies — offer in some ways the nearest parallel to the debt concerns dominating recent debate. And it occurred to me that it would be useful to have a side-by-side of Britain and France.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Twenties Tales', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T16:36:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7322c93-413e-54be-b6bf-2d4db58cf3d7', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7322c93-413e-54be-b6bf-2d4db58cf3d7'}, {'abstract': 'The recall of Toyota Tacoma pickups is to fix a rust problem that could allow the spare tire to fall from beneath the vehicle.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/toyota-recalling-150000-tacoma-pickups/', 'snippet': 'The recall of Toyota Tacoma pickups is to fix a rust problem that could allow the spare tire to fall from beneath the vehicle.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:18 p.m. | Updated Toyota is recalling about 150,000 2001-4 Tacoma pickups to fix a rust problem that could allow the spare tire to fall from beneath the vehicle, according to a report from the automaker posted on the Web site of the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toyota Recalling 150,000 Tacoma Pickups', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Utility Vehicles and Light Trucks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Auto Safety', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T16:36:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc250966-ba7b-5426-81d8-998e3e394c82', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc250966-ba7b-5426-81d8-998e3e394c82'}, {'abstract': 'Federal mediators will attempt to help break the stalemate in the N.H.L. lockout.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/mediators-to-join-n-h-l-talks/', 'snippet': 'Federal mediators will attempt to help break the stalemate in the N.H.L. lockout.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:00 p.m. | Updated Federal mediators are scheduled to join the N.H.L. and players’ association Wednesday in New York, the first negotiating session between the two sides in a week.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mediators to Join N.H.L. Talks on Wednesday', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mediators Joining Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARBITRATION, CONCILIATION AND MEDIATION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettman, Gary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, George H', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fehr, Donald', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T16:40:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcb955f3-c7ba-5afc-b920-dc821bfd28f6', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcb955f3-c7ba-5afc-b920-dc821bfd28f6'}, {'abstract': 'Tickets are available for our all-day hack event on Saturday, Dec. 8. Get your ticket today via Eventbrite.', 'web_url': 'https://open.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/register-now-for-timesopen-2012-hack-day/', 'snippet': 'Tickets are available for our all-day hack event on Saturday, Dec. 8. Get your ticket today via Eventbrite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tickets are available for our all-day hack event on Saturday, Dec. 8. Join us for a day filled with learning, coding, tinkering, having fun and hanging out with some of the best developers in NYC. Get your ticket today via Eventbrite.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Register Now for TimesOpen 2012 Hack Day', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T16:47:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Fiore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fiore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf3e2294-f341-5716-bebb-11424106f838', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf3e2294-f341-5716-bebb-11424106f838'}, {'abstract': 'Budget airlines like Allegiant can come with trade-offs when taking a family vacation.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/a-budget-trip-to-orlando-for-a-holiday-break/', 'snippet': 'Budget airlines like Allegiant can come with trade-offs when taking a family vacation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, our Thanksgiving was memorable mostly for the deer we hit on the drive to our holiday destination. This year, we had a travel challenge of a different sort: Fly to Florida for a family vacation, on a budget.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Budget Trip to Orlando for a Holiday Break', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'pr