: 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Schweber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9677952b-4dba-5da8-91ce-d928e75cc86c', 'word_count': 648, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9677952b-4dba-5da8-91ce-d928e75cc86c'}, {'abstract': 'Tonight at 7:15, watch a live interview with Damon and Van Sant about their latest collaboration, “Promised Land.”', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/matt-damon-and-gus-van-sant-tonight-right-here-on-the-blog/', 'snippet': 'Tonight at 7:15, watch a live interview with Damon and Van Sant about their latest collaboration, “Promised Land.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hugo Lindgren, the editor of the magazine, interviewed the director Gus Van Sant and the actor Matt Damon (you can tell he is an actor by the way that he is acting in the magazine’s “14 Actors Acting” package) about their third film together, “Promised Land.” They were joined by John Krasinski, who co-stars in the film, which he and Damon wrote together. The sold-out event took place in the TimesCenter in Manhattan on Tuesday evening, but you can watch it right here on the 6th Floor blog.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Matt Damon and Gus Van Sant. Tonight. Right Here. On the Blog.', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Damon, Matt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krasinski, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Sant, Gus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T17:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Staff', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Staff'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9e164ae-e270-567d-bcad-7e7211ee0de9', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9e164ae-e270-567d-bcad-7e7211ee0de9'}, {'abstract': 'The new space, which will focus on Jacobean works, will be named after the actor and director Sam Wanamaker.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/shakespeares-globe-sets-2014-opening-date-for-indoor-theater/', 'snippet': 'The new space, which will focus on Jacobean works, will be named after the actor and director Sam Wanamaker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leaders of the open-air Shakespeare’s Globe theater in London said on Tuesday that its new indoor theater space will open in January 2014 and be named for Sam Wanamaker, the American actor and director who led the decades-long effort to rebuild the Globe on the south bank of the Thames.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shakespeare’s Globe Sets 2014 Opening Date for Indoor Theater', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Globe Indoor Theater Named for Wanamaker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dromgoole, Dominic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wanamaker, Sam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Shakespeare's Globe Theater", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T17:05:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfb16185-a5f4