ma steal the 2012 election? Virginia’s attorney general seems to think so.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apparently, there are limits to what voter fraud conspiracy theorists will say. Take Virginia’s attorney general, Ken Cuccinelli, who was a major backer of the law passed by his state requiring voters to present ID before they cast a ballot. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Life on the Voter-Fraud Fringe', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identification Devices', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuccinelli, Kenneth T II', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T19:04:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d03c6826-9c31-54e8-b29d-1094175bdec0', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d03c6826-9c31-54e8-b29d-1094175bdec0'}, {'abstract': 'After going dark last year because of political revolution, the Cairo Film Festival was set to come back in 2012 with a slate of political, edgy movies. But the festival, which was scheduled to begin Tuesday, had to be postponed once again.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/in-cairo-politics-on-screen-delayed-by-uprising-in-the-streets/', 'snippet': 'After going dark last year because of political revolution, the Cairo Film Festival was set to come back in 2012 with a slate of political, edgy movies. But the festival, which was scheduled to begin Tuesday, had to be postponed once again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After going dark last year because of political revolution, the Cairo Film Festival was set to come back in 2012 stronger than ever: entries from 64 countries, 3 competitions and a slate of political, edgy movies. But the opening of the festival, which was scheduled for Tuesday, had to be postponed once again because of political unrest in the city. Opening night is now scheduled for Wednesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/arts/27rdv-filmfest/27rdv-filmfest-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 720, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/arts/27rdv-filmfest/27rdv-filmfest-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 720, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/arts/27rdv-filmfest/27rdv-filmfest-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/27/arts/27rdv-filmfest/27rdv-filmfest-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/arts/27rdv-filmfest/27rdv-filmfest-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Cairo, Politics on Screen Delayed by Uprising in the Streets', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'va