: 25, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9d16007-ad07-5d13-afba-30da6f43fa3c'}, {'abstract': 'SAC Capital Advisors, Steven A. Cohen’s hedge fund behemoth, plans a conference call on Wednesday to calm its investors and allay concerns related to the latest insider trading case involving the firm.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/sac-to-hold-client-call-amid-insider-trading-case/', 'snippet': 'SAC Capital Advisors, Steven A. Cohen’s hedge fund behemoth, plans a conference call on Wednesday to calm its investors and allay concerns related to the latest insider trading case involving the firm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAC Capital Advisors, the hedge fund giant hit with a new insider trading charge last week, plans to hold a conference call on Wednesday morning to reassure investors and allay concerns related to the latest case.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'SAC Capital to Try to Reassure Investors', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'SAC Capital to Try to Reassure Investors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Steven A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martoma, Mathew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SAC Capital Advisors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T20:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58a4aa9f-a5d9-57a3-8468-e564a8d0cfe1', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58a4aa9f-a5d9-57a3-8468-e564a8d0cfe1'}, {'abstract': '“Baking for Friends” includes recipes for chocolate shortbread and earthy Guinness brownies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/dining/a-hamptons-bakery-shares.html', 'snippet': '“Baking for Friends” includes recipes for chocolate shortbread and earthy Guinness brownies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The baker looking for holiday ideas would do well to turn to Kathleen King, who is based in Southampton, N.Y., and who has made a huge success of her Tate’s Bake Shop cookies. Her latest book, “Baking for Friends,” offers more than 120 straightforward recipes for everything from breakfast treats to lavish cakes. I could not stop eating her cinnamon swirl scones, which are made like cinnamon buns, or the fresh fig cake, which reinvents fruitcake (I brushed it with rum syrup while it was still warm). The cookies include chocolate chip with crushed candy canes, chocolate shortbreads and even old-fashioned pfeffernüsse. And consider the earthy Guinness brownies to cut in small squares and serve with eggnog.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/dining/28STUFF_BAKE/28STUFF5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 793, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/dining/28STUFF_BAKE/28STUFF5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1587, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hamptons Bakery Shares', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Hamptons Bakery Shares', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Kathleen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T20:33:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/22511c0c-10c5-5644-a3cf-be0338326aa9', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22511c0c-10c5-5644-a3cf-be0338326aa9'}, {'abstract': 'What we’re reading now from L’Oréal’s soon-to-be new acquisition and Paul Deneve’s open letter to WWD.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/fashion-news-were-reading-now-20/', 'snippet': 'What we’re reading now from L’Oréal’s soon-to-be new acquisition and Paul Deneve’s open letter to WWD.', 'lead_paragraph': 'L’Oréal is buying the makeup brand Urban Decay, and according to The Los Angeles Times, Nicolas Hieronimus, L’Oréal Luxe’s president, said that the acquisition was meant to target younger customers and “beef up” the company’s portfolio.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fashion News We’re Reading Now', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T20:37:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a823f2b-ff97-54c4-9358-245b373c89e6', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a823f2b-ff97-54c4-9358-245b373c89e6'}, {'abstract': 'First there was the book. Now there is the festival. The Southbank Centre announced the details Tuesday morning of a yearlong event called The Rest Is Noise.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/alex-ross-inspires-a-festival-all-20th-century-music-all-the-time/', 'snippet': 'First there was the book. Now there is the festival. The Southbank Centre announced the details Tuesday morning of a yearlong event called The Rest Is Noise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — First there was the book. Now there is the festival. The Southbank Centre announced the details Tuesday morning of The Rest Is Noise, a year-long festival of 20th-century music inspired by Alex Ross’s 2007 book of the same name. Mr. Ross, a music critic for The New Yorker magazine, won considerable acclaim for “The Rest Is Noise,” a sweeping survey of 20th-century classical music.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/arts/27rdv-noise/27rdv-noise-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/arts/27rdv-noise/27rdv-noise-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/arts/27rdv-noise/27rdv-noise-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/27/arts/27rdv-noise/27rdv-noise-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/27/arts/27rdv-noise/27rdv-noise-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alex Ross Inspires a Festival: All 20th-Century Music, All the Time', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T20:37:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8b61e92-c3de-54c3-95ec-3c1b047fec75', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8b61e92-c3de-54c3-95ec-3c1b047fec75'}, {'abstract': 'Frustration has boiled over since ArcelorMittal, the world’s largest steel maker, announced plans to scale back one of its three major French factories and eliminate hundreds of jobs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/business/global/labor-dispute-pits-france-against-arcelormittal.html', 'snippet': 'Frustration has boiled over since ArcelorMittal, the world’s largest steel maker, announced plans to scale back one of its three major French factories and eliminate hundreds of jobs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — It has been only a month since the French government, concerned about the country’s declining competitiveness, began its “Say Oui to France” advertising campaign to attract foreign investment. But ArcelorMittal, the Luxembourg-based company with Indian roots that is the world’s biggest steel maker, has been hearing a distinctly harsher message.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/business/ARCELOR-1/ARCELOR-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/28/business/ARCELOR-1/ARCELO