elsewhere-41/', 'snippet': 'Photos from Egypt, Democratic Republic of Congo, Gaza and New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos from Egypt, Democratic Republic of Congo, Gaza and New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Egypt and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T22:20:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aac733a0-df80-535d-9af6-52e0d12d9ad5', 'word_count': 16, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aac733a0-df80-535d-9af6-52e0d12d9ad5'}, {'abstract': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Tuesday’s selection includes small merchants accusing Amazon of highhandedness, a look at how PRWeb works and President Obama’s anti-hacking moves.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/todays-scuttlebot-personal-drones-and-age-bias-in-silicon-valley/', 'snippet': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Tuesday’s selection includes small merchants accusing Amazon of highhandedness, a look at how PRWeb works and President Obama’s anti-hacking...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Loads of interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently. See more here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Personal Drones, and Age Bias in Silicon Valley', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T22:45:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa7487a8-c852-55d9-8c56-9fb05d3c9c17', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa7487a8-c852-55d9-8c56-9fb05d3c9c17'}, {'abstract': 'The Clarion Music Society’s celebration of Salamone Rossi’s music on Monday included work by his contemporaries Monteverdi and Gesualdo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/arts/music/clarion-music-society-at-the-five-borough-music-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The Clarion Music Society’s celebration of Salamone Rossi’s music on Monday included work by his contemporaries Monteverdi and Gesualdo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The attention given the Mantuan composer Salamone Rossi is still sometimes tinged with condescension, as astonishment over the participation of a Jewish composer in the musical life of early-17th-century Italy replaces any consideration of his work’s merit. On Monday evening the Clarion Music Society presented an intelligently devised and lovingly offered concert of vocal music by Rossi that illuminated its place in the Jewish liturgy and juxtaposed it with works by Monteverdi and Gesualdo. Here Rossi’s music revealed him to be part of — and sometimes leading — a wider group of composers who were testing the limits of harmony and expressive effects. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/228CLARION/228CLARION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 917, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/228CLARION/228CLARION-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1795, 'width': 1608, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/228CLARION/228CLARION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/228CLARION/228CLARION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/228CLARION/228CLARION-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Exploring Rossi’s Place in the Jewish Liturgy and in a Wider World of Experimentation', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exploring Rossi’s Place in the Jewish Liturgy And in a Wider World of Experimentation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rossi, Salamone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clarion Music Society', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-27T22:51:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/07b8c504-e7fe-5fe0-af1d-8ea75c8baa07', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07b8c504-e7fe-5fe0-af1d-8ea75c8baa07'}, {'abstract': 'The concert presented by the Juilliard String Quartet on Monday at Alice Tully Hall illustrated the bond that has formed among the members.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/arts/music/juilliard-string-quartet-at-alice-tully-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The concert presented by the Juilliard String Quartet on Monday at Alice Tully Hall illustrated the bond that has formed among the members.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a year has passed since Joseph Lin became the latest first violinist of the Juilliard String Quartet, a venerable institution formed in 1946 at the school whose name it bears. After the departure of Robert Mann, who helped to found the group, two more fine players assumed the position, then left it: Joel Smirnoff, who slid over from his second-violin seat in 1997, then departed in 2008; and Nick Eanet, whose health limited his tenure to only a year.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/QUARTET/QUARTET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/QUARTET/QUARTET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1447, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'l