iginally planned. He said on his Web site on Tuesday that the United States State Department had withdrawn an invitation to play a concert sponsored by the United States Embassy in Manama, the capital. He had said earlier that the State Department had asked him to be a cultural ambassador to Bahrain, a religiously conservative Muslim country, “promoting music, freedom and positive party power.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Andrew W.K.’s Bahrain Trip Is Canceled', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nuland, Victoria J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilkes-Krier, Andrew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahrain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T00:21:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f74f587e-983b-5a61-a77c-4d761d6b352e', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f74f587e-983b-5a61-a77c-4d761d6b352e'}, {'abstract': 'A group of Egyptian filmmakers is making an effort to explain the roots of the current crisis by posting a series of interviews with demonstrators on YouTube.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/egyptians-explain-their-return-to-the-streets/', 'snippet': 'A group of Egyptian filmmakers is making an effort to explain the roots of the current crisis by posting a series of interviews with demonstrators on YouTube.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | Wednesday, 9:38 a.m. With tens of thousands of protesters again filling Cairo’s Tahrir Square and the streets of other Egyptians cities on Tuesday, chanting for the country’s president to “Leave!” just five months after he was elected, the mood in the square reminded many of the 18 days of protest that toppled Hosni Mubarak last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egyptians Explain Their Return to the Streets', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T00:22:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/309e4d31-5081-5463-bc3e-8ced0b7b2506', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/309e4d31-5081-5463-bc3e-8ced0b7b2506'}, {'abstract': 'Americans have been getting better at paying off their debt in the last year, with a glaring exception: student loans.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/student-loan-debt-rising-and-often-not-being-paid-back/', 'snippet': 'Americans have been getting better at paying off their debt in the last year, with a glaring exception: student loans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans have been getting better at paying off their debt in the last year, with a glaring exception: student loans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multime