Sandy’s Rising Costs', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hurricane Sandy&#8217;s Rising Costs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T01:50:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/35911027-fa04-5aa1-bf43-71cd3b9cf68b', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35911027-fa04-5aa1-bf43-71cd3b9cf68b'}, {'abstract': 'A grudging Republican acceptance of additional revenues doesn’t show real flexibility in the negotiations over the “fiscal cliff.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/opinion/republicans-still-dodge-reality-on-taxes.html', 'snippet': 'A grudging Republican acceptance of additional revenues doesn’t show real flexibility in the negotiations over the “fiscal cliff.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Congressional Republicans seem to think they are being flexible on taxes simply because a few of them have grudgingly admitted that some new revenues can be part of the current fiscal negotiations. We’re unimpressed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Dodging Reality on Taxes', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still Dodging Reality on Taxes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T02:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/600dc871-3804-519c-8a4e-8dd2cc43a192', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/600dc871-3804-519c-8a4e-8dd2cc43a192'}, {'abstract': 'One in eight Americans get government assistance to buy food, yet many more are eligible.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/hunger-in-plain-sight/', 'snippet': 'One in eight Americans get government assistance to buy food, yet many more are eligible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are hungry people out there, actually; they’re just largely invisible to the rest of us, or they look so much like us that it’s hard to tell. The Supplemental Assistance Nutrition Program, better known as SNAP and even better known as food stamps, currently has around 46 million participants, a record high. That’s one in eight Americans — 10 people in your subway car, one or two on every line at Walmart.We wouldn’t wish that on anyone, but as it stands, the number should be higher[1]: many people are unaware that they’re eligible for SNAP, and thus the participation rate is probably around three-quarters of what it should be.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hunger in Plain Sight', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Banks and Pantries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T02:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/680f4fcf-0763-5dc3-8114-cafd04cf3a41', 'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/680f4fcf-0763-5dc3-8114-cafd04cf3a41'}, {'abstract': 'As a young man in Rome, I fought the 1970s orthodoxies to find my voice as a composer. Today, music is transformed. But our new toys need to be used wisely.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/27/the-reconstruction-of-rome/', 'snippet': 'As a young man in Rome, I fought the 1970s orthodoxies to find my voice as a composer. Today, music is transformed. But our new toys need to be used wisely.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Reconstruction of Rome', 'kicker': 'The Score', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Americans Abroad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Seventies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T02:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Beaser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beaser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b88d2036-7ba6-5885-af70-575e0143cf26', 'word_count': 2848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b88d2036-7ba6-5885-af70-575e0143cf26'}, {'abstract': 'The high turnout for President Obama among Latinos was partly due to a civic campaign generated by Hispanic television and grass-roots groups that urged viewers to register and vote.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/us/politics/for-latino-groups-grass-roots-efforts-paid-off-in-higher-number-of-voters.html', 'snippet': 'The high turnout for President Obama among Latinos was partly due to a civic campaign generated by Hispanic television and grass-roots groups that urged viewers to register and vote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — On Election Day, President Obama got 71 percent of the Latino vote nationally because, in the end, Latinos preferred his message over Mitt Romney’s.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Latino Groups, Grass-Roots Efforts Paid Off in Higher Number of Voters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Latino Groups, Grass-Roots Efforts Paid Off in Higher Number of Voters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Univision', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Telemundo Communications Group Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T02:01:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07eb6bd0-a2cc-59bf-a9c6-8ec213a077e7', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07eb6bd0-a2cc-59bf-a9c6-8ec213a077e7'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Communications Commission needs to end the outrageously high rates that private telephone companies charge for phone calls made by prisoners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/opinion/a-needless-charge-for-prison-families.html', 'snippet': 'The Federal Communications Commission needs to end the outrageously high rates that private telephone companies charge for phone calls made by prisoners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After nearly a decade of delay, the Federal Communications Commission is finally focusing on the private telephone companies that charge outrageously high rates for the calls that many of the nation’s 1.6 million prison inmates make to stay in contact with their families. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Needless Charge for Prison Families', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Needless Charge for Prison Families', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T02:03:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d387c4b3-17e1-5a6d-88d5-ac022731f5f0', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d387c4b3-17e1-5a6d-88d5-ac022731f5f0'}, {'abstract': 'When the State Legislature meets in January, Senator Jeffrey D. Klein and a faction of four fellow Democrats may hold the chamber’s fate in their hands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/nyregion/jeffrey-d-kleins-group-favors-coalition-with-new-york-senate-republicans.html', 'snippet': 'When the State Legislature meets in January, Senator Jeffrey D. Klein and a faction of four fellow Democrats may hold the chamber’s fate in their hands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeffrey D. Klein has been taking calls from labor leaders and rank-and-file state senators. He ate pasta with the Senate majority leader, Dean G. Skelos, a Republican from Long Island. And he sat down, he said, to “clear the air” with the minority leader, John L. Sampson, a Brooklyn Democrat.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/nyregion/y-JP-KLEIN/y-JP-KLEIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/28/nyregion/y-JP-KLEIN/y-JP-KLEIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/nyregion/y-JP-KLEIN/y-JP-KLEIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/nyregion/y-JP-KLEIN/y-JP-KLEIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/nyregion/y-JP-KLEIN/y-JP-KLEIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/28/nyregion/y-JP-KLEIN/y-JP-KLEIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/nyregion/y-JP-KLEIN/y-JP-KLEIN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Top Breakaway Democrat Favors G.O.P. Coalition in State Senate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Top Breakaway Democrat Favors G.O.P. Coalition in State Senate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeffrey D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T02:04:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8105adc-31cf-5ab0-9caa-796065274802', 'word_count': 872, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8105adc-31cf-5ab0-9caa-796065274802'}, {'abstract': 'Fire officials said a door will slow the spread of a blaze, and a wet towel or cloth underneath can block the smoke, which is usually the real killer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/nyregion/a-closed-door-the-best-ally-in-a-home-fire.html', 'snippet': 'Fire officials said a door will slow the spread of a blaze, and a wet towel or cloth underneath can block the smoke, which is usually the real killer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early Thanksgiving morning, a neighbor in my building died when her bed caught fire. The woman, who was 87, usually took a sputtering old radio to bed at night, and fire marshals believe some fault in its wiring started the fire. She lived and died alone. No one else was hurt. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Closed Door: The Best Ally in a Home Fire', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Closed Door: The Best Ally In a Home Fire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T02:04:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8e038fd-7feb-5d6e-b223-007af3cf6dd4', 'word_count': 746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8e038fd-7feb-5d6e-b223-007af3cf6dd4'}, {'abstract': 'A survey suggested that companies were likely to buy more of their own shares after this year because taxes on those gains were expected to grow less than a proposed tax increase on dividends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/business/companies-are-expected-to-increase-buybacks.html', 'snippet': 'A survey suggested that companies were likely to buy more of their own shares after this year because taxes on those gains were expected to grow less than a proposed tax increase on dividends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Investors are bracing for companies to ramp up purchases of their own shares in response to expected tax changes in the new year, despite growing criticism of buybacks. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Buybacks Expected to Increase', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Buybacks Expected To Increase', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Gains Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T02:04:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathaniel Popper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Popper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97193f47-59dd-5b1e-9f32-2ed43e423a49', 'word_count': 1165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97193f47-59dd-5b1e-9f32-2ed43e423a49'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama should move quickly to withdraw all forces in the next year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/opinion/the-pace-of-leaving-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama should move quickly to withdraw all forces in the next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seventeen months ago, President Obama said that the 30,000 American troops deployed to Afghanistan for the “surge” would be home by this September, and he made good on that promise. He also said troop reductions would continue at a “steady pace” until the remaining 66,000 were out by the end of 2014. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pace of Leaving Afghanistan', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Pace of Leaving Afghanistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T02:04:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/824a3bd3-0871-5e25-85b7-a523fda13a7f', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/824a3bd3-0871-5e25-85b7-a523fda13a7f'}, {'abstract': 'American consumer confidence rose to the highest level in five years in November, according to preliminary figures, but two families’ holiday shopping illustrates how regional differences persist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/business/two-families-show-an-uneven-rise-in-consumer-confidence.html', 'snippet': 'American consumer confidence rose to the highest level in five years in November, according to preliminary figures, but two families’ holiday shopping illustrates how regional differences persist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Angelina Sam couldn’t afford to celebrate Christmas last year, serving peanut butter, soup and rice for the holiday meal. And she didn’t buy gifts for her husband or 2-year-old son.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/business/SHOP/SHOP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/28/business/SHOP/SHOP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidt