tion': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3911477-a590-5ff9-bd9a-93ad39143775', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3911477-a590-5ff9-bd9a-93ad39143775'}, {'abstract': '“We truly feel a local presence will create demand,” said Smith’s chief executive, Bryan Hansel.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/smith-electrics-third-american-factory-to-be-in-chicago/', 'snippet': '“We truly feel a local presence will create demand,” said Smith’s chief executive, Bryan Hansel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Smith Electric Vehicles was originally a British company, making plug-in versions of what the English call “milk floats,” but in early 2011 the American operation acquired the British parent. From its home manufacturing base in Kansas City, Mo., the company has steadily expanded. In late 2011, the company announced that it would build electric trucks in the Bronx. And on Wednesday, Smith will make public its plans for a third American factory — in Chicago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Smith Electric’s 3rd American Factory to Be in Chicago', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T05:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fafe978-a516-5a15-b828-9e6941405a8b', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fafe978-a516-5a15-b828-9e6941405a8b'}, {'abstract': '“Canyon,” by Robert Rauschenberg, will go on display on Wednesday at the Museum of Modern Art after being captured in a contest with the Metropolitan Museum of Art, where it had resided on and off since 2005.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/arts/design/moma-gains-treasure-that-metropolitan-museum-of-art-also-coveted.html', 'snippet': '“Canyon,” by Robert Rauschenberg, will go on display on Wednesday at the Museum of Modern Art after being captured in a contest with the Metropolitan Museum of Art, where it had resided on and off since 2005.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Glenn D. Lowry arrived 17 years ago as director of the Museum of Modern Art, he and the curator Kirk Varnedoe sat down and wrote out a list of the 10 works they most wanted. “Canyon,” a landmark of 20th-century art by Robert Rauschenberg, was at the top, Mr. Lowry recalled.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/28MOMA/28MOMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/28MOMA/28MOMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/28MOMA/28MOMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 837, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/28MOMA/28MOMA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1673, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012