 debt crisis that began in Greece and has spread across much of Europe’s periphery. On Tuesday, it passed another round of  tax increases and spending cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since the spring of 2010, Portugal has been battered by the debt crisis that began in Greece and has spread across much of Europe’s periphery. On Tuesday, it passed another round of  tax increases and spending cuts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/world/europe/20121127-PORTUGAL-slide-Z7CX/20121127-PORTUGAL-slide-Z7CX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/world/europe/20121127-PORTUGAL-slide-Z7CX/20121127-PORTUGAL-slide-Z7CX-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/world/europe/20121127-PORTUGAL-slide-Z7CX/20121127-PORTUGAL-slide-Z7CX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/26/world/europe/20121127-PORTUGAL-slide-Z7CX/20121127-PORTUGAL-slide-Z7CX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/world/europe/20121127-PORTUGAL-slide-Z7CX/20121127-PORTUGAL-slide-Z7CX-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Portugal Passes Another Austere Budget', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portugal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T05:38:36+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/f0c88818-8755-57bd-8131-5e3b067f2664', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/f0c88818-8755-57bd-8131-5e3b067f2664'}, {'abstract': 'Protests and work stoppages have become much more common, as daily life for many Portuguese families has become a struggle to stay afloat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/world/europe/portuguese-join-europes-chorus-of-discontent.html', 'snippet': 'Protests and work stoppages have become much more common, as daily life for many Portuguese families has become a struggle to stay afloat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until a few months ago, Portugal was seen as a role model in the grinding euro zone crisis, adopting deep spending cuts and raising taxes to reduce its deficit without the outcry, protests and strikes that austerity policies have set off in other Southern European countries. International lenders praised the Portuguese government even as they arranged a 78 billion euro bailout for the country last year, following similar deals with Greece and Ireland.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/world/PORTUGAL-4/PORTUGAL-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/28/world/PORTUGAL-4/PORTUGAL-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/world/PORTUGAL-4/PORTU