 of the passenger bus, with 30 people aboard, swerved to try to avoid a pedestrian Wednesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/nyregion/bus-plows-into-long-island-house-killing-boy-6.html', 'snippet': 'The Hempstead, N.Y., police said the driver of the passenger bus, with 30 people aboard, swerved to try to avoid a pedestrian Wednesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A passenger bus trying to avoid a pedestrian slammed into a private home in Nassau County on Tuesday, killing a 6-year-old boy, the police said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bus Plows Into L.I. House, Killing Boy, 6', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bus Plows Into L.I. House, Killing Boy, 6', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hempstead (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T05:57:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edf8efad-9432-52bc-9d9e-5be0bb47af4e', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edf8efad-9432-52bc-9d9e-5be0bb47af4e'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (NBC) CHRISTMAS IN ROCKEFELLER CENTER In this 80th tree-lighting ceremony, Trace Adkins, Tony Bennett, Mariah Carey, Cee Lo Green, Victoria Justice, Chris Mann, Scotty McCreery, Rod Stewart, Il Volo, Billy Crystal, Bette Midler and others will gather around a towering Norway spruce. The 80-foot-tall tree (being positioned in Rockefeller Center, above) was donated by Joe Balku of Flanders, N.J., and secured before Hurricane Sandy with more than 10,000 feet of rope and 2,000 feet of aircraft cable. It will be covered with 45,000 LED lights and topped with a Swarovski crystal star through Jan. 7. Then it will be milled for lumber for Habitat for Humanity. The Rockettes will put a little kick into the festivities, presided over by Al Roker and Savannah Guthrie of NBC’s “Today” show. A preview show begins at 7. “SNL Christmas,” at 9, features holiday sketches from “Saturday Night Live.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T06:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/14003dc8-e615-5569-bf3a-825f093d66f1', 'word_count': 765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14003dc8-e615-5569-bf3a-825f093d66f1'}, {'abstract': 'A report finds troubling signs of political interference from the highest levels into the investigation of the fraud at the financial institution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/world/asia/inquiry-into-kabul-bank-fraud-hits-snags.html', 'snippet': 'A report finds troubling signs of political interference from the highest levels into the investigation of the fraud at the financial institution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Persistent political interference has hampered efforts to unravel the colossal fraud at Kabul Bank, with President Hamid Karzai and a small panel of his top aides actually dictating to prosecutors who should be charged and who should not, according to Afghan and Western officials and the results of a public inquiry into the scandal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Political Meddling Hampers Inquiry Into Kabul Bank Debacle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Political Meddling Hampers Inquiry Into Kabul Bank Debacle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kabul Bank', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Mahmoud', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ponzi and Pyramid Schemes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T06:15:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af7f24ef-54b2-58f1-8cc2-e38ce87f1c12', 'word_count': 969, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af7f24ef-54b2-58f1-8cc2-e38ce87f1c12'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/news-quiz-november-28-2012/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | November 28, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T07:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31537298-9adb-501e-aaca-c8542a3c98ae', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31537298-9adb-501e-aaca-c8542a3c98ae'}, {'abstract': 'News, arts and sports from today’s International Herald Tribune.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/iht-quick-read-nov-28/', 'snippet': 'News, arts and sports from today’s International Herald Tribune.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWS While finance ministers from the euro zone and the International Monetary Fund bridged their main differences over a bailout for Greece early Tuesday, bringing closer the release of long-delayed emergency aid, what they left undecided means this long-running drama — and the cohesion of the euro union — is far from settled. James Kanter reports from Brussels.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/business/EURO/EURO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/business/EURO/EURO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1343, 'width': 2048, 'subType'