Knight Capital Group, a financial services firm that suffered a $440 million trading loss in August because of a technology error.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two firms have offered to buy the Knight Capital Group, a financial services firm that suffered a $440 million trading loss in August because of a technology error.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Firms Make Offers For Knight', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Firms Make Offers For Knight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knight Capital Group Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Virtu Financial', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T13:54:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced and Nathaniel Popper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Popper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1094a97a-2d5b-5c1f-ae84-889df68d2eb5', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1094a97a-2d5b-5c1f-ae84-889df68d2eb5'}, {'abstract': 'Neither tribalism nor some fountainhead of darkness — nor King Leopold’s ghost — wholly explains this latest headline: “Congo Slips Into Chaos Again as Rebels Gain.”', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/the-source-of-congos-bleeding/', 'snippet': 'Neither tribalism nor some fountainhead of darkness — nor King Leopold’s ghost — wholly explains this latest headline: “Congo Slips Into Chaos Again as Rebels Gain.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yet another of those recurrent headlines just surfaced — “Congo Slips Into Chaos Again as Rebels Gain” — and I tried to add up the death toll since I first covered the Congo in 1967. It can approach 10 million, depending on how you count. Then I tried to work out why. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Source of Congo’s Bleeding', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Congo, Democratic Republic of (Congo-Kinshasa)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T13:57:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mort Rosenblum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mort', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenblum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a43c4cb8-af6f-56d3-b2cc-bc7213a9c825', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a43c4cb8-af6f-56d3-b2cc-bc7213a9c825'}, {'abstract': 'Borgo combines style and function in his structured carrier, complete with multiple storage trays, a beveled mirror and key.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/the-get-eddie-borgos-jewelry-box/', 'snippet': 'Borgo combines style and function in his structured carrier, complete with multiple storage trays, a beveled mirror and key.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Raise your hand if you’re one of those women who hangs her necklaces on doorknob, hook, nail, mirror corner or other handy household fixture. Well, it’s ladies like you who have inspired the jewelry designer Eddie Borgo to go into the box making business. “Where she keeps her jewelry should be as special as the jewelry itself,” says Borgo of his customer, commenting simultaneously on what he thought was a limited number of beautiful bijoux keepers on the market. His, a structured carrier that features multiple storage trays, a beveled mirror and lock-and-go key, was modeled after a train case that Borgo’s mother used for travel. Decorated with custom hardware and covered in leather embossed to look like exotic skins — stingray or snake — the box comes in four colorways, including navy with gold metal embellishments (shown here). Inside, compartments accommodate sets of cuffs, smaller pendants, larger collars and necklaces. “For every piece in a modern jewelry collection,” Borgo explains. So you can leave the doorknobs alone.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Eddie Borgo’s Jewelry Box', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Off the Doorknob and Into a Box', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T14:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'Herman', 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5477efd8-fcad-58f3-bf2f-f3eab34f5e1f', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5477efd8-fcad-58f3-bf2f-f3eab34f5e1f'}, {'abstract': 'At Germany’s annual press ball, journalists were drinking away the realization that their industry is facing its biggest crisis since World War II.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/party-like-its-2012/', 'snippet': 'At Germany’s annual press ball, journalists were drinking away the realization that their industry is facing its biggest crisis since World War II.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Germany officially opened its winter party season last Friday with the annual Bundespresseball, the national press ball. The occasion has been bringing together politicians, journalists and social butterflies since 1951, and after almost a decade away from Berlin, I jumped on the chance to hobnob with the movers and shakers of Angela Merkel’s Germany.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Party Like It’s 2012', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Maiziere, Thomas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gauck, Joachim', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Times', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Frankfurter Allgemeine Zeitung', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T14:13:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lucian Kim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lucian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5159e212-c442-5e0b-a8dd-674bde11843f', 'word_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5159e212-c442-5e0b-a8dd-674bde11843f'}