ion of “immortal jellyfish,” he heads to one of several karaoke bars in Shirahama. His favorite ones are Kibarashi and Flipper, which has a dolphin as its icon. Last year Kubota won Flipper’s annual karaoke championship. He took me there one afternoon to show me his plaque. But it wasn’t on the wall. The attendant explained to us, with great remorse, that it had been thrown out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/magazine/28-jellyfish-man/28-jellyfish-man-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 172, 'width': 182, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/magazine/28-jellyfish-man/28-jellyfish-man-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 172, 'width': 182, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/magazine/28-jellyfish-man/28-jellyfish-man-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/28/magazine/28-jellyfish-man/28-jellyfish-man-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/magazine/28-jellyfish-man/28-jellyfish-man-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Immortal Jellyfish Man Has a Song for You', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jellyfish', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Karaoke', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T16:11:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathaniel Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91880ee2-59f6-526d-91b7-ed9644cb7d62', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91880ee2-59f6-526d-91b7-ed9644cb7d62'}, {'abstract': 'The recent loss of seven Yellowstone wolves wearing high-tech research collars is renewing the decades-old arguments about when and where hunters should be allowed to shoot the charismatic predators.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/research-animals-lost-in-wolf-hunts-near-yellowstone/', 'snippet': 'The recent loss of seven Yellowstone wolves wearing high-tech research collars is renewing the decades-old arguments about when and where hunters should be allowed to shoot the charismatic predators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bullet that killed one of Yellowstone National Park’s most popular wolves was felt halfway around the world by Gwen Deniel, of Brittany, France. She cried when she learned that the animal, which wore a research collar, was shot by a hunter in Wyoming’s Shoshone National Forest, a few miles outside the park boundary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Research Animals Lost in Wolf Hunts Near Yellowstone', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunting and Trapping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wolves', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Douglas W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name