 major weapon in the arsenal for mitigating climate change. It has been slow, though, to develop. One reason is cost. Power plants equipped with CCS cost roughly double ones that don’t have it. The technology is also still not completely proven. And there are fears that stored gas could escape to the surface.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Costs of Burying Carbon Emissions', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T16:27:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Reed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcf43d44-cbad-597c-9e19-79bb8217c2b4', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcf43d44-cbad-597c-9e19-79bb8217c2b4'}, {'abstract': 'Stuntmen perform at the Jhiri fair in Jammu, Jammu and Kashmir.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/image-of-the-day-nov-28/', 'snippet': 'Stuntmen perform at the Jhiri fair in Jammu, Jammu and Kashmir.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: Nov. 28', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T16:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/428bc8b4-a550-5077-b294-e435b1d0cd10', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/428bc8b4-a550-5077-b294-e435b1d0cd10'}, {'abstract': 'The Taviani brothers, now in their 80s, talk about their film “Caesar Must Die,” Italy’s entry for best foreign language film.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/even-in-their-80s-brothers-behind-the-camera/', 'snippet': 'The Taviani brothers, now in their 80s, talk about their film “Caesar Must Die,” Italy’s entry for best foreign language film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In their long and distinguished careers, which began in Italy in the 1950s, the brothers Paolo and Vittorio Taviani have won many awards for the films they have directed together, including prizes at the Cannes Film Festival for “Padre Padrone” in 1977 and “The Night of the Shooting Stars” in 1982. One top prize, however, has eluded them: they have never won the Oscar for best foreign-language film.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even in Their 80s, Brothers Behind the Camera', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taviani, Paolo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taviani, Vittorio', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T16:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba90e338-a09b-509e-9ae1-7ee7a6348742', 'word_count': 1167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba90e338-a09b-509e-9ae1-7ee7a6348742'}, {'abstra