one, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/us/TAXTALK-LN/TAXTALK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/23/us/TAXTALK-LN/TAXTALK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/us/TAXTALK-LN/TAXTALK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/us/TAXTALK-LN/TAXTALK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1280, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/us/TAXTALK-LN/TAXTALK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/23/us/TAXTALK-LN/TAXTALK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/23/us/TAXTALK-LN/TAXTALK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Look Before You Leap: Understanding the Mathematics of the Fiscal Cliff', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T17:47:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Honner and Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Honner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eedb810b-caf7-5128-a70c-448b3ab4cae7', 'word_count': 1901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eedb810b-caf7-5128-a70c-448b3ab4cae7'}, {'abstract': 'Pete Wells extols the struggling restaurants that have created communities, and asks readers to share memories.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/sandys-less-heralded-victims-the-places-that-bring-new-yorkers-together/', 'snippet': 'Pete Wells extols the struggling restaurants that have created communities, and asks readers to share memories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The accuracy of Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s statement on Monday that Hurricane Sandy had been “more impactful” than Katrina can be debated. Without taking sides, I think it’s safe to say that if your house or business went underwater last month, Sandy’s effect was the same as Katrina’s: terrible, life-altering destruction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sandy’s Less-Heralded Victims: The Places That Bring New Yorkers Together', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordinier, Jeff', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lomonaco, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheraton, Mimi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wells, Pete', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nathans Famous Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Totonno's Pizzeria Napolitano (Brooklyn, NY)", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T17:49:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/725184f4-f131-5082-88be-c103278028cd', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/725184f4-f131-5082-88be-c103278028cd'}, {'abstract': 'An Oregonian salt with the elegance of a fine fleur de sel, the delicate crunch of Maldon and the blindingly white flakes of a Caribbean beach at noon.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/finishing-touch-jacobsen-sea-salt/', 'snippet': 'An Oregonian salt with the elegance of a fine fleur de sel, the delicate crunch of Maldon and the blindingly white flakes of a Caribbean beach at noon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ben Jacobsen started making sea salt professionally only last year, but the crystalline flakes coaxed from water he gathers from Netarts Bay on the Oregon coast have the elegance of a fine fleur de sel, the delicate crunch of Maldon and the blindingly white flakes of a Caribbean beach at noon. If the sign of a good finishing salt is a balance of salinity and minerality, the flavor you find in a pinch of Jacobsen Salt is so pitch-perfect it tastes like it’s from a centuries-old European workshop instead of a start-up in the Pacific Northwest.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finishing Touch | Jacobsen Sea Salt', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Delicate Flavor By the Pinch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomfield, April', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T17:56:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oliver Strand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oliver', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23c9d138-8999-56ae-b18d-ea63a64d445f', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23c9d138-8999-56ae-b18d-ea63a64d445f'}, {'abstract': 'Knowing a harsh reaction would only isolate it more, Israel also toned down its threats of countermeasures after a vote Thursday on elevating Palestinians’ United Nations status.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/world/middleeast/israel-plays-down-significance-of-palestinians-un-bid.html', 'snippet': 'Knowing a harsh reaction would only isolate it more, Israel also toned down its threats of countermeasures after a vote Thursday on elevating Palestinians’ United Nations status.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — With Western support swelling in favor of a Palestinian bid for enhanced status at the United Nations, Israel engaged in damage control on Wednesday, a day before the vote. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Plays Down Importance of U.N. Bid by Palestinians', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Plays Down Significance of Palestinians’ U.N. Bid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T17:58:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1c19c00-c83d-5067-9fb1-9a9ddc689230', 'word_count': 881, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1c19c00-c83d-5067-9fb1-9a9ddc689230'}, {'abstract': 'Occupy Sandy, an Occupy Wall Street offshoot that helped storm victims, will show a new documentary outdoors tonight on the side of a building without a permit or the owner’s permission.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/occupy-movements-next-guerrilla-effort-a-film-screening/', 'snippet': 'Occupy Sandy, an Occupy Wall Street offshoot that helped storm victims, will show a new documentary outdoors tonight on the side of a building without a permit or the owner’s permission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost from the moment Hurricane Sandy struck New York, an ad hoc offshoot of Occupy Wall Street set to work collecting food and clothing for victims of the storm and sending volunteers to hard-hit areas like Red Hook, Brooklyn, and the Rockaways in Queens to clean out flooded basements and to repair damaged houses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Occupy’ Movement’s Next Guerrilla Effort: A Film Screening', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fox, Josh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T17:59:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6170e6c3-a1aa-5986-8425-7145f877589d', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6170e6c3-a1aa-5986-8425-7145f877589d'}, {'abstract': 'Gate Guru has partnered with the Avis-Budget Group to offer discounted last-minute car rentals.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/an-airport-app-takes-you-outside-to-a-rental-car/', 'snippet': 'Gate Guru has partnered with the Avis-Budget Group to offer discounted last-minute car rentals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gate Guru, the app that functions like a Yelp for travelers who want to eat, shop or even get a manicure at an airport, is venturing into new territory.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Airport App Takes You Outside, to a Rental Car', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Airport App Takes You Outside, to a Rental Car', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Avis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T18:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Drake', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drake', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecfe23ec-17e1-53ba-b6be-26aeb993e66d', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecfe23ec-17e1-53ba-b6be-26aeb993e66d'}, {'abstract': 'Many banks limit customers’ legal options by including arbitration clauses in checking account agreements.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/how-banks-limit-your-options-in-a-dispute/', 'snippet': 'Many banks limit customers’ legal options by including arbitration clauses in checking account agreements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ninety percent of Americans use checking accounts, but they are often unaware that agreements with their bank limit their legal options if there is a disagreement, a new report from an arm of the Pew Charitable Trusts finds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Banks Limit Your Options in a Dispute', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARBITRATION, CONCILIATION AND MEDIATION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Charitable Trusts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T18:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4562c00d-d635-526a-a263-9e451984ccd9', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4562c00d-d635-526a-a263-9e451984ccd9'}, {'abstract': 'If it succeeds in completing a charter by Thursday, Egypt’s constitutional assembly could make moot the power struggle between the courts and President Mohamed Morsi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/world/middleeast/wrangling-in-egypt-as-constitution-deadline-looms.html', 'snippet': 'If it succeeds in completing a charter by Thursday, Egypt’s constitutional assembly could make moot the power struggle between the courts and President Mohamed Morsi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Leaders of the assembly drafting a new constitution said Wednesday that they would complete their work by the next morning, a move that appeared aimed at trying to sidestep a power struggle between Egypt’s president and the courts over control of the political transition.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/world/egypt1/egypt1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/29/world/egypt1/egypt1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/world/egypt1/egypt1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/world/egypt1/egypt1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/world/egypt1/egypt1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/world/egypt1/egypt1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'imag