k Series', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'SLS AMG Black Series: A Little More Horsepower Is Never Enough', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Los Angeles Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T18:25:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerry Garrett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garrett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4168c07-5f55-5d43-9887-3a9afd5a64df', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4168c07-5f55-5d43-9887-3a9afd5a64df'}, {'abstract': 'Ray Tintori, the special-effects unit director for “Beasts of the Southern Wild,” discusses how the beasts of the title were created.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/below-the-line-the-beasts-of-beasts-of-the-southern-wild/', 'snippet': 'Ray Tintori, the special-effects unit director for “Beasts of the Southern Wild,” discusses how the beasts of the title were created.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The drama “Beasts of the Southern Wild,” which recently added the Gotham Awards to its prize mantle, explores a\xa0 fictionalized bayou community called the Bathtub. Directed by Benh Zeitlin and co-written by Mr. Zeitlin and Lucy Alibar, the film focuses on young Hushpuppy (Quvenzhané Wallis) and\xa0 how she handles both the failing health of her father (Dwight Henry) and a storm that threatens to wash away the world she has known.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/movies/beasts-4/beasts-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 532, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/movies/beasts-4/beasts-4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 532, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/movies/beasts-4/beasts-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/28/movies/beasts-4/beasts-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/movies/beasts-4/beasts-4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Below the Line: The Beasts of ‘Beasts of the Southern Wild’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Beasts of the Southern Wild (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pigs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tintori, Ray', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zeitlin, Benh', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T18:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3c8bf94-f6b3-5773-b388-bdf9d089afe8', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3c8bf94-f6b3-5773-b388-bdf9d089afe8'}, {'abstract': 'Many obese Type 2 diabetics who undergo gastric bypass surgery do not experience a remission of diabetes, and of those that do, about a third redevelop diabetes within five years of their operation.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/weight-loss-surgery-may-not-combat-diabetes-long-term/', 'snippet': 'Many obese Type 2 diabetics who undergo gastric bypass surgery do not experience a remission of diabetes, and of those that do, about a third redevelop diabetes within five years of their operation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Weight loss surgery, which in recent years has been seen as an increasingly attractive option for treating Type 2 diabetes, may not be as effective against the disease as it was initially thought to be, according to a new report. The study found that many obese Type 2 diabetics who undergo gastric bypass surgery do not experience a remission of their disease, and of those that do, about a third redevelop diabetes within five years of their operation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/17/health/well_diabetes/well_diabetes-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/17/health/well_diabetes/well_diabetes-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/17/health/well_diabetes/well_diabetes-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 489, 'width': 733, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/17/health/well_diabetes/well_diabetes-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 489, 'width': 733, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/17/health/well_diabetes/well_diabetes-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/17/health/well_diabetes/well_diabetes-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/17/health/well_diabetes/well_diabetes-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weight Loss Surgery May Not Combat Diabetes Long-Term', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bariatric Surgery', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T18:34:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9e46bb3-434b-5949-9238-e9ed1e65c7f5', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9e46bb3-434b-5949-9238-e9ed1e65c7f5'}, {'abstract': 'Based on effective field goal percentage, the Washington Wizards are the worst shooting team in the N.B.A., which is one reason for their 0-12 start.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/keeping-score-blame-shooting-woes-for-wizards-horrid-start/', 'snippet': 'Based on effective field goal percentage, the Washington Wizards are the worst shooting team in the N.B.A., which is one reason for their 0-12 start.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last season the Charlotte Bobcats might have been the worst team in N.B.A. history. They finished 7-59 and their winning percentage was .106, a league record for futility. But the 2011-12 Bobcats may soon have some company. On Monday the Washington Wizards became just the 11th N.B.A. team to start a season with 12 straight losses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: Blame Shooting Woes for Wizards’ Horrid Start', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ariza, Trevor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Wizards', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T18:35:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Kubatko', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kubatko', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5395db0e-ae9b-5010-9e33-534fb67a65f0', 'word_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5395db0e-ae9b-5010-9e33-534fb67a65f0'}, {'abstract': 'Explaining what would happen if the White House and Congress can’t reach a debt deal.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/what-happens-if-we-go-over-the-so-called-fiscal-cliff/', 'snippet': 'Explaining what would happen if the White House and Congress can’t reach a debt deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Taxes would rise for nearly every taxpayer and many businesses. Financing for most federal programs, military and domestic, would be cut. Many economists say that while annual budget deficits are too high, these new taxes and spending cuts would be too much deficit reduction, too suddenly, for a weak economy. More than $500 billion equals roughly 3 percent to 4 percent of gross domestic product. The Congressional Budget Office has said the result would be a short recession, though some analysts say the measures could be managed so they do less damage. “Slope,” they argue, is a better metaphor than cliff.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Happens if We Go Over the So-Called ‘Fiscal Cliff’?', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T18:35:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9b23bd2-98ae-5b43-813e-d28bf38f9932', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9b23bd2-98ae-5b43-813e-d28bf38f9932'}, {'abstract': 'The two-hour retrospective will be broadcast on Dec. 31, hours before the ball drop broadcast that bears Dick Clark’s name.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/abc-to-broadcast-dick-clark-special-on-new-years-eve/', 'snippet': 'The two-hour retrospective will be broadcast on Dec. 31, hours before the ball drop broadcast that bears Dick Clark’s name.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABC will show a two-hour retrospective of Dick Clark’s life on Dec. 31, hours before the ball drop broadcast that bears his name, the network said Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ABC to Broadcast Dick Clark Special on New Year’s Eve', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Remembering Dick Clark On New Year’s Eve', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Dick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seacrest, Ryan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Times Square and 42nd Street (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T18:37:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2ef6821-1ef1-5475-b509-2597b65d7865', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2ef6821-1ef1-5475-b509-2597b65d7865'}, {'abstract': 'Explaining the tax increases that would take place at the end of the year if a deal on the so-called ‘fiscal cliff’ is not reached.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/what-tax-increases-are-in-store-at-the-end-of-2012/', 'snippet': 'Explaining the tax increases that would take place at the end of the year if a deal on the so-called ‘fiscal cliff’ is not reached.', 'lead_paragraph': ' When a tax cut expires, the practical effect is a tax increase. And a slew of tax cuts — $400 billion for 2013 — expire on Dec. 31: All of the Bush-era rate reductions; smaller tax cuts that periodically expire for businesses and individuals; and the 2-percentage-point cut in payroll taxes that Mr. Obama pushed in 2010, which increased an average worker’s take-home pay by about $1,000 a year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Tax Increases Are in Store at the End of 2012?', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T18:38:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e5ad94c-69b1-589c-9e59-d7d4ab29c58d', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e5ad94c-69b1-589c-9e59-d7d4ab29c58d'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama said that he hoped to resolve a fiscal impasse before Christmas, but lawmakers should not wait to preserve current rates for income under $250,000.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/us/politics/president-obama-asks-congress-to-keep-tax-cuts-for-middle-class.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama said that he hoped to resolve a fiscal impasse before Christmas, but lawmakers should not wait to preserve current rates for income under $250,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama surrounded himself with taxpayers on Wednesday to pitch his plan to preserve current rates for the middle class and raise them for the wealthy. A day before, he met with small-business owners for the same purpose. On Friday, he plans to fly to Pennsylvania to tour a factory to make the same point.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/us/subCLIFF/subCLIFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/29/us/subCLIFF/subCLIFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/us/subCLIFF/subCLIFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/us/subCLIFF/subCLIFF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1183, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/us/subCLIFF/subCLIFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/us/subCLIFF/subCLIFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/us/subCLIFF/subCLIFF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Tilts Tax Debate Away From Spending Cuts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Tilts Tax Debate Away From Spending Cuts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T18:41:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fea95e7a-b7d5-58f5-9e8e-fdf2ed9d6b0c', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fea95e7a-b7d5-58f5-9e8e-fdf2ed9d6b0c'}, {'abstract': 'An explanation of what spending would be cut if a deal is not reached on the so-called ‘fiscal cliff.’', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/what-spending-would-be-cut-if-a-debt-deal-is-not-reached/', 'snippet': 'An explanation of what spending would be cut if a deal is not reached on the so-called ‘fiscal cliff.’', 'lead_paragraph': 'An emergency unemployment-compensation program is expiring, which would save $26 billion but end payments to millions of Americans who remain jobless and have exhausted state benefits. Medicare payments to doctors would be reduced 27 percent, or $11 billion, because this year Congress has not passed the usual so-called “doc fix” to block the cuts, which otherwise are required by a 1990s cost-control law.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Spending Would be Cut if a Debt Deal is Not Reached?', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T18:42:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73c72e15-11d2-5c28-93b3-9ab39e6f4ce8', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73c72e15-11d2-5c28-93b3-9ab39e6f4ce8'}, {'abstract': 'The fiscal and economic threat created by the parties was part intentional, part coincidental.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/explaining-the-origin-of-the-fiscal-threat/', 'snippet': 'The fiscal and economic threat created by the parties was part intentional, part coincidental.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fiscal and economic threat created by the parties was part intentional, part coincidental.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Explaining the Origin of the Fiscal Threat', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T18:45:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b99ff79-564a-5de2-8ef0-eda90ce5313c', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b99ff79-564a-5de2-8ef0-eda90ce5313c'}, {'abstract': 'It’s not exactly “War and Peace” redux.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/first-official-twitter-fiction-festival-begins/', 'snippet': 'It’s not exactly “War and Peace” redux.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twitter has already made a mark in the literary world, through experiments like Jennifer Egan’s tweet-by-tweet New Yorker story, “Black Box,” and Ben Okri’s line-a-day poem — not to mention the continuing debate over whether that microblogging service has turned the once-contentious literary world into a boring mutual appreciation society. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Official Twitter Fiction Festival Begins', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Imagine #WarandPeace', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T18:48:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94ea432c-6adf-5e33-b4fc-200a0ac9a19c', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94ea432c-6adf-5e33-b4fc-200a0ac9a19c'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Susan Collins of Maine, expressed doubts on Wednesday over the Obama administration’s handling of the attack in Libya, further clouding Susan E. Rice’s prospects as secretary of state.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/another-key-republican-senator-expresses-concern-over-rice/', 'snippet': 'Senator Susan Collins of Maine, expressed doubts on Wednesday over the Obama administration’s handling of the attack in Libya, further clouding Susan E. Rice’s prospects as secretary of state.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:20 p.m. | Updated  President Obama came to the defense of Susan E. Rice, his embattled ambassador to the United Nations, on Wednesday even as she came under fire from another Republican senator and saw her prospects for becoming secretary of state further clouded.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Calls Rice ‘Extraordinary,’ as Another Republican Voices Concerns', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi