at suffered water damage from Hurricane Sandy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Spot a Water-Damaged Car', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T19:22:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efa639fe-09d2-5cb5-96ff-f662cdb6a4ef', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efa639fe-09d2-5cb5-96ff-f662cdb6a4ef'}, {'abstract': 'There seems to be a different tablet for every man, woman, child and mutant. We offer a rundown on e-readers, tablets and mini-tablets for holiday gift-givers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/technology/personaltech/tablets-are-hot-holiday-gifts-but-which-one-to-buy-review.html', 'snippet': 'There seems to be a different tablet for every man, woman, child and mutant. We offer a rundown on e-readers, tablets and mini-tablets for holiday gift-givers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The other day, I joined NPR for a segment about high-tech holiday gifts. I was ready for the calls from listeners. I’d brushed up on cameras, phones, laptops, music players and game consoles. I was prepared to talk about limiting screen time, digital addiction, cyberbullying. I knew where to get the best deals.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/pogue-75/pogue-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/pogue-75/pogue-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hot Gift Is a Tablet, but Which to Buy?', 'kicker': 'State of the Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hot Gift\r\nIs a Tablet,\r\nBut Which\r\nTo Buy?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T19:27:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc0f3a3b-122b-5c14-a301-fff2b07450e9', 'word_count': 1304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc0f3a3b-122b-5c14-a301-fff2b07450e9'}, {'abstract': 'Is Tottenham-Arsenal the best soccer rivalry? Fulham-Chelsea? Goal readers, how do you vote?', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/what-are-the-best-soccer-rivalries/', 'snippet': 'Is Tottenham-Arsenal the best soccer rivalry? Fulham-Chelsea? Goal readers, how do you vote?', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Vecsey: What are the great local rivalries in world sports? The other day I wrote a column comparing the new Knicks-Nets rivalry to other New York rivalries. Some readers insisted the old Brooklyn Dodgers-New York Giants baseball rivalry was the best in American 