icle/d6558e69-0afc-55d4-9696-3b61b4f57458', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6558e69-0afc-55d4-9696-3b61b4f57458'}, {'abstract': 'In “Buddy: How a Rooster Made Me a Family Man,” Brian McGrory writes about his new, blended family and the title character who sometimes seemed to rule the roost.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/books/brian-mcgrorys-buddy-how-a-rooster-made-me-a-family-man.html', 'snippet': 'In “Buddy: How a Rooster Made Me a Family Man,” Brian McGrory writes about his new, blended family and the title character who sometimes seemed to rule the roost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brian McGrory, a former Boston Globe metro editor who now writes a twice-a-week column, has a sure hand for polished storytelling. In “Buddy,” his first nonfiction book, he is able to wring maximum comic effect from the Terrible Pet genre and also to tell a heartwarming family tale without trying too noticeably to warm the heart. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/book1/book1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 856, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/book1/book1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2023, 'width': 1692, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/book1/book1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/book1/book1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/book1/book1-thumb