ne': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/c2fa9137-9951-53de-8d08-9b1712a179f4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/c2fa9137-9951-53de-8d08-9b1712a179f4'}, {'abstract': 'The feud started when Jenny Johnson, a comic from Houston, took a potshot at Chris Brown and his 2009 assault on then-girlfriend Rihanna.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/fashion/chris-brown-deletes-twitter-account-after-rant.html', 'snippet': 'The feud started when Jenny Johnson, a comic from Houston, took a potshot at Chris Brown and his 2009 assault on then-girlfriend Rihanna.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE singer Chris Brown deleted his Twitter account last Sunday, after a profane and misogynistic rant against a comedy writer. The feud started when Jenny Johnson, a comic from Houston, took a potshot at Mr. Brown and his 2009 assault on then-girlfriend Rihanna. The 23-year-old singer replied with an expletive-laced tirade that was shared with his 11 million (make that former) Twitter followers. Here are some responses:', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/fashion/29HASHTAG_SPAN/29HASHTAG_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 477, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/29/fashion/29HASHTAG_SPAN/29HASHTAG_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 477}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/fashion/29HASHTAG_SPAN/29HASHTAG_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 815, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/fashion/29HASHTAG_SPAN/29HASHTAG_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1629, '