cker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Came; I Sawed; I Got a Hat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Chainsaw Gang (TV Program)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Country Music Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'American Chainsaw (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Geographic Channel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tools', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T23:13:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/41140e74-0b15-5c26-b640-714ec04f7696', 'word_count': 996, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41140e74-0b15-5c26-b640-714ec04f7696'}, {'abstract': 'Inspired by rock formations, UN Studio designs a new seating collection for Walter Knoll.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/garden/between-a-rock-and-a-soft-place.html', 'snippet': 'Inspired by rock formations, UN Studio designs a new seating collection for Walter Knoll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ben van Berkel, a founder of UN Studio, the Dutch architectural practice whose projects range from a sculpture in Millennium Park in Chicago to the Dance Palace in St. Petersburg, Russia, is an architect with a flair for furniture design. His My Chair for Walter Knoll, the 150-year-old German furniture manufacturer (not part of Knoll International, which was founded by Walter’s son, Hans) won a Red Dot Best of the Best award in 2009. Seating Stones, the firm’s latest project, attempts to repeat that success. The design, inspired by rock formations, with a flowing organic shape, radiates a playful charm and can be used alone or grouped in seemingly endless variations. The chair’s steel frame, padded in a high-grade foam, can be upholstered in a broad, colorful array of fabrics. Prices start from $3,885; through M2L, m2l.com or (212) 832-8222.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29FURNITURE_SPAN/29FURNITURE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29FURNITURE_SPAN/29FURNITURE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29FURNITURE_SPAN/29FURNITURE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 848, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29FURNITURE_SPAN/29FURNITURE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1547, 'width': 1869, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29FURNITURE_SPAN/29FURNITURE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29FURNITURE_SPAN/29FURNITURE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29FURNITURE_SPAN/29FURNITURE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Between a Rock and a Soft Place', 'kicker': 'Currents | Furniture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Between a Rock and a Soft Place', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chairs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'M2L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UN Studio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T23:14:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arlene Hirst', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arlene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirst', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc135c11-8315-5433-9e0f-b4339db0b867', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc135c11-8315-5433-9e0f-b4339db0b867'}, {'abstract': 'Jaime Hayon designs a new boutique for the company on Madison Avenue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/garden/lladro-opens-on-madison-avenue.html', 'snippet': 'Jaime Hayon designs a new boutique for the company on Madison Avenue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lladró, the Spanish producer of romantic figurines in milky shades of porcelain, has been stirring the pot. In 2006, it hired the flamboyant designer Jaime Hayon to oversee new collections. Parrots and knobby-headed aliens joined the shepherdesses and ballerinas, and bright lace-up shoes like the ones Mr. Hayon designed for Camper started appearing on some little statues.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29OPEN1_SPAN/29OPEN1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29OPEN1_SPAN/29OPEN1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29OPEN1_SPAN/29CURR4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29OPEN1_SPAN/29CURR4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29OPEN1_SPAN/29OPEN1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29OPEN1_SPAN/29OPEN1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29OPEN1_SPAN/29OPEN1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Warm Reception for Lladró', 'kicker': 'Currents | Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Warm Reception for Lladró', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lladro SA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T23:14:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Lasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0eba9255-9c33-56c9-b457-61a23d56d373', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0eba9255-9c33-56c9-b457-61a23d56d373'}, {'abstract': 'The PossibiliTree is easy to assemble and won’t shed needles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/garden/the-possibilitree-offers-an-alternative-to-the-evergreen.html', 'snippet': 'The PossibiliTree is easy to assemble and won’t shed needles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re tired of hauling home a live Christmas tree and the attendant mess of needle-dropping evergreens, not to mention the trials of disposal — yet you scorn plastic substitutes — the PossibiliTree might be for you. It was designed in 1982 by Richard Babcock, a Minneapolis architect, for his own home. Decades later, his daughter, her husband and her husband’s sister have turned it into a business, albeit a small custom one. The trees are all made from cherry, walnut or maple and are available in hanging and tabletop versions. The six-foot-tall hanging tree (53 inches at its widest point; $425) is designed to float 18 inches above the floor. There is a three-foot-tall table model (28 inches at its widest; $215) Both trees roll into a compact bundle for storage. Information: possibilitree.com or (612) 220-2639.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29DECOR1/29CURR2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 695, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29DECOR1/29CURR2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1391, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29DECOR1/29CURR2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29DECOR1/29CURR2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29DECOR1/29CURR2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Alternative Christmas Tree', 'kicker': 'Currents | Décor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Alternative Christmas Tree', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas Trees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Babcock, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T23:15:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arlene Hirst', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arlene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirst', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/722228dd-1ac8-58b6-8c26-c0a142737625', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/722228dd-1ac8-58b6-8c26-c0a142737625'}, {'abstract': 'Discounts on lighting, rugs, furniture and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/garden/sales-at-leucos-usa-luceplan-usa-and-others.html', 'snippet': 'Discounts on lighting, rugs, furniture and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leucos USA and Luceplan USA are having a warehouse sale from Friday to Sunday, with up to 70 percent off lighting and accessories (the Gio Ponti sconce for Leucos, regularly $3,520, will be $1,056; the Berenice table LED for Luceplan, regularly $590, will be $236); 70-