 Alegría Hudes, whose Pulitzer Prize winner, “Water by the Spoonful,” begins a run in New York this month, writing plays keeps her tethered to her family and hometown, Philadelphia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/theater/for-quiara-alegria-hudes-plays-are-family.html', 'snippet': 'For Quiara Alegría Hudes, whose Pulitzer Prize winner, “Water by the Spoonful,” begins a run in New York this month, writing plays keeps her tethered to her family and hometown, Philadelphia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE playwright Quiara Alegría Hudes lives in an eighth-floor apartment in Washington Heights with mesmerizing views of the Hudson. But she never strays far from Philadelphia, the city of her birth and the setting of nearly all her plays. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02QUIARA2_SPAN/02QUIARA2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02QUIARA2_SPAN/02QUIARA2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02QUIARA2_SPAN/02QUIARA2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02QUIARA2_SPAN/02QUIARA2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02QUIARA2_SPAN/02QUIARA2_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/12/02