nts finished here on Monday evening. The Mitchell Open Board-a-Match Teams was won by Michael Becker and Aubrey Strul of Boca Raton, Fla.; Steve Garner of Chicago; Howard Weinstein of Omaha; and Walid Elahmady and Tarek Sadek from Egypt. They finished one-and-one-third boards ahead of Ralph Katz of Burr Ridge, Ill.; Nick Nickell of New York City; Eric Rodwell of Clearwater Beach, Fla.; Bobby Levin of Henderson, Nev.; and Steve Weinstein of Andes, N.Y. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/card/card-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/arts/card/card-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mitchell Open Board-a-Match Teams', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-28T23:26:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5775da4a-29cd-54aa-8c09-3b085df5b31e', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5775da4a-29cd-54aa-8c09-3b085df5b31e'}, {'abstract': 'In Raleigh, N.C., a family trades 3,200 square feet of wasted space for lower taxe