chief executive, served Champagne and took lunch orders.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/business/Unitedjp/Unitedjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/29/business/Unitedjp/Unitedjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/business/Unitedjp/Unitedjp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/business/Unitedjp/Unitedjp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1392, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/business/Unitedjp/Unitedjp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/business/Unitedjp/Unitedjp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/business/Unitedjp/Unitedjp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For United, Big Problems at Biggest Airline', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Problems for Biggest Airline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smisek, Jeffery A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Continental Airlines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Airlines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Continental Holdings Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T00:55:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jad Mouawad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mouawad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b686ecc0-0a67-58c6-8dcd-6bf0bd1161e5', 'word_count': 1407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b686ecc0-0a67-58c6-8dcd-6bf0bd1161e5'}, {'abstract': 'What makes a piece of design a good gift? In a word, soul.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/garden/holiday-gifts-with-soul.html', 'snippet': 'What makes a piece of design a good gift? In a word, soul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY 7-year-old daughter, Shan, was glued to an “iCarly” marathon on a recent morning, slow to mute the TV during commercials, as her father has ordered. Instead, she chimed in with the pitches, repeating three little words, nine little letters, that every parent dreads, especially at holiday time.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29GIFT_SPAN/29JPGIFT9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29GIFT_SPAN/29JPGIFT9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29GIFT_SPAN/29JPGIFT9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29GIFT_SPAN/29JPGIFT9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29GIFT_SPAN/29JPGIFT9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29GIFT_SPAN/29JPGIFT9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/garden/29GIFT_SPAN/29JPGIFT9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Than Meets the Eye', 'kicker': 'The Details', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Than Meets the Eye', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T00:59:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Lasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1eedad3c-7aec-5488-a01a-a092086b6dff', 'word_count': 1273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1eedad3c-7aec-5488-a01a-a092086b6dff'}, {'abstract': 'Environmental news highlights for Wednesday, Nov. 28.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/on-our-radar-approaching-the-doha-climate-talks/', 'snippet': 'Environmental news highlights for Wednesday, Nov. 28.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the eve of the Doha climate summit, a foreign-policy expert reviews where things stand, while a Pakistani negotiator wonders if the chance to keep the temperature from rising more than two degrees Celsius is fast disappearing. “The window of opportunity is so small now that every misstep or lack of action could put the world in uncharted territory,” he writes. [Council on Foreign Relations] [The Express Tribune]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Approaching the Doha Climate Talks', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T01:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e306cefd-9322-5e9a-8136-2f0b1fe0143a', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e306cefd-9322-5e9a-8136-2f0b1fe0143a'}, {'abstract': 'What is “the press” today? It is a question without a simple answer, either in today’s rapidly changing media landscape or in Supreme Court doctrine.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/press-clips/', 'snippet': 'What is “the press” today? It is a question without a simple answer, either in today’s rapidly changing media landscape or in Supreme Court doctrine.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Justice Samuel A. Alito Jr. offered a provocative defense the other day of the Citizens United decision and its robust view of the First Amendment’s application to corporate speech. The 2010 decision, which invalidated federal restrictions on corporate campaign spending, has been criticized by, among others, many news organizations, including this one. But the press, above all, should have received Citizens United gratefully, Justice Alito suggested, because after all, newspapers are published by corporations. So without protection for corporate speech, consider how the press would have fared, he continued, in such landmark cases as New York Times v. Sullivan, which provided a strong defense against libel suits by public figures, or the Pentagon Papers case, which upheld the right to publish government secrets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Press Clips', 'kicker': 'Opinionator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens United v Federal Election Commission (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Denniston, Lyle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldstein, Thomas C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Potter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SCOTUSblog', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T01:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/915813f4-bf13-5b0e-97ce-9fc7ad4bc17a', 'word_count': 1286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/915813f4-bf13-5b0e-97ce-9fc7ad4bc17a'}, {'abstract': 'Despite an Israeli concession to permit fishing up to six nautical miles from shore, forces detained a Palestinian fisherman as his crew tried to venture farther into the Mediterranean Sea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/world/middleeast/israel-seizes-gaza-fishing-boats-near-offshore-limit.html', 'snippet': 'Despite an Israeli concession to permit fishing up to six nautical miles from shore, forces detained a Palestinian fisherman as his crew tried to venture farther into the Mediterranean Sea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GAZA — Despite an Israeli concession to permit Gazans to fish up to six nautical miles from shore rather than three, Israeli forces detained a Palestinian fisherman and seized two boats as their crews tried to venture farther into the Mediterranean Sea. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Seizes 2 Gaza Boats Near New Offshore Limit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Seizes 2 Gaza Boats Near New Offshore Limit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mediterranean Sea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T01:02:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fares Akram and Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fares', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akram', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3feed58-eb2e-5547-82a6-493ce4a37c75', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3feed58-eb2e-5547-82a6-493ce4a37c75'}, {'abstract': '“Without his invention we’d still be getting only black-and-white pictures from our digital cameras,” an industry expert said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/business/bryce-bayer-inventor-of-a-filter-to-make-color-digital-pictures-dies-at-83.html', 'snippet': '“Without his invention we’d still be getting only black-and-white pictures from our digital cameras,” an industry expert said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bryce Bayer, a retired Eastman Kodak research scientist who invented the checkerboard-like filter that has allowed millions of digital cameras to capture vivid color images, died on Nov. 13 in Bath, Me. He was 83. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/business/BAYER-obit/BAYER-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/business/BAYER-obit/BAYER-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1220, 'width': 845, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/business/BAYER-obit/BAYER-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/business/BAYER-obit/BAYER-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',