': '2012-11-29T01:59:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/72a2106b-8f9c-506e-ad83-f010652af707', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72a2106b-8f9c-506e-ad83-f010652af707'}, {'abstract': 'More brands that aren’t traditionally linked with the winter holidays are offering campaigns with holiday themes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/business/media/more-brands-offer-campaigns-with-holiday-themes.html', 'snippet': 'More brands that aren’t traditionally linked with the winter holidays are offering campaigns with holiday themes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE of the more unusual traditions of Christmas in America is the skein of commercials with holiday themes that appear each year — not only from retailers, which would be expected to advertise in the mad dash to Dec. 25, but also from marketers outside that realm. Brands like Coca-Cola, Miller beers and Norelco have become known for decades of seasonal greetings.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/business/Adco2/Adco2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/business/Adco2/Adco2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1384, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/business/Adco2/Adco2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/business/Adco2/Adco2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/business/Adco2/Adco2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marketers Find Ways to Link Their Brands to the Season', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marketers Find Ways to Link Their Brands To the Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T02:02:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9453a8a3-c78c-5ddd-97a9-ea63c6303cab', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9453a8a3-c78c-5ddd-97a9-ea63c6303cab'}, {'abstract': 'An Orange County ordinance prohibiting registered sex offenders from entering county parks was struck down by a panel of judges, who said the ban was pre-empted by state law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/us/california-sex-offender-ban-in-parks-is-struck-down.html', 'snippet': 'An Orange County ordinance prohibiting registered sex offenders from entering county parks was struck down by a panel of judges, who said the ban was pre-empted by state law.', 'lead_paragraph': ' An Orange County law prohibiting registered sex offenders from entering county parks has been struck down. The county government’s ban spawned similar laws in many of the cities within the county, rendering almost half of all public parks within Orange County off limits to sex offenders. In a unanimous decision this month, the three-judge panel of the Orange County Superior Court said that the ordinance was pre-empted by state law, and that the “adverse effect” of the ordinance on the “transient citizens of the state” outweighed possible benefits of the bans. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Sex-Offender Ban in Parks Is Struck Down', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Sex-Offender Ban In Parks Is Struck Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Orange County (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T02:07:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f528d7b-980e-5cd4-9a77-939a3384f857', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f528d7b-980e-5cd4-9a77-939a3384f857'}, {'abstract': 'Hyundai introduces a concept Veloster that has a lot of utility. And the roof is made from truck tarps.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/28/hyundai-veloster-c3-roll-top-concept-an-idea-machine/', 'snippet': 'Hyundai introduces a concept Veloster that has a lot of utility. And the r