river, and it won’t cause that much of a stir. Chances are it has been in the bag only a couple of years and hits crooked shots anyway.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Proposed Rule Riles Recreational Players', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Proposed Rule Riles Recreational Players', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Golf Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T03:02:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fbcc571-e06d-5b83-a86a-670b2899029e', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fbcc571-e06d-5b83-a86a-670b2899029e'}, {'abstract': 'The suit, in which Officer Craig Matthews of the Bronx had complained about numerical quotas for arrests, summonses and stops, had been dismissed in April.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/nyregion/court-reinstates-police-officers-lawsuit-over-arrest-quotas.html', 'snippet': 'The suit, in which Officer Craig Matthews of the Bronx had complained about numerical quotas for arrests, summonses and stops, had been dismissed in April.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal appeals court on Wednesday reinstated a lawsuit filed by a New York City police officer who accused his superiors of violating his First Amendment rights by punishing him for reporting the existence of an illegal arrest-quota system.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Officer’s Lawsuit Over Quotas Is Reinstated', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Officer’s Lawsuit Over Quotas Is Reinstated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matthews, Craig', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T03:03:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fca80ce3-6417-5399-9cae-a9c9423b2eea', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fca80ce3-6417-5399-9cae-a9c9423b2eea'}, {'abstract': 'Renee Jackson works, and supports a daughter, but cannot find an apartment within her means.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/nyregion/an-eviction-followed-by-a-parade-of-homeless-shelters.html', 'snippet': 'Renee Jackson works, and supports a daughter, but cannot find an apartment within her means.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If only he knew.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365,