s.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/i-b-m-and-ohio-state-university-to-open-center-for-big-data/', 'snippet': 'I.B.M. is opening a new data analytics center in Ohio, where it plans to hire 500 business analysts and researchers over the next three years. It will also work with Ohio State University to train students to fill a predicted skills gap in the fas...', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is plenty of debate about just how much Big Data analytics can help businesses make smarter decisions to increase sales and cut costs. Yet there seems to be no debate that there is already a shortage of data scientists and business analysts to feed the Big Data boom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I.B.M. and Ohio State University to Open Center for Big Data', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Business Machines Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ohio State University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T05:01:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d053d17-b95a-5d9f-a815-ca825f9355d1', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d053d17-b95a-5d9f-a815-ca825f9355d1'}, {'abstract': 'Can you solve the mystery of a circus trainer who had a run-in with a zebra?', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/think-like-a-doctor-the-circus-trainers-headache/', 'snippet': 'Can you solve the mystery of a circus trainer who had a run-in with a zebra?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Challenge: Can you solve the case of an animal trainer who develops an excruciating headache after a run-in with a zebra?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/health/28tlad_ctscan/28tlad_ctscan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/health/28tlad_ctscan/28tlad_ctscan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1582, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/health/28tlad_ctscan/28tlad_ctscan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/28/health/28tlad_ctscan/28tlad_ctscan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/health/28tlad_ctscan/28tlad_ctscan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Think Like a Doctor: The Circus Trainer’s Headache', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T05:01:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Sanders, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanders', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94a6ef91-e147-50a5-9b52-71088eaf7dfd', 'word_count': 1297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94a6ef91-e147-50a5-9b52-71088eaf7dfd'}, {'abstract': 'A sharply critical report says the agency has not put in place safeguards against fraud and abuse in encouraging the switch to electronic medical records.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/business/medicare-is-faulted-in-electronic-medical-records-conversion.html', 'snippet': 'A sharply critical report says the agency has not put in place safeguards against fraud and abuse in encouraging the switch to electronic medical records.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The conversion to electronic medical records — a critical piece of the Obama administration’s plan for health care reform — is “vulnerable” to fraud and abuse because of the failure of Medicare officials to develop appropriate safeguards, according to a sharply critical report to be issued Thursday by federal investigators.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/business/RECORDS-alt/RECORDS-alt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/business/RECORDS-alt/RECORDS-alt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1401, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicare Is Faulted on Shift to Electronic Records', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Medicare Is Faulted on Shift to Electronic Records', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronic Health Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Human Services Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of Inspector General', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T05:05:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6df930e5-aa63-5a92-80d1-ebddd9938a2e', 'word_count': 1222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6df930e5-aa63-5a92-80d1-ebddd9938a2e'}, {'abstract': 'Edgar Valdez Villareal, who the authorities contend is an American-born drug kingpin known as “El Barbie,” accused  the head of the public security department of taking bribes from him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/world/americas/mexican-drug-suspect-accuses-officials-of-corruption.html', 'snippet': 'Edgar Valdez Villareal, who the authorities contend is an American-born drug kingpin known as “El Barbie,” accused  the head of the public security department of taking bribes from him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Edgar Valdez Villareal, who the authorities contend is an American-born drug kingpin known as “El Barbie,” accused top government officials, including the head of the public security department, of taking bribes from him. Mr. Villareal leveled the charges from jail, where he is awaiting trial on drug trafficking charges, in a letter published Wednesday in Reforma, a leading newspaper, and also delivered to several news organizations by his lawyer. The officials, he wrote, “are part of the criminal structure of this country.” A government spokesman, in a statement, called Mr. Villareal’s letter an effort to discredit the federal police and blackmail the authorities into giving him better prison conditions. He was captured in August 2010. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexican Drug Suspect Accuses Officials of Corruption', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Drug Suspect Accuses Officials of Corruption', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Villareal, Edgar Valdez', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T05:38:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/eab3f0ad-85b5-5ba4-9bb1-a44758c86339', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eab3f0ad-85b5-5ba4-9bb1-a44758c86339'}, {'abstract': 'Pople’s Daily Online deleted a story that gave that title to Kim Jong-un, seemingly misinterpreting a parody in The Onion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/world/asia/china-north-korea-leader-is-sexiest-man-no-longer.html', 'snippet': 'Pople’s Daily Online deleted a story that gave that title to Kim Jong-un, seemingly misinterpreting a parody in The Onion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People’s Daily Online on Wednesday deleted a story and 55-photo slide show that named Kim Jong-un, the young, chubby ruler of North Korea, the “Sexiest Man Alive of 2012.” The package by the People’s Daily Online, which is run by People’s Daily, the Communist Party mouthpiece, appeared to misinterpret a parody in The Onion, a satirical newspaper and Web site, about Mr. Kim being ranked the “sexiest man,” treating it as serious news. An editor at People’s Daily Online told The Associated Press on Wednesday that the news organization had now realized the Onion story was satire. The editor added that People’s Daily Online had picked up the story from the Web site of Guangming Daily, a major party newspaper. He Ning, an editor at Guangming Daily, said in an interview that she had picked up the article from another Web site and “had no idea that the news was satire.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: North Korea Leader Is ‘Sexiest Man’ No Longer', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: North Korea Leader Is ‘Sexiest Man’ No Longer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Onion, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Daily", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T05:42:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a2c0467-706e-50e4-a87d-0350825dfa47', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a2c0467-706e-50e4-a87d-0350825dfa47'}, {'abstract': 'María Lourdes Afiuni was put on trial on Wednesday nearly three years after being charged with corruption and abuse of power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/world/americas/venezuelan-judge-is-tried-3-years-after-being-charged.html', 'snippet': 'María Lourdes Afiuni was put on trial on Wednesday nearly three years after being charged with corruption and abuse of power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A jailed judge at the center of one of the country’s most prominent human rights cases was put on trial on Wednesday nearly three years after being charged with corruption and abuse of power. The judge, María Lourdes Afiuni, refused to enter the courtroom, and the judge presiding over her case ordered the trial to proceed without her. Ms. Afiuni was arrested in December 2009 after ruling that a jailed businessman should be freed while awaiting trial, a move that angered President Hugo Chávez. Ms. Afiuni’s lawyer had revealed in recent days that she was raped while in prison in 2010, became pregnant and had an abortion. A prison official said there was no rape.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuelan Judge Is Tried 3 Years After Being Charged', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuela: Judge Is Tried 3 Years After Being Charged', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Afiuni, Maria Lourdes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T05:48:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/102da1da-a713-5a93-9794-8cccb5f8882b', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/102da1da-a713-5a93-9794-8cccb5f8882b'}, {'abstract': 'The Jindal Steel and Power vs. Zee News case is just the latest example, analysts say.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/in-india-paid-news-has-soared-with-competition/', 'snippet': 'The Jindal Steel and Power vs. Zee News case is just the latest example, analysts say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Indian television news, hidden cameras are often used to catch a politician accepting a bribe or a big business giving one. A recent “sting” operation also had a conglomerate’s executives on camera, but it was the journalists who got stung.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is ‘Extortion’ the New ‘Ad Sales’ in India’s News Industry?', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jindal, Naveen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian National Congress', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T05:55:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sruthi Gottipati', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sruthi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gottipati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6cb26b2-40a4-56e6-ac2b-fd6dc5c4440c', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6cb26b2-40a4-56e6-ac2b-fd6dc5c4440c'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/arts/television/whats-on-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:45 A.M. (MoreMax) BEGINNERS (2011) In the first of two father-and-son tales starring Ewan McGregor, Christopher Plummer (above left, with Mr. McGregor), in an Oscar-winning role, plays Hal, the septuagenarian father of Oliver (Mr. McGregor), for whom he has two announcements: that he is gay and that he has terminal cancer. This film from the writer and director Mike Mills weaves together two love stories, one past and one present, that gradually fuse into a single life. Goran Visnjic plays Hal’s much younger partner; Mélanie Laurent is Anna, the French actress who sweeps Oliver away from his misery; and a scene-stealing Cosmo is Arthur, Hal’s Jack Russell terrier. “So much of ‘Beginners’ seems, looks, sounds, feels so hermetically perfect you may long for some air to blow, stir and even mess up its bright Los Angeles homes, the swanky old hotel where Anna stays and all these precious moments,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. “Even so, the movie’s attractions are undeniable, including its narrative design, which seems more complex than it is, but is engaging to piece together. And the performers are charming, particularly Ms. Laurent and Mr. Plummer, with his killer eyes (still seducing after all these years) and a voice that echoes in your ears.” In “Big Fish” (2003), at 6:50 p.m. on HBO Signature, Albert Finney plays Edward Bloom (Mr. McGregor is his youthful version), a traveling salesman from Alabama who has spent a lifetime embellishing the truth in this fantasy from Tim Burton, adapted from the novel by Daniel Wallace. Billy Crudup is Bloom’s estranged son, Will, a reporter in Paris who has been summoned home for a deathbed reconciliation, during which Edward elaborates on his biography. Edward’s doctor asks: Wouldn’t Will prefer to believe that on the day of his birth his father was subduing a legendary catfish rather than selling household gadgets in Wichita? “The movie insists that the only possible answer is yes, and thus chooses maudlin moonshine over engagement with the difficulties of real life, which is exactly the choice Edward has made,” A. O. Scott wrote in The Times. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T06:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/accf9b5a-fe12-5813-ac85-a2e4d2908678', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/accf9b5a-fe12-5813-ac85-a2e4d2908678'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/news-quiz-november-29-2012/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | November 29, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T07:30:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66dc06cb-0d32-5c2d-87cf-947554e670c0', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66dc06cb-0d32-5c2d-87cf-947554e670c0'}, {'abstract': 'News and arts from today’s International Herald Tribune.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/iht-quick-read-nov-29/', 'snippet': 'News and arts from today’s International Herald Tribune.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWS Leaders of the Egyptian assembly drafting a new constitution said Wednesday that they would complete their work by the next morning, a move that appeared aimed at trying to defuse a political crisis that has gripped the country since the president issued an edict that put his decisions above judicial scrutiny. David D. Kirkpatrick reports from Cairo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/world/middleeast/29egypt/29egypt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/29/world/middleeast/29egypt/29egypt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/world/middleeast/29egypt/29egypt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/world/middleeast/29egypt/29egypt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/world/middleeast/29egypt/29egypt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/world/middleeast/29egypt/29egypt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/world/middleeast/29egypt