b_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/plastics-bans-in-the-works-for-delhi-and-shanghai/', 'snippet': 'India and China are starting to implement curbs on plastic bags and restrictions on excessive packaging.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Two recent items of news from Asia appear to show that the region’s nations are starting to take seriously the ever-growing amounts of plastic trash they produce.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Delhi and Shanghai Aim to Reduce Plastic Trash', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China Daily', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T09:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bettina Wassener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bettina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wassener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/824697cf-4843-5429-88c8-3f74b19f7db5', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/824697cf-4843-5429-88c8-3f74b19f7db5'}, {'abstract': 'What did The Onion say about Kim Jong-un that was quoted in the People’s Daily of China?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/parody-article-taken-seriously/', 'snippet': 'What did The Onion say about Kim Jong-un that was quoted in the People’s Daily of China?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Kim Jong-un Seems to Get a New Title: Heartthrob,” Edward Wong writes about a parody by the satirical newspaper The Onion that was apparently taken seriously by the Chinese Communist Party’s official news site.', 'source': 