y statute.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/world/europe/leveson-report-phone-hacking-scandal-britain.html', 'snippet': 'An inquiry triggered by The News of the World scandal recommended a new system of press regulation that would be backed by parliamentary statute.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — After months of hearings, a long-awaited report on the behavior of British newspapers embroiled in the phone hacking scandal recommended on Thursday a new system of press regulation that would be backed by parliamentary statute, setting up what threatened to develop into an acrimonious political debate about curbs on Britain’s 300-year-old tradition of broad press freedom.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/world/hacking/hacking-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/world/hacking/hacking-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1372, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/world/hacking/hacking-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/30/world/hacking/hacking-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/world/hacking/hacking-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hacking Report Says New Regulatory System Needed for British Newspapers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hacking Report Says New Regulatory System Needed for British Newspapers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News International Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Press Complaints Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leveson, Brian (1949- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T09:27:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns and Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/058aaa67-4017-5cc4-b9e7-fcd5c53cf742', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/058aaa67-4017-5cc4-b9e7-fcd5c53cf742'}, {'abstract': 'Her interest in human rights and labor issues in Bangladesh led Taslima Akhter to photography. This week, as she has four times before, she raced to a factory fire that killed workers left with no way out.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/fighting-hopelessness-amid-ashes/', 'snippet': 'Her interest in human rights and labor issues in Bangladesh led Taslima Akhter to photography. This week, as she has four times before, she raced to a factory fire that killed workers left with no way out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Taslima Akhter was overcome with emotion when she arrived at the Tazreen Fashions garment factory on the outskirts of Dhaka, Bangladesh, on Sunday evening, four hours after fire tore through the building. She watched firefighters battle the blaze — which killed at least 112 people\xa0— as throngs of workers and family members waited to see if their loved ones\xa0had survived.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting Hopelessness Amid Ashes', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dhaka (Bangladesh)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T10:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fe67644-53eb-5403-b443-80326c523864', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fe67644-53eb-5403-b443-80326c523864'}, {'abstract': 'The opportunity to choose strong reformers to head key agencies may yield to the goal of pleasing prominent people in the financial sector, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/dropping-the-ball-on-financial-regulation/', 'snippet': 'The opportunity to choose strong reformers to head key agencies may yield to the goal of pleasing prominent people in the financial sector, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Johnson is the Ronald A. Kurtz Professor of Entrepreneurship at the M.I.T. Sloan School of Management and co-author of “White House Burning: The Founding Fathers, Our National Debt, and Why It Matters to You.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dropping the Ball on Financial Regulation', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krawcheck, Sallie L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T10:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9489b4d-0720-59f0-8910-53e8d46e49cc', 'word_count': 1141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9489b4d-0720-59f0-8910-53e8d46e49cc'}, {'abstract': 'In the three years since this blog wrote last about the problem of older people who hoard, new treatments and services have become available.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/new-help-for-hoarders/', 'snippet': 'In the three years since this blog wrote last about the problem of older people who hoard, new treatments and services have become available.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were times, Sandra Stark remembers, when she couldn’t use her kitchen or sit on her sofa. Her collections — figurines, vases, paperweights — had overtaken every closet, drawer and surface. Stacks of clothing and old magazines added to the clutter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Help for Hoarders', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hoarding', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T10:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56f64433-cc85-5902-accc-94adeb8df275', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56f64433-cc85-5902-accc-94adeb8df275'}, {'abstract': 'Read a Times review of a deranged new show, “Killer Karaoke,” then tell us what your signature karaoke song would be, as well as your thoughts on the concept of this show in general.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/whats-your-karaoke-song/', 'snippet': 'Read a Times review of a deranged new show, “Killer Karaoke,” then tell us what your signature karaoke song would be, as well as your thoughts on the concept of this show in general.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Have you ever sung karaoke? Even if you haven’t, what song do you think you would choose to belt out if you were handed the mic? Why? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None,