e of Sunday’s games, with the benefit of film analysis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A closer look at some Week 12 games, with the benefit of film analysis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week 12 N.F.L. Film Review', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T10:09:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/056119e3-8019-51bf-a5d9-6d5c5380531a', 'word_count': 1395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/056119e3-8019-51bf-a5d9-6d5c5380531a'}, {'abstract': 'The 18-year-old star Justin Bieber toggled between high-definition popstravaganza and sneaky intimacy in his concert Wednesday night at Madison Square Garden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/arts/music/justin-bieber-at-madison-square-garden.html', 'snippet': 'The 18-year-old star Justin Bieber toggled between high-definition popstravaganza and sneaky intimacy in his concert Wednesday night at Madison Square Garden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every minute, on the minute, they yelled. On Wednesday night the screen high above the Madison Square Garden stage was counting down the time until Justin Bieber, the post-boy, not-quite-man pop star, would take the stage. Each time the clock counted down past a “:00,” out came the shrieks: real throaty noises, crescendoing to a squeal and then retreating. The tiny kids, the preteens, the teenagers, even a few of the moms — they all did it. That’s the ritual, and it always has been. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'sourc