 it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/magazine/the-autism-advantage.html', 'snippet': 'Thorkil Sonne is betting that, given the right environment, an autistic adult could not just hold down a job but also be the best person for it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Thorkil Sonne and his wife, Annette, learned that their 3-year-old son, Lars, had autism, they did what any parent who has faith in reason and research would do: They started reading. At first they were relieved that so much was written on the topic. “Then came sadness,” Annette says. Lars would have difficulty navigating the social world, they learned, and might never be completely independent. The bleak accounts of autistic adults who had to rely on their parents made them fear the future.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/magazine/02autism1/02autism1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/12/02/magazine/02autism1/02autism1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/magazine/02autism1/mag-02Autism-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/magazine/02autism1/mag-02Autism-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/magazine/02autism1/02autism1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/12/02/magazine/02autism1/02autism1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/magazine/02autism1/02autism1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Autism Advantage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Autism Inc.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Specialisterne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sonne, Thorkil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denmark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T12:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gareth Cook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gareth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cook', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81deb1a3-d7f3-5558-a2da-85c75c6c5c8d', 'word_count': 4446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81deb1a3-d7f3-5558-a2da-85c75c6c5c8d'}, {'abstract': 'If you take the leap and add overhead to handle the extra sales you are expecting but those sales don’t appear, your business can fail.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/what-it-takes-to-crack-the-lower-middle-market/', 'snippet': 'If you take the leap and add overhead to handle the extra sales you are expecting but those sales don’t appear, your business can fail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When people think about small businesses, they often think about those in what is known as the lower middle market. These businesses typically do more than $5 million a year in sales, and they often have more than 25 employees. It’s good work if you can get it. For one thing, if your business is in this group, you are likely to get regular offers from people who are interested in buying your company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What It Takes to Crack the Lower Middle Market', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T12:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Patrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patrick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5b2f086-53c6-56b2-a0fd-e04ec00a68c7', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5b2f086-53c6-56b2-a0fd-e04ec00a68c7'}, {'abstract': 'The New York City men’s wear brand Isaora has blended two of the season’s popular cold-weather trends: the down jacket and the pullover.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/an-alternative-approach-to-down-isaora-down-pullover/', 'snippet': 'The New York City men’s wear brand Isaora has blended two of the season’s popular cold-weather trends: the down jacket and the pullover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York City men’s wear brand Isaora has blended two of the season’s popular cold-weather trends: the down jacket and the pullover.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Alternative Approach to Down', 'kicke