', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taliban Warlord Said to Have Been Wounded in Pakistan Bombing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nazir, Maulavi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T12:42:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Declan Walsh and Ismail Khan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ismail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddd6f7d3-4126-538d-ae4d-49a4f227e268', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddd6f7d3-4126-538d-ae4d-49a4f227e268'}, {'abstract': 'A Boston Globe writer argues that General Manager Mike Tannenbaum needs to be moved aside to start the rebuilding of the Jets.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/a-case-for-keeping-rex-ryan/', 'snippet': 'A Boston Globe writer argues that General Manager Mike Tannenbaum needs to be moved aside to start the rebuilding of the Jets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Continual “self-inflicted wounds” seem to be a sign that …1) You should put away the sharp implements.2) You should get some outside help. Greg A. Bedard of The Boston Globe recently made that case for the Jets, but first he argued that Woody Johnson needed to make one key call, around which everything else will pivot. Here are some extended excerpts from Bedard; you should read the whole thing. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Case for Keeping Rex Ryan', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tannenbaum, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T12:43:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca89b290-a255-5055-ac73-d3bcef3d7fad', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca89b290-a255-5055-ac73-d3bcef3d7fad'}, {'abstract': 'A sharply critical report says the agency, while encouraging the switch to electronic medical records, has not developed appropriate safeguards against fraud and abuse.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/daily-report-medicare-is-faulted-on-shift-to-electronic-records/', 'snippet': 'A sharply critical report says the agency, while encouraging the switch to electronic medical records, has not developed appropriate safeguards against fraud and abuse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The use of electronic medical records has been central to the aim of overhauling health care in America. Advocates contend that electronic records systems will improve patient care and lower costs through better coordination of medical services. The privacy protection of those records has been a primary concern.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: Medicare Is Faulted on Shift to Electronic Records', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronic Health Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T12:50:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c7eafe8-f685-53cc-bf4c-55926145ec3f', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c7eafe8-f685-53cc-bf4c-55926145ec3f'}, {'abstract': 'New York stages have recently been crowded with productions of Chekhov.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/theater/ben-brantley-on-chekhov-on-new-york-stages.html', 'snippet': 'New York stages have recently been crowded with productions of Chekhov.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A SOUND rises from the throat of a terminally ill woman in the second act of Chekhov’s “Ivanov,” and it is the noise of life itself. You can hear it rendered, with nuanced form and contradictory content, by Joely Richardson in the Classic Stage Company’s current revival of this early play by Anton Chekhov, one of a multitude of productions of his work that opened in New York and London this year.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02CHEKHOV1_SPAN/02CHEKHOV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02CHEKHOV1_SPAN/02CHEKHOV-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02CHEKHOV1_SPAN/02CHEKHOV-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 778, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02CHEKHOV1_SPAN/02CHEKHOV-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1556, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/0