s that it will find a larger audience at the box office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No Broadway show is losing money faster than “Scandalous,” the $9 million musical about the turbulent life of early-20th-century evangelist Aimee Semple McPherson. Given its weak ticket sales and largely negative reviews, many veteran Broadway producers would have closed the show soon after it opened on Nov. 15. And yet “Scandalous” continues to run.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29artsbeat-scandalous/29artsbeat-scandalous-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29artsbeat-scandalous/29artsbeat-scandalous-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1339, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29artsbeat-scandalous/29artsbeat-scandalous-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29artsbeat-scandalous/29artsbeat-scandalous-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29artsbeat-scandalous/29artsbeat-scandalous-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Scandalous’ Producers Keep Faith in a Struggling Show', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Scandalous’ Producers Keep the Show Going', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name