', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202-BTB/1202-BTB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 721, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202-BTB/1202-BTB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1441, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202-BTB/1202-BTB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202-BTB/1202-BTB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202-BTB/1202-BTB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pete Townshend: By the Book', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pete Townshend', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Townshend, Pete', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T16:26:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce915769-74f3-5b8f-a8a0-026fed013f5d', 'word_count': 1514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce915769-74f3-5b8f-a8a0-026fed013f5d'}, {'abstract': 'How to guard against food-poisoning-like symptoms when cooking red kidney beans.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/a-query-on-cooking-beans-safely/', 'snippet': 'How to guard against food-poisoning-like symptoms when cooking red kidney beans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One reader of my bean hole story this week advised me that red kidney beans should always be boiled for 10 minutes in order to kill certain proteins that can cause intestinal distress with symptoms similar to food poisoning. After a bit of research, I found that these beans do indeed contain a particularly high concentration of proteins called lectins that can cause discomfort unless changed to a harmless derivative by heat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Query on Cooking Beans Safely', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schlesinger, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T16:32:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Willoughby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Willoughby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99e2740b-9e00-5da0-bf3e-5fada340a6fa', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99e2740b-9e00-5da0-bf3e-5fada340a6fa'}, {'abstract': 'Serge Klarsfeld, a lifelong Nazi hunter (or “militant of memory,” as he prefers to call himself), has compiled a colossal new work documenting 76,000 deported Jews.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/a-life-dedicated-to-pursuing-nazis-and-remembering-their-victims/', 'snippet': 'Serge Klarsfeld, a lifelong Nazi hunter (or “militant of memory,” as he prefers to call himself), has compiled a colossal new work documenting 76,000 deported Jews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Serge Klarsfeld tells it, he had the “luck” to see his father and other French Jews in Nazi-occupied Nice carted off to Auschwitz by Germans. It spared him the pain of seeing them rounded up, as often happened, by their own French countrymen. Since Sept. 30, 1943, when he huddled behind a secret closet wall with his mother and sister while his father was seized by the SS for deportation and death, Mr. Klarsfeld, now a prominent French lawyer, has dedicated his life to memorializing victims of the Holocaust and bringing their killers to justice, most notably the notorious Gestapo chief in France, Klaus Barbie.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/nyregion/29cityroom-nazi/29cityroom-nazi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/nyregion/29cityroom-nazi/29cityroom-nazi-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1405, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/nyregion/29cityroom-nazi/29cityroom-nazi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/30/nyregion/29cityroom-nazi/29cityroom-nazi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/nyregion/29cityroom-nazi/29cityroom-nazi-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'widt