, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T16:43:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17dcaf33-0782-54d2-bd7c-59b00b61234e', 'word_count': 1286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17dcaf33-0782-54d2-bd7c-59b00b61234e'}, {'abstract': 'The third installment of the festival includes 10 programs – most of them double or triple bills, with collaborations between the ensembles and soloists – and runs from Jan. 25 through March 21.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/ecstatic-music-festival-unveils-genre-crossing-line-up/', 'snippet': 'The third installment of the festival includes 10 programs – most of them double or triple bills, with collaborations between the ensembles and soloists – and runs from Jan. 25 through March 21.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In its first two seasons, the Ecstatic Music Festival has helped transform Merkin Concert Hall from a relatively staid chamber music hall in the shadow of Lincoln Center into a lively home for the experimental, genre-crossing music of the indie classical world. The third installment of the festival includes 10 programs – most of them double or triple bills, with collaborations between the ensembles and soloists – and runs from Jan. 25 through March 21.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ecstatic Music Festival Unveils Genre-Crossing Line-Up', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Broad Lineup For Ecstatic Festival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ecstatic Music Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenstein, Judd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Merkin Concert Hall', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T16:45:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d743a34-d527-5ecb-9e4b-fdcd49507198', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d743a34-d527-5ecb-9e4b-fdcd49507198'}, {'abstract': 'Manslaughter convictions against Continental Airlines were overturned in a case involving an Air France Concorde jet whose deadly crash hastened the end of commercial supersonic travel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/business/global/french-court-overturns-conviction-in-concorde-crash.html', 'snippet': 'Manslaughter convictions against Continental Airlines were overturned in a case involving an Air France Concorde jet whose deadly crash hastened the end of commercial supersonic travel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — A French appeals court on Thursday overturned the involuntary manslaughter conviction against Continental Airlines for its role in the crash in 2000 of an Air France Concorde jet outside Paris that killed 113 people and hastened the end of commercial supersonic travel.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/business/Concord2/Concord2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/business/Concord2/Concord2-superJumbo