ount': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3f86152-abe9-5433-af51-cfe65b172d68'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Simkin’s repertory at the American Ballet Theater has included the Nutcracker-Prince in “The Nutcracker,” Benvolio in “Romeo and Juliet,” the Bronze Idol in “La Bayadère,” Franz in “Coppélia,” and Puck in “The Dream.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/american-ballet-theater-dancer-daniil-simkin-promoted-to-principal/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Simkin’s repertory at the American Ballet Theater has included the Nutcracker-Prince in “The Nutcracker,” Benvolio in “Romeo and Juliet,” the Bronze Idol in “La Bayadère,” Franz in “Coppélia,” and Puck in “The Dream.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniil Simkin, who joined American Ballet Theater as a soloist in 2008, has been promoted to principal dancer effective immediately, Kevin McKenzie, the company’s artistic director, announced on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Ballet Theater Dancer Daniil Simkin Promoted to Principal', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T17:11:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27201bff-0e7c-5edc-b356-29787208499d', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27201bff-0e7c-5edc-b356-29787208499d'}, {'abstract': 'Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. made a surprise stop at a newly opened Costco in Washington on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/biden-shops-at-costco/', 'snippet': 'Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. made a surprise stop at a newly opened Costco in Washington on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:17 p.m. | Updated  A time of austerity in the nation’s capital? Not for Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr., who went on a holiday shopping spree at a new Costco store on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden Shops at Costco', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T17:12:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/319b0e1c-6ea0-5b20-b1bd-fc3d2d810478', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/319b0e1c-6ea0-5b20-b1bd-fc3d2d810478'}, {'abstract': 'The new film “Lincoln” doesn’t just get history right – it advances a novel historical argument.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/steven-spielberg-historian/', 'snippet': 'The new film “Lincoln” doesn’t just get history right – it advances a novel historical argument.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having worked before at the intersection of Hollywood and history, helping a tiny bit with a respectable movie about the Cuban missile crisis called “Thirteen Days,” I approached the new movie “Lincoln” with measured expectations. I had seen how a film could immerse viewers in onscreen time travel without messing up the history too much. But that was the most I hoped for. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steven Spielberg, Historian', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutional Amendments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spielberg, Steven', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T17:13:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Zelikow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zelikow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b83fee5-a654-54bf-8fa0-8fdd8afdd071', 'word_count': 1813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b83fee5-a654-54bf-8fa0-8fdd8afdd071'}, {'abstract': 'Daniel Swee, casting director, explains how he chose actors for a revival of “Golden Boy.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/theater/casting-golden-boy-for-broadway.html', 'snippet': 'Daniel Swee, casting director, explains how he chose actors for a revival of “Golden Boy.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'NINETEEN actors will take their bows when “Golden Boy,” Lincoln Center Theater’s revival of Clifford Odets’s 1937 play, opens Thursday on Broadway at the Belasco Theater. A few, like the Emmy winner Tony Shalhoub of “Monk,” will be familiar faces; many more will be recognizable in that “I know I know him” way that lets character actors both pay the bills and ride the subway in peace. At least two have previous experience with Odets, having worked with the director Bartlett Sher on his acclaimed 2006 revival of “Awake and Sing!”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29GOLDEN_SPAN/29GOLDEN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29GOLDEN_SPAN/29GOLDEN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29GOLDEN_SPAN/29GOLDEN_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29GOLDEN_SPAN/29GOLDEN_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29GOLDEN_SPAN/29GOLDEN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29GOLDEN_SPAN/29GOLDEN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29GOLDEN_SPAN/29GOLDEN_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Find That Golden Boy and Entourage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Find That Golden Boy and Entourage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shalhoub, Tony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 4