367608-0e03-54e9-bac0-990a330fe432'}, {'abstract': 'The actor in a scene from the 2012 production of Ayad Akhtar’s play “Disgraced,” at the Claire Tow Theater at Lincoln Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/theater/100000001881318/aasid-mandvi.html', 'snippet': 'The actor in a scene from the 2012 production of Ayad Akhtar’s play “Disgraced,” at the Claire Tow Theater at Lincoln Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The actor in a scene from the 2012 production of Ayad Akhtar’s play “Disgraced,” at the Claire Tow Theater at Lincoln Center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/video-aasif/video-aasif-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/video-aasif/video-aasif-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/video-aasif/video-aasif-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/09/arts/video-aasif/video-aasif-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Aasif Mandvi (2012)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Disgraced (Play)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AKHTAR, AYAD', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandvi, Aasif', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T18:08:17+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'David Frank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/c7550f9c-bf02-5671-a62c-55b52458e099', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/c7550f9c-bf02-5671-a62c-55b52458e099'}, {'abstract': 'We’re excited to introduce “In Performance,” a regular theater video series, that kicks off this week with Aasif Mandvi in a scene from Ayad Akhtar’s play “Disgraced.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/in-performance-aasif-mandvi-of-disgraced/', 'snippet': 'We’re excited to introduce “In Performance,” a regular theater video series, that kicks off this week with Aasif Mandvi in a scene from Ayad Akhtar’s play “Disgraced.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’re excited to introduce “In Performance,” a regular theater video series, that kicks off this week with Aasif Mandvi in a scene from Ayad Akhtar’s “Disgraced,” now at the Claire Tow Theater at Lincoln Center. “In Performance,” which features actors performing monologues and songs from their current shows, has only a few simple rules: Scenes are about two minutes long. The actors wear street clothes and no stage makeup. And, of course, they keep their language clean.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Aasif Mandvi of ‘Disgraced’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandvi, Aasif', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T18:09:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d30bb5ad-08b3-5e0d-8662-846570357f92', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d30bb5ad-08b3-5e0d-8662-846570357f92'}, {'abstract': 'Attacks across the country left 32 dead in Hilla and killed 16 more in Karbala, Falluja, Mosul and Baghdad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/world/middleeast/bombings-in-iraq-kill-at-least-48.html', 'snippet': 'Attacks across the country left 32 dead in Hilla and killed 16 more in Karbala, Falluja, Mosul and Baghdad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — As workers gathered for breakfast on Thursday at a restaurant in Hilla, a Shiite-dominated city south of the capital, an explosives-laden car parked outside blew up, sending shrapnel ripping through the crowd. As an ambulance raced to the scene, another car was in pursuit, driven by a suicide bomber — who detonated his payload just as the first responders gathered.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/world/middleeast/30iraq/30iraq-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/30/world/middleeast/30iraq/30iraq-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/world/middleeast/30iraq/30iraq-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/world/middleeast/30iraq/30iraq-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 204