mpany say they are in active talks with about 110 suitors.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:22 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Gives Final Approval to Hostess’s Wind-Down Plan', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hostess Brands', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T18:24:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5de07a95-ef15-51d4-b666-3d9eed85f709', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5de07a95-ef15-51d4-b666-3d9eed85f709'}, {'abstract': 'The premiere of a short documentary about climate change and Occupy Wall Street’s storm-relief efforts was presented in flash-mob style.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/psst-were-showing-a-film-on-this-guys-wall-and-oh-dont-warn-him/', 'snippet': 'The premiere of a short documentary about climate change and Occupy Wall Street’s storm-relief efforts was presented in flash-mob style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a Hollywood film premiere, sequined starlets drift across red carpets. At an Occupy Wall Street film premiere, people trespass on gas station parking lots.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/nyregion/29sandyfilm1-cityroom/29sandyfilm1-cityroom-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/nyregion/29sandyfilm1-cityroom/29sandyfilm1-cityroom-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1346, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/nyregion/29sandyfilm1-cityroom/29sandyfilm1-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/nyregion/29sandyfilm1-cityroom/29sandyfilm1-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/nyregion/29sandyfilm1-cityroom/29sandyfilm1-cityroom-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Psst, We’re Showing a Film on This Guy’s Wall, and, Oh, Don’t Warn Him', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fox, Josh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKibben, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T18:24:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6988141b-f207-5bbe-b2be-a0737ea31b21', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6988141b-f207-5bbe-b2be-a0737ea31b21'}, {'abstract': 'Inside Battersby, one of the most buzzed-about restaurants in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/edible-selby-batter-up/', 'snippet': 'Inside Battersby, one of the most buzzed-about restaurants in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We didn’t even write down on paper what the menu would be until the night before we opened,” says Joseph Ogrodnek, half of the chef duo behind Battersby, one of the most buzzed-about restaurants in Brooklyn. Food was the one part of opening a restaurant that Ogrodnek and his partner, Walker Stern, who cooked together at Alain Ducasse at the Essex House, knew they had in the bag. Their pork shoulder, served with coco beans, literally melts in the mouth. Even their kale salad, dressed with fish sauce and lime juice and mixed with kohlrabi, stands out among the seemingly endless iterations of kale salads across the city. Ogrodnek and Stern had intended to keep their menu simple, and their prices low, but they abandoned that approach. “Our original plan was to keep it low-end, or more casual,” Ogrodnek says. “But as we got in the kitchen, we realized we couldn’t do that.” Brooklyn is grateful.Related: Interactive slideshow • Video Feature', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '70', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Edible Selby | Batter Up', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Batter Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T18:25:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Todd Selby and Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Todd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Selby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3734eeb-a278-5aa2-8867-9370a3576836', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3734eeb-a278-5aa2-8867-9370a3576836'}, {'abstract': 'Children’s submissions depicting the storm that pummeled the city in late October.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/11/26/nyregion/kdtn-sandy-ss.html', 'snippet': 'Children’s submissions depicting the storm that pummeled the city in late October.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Children’s submissions depicting the storm that pummeled the city in late October.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/nyregion/kdtn-sandy-ss-slide-V3L8/kdtn-sandy-ss-slide-V3L8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/26/nyregion/kdtn-sandy-ss-slide-V3L8/kdtn-sandy-ss-slide-V3L8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 444}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/nyregion/kdtn-sandy-ss-slide-V3L8/kdtn-sandy-ss-slide-V3L8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/nyregion/kdtn-sandy-ss-slide-V3L8/kdtn-sandy-ss-slide-V3L8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1479, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/nyregion/kdtn-sandy-ss-slide-V3L8/kdtn-sandy-ss-slide-V3L8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/26/nyregion/kdtn-sandy-ss-slide-V3L8/kdtn-sandy-ss-slide-V3L8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/26/nyregion/kdtn-sandy-ss-slide-V3L8/kdtn-sandy-ss-slide-V3L8-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kids Draw the News: Hurricane Sandy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T18:27:58+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/70e22b9d-b32d-51bd-9d10-4d2f7e7ed989', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/70e22b9d-b32d-51bd-9d10-4d2f7e7ed989'}, {'abstract': '“Top Chef’s” online offshoot, “Last Chance Kitchen,” is in some ways even better than its broadcast parent.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/watchlist-last-chance-kitchen-the-rare-web-series-to-challenge-the-tv-original/', 'snippet': '“Top Chef’s” online offshoot, “Last Chance Kitchen,” is in some ways even better than its broadcast parent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every self-respecting television show has an online extension these days — webisodes, behind-the-scenes clips, comic Q&A’s with the stars. But no one has integrated TV and Internet offerings as completely as the producers of Bravo’s “Top Chef.” For the second season in a row they are offering the Web series “Top Chef: Last Chance Kitchen” as an essential part of their menu — the starch to the TV show’s protein.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watchlist: ‘Last Chance Kitchen,’ the Rare Web Series to Challenge the TV Original', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web-Original Programming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bravo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T18:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c083297-99a9-5166-96b5-73c8204bb533', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c083297-99a9-5166-96b5-73c8204bb533'}, {'abstract': 'Former Gov. Mitt Romney visited the White House on Thursday for a private lunch with President Obama, their first encounter since the presidential election', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/romney-arrives-to-dine-with-obama/', 'snippet': 'Former Gov. Mitt Romney visited the White House on Thursday for a private lunch with President Obama, their first encounter since the presidential election', 'lead_paragraph': '4:15 p.m. | Updated  Former Gov. Mitt Romney visited the White House on Thursday for a private lunch with President Obama, their first encounter since the presidential election as both men try to put the bitterness of a hard-fought and often nasty campaign behind them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Visits the White House', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White House (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T18:34:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bef4290-22a9-5a5b-b1c7-c9312341c1b2', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bef4290-22a9-5a5b-b1c7-c9312341c1b2'}, {'abstract': 'The concert, “A Special Evening With Neil Young & Crazy Horse,” will be held at the Borgata Hotel Casino & Spa on Dec. 6, and all proceeds will go to the American Red Cross’s storm relief fund.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/neil-young-announces-hurricane-sandy-benefit-concert/', 'snippet': 'The concert, “A Special Evening With Neil Young & Crazy Horse,” will be held at the Borgata Hotel Casino & Spa on Dec. 6, and all proceeds will go to the American Red Cross’s storm relief fund.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Neil Young and Crazy Horse will do a benefit concert at a casino in Atlantic City to raise money for people displaced by Hurricane Sandy.\xa0The concert, “A Special Evening With Neil Young & Crazy Horse,” will be held at the Borgata Hotel Casino & Spa on Dec. 6, a publicist for Mr. Young announced on Thursday. Everest, an alternative rock band from Los Angeles, will open the show. Tickets, which go on sale Friday on the casino’s Web site, will cost $75 to $150.\xa0Mr. Young has pledged all the proceeds will go to the American Red Cross’s relief fund for victims of the storm.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29artsbeat-neil/29artsbeat-neil-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29artsbeat-neil/29artsbeat-neil-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29artsbeat-neil/29artsbeat-neil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29artsbeat-neil/29artsbeat-neil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29artsbeat-neil/29artsbeat-neil-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Neil Young Announces Hurricane Sandy Benefit Concert', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Neil Young Announces Hurricane Benefit Show', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crazy Horse', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Neil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN RED CROSS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T18:36:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e70cac7-9ceb-5043-9fe2-e2df0adaa47c', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e70cac7-9ceb-5043-9fe2-e2df0adaa47c'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of Iwase Yoshiyuki’s photographs of the ama divers in Japan, a majority of whom are women and plunge as deep as 80 feet into the sea to collect pearls, abalone and prized coral.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/the-women-who-free-dive-finding-riches-in-the-sea/', 'snippet': 'A selection of Iwase Yoshiyuki’s photographs of the ama divers in Japan, a majority of whom are women and plunge as deep as 80 feet into the sea to collect pearls, abalone and prized coral.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s cover story is about a small sea creature that can live forever. Called the “immortal jellyfish,” but also referred to as the Benjamin Button jellyfish, it can regenerate itself over and over. Only one man in the world keeps them in a lab, a Japanese scientist named Shin Kubota. As Nathaniel Rich writes, Kubota is currently “our best chance for understanding this unique strand of biological immortality.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/magazine/28-ama-divers-slide-KY6C/28-ama-divers-slide-KY6C-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 875, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/28/magazine/28-ama-divers-slide-KY6C/28-ama-divers-slide-KY6C-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1750, 'width