article/8c620f1d-1a89-59f6-861c-3e90e5690fb3', 'word_count': 1238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c620f1d-1a89-59f6-861c-3e90e5690fb3'}, {'abstract': 'The theme of the Disney ride is the individual, custom design of the cars.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/test-track-at-epcot-offers-hands-on-design-experience/', 'snippet': 'The theme of the Disney ride is the individual, custom design of the cars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the attractions at Disney’s Epcot Center in Florida has been the General Motors test track ride. After being closed for several months, a refurbished and reimagined version of the ride opens on Dec. 6. It’s now called Test Track Presented by Chevrolet.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Track at Epcot Offers Hands-On Design Experience', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.M. Test Track Reopens at Epcot Center', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMUSEMENT AND THEME PARKS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T18:41:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Patton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b6f2841-0e4e-5956-a199-34d07b8130ad', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b6f2841-0e4e-5956-a199-34d07b8130ad'}, {'abstract': 'The Museum of Modern Art has acquired the first 14 titles in a planned collection of about 40 games, including Pac-Man, Tetris and The Sims.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/moma-adds-video-games-to-its-collection/', 'snippet': 'The Museum of Modern Art has acquired the first 14 titles in a planned collection of about 40 games, including Pac-Man, Tetris and The Sims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you have been disparaging video games – or, perhaps, trying to wean yourself from an addiction to them – it’s time to think again. Video games are now high culture, with the imprimatur of the Museum of Modern Art, which announced on Thursday that it has acquired the first 14 titles in a planned collection of about 40 games. These constitute a new category among the museum’s collections, and will be on display in the Philip Johnson Galleries starting in March. (An exhibition devoted to video games will open in December at the Museum of the Moving Image, and another exhibition, at the Smithsonian American Art Museum, closed in September.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29artsbeat-video/29artsbeat-video-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29artsbeat-video/29artsbeat-video-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/arts/29artsbeat-video/29artsbeat-video-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'ima