rt. | New York City’s race for mayor gets under way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lunch meeting for two former rivals. | The stakes for same-sex marriage as it reaches the Supreme Court. | New York City’s race for mayor gets under way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast Politics | Romney Visits the White House', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NEW YORK CITY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T19:42:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c87b569-1bc3-5e76-b0e8-57a338623e41', 'word_count': 29, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c87b569-1bc3-5e76-b0e8-57a338623e41'}, {'abstract': 'Because of a unique dual-class share structure, Orient-Express directors control the company and have the power to block any takeover bid.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/at-orient-express-the-board-holds-all-the-cards/', 'snippet': 'Because of a unique dual-class share structure, Orient-Express directors control the company and have the power to block any takeover bid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Orient-Express Hotels, the Bermuda-based owner of luxury hotels, has received an unsolicited offer to be acquired by the Indian Hotels Company, a subsidiary of the Tata Group. In surveying the potential battle for control, I am certain of only one thing: It’s good to be a director of Orient-Express – and it’s likely to stay that way. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Orient-Express, the Board Holds All the Cards', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orient-Express Hotels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tata Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T19:44:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d804000-f579-56ac-bba8-246b523eac6d', 'word_count': 1304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d804000-f579-56ac-bba8-246b523eac6d'}, {'abstract': 'Tyrann Mathieu, the L.S.U. defensive back thrown off the team earlier this year, will try for an N.F.L. career.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/mathieu-announces-for-n-f-l-draft/', 'snippet': 'Tyrann Mathieu, the L.S.U. defensive back thrown off the team earlier this year, will try for an N.F.L. career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In perhaps Thursday’s least surprising news, Louisiana State’s deposed defensive back Tyrann Mathieu announced that he was making himself eligible for the 2013 N.F.L. draft. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/sports/ncaafootball/29tyrann/29tyrann-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/29/sports/ncaafootball/