s Skyactiv technology rollout with the new Mazda 6, a design based on the Takeri concept shown in New York this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Introduced on Thursday: 2014 Skyactiv Mazda 6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mazda 6: And Now a Diesel', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Los Angeles Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mazda Motor Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T20:19:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tori Tellem', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tellem', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90aa1980-f187-5aff-8798-3cb63110651c', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90aa1980-f187-5aff-8798-3cb63110651c'}, {'abstract': 'The world premiere of Mohammed Fairouz’s opera “Sumeida’s Song” will open the Prototype festival in January.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/fairouz-opera-premiere-will-open-the-prototype-festival/', 'snippet': 'The world premiere of Mohammed Fairouz’s opera “Sumeida’s Song” will open the Prototype festival in January.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The world premiere of Mohammed Fairouz’s “Sumeida’s Song,” an opera based on the Egyptian playwright Tawfiq El-Hakim’s “Song of Death,” will be directed by David Herskovits, and conducted by Steven Osgood, with a cast that includes Rachel Calloway, Dan Kempson, Edwin Vega and Amelia Watkins. The show is to open the first Protoype: Opera/Theater/Now festival, which runs Jan. 9 to Jan. 18 in New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fairouz Opera Premiere Will Open the Prototype Festival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fairouz, Mohammed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HERE Arts Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T20:26:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3091de8c-010f-5444-a03d-3e8bab60eaef', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3091de8c-010f-5444-a03d-3e8bab60eaef'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Levine will lead the Metropolitan Opera orchestra at Carnegie Hall, which will be his first public performance in two years after a series of health problems.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/levines-comeback-concert-to-include-work-by-schubert-and-beethoven/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Levine will lead the Metropolitan Opera orchestra at Carnegie Hall, which will be his first public performance in two years after a series of health problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Schubert’s Symphony No. 9, “The Great”; the prelude to Act I of Wagner’s “Lohengrin”; and Beethoven’s Piano Concerto No. 4, with Evgeny Kissin as soloist, will make up the program for James Levine’s comeback as a conductor on May 19. Mr. Levine will lead the Metropolitan Opera orchestra at Carnegie Hall, and it will be his first public performance in two years after a series of health problems. The program replaces another one, which was announced when it was not clear whether Mr. Levine could conduct and no conductor was listed. The lineup then was Sibelius’ Symphony No. 4, the Grieg piano concerto and Schumann’s “Konzertstück” for four horns and orchestra.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Levine’s Comeback Concert to Include Work by Schubert and Beethoven', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Levine Plans Comeback', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levine, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luisi, Fabio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T20:27:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acd64121-7f08-5566-aaf9-133c4f0fdbd2', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acd64121-7f08-5566-aaf9-133c4f0fdbd2'}, {'abstract': 'A new online venture offers original literary readings by video.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/book-forum/', 'snippet': 'A new online venture offers original literary readings by video.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent years, the literary community has been experimenting more and more with video. Publishers now produce slick YouTube trailers to promote new novels, and scrappy journals have begun innovative video series, like Electric Literature’s wacky animations based on short-story excerpts. Now comes an online venture, Henry, which films serious writers like Sam Lipsyte, Ben Marcus and Christine Schutt reading three-minute snippets from their work. “Our aim is to provide access to literary readings for people who don’t live in proximity to KGB Bar or the small places in Brooklyn where readings are usually held,” said Katherine Bernard, a writer for Vogue and the Paris Review Daily, who founded the site with her boyfriend, Shayne Barr, a Columbia M.F.A. writing graduate, and Jerone Hsu, the founder of the think tank Prime Produce. Barr and Bernard were inspired to begin Henry after attending an illuminating reading by the short-story writer Gary Lutz. “His work is emotionally devastating,” Barr says. “We were expecting to be brought to tears by his reading, but when he began to read he was sort of giggling through the lines, and we became aware for the first time of this ripple of humor that’s coursing through the text.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '62', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Forum', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Book Forum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T20:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d3a6810-b99e-5897-97a7-23c65a646018', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d3a6810-b99e-5897-97a7-23c65a646018'}, {'abstract': 'The i3 Concept Coupe is a sporty, three-door version of BMW’s previously shown i3 city car.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/bmw-i3-concept-coupe-looks-only-