ajor': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T21:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b1cbcbe-88ff-5707-bc93-56400d5137d1', 'word_count': 1190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b1cbcbe-88ff-5707-bc93-56400d5137d1'}, {'abstract': 'Each of the Big Four accounting firms has some involvement in the controversy over Hewlett-Packard’s acquisition of the software company Autonomy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/business/auditors-clash-in-hp-deal-for-autonomy.html', 'snippet': 'Each of the Big Four accounting firms has some involvement in the controversy over Hewlett-Packard’s acquisition of the software company Autonomy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The battle over Hewlett-Packard’s claim that it was bamboozled when it bought Autonomy, a British software company, has been long on angry rhetoric and short on details about the accounting that was supposedly wrong and led to an $8.8 billion write-down.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Clash of Auditors in H.P. Deal', 'kicker': 'High & Low Finance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Clash Of Auditors In H.P. Deal And Loss', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'KPMG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Autonomy Corp PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ERNST & YOUNG', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deloitte Consulting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hewlett-Packard Company', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T21:06:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a59aed6c-a007-50e1-8d2e-5b669e4fd35c', 'word_count': 1451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a59aed6c-a007-50e1-8d2e-5b669e4fd35c'}, {'abstract': 'At times, Andre Miller and Ty Lawson are fantastic as a pairing, but it is difficult to see how they complement each other in the Nuggets’ offense.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/the-nuggets-split-personality-backcourt/', 'snippet': 'At times, Andre Miller and Ty Lawson are fantastic as a pairing, but it is difficult to see how they complement each other in the Nuggets’ offense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Karl’s offense in Denver is famously simple: run hard for transition attempts, attack the rim off the dribble, don’t hold the ball. The common-sense goal is to accumulate as many layups, free throws and assists as possible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Nuggets’ Split-Personality Backcourt', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karl, George', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawson, Ty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Andre', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Nuggets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T21:06:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Beckley Mason', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Beckley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mason', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b600f5a8-f8bb-52f3-ae0b-5405a8364e36', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b600f5a8-f8bb-52f3-ae0b-5405a8364e36'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Patriarch,” David Nasaw writes about Joseph P. Kennedy, a larger-than-life paterfamilias who endowed his children with a sense of destiny and his own driving will.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/books/david-nasaws-patriarch-on-joseph-p-kennedy.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Patriarch,” David Nasaw writes about Joseph P. Kennedy, a larger-than-life paterfamilias who endowed his children with a sense of destiny and his own driving will.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He was one of the most famous fathers in history and a mythic figure in the public imagination: Wall Street tycoon, Hollywood buccaneer, notorious proponent of appeasement during World War II and, most especially, larger-than-life paterfamilias who endowed his children — John F. Kennedy, Robert F. Kennedy and Edward M. Kennedy, among them — with a sense of destiny and his own driving will. He was the ruthless outsider who charmed, bullied and manipulated his way into the corridors of power; the charismatic and intimidating magnate whose progeny, his latest biographer, David Nasaw, writes, “would complete the journey from Dunganstown, Ireland, to East Boston to the pinnacle of American political power and social prominence that their father had begun.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30BOOK/30BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 712, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30BOOK/30BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 712, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30BOOK/30BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30BOOK/30BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30BOOK/30BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Just Wait Till Your Father Gets Home', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Just Wait Till Your Father Gets Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Joseph P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nasaw, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T21:09:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c87480b-a1dd-5048-bf85-07be72860dff', 'word_count': 1445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c87480b-a1dd-5048-bf85-07be72860dff'}, {'abstract': 'A bill, approved by the Judiciary Committee, would require law enforcement officials to obtain a warrant from a judge before gaining access to messages in individual accounts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/technology/senate-committee-approves-stricter-privacy-for-e-mail.html', 'snippet': 'A bill, approved by the Judiciary Committee, would require law enforcement officials to obtain a warrant from a judge before gaining access to messages in individual accounts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Senate Judiciary Committee on Thursday approved a bill that would strengthen privacy protection for e-mails by requiring law enforcement officials to obtain a warrant from a judge in most cases before gaining access to messages in individual accounts stored electronically. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/business/Email/Email-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/business/Email/Email-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1437, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Panel Approves a Bill to Safeguard E-Mail', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Panel Approves a Bill To Safeguard E-Mail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T21:15:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c23fb422-c938-54c6-b2d7-71dde4dce049', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c23fb422-c938-54c6-b2d7-71dde4dce049'}, {'abstract': 'The recent post on what not to save on while traveling got some terrific responses. Here is a selection.', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/penny-for-your-pound-foolish-thoughts/', 'snippet': 'The recent post on what not to save on while traveling got some terrific responses. Here is a selection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The recent post on what not to save on while traveling got some terrific responses. Most readers agreed with Seth that even frugal traveling should have its limits:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Penny for Your Pound-Foolish Thoughts', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T21:19:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE NEW YORK TIMES', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f0fac22-192a-5d13-b9f1-c6976a3412ae', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f0fac22-192a-5d13-b9f1-c6976a3412ae'}, {'abstract': 'So far, Democrats have been the only ones who have been serious about Medicare’s future, because they’re the only ones who are not conflicted about its mission.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/medicare-off-the-menu/', 'snippet': 'So far, Democrats have been the only ones who have been serious about Medicare’s future, because they’re the only ones who are not conflicted about its mission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama served a lunch of white turkey chili today to the man who accused him of having “robbed” Medicare of $716 billion. The president, trying to show magnanimity, was undoubtedly too polite to bring up this outrageous charge by Mitt Romney, one of the lowest in a dishonest campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicare Off the Menu', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T21:20:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/515c3f3b-8af7-571e-b723-cdf2551e3593', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/515c3f3b-8af7-571e-b723-cdf2551e3593'}, {'abstract': 'Creative Commons, a literary festival sponsored by the South Asian Women’s Creative Collective, links different types of artists who explore storytelling in the digital age.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/nyregion/literary-festival-by-south-asian-womens-creative-collective.html', 'snippet': 'Creative Commons, a literary festival sponsored by the South Asian Women’s Creative Collective, links different types of artists who explore storytelling in the digital age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our media may have multiplied, diversified and metastasized almost to the breaking point, but our need to tell and be told simple human stories is intact. This weekend the South Asian Women’s Creative Collective is sponsoring Creative Commons, a “transmedia literary festival” that explores this paradox. Featuring artists working on the stage, page and screen, the events are linked by their exploration of storytelling in the digital age.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30MISER1/30MISER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30MISER1/30MISER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30MISER1/30MISER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30MISER1/30MISER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30MISER1/30MISER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Literary Festival Examines Digital Age', 'kicker': 'Weekend Miser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "South Asian Women's Creative Collective", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Public Library', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wikipedia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T21:20:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. C. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8436b656-1692-5f3f-b71f-23dbb917b02a', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8436b656-1692-5f3f-b71f-23dbb917b02a'}, {'abstract': 'A D.I.Y. solution to tie-dye the Japanese way, courtesy of Jane Palmer.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/to-dye-for/', 'snippet': 'A D.I.Y. solution to tie-dye the Japanese way, courtesy of Jane Palmer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When designers want their fabric colors to come naturally, they call Jane Palmer. The L.A.-based dye artisan behind Noon Design Studio, Palmer has a reputation for bringing a chemist’s fastidiousness and consistency to the often erratic art of vegetable dyeing. Her vivid custom hues, obtained via roots, bark, mineral powders and even crushed insects, lend artisanal loveliness to the collections of clients like Dosa’s Christina Kim and the cool-kid interiors firm Commune, for whom Palmer recently produced blankets dyed with natural indigo, chestnuts and French yellow flowers.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'hea