ed about the fate of the daily-deals pioneer’s chief executive, Andrew Mason. More specifically, that the company’s board would discuss at a meeting on Thursday whether he should remain in his post.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Status Quo at Groupon as Board Stands by Chief', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mason, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Groupon Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T22:42:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4c63cc3-ba57-59ed-9b86-fe72394efc42', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4c63cc3-ba57-59ed-9b86-fe72394efc42'}, {'abstract': '“Matisse: In Search of True Painting,” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, is one of the most thrillingly instructive exhibitions about this painter, or painting in general, that you may ever see.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/arts/design/matisse-exhibition-at-the-metropolitan-museum-of-art.html', 'snippet': '“Matisse: In Search of True Painting,” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, is one of the most thrillingly instructive exhibitions about this painter, or painting in general, that you may ever see.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The great French modernist Henri Matisse (1869-1954) was not a joiner. In the early 20th century he led the brief blitz of the Fauves — those “wild beasts” of fiery colors and blunt textures — but otherwise abstained from the signal movements of modern art.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30MATISSE1/30MATISSE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 273, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30MATISSE1/30MATISSE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 273}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30MATISSE1/30MATISSE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 466, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30MATISSE1/30MATISSE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 933, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30MATISSE1/30MATISSE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30MATISSE1/30MATISSE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30MATISSE1/30MATISSE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Evolving Toward Ecstasy', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Evolving Toward Ecstasy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matisse, Henri', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T22:44:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bac1d2e-e4a4-56c0-b6e7-a78a3eb6f663', 'word_count': 1373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bac1d2e-e4a4-56c0-b6e7-a78a3eb6f663'}, {'abstract': 'The insurance company, which works with Macy’s to sell toy versions of its duck mascot in support of pediatric cancer hospitals, is enlisting a range of social-networking sites.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/from-its-charity-efforts-aflac-learns-what-works-in-social-media/', 'snippet': 'The insurance company, which works with Macy’s to sell toy versions of its duck mascot in support of pediatric cancer hospitals, is enlisting a range of social-networking sites.', 'lead_paragraph': ' These are early days for marketers trying to figure out what role social media should play in their efforts to woo consumers. One major advertiser, the insurance company Aflac, is adjusting its strategies to generate a deeper emotional connection — and spur more donations — for its big annual holiday season charity fund-raiser.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Its Charity Efforts, Aflac Learns What Works in Social Media', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFLAC INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Macy's Inc", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-29T22:50:46+0000', 'document_type': 'artic