tor Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Stock Car Auto Racing', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T00:22:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerry Garrett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garrett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/745379c3-84d7-5be3-84d8-f9b336492ce3', 'word_count': 536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/745379c3-84d7-5be3-84d8-f9b336492ce3'}, {'abstract': 'After taking a hit on investments in biofuel companies, Vinod Khosla seems unwavering in his commitment to the clean energy industry, pouring more money into start-ups.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/11/29/despite-setbacks-investor-is-bullish-on-clean-technology/', 'snippet': 'After taking a hit on investments in biofuel companies, Vinod Khosla seems unwavering in his commitment to the clean energy industry, pouring more money into start-ups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vinod Khosla crowed about the clean energy industry last year. Three of the biofuel start-ups in his venture capital portfolio had just gone public, and the stocks had risen considerably after their debuts. “I challenge anybody to claim that clean tech done right is a disaster,” Mr. Khosla said at a conference, rebuffing recent criticism. “We’ve generated more profits there than anybody has.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Setbacks, Investor Is Bullish on Clean Technology', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Long-Term Vision', 'name': None, 'seo': None, '