nyt://article/cee2f841-1e47-5483-90c7-58b987c97f22'}, {'abstract': 'Even after Palestine gained recognition as a nonmember state at the United Nations, the two countries seemed stuck in the same stalemate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/world/middleeast/palestinians-and-israel-seek-next-step-after-vote.html', 'snippet': 'Even after Palestine gained recognition as a nonmember state at the United Nations, the two countries seemed stuck in the same stalemate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Saeb Erekat, a senior Palestinian official, recently said that the day after Palestine gained recognition as a nonmember state at the United Nations, “Life will not be the same.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Vote, Palestinians and Israel Search for the Next Step', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Vote, Palestinians and Israel Search for the Next Step', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestine Liberation Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Jerusalem', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T00:29:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2f0dca1-1a53-5a03-838e-8bc34540b20e', 'word_count': 1119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2f0dca1-1a53-5a03-838e-8bc34540b20e'}, {'abstract': 'Curiosity, the NASA Mars rover, has not found the building blocks of life in that planet’s dirt, the agency said Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/science/space/nasa-plays-down-mars-speculation.html', 'snippet': 'Curiosity, the NASA Mars rover, has not found the building blocks of life in that planet’s dirt, the agency said Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Curiosity, the NASA Mars rover, has not found the building blocks of life in that planet’s dirt, the agency said Thursday. “Rumors and speculation that there are major new findings from the mission at this early stage are incorrect,” NASA’s Jet Propulsion Laboratory in Pasadena, Calif., said in a statement. Tamping down expectations about a news conference scheduled for Monday, NASA said, “The instruments on the rover have not detected any definitive evidence of Martian organics.” Speculation was fueled last week when the mission’s project scientist told a reporter that data from Curiosity would be “one for the history books.” NASA later clarified that the scientist was speaking generally. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NASA Plays Down Mars Speculation', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Space', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nasa Plays Down Mars Speculation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mars (Planet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Curiosity (Mars Rover)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T00:47:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f248f51b-9929-55ed-88b3-e5ede5034ceb', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f248f51b-9929-55ed-88b3-e5ede5034ceb'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Fraser’s film, “My Brothers,” describes a road trip in a barely working van, in search of a link to a father.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/movies/my-brothers-directed-by-paul-fraser.html', 'snippet': 'Paul Fraser’s film, “My Brothers,” describes a road trip in a barely working van, in search of a link to a father.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The road trip that squabbling Irish siblings make in “My Brothers,” the directorial debut of Paul Fraser, takes place over Halloween weekend in 1987. But the movie’s drab, working-class milieu is closer to the kitchen-sink realism of Anglo-Irish films from the early 1960s. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30MYBROTHERS_SPAN/30MYBROTHERS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30MYBROTHERS_SPAN/30MYBROTHERS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption'