 said Thursday. Falling birthrates among immigrant women were driving the drop, said the center, analyzing federal data. The birthrate declined by 14 percent among foreign-born women from 2007 to 2010, more than double the 6 percent drop among American-born women over the same period. The rate for Mexican immigrants fell by 23 percent. The report found no decline in the number of foreign-born women of childbearing age, and cited economic distress as the likely reason for the decline. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Immigrants Drive Drop in Birthrate', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Immigrants Drive Drop In Birthrate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Rates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T00:53:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3291914-8bde-55d0-a9e7-28e5b950a684', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3291914-8bde-55d0-a9e7-28e5b950a684'}, {'abstract': 'Seeking to position themselves favorably in the early stages of the New York mayoral campaign, four presumptive Democratic candidates outlined their credentials to a business-oriented audience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/nyregion/100000001930888/after-mayor-bloomberg.html', 'snippet': 'Seeking to position the