, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tango', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T02:13:46+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/3fa339df-8408-5168-8cdb-8544d8bb5205', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/3fa339df-8408-5168-8cdb-8544d8bb5205'}, {'abstract': 'Taxpayers should applaud a new law that protects whistle-blowers’ rights, who too often suffered retaliation by their superiors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/opinion/new-protections-for-whistle-blowers.html', 'snippet': 'Taxpayers should applaud a new law that protects whistle-blowers’ rights, who too often suffered retaliation by their superiors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daring to blow the whistle on government waste, fraud and mismanagement has never been an easy course for federal workers, who too often suffered retaliation by their superiors. Finally, on Tuesday, after a 13-year trip through Congress, legislation more firmly protecting whistle-blowers’ rights was signed by President Obama. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Protections for Whistle-Blowers', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Protections for Whistle-Blowers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whistle-Blowers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Security Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T02:14:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f84d1283-8e99-5ff5-9357-e1940af0d7fb', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f84d1283-8e99-5ff5-9357-e1940af0d7fb'}, {'abstract': 'In the German film “What a Man,” Matthias Schweighöfer learns to accept himself as he is, even if it’s not what his girlfriend wanted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/movies/what-a-man-by-matthias-schweighofer.html', 'snippet': 'In the German film “What a Man,” Matthias Schweighöfer learns to accept himself as he is, even if it’s not what his girlfriend wanted.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I may be unhappy, but I’m orderly,” says poor Alex (Matthias Schweighöfer), a timid schoolteacher in Frankfurt. Why so unhappy? Simple: Alex can’t catch a break. Certainly not from Carolin (Mavie Hörbiger), his icy live-in girlfriend, who keeps a closet loaded with sexual accessories and fools around with a manly-man neighbor (Thomas Kretschmann). (Mortified, Alex moves out.) And not even from his bud Okke (Elyas M’Barek), who tries to help Alex find his inner machismo by taking him to nightclubs, boxing gyms and paintball battles, and dressing him like Eminem. Eventually, Alex tries a forest camp of Robert Bly-like testosterone building — but with axes and trees, not lectures.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30RDP_WHAT_SPAN/30RDP_WHAT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30RDP_WHAT_SPAN/30RDP_WHAT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30RDP_WHAT_SPAN/30RDP_WHAT_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30RDP_WHAT_SPAN/30RDP_WHAT_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 933, 'width': 1400, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30RDP_WHAT_SPAN/30RDP_WHAT_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30RDP_WHAT_SPAN/30RDP_WHAT_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30RDP_WHAT_SPAN/30RDP_WHAT_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Schoolteacher Searching for His Machismo', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What a Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'What a Man (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweighofer, Matthias', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T02:16:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9785ed2a-cac5-5051-b949-d9bb875c6a29', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9785ed2a-cac5-5051-b949-d9bb875c6a29'}, {'abstract': 'Requiring agencies to translate essential public documents into six languages besides English is progress in a county that has had its share of anti-immigrant resentment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/opinion/suffolk-county-turns-a-page.html', 'snippet': 'Requiring agencies to translate essential public documents into six languages besides English is progress in a county that has had its share of anti-immigrant resentment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steve Bellone, the Suffolk County executive, signed an executive order on Nov. 14 requiring county agencies to translate essential public documents and forms into six languages besides English and to provide translation services for residents who don’t speak English well. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suffolk County Turns a Page', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suffolk County Turns a Page', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bellone, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levy, Steven A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Suffolk County (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value':