n reflection, “Walk Away Renee” revisits the personal universe of its director, Jonathan Caouette, through his schizophrenic mother’s latest travails. Mr. Caouette’s 2004 autobiographical whatzit, “Tarnation,” was celebrated as both fearless tell-all and nano-budgeted digital feat. This less flashy and performative follow-up plays like a ruminative shuffle through captioned family albums, primed by cyclical mental health dramas.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30RDP_WLAK_SPAN/30RDP_WLAK_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30RDP_WLAK_SPAN/30RDP_WLAK_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30RDP_WLAK_SPAN/30RDP_WLAK_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30RDP_WLAK_SPAN/30RDP_WLAK_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30RDP_WLAK_SPAN/30RDP_WLAK_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30RDP_WLAK_SPAN/30RDP_WLAK_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30RDP_WLAK_SPAN/30RDP_WLAK_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'widt