ear-long study of two Canadian university hockey teams, despite years of discussion about risks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/sports/hockey/hockey-coaches-defy-doctors-on-concussions-study-finds.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers noted an entrenched culture of playing through head injuries during a year-long study of two Canadian university hockey teams, despite years of discussion about risks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite several years of intensive research, coverage and discussion about the dangers of concussions, the idea of playing through head injuries is so deeply rooted in hockey culture that two university teams kept concussed players on the ice even though they were taking part in a major concussion study.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/sports/brain-1/brain-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/sports/brain-1/brain-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Report Urges ‘Cultural Shift’ as Hockey Coaches Defy Concussion Specialists', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Report Urges ‘Cultural Shift’ as Coaches Defy Concussion Specialists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Western Ontario', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'H