 you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | November 30, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T06:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35492113-a3d4-5131-b089-9c417bcf0521', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35492113-a3d4-5131-b089-9c417bcf0521'}, {'abstract': 'News, arts and sports from today’s International Herald Tribune.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/iht-quick-read-nov-30/', 'snippet': 'News, arts and sports from today’s International Herald Tribune.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWS Security forces in Myanmar mounted a violent raid Thursday against Buddhist monks and villagers protesting the expansion of a copper mine, using incendiary devices to set fire to protesters’ encampments, according to witnesses. The crackdown was the largest since President Thein Sein’s government came to power 20 months ago, and analysts said its brutality — online photos showed monks with badly seared skin — could hamper the president’s efforts to convince the country he has made a clean break from the military governments of the past. Thomas Fuller reports from Bangkok. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'IHT Quick Read: Nov. 30', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T06:52:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk'