ritical Thinking, Nov. 30, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T09:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1a90e65-82c7-5da5-a545-25d769cf31b0', 'word_count': 45, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1a90e65-82c7-5da5-a545-25d769cf31b0'}, {'abstract': 'As excitement heats up in India about the affordable health care industry, some questions remain.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/venture-capital-is-attracted-to-indias-affordable-health-care-business-which-targets-the-poor/', 'snippet': 'As excitement heats up in India about the affordable health care industry, some questions remain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Health care experts, investors and government officials gathered at New Delhi’s Habitat Center on Friday to discuss one of the most promising new investment areas in India: affordable health care.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should Health Care for the Very Poor Be a Fast-Growth Business?', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microfinance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T09:34:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a54179b2-191e-5e50-87f9-bc4a4124de8e', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a54179b2-191e-5e50-87f9-bc4a4124de8e'}, {'abstract': 'Why is the fact that the U.N. has granted Palestine this status so significant?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/u-n-general-assembly-grants-palestine-elevated-status/', 'snippet': 'Why is the fact that the U.N. has granted Palestine this status so significant?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Palestine Wins Status of State in Vote by U.N. Assembly,” Ethan Bronner and Christine Hauser report on the vote to grant Palestine the upgraded status of nonmember observer state in the United Nations. Below, some questions based on the article that might help provide a general understanding of this news. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/world/30palestine_337-LN/30palestine_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/30/world/30palestine_337-LN/30palestine_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/world/30palestine_337-LN/30palestine_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/world/30palestine_337-LN/30palestine_337-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1454, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail',