utside the agency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Japan’s space agency said on Friday that information on one of its newest rockets was stolen from a desktop computer by someone using a computer virus. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan’s Space Agency Says Rocket Information Was Stolen by Computer Virus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan: Rocket Data Stolen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Japan Aerospace Exploration Agency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T15:02:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c5b3b19-6a32-5595-821c-a95162f09c9d', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c5b3b19-6a32-5595-821c-a95162f09c9d'}, {'abstract': 'Jeff Zucker, late of NBC, has been given the reins at CNN and hopes to make it more relevant when there isn’t breaking news; Syria shuts down the Internet; the report on phone-hacking puts the pressure on British politicians; and, Steve Somers, the WFAN host.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/the-breakfast-meeting-zucker-to-run-cnn-and-a-late-night-sports-crooner/', 'snippet': 'Jeff Zucker, late of NBC, has been given the reins at CNN and hopes to make it more relevant when there isn’t breaking news; Syria shuts down the Internet; the report on phone-hacking puts the pressure on British politicians; and, Steve Somers, th...', 'lead_paragraph': 'CNN announced on Thursday that the rumors were true, and that Jeff Zucker, the former chief executive of NBC, would be its new leader, Bill Carter and Brian Stelter report. In an interview, Mr. Zucker, who said he first began his discussions with the network around Labor Day, said he would focus on finding a consistent audience when there wasn’t breaking news. “CNN has to find the right programming that exists in between the 25 nights a year when it is most relevant,” he said. “Beyond the fact that we are committed to news and journalism, everything else is open for discussion.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Zucker to Run CNN, and a Late-Night Sports Crooner', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zucker, Jeff', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barnes & Noble Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Press Complaints Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WFAN-AM', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T15:04:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6a92072-b3d6-5876-9197-38ed389ae6d4', 'word_count': 648, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6a92072-b3d6-5876-9197-38ed389ae6d4'}, {'abstract': 'The Spurs angered the N.B.A. commissioner but found support among sportswriters in the court of public opinion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/01/sports/spurs-rest-stars-stirring-debate-on-ethics-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'The Spurs angered the N.B.A. commissioner but found support among sportswriters in the court of public opinion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It tells you everything you need to know about N.B.A. Commissioner David Stern’s current standing in public opinion that he was instantly declared the loser in Thursday night’s hissing match with the perpetually grumpy coach of the Spurs, Gregg Popovich. Understand that siding with Popovich is a lot like snuggling with a porcupine. You can never get entirely comfortable and something sharp is going to poke you in the ribs at some point. But siding with Stern, the angry emperor? Bring on 10 porcupines.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/01/sports/basketball/01leadingpic/01leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/01/sports/basketball/01leadingpic/01leadingpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1448, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/01/sports/basketball/01leadingpic/01leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': 