ek on how elections should be conducted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/01/world/asia/nepals-political-leaders-given-more-time-to-agree-on-government.html', 'snippet': 'A spokesman for President Ram Baran Yadav of Nepal said the political parties were committed to having a conclusion next week on how elections should be conducted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Nepal’s president has granted political leaders one more week to reach agreement on a new coalition government that would hold elections next year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nepal’s Political Leaders Given More Time to Agree on Government', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nepal’s Political Leaders Are Given More Time to Agree on Government', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nepal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yadav, Ram Baran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Unified Communist Party of Nepal (Maoist)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bhattarai, Baburam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T15:25:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd18050e-b9bd-558f-b9dc-f27c117c3ce3', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd18050e-b9bd-558f-b9dc-f27c117c3ce3'}, {'abstract': 'For this dream dozen, it was a year to score big.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/twelve-for-12/', 'snippet': 'For this dream dozen, it was a year to score big.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For this dream dozen, it was a year to score big.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '148', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Twelve for 12', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Twelve for ’12', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T15:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacob Brown and Graeme Mitchell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Graeme', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mitchell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2af3c7c6-fd5b-5002-8573-2c2666290876', 'word_count': 16, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2af3c7c6-fd5b-5002-8573-2c2666290876'}, {'abstract': 'The Chinese Communist Party, which presided over the deaths of tens of millions of people during the Great Famine, has yet to even acknowledge the calamity.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/the-great-silence-of-china/', 'snippet': 'The Chinese Communist Party, which presided over the deaths of tens of millions of people during the Great Famine, has yet to even acknowledge the calamity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — On Thursday, China released Feng Xiaogang’s “Back to 1942,” a blockbuster film about the 1942-43 Henan famine, during which roughly three million people starved to death following a drought exacerbated by the Japanese invasion. The film made over $480,000 on its first day and is tipped to break box-office records.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Great Silence of China', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None,