small-business owners in their 50s who have saved little for retirement but can now afford to put aside a lot of money each year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH the prospect of significant changes in tax rates and deduction limits, taxpayers have been coming up with all sorts of strategies to save on their taxes, some riskier than others. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/01/business/wealth-matters/wealth-matters-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/12/01/business/wealth-matters/wealth-matters-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/01/business/wealth-matters/wealth-matters-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 568, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/01/business/wealth-matters/wealth-matters-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1136, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Save for Retirement in Just 10 Years? It’s Doable, but Risky', 'kicker': 'Wealth Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Save for Retirement In Just 10 Years? It’s Doable, but Risky', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T15:42:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/971487f6-ab29-5839-a98a-6ce5e64177b1', 'word_count': 1365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/971487f6-ab29-5839-a98a-6ce5e64177b1'}, {'abstract': 'The lesser flamingo is in danger of losing one of its premier mating lakes, in Tanzania, East Africa, to industrial construction.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/flamingos-at-risk-of-losing-a-mating-lake/', 'snippet': 'The lesser flamingo is in danger of losing one of its premier mating lakes, in Tanzania, East Africa, to industrial construction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year, rippling pink streamers descend from the sky and settle on Lake Natron in Tanzania, materializing into thousands of mating flamingo pairs. East Africa is home to 75 percent of the world’s population of lesser flamingos, and Lake Natron offers the most important breeding ground for these otherwise nomadic birds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Flamingos at Risk of Losing a Mating Lake', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flamingos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kikwete, Jakaya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Union for Conservation of Nature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tanzania', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T15:58:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma Bryce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bryce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe9f6c99-1aef-51b5-8486-ddf91ceea4c3', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe9f6c99-1aef-51b5-8486-ddf91ceea4c3'}, {'abstract': 'Academy voters can vote online, but those who want a paper ballot have two more weeks to request one.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/academy-extends-deadline-to-request-paper-ballots/', 'snippet': 'Academy voters can vote online, but those who want a paper ballot have two more weeks to request one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the changes that may most affect this season’s Oscar race is also the most procedural: the switch to online voting. After 84 years of mail-in (or walk-in) ballots only, the Academy has allowed members to have their say digitally this year, though they must register online (and pay their dues) first. Paper ballots are available for those who request them; yesterday, the Academy announced that the deadline to do so would be moved from today to Dec. 14. “We’re extending the deadline for requesting paper ballots to make completely sure that no member who prefers this method misses the boat,” Ric Robertson, the chief operating officer of the Academy, said in a statement. A majority of members, the statement says, have already registered.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30carpetbagger-ballot/30carpetbagger-ballot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 607, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30carpetbagger-ballot/30carpetbagger-ballot-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1214, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'ran