amination of the December dilemma: How Jews cope with “the only American national holiday rooted in a specific religious tradition that a significant minority of Americans fail to share.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hanumas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hanumas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hanukkah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Plaut, Joshua Eli', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T16:48:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elinor Lipman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elinor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7535ac9d-b8bd-5fff-b938-9cf5df5bfcf5', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7535ac9d-b8bd-5fff-b938-9cf5df5bfcf5'}, {'abstract': 'The Turkish prime minister calls for legal action against “Magnficent Century,” which is set in the reign of Suleiman the Magnificent.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/steamy-turkish-tv-drama-draws-fire-from-prime-minister/', 'snippet': 'The Turkish prime minister calls for legal action against “Magnficent Century,” which is set in the reign of Suleiman the Magnificent.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Magnificent Century,” a sort of Ottoman-era “Sex and the City” set during the reign of Sultan Suleiman the Magnificent, is wildly popular in Turkey and across the Middle East. But one person who is decidedly not a fan is Turkey’s conservative prime minister, Recep Tayyip Erdogan, who is so incensed at the show’s steamy depiction of the heroic sultan that he has urged legal action against the series. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steamy Turkish TV Drama Draws Fire From Prime Minister', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erdogan, Recep Tayyip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hurriyet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T16:48:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f70a152-f861-5417-b3a8-16a6d1bfbf73', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f70a152-f861-5417-b3a8-16a6d1bfbf73'}, {'abstract': 'Larry McMurtry’s breezy tour, with many artifacts, of Custer and the Battle of the Little Bighorn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/books/review/custer-by-larry-mcmurtry.html', 'snippet': 'Larry McMurtry’s breezy tour, with many artifacts, of Custer and the Battle of the Little Bighorn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A full 136 years after the last bluecoat in the Seventh Cavalry fell, the literary autopsy of the Battle of the Little Bighorn shows no sign of letting up, with fresh students drawn to the historical morgue every year. George Armstrong Custer — we can’t quit you.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202EGAN/1202EGAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 891, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202EGAN/1202EGAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1783, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202EGAN/1202EGAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202EGAN/1202EGAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202EGAN/1202EGAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The West', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The West', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMurtry, Larry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Custer, George Armstrong', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T16:48:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c36a195-793b-51ff-8ef7-b6a18086c39e', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c36a195-793b-51ff-8ef7-b6a18086c39e'}, {'abstract': 'Jacob Tomsky’s memoir about his 10-plus years in the hotel business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/books/review/heads-in-beds-by-jacob-tomsky.html', 'snippet': 'Jacob Tomsky’s memoir about his 10-plus years in the hotel business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you check in at your hotel, hand the desk agent a $20 bill, smile and say, “Whatever you can do for me, I’d appreciate it.” Don’t look at her name tag, and if you do, don’t use her name. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '45', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hotels', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hotels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tomsky, Jacob', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T16:49:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clancy Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc56a715-b16b-5265-83ab-9a38e4b04d6a', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc56a715-b16b-5265-83ab-9a38e4b04d6a'}, {'abstract': '“The Graphic Canon” reimagines the world’s literature as comics and visual art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/books/review/the-graphic-canon-edited-by-russ-kick.html', 'snippet': '“The Graphic Canon” reimagines the world’s literature as comics and visual art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a synergistic relationship between language and art that is rooted deep within our nature. Great literature leaves us not just with extraordinary stories; the language also leaves an image — a rich and expansive painting of the world written on the page. In “The Graphic Canon,” the world’s literature is reimagined as comics and visual art, and with it the editor, Russ Kick, has struck a chord. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202-Weatherwax/1202-Weatherwax-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 740, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202-Weatherwax/1202-Weatherwax-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1481, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202-Weatherwax/1202-Weatherwax-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202-Weatherwax/1202-Weatherwax-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202-Weatherwax/1202-Weatherwax-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Lit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Graphic Lit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kick, Russ', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '20