ine’s family drama will play its final performance at the Barrow Street Theater in January.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/an-off-broadway-rarity-tribes-recoups-its-investment/', 'snippet': 'Nina Raine’s family drama will play its final performance at the Barrow Street Theater in January.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even on Broadway, the vast majority of shows end up losing money. So the news that the Off-Broadway play “Tribes,” by Nina Raine, has recouped its investment makes it the little engine that could. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30artsbeat-tribes/30artsbeat-tribes-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30artsbeat-tribes/30artsbeat-tribes-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30artsbeat-tribes/30artsbeat-tribes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30artsbeat-tribes/30artsbeat-tribes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30artsbeat-tribes/30artsbeat-tribes-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Off-Broadway Rarity: ‘Tribes’ Recoups Its Investment', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doumanian, Jean', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morfee, Scott', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raine, Nina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barrow Street Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T16:53:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd3a7e04-3b45-5650-a212-0017a06db8f7', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd3a7e04-3b45-5650-a212-0017a06db8f7'}, {'abstract': 'Fifty portraits of Jews who have influenced sports in the locker room and beyond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/books/review/jewish-jocks-edited-by-franklin-foer-and-marc-tracy.html', 'snippet': 'Fifty portraits of Jews who have influenced sports in the locker room and beyond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to imagine two words less likely to appear in the same sentence than “Jewish” and “jocks.” The very image is something of a punch line. Scroll back to the 1980 slapstick classic “Airplane!” The flight attendant is walking down the aisle with an armful of bulky reading material. She comes upon an extremely frail woman who asks for “anything light.” The flight attendant reaches into the pile and pulls out a pamphlet the size of a takeout menu. “How about this?” she purrs. “Famous Jewish Sports Legends.” ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '49', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/books/review/1202OSHINSKY/1202OSHINSKY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtyp