com/2012/12/02/books/review/paperback-row.html', 'snippet': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MR. FOX,  by Helen Oyeyemi. (Riverhead, $16.) Playfully weaving variations of the Bluebeard myth, Oyeyemi’s captivating novel is presented in the alternating voices of St. John Fox, a celebrated slasher novelist in midcentury Manhattan; Daphne, his neglected wife; and Mary Foxe, his imaginary muse (and creative sparring partner), who challenges him to embrace intimacy over violence and death.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '72', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T17:12:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ihsan Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ihsan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ae4755b-9423-5a66-b88a-a3f0e792089f', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ae4755b-9423-5a66-b88a-a3f0e792089f'}, {'abstract': 'The San Antonio Spurs turned an early-season N.B.A. game into a national debate.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/the-coach-vs-the-commissioner/', 'snippet': 'The San Antonio Spurs turned an early-season N.B.A. game into a national debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The San Antonio Spurs and the Heat played in Miami on Thursday night, but it was really played at the intersection of sport and entertainment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/