l', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Plutnicki', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Plutnicki', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd684603-03f3-576d-ba3d-404b6193e700', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd684603-03f3-576d-ba3d-404b6193e700'}, {'abstract': 'David Wright could become the first star in Mets history to spend his entire career with the club.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/forever-a-met-and-probably-never-a-yankee/', 'snippet': 'David Wright could become the first star in Mets history to spend his entire career with the club.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By agreeing to a huge, new contract with the Mets, David Wright could become the first star in the team’s history who will spend his entire career with the club. Until now, the team’s best players — Tom Seaver, Keith Hernandez, Gary Carter, Mike Piazza, Darryl Strawberry, Johan Santana — either arrived in Queens from somewhere else or started with the Mets and then went elsewhere.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Forever a Met, and Probably Never a Yankee', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T17:17:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Schreiber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schreiber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/409b5645-6f0e-52a7-ad53-86f18a63970d', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/409b5645-6f0e-52a7-ad53-86f18a63970d'}, {'abstract': 'An auction will offer George Harrison’s leather jacket, a pair of his boots and an old Paul McCartney guitar.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/cleaning-out-the-beatles-closets/', 'snippet': 'An auction will offer George Harrison’s leather jacket, a pair of his boots and an old Paul McCartney guitar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The leather jacket that George Harrison wore when he first began performing with the Beatles in Liverpool and Hamburg will be auctioned off along with other musical memorabilia on Dec. 12 at Bonhams in London. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cleaning Out the Beatles’ Closets', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrison, George', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lennon, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCartney, Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beatles, The', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Quarrymen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liverpool (England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T17:18:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1307855-0995-5148-8a13-75de9731db1d', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1307855-0995-5148-8a13-75de9731db1d'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of events this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/arts/dec-2-dec-8.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of events this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THIS year BILLY JOE SHAVER released a pair of live albums. One, “Live at Billy Bob’s Texas” (Smith Music Group), was recorded in 2011, and the other, “Live From Austin, Tx.” (New West), was recorded in 1984. In terms of quality there’s not much air between them. On both Mr. Shaver — a Texas country star known for his dry wit and loose tongue — runs through a catalog of self-deprecating bad-behavior songs. Sure, the years between have done a little number on his voice, but what it lost in power he makes up for with curious inflections, little scrapes and twists that one learns over a lifetime of getting people’s attention in loud bars. Mr. Shaver will be playing at Hill Country Barbecue, one of the city’s underappreciated live music rooms — not just for the music, which spans the variety of Southern roots, from hillbilly swing to bluegrass to Texas country, but also because dinner reservations are available. 10 p.m. Wednesday, 30 West 26th Street, Manhattan, (212) 255-4544, music.hillcountryny.com; $25.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02GUIDE2_SPAN/02GUIDE2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02GUIDE2_SPAN/02GUIDE2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02GUIDE2_SPAN/02GUIDE2_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'