-again/', 'snippet': 'Luiz Felipe Scolari will lead Brazil into the 2014 World Cup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jose Maria Marin left little doubt that Luiz Felipe Scolari would be appointed Brazil’s manager for a second time when, having relieved the team’s former boss Mano Menezes of his duties on Friday, he revealed that the next national team trainer would be Brazilian, have a “winning profile” and be best suited to help the Selecão “realise the dream of a home championship.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/sports/soccer/30scolari/30scolari-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/sports/soccer/30scolari/30scolari-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/sports/soccer/30scolari/30scolari-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/30/sports/soccer/30scolari/30scolari-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/sports/soccer/30scolari/30scolari-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil Wraps Itself in Scolari’s Embrace Again', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 