//article/1110b326-dd47-5d4e-8496-f4b8637628f0'}, {'abstract': 'A Brookings Institution survey found that nearly half of the world’s poorest cities never suffered any decline from the Great Recession, and most of those that did have recovered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/01/business/economy/an-uneven-recovery-in-the-worlds-cities.html', 'snippet': 'A Brookings Institution survey found that nearly half of the world’s poorest cities never suffered any decline from the Great Recession, and most of those that did have recovered.', 'lead_paragraph': '“So the last shall be first, and the first last.” ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Uneven Recovery in the Cities of the World', 'kicker': 'Off the Charts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Uneven Recovery In the Cities Of the World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross National Product (GNP)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T18:41:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65adda81-2b70-5b41-b76b-6b5259c62824', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65adda81-2b70-5b41-b76b-6b5259c62824'}, {'abstract': 'Seventy-four years ago Georgia O’Keeffe discovered a tropical dreamland. Today, visitors can still see Maui as she painted it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/travel/georgia-okeeffes-hawaii.html', 'snippet': 'Seventy-four years ago Georgia O’Keeffe discovered a tropical dreamland. Today, visitors can still see Maui as she painted it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EARLY in 1939, Georgia O’Keeffe, the artist most famous for depicting the arid Southwest, suddenly decided to paint America’s diametrically opposite landscape — the lush tropical valleys of Hawaii. In an era when advertisers often hired fine artists to add a touch of class to their campaigns, the “least commercial artist in the U.S.” (as Time Magazine described her) was persuaded by the Dole pineapple company to visit the remote Pacific archipelago and produce two canvases. The offer came at a critical time in O’Keeffe’s life. She was 51, her career seemed to be stalling (critics were calling her focus on New Mexico limited, and branding her desert images “a kind of mass production”), and her marriage to Alfred Stieglitz was under serious strain.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/travel/02HAWAII_SPAN/02HAWAII_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/12/02/travel/02HAWAII_SPAN/02HAWAII_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 358}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/travel/02HAWAII_SPAN/02JPHAWAII1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/travel/02HAWAII_SPAN/02JPHAWAII1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1223, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/travel/02HAWAII_SPAN/02HAWAII_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/12/02/travel/02HAWAII_SPAN/02HAWAII_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'O’Keeffe’s Hawaii', 'kicker': 'Footsteps', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'O’Keeffe’s Hawaii', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maui (Hawaii)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Keeffe, Georgia", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T18:42:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tony Perrottet', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perrottet', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cb182b0-8322-56ad-9757-fc5df9b8a4b2', 'word_count': 2838, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cb182b0-8322-56ad-9757-fc5df9b8a4b2'}, {'abstract': 'Poetry, songs and kombucha at the Cafe Attitude.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/travel/a-night-in-bohemian-hana.html', 'snippet': 'Poetry, songs and kombucha at the Cafe Attitude.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GEORGIA O’KEEFFE was an artistic pioneer in Hana. Today there are entire communities of poets, musicians and organic farmers thriving deep in the rain forest. In recent years, a new wave of these gastronomy-loving young farmers have congregated in the fertile area called Kipahulu, south of Hana, living an off-the-grid life on their own delicious tropical produce. Some operate humble fruit and vegetable stands along the road, or blend smoothies for tourists. On Whispering Winds Bamboo farm, I was strolling the crops with a farmer named Ryan, when a group of people sped past us, clinging onto an all-terrain vehicle. “That’s Woody Harrelson and his family,” Ryan said with a shrug. “He has a place next door.”', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Night in Bohemian Hana', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Night In Bohemian Hana', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T18:42:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tony Perrottet', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perrottet', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d8bc101-d5ee-5193-adaf-510396ec0820', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d8bc101-d5ee-5193-adaf-510396ec0820'}, {'abstract': 'Marshawn Lynch is a must-start, but keep expectations low as he, Jay Cutler and other Bears and Seahawks are among our unfavorable matchup picks for Week 13.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/week-13-in-fantasy-football-favorable-and-unfavorable-matchups-2/', 'snippet': 'Marshawn Lynch is a must-start, but keep expectations low as he, Jay Cutler and other Bears and Seahawks are among our unfavorable matchup picks for Week 13.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jason and Justin Sablich will provide fantasy football advice and analysis throughout the season on this blog and on Twitter @5thDownFantasy. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week 13 in Fantasy Football: Favorable and Unfavorable Matchups', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Personnel File', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cutler, Jay', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Marshawn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bears', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T18:42:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Sablich and Jason Sablich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7406294-4ee0-5b91-bb80-4ab7c0aee75d', 'word_count': 2250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7406294-4ee0-5b91-bb80-4ab7c0aee75d'}, {'abstract': 'On a high-altitude adventure along South Korea’s mountainous spine, discovering the ancient pull of the peaks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/travel/along-the-trail-of-koreas-mountain-spirits.html', 'snippet': 'On a high-altitude adventure along South Korea’s mountainous spine, discovering the ancient pull of the peaks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE titanium spork was a Christmas gift from my brother Gregory, a choice that seemed random at the time. I had no use for ultra-lightweight dual-use cutlery. But nine months later, almost 7,000 miles from my home in New York City and nearly catatonic with exhaustion, I was thankful for its lack of heft. Gregory; my husband, Joe; and I had been hiking for 12 hours while hoisting a 30-pound backpack over steep and slippery rock in a thick mist. After nightfall, headlamps fading, we spotted dots of light below us in the dark, and heard the eerie whoosh of a wind generator. We stumbled down to the Satgat-jae shelter, a basic cabin for hikers perched at over 4,200 feet in South Korea’s Deogyusan National Park. I unpacked my spork. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/travel/02EXPLORER1_SPAN/02EXPLORER1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/12/02/travel/02EXPLORER1_SPAN/02EXPLORER1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/travel/02EXPLORER1_SPAN/02EXPLORER1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/travel/02EXPLORER1_SPAN/02EXPLORER1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/travel/02EXPLORER1_SPAN/02EXPLORER1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'th