, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethanol', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN AUTOMOBILE ASSN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T19:42:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2ea2373-8010-50f4-9546-0b6a33569b53', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2ea2373-8010-50f4-9546-0b6a33569b53'}, {'abstract': 'Times critics on “Killing Them Softly,” “Dragon” and “King Kelly.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/this-weeks-movies-nov-30/', 'snippet': 'Times critics on “Killing Them Softly,” “Dragon” and “King Kelly.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Times critics offer their thoughts on the crime drama “Killing Them Softly” with Brad Pitt, the martial arts film “Dragon” and “King Kelly,” a film shot almost entirely with cellphones. See all of this week’s reviews here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week’s Movies: Nov. 30', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pitt, Brad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T19:49:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f36c565-d993-5b18-9dd1-a93b1cba32eb', 'word_count': 39, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f36c565-d993-5b18-9dd1-a93b1cba32eb'}, {'abstract': 'The independence of college vs. the old rules at home. If you’ve experienced culture clash during that first winter break, a Times reporter wants to hear your story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/booming/at-home-for-first-winter-break-discuss.html', 'snippet': 'The independence of college vs. the old rules at home. If you’ve experienced culture clash during that first winter break, a Times reporter wants to hear your story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m a Times reporter writing an article about what happens when college freshmen come home for that looonnnggg winter break: parents have become accustomed to the quiet, the neatness, the freedom ... and the students are now used to following their own rules. CLASH!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Home for First Winter Break. Discuss.', 'kicker': 'The Friday Question', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T19:49:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jan Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9356341e-fb27-56f3-9a33-d7d9142b1c4d', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9356341e-fb27-56f3-9a33-d7d9142b1c4d'}, {'abstract': 'The fate of “The Mob Doctor” and “Emily Owens, M.D.” suggest that viewers may be tiring of the genre.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/are-tv-viewers-sick-of-medical-dramas/', 'snippet': 'The fate of “The Mob Doctor” and “Emily Owens, M.D.” suggest that viewers may be tiring of the genre.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Medical dramas are one of television’s oldest and most reliable staples, but based on Nielsen ratings from this season viewers may be growing tired of the genre. Two first-year-resident programs, “The Mob Doctor” on Fox and “Emily Owens, M.D.” on the CW network, were effectively fired on Wednesday after dismal fall performances.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30artsbeat-medical/30artsbeat-medical-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 805, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30artsbeat-medical/30artsbeat-medical-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 805, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30artsbeat-medical/30artsbeat-medical-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30artsbeat-medical/30artsbeat-medical-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/arts/30artsbeat-medical/30artsbeat-medical-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Are TV Viewers Sick of Medical Dramas?', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CW Television Network', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T19:50:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87a2c6c6-6bc1-5447-acdb-169e2c0fb084', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87a2c6c6-6bc1-5447-acdb-169e2c0fb084'}, {'abstract': 'Switching sides in the battle that is holiday shopping.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/a-little-give-and-take/', 'snippet': 'Switching sides in the battle that is holiday shopping.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is there anything more satisfying than complaining about the commercialization of Christmas? Could there be a better use of righteous indignation? Let us raise a chorus of voices against the traffic, which is like crawling into a pot of failed fudge, or the misguided dream of finding a parking place, which spawns a vigilant circling of the sixth floor of the garage. It felt so pushy all those years the store decorations went up the day after Thanksgiving, except that now they go up two weeks before Halloween. The carols jingle, flaying our last nerve, while we spend money we don’t have to buy gifts they won’t enjoy. In the process, we shave off just a little more of whatever sense of holiday wonder we ever possessed in the first place.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '161', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Little Give and Take', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Little Give and Take', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T19:54:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Patchett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patchett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fce1cee3-8e88-5dbd-8fd5-d100567f1e97', 'word_count': 1250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fce1cee3-8e88-5dbd-8fd5-d100567f1e97'}, {'abstract': 'By prevailing in the ratings for the month of November, “Good Morning America” gave more evidence of the changing of the guard in morning TV.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/good-morning-america-notches-first-sweeps-win-over-today/', 'snippet': 'By prevailing in the ratings for the month of November, “Good Morning America” gave more evidence of the changing of the guard in morning TV.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABC’s “Good Morning America” has won its first television sweeps month in nearly 20 years, reflecting its newfound status as America’s No. 1 morning show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Good Morning America’ Notches First Sweeps Win Over ‘Today’', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T19:54:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/228680d1-8c9c-52af-8e0f-7b950f40689c', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/228680d1-8c9c-52af-8e0f-7b950f40689c'}, {'abstract': 'The pilot for the ABC nighttime soap “Revenge,” ostensibly set in the Hamptons, was made in and around Southport, N.C., where the real beach house that stars in it is on the market for almost $1.6 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/realestate/nose-prints-on-the-glass-a-beach-houses-star-turn-in-revenge.html', 'snippet': 'The pilot for the ABC nighttime soap “Revenge,” ostensibly set in the Hamptons, was made in and around Southport, N.C., where the real beach house that stars in it is on the market for almost $1.6 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON the ABC nighttime soap “Revenge,” the character Emily Thorne (Emily VanCamp) moves into her childhood charmer of a beach house, where she plots how to undermine those who destroyed her family. The show, ostensibly set in the Hamptons, is now shot mostly at a California studio. But the pilot was made in and around Southport, N.C., where the real beach house went on the market about six and a half months ago, for almost $1.6 million.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nose Prints on the Glass: A Beach House’s Star Turn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nose Prints on the Glass: A Beach House’s Star Turn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T19:57:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jan Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52a742f9-7806-5743-b390-1574ee6073e1', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52a742f9-7806-5743-b390-1574ee6073e1'}, {'abstract': 'Bucks readers discuss their retirement savings strategies.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/catching-up-on-retirement-savings/', 'snippet': 'Bucks readers discuss their retirement savings strategies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Sullivan writes this week in his Wealth Matters column about a defined-benefit plan aimed at small-business owners in their 50s who have saved little for retirement. The plan allows them to make annual contributions of as much as $255,000. The owners can then deduct that money as a business expense, resulting in a significant tax savings. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Catching Up on Retirement Savings', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Savings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T19:58:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f115fa89-6cbb-5a04-aabd-fb900af0cfea', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f115fa89-6cbb-5a04-aabd-fb900af0cfea'}, {'abstract': 'If Balenciaga wants to go in a different direction, Alexander Wang could be a good choice as creative director.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/waiting-for-alexander/', 'snippet': 'If Balenciaga wants to go in a different direction, Alexander Wang could be a good choice as creative director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT looks as if Alexander Wang will be the next designer of Balenciaga. The company hasn’t commented on various media reports, but an announcement is expected as early as Monday. There has been plenty of reaction on Twitter, with probably more people favoring a Wang-designed Balenciaga than not, but the skeptics have some choice words, like “I hate this.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Waiting for Alexander', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Waiting for Alexander', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghesquiere, Nicolas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang, Alexander', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BALENCIAGA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PPR', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T19:59:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bff36cb5-5752-5994-8855-9e4dd3b1c85c', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bff36cb5-5752-5994-8855-9e4dd3b1c85c'}, {'abstract': 'If Dwyane Wade’s explosiveness is a thing of the past, the writer says, he can continue to help the Heat by developing a reliable 3-point shot and making post-ups a bigger part of his game.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/foot-injury-leaves-a-marvel-looking-rather-normal/', 'snippet': 'If Dwyane Wade’s explosiveness is a thing of the past, the writer says, he can continue to help the Heat by developing a reliable 3-point shot and making post-ups a bigger part of his game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dwyane Wade has always gotten away with it. Whether it’s deciding to shoot a bad jump shot or gambling on defense, Wade’s athleticism and anticipation have always bailed him out. He had a knack for following those troubling plays with an unstoppable drive through the defense, or by soaring in to block a much taller player at the rim.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/sports/basketball/30wade/30wade-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/sports/basketball/30wade/30wade-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1511, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/sports/basketball/30wade/30wade-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/30/sports/basketball/30wade/30wade-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/30/sports/basketball/30wade/30wade-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'head