ess Huguette M. Clark sold for $22.5 million, the most expensive sale of the week, according to city records. Mrs. Clark died in May at age 104, leaving two wills, a $400 million fortune and no direct heirs.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Ticket | Sold for $22.5 Million', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '$22,500,000', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Huguette M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soros, Susan Weber', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fifth Avenue (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T20:32:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e07e6f5-dfd0-5f35-a497-8e8e7342279e', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e07e6f5-dfd0-5f35-a497-8e8e7342279e'}, {'abstract': 'David Tanis sings the praises of the sweet, floral, fragrant Meyer lemon.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/the-meyer-lemon-all-sweet-no-pucker/', 'snippet': 'David Tanis sings the praises of the sweet, floral, fragrant Meyer lemon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s City Kitchen column there’s a recipe for a simple Meyer lemon vinaigrette that’s a bit on the chunky side, almost salsalike. And it takes only one Meyer lemon (or two small ones) to make it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Meyer Lemon: All Sweet, No Pucker', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicke