, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6af8a33-da53-5859-b3b7-8fa5f98a506c', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6af8a33-da53-5859-b3b7-8fa5f98a506c'}, {'abstract': 'The Holiday issue of T celebrates the season with a look back at some of the year’s most illustrious people.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/now-online-t-holiday-2012/', 'snippet': 'The Holiday issue of T celebrates the season with a look back at some of the year’s most illustrious people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Holiday issue of T celebrates the season with a look back at some of the year’s most illustrious people. Our man on the cover, Jude Law, talks with Sarah Lyall about turning 40 in Hollywood; Paul Rudd discusses his turn on Broadway in “Grace”; and the photographer Graeme Mitchell presents a portfolio of a dozen newsmakers, from the director Ang Lee to the Olympian Gabrielle Douglas. Elsewhere, we tag along with the artist Leo Villareal as he installs a mammoth public artwork on San Francisco’s Bay Bridge, and drop in on Vacheron Constantin’s recently opened watchmaking institute in Texas. We also take stock of the year — literally — with a roundup of calendar watches, emerald rings and beauty remedies, along with a heaving array of gift-worthy goods for everyone (including yourself). See all from the issue »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'T Holiday 2012', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T23:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/228d88f1-9389-5652-91ed-dc2a63da32aa', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/228d88f1-9389-5652-91ed-dc2a63da32aa'}, {'abstract': 'The soprano Jennifer Zetlan performed on Thursday at Alice Tully Hall in a recital that was her prize for winning the Alice Tully Vocal Arts Award.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/01/arts/music/jennifer-zetlan-soprano-at-alice-tully-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The soprano Jennifer Zetlan performed on Thursday at Alice Tully Hall in a recital that was her prize for winning the Alice Tully Vocal Arts Award.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first sound out of Jennifer Zetlan’s mouth on Thursday evening was a wordless “O” that began quietly, as if emanating from her subconscious. Then it grew fuller and rounder, billowing out with a gentle, melismatic flutter before settling into the simple melody of Handel’s “O sleep, why dost thou leave me?” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid All the Words, a Particular Sound Stands Out', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid All the Words, a Particular Sound Stands Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alice Tully Hall (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zetlan, Jennifer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T23:03:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/75b77fe1-1f17-5202-b55d-ed0c28f09960', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75b77fe1-1f17-5202-b55d-ed0c28f09960'}, {'abstract': 'A look at some of the titles in the Cinema Archives series, from 20th Century Fox.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/movies/homevideo/the-cinema-archives-series-from-20th-century-fox.html', 'snippet': 'A look at some of the titles in the Cinema Archives series, from 20th Century Fox.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S been six months since 20th Century Fox introduced its Cinema Archives series, that venerable studio’s response to the successful manufactured-on-demand lines of no-frills DVD-R editions of older films introduced by Warner Brothers, Sony and MGM/UA. But every time I sit down to write about it, another batch of titles arrives, which seems like a good excuse to put it off for another few weeks.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02KEHR1_SPAN/02SUBKEHR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02KEHR1_SPAN/02SUBKEHR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02KEHR1_SPAN/02SUBKEHR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02KEHR1_SPAN/02SUBKEHR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1548, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/arts/02KEHR1_SPAN/02SUBKEHR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, '