st exhibition in the Matrix contemporary art series encompasses the global effects of violence, corruption and the misuse of power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/02/nyregion/ahmed-alsoudani-matrix-165-at-the-wadsworth-atheneum-museum-of-art-in-hartford.html', 'snippet': 'The subject of the newest exhibition in the Matrix contemporary art series encompasses the global effects of violence, corruption and the misuse of power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARTFORD — With their brightly colored jumbles of cartoonish forms, the six paintings in “Ahmed Alsoudani/Matrix 165,” the newest exhibition in the Matrix contemporary art series at the Wadsworth Atheneum Museum of Art, at first seem cheery. But closer observation reveals content quite different. Broken pipes and tubes curl around thorny growths and disembodied limbs. Eyeballs pop from contorted faces with mouths agape as if howling. There are fleshless bones, shards of glass, bits of machinery, and in one image, something resembling a bloodied, bandaged stump. “I use a happy color palette for a hard subject,” Mr. Alsoudani said.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/nyregion/02ARTSCT2/02ARTSCT2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 743, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/nyregion/02ARTSCT2/02ARTSCT2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1487, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/nyregion/02ARTSCT2/02ARTSCT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/12/02/nyregion/02ARTSCT2/02ARTSCT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/02/nyregion/02ARTSCT2/02ARTSCT2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trying to Make Sense Out of Chaos', 'kicker': 'Arts | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trying to Make Sense Out of Chaos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hartford (Conn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wadsworth Atheneum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-11-30T23:48:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Hodara', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodara', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b88c80d8-5aa1-54ec-8b7e-12716efb609c', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b88c80d8-5aa1-54ec-8b7e-12716efb609c'}, {'abstract': 'Readers discuss whether President Obama should pick Susan E. Rice to be secretary of state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/12/01/opinion/the-partisan-bickering-over-susan-rices-future.html', 'snippet': 'Readers discuss whether President Obama should pick Susan E. Rice to be secretary of state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Partisan Bickering Over Susan Rice’s Future', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Partisan Bickering Over Susan Rice’s Future', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'va